#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/arraymesh.rst:368
msgid "Put together, the rectangle generation code looks like:"
msgstr "ເມື່ອນຳມາລວມກັນ, ໂຄ້ດການສ້າງຮູບສີ່ແຈສາກຈະມີລັກສະນະດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/arraymesh.rst:451
msgid "For a more complex example, see the sphere generation section below."
msgstr "ສຳລັບຕົວຢ່າງທີ່ຊັບຊ້ອນກວ່າ, ໃຫ້ເບິ່ງພາກສ່ວນການສ້າງໜ່ວຍມົນຢູ່ຂ້າງລຸ່ມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/arraymesh.rst:454
msgid "Generating a sphere"
msgstr "ການສ້າງໜ່ວຍມົນ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/arraymesh.rst:456
msgid ""
"Here is sample code for generating a sphere. Although the code is presented "
"in GDScript, there is nothing Godot specific about the approach to "
"generating it. This implementation has nothing in particular to do with "
"ArrayMeshes and is just a generic approach to generating a sphere. If you "
"are having trouble understanding it or want to learn more about procedural "
"geometry in general, you can use any tutorial that you find online."
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ຄືຕົວຢ່າງໂຄ້ດສຳລັບການສ້າງໜ່ວຍມົນ. ເຖິງວ່າໂຄ້ດຈະຖືກນຳສະເໜີໃນ GDScript, ແຕ່ບໍ່ມີຫຍັງທີ່ເປັນ ຂອງ "
"Godot ໂດຍສະເພາະກ່ຽວກັບວິທີການສ້າງມັນ. ການນຳໃຊ້ນີ້ບໍ່ໄດ້ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັບ ArrayMeshes ໂດຍສະເພາະ ແລ"
"ະ ເປັນພຽງວິທີການທົ່ວໄປໃນການສ້າງໜ່ວຍມົນ. ຖ້າເຈົ້າມີບັນຫາໃນການເຮັດຄວາມເຂົ້າໃຈ ຫຼື ຕ້ອງການຮຽນຮູ້ເພີ່ມເຕີ"
"ມກ່ຽວກັບເລຂາຄະນິດແບບໂປຣຊີເດິຣໍ (procedural geometry) ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປ, ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ບົດຮຽນໃດກໍໄດ້ທີ່"
"ເຈົ້າພົບໃນອອນໄລນ໌."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/arraymesh.rst:571
msgid "Saving"
msgstr "ການບັນທຶກ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/arraymesh.rst:573
msgid ""
"Finally, we can use the :ref:`ResourceSaver <class_resourcesaver>` class to "
"save the ArrayMesh. This is useful when you want to generate a mesh and then "
"use it later without having to re-generate it."
msgstr ""
"ໃນທີ່ສຸດ, ພວກເຮົາສາມາດໃຊ້ຄລາສ :ref:`ResourceSaver <class_resourcesaver>` ເພື່ອບັນທຶກ "
"ArrayMesh. ນີ້ມີປະໂຫຍດເມື່ອເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການສ້າງ mesh ແລ້ວນຳໄປໃຊ້ໃນພາຍຫຼັງ ໂດຍບໍ່ຕ້ອງສ້າງມັນໃຫມ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/meshdatatool.rst:4
msgid "Using the MeshDataTool"
msgstr "ການນຳໃຊ້ MeshDataTool"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/meshdatatool.rst:6
msgid ""
"The :ref:`MeshDataTool <class_meshdatatool>` is not used to generate "
"geometry. But it is helpful for dynamically altering geometry, for example "
"if you want to write a script to tessellate, simplify, or deform meshes."
msgstr ""
":ref:`MeshDataTool <class_meshdatatool>` ບໍ່ໄດ້ຖືກນຳໃຊ້ເພື່ອສ້າງເລຂາຄະນິດ. ແຕ່ມັນມີປະໂຫຍດ"
"ໃນການປ່ຽນແປງເລຂາຄະນິດແບບໄດນາມິກ, ຕົວຢ່າງ: ຖ້າທ່ານຕ້ອງການຂຽນສະຄຣິບເພື່ອແບ່ງຍ່ອຍ, ເຮັດໃຫ້ງ່າຍຂຶ້"
"ນ, ຫຼື ປ່ຽນຮູບຮ່າງຂອງເມສ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/meshdatatool.rst:9
msgid ""
"The MeshDataTool is not as fast as altering arrays directly "
"using :ref:`ArrayMesh <class_arraymesh>`. However, it provides more "
"information and tools to work with meshes than the ArrayMesh does. When the "
"MeshDataTool is used, it calculates mesh data that is not available in "
"ArrayMeshes such as faces and edges, which are necessary for certain mesh "
"algorithms. If you do not need this extra information then it may be better "
"to use an ArrayMesh."
msgstr ""
"MeshDataTool ບໍ່ໄດ້ໄວເທົ່າກັບການປ່ຽນແປງອາເຣໂດຍກົງໂດຍໃຊ້ :ref:`ArrayMesh "
"<class_arraymesh>`. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ມັນໃຫ້ຂໍ້ມູນ ແລະ ເຄື່ອງມືໃນການເຮັດວຽກກັບ meshes ຫຼາຍກວ່າ "
"ArrayMesh. ເມື່ອໃຊ້ MeshDataTool, ມັນຈະຄິດໄລ່ຂໍ້ມູນ mesh ທີ່ບໍ່ມີຢູ່ໃນ ArrayMeshes ເຊັ່ນ: ໜ້າ "
"(faces) ແລະ ຂອບ (edges), ເຊິ່ງຈຳເປັນສຳລັບອັນກໍຣິທຶມ mesh ບາງຢ່າງ. ຖ້າເຈົ້າບໍ່ຕ້ອງການຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີ"
"ມນີ້, ມັນອາດຈະດີກວ່າ ທີ່ຈະໃຊ້ ArrayMesh."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/meshdatatool.rst:14
msgid ""
"MeshDataTool can only be used on Meshes that use the PrimitiveType "
"``Mesh.PRIMITIVE_TRIANGLES``."
msgstr ""
"MeshDataTool ສາມາດໃຊ້ໄດ້ກັບ Meshes ທີ່ໃຊ້ PrimitiveType "
"``Mesh.PRIMITIVE_TRIANGLES`` ເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/meshdatatool.rst:16
msgid ""
"We initialize the MeshDataTool from an ArrayMesh by "
"calling :ref:`create_from_surface() "
"<class_meshdatatool_method_create_from_surface>`. If there is already data "
"initialized in the MeshDataTool, calling ``create_from_surface()`` will "
"clear it for you. Alternatively, you can call :ref:`clear() "
"<class_meshdatatool_method_clear>` yourself before re-using the MeshDataTool."
msgstr ""
"ພວກເຮົາເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ MeshDataTool ຈາກ ArrayMesh ໂດຍການເອີ້ນ :ref:`create_from_surface() "
"<class_meshdatatool_method_create_from_surface>`. ຖ້າມີຂໍ້ມູນທີ່ຖືກເລີ່ມຕົ້ນໄວ້ແລ້ວໃນ "
"MeshDataTool, ການເອີ້ນ ``create_from_surface()`` ຈະລຶບຂໍ້ມູນນັ້ນໃຫ້ເຈົ້າ. ຫຼື ເຈົ້າສາມາດເອີ້ນ "
":ref:`clear() <class_meshdatatool_method_clear>` ດ້ວຍຕົວເອງກ່ອນທີ່ຈະນຳໃຊ້ "
"MeshDataTool ອີກຄັ້ງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/meshdatatool.rst:19
msgid ""
"In the examples below, assume an ArrayMesh called ``mesh`` has already been "
"created. See :ref:`ArrayMesh tutorial <doc_arraymesh>` for an example of "
"mesh generation."
msgstr ""
"ໃນຕົວຢ່າງຂ້າງລຸ່ມນີ້, ສົມມຸດວ່າ ArrayMesh ທີ່ຊື່ວ່າ ``mesh`` ໄດ້ຖືກສ້າງຂຶ້ນແລ້ວ. ເບິ່ງ "
":ref:`ArrayMesh tutorial <doc_arraymesh>` ສຳລັບຕົວຢ່າງການສ້າງ mesh."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/meshdatatool.rst:32
msgid ""
"``create_from_surface()`` uses the vertex arrays from the ArrayMesh to "
"calculate two additional arrays, one for edges and one for faces, for a "
"total of three arrays."
msgstr ""
"``create_from_surface()`` ໃຊ້ vertex arrays ຈາກ ArrayMesh ເພື່ອຄິດໄລ່ອາເຣເພີ່ມເຕີມສອງ"
"ອັນ, ອັນໜຶ່ງສຳລັບຂອບ (edges) ແລະ ອີກອັນໜຶ່ງສຳລັບໜ້າ (faces), ລວມທັງໝົດເປັນສາມອາເຣ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/meshdatatool.rst:35
msgid ""
"An edge is a connection between any two vertices. Each edge in the edge "
"array contains a reference to the two vertices it is composed of, and up to "
"two faces that it is contained within."
msgstr ""
"ຂອບ (edge) ແມ່ນການເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ລະຫວ່າງສອງຈຸດຈອມ (vertices) ໃດໆ. ແຕ່ລະຂອບໃນ edge array ຈະມີ"
"ການອ້າງອີງເຖິງສອງຈຸດຈອມທີ່ປະກອບເປັນມັນ, ແລະ ໜ້າ (faces) ສູງສຸດສອງໜ້າທີ່ມັນຢູ່ພາຍໃນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/meshdatatool.rst:38
msgid ""
"A face is a triangle made up of three vertices and three corresponding "
"edges. Each face in the face array contains a reference to the three "
"vertices and three edges it is composed of."
msgstr ""
"ໜ້າ (face) ແມ່ນຮູບສາມແຈທີ່ປະກອບດ້ວຍສາມຈຸດຈອມ ແລະ ສາມຂອບທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງ. ແຕ່ລະໜ້າໃນ face array "
"ຈະມີການອ້າງອີງເຖິງສາມຈຸດຈອມ ແລະ ສາມຂອບທີ່ປະກອບເປັນມັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/meshdatatool.rst:41
msgid ""
"The vertex array contains edge, face, normal, color, tangent, uv, uv2, bone, "
"and weight information connected with each vertex."
msgstr ""
"ອາເຣຈຸດຈອມປະກອບມີຂໍ້ມູນ ຂອບ, ໜ້າ, ນໍມໍ, ສີ, ແທນເຈນ, uv, uv2, ກະດູກ, ແລະ ນ້ຳໜັກ ທີ່ເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ກັບແຕ່"
"ລະຈຸດຈອມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/meshdatatool.rst:44
msgid ""
"To access information from these arrays you use a function of the form "
"``get_****()``:"
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອເຂົ້າເຖິງຂໍ້ມູນຈາກອາເຣເຫຼົ່ານີ້ ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງໃຊ້ຟັງຊັນໃນຮູບແບບ ``get_****()``:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/meshdatatool.rst:61
msgid ""
"What you choose to do with these functions is up to you. A common use case "
"is to iterate over all vertices and transform them in some way:"
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງທີ່ເຈົ້າເລືອກເຮັດກັບຟັງຊັນເຫຼົ່ານີ້ແມ່ນຂຶ້ນກັບເຈົ້າ. ກໍລະນີການນຳໃຊ້ທົ່ວໄປແມ່ນ ການວົນລູບ (iterate) ຜ່ານຈຸດ"
"ຈອມທັງໝົດ ແລະ ປ່ຽນຮູບຮ່າງ (transform) ພວກມັນໃນບາງທາງ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/meshdatatool.rst:81
msgid ""
"These modifications are not done in place on the ArrayMesh. If you are "
"dynamically updating an existing ArrayMesh, first delete the existing "
"surface before adding a new one using :ref:`commit_to_surface() "
"<class_meshdatatool_method_commit_to_surface>`:"
msgstr ""
"ການດັດແກ້ເຫຼົ່ານີ້ບໍ່ໄດ້ເຮັດໂດຍກົງໃສ່ ArrayMesh. ຖ້າເຈົ້າກຳລັງອັບເດດ ArrayMesh ທີ່ມີຢູ່ ແບບໄດນາມິກ, ໃ"
"ຫ້ລຶບ surface ທີ່ມີຢູ່ກ່ອນ ແລ້ວຈຶ່ງເພີ່ມອັນໃຫມ່ໂດຍໃຊ້ :ref:`commit_to_surface() "
"<class_meshdatatool_method_commit_to_surface>`:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/meshdatatool.rst:95
msgid ""
"Below is a complete example that turns a spherical mesh called ``mesh`` into "
"a randomly deformed blob complete with updated normals and vertex colors. "
"See :ref:`ArrayMesh tutorial <doc_arraymesh>` for how to generate the base "
"mesh."
msgstr ""
"ຂ້າງລຸ່ມນີ້ແມ່ນຕົວຢ່າງທີ່ສົມບູນ ທີ່ປ່ຽນ spherical mesh ທີ່ຊື່ວ່າ ``mesh`` ໃຫ້ເປັນກ້ອນ (blob) ທີ່ບິດເບືອນ"
"ແບບສຸ່ມ ພ້ອມທັງອັບເດດ normals ແລະ vertex colors. ເບິ່ງ :ref:`ArrayMesh tutorial "
"<doc_arraymesh>` ສຳລັບວິທີການສ້າງ base mesh."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/surfacetool.rst:4
msgid "Using the SurfaceTool"
msgstr "ການນຳໃຊ້ SurfaceTool"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/surfacetool.rst:6
msgid ""
"The :ref:`SurfaceTool <class_surfacetool>` provides a useful interface for "
"constructing geometry. The interface is similar to the :ref:`ImmediateMesh "
"<class_ImmediateMesh>` class. You set each per-vertex attribute (e.g. "
"normal, uv, color) and then when you add a vertex it captures the attributes."
msgstr ""
":ref:`SurfaceTool <class_surfacetool>` ໃຫ້ອິນເຕີເຟສທີ່ມີປະໂຫຍດສຳລັບການສ້າງເລຂາຄະນິດ. ອິ"
"ນເຕີເຟສນີ້ຄ້າຍຄືກັບຄລາສ :ref:`ImmediateMesh <class_ImmediateMesh>`. ເຈົ້າກຳນົດ ຄຸນລັກສະນ"
"ະ (attribute) ຂອງແຕ່ລະຈຸດຈອມ (ເຊັ່ນ normal, uv, color) ແລະ ເມື່ອເຈົ້າເພີ່ມ ຈຸດຈອມ ມັນຈະເກັ"
"ບກຳຄຸນລັກສະນະເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນໄວ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/surfacetool.rst:11
msgid ""
"The SurfaceTool also provides some useful helper functions like ``index()`` "
"and ``generate_normals()``."
msgstr ""
"SurfaceTool ຍັງມີຟັງຊັນຕົວຊ່ວຍທີ່ມີປະໂຫຍດບາງຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ ``index()`` ແລະ ``generate_normals"
"()``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/surfacetool.rst:13
msgid "Attributes are added before each vertex is added:"
msgstr "ຄຸນລັກສະນະຕ່າງໆຈະຖືກເພີ່ມກ່ອນທີ່ຈະເພີ່ມແຕ່ລະຈຸດຈອມ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/surfacetool.rst:36
msgid ""
"When finished generating your geometry with the :ref:`SurfaceTool "
"<class_surfacetool>`, call ``commit()`` to finish generating the mesh. If "
"an :ref:`ArrayMesh <class_ArrayMesh>` is passed to ``commit()``, then it "
"appends a new surface to the end of the ArrayMesh. While if nothing is "
"passed in, ``commit()`` returns an ArrayMesh."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອສ້າງເລຂາຄະນິດດ້ວຍ :ref:`SurfaceTool <class_surfacetool>` ສຳເລັດແລ້ວ, ໃຫ້ເອີ້ນ "
"``commit()`` ເພື່ອສິ້ນສຸດການສ້າງ mesh. ຖ້າສົ່ງ :ref:`ArrayMesh <class_ArrayMesh>` ໃຫ້ກັ"
"ບ ``commit()``, ມັນຈະເພີ່ມ surface ໃຫມ່ຕໍ່ທ້າຍ ArrayMesh. ແຕ່ຖ້າບໍ່ໄດ້ສົ່ງຫຍັງເຂົ້າໄປ, "
"``commit()`` ຈະສົ່ງຄ່າກັບມາເປັນ ArrayMesh ໃຫມ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/surfacetool.rst:58
msgid "The code below creates a triangle without indices."
msgstr "ໂຄ້ດຂ້າງລຸ່ມນີ້ສ້າງຮູບສາມແຈໂດຍບໍ່ມີດັດຊະນີ (indices)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/surfacetool.rst:107
msgid ""
"You can optionally add an index array, either by calling ``add_index()`` and "
"adding vertices to the index array manually, or by calling ``index()`` once, "
"which generates the index array automatically and shrinks the vertex array "
"to remove duplicate vertices."
msgstr ""
"ເຈົ້າສາມາດເລືອກເພີ່ມ index array ໄດ້, ໂດຍການເອີ້ນ ``add_index()`` ແລະ ເພີ່ມຈຸດຈອມໃສ່ "
"index array ດ້ວຍຕົວເອງ, ຫຼື ເອີ້ນ ``index()`` ຄັ້ງດຽວ ເຊິ່ງຈະສ້າງ index array ໃຫ້ໂດຍ ອັດຕະ"
"ໂນມັດ ແລະ ຫຼຸດຂະໜາດ vertex array ເພື່ອລຶບຈຸດຈອມທີ່ຊ້ຳກັນອອກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/surfacetool.rst:175
msgid ""
"Similarly, if you have an index array, but you want each vertex to be unique "
"(e.g. because you want to use unique normals or colors per face instead of "
"per-vertex), you can call ``deindex()``."
msgstr ""
"ໃນທຳນອງດຽວກັນ, ຖ້າເຈົ້າມີ index array ແຕ່ຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ແຕ່ລະຈຸດຈອມມີຄວາມເປັນເອກະລັກ (ເຊັ່ນ: ເພາະ"
"ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການໃຊ້ normal ຫຼື ສີ ທີ່ແຍກກັນແຕ່ລະໜ້າ ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນແຕ່ລະຈຸດຈອມ), ເຈົ້າສາມາດເອີ້ນ "
"``deindex()``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/surfacetool.rst:187
msgid ""
"If you don't add custom normals yourself, you can add them using "
"``generate_normals()``, which should be called after generating geometry and "
"before committing the mesh using ``commit()`` or ``commit_to_arrays()``. "
"Calling ``generate_normals(true)`` will flip the resulting normals. As a "
"side note, ``generate_normals()`` only works if the primitive type is set to "
"``Mesh.PRIMITIVE_TRIANGLES``."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເຈົ້າບໍ່ໄດ້ເພີ່ມ normal ດ້ວຍຕົວເອງ, ເຈົ້າສາມາດເພີ່ມພວກມັນໄດ້ໂດຍໃຊ້ ``generate_normals()``, "
"ເຊິ່ງຄວນເອີ້ນຫຼັງຈາກສ້າງເລຂາຄະນິດ ແລະ ກ່ອນທີ່ຈະຢືນຢັນ mesh ດ້ວຍ ``commit()`` ຫຼື "
"``commit_to_arrays()``. ການເອີ້ນ ``generate_normals(true)`` ຈະກັບດ້ານ normals ທີ່ໄ"
"ດ້. ໝາຍເຫດ, ``generate_normals()`` ຈະເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ກໍຕໍ່ເມື່ອ primitive type ຖືກກຳນົດ ເປັນ "
"``Mesh.PRIMITIVE_TRIANGLES``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/surfacetool.rst:192
msgid ""
"You may notice that normal mapping or other material properties look broken "
"on the generated mesh. This is because normal mapping **requires** the mesh "
"to feature *tangents*, which are separate from *normals*. You can either add "
"custom tangents manually, or generate them automatically with "
"``generate_tangents()``. This method requires that each vertex have UVs and "
"normals set already."
msgstr ""
"ເຈົ້າອາດຈະສັງເກດເຫັນວ່າ normal mapping ຫຼື ຄຸນສົມບັດວັດສະດຸອື່ນໆເບິ່ງຄືວ່າເພ ເທິງ mesh ທີ່ສ້າງຂຶ້ນ. ນີ້"
"ແມ່ນຍ້ອນວ່າ normal mapping **ຕ້ອງການ** ໃຫ້ mesh ມີ *tangents*, ເຊິ່ງແຍກອອກຈາກ "
"*normals*. ເຈົ້າສາມາດເພີ່ມ tangents ດ້ວຍຕົວເອງ ຫຼື ສ້າງພວກມັນ ໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດດ້ວຍ "
"``generate_tangents()``. ວິທີນີ້ຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ແຕ່ລະຈຸດຈອມມີ UVs ແລະ normals ກຳນົດໄວ້ແລ້ວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/surfacetool.rst:212
msgid ""
"By default, when generating normals, they will be calculated on a per-vertex "
"basis (i.e. they will be \"smooth normals\"). If you want flat vertex "
"normals (i.e. a single normal vector per face), when adding vertices, call "
"``add_smooth_group(i)`` where ``i`` is a unique number per vertex. "
"``add_smooth_group()`` needs to be called while building the geometry, e.g. "
"before the call to ``add_vertex()``."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ເມື່ອສ້າງ normals, ພວກມັນຈະຖືກຄິດໄລ່ຕາມແຕ່ລະຈຸດຈອມ (ນັ້ນຄື \"smooth normals\")"
". ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການ flat vertex normals (ນັ້ນຄື vector normal ດຽວຕໍ່ໜ້າ), ເມື່ອເພີ່ມ ຈຸດຈອມ, ໃ"
"ຫ້ເອີ້ນ ``add_smooth_group(i)`` ໂດຍທີ່ ``i`` ແມ່ນຕົວເລກສະເພາະຕໍ່ຈຸດຈອມ. "
"``add_smooth_group()`` ຕ້ອງຖືກເອີ້ນໃນຂະນະທີ່ກຳລັງສ້າງເລຂາຄະນິດ, ເຊັ່ນ: ກ່ອນການເອີ້ນ "
"``add_vertex()``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/immediatemesh.rst:4
msgid "Using ImmediateMesh"
msgstr "ການນຳໃຊ້ ImmediateMesh"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/immediatemesh.rst:6
msgid ""
"The :ref:`ImmediateMesh <class_ImmediateMesh>` is a convenient tool to "
"create dynamic geometry using an OpenGL 1.x-style API. Which makes it both "
"approachable to use and efficient for meshes which need to be updated every "
"frame."
msgstr ""
":ref:`ImmediateMesh <class_ImmediateMesh>` ແມ່ນເຄື່ອງມືທີ່ສະດວກໃນການສ້າງເລຂາຄະນິດ ແບບ"
"ໄດນາມິກໂດຍໃຊ້ API ແບບ OpenGL 1.x. ເຊິ່ງເຮັດໃຫ້ມັນເຂົ້າເຖິງໄດ້ງ່າຍ ແລະ ມີປະສິດທິພາບ ສຳລັບ "
"meshes ທີ່ຕ້ອງມີການອັບເດດໃນທຸກໆເຟຣມ (frame)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/immediatemesh.rst:10
msgid ""
"Generating complex geometry (several thousand vertices) with this tool is "
"inefficient, even if it's done only once. Instead, it is designed to "
"generate simple geometry that changes every frame."
msgstr ""
"ການສ້າງເລຂາຄະນິດທີ່ຊັບຊ້ອນ (ຫຼາຍພັນຈຸດຈອມ) ດ້ວຍເຄື່ອງມືນີ້ແມ່ນບໍ່ມີປະສິດທິພາບ, ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າ ຈະເຮັດພຽງຄັ້ງ"
"ດຽວກໍຕາມ. ແຕ່ມັນຖືກອອກແບບມາເພື່ອສ້າງເລຂາຄະນິດແບບງ່າຍໆ ທີ່ປ່ຽນແປງໃນທຸກໆເຟຣມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/immediatemesh.rst:13
msgid ""
"First, you need to create a :ref:`MeshInstance3D <class_meshinstance3d>` and "
"add an :ref:`ImmediateMesh <class_ImmediateMesh>` to it in the Inspector."
msgstr ""
"ທຳອິດ, ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງສ້າງ :ref:`MeshInstance3D <class_meshinstance3d>` ແລະ ເພີ່ມ "
":ref:`ImmediateMesh <class_ImmediateMesh>` ໃສ່ໃນ Inspector."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/immediatemesh.rst:16
msgid ""
"Next, add a script to the MeshInstance3D. The code for the ImmediateMesh "
"should go in the ``_process()`` function if you want it to update each "
"frame, or in the ``_ready()`` function if you want to create the mesh once "
"and not update it. If you only generate a surface once, the ImmediateMesh is "
"just as efficient as any other kind of mesh as the generated mesh is cached "
"and reused."
msgstr ""
"ຕໍ່ໄປ, ເພີ່ມສະຄຣິບໃສ່ MeshInstance3D. ໂຄ້ດສຳລັບ ImmediateMesh ຄວນຢູ່ໃນຟັງຊັນ ``_process()"
"`` ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ມັນອັບເດດແຕ່ລະເຟຣມ, ຫຼື ຢູ່ໃນຟັງຊັນ ``_ready()`` ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການສ້າງ mesh ພ"
"ຽງຄັ້ງດຽວ ແລະ ບໍ່ມີການອັບເດດ. ຖ້າເຈົ້າສ້າງ surface ພຽງຄັ້ງດຽວ, ImmediateMesh ຈະມີປະສິດທິພາບ "
"ຄືກັບ mesh ປະເພດອື່ນໆ ເພາະ mesh ທີ່ສ້າງຂຶ້ນຈະຖືກເກັບໄວ້ໃນ cache ແລະ ນຳມາໃຊ້ໃໝ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/immediatemesh.rst:22
msgid ""
"To begin generating geometry you must call ``surface_begin()``. "
"``surface_begin()`` takes a ``PrimitiveType`` as an argument. "
"``PrimitiveType`` instructs the GPU how to arrange the primitive based on "
"the vertices given whether it is triangles, lines, points, etc. A complete "
"list can be found under the :ref:`Mesh <class_mesh>` class reference page."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອເລີ່ມຕົ້ນການສ້າງເລຂາຄະນິດ ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງເອີ້ນ ``surface_begin()``. ``surface_begin()`` ຮັບຄ່"
"າ ``PrimitiveType`` ເປັນພາຣາມິເຕີ. ``PrimitiveType`` ຈະບອກ GPU ວ່າຈະຈັດວາງ "
"primitive ແນວໃດໂດຍອີງໃສ່ຈຸດຈອມທີ່ໃຫ້ມາ ບໍ່ວ່າຈະເປັນຮູບສາມແຈ, ເສັ້ນ, ຈຸດ, ແລະ ອື່ນໆ. ລາຍຊື່ທັງໝົດສ"
"າມາດເບິ່ງໄດ້ໃນໜ້າອ້າງອີງຄລາສ :ref:`Mesh <class_mesh>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/immediatemesh.rst:28
msgid ""
"Once you have called ``surface_begin()`` you are ready to start adding "
"vertices. You add vertices one at a time. First you add vertex specific "
"attributes such as normals or UVs using ``surface_set_****()`` (e.g. "
"``surface_set_normal()``). Then you call ``surface_add_vertex()`` to add a "
"vertex with those attributes. For example:"
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອເຈົ້າເອີ້ນ ``surface_begin()`` ແລ້ວ ເຈົ້າກໍພ້ອມທີ່ຈະເລີ່ມເພີ່ມຈຸດຈອມ. ເຈົ້າເພີ່ມຈຸດຈອມ ເທື່ອລະອັ"
"ນ. ທຳອິດ ເຈົ້າເພີ່ມຄຸນລັກສະນະສະເພາະຂອງຈຸດຈອມ ເຊັ່ນ normals ຫຼື UVs ໂດຍໃຊ້ "
"``surface_set_****()`` (ເຊັ່ນ ``surface_set_normal()``). ຈາກນັ້ນ ເຈົ້າເອີ້ນ "
"``surface_add_vertex()`` ເພື່ອເພີ່ມຈຸດຈອມພ້ອມກັບຄຸນລັກສະນະເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນ. ຕົວຢ່າງ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/immediatemesh.rst:42
msgid ""
"Only attributes added before the call to ``surface_add_vertex()`` will be "
"included in that vertex. If you add an attribute twice before calling "
"``surface_add_vertex()``, only the second call will be used."
msgstr ""
"ສະເພາະຄຸນລັກສະນະທີ່ເພີ່ມກ່ອນການເອີ້ນ ``surface_add_vertex()`` ເທົ່ານັ້ນທີ່ຈະຖືກລວມເຂົ້າ ໃນຈຸດຈອມ"
"ນັ້ນ. ຖ້າເຈົ້າເພີ່ມຄຸນລັກສະນະສອງຄັ້ງກ່ອນທີ່ຈະເອີ້ນ ``surface_add_vertex()``, ຈະມີພຽງການເອີ້ນຄັ້ງທີສ"
"ອງເທົ່ານັ້ນທີ່ຖືກນຳໃຊ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/immediatemesh.rst:46
msgid ""
"Finally, once you have added all your vertices call ``surface_end()`` to "
"signal that you have finished generating the surface. You can call "
"``surface_begin()`` and ``surface_end()`` multiple times to generate "
"multiple surfaces for the mesh."
msgstr ""
"ໃນທີ່ສຸດ, ເມື່ອເຈົ້າເພີ່ມຈຸດຈອມທັງໝົດແລ້ວ ໃຫ້ເອີ້ນ ``surface_end()`` ເພື່ອສົ່ງສັນຍານວ່າ ເຈົ້າໄດ້ສ້າງ "
"surface ສຳເລັດແລ້ວ. ເຈົ້າສາມາດເອີ້ນ ``surface_begin()`` ແລະ ``surface_end()`` ຫຼາຍຄັ້ງ"
"ເພື່ອສ້າງຫຼາຍ surfaces ໃຫ້ກັບ mesh ດຽວກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/immediatemesh.rst:50
msgid ""
"The example code below draws a single triangle in the ``_ready()`` function."
msgstr "ຕົວຢ່າງໂຄ້ດຂ້າງລຸ່ມນີ້ແຕ້ມຮູບສາມແຈອັນດຽວໃນຟັງຊັນ ``_ready()``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/immediatemesh.rst:78
msgid ""
"The ImmediateMesh can also be used across frames. Each time you call "
"``surface_begin()`` and ``surface_end()``, you are adding a new surface to "
"the ImmediateMesh. If you want to recreate the mesh from scratch each frame, "
"call ``clear_surfaces()`` before calling ``surface_begin()``."
msgstr ""
"ImmediateMesh ຍັງສາມາດຖືກໃຊ້ຂ້າມເຟຣມໄດ້. ທຸກໆຄັ້ງທີ່ເຈົ້າເອີ້ນ ``surface_begin()`` ແລະ "
"``surface_end()``, ເຈົ້າກຳລັງເພີ່ມ surface ໃຫມ່ໃຫ້ກັບ ImmediateMesh. ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການ ສ້າງ "
"mesh ໃຫມ່ທັງໝົດໃນແຕ່ລະເຟຣມ, ໃຫ້ເອີ້ນ ``clear_surfaces()`` ກ່ອນທີ່ຈະເອີ້ນ ``surface_begin"
"()``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/procedural_geometry/immediatemesh.rst:101
msgid ""
"The above code will dynamically create and draw a single surface each frame."
msgstr "ໂຄ້ດຂ້າງເທິງຈະສ້າງ ແລະ ແຕ້ມ surface ອັນດຽວແບບໄດນາມິກໃນແຕ່ລະເຟຣມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:4
msgid "3D text"
msgstr "ຂໍ້ຄວາມ 3D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:9
msgid ""
"In a project, there may be times when text needs to be created as part of a "
"3D scene and not just in the HUD. Godot provides 2 methods to do this: the "
"Label3D node and the TextMesh *resource* for a MeshInstance3D node."
msgstr ""
"ໃນໂປຣເຈັກ, ອາດຈະມີບາງຄັ້ງທີ່ຂໍ້ຄວາມຕ້ອງຖືກສ້າງຂຶ້ນເປັນສ່ວນໜຶ່ງຂອງສາກ 3D ແລະ ບໍ່ແມ່ນພຽງແຕ່ ໃນ HUD. "
"Godot ມີ 2 ວິທີໃນການເຮັດສິ່ງນີ້: ໂນດ Label3D ແລະ TextMesh *ຣີຊອດ (resource)* ສຳລັບໂນດ "
"MeshInstance3D."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:13
msgid ""
"Additionally, Godot makes it possible to position Control nodes according to "
"a 3D point's position on the camera. This can be used as an alternative to "
"\"true\" 3D text in situations where Label3D and TextMesh aren't flexible "
"enough."
msgstr ""
"ນອກຈາກນັ້ນ, Godot ຍັງຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສາມາດວາງຕຳແໜ່ງໂນດ Control ຕາມຕຳແໜ່ງຂອງຈຸດ 3D ເທິງກ້ອງໄດ້. ສິ່ງ"
"ນີ້ສາມາດໃຊ້ເປັນທາງເລືອກແທນຂໍ້ຄວາມ 3D \"ແທ້\" ໃນສະຖານະການທີ່ Label3D ແລະ TextMesh ບໍ່ມີຄວາມ"
"ຢືດຢຸ່ນພໍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:19
msgid ""
"You can see 3D text in action using the `3D Labels and Texts demo project "
"<https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/3d/"
"labels_and_texts>`__."
msgstr ""
"ເຈົ້າສາມາດເບິ່ງການເຮັດວຽກຂອງຂໍ້ຄວາມ 3D ໄດ້ໂດຍໃຊ້ `3D Labels and Texts demo project "
"<https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/3d/"
"labels_and_texts>`__."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:22
msgid ""
"This page does **not** cover how to display a GUI scene within a 3D "
"environment. For information on how to achieve that, see the `GUI in 3D "
"<https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/viewport/"
"gui_in_3d>`__ demo project."
msgstr ""
"ໜ້ານີ້ **ບໍ່ໄດ້** ກວມເອົາວິທີການສະແດງສາກ GUI ພາຍໃນສະພາບແວດລ້ອມ 3D. ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນ ກ່ຽວກັບວິທີການເຮັ"
"ດສິ່ງນັ້ນ, ໃຫ້ເບິ່ງໂປຣເຈັກຕົວຢ່າງ `GUI in 3D <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-"
"demo-projects/tree/master/viewport/gui_in_3d>`__."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:28
msgid "Label3D"
msgstr "Label3D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:32
msgid ""
"Label3D behaves like a Label node, but in 3D space. Unlike the Label node, "
"this Label3D node does **not** inherit properties of a GUI theme. However, "
"its look remains customizable and uses the same font subresource as Control "
"nodes (including support for :abbr:`MSDF (Multi-channel Signed Distance "
"Font)` font rendering)."
msgstr ""
"Label3D ເຮັດວຽກຄືກັບໂນດ Label, ແຕ່ຢູ່ໃນພື້ນທີ່ 3D. ບໍ່ຄືກັບໂນດ Label, ໂນດ Label3D ນີ້ **ບໍ່ໄ"
"ດ້** ສືບທອດຄຸນສົມບັດຂອງ GUI theme. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ຮູບລັກສະນະຂອງມັນຍັງສາມາດປັບແຕ່ງໄດ້ ແລະ ໃຊ້ "
"font subresource ດຽວກັນກັບໂນດ Control (ລວມທັງການຮອງຮັບການສະແດງຜົນຟອນ :abbr:`MSDF "
"(Multi-channel Signed Distance Font)`)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:39
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:97
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:136
#: ../../docs/tutorials/i18n/localization_using_gettext.rst:19
msgid "Advantages"
msgstr "ຂໍ້ດີ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:41
msgid ""
"Label3D is faster to generate than TextMesh. While both use a caching "
"mechanism to only render new glyphs once, Label3D will still be faster to "
"(re)generate, especially for long text. This can avoid stuttering during "
"gameplay on low-end CPUs or mobile."
msgstr ""
"Label3D ສາມາດສ້າງໄດ້ໄວກວ່າ TextMesh. ເຖິງວ່າທັງສອງຈະໃຊ້ກົນໄກການເຮັດ cache ເພື່ອສະແດງຜົນ ຕົ"
"ວອັກສອນໃຫມ່ພຽງຄັ້ງດຽວ, ແຕ່ Label3D ກໍຍັງໄວກວ່າໃນການສ້າງ (ຫຼື ສ້າງໃຫມ່), ໂດຍສະເພາະ ຂໍ້ຄວາມທີ່ຍາ"
"ວ. ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດຊ່ວຍຫຼີກລ່ຽງການກະຕຸກໃນລະຫວ່າງການຫຼິ້ນເກມເທິງ CPU ລະດັບຕ່ຳ ຫຼື ມືຖື."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:45
msgid ""
"Label3D can use bitmap fonts and dynamic fonts (with and without :abbr:`MSDF "
"(Multi-channel Signed Distance Font)` or mipmaps). This makes it more "
"flexible on that aspect compared to TextMesh, especially for rendering fonts "
"with self-intersecting outlines or colored fonts (emoji)."
msgstr ""
"Label3D ສາມາດໃຊ້ bitmap fonts ແລະ dynamic fonts (ທັງແບບມີ ແລະ ບໍ່ມີ :abbr:`MSDF "
"(Multi-channel Signed Distance Font)` ຫຼື mipmaps). ສິ່ງນີ້ເຮັດໃຫ້ມັນມີຄວາມຢືດຢຸ່ນກວ່າ ເມື່ອທ"
"ຽບກັບ TextMesh, ໂດຍສະເພາະສຳລັບການສະແດງຜົນຟອນທີ່ມີເສັ້ນຂອບຕັດກັນ ຫຼື ຟອນທີ່ມີສີ (emoji)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:52
msgid ""
"See :ref:`doc_gui_using_fonts` for guidelines on configuring font imports."
msgstr "ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_gui_using_fonts` ສຳລັບຄຳແນະນຳໃນການຕັ້ງຄ່າການນຳເຂົ້າຟອນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:57
msgid ""
"By default, Label3D has limited interaction with a 3D environment. It can be "
"occluded by geometry and lit by light sources if the **Shaded** flag is "
"enabled. However, it will not cast shadows even if **Cast Shadow** is set to "
"**On** in the Label3D's GeometryInstance3D properties. This is because the "
"node internally generates a quad mesh (one glyph per quad) with transparent "
"textures and has the same limitations as Sprite3D. Transparency sorting "
"issues can also become apparent when several Label3Ds overlap, especially if "
"they have outlines."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, Label3D ມີການໂຕ້ຕອບກັບສະພາບແວດລ້ອມ 3D ຢ່າງຈຳກັດ. ມັນສາມາດຖືກບັງ (occluded) ໂ"
"ດຍເລຂາຄະນິດ ແລະ ໄດ້ຮັບແສງຈາກແຫຼ່ງກຳເນີດແສງໄດ້ຖ້າເປີດໃຊ້ **Shaded**. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ມັນຈະ ບໍ່ເກີ"
"ດເງົາ ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຈະຕັ້ງ **Cast Shadow** ເປັນ **On** ໃນຄຸນສົມບັດ GeometryInstance3D ຂອງ "
"Label3D. ນີ້ແມ່ນຍ້ອນວ່າພາຍໃນໂນດຈະສ້າງ quad mesh (ໜຶ່ງຕົວອັກສອນຕໍ່ໜຶ່ງ quad) ດ້ວຍ "
"transparent textures ແລະ ມີຂໍ້ຈຳກັດຄືກັນກັບ Sprite3D. ບັນຫາການຈັດລຽງຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ "
"(Transparency sorting) ຍັງສາມາດ ເຫັນໄດ້ຊັດເຈນເມື່ອມີ Label3D ຫຼາຍອັນຊ້ອນທັບກັນ, ໂດຍສະເພາະ"
"ຖ້າມີເສັ້ນຂອບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:65
msgid ""
"This can be mitigated by setting the Label3D's transparency mode to **Alpha "
"Cut**, at the cost of less smooth text rendering. The **Opaque Pre-Pass** "
"transparency mode can preserve text smoothness while allowing the Label3D to "
"cast shadows, but some transparency sorting issues will remain."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດຫຼຸດຜ່ອນໄດ້ໂດຍການຕັ້ງໂໝດຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສຂອງ Label3D ເປັນ **Alpha Cut**, ແຕ່ຈະຕ້ອງແລກກັ"
"ບ ການສະແດງຜົນຂໍ້ຄວາມທີ່ລຽບນຽນໜ້ອຍລົງ. ໂໝດຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ **Opaque Pre-Pass** ສາມາດຮັກສາ ຄວາ"
"ມລຽບນຽນຂອງຂໍ້ຄວາມໃນຂະນະທີ່ຍັງຍອມໃຫ້ Label3D ເກີດເງົາໄດ້, ແຕ່ບັນຫາການຈັດລຽງຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ ບາງຢ່າ"
"ງຈະຍັງຄົງຢູ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:70
msgid ""
"See :ref:`Transparency sorting "
"<doc_3d_rendering_limitations_transparency_sorting>` section in the 3D "
"rendering limitations page for more information."
msgstr ""
"ເບິ່ງພາກສ່ວນ :ref:`Transparency sorting "
"<doc_3d_rendering_limitations_transparency_sorting>` ໃນໜ້າຂໍ້ຈຳກັດການສະແດງຜົນ 3D ສ"
"ຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:73
msgid ""
"Text rendering quality can also suffer when the Label3D is viewed at a "
"distance. To improve text rendering quality, :ref:`enable mipmaps on the "
"font <doc_using_fonts_mipmaps>` or :ref:`switch the font to use MSDF "
"rendering <doc_using_fonts_msdf>`."
msgstr ""
"ຄຸນນະພາບການສະແດງຜົນຂໍ້ຄວາມອາດຈະຫຼຸດລົງເມື່ອເບິ່ງ Label3D ຈາກໄລຍະໄກ. ເພື່ອປັບປຸງຄຸນນະພາບ ການສະ"
"ແດງຜົນຂໍ້ຄວາມ, :ref:`ເປີດໃຊ້ mipmaps ເທິງຟອນ <doc_using_fonts_mipmaps>` ຫຼື :ref:`ປ່ຽນ"
"ຟອນໄປໃຊ້ການສະແດງຜົນແບບ MSDF <doc_using_fonts_msdf>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:78
msgid "TextMesh"
msgstr "TextMesh"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:82
msgid ""
"The TextMesh resource has similarities to Label3D. They both display text in "
"a 3D scene, and will use the same font subresource. However, instead of "
"generating transparent quads, TextMesh generates 3D geometry that represents "
"the glyphs' contours and has the properties of a mesh. As a result, a "
"TextMesh is shaded by default and automatically casts shadows onto the "
"environment. A TextMesh can also have a material applied to it (including "
"custom shaders)."
msgstr ""
"ຣີຊອດ TextMesh ມີຄວາມຄ້າຍຄືກັບ Label3D. ທັງສອງສະແດງຂໍ້ຄວາມໃນສາກ 3D, ແລະ ຈະໃຊ້ font "
"subresource ດຽວກັນ. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ແທນທີ່ຈະສ້າງ quads ທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສ, TextMesh ຈະສ້າງເລຂາຄະນິດ "
"3D ທີ່ເປັນຕົວແທນຂອງຂອບຕົວອັກສອນ ແລະ ມີຄຸນສົມບັດຂອງ mesh. ຜົນກໍຄື, TextMesh ຈະຖືກ shaded ໂດຍ"
"ເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ ແລະ ເກີດເງົາໃສ່ສະພາບແວດລ້ອມໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ. TextMesh ຍັງສາມາດໃສ່ material ໄດ້ (ລວມ"
"ທັງ custom shaders)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:89
msgid ""
"Here is an example of a texture and how it's applied to the mesh. You can "
"use the texture below as a reference for the generated mesh's UV map:"
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ແມ່ນຕົວຢ່າງຂອງ texture ແລະ ວິທີການທີ່ມັນຖືກນຳໃຊ້ກັບ mesh. ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ texture ຂ້າງລຸ່ມນີ້ເປັນບ່"
"ອນອ້າງອີງສຳລັບ UV map ຂອງ mesh ທີ່ສ້າງຂຶ້ນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:99
msgid "TextMesh has a few advantages over Label3D:"
msgstr "TextMesh ມີຂໍ້ດີບາງຢ່າງຫຼາຍກວ່າ Label3D:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:101
msgid "TextMesh can use a texture to modify text color on a per-side basis."
msgstr "TextMesh ສາມາດໃຊ້ texture ເພື່ອປ່ຽນສີຂໍ້ຄວາມໃນແຕ່ລະດ້ານໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:102
msgid "TextMesh geometry can have actual depth to it, giving glyphs a 3D look."
msgstr ""
"ເລຂາຄະນິດຂອງ TextMesh ສາມາດມີຄວາມເລິກແທ້ໆ, ເຮັດໃຫ້ຕົວອັກສອນເບິ່ງເປັນ 3D."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:103
msgid "TextMesh can use custom shaders, unlike Label3D."
msgstr "TextMesh ສາມາດໃຊ້ custom shaders ໄດ້, ເຊິ່ງ Label3D ເຮັດບໍ່ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:108
msgid "There are some limitations to TextMesh:"
msgstr "ມີຂໍ້ຈຳກັດບາງຢ່າງສຳລັບ TextMesh:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:110
msgid ""
"No built-in outline support, unlike Label3D. This can be simulated using "
"custom shaders though."
msgstr ""
"ບໍ່ມີການຮອງຮັບເສັ້ນຂອບໃນຕົວ, ບໍ່ຄືກັບ Label3D. ແຕ່ສາມາດຈຳລອງໄດ້ໂດຍໃຊ້ custom shaders."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:112
msgid ""
"Only dynamic fonts are supported (``.ttf``, ``.otf``, ``.woff``, "
"``.woff2``). Bitmap fonts in the ``.fnt`` or ``.font`` formats are **not** "
"supported."
msgstr ""
"ຮອງຮັບສະເພາະ dynamic fonts ເທົ່ານັ້ນ (``.ttf``, ``.otf``, ``.woff``, ``.woff2``). "
"ຟອນແບບ Bitmap ໃນຮູບແບບ ``.fnt`` ຫຼື ``.font`` ແມ່ນ **ບໍ່** ຮອງຮັບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:114
msgid ""
"Fonts with self-intersecting outlines will not render correctly. If you "
"notice rendering issues on fonts downloaded from websites such as Google "
"Fonts, try downloading the font from the font author's official website "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"ຟອນທີ່ມີເສັ້ນຂອບຕັດກັນເອງຈະສະແດງຜົນບໍ່ຖືກຕ້ອງ. ຖ້າເຈົ້າພົບຫາບັນຫາການສະແດງຜົນໃນຟອນທີ່ດາວໂຫລດ ຈາກເວັ"
"ບໄຊເຊັ່ນ Google Fonts, ໃຫ້ລອງດາວໂຫລດຟອນຈາກເວັບໄຊທາງການຂອງຜູ້ສ້າງຟອນແທນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:118
msgid ""
"Antialiasing the text rendering requires a full-scene antialiasing method to "
"be enabled such as MSAA, FXAA and temporal antialiasing (TAA). If no "
"antialiasing method is enabled, text will appear grainy, especially at a "
"distance. See :ref:`doc_3d_antialiasing` for more information."
msgstr ""
"ການລົບຮອຍຢັກ (Antialiasing) ຂອງການສະແດງຜົນຂໍ້ຄວາມຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ເປີດໃຊ້ວິທີການລົບຮອຍຢັກ ແບບທັງສາ"
"ກ ເຊັ່ນ MSAA, FXAA ແລະ TAA. ຖ້າບໍ່ມີການເປີດໃຊ້ວິທີການລົບຮອຍຢັກ, ຂໍ້ຄວາມຈະເບິ່ງຄື ເປັນເມັດໆ, ໂດຍສ"
"ະເພາະໃນໄລຍະໄກ. ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_3d_antialiasing` ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:124
msgid "Projected Label node (or any other Control)"
msgstr "ໂນດ Label ທີ່ຖືກສາຍພາບ (ຫຼື Control ອື່ນໆ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:126
msgid ""
"There is a last solution that is more complex to set up, but provides the "
"most flexibility: projecting a 2D node onto 3D space. This can be achieved "
"using the return value "
"of :ref:`unproject_position<class_Camera3D_method_unproject_position>` "
"method on a Camera3D node in a script's ``_process()`` function. This return "
"value should then be used to set the ``position`` property of a Control node."
msgstr ""
"ມີທາງອອກສຸດທ້າຍທີ່ການຕັ້ງຄ່າຊັບຊ້ອນກວ່າ, ແຕ່ໃຫ້ຄວາມຢືດຢຸ່ນສູງສຸດ: ຄືການສາຍພາບ (projecting) ໂນດ "
"2D ລົງໃນພື້ນທີ່ 3D. ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ໂດຍການໃຊ້ຄ່າທີ່ສົ່ງກັບມາຈາກເມທອດ "
":ref:`unproject_position<class_Camera3D_method_unproject_position>` ເທິງໂນດ "
"Camera3D ໃນຟັງຊັນ ``_process()`` ຂອງສະຄຣິບ. ຈາກນັ້ນຄວນໃຊ້ຄ່ານີ້ເພື່ອຕັ້ງຄ່າຄຸນສົມບັດ "
"``position`` ຂອງໂນດ Control."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:132
msgid ""
"See the `3D waypoints <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/"
"tree/master/3d/waypoints>`__ demo for an example of this."
msgstr ""
"ເບິ່ງຕົວຢ່າງເລື່ອງນີ້ໄດ້ທີ່ເດໂມ `3D waypoints <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-"
"demo-projects/tree/master/3d/waypoints>`__."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:138
msgid ""
"Any Control node can be used, including Label, RichTextLabel or even nodes "
"such as Button. This allows for powerful formatting and GUI interaction."
msgstr ""
"ສາມາດໃຊ້ໂນດ Control ໃດກໍໄດ້, ລວມທັງ Label, RichTextLabel ຫຼື ແມ່ນແຕ່ໂນດເຊັ່ນ Button. ສິ່ງ"
"ນີ້ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ມີການຈັດຮູບແບບທີ່ມີປະສິດທິພາບ ແລະ ການໂຕ້ຕອບກັບ GUI ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:140
msgid ""
"The script-based approach allows for complete freedom in positioning. For "
"example, this makes it considerably easier to pin Controls to the screen's "
"edges when they go off-screen (for in-game 3D markers)."
msgstr ""
"ວິທີການທີ່ໃຊ້ສະຄຣິບຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ມີອິດສະຫຼະໃນການວາງຕຳແໜ່ງຢ່າງສົມບູນ. ຕົວຢ່າງ, ສິ່ງນີ້ເຮັດໃຫ້ ການປັກໝຸດ "
"Controls ໄວ້ທີ່ຂອບຂອງໜ້າຈໍເມື່ອພວກມັນອອກນອກໜ້າຈໍເຮັດໄດ້ງ່າຍຂຶ້ນຫຼາຍ (ສຳລັບຕົວໝາຍ 3D ໃນເກມ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:143
msgid ""
"Control theming is obeyed. This allows for easier customization that "
"globally applies to the project."
msgstr ""
"ປະຕິບັດຕາມ Control theming. ສິ່ງນີ້ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ການປັບແຕ່ງທີ່ໃຊ້ກັບທັງໂປຣເຈັກເຮັດໄດ້ງ່າຍຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:149
msgid ""
"Projected Controls cannot be occluded by 3D geometry in any way. You can use "
"a RayCast to fully hide the control if its target position is occluded by a "
"collider, but this doesn't allow for partially hiding the control behind a "
"wall."
msgstr ""
"Projected Controls ບໍ່ສາມາດຖືກບັງໂດຍເລຂາຄະນິດ 3D ໄດ້ໃນທາງໃດເລີຍ. ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ RayCast "
"ເພື່ອເຊື່ອງຄອນໂທຣລທັງໝົດໄດ້ຖ້າຕຳແໜ່ງເປົ້າໝາຍຖືກບັງໂດຍ collider, ແຕ່ສິ່ງນີ້ບໍ່ສາມາດ ເຊື່ອງຄອນໂທຣລບາງ"
"ສ່ວນໄວ້ທາງຫຼັງຝາໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:153
msgid ""
"Changing text size depending on distance by adjusting the Control's "
"``scale`` property is possible, but it needs to be done manually. Label3D "
"and TextMesh automatically take care of this, at the cost of less "
"flexibility (can't set a minimum/maximum text size in pixels)."
msgstr ""
"ການປ່ຽນຂະໜາດຂໍ້ຄວາມຕາມໄລຍະຫ່າງໂດຍການປັບຄຸນສົມບັດ ``scale`` ຂອງ Control ສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້, ແຕ່"
"ຕ້ອງເຮັດດ້ວຍຕົວເອງ. Label3D ແລະ TextMesh ຈະຈັດການເລື່ອງນີ້ໃຫ້ໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ, ແຕ່ຈະມີຄວາມຢືດຢຸ່ນ"
"ໜ້ອຍກວ່າ (ບໍ່ສາມາດກຳນົດຂະໜາດຂໍ້ຄວາມຕ່ຳສຸດ/ສູງສຸດເປັນພິກເຊວໄດ້)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:157
msgid ""
"Handling resolution and aspect ratio changes must be taken into account in "
"the script, which can be challenging."
msgstr ""
"ການຈັດການກັບການປ່ຽນແປງຄວາມລະອຽດ ແລະ ອັດຕາສ່ວນພາບ (aspect ratio) ຕ້ອງໄດ້ຖືກພິຈາລະນາ ໃນສ"
"ະຄຣິບ, ເຊິ່ງອາດຈະເປັນເລື່ອງທີ່ທ້າທາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:161
msgid "Should I use Label3D, TextMesh or a projected Control?"
msgstr "ຂ້ອຍຄວນໃຊ້ Label3D, TextMesh ຫຼື projected Control?"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:163
msgid ""
"In most scenarios, Label3D is recommended as it's easier to set up and "
"provides higher rendering quality (especially if 3D antialiasing is "
"disabled)."
msgstr ""
"ໃນສະຖານະການສ່ວນໃຫຍ່, ແນະນຳໃຫ້ໃຊ້ Label3D ເພາະມັນຕັ້ງຄ່າງ່າຍກວ່າ ແລະ ໃຫ້ຄຸນນະພາບ ການສະແດງຜົ"
"ນທີ່ສູງກວ່າ (ໂດຍສະເພາະຖ້າປິດການລົບຮອຍຢັກ 3D)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:166
msgid ""
"For advanced use cases, TextMesh is more flexible as it allows styling the "
"text with custom shaders. Custom shaders allow for modifying the final "
"geometry, such as curving the text along a surface. Since the text is actual "
"3D geometry, the text can optionally have depth to it and can also "
"contribute to global illumination."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບການນຳໃຊ້ຂັ້ນສູງ, TextMesh ມີຄວາມຢືດຢຸ່ນກວ່າ ເພາະມັນຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສາມາດແຕ່ງສະໄຕລ໌ຂໍ້ຄວາມ ດ້ວຍ "
"custom shaders ໄດ້. Custom shaders ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສາມາດປ່ຽນແປງເລຂາຄະນິດຂັ້ນສຸດທ້າຍ ເຊັ່ນ ການເຮັດໃ"
"ຫ້ຂໍ້ຄວາມໂຄ້ງໄປຕາມພື້ນຜິວ. ເນື່ອງຈາກຂໍ້ຄວາມເປັນເລຂາຄະນິດ 3D ແທ້ໆ, ຂໍ້ຄວາມຈຶ່ງສາມາດມີຄວາມເລິກໄດ້ ແລ"
"ະ ຍັງສາມາດມີສ່ວນຮ່ວມໃນ global illumination ໄດ້ອີກດ້ວຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_text.rst:172
msgid ""
"If you need features such as BBCode or Control theming support, then using a "
"projected RichTextLabel node is the only way to go."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການຄຸນສົມບັດເຊັ່ນ BBCode ຫຼື ການຮອງຮັບ Control theming, ການໃຊ້ໂນດ "
"RichTextLabel ທີ່ຖືກສາຍພາບ (projected) ແມ່ນທາງດຽວທີ່ເຮັດໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:4
msgid "3D rendering limitations"
msgstr "ຂໍ້ຈຳກັດຂອງການສະແດງຜົນ 3D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:9
msgid ""
"Due to their focus on performance, real-time rendering engines have many "
"limitations. Godot's renderer is no exception. To work effectively with "
"those limitations, you need to understand them."
msgstr ""
"ເນື່ອງຈາກການໃຫ້ຄວາມສຳຄັນກັບປະສິດທິພາບ, ເອັນຈິນການສະແດງຜົນແບບຣຽວໄທມ໌ (real-time "
"rendering) ຈຶ່ງມີຂໍ້ຈຳກັດຫຼາຍຢ່າງ. ຕົວສະແດງຜົນຂອງ Godot ກໍບໍ່ແມ່ນຂໍ້ຍົກເວັ້ນ. ເພື່ອເຮັດວຽກກັບ ຂໍ້ຈຳກັດເ"
"ຫຼົ່ານັ້ນຢ່າງມີປະສິດທິພາບ, ເເຈົ້າຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງເຂົ້າໃຈພວກມັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:14
msgid "Texture size limits"
msgstr "ຂໍ້ຈຳກັດຂະໜາດຂອງ Texture"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:16
msgid ""
"On desktops and laptops, textures larger than 8192×8192 may not be supported "
"on older devices. You can check your target GPU's limitations on "
"`GPUinfo.org <https://www.gpuinfo.org/>`__."
msgstr ""
"ເທິງເດັສທັອບ ແລະ ແລັບທັອບ, texture ທີ່ມີຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ກວ່າ 8192×8192 ອາດຈະບໍ່ຮອງຮັບ ໃນອຸປະກອນຮຸ່ນເ"
"ກົ່າ. ເຈົ້າສາມາດກວດສອບຂໍ້ຈຳກັດຂອງ GPU ເປົ້າໝາຍໄດ້ທີ່ `GPUinfo.org <https://"
"www.gpuinfo.org/>`__."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:20
msgid ""
"Mobile GPUs are typically limited to 4096×4096 textures. Also, some mobile "
"GPUs don't support repeating non-power-of-two-sized textures. Therefore, if "
"you want your texture to display correctly on all platforms, you should "
"avoid using textures larger than 4096×4096 and use a power of two size if "
"the texture needs to repeat."
msgstr ""
"GPU ຂອງມືຖືປົກກະຕິແລ້ວຈະຖືກຈຳກັດຢູ່ທີ່ texture ຂະໜາດ 4096×4096. ນອກຈາກນັ້ນ, GPU ມືຖືບາງລຸ້ນຍັງບໍ່"
"ຮອງຮັບການເຮັດຊ້ຳ (repeating) ຂອງ texture ທີ່ມີຂະໜາດບໍ່ແມ່ນກຳລັງສອງ (non-power-of-two). "
"ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ texture ສະແດງຜົນໄດ້ຢ່າງຖືກຕ້ອງໃນທຸກແພລັດຟອມ, ເຈົ້າຄວນ ຫຼີກລ່ຽງການໃຊ້ "
"texture ທີ່ມີຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ກວ່າ 4096×4096 ແລະ ໃຊ້ຂະໜາດທີ່ເປັນກຳລັງສອງ ຖ້າ texture ນັ້ນຕ້ອງມີການເຮັ"
"ດຊ້ຳ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:26
msgid ""
"To limit the size of a specific texture that may be too large to render, you "
"can set the **Process > Size Limit** import option to a value greater than "
"``0``. This will reduce the texture's dimensions on import (preserving "
"aspect ratio) without affecting the source file."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອຈຳກັດຂະໜາດຂອງ texture ໃດໜຶ່ງທີ່ອາດຈະໃຫຍ່ເກີນໄປທີ່ຈະສະແດງຜົນ, ເຈົ້າສາມາດຕັ້ງຄ່າ ຕົວເລືອກການນ"
"ຳເຂົ້າ **Process > Size Limit** ໃຫ້ມີຄ່າຫຼາຍກວ່າ ``0``. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະຫຼຸດຂະໜາດ ຂອງ texture ລົງໃ"
"ນຕອນນຳເຂົ້າ (ໂດຍຮັກສາອັດຕາສ່ວນພາບໄວ້) ໂດຍບໍ່ມີຜົນກະທົບຕໍ່ໄຟລ໌ຕົ້ນສະບັບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:34
msgid "Color banding"
msgstr "ການເກີດແຖບສີ (Color banding)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:36
msgid ""
"When using the Forward+ or Mobile rendering methods, Godot's 3D engine "
"renders internally in HDR. However, the rendering output will typically be "
"written to a lower precision buffer. This can result in visible banding, "
"especially when using untextured materials. For performance reasons, color "
"precision is also lower when using the Mobile rendering method compared to "
"Forward+."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອໃຊ້ວິທີການສະແດງຜົນ Forward+ ຫຼື Mobile, ເອັນຈິນ 3D ຂອງ Godot ຈະສະແດງຜົນ ພາຍໃນເປັນ "
"HDR. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ຜົນການສະແດງຜົນປົກກະຕິແລ້ວຈະຖືກຂຽນລົງໃນ buffer ທີ່ມີ ຄວາມລະອຽດຕ່ຳກວ່າ. ສິ່ງນີ້"
"ອາດຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເຫັນການເກີດແຖບສີ (banding) ໄດ້, ໂດຍສະເພາະ ເມື່ອໃຊ້ວັດສະດຸທີ່ບໍ່ມີ texture. ເພື່ອເຫດ"
"ຜົນທາງດ້ານປະສິດທິພາບ, ຄວາມລະອຽດຂອງສີ ກໍຈະຕ່ຳກວ່າເມື່ອໃຊ້ວິທີ Mobile ເມື່ອທຽບກັບ Forward+."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:43
msgid ""
"When using the Compatibility rendering method, internal HDR rendering is not "
"used and the color precision is the lowest of all rendering methods. This "
"also applies to 2D rendering, where banding may be visible when using smooth "
"gradient textures."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອໃຊ້ວິທີການສະແດງຜົນ Compatibility, ຈະບໍ່ມີການໃຊ້ການສະແດງຜົນ HDR ພາຍໃນ ແລະ ຄວາມລະອຽດຂ"
"ອງສີຈະຕ່ຳທີ່ສຸດໃນບັນດາວິທີການສະແດງຜົນທັງໝົດ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຍັງລວມເຖິງການສະແດງຜົນ 2D ນຳ, ເຊິ່ງອາດຈະເຫັນແຖບ"
"ສີໄດ້ເມື່ອໃຊ້ texture ແບບໄລ່ສີ (gradient) ທີ່ລຽບນຽນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:47
msgid "There are two main ways to alleviate banding:"
msgstr "ມີສອງວິທີຫຼັກໃນການຫຼຸດຜ່ອນການເກີດແຖບສີ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:49
msgid ""
"If using the Forward+ or Forward Mobile rendering methods, enable :ref:`Use "
"Debanding<class_ProjectSettings_property_rendering/anti_aliasing/quality/"
"use_debanding>` in **Project Settings > Rendering > Anti Aliasing**. This "
"applies a fullscreen debanding shader as a post-processing effect and is "
"very cheap."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າໃຊ້ວິທີ Forward+ ຫຼື Forward Mobile, ໃຫ້ເປີດໃຊ້ :ref:`Use "
"Debanding<class_ProjectSettings_property_rendering/anti_aliasing/quality/"
"use_debanding>` ໃນ **Project Settings > Rendering > Anti Aliasing**. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະໃຊ້ "
"debanding shader ແບບທົ່ວໜ້າຈໍເປັນ post-processing effect ແລະ ໃຊ້ຊັບພະຍາກອນໜ້ອຍຫຼາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:53
msgid ""
"Alternatively, bake some noise into your textures. This is mainly effective "
"in 2D, e.g. for vignetting effects. In 3D, you can also use a `custom "
"debanding shader <https://github.com/fractilegames/godot-gles2-debanding-"
"material>`__ to be applied on your *materials*. This technique works even if "
"your project is rendered with low color precision, which means it will work "
"when using the Mobile and Compatibility rendering methods."
msgstr ""
"ອີກວິທີໜຶ່ງຄື ການໃສ່ noise (ສັນຍານລົບ) ເຂົ້າໄປໃນ texture ຂອງທ່ານ. ວິທີນີ້ໄດ້ຜົນດີໃນ 2D ເຊັ່ນ: ສຳລັບ"
"ເອັບເຟັກ vignetting. ໃນ 3D, ທ່ານຍັງສາມາດໃຊ້ `custom debanding shader <https://"
"github.com/fractilegames/godot-gles2-debanding-material>`__ ເພື່ອນຳໄປໃຊ້ກັບ "
"*materials* ຂອງທ່ານ. ເຕັກນິກນີ້ໃຊ້ໄດ້ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າໂປຣເຈັກຂອງທ່ານຈະຖືກສະແດງຜົນດ້ວຍ ຄວາມລະອຽດສີຕ່"
"ຳ, ເຊິ່ງໝາຍຄວາມວ່າຈະໃຊ້ໄດ້ກັບວິທີ Mobile ແລະ Compatibility."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:60
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:64
msgid "Color banding comparison (contrast increased for more visibility)"
msgstr "ການປຽບທຽບແຖບສີ (ເພີ່ມ contrast ເພື່ອໃຫ້ເຫັນໄດ້ຊັດເຈນຂຶ້ນ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:68
msgid ""
"See `Banding in Games: A Noisy Rant (PDF) <https://loopit.dk/"
"banding_in_games.pdf>`__ for more details about banding and ways to combat "
"it."
msgstr ""
"ເບິ່ງ `Banding in Games: A Noisy Rant (PDF) <https://loopit.dk/"
"banding_in_games.pdf>`__ ສຳລັບລາຍລະອຽດເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບການເກີດແຖບສີ ແລະ ວິທີການແກ້ໄຂ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:72
msgid "Depth buffer precision"
msgstr "ຄວາມລະອຽດຂອງ Depth buffer"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:74
msgid ""
"To sort objects in 3D space, rendering engines rely on a *depth buffer* "
"(also called *Z-buffer*). This buffer has a finite precision: 32-bit on "
"desktop platforms, 24-bit on mobile platforms (for performance reasons). If "
"two different objects end up on the same buffer value, then Z-fighting will "
"occur. This will materialize as textures flickering back and forth as the "
"camera moves or rotates."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອຈັດລຽງວັດຖຸໃນພື້ນທີ່ 3D, ເອັນຈິນການສະແດງຜົນຈະອາໄສ *depth buffer* (ຫຼື ເອີ້ນວ່າ *Z-"
"buffer*). buffer ນີ້ມີຄວາມລະອຽດທີ່ຈຳກັດ: 32-bit ເທິງເດັສທັອບ, 24-bit ເທິງມືຖື (ເພື່ອເຫດຜົນ ທ"
"າງດ້ານປະສິດທິພາບ). ຖ້າວັດຖຸສອງອັນທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນມີຄ່າ buffer ດຽວກັນ, ຈະເກີດ Z-fighting. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະສ"
"ະແດງອອກມາເປັນ texture ທີ່ກະພິບໄປມາໃນຂະນະທີ່ກ້ອງເຄື່ອນທີ່ ຫຼື ໝຸນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:81
msgid ""
"To make the depth buffer more precise over the rendered area, you should "
"*increase* the Camera node's **Near** property. However, be careful: if you "
"set it too high, players will be able to see through nearby geometry. You "
"should also *decrease* the Camera node's **Far** property to the lowest "
"permissible value for your use case, though keep in mind it won't impact "
"precision as much as the **Near** property."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອເຮັດໃຫ້ depth buffer ມີຄວາມລະອຽດຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນໃນພື້ນທີ່ສະແດງຜົນ, ທ່ານຄວນ *ເພີ່ມ* ຄ່າ **Near** ຂ"
"ອງໂນດ Camera. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ຕ້ອງລະວັງ: ຖ້າຕັ້ງໄວ້ສູງເກີນໄປ, ຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນຈະສາມາດ ເບິ່ງທະລຸເລຂາຄະນິດທີ່ຢູ່ໃ"
"ກ້ໆໄດ້. ທ່ານຍັງຄວນ *ຫຼຸດ* ຄ່າ **Far** ຂອງໂນດ Camera ໃຫ້ຢູ່ໃນ ຄ່າຕ່ຳສຸດທີ່ຍອມຮັບໄດ້ສຳລັບການນຳໃຊ້ຂ"
"ອງທ່ານ, ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າມັນຈະບໍ່ມີຜົນຕໍ່ຄວາມລະອຽດຫຼາຍ ເທົ່າກັບຄ່າ **Near** ກໍຕາມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:88
msgid ""
"If you only need high precision when the player can see far away, you could "
"change it dynamically based on the game conditions. For instance, if the "
"player enters an airplane, the **Near** property can be temporarily "
"increased to avoid Z-fighting in the distance. It can then be decreased once "
"the player leaves the airplane."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າທ່ານຕ້ອງການຄວາມລະອຽດສູງສະເພາະຕອນທີ່ຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນເບິ່ງເຫັນໄດ້ໄກໆ, ທ່ານສາມາດປ່ຽນມັນແບບໄດນາມິກ ຕາມເງື່ອ"
"ນໄຂຂອງເກມ. ຕົວຢ່າງ: ຖ້າຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນຂຶ້ນເຮືອບິນ, ຄ່າ **Near** ສາມາດເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນຊົ່ວຄາວ ເພື່ອຫຼີກລ່ຽງ Z-"
"fighting ໃນໄລຍະໄກ. ຈາກນັ້ນກໍສາມາດຫຼຸດລົງໄດ້ເມື່ອຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນອອກຈາກເຮືອບິນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:94
msgid ""
"Depending on the scene and viewing conditions, you may also be able to move "
"the Z-fighting objects further apart without the difference being visible to "
"the player."
msgstr ""
"ຂຶ້ນກັບສາກ ແລະ ເງື່ອນໄຂການເບິ່ງ, ທ່ານອາດຈະສາມາດຍ້າຍວັດຖຸທີ່ເກີດ Z-fighting ໃຫ້ຫ່າງອອກຈາກກັນ ຕື່ມ"
"ອີກ ໂດຍທີ່ຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນບໍ່ສັງເກດເຫັນຄວາມແຕກຕ່າງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:98
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:102
msgid ""
"Z-fighting comparison (before and after tweaking the scene by offsetting the "
"Label3D away from the floor)"
msgstr ""
"ການປຽບທຽບ Z-fighting (ກ່ອນ ແລະ ຫຼັງການປັບແຕ່ງສາກໂດຍການຍ້າຍ Label3D ໃຫ້ຫ່າງຈາກພື້ນ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:107
msgid "Transparency sorting"
msgstr "ການຈັດລຽງຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ (Transparency sorting)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:109
msgid ""
"In Godot, transparent materials are drawn after opaque materials. "
"Transparent objects are sorted back to front before being drawn based on the "
"Node3D's position, not the vertex position in world space. Due to this, "
"overlapping objects may often be sorted out of order. To fix improperly "
"sorted objects, tweak the material's :ref:`Render Priority "
"<class_Material_property_render_priority>` property or the "
"node's :ref:`Sorting Offset "
"<class_VisualInstance3D_property_sorting_offset>`. Render Priority will "
"force specific materials to appear in front of or behind other transparent "
"materials, while Sorting Offset will move the object forward or backward for "
"the purpose of sorting. Even then, these may not always be sufficient."
msgstr ""
"ໃນ Godot, ວັດສະດຸໂປ່ງໃສຈະຖືກແຕ້ມຫຼັງຈາກວັດສະດຸທີ່ທຶບແສງ (opaque). ວັດຖຸທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສຈະຖືກ ຈັດລຽງຈາກຫຼັ"
"ງມາໜ້າກ່ອນການແຕ້ມ ໂດຍອີງໃສ່ຕຳແໜ່ງຂອງ Node3D, ບໍ່ແມ່ນຕຳແໜ່ງຂອງ vertex ໃນ world space. ຍ້ອ"
"ນເຫດນີ້, ວັດຖຸທີ່ຊ້ອນທັບກັນມັກຈະຖືກຈັດລຽງຜິດລຳດັບ. ເພື່ອແກ້ໄຂ ວັດຖຸທີ່ຈັດລຽງບໍ່ຖືກຕ້ອງ, ໃຫ້ປັບຄຸນສົມບັດ "
":ref:`Render Priority <class_Material_property_render_priority>` ຂອງ "
"material ຫຼື :ref:`Sorting Offset "
"<class_VisualInstance3D_property_sorting_offset>` ຂອງໂນດ. Render Priority ຈະບັ"
"ງຄັບໃຫ້ material ໃດໜຶ່ງປາກົດຢູ່ທາງໜ້າ ຫຼື ທາງຫຼັງ material ໂປ່ງໃສອື່ນໆ, ໃນຂະນະທີ່ Sorting "
"Offset ຈະຍ້າຍວັດຖຸໄປທາງໜ້າ ຫຼື ທາງຫຼັງເພື່ອຈຸດປະສົງໃນການຈັດລຽງ. ເຖິງຢ່າງນັ້ນ, ສິ່ງເຫຼົ່ານີ້ກໍອາດຈະບໍ່ພຽງ"
"ພໍສະເໝີໄປ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:122
msgid ""
"Transparent objects are not rendered to the normal-roughness buffer, as they "
"are drawn after opaque geometry. As a result, features that rely on the "
"normal-roughness buffer will not affect transparent materials."
msgstr ""
"ວັດຖຸທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສຈະບໍ່ຖືກສະແດງຜົນລົງໃນ normal-roughness buffer, ເພາະພວກມັນຖືກແຕ້ມຫຼັງຈາກ ເລຂາຄະ"
"ນິດທີ່ທຶບແສງ. ຜົນກໍຄື, ຟີເຈີທີ່ອາໄສ normal-roughness buffer ຈະບໍ່ມີຜົນຕໍ່ ວັດສະດຸທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:126
msgid ""
"Some rendering engines feature *order-independent transparency* techniques "
"to alleviate this, but this is costly on the GPU. Godot currently doesn't "
"provide this feature. There are still several ways to avoid this problem:"
msgstr ""
"ເອັນຈິນການສະແດງຜົນບາງອັນມີເຕັກນິກ *order-independent transparency* ເພື່ອຫຼຸດຜ່ອນບັນຫານີ້, ແຕ່"
"ມັນໃຊ້ຊັບພະຍາກອນ GPU ສູງ. ປະຈຸບັນ Godot ຍັງບໍ່ມີຟີເຈີນີ້. ແຕ່ຍັງມີຫຼາຍວິທີໃນການຫຼີກລ່ຽງບັນຫານີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:130
msgid ""
"Only make materials transparent if you actually need it. If a material only "
"has a small transparent part, consider splitting it into a separate "
"material. This will allow the opaque part to cast shadows and will also "
"improve performance."
msgstr ""
"ເຮັດໃຫ້ material ໂປ່ງໃສສະເພາະຕອນທີ່ຈຳເປັນແທ້ໆເທົ່ານັ້ນ. ຖ້າ material ມີສ່ວນໂປ່ງໃສພຽງແຕ່ ເລັກນ້ອ"
"ຍ, ໃຫ້ພິຈາລະນາແຍກມັນອອກເປັນ material ຕ່າງຫາກ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສ່ວນທີ່ທຶບແສງ ສາມາດເກີດເງົາໄດ້ ແລ"
"ະ ຍັງຊ່ວຍເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບອີກດ້ວຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:134
msgid ""
"If your texture mostly has fully opaque and fully transparent areas, you can "
"use alpha testing instead of alpha blending. This transparency mode is "
"faster to render and doesn't suffer from transparency issues. Enable "
"**Transparency > Transparency** to **Alpha Scissor** in StandardMaterial3D, "
"and adjust **Transparency > Alpha Scissor Threshold** accordingly if needed. "
"Note that MSAA will not antialias the texture's edges unless alpha "
"antialiasing is enabled in the material's properties. However, FXAA, TAA and "
"supersampling will be able to antialias the texture's edges regardless of "
"whether alpha antialiasing is enabled on the material."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າ texture ຂອງທ່ານສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ມີພື້ນທີ່ທີ່ທຶບແສງທັງໝົດ ແລະ ໂປ່ງໃສທັງໝົດ, ທ່ານສາມາດໃຊ້ alpha "
"testing ແທນ alpha blending. ໂໝດຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສນີ້ສະແດງຜົນໄດ້ໄວກວ່າ ແລະ ບໍ່ມີບັນຫາເລື່ອງການຈັດລຽ"
"ງ ຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ. ໃຫ້ເປີດໃຊ້ **Transparency > Transparency** ເປັນ **Alpha Scissor** ໃ"
"ນ StandardMaterial3D, ແລະ ປັບ **Transparency > Alpha Scissor Threshold** ຕາມຄວ"
"າມຈຳເປັນ. ໝາຍເຫດວ່າ MSAA ຈະບໍ່ ລົບຮອຍຢັກທີ່ຂອບຂອງ texture ນອກຈາກຈະເປີດໃຊ້ alpha "
"antialiasing ໃນຄຸນສົມບັດຂອງ material. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, FXAA, TAA ແລະ supersampling ຈະສ"
"າມາດລົບຮອຍຢັກທີ່ຂອບຂອງ texture ໄດ້ ບໍ່ວ່າຈະເປີດໃຊ້ alpha antialiasing ເທິງ material ຫຼື ບໍ່ກໍ"
"ຕາມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:144
msgid ""
"If you need to render semi-transparent areas of the texture, alpha scissor "
"isn't suitable. Instead, setting the StandardMaterial3D's **Transparency > "
"Transparency** property to **Depth Pre-Pass** can sometimes work (at a "
"performance cost). You can also try the **Alpha Hash** mode."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າທ່ານຕ້ອງການສະແດງຜົນພື້ນທີ່ທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສບາງສ່ວນຂອງ texture, alpha scissor ຈະບໍ່ເໝາະສົມ. ແຕ່ການຕັ້"
"ງຄ່າ **Transparency > Transparency** ຂອງ StandardMaterial3D ເປັນ **Depth Pre-"
"Pass** ບາງຄັ້ງກໍໄດ້ຜົນ (ແຕ່ຕ້ອງແລກກັບປະສິດທິພາບ). ທ່ານຍັງສາມາດລອງໃຊ້ໂໝດ **Alpha Hash** ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:149
msgid ""
"If you want a material to fade with distance, use the StandardMaterial3D "
"distance fade mode **Pixel Dither** or **Object Dither** instead of **Pixel "
"Alpha**. This will make the material opaque, which also speeds up rendering."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າທ່ານຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ material ຈາງລົງຕາມໄລຍະຫ່າງ, ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ໂໝດ distance fade ຂອງ "
"StandardMaterial3D ແບບ **Pixel Dither** ຫຼື **Object Dither** ແທນ **Pixel "
"Alpha**. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ material ກາຍເປັນແບບທຶບແສງ, ເຊິ່ງຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ການສະແດງຜົນໄວຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:153
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_rendering_limitations.rst:157
msgid ""
"Transparency sorting comparison (alpha-blended materials on the left, alpha "
"scissor materials on the right)"
msgstr ""
"ການປຽບທຽບການຈັດລຽງຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ (material ແບບ alpha-blended ຢູ່ເບື້ອງຊ້າຍ, material ແບ"
"ບ alpha scissor ຢູ່ເບື້ອງຂວາ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:4
msgid "Standard Material 3D and ORM Material 3D"
msgstr "Standard Material 3D ແລະ ORM Material 3D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:9
msgid ""
"``StandardMaterial3D`` and ``ORMMaterial3D`` (Occlusion, Roughness, "
"Metallic) are default 3D materials that aim to provide most of the features "
"artists look for in a material, without the need for writing shader code. "
"However, they can be converted to shader code if additional functionality is "
"needed."
msgstr ""
"``StandardMaterial3D`` ແລະ ``ORMMaterial3D`` (Occlusion, Roughness, "
"Metallic) ແມ່ນ material 3D ມາດຕະຖານທີ່ມີຈຸດປະສົງເພື່ອໃຫ້ຟີເຈີສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ທີ່ສິລະປິນຕ້ອງການໃນ "
"material ໂດຍບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງຂຽນ shader code. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ພວກມັນສາມາດຖືກແປງເປັນ shader "
"code ໄດ້ ຖ້າຕ້ອງການຟັງຊັນເພີ່ມເຕີມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:14
msgid "This tutorial explains the parameters present in both materials."
msgstr "ບົດຮຽນນີ້ຈະອະທິບາຍພາຣາມິເຕີທີ່ມີຢູ່ໃນ material ທັງສອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:16
msgid ""
"There are 4 ways to add these materials to an object. A material can be "
"added in the *Material* property of the mesh. It can be added in the "
"*Material* property of the node using the mesh (such as a MeshInstance3D "
"node), the *Material Override* property of the node using the mesh, and the "
"*Material Overlay*."
msgstr ""
"ມີ 4 ວິທີໃນການເພີ່ມ material ເຫຼົ່ານີ້ໃສ່ວັດຖຸ. material ສາມາດເພີ່ມໄດ້ໃນຄຸນສົມບັດ *Material* ຂອ"
"ງ mesh. ມັນຍັງສາມາດເພີ່ມໄດ້ໃນຄຸນສົມບັດ *Material* ຂອງໂນດທີ່ໃຊ້ mesh (ເຊັ່ນໂນດ "
"MeshInstance3D), ຄຸນສົມບັດ *Material Override* ຂອງໂນດທີ່ໃຊ້ mesh, ແລະ *Material "
"Overlay*."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:23
msgid ""
"If you add a material to the mesh itself, every time that mesh is used it "
"will have that material. If you add a material to the node using the mesh, "
"the material will only be used by that node, it will also override the "
"material property of the mesh. If a material is added in the *Material "
"Override* property of the node, it will only be used by that node. It will "
"also override the regular material property of the node and the material "
"property of the mesh."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າທ່ານເພີ່ມ material ໃສ່ mesh ໂດຍກົງ, ທຸກໆຄັ້ງທີ່ mesh ນັ້ນຖືກໃຊ້ ມັນຈະມີ material ນັ້ນ. ຖ້າທ່ານເ"
"ພີ່ມ material ໃສ່ໂນດທີ່ໃຊ້ mesh, material ຈະຖືກໃຊ້ສະເພາະໂດຍໂນດນັ້ນ ແລະ ມັນຍັງຈະໄປ "
"override ຄຸນສົມບັດ material ຂອງ mesh. ຖ້າເພີ່ມ material ໃນຄຸນສົມບັດ *Material "
"Override* ຂອງໂນດ, ມັນຈະຖືກໃຊ້ສະເພາະໂດຍໂນດນັ້ນ ແລະ ຈະ override ທັງ ຄຸນສົມບັດ material ປົ"
"ກກະຕິຂອງໂນດ ແລະ material ຂອງ mesh."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:30
msgid ""
"The *Material Overlay* property will render a material **over** the current "
"one being used by the mesh. As an example, this can be used to put a "
"transparent shield effect on a mesh."
msgstr ""
"ຄຸນສົມບັດ *Material Overlay* ຈະສະແດງຜົນ material **ຊ້ອນທັບ** material ປັດຈຸບັນທີ່ mesh ໃ"
"ຊ້ຢູ່. ຕົວຢ່າງ: ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດໃຊ້ເພື່ອໃສ່ເອັບເຟັກໂລ່ປ້ອງກັນທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສໃສ່ mesh ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:34
msgid "BaseMaterial 3D settings"
msgstr "ການຕັ້ງຄ່າ BaseMaterial 3D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:36
msgid ""
"StandardMaterial3D has many settings that determine the look of a material. "
"All of these are under the BaseMaterial3D category"
msgstr ""
"StandardMaterial3D ມີການຕັ້ງຄ່າຫຼາຍຢ່າງທີ່ກຳນົດຮູບລັກສະນະຂອງ material. ທັງໝົດນີ້ແມ່ນຢູ່ໃນໝວດໝູ່ "
"BaseMaterial3D."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:41
msgid ""
"ORM materials are almost exactly the same with one difference. Instead of "
"separate settings and textures for occlusion, roughness, and metallic, there "
"is a single ORM texture. The different color channels of that texture are "
"used for each parameter. Programs such as Substance Painter and Armor Paint "
"will give you the option to export in this format, for these two programs "
"it's with the export preset for unreal engine, which also uses ORM textures."
msgstr ""
"ORM materials ແມ່ນເກືອບຈະຄືກັນທຸກຢ່າງແຕ່ມີຈຸດແຕກຕ່າງໜຶ່ງ. ແທນທີ່ຈະມີການຕັ້ງຄ່າ ແລະ texture ແຍກກັ"
"ນສຳລັບ occlusion, roughness, ແລະ metallic, ແຕ່ມັນຈະມີ ORM texture ພຽງອັນດຽວ. ຊ່ອງສີ "
"(color channels) ທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນຂອງ texture ນັ້ນຈະຖືກໃຊ້ສຳລັບແຕ່ລະພາຣາມິເຕີ. ໂປຣແກຣມເຊັ່ນ "
"Substance Painter ແລະ Armor Paint ຈະມີຕົວເລືອກໃຫ້ export ໃນຮູບແບບນີ້, ເຊິ່ງໃນສອງໂປຣແກຣ"
"ມນີ້ມັນຄື export preset ສຳລັບ Unreal Engine ເຊິ່ງໃຊ້ ORM textures ຄືກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:48
msgid "Transparency"
msgstr "ຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ (Transparency)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:50
msgid ""
"By default, materials in Godot are opaque. This is fast to render, but it "
"means the material can't be seen through even if you use a transparent "
"texture in the **Albedo > Texture** property (or set **Albedo > Color** to a "
"transparent color)."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, material ໃນ Godot ຈະເປັນແບບທຶບແສງ (opaque). ສິ່ງນີ້ສະແດງຜົນໄດ້ໄວ, ແຕ່ ມັນໝາຍຄ"
"ວາມວ່າ material ຈະເບິ່ງທະລຸບໍ່ໄດ້ ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າທ່ານຈະໃຊ້ texture ທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສໃນ ຄຸນສົມບັດ "
"**Albedo > Texture** (ຫຼື ຕັ້ງ **Albedo > Color** ເປັນສີທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສ) ກໍຕາມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:54
msgid ""
"To be able to see through a material, the material needs to be made "
"*transparent*. Godot offers several transparency modes:"
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອໃຫ້ສາມາດເບິ່ງທະລຸ material ໄດ້, material ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງຖືກເຮັດໃຫ້ *ໂປ່ງໃສ*. Godot ມີໂໝດຄວາ"
"ມໂປ່ງໃສຫຼາຍຮູບແບບ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:57
msgid ""
"**Disabled:** Material is opaque. This is the fastest to render, with all "
"rendering features supported."
msgstr ""
"**Disabled:** Material ເປັນແບບທຶບແສງ. ນີ້ແມ່ນວິທີທີ່ສະແດງຜົນໄວທີ່ສຸດ ແລະ ຮອງຮັບ ຟີເຈີການສະແດງ"
"ຜົນທັງໝົດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:60
msgid ""
"**Alpha:** Material is transparent. Semi-transparent areas are drawn with "
"blending. This is slow to render, but it allows for partial transparency "
"(also known as translucency). Materials using alpha blending also can't cast "
"shadows, and are not visible in screen-space reflections."
msgstr ""
"**Alpha:** Material ເປັນແບບໂປ່ງໃສ. ພື້ນທີ່ທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສບາງສ່ວນຈະຖືກແຕ້ມດ້ວຍການ blending. ສິ່ງນີ້ສະ"
"ແດງຜົນຊ້າ, ແຕ່ມັນຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ມີຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສບາງສ່ວນ (ຫຼື ເອີ້ນວ່າ translucency). material ທີ່ໃຊ້ "
"alpha blending ຍັງບໍ່ສາມາດເກີດເງົາໄດ້ ແລະ ບໍ່ເຫັນໃນ screen-space reflections."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:65
msgid "**Alpha** is a good fit for particle effects and VFX."
msgstr "**Alpha** ເໝາະສຳລັບ particle effects ແລະ VFX."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:67
msgid ""
"**Alpha Scissor:** Material is transparent. Semi-transparent areas whose "
"opacity is below **Alpha Scissor Threshold** are not drawn (above this "
"opacity, these are drawn as opaque). This is faster to render than Alpha and "
"doesn't exhibit transparency sorting issues. The downside is that this "
"results in \"all or nothing\" transparency, with no intermediate values "
"possible. Materials using alpha scissor can cast shadows."
msgstr ""
"**Alpha Scissor:** Material ເປັນແບບໂປ່ງໃສ. ພື້ນທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສບາງສ່ວນທີ່ມີຄວາມທຶບຕ່ຳກວ່າ **Alpha "
"Scissor Threshold** ຈະບໍ່ຖືກແຕ້ມ (ຖ້າສູງກວ່າຄ່ານີ້ ຈະຖືກແຕ້ມແບບທຶບແສງ). ສິ່ງນີ້ສະແດງຜົນໄວກວ່າ "
"Alpha ແລະ ບໍ່ມີບັນຫາເລື່ອງການຈັດລຽງຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ. ຂໍ້ເສຍຄື ມັນຈະເປັນຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສແບບ \"ມີ ຫຼື ບໍ່ມີເລີ"
"ຍ\", ໂດຍບໍ່ມີຄ່າລະຫວ່າງກາງ. material ທີ່ໃຊ້ alpha scissor ສາມາດເກີດເງົາໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:74
msgid ""
"**Alpha Scissor** is ideal for foliage and fences, since these have hard "
"edges and require correct sorting to look good."
msgstr ""
"**Alpha Scissor** ເໝາະສຳລັບໃບໄມ້ ແລະ ຮົ້ວ, ເພາະສິ່ງເຫຼົ່ານີ້ມີຂອບທີ່ແຂງ ແລະ ຕ້ອງການການຈັດລຽງທີ່"
"ຖືກຕ້ອງເພື່ອໃຫ້ເບິ່ງດີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:77
msgid ""
"**Alpha Hash:** Material is transparent. Semi-transparent areas are drawn "
"using dithering. This is also \"all or nothing\" transparency, but dithering "
"helps represent partially opaque areas with limited precision depending on "
"viewport resolution. Materials using alpha hash can cast shadows."
msgstr ""
"**Alpha Hash:** Material ເປັນແບບໂປ່ງໃສ. ພື້ນທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສບາງສ່ວນຈະຖືກແຕ້ມໂດຍໃຊ້ dithering. ນີ້"
"ກໍເປັນຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສແບບ \"ມີ ຫຼື ບໍ່ມີເລີຍ\" ຄືກັນ, ແຕ່ dithering ຈະຊ່ວຍສະແດງພື້ນທີ່ທີ່ ທຶບແສງບາງສ່ວນດ້ວ"
"ຍຄວາມລະອຽດທີ່ຈຳກັດຂຶ້ນກັບຄວາມລະອຽດຂອງ viewport. material ທີ່ໃຊ້ alpha hash ສາມາດເກີດເງົາ"
"ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:82
msgid ""
"**Alpha Hash** is suited for realistic-looking hair, although stylized hair "
"may work better with alpha scissor."
msgstr ""
"**Alpha Hash** ເໝາະສຳລັບເສັ້ນຜົມທີ່ເບິ່ງສົມຈິງ, ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຜົມແບບ stylized ອາດຈະ ໃຊ້ໄດ້ດີກວ່າກັ"
"ບ alpha scissor."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:85
msgid ""
"**Depth Pre-Pass:** This renders the object's fully opaque pixels via the "
"opaque pipeline first, then renders the rest with alpha blending. This "
"allows transparency sorting to be *mostly* correct (albeit not fully so, as "
"partially transparent regions may still exhibit incorrect sorting). "
"Materials using depth prepass can cast shadows."
msgstr ""
"**Depth Pre-Pass:** ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະສະແດງຜົນພິກເຊວທີ່ທຶບແສງທັງໝົດຂອງວັດຖຸຜ່ານ opaque pipeline ກ່ອ"
"ນ, ຈາກນັ້ນຈຶ່ງສະແດງສ່ວນທີ່ເຫຼືອດ້ວຍ alpha blending. ສິ່ງນີ້ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ການຈັດລຽງຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ *ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່* "
"ຖືກຕ້ອງ (ເຖິງຈະບໍ່ທັງໝົດກໍຕາມ, ເພາະພື້ນທີ່ທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສບາງສ່ວນອາດຈະຍັງມີການ ຈັດລຽງທີ່ຜິດພາດ). material "
"ທີ່ໃຊ້ depth prepass ສາມາດເກີດເງົາໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:93
msgid ""
"Godot will automatically force the material to be transparent with alpha "
"blending if *any* of these conditions is met:"
msgstr ""
"Godot ຈະບັງຄັບໃຫ້ material ເປັນແບບໂປ່ງໃສດ້ວຍ alpha blending ໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ ຖ້າເຂົ້າເງື່ອນໄ"
"ຂ *ໃດໜຶ່ງ* ດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:96
msgid "Setting the transparency mode to **Alpha** (as described here)."
msgstr "ຕັ້ງໂໝດຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສເປັນ **Alpha** (ຕາມທີ່ໄດ້ອະທິບາຍໄວ້ນີ້)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:97
msgid "Setting a blend mode other than the default **Mix**"
msgstr "ຕັ້ງໂໝດ blend ເປັນຢ່າງອື່ນທີ່ບໍ່ແມ່ນ **Mix** ທີ່ເປັນຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:98
msgid "Enabling **Refraction**, **Proximity Fade**, or **Distance Fade**."
msgstr "ເປີດໃຊ້ **Refraction**, **Proximity Fade**, ຫຼື **Distance Fade**."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:100
msgid ""
"Comparison between alpha blending (left) and alpha scissor (right) "
"transparency:"
msgstr ""
"ການປຽບທຽບລະຫວ່າງຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສແບບ alpha blending (ຊ້າຍ) ແລະ alpha scissor (ຂວາ):"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:106
msgid ""
"Alpha-blended transparency has several :ref:`limitations "
"<doc_3d_rendering_limitations_transparency_sorting>`:"
msgstr ""
"ຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສແບບ Alpha-blended ມີ :ref:`ຂໍ້ຈຳກັດ "
"<doc_3d_rendering_limitations_transparency_sorting>` ຫຼາຍຢ່າງ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:109
msgid ""
"Alpha-blended materials are significantly slower to render, especially if "
"they overlap."
msgstr ""
"ວັດສະດຸທີ່ມີການປະສົມອັນຟາ (Alpha-blended) ຈະໃຊ້ເວລາປະມວນຜົນຊ້າກວ່າຢ່າງຫຼວງຫຼາຍ, ໂດຍສະເພາະແມ່"
"ນຖ້າມັນຊ້ອນທັບກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:111
msgid ""
"Alpha-blended materials may exhibit sorting issues when transparent surfaces "
"overlap each other. This means that surfaces may render in the incorrect "
"order, with surfaces in the back appearing to be in front of those which are "
"actually closer to the camera."
msgstr ""
"ວັດສະດຸທີ່ມີການປະສົມອັນຟາອາດຈະເກີດບັນຫາການຈັດລຽງລຳດັບເມື່ອພື້ນຜິວທີ່ມີຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສຊ້ອນທັບກັນ.\n"
"ນີ້ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າພື້ນຜິວຕ່າງໆອາດຈະສະແດງຜົນໃນລຳດັບທີ່ບໍ່ຖືກຕ້ອງ, ໂດຍພື້ນຜິວທີ່ຢູ່ທາງຫຼັງຈະປະກົດຂຶ້ນມາຢູ່ທາງໜ້າຂອ"
"ງພື້ນຜິວທີ່ຢູ່ໃກ້ກັບກ້ອງຫຼາຍກວ່າຕົວຈິງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:115
msgid ""
"Alpha-blended materials don't cast shadows, although they can receive "
"shadows."
msgstr ""
"ວັດສະດຸທີ່ມີການປະສົມອັນຟາຈະບໍ່ເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດເງົາ, ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າມັນຈະສາມາດຮັບເງົາໄດ້ກໍຕາມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:116
msgid ""
"Alpha-blended materials don't appear in any reflections (other than "
"reflection probes)."
msgstr ""
"ວັດສະດຸທີ່ມີການປະສົມອັນຟາຈະບໍ່ປະກົດຢູ່ໃນເງົາສະທ້ອນໃດໆ (ຍົກເວັ້ນໃນ reflection probes)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:118
msgid ""
"Screen-space reflections and sharp SDFGI reflections don't appear on alpha-"
"blended materials. When SDFGI is enabled, rough reflections are used as a "
"fallback regardless of material roughness."
msgstr ""
"Screen-space reflections ແລະ SDFGI reflections ທີ່ຄົມຊັດຈະບໍ່ປາກົດເທິງ material ແບບ "
"alpha-blended. ເມື່ອເປີດໃຊ້ SDFGI, ຈະມີການໃຊ້ rough reflections ເປັນ fallback ໂດຍບໍ່ຄຳ"
"ນຶງເຖິງຄວາມຫຍາບ (roughness) ຂອງ material."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:122
msgid ""
"Before using the **Alpha** transparency mode, always consider whether "
"another transparency mode is more suited for your needs."
msgstr ""
"ກ່ອນທີ່ຈະໃຊ້ໂໝດຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສແບບ **Alpha**, ໃຫ້ພິຈາລະນາສະເໝີວ່າໂໝດຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສອື່ນ ເໝາະສົມກັບຄວາມ"
"ຕ້ອງການຂອງທ່ານຫຼາຍກວ່າຫຼືບໍ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:128
msgid "Alpha Antialiasing"
msgstr "Alpha Antialiasing (ການລົບຮອຍຢັກຂອງ Alpha)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:132
msgid ""
"This property is only visible when the transparency mode is **Alpha "
"Scissor** or **Alpha Hash**."
msgstr ""
"ຄຸນສົມບັດນີ້ຈະເຫັນໄດ້ສະເພາະຕອນທີ່ໂໝດຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສເປັນ **Alpha Scissor** ຫຼື **Alpha Hash**."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:135
msgid ""
"While alpha scissor and alpha hash materials are faster to render than alpha-"
"blended materials, they exhibit hard edges between opaque and transparent "
"regions. While it's possible to use post-processing-based :ref:`antialiasing "
"techniques <doc_3d_antialiasing>` such as FXAA and TAA, this is not always "
"desired as these techniques tend to make the final result look blurrier or "
"exhibit ghosting artifacts."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າ material ແບບ alpha scissor ແລະ alpha hash ຈະສະແດງຜົນໄດ້ໄວກວ່າ material "
"ແບບ alpha-blended, ແຕ່ພວກມັນຈະເຫັນຂອບທີ່ແຂງລະຫວ່າງສ່ວນທີ່ທຶບແສງ ແລະ ໂປ່ງໃສ. ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຈະສາ"
"ມາດໃຊ້ເຕັກນິກ :ref:`antialiasing <doc_3d_antialiasing>` ທີ່ເປັນ post-processing ເຊັ່"
"ນ FXAA ແລະ TAA ໄດ້, ແຕ່ກໍບໍ່ແມ່ນສິ່ງທີ່ຕ້ອງການສະເໝີໄປ ເພາະ ເຕັກນິກເຫຼົ່ານີ້ມັກຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ຜົນລັດຂັ້ນສຸດທ້າຍເ"
"ບິ່ງເບຼີ (blurry) ຫຼື ເກີດພາບຊ້ອນ (ghosting)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:142
msgid "There are 3 alpha antialiasing modes available:"
msgstr "ມີ 3 ໂໝດ alpha antialiasing ໃຫ້ເລືອກ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:144
msgid ""
"**Disabled:** No alpha antialiasing. Edges of transparent materials will "
"appear aliased unless a post-processing-based antialiasing solution is used."
msgstr ""
"**Disabled:** ບໍ່ມີ alpha antialiasing. ຂອບຂອງ material ໂປ່ງໃສຈະເຫັນເປັນຮອຍຢັກ ນອກຈາ"
"ກຈະໃຊ້ post-processing antialiasing."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:146
msgid ""
"**Alpha Edge Blend:** Results in a smooth transition between opaque and "
"transparent areas. Also known as \"alpha to coverage\"."
msgstr ""
"**Alpha Edge Blend:** ເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດການປ່ຽນຜ່ານທີ່ລຽບນຽນລະຫວ່າງສ່ວນທຶບແສງ ແລະ ໂປ່ງໃສ. ຫຼື ເອີ້ນ"
"ວ່າ \"alpha to coverage\"."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:148
msgid ""
"**Alpha Edge Clip:** Results in a sharp, but still antialiased transition "
"between opaque and transparent areas. Also known as \"alpha to coverage + "
"alpha to one\"."
msgstr ""
"**Alpha Edge Clip:** ເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດການປ່ຽນຜ່ານທີ່ຄົມຊັດແຕ່ຍັງມີການລົບຮອຍຢັກລະຫວ່າງສ່ວນ ທຶບແສງ ແລ"
"ະ ໂປ່ງໃສ. ຫຼື ເອີ້ນວ່າ \"alpha to coverage + alpha to one\"."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:152
msgid ""
"When the alpha antialiasing mode is set to **Alpha Edge Blend** or **Alpha "
"Edge Clip**, a new **Alpha Antialiasing Edge** property becomes visible "
"below in the inspector. This property controls the threshold below which "
"pixels should be made transparent. While you've already defined an alpha "
"scissor threshold (when using **Alpha Scissor** only), this additional "
"threshold is used to smoothly transition between opaque and transparent "
"pixels. **Alpha Antialiasing Edge** must *always* be set to a value that is "
"strictly below the alpha scissor threshold. The default of ``0.3`` is a "
"sensible value with an alpha scissor of threshold of ``0.5``, but remember "
"to adjust this alpha antialiasing edge when modifying the alpha scissor "
"threshold."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອຕັ້ງໂໝດ alpha antialiasing ເປັນ **Alpha Edge Blend** ຫຼື **Alpha Edge Clip**, ຄຸ"
"ນສົມບັດ **Alpha Antialiasing Edge** ໃຫມ່ຈະປາກົດຂຶ້ນໃນ inspector. ຄຸນສົມບັດນີ້ ຄວບຄຸມຄ່າ "
"threshold ທີ່ພິກເຊວຄວນຈະໂປ່ງໃສ. ໃນຂະນະທີ່ທ່ານໄດ້ກຳນົດ alpha scissor threshold ໄວ້ແລ້ວ (ເ"
"ມື່ອໃຊ້ **Alpha Scissor**), threshold ເພີ່ມເຕີມນີ້ຈະຖືກໃຊ້ເພື່ອ ປ່ຽນຜ່ານລະຫວ່າງພິກເຊວທີ່ທຶບແສງ ແ"
"ລະ ໂປ່ງໃສໃຫ້ລຽບນຽນ. **Alpha Antialiasing Edge** ຕ້ອງຖືກຕັ້ງໃຫ້ມີຄ່າຕ່ຳກວ່າ alpha "
"scissor threshold *ສະເໝີ*. ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ ``0.3`` ແມ່ນຄ່າທີ່ເໝາະສົມເມື່ອໃຊ້ alpha scissor "
"threshold ທີ່ ``0.5``, ແຕ່ຢ່າລືມປັບ alpha antialiasing edge ນີ້ເມື່ອມີການປ່ຽນແປງ alpha "
"scissor threshold."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:163
msgid ""
"If you find the antialiasing effect not effective enough, try increasing "
"**Alpha Antialiasing Edge** while making sure it's below **Alpha Scissor "
"Threshold** (if the material uses alpha scissor). On the other hand, if you "
"notice the texture's appearance visibly changing as the camera moves closer "
"to the material, try decreasing **Alpha Antialiasing Edge**."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າທ່ານຮູ້ສຶກວ່າເອັບເຟັກ antialiasing ຍັງບໍ່ໄດ້ຜົນດີພໍ, ໃຫ້ລອງເພີ່ມ **Alpha Antialiasing "
"Edge** ໂດຍກວດສອບໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າມັນຕ່ຳກວ່າ **Alpha Scissor Threshold** (ຖ້າ material ໃຊ້ "
"alpha scissor). ໃນທາງກັບກັນ, ຖ້າທ່ານສັງເກດເຫັນວ່າຮູບລັກສະນະຂອງ texture ປ່ຽນແປງຢ່າງຊັດເຈນເ"
"ມື່ອກ້ອງ ເຄື່ອນທີ່ເຂົ້າໃກ້ material, ໃຫ້ລອງຫຼຸດ **Alpha Antialiasing Edge** ລົງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:171
msgid ""
"For best results, MSAA 3D should be set to at least 2× in the Project "
"Settings when using alpha antialiasing. This is because this feature relies "
"on alpha to coverage, which is a feature provided by MSAA."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອໃຫ້ໄດ້ຜົນລັດທີ່ດີທີ່ສຸດ, ຄວນຕັ້ງ MSAA 3D ຢ່າງໜ້ອຍ 2× ໃນ Project Settings ເມື່ອໃຊ້ alpha "
"antialiasing. ນີ້ແມ່ນຍ້ອນວ່າຟີເຈີນີ້ອາໄສ alpha to coverage, ເຊິ່ງເປັນ ຟີເຈີທີ່ມີໃຫ້ໂດຍ MSAA."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:175
msgid ""
"Without MSAA, a fixed dithering pattern is applied on the material's edges, "
"which isn't very effective at smoothing out edges (although it can still "
"help a little)."
msgstr ""
"ຫາກບໍ່ມີ MSAA, ຈະມີການໃຊ້ dithering pattern ແບບຄົງທີ່ກັບຂອບຂອງ material, ເຊິ່ງ ບໍ່ຄ່ອຍມີປະສິດ"
"ທິພາບໃນການເຮັດໃຫ້ຂອບລຽບນຽນ (ເຖິງວ່າມັນຈະຊ່ວຍໄດ້ເລັກນ້ອຍກໍຕາມ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:180
msgid "Blend Mode"
msgstr "ໂໝດການປະສົມ (Blend Mode)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:182
msgid ""
"Controls the blend mode for the material. Keep in mind that any mode other "
"than *Mix* forces the object to go through the transparent pipeline."
msgstr ""
"ຄວບຄຸມໂໝດການປະສົມສຳລັບ material. ຈື່ໄວ້ວ່າໂໝດໃດໆກໍຕາມທີ່ບໍ່ແມ່ນ *Mix* ຈະບັງຄັບ ໃຫ້ວັດຖຸຖືກສະແດງຜົ"
"ນຜ່ານ transparent pipeline."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:185
msgid ""
"**Mix:** Default blend mode, alpha controls how much the object is visible."
msgstr "**Mix:** ໂໝດເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, alpha ຈະຄວບຄຸມວ່າວັດຖຸເບິ່ງເຫັນໄດ້ຫຼາຍປານໃດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:186
msgid ""
"**Add:** The final color of the object is added to the color of the screen, "
"nice for flares or some fire-like effects."
msgstr ""
"**Add:** ສີຂັ້ນສຸດທ້າຍຂອງວັດຖຸຈະຖືກບວກເຂົ້າກັບສີຂອງໜ້າຈໍ, ເໝາະສຳລັບແສງແຟຼ (flares) ຫຼື ເອັບເຟັກທີ່ຄ້"
"າຍຄືໄຟ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:188
msgid ""
"**Subtract:** The final color of the object is subtracted from the color of "
"the screen."
msgstr "**Subtract:** ສີຂັ້ນສຸດທ້າຍຂອງວັດຖຸຈະຖືກລົບອອກຈາກສີຂອງໜ້າຈໍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:190
msgid ""
"**Multiply:** The final color of the object is multiplied with the color of "
"the screen."
msgstr "**Multiply:** ສີຂັ້ນສຸດທ້າຍຂອງວັດຖຸຈະຖືກຄູນເຂົ້າກັບສີຂອງໜ້າຈໍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:192
msgid ""
"**Premultiplied Alpha:** The color of the object is expected to have already "
"been multiplied by the alpha. This behaves like **Add** when the alpha is "
"``0.0`` (fully transparent) and like **Mix** when the alpha is ``1.0`` "
"(opaque)."
msgstr ""
"**Premultiplied Alpha:** ສີຂອງວັດຖຸຈະຖືກສົມມຸດວ່າໄດ້ຄູນກັບ alpha ໄວ້ແລ້ວ. ມັນຈະ ເຮັດວຽກຄືກັບ "
"**Add** ເມື່ອ alpha ເປັນ ``0.0`` (ໂປ່ງໃສທັງໝົດ) ແລະ ຄືກັບ **Mix** ເມື່ອ alpha ເປັນ "
"``1.0`` (ທຶບແສງ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:199
msgid "Cull Mode"
msgstr "Cull Mode (ໂໝດການຕັດຜິວ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:201
msgid ""
"Determines which side of the object is not drawn when backfaces are rendered:"
msgstr ""
"ກຳນົດວ່າດ້ານໃດຂອງວັດຖຸທີ່ຈະບໍ່ຖືກແຕ້ມເມື່ອມີການສະແດງຜົນດ້ານຫຼັງ (backfaces):"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:203
msgid "**Back:** The back of the object is culled when not visible (default)."
msgstr "**Back:** ດ້ານຫຼັງຂອງວັດຖຸຈະຖືກຕັດອອກເມື່ອເບິ່ງບໍ່ເຫັນ (ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:204
msgid "**Front:** The front of the object is culled when not visible."
msgstr "**Front:** ດ້ານໜ້າຂອງວັດຖຸຈະຖືກຕັດອອກເມື່ອເບິ່ງບໍ່ເຫັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:205
msgid ""
"**Disabled:** Used for objects that are double-sided (no culling is "
"performed)."
msgstr "**Disabled:** ໃຊ້ສຳລັບວັດຖຸທີ່ມີສອງດ້ານ (ຈະບໍ່ມີການຕັດຜິວ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:209
#: ../../docs/tutorials/assets_pipeline/importing_3d_scenes/available_formats.rst:85
msgid ""
"By default, Blender has backface culling disabled on materials and will "
"export materials to match how they render in Blender. This means that "
"materials in Godot will have their cull mode set to **Disabled**. This can "
"decrease performance since backfaces will be rendered, even when they are "
"being culled by other faces. To resolve this, enable **Backface Culling** in "
"Blender's Materials tab, then export the scene to glTF again."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, Blender ຈະປິດການຕັດຜິວດ້ານຫຼັງ (backface culling) ໃນ material ແລະ ຈະ "
"export material ເພື່ອໃຫ້ກົງກັບການສະແດງຜົນໃນ Blender. ນັ້ນໝາຍຄວາມວ່າ material ໃນ Godot "
"ຈະຖືກຕັ້ງ cull mode ເປັນ **Disabled**. ສິ່ງນີ້ອາດຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ປະສິດທິພາບຫຼຸດລົງເນື່ອງຈາກ ດ້ານຫຼັງຈະຖືກ"
"ສະແດງຜົນ ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າມັນຈະຖືກບັງໂດຍຜິວອື່ນກໍຕາມ. ເພື່ອແກ້ໄຂບັນຫານີ້, ໃຫ້ ເປີດໃຊ້ **Backface "
"Culling** ໃນແຖບ Materials ຂອງ Blender, ແລ້ວ export ສາກເປັນ glTF ອີກຄັ້ງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:217
msgid "Depth Draw Mode"
msgstr "Depth Draw Mode (ໂໝດການແຕ້ມຄວາມເລິກ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:219
msgid "Specifies when depth rendering must take place."
msgstr "ລະບຸວ່າການສະແດງຜົນຄວາມເລິກຄວນເກີດຂຶ້ນຕອນໃດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:221
msgid "**Opaque Only (default):** Depth is only drawn for opaque objects."
msgstr ""
"**Opaque Only (ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ):** ຄວາມເລິກຈະຖືກແຕ້ມສະເພາະວັດຖຸທີ່ທຶບແສງເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:222
msgid ""
"**Always:** Depth draw is drawn for both opaque and transparent objects."
msgstr "**Always:** ຄວາມເລິກຈະຖືກແຕ້ມທັງວັດຖຸທີ່ທຶບແສງ ແລະ ໂປ່ງໃສ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:223
msgid ""
"**Never:** No depth draw takes place (do not confuse this with the No Depth "
"Test option below)."
msgstr ""
"**Never:** ຈະບໍ່ມີການແຕ້ມຄວາມເລິກເກີດຂຶ້ນ (ຢ່າສັບສົນກັບຕົວເລືອກ No Depth Test ດ້ານລຸ່ມ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:225
msgid ""
"**Depth Pre-Pass:** For transparent objects, an opaque pass is made first "
"with the opaque parts, then transparency is drawn above. Use this option "
"with transparent grass or tree foliage."
msgstr ""
"**Depth Pre-Pass:** ສຳລັບວັດຖຸທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສ, ຈະມີການແຕ້ມສ່ວນທີ່ທຶບແສງກ່ອນ, ຈາກນັ້ນຈຶ່ງແຕ້ມ ສ່ວນທີ່ໂປ່ງໃ"
"ສຊ້ອນທັບ. ໃຊ້ຕົວເລືອກນີ້ກັບຫຍ້າ ຫຼື ໃບໄມ້ທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:232
msgid "No Depth Test"
msgstr "No Depth Test (ບໍ່ມີການທົດສອບຄວາມເລິກ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:234
msgid ""
"In order for close objects to appear over far away objects, depth testing is "
"performed. Disabling it has the result of objects appearing over (or under) "
"everything else."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອໃຫ້ວັດຖຸທີ່ຢູ່ໃກ້ປາກົດທັບວັດຖຸທີ່ຢູ່ໄກ, ຈະມີການເຮັດ depth testing. ການປິດມັນຈະສົ່ງຜົນໃຫ້ ວັດຖຸປາກົດຢູ່ເ"
"ທິງ (ຫຼື ຢູ່ກ້ອງ) ທຸກສິ່ງທຸກຢ່າງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:238
msgid ""
"Disabling this makes the most sense for drawing indicators in world space, "
"and works very well with the *Render Priority* property of Material (see the "
"bottom of this page)."
msgstr ""
"ການປິດຄຸນສົມບັດນີ້ເໝາະສຳລັບການແຕ້ມຕົວຊີ້ບອກ (indicators) ໃນ world space, ແລະ ໃຊ້ໄດ້ດີຫຼາຍກັບຄຸ"
"ນສົມບັດ *Render Priority* ຂອງ Material (ເບິ່ງທີ່ສ່ວນທ້າຍຂອງໜ້ານີ້)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:245
msgid "Depth Test"
msgstr "Depth Test (ການທົດສອບຄວາມເລິກ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:247
msgid ""
"This can be used to invert the standard depth test. When set to "
"**Inverted**, the object will only appear when occluded, and will be hidden "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດໃຊ້ເພື່ອປີ້ນການທົດສອບຄວາມເລິກມາດຕະຖານ. ເມື່ອຕັ້ງເປັນ **Inverted**, ວັດຖຸຈະ ປາກົດສະເພ"
"າະຕອນທີ່ຖືກບັງ (occluded) ເທົ່ານັ້ນ, ແລະ ຈະຖືກເຊື່ອງໄວ້ໃນກໍລະນີອື່ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:250
msgid "This has no effect if **No Depth Test** is enabled."
msgstr "ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະບໍ່ມີຜົນຖ້າເປີດໃຊ້ **No Depth Test**."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:258
msgid "Shading mode"
msgstr "Shading mode (ໂໝດການໃຫ້ແສງເງົາ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:260
msgid ""
"Materials support three shading modes: **Per-Pixel**, **Per-Vertex**, and "
"**Unshaded**."
msgstr ""
"Material ຮອງຮັບ 3 ໂໝດ shading: **Per-Pixel**, **Per-Vertex**, ແລະ "
"**Unshaded**."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:263
msgid "Three spheres showing the Per-Pixel, Per-Vertex, and Unshaded modes."
msgstr "ໜ່ວຍມົນສາມໜ່ວຍທີ່ສະແດງໂໝດ Per-Pixel, Per-Vertex, ແລະ Unshaded."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:267
msgid ""
"The **Per-Pixel** shading mode calculates lighting for each pixel, and is a "
"good fit for most use cases. However, in some cases you may want to increase "
"performance by using another shading mode."
msgstr ""
"ໂໝດ **Per-Pixel** ຈະຄິດໄລ່ແສງສຳລັບແຕ່ລະພິກເຊວ, ແລະ ເໝາະສົມກັບການນຳໃຊ້ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່. ແນວໃດກໍຕາ"
"ມ, ໃນບາງກໍລະນີທ່ານອາດຈະຕ້ອງການເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບໂດຍການໃຊ້ໂໝດ shading ອື່ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:271
msgid ""
"The **Per-Vertex** shading mode, often called \"vertex shading\" or \"vertex "
"lighting\", instead calculates lighting once for each vertex, and "
"interpolates the result between each pixel."
msgstr ""
"ໂໝດ **Per-Vertex**, ມັກຈະເອີ້ນວ່າ \"vertex shading\" ຫຼື \"vertex lighting\", ຈະຄິດໄ"
"ລ່ແສງພຽງຄັ້ງດຽວສຳລັບແຕ່ລະຈຸດຈອມ (vertex), ແລະ ເຮັດການ interpolate ຜົນລັດ ລະຫວ່າງແຕ່ລະພິກເ"
"ຊວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:275
msgid ""
"On low-end or mobile devices, using per-vertex lighting can considerably "
"increase rendering performance. When rendering several layers of "
"transparency, such as when using particle systems, using per-vertex shading "
"can improve performance, especially when the camera is close to particles."
msgstr ""
"ໃນອຸປະກອນລະດັບຕ່ຳ ຫຼື ມືຖື, ການໃຊ້ per-vertex lighting ສາມາດເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບການສະແດງຜົນ ໄດ້ຢ່"
"າງຫຼວງຫຼາຍ. ເມື່ອມີການສະແດງຜົນຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສຫຼາຍໆຊັ້ນ ເຊັ່ນ ຕອນທີ່ໃຊ້ particle systems, ການໃຊ້ "
"per-vertex shading ສາມາດປັບປຸງປະສິດທິພາບໄດ້, ໂດຍສະເພາະເມື່ອກ້ອງຢູ່ໃກ້ກັບ particle."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:280
msgid "You can also use per-vertex lighting to achieve a retro look."
msgstr "ທ່ານຍັງສາມາດໃຊ້ per-vertex lighting ເພື່ອໃຫ້ໄດ້ຮູບລັກສະນະແບບ retro."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:282
msgid "Two cubes with a brick texture, one shaded and one unshaded."
msgstr ""
"ກ້ອນສີ່ຫຼ່ຽມສອງອັນທີ່ມີ texture ລາຍດິນຈີ່, ອັນໜຶ່ງມີ shading ແລະ ອີກອັນໜຶ່ງເປັນ unshaded."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:286
msgid "Texture from `AmbientCG <https://ambientcg.com/view?id=Bricks051>`__"
msgstr "Texture ຈາກ `AmbientCG <https://ambientcg.com/view?id=Bricks051>`__"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:288
msgid ""
"The **Unshaded** shading mode does not calculate lighting at all. Instead, "
"the **Albedo** color is output directly. Lights will not affect the material "
"at all, and unshaded materials will tend to appear considerably brighter "
"than shaded materials."
msgstr ""
"ໂໝດ **Unshaded** ຈະບໍ່ມີການຄິດໄລ່ແສງເລີຍ. ແຕ່ສີ **Albedo** ຈະຖືກສະແດງຜົນອອກມາໂດຍກົງ. ແສງ"
"ຈະບໍ່ມີຜົນຕໍ່ material ເລີຍ, ແລະ material ທີ່ເປັນ unshaded ມັກຈະປາກົດແຈ້ງກວ່າ material ທີ່ມີ "
"shading ຢ່າງເຫັນໄດ້ຊັດເຈນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:293
msgid ""
"Rendering unshaded is useful for some specific visual effects. If maximum "
"performance is needed, it can also be used for particles, or low-end or "
"mobile devices."
msgstr ""
"ການສະແດງຜົນແບບ unshaded ມີປະໂຫຍດສຳລັບ visual effects ບາງຢ່າງໂດຍສະເພາະ. ຖ້າຕ້ອງການ ປ"
"ະສິດທິພາບສູງສຸດ, ມັນຍັງສາມາດໃຊ້ສຳລັບ particle, ຫຼື ອຸປະກອນລະດັບຕ່ຳ ແລະ ມືຖືໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:298
msgid "Diffuse Mode"
msgstr "Diffuse Mode (ໂໝດການກະຈາຍແສງ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:300
msgid ""
"Specifies the algorithm used by diffuse scattering of light when hitting the "
"object. The default is **Burley**. Other modes are also available:"
msgstr ""
"ລະບຸອັນກໍຣິທຶມທີ່ໃຊ້ໃນການກະຈາຍແສງ (diffuse scattering) ເມື່ອແສງກະທົບວັດຖຸ. ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ ແມ່ນ "
"**Burley**. ຍັງມີໂໝດອື່ນໆໃຫ້ເລືອກ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:303
msgid ""
"**Burley:** Default mode, the original Disney Principled PBS diffuse "
"algorithm."
msgstr ""
"**Burley:** ໂໝດເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ເປັນອັນກໍຣິທຶມ diffuse ດັ້ງເດີມຂອງ Disney Principled PBS."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:304
msgid "**Lambert:** Is not affected by roughness."
msgstr "**Lambert:** ບໍ່ໄດ້ຮັບຜົນກະທົບຈາກຄວາມຫຍາບ (roughness)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:305
msgid ""
"**Lambert Wrap:** Extends Lambert to cover more than 90 degrees when "
"roughness increases. Works great for hair and simulating cheap subsurface "
"scattering. This implementation is energy conserving."
msgstr ""
"**Lambert Wrap:** ຂະຫຍາຍ Lambert ໃຫ້ກວມເອົາຫຼາຍກວ່າ 90 ອົງສາເມື່ອຄວາມຫຍາບເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນ. ໃຊ້ໄດ້"
"ດີຫຼາຍສຳລັບເສັ້ນຜົມ ແລະ ການຈຳລອງ subsurface scattering ແບບງ່າຍໆ. ວິທີນີ້ ມີການຮັກສາພະລັງງາ"
"ນ (energy conserving)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:308
msgid ""
"**Toon:** Provides a hard cut for lighting, with smoothing affected by "
"roughness. It is recommended you disable sky contribution from your "
"environment's ambient light settings or disable ambient light in the "
"StandardMaterial3D to achieve a better effect."
msgstr ""
"**Toon:** ໃຫ້ການຕັດແສງທີ່ແຂງ, ໂດຍຄວາມລຽບນຽນຈະໄດ້ຮັບຜົນກະທົບຈາກຄວາມຫຍາບ. ແນະນຳໃຫ້ ປິດ "
"sky contribution ຈາກການຕັ້ງຄ່າ ambient light ຂອງ environment ຫຼື ປິດ ambient light "
"ໃນ StandardMaterial3D ເພື່ອໃຫ້ໄດ້ເອັບເຟັກທີ່ດີຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:316
msgid "Specular Mode"
msgstr "Specular Mode (ໂໝດການສະທ້ອນແສງ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:318
msgid ""
"Specifies how the specular blob will be rendered. The specular blob "
"represents the shape of a light source reflected in the object."
msgstr ""
"ລະບຸວ່າ specular blob (ຈຸດສະທ້ອນແສງ) ຈະຖືກສະແດງຜົນແນວໃດ. specular blob ເປັນຕົວແທນຂອງຮູ"
"ບຮ່າງຂອງແຫຼ່ງກຳເນີດແສງທີ່ສະທ້ອນໃນວັດຖຸ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:321
msgid "**SchlickGGX:** The most common blob used by PBR 3D engines nowadays."
msgstr "**SchlickGGX:** blob ທີ່ນິຍົມໃຊ້ທີ່ສຸດໃນເອັນຈິນ PBR 3D ໃນປັດຈຸບັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:322
msgid ""
"**Toon:** Creates a toon blob, which changes size depending on roughness."
msgstr "**Toon:** ສ້າງ toon blob, ເຊິ່ງປ່ຽນຂະໜາດຕາມຄວາມຫຍາບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:323
msgid "**Disabled:** Sometimes the blob gets in the way. Begone!"
msgstr "**Disabled:** ບາງຄັ້ງ blob ກໍກີດຂວາງ. ປິດມັນໄປເລີຍ!"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:328
msgid "Disable Ambient Light"
msgstr "ປິດ Ambient Light"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:330
msgid ""
"Makes the object not receive any kind of ambient lighting that would "
"otherwise light it."
msgstr "ເຮັດໃຫ້ວັດຖຸບໍ່ໄດ້ຮັບແສງ ambient ໃດໆ ທີ່ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ມັນແຈ້ງຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:334
msgid "Disable Fog"
msgstr "ປິດໝອກ (Disable Fog)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:336
msgid ""
"Makes the object unaffected by depth-based or volumetric fog. This is useful "
"for particles or other additively blended materials that would otherwise "
"show the shape of the mesh (even in places where it would be invisible "
"without the fog)."
msgstr ""
"ເຮັດໃຫ້ວັດຖຸບໍ່ໄດ້ຮັບຜົນກະທົບຈາກໝອກແບບ depth-based ຫຼື volumetric. ສິ່ງນີ້ມີປະໂຫຍດ ສຳລັບ "
"particle ຫຼື material ອື່ນໆທີ່ໃຊ້ການປະສົມແບບ additively ເຊິ່ງອາດຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ ເຫັນຮູບຮ່າງຂອງ "
"mesh (ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າໃນຈຸດທີ່ມັນຄວນຈະເບິ່ງບໍ່ເຫັນຖ້າບໍ່ມີໝອກ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:339
msgid "Disable Specular Occlusion"
msgstr "ປິດ Specular Occlusion"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:341
msgid ""
"Makes the object not have its reflections reduced where they would usually "
"be occluded."
msgstr ""
"ເຮັດໃຫ້ວັດຖຸບໍ່ມີການຫຼຸດແສງສະທ້ອນໃນຈຸດທີ່ປົກກະຕິແລ້ວຄວນຈະຖືກບັງ (occluded)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:344
msgid "Vertex Color"
msgstr "Vertex Color (ສີຂອງຈຸດຈອມ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:346
msgid ""
"This setting allows choosing what is done by default to vertex colors that "
"come from your 3D modeling application. By default, they are ignored."
msgstr ""
"ການຕັ້ງຄ່ານີ້ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ເລືອກໄດ້ວ່າຈະເຮັດແນວໃດກັບ vertex colors ທີ່ມາຈາກແອັບພລິເຄຊັນ 3D modeling ຂ"
"ອງທ່ານ. ໂດຍເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ພວກມັນຈະຖືກລະເລີຍ (ignored)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:352
msgid "Use as Albedo"
msgstr "ໃຊ້ເປັນ Albedo"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:354
msgid "Choosing this option means vertex color is used as albedo color."
msgstr "ການເລືອກຕົວເລືອກນີ້ໝາຍເຖິງການໃຊ້ vertex color ເປັນສີ albedo."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:357
msgid "Is sRGB"
msgstr "ເປັນ sRGB"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:359
msgid ""
"Most 3D modeling software will likely export vertex colors as sRGB, so "
"toggling this option on will help them look correct."
msgstr ""
"ຊອບແວ 3D modeling ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ມັກຈະ export vertex colors ເປັນ sRGB, ດັ່ງນັ້ນ ການເປີດຕົວເລືອກ"
"ນີ້ຈະຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ພວກມັນເບິ່ງຖືກຕ້ອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:363
msgid "Albedo"
msgstr "Albedo (ສີພື້ນຜິວ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:365
msgid ""
"*Albedo* is the base color for the material, on which all the other settings "
"operate. When set to *Unshaded*, this is the only color that is visible. In "
"previous versions of Godot, this channel was named *Diffuse*. The change of "
"name mainly happened because, in PBR (Physically Based Rendering), this "
"color affects many more calculations than just the diffuse lighting path."
msgstr ""
"*Albedo* ແມ່ນສີພື້ນຖານສຳລັບ material, ເຊິ່ງການຕັ້ງຄ່າອື່ນໆທັງໝົດຈະເຮັດວຽກເທິງສີນີ້. ເມື່ອຕັ້ງເປັນ "
"*Unshaded*, ນີ້ຈະເປັນສີດຽວທີ່ເຫັນໄດ້. ໃນ Godot ລຸ້ນກ່ອນໆ, ຊ່ອງນີ້ ເຄີຍມີຊື່ວ່າ *Diffuse*. ການປ່ຽນ"
"ຊື່ເກີດຂຶ້ນຍ້ອນວ່າໃນ PBR (Physically Based Rendering), ສີນີ້ມີຜົນຕໍ່ການຄິດໄລ່ຫຼາຍຢ່າງກວ່າພຽງແຕ່ເສັ້"
"ນທາງແສງ diffuse."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:371
msgid "Albedo color and texture can be used together as they are multiplied."
msgstr ""
"ສີ ແລະ texture ຂອງ Albedo ສາມາດໃຊ້ຮ່ວມກັນໄດ້ ເພາະພວກມັນຈະຖືກຄູນເຂົ້າກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:373
msgid ""
"*Alpha channel* in albedo color and texture is also used for the object "
"transparency. If you use a color or texture with *alpha channel*, make sure "
"to either enable transparency or *alpha scissoring* for it to work."
msgstr ""
"*Alpha channel* ໃນສີ ແລະ texture ຂອງ albedo ຍັງຖືກໃຊ້ສຳລັບຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສຂອງວັດຖຸນຳ. ຖ້າທ່ານ"
"ໃຊ້ສີ ຫຼື texture ທີ່ມີ *alpha channel*, ໃຫ້ກວດສອບວ່າໄດ້ເປີດໃຊ້ຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ ຫຼື *alpha "
"scissoring* ເພື່ອໃຫ້ມັນເຮັດວຽກໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:378
msgid "Metallic"
msgstr "Metallic (ຄວາມເປັນໂລຫະ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:380
msgid ""
"Godot uses a metallic model over competing models due to its simplicity. "
"This parameter defines how reflective the material is. The more reflective, "
"the less diffuse/ambient light affects the material and the more light is "
"reflected. This model is called \"energy-conserving\"."
msgstr ""
"Godot ໃຊ້ໂມເດວ metallic ແທນໂມເດວອື່ນໆຍ້ອນຄວາມງ່າຍດາຍຂອງມັນ. ພາຣາມິເຕີນີ້ນິຍາມວ່າ "
"material ມີຄວາມສະທ້ອນແສງຫຼາຍປານໃດ. ຍິ່ງສະທ້ອນຫຼາຍ, ແສງ diffuse/ambient ກໍຈະມີຜົນ ຕໍ່ "
"material ໜ້ອຍລົງ ແລະ ແສງຈະຖືກສະທ້ອນອອກມາຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນ. ໂມເດວນີ້ເອີ້ນວ່າ \"energy-conserving\"."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:385
msgid ""
"The *Specular* parameter is a general amount for the reflectivity (unlike "
"*Metallic*, this is not energy-conserving, so leave it at ``0.5`` and don't "
"touch it unless you need to)."
msgstr ""
"ພາຣາມິເຕີ *Specular* ແມ່ນປະລິມານທົ່ວໄປສຳລັບຄວາມສະທ້ອນ (ບໍ່ຄືກັບ *Metallic*, ສິ່ງນີ້ ບໍ່ແມ່ນ "
"energy-conserving, ດັ່ງນັ້ນໃຫ້ປະໄວ້ທີ່ ``0.5`` ແລະ ບໍ່ຕ້ອງໄປປັບມັນ ນອກຈາກຈະຈຳເປັນ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:389
msgid ""
"The minimum internal reflectivity is ``0.04``, so it's impossible to make a "
"material completely unreflective, just like in real life."
msgstr ""
"ຄວາມສະທ້ອນພາຍໃນຕ່ຳສຸດແມ່ນ ``0.04``, ດັ່ງນັ້ນມັນຈຶ່ງເປັນໄປບໍ່ໄດ້ທີ່ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ material ບໍ່ສະທ້ອນແສງເລີ"
"ຍ, ຄືກັນກັບໃນຊີວິດຈິງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:395
msgid "Roughness"
msgstr "Roughness (ຄວາມຫຍາບ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:397
msgid ""
"*Roughness* affects the way reflection happens. A value of ``0`` makes it a "
"perfect mirror while a value of ``1`` completely blurs the reflection "
"(simulating natural microsurfacing). Most common types of materials can be "
"achieved with the right combination of *Metallic* and *Roughness*."
msgstr ""
"*Roughness* ມີຜົນຕໍ່ວິທີການສະທ້ອນແສງ. ຄ່າ ``0`` ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ມັນເປັນຄືແວ່ນແຍງທີ່ສົມບູນແບບ ໃນຂະນະທີ່ຄ່"
"າ ``1`` ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ການສະທ້ອນເບຼີໄປທັງໝົດ (ຈຳລອງພື້ນຜິວແບບທຳມະຊາດ). ປະເພດ material ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ສ"
"າມາດເຮັດໄດ້ດ້ວຍການປະສົມປະສານທີ່ເໝາະສົມລະຫວ່າງ *Metallic* ແລະ *Roughness*."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:405
msgid "Emission"
msgstr "Emission (ການເປັ່ງແສງ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:407
msgid ""
"*Emission* specifies how much light is emitted by the material (keep in mind "
"this does not include light surrounding geometry unless :ref:`VoxelGI "
"<doc_using_voxel_gi>` or :ref:`SDFGI <doc_using_sdfgi>` are used). This "
"value is added to the resulting final image and is not affected by other "
"lighting in the scene."
msgstr ""
"*Emission* ລະບຸວ່າ material ເປັ່ງແສງອອກມາຫຼາຍປານໃດ (ຈື່ໄວ້ວ່າສິ່ງນີ້ບໍ່ລວມເຖິງແສງ ທີ່ຈະໄປກະທົບເລ"
"ຂາຄະນິດອ້ອມຂ້າງ ນອກຈາກຈະໃຊ້ :ref:`VoxelGI <doc_using_voxel_gi>` ຫຼື :ref:`SDFGI "
"<doc_using_sdfgi>`). ຄ່ານີ້ຈະຖືກບວກເຂົ້າກັບພາບຂັ້ນສຸດທ້າຍ ແລະ ບໍ່ໄດ້ຮັບ ຜົນກະທົບຈາກແສງອື່ນໆໃນສາ"
"ກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:415
msgid "Normal map"
msgstr "Normal map"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:417
msgid ""
"Normal mapping allows you to set a texture that represents finer shape "
"detail. This does not modify geometry, only the incident angle for light. In "
"Godot, only the red and green channels of normal maps are used for better "
"compression and wider compatibility."
msgstr ""
"Normal mapping ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ທ່ານສາມາດຕັ້ງ texture ທີ່ສະແດງລາຍລະອຽດຮູບຮ່າງທີ່ລະອຽດຂຶ້ນ. ສິ່ງນີ້ບໍ່ໄດ້ປ່ຽນ"
"ແປງເລຂາຄະນິດ, ແຕ່ປ່ຽນພຽງແຕ່ມຸມຕົກກະທົບຂອງແສງ. ໃນ Godot, ຈະໃຊ້ສະເພາະ ຊ່ອງສີແດງ (red) ແລ"
"ະ ຂຽວ (green) ຂອງ normal maps ເພື່ອການບີບອັດທີ່ດີກວ່າ ແລະ ການຮອງຮັບ ທີ່ກວ້າງຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:426
msgid ""
"Godot requires the normal map to use the X+, Y+ and Z+ coordinates, this is "
"known as OpenGL style. If you've imported a material made to be used with "
"another engine it may be DirectX style, in which case the normal map needs "
"to be converted so its Y axis is flipped."
msgstr ""
"Godot ຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ normal map ໃຊ້ພິກັດ X+, Y+ ແລະ Z+, ເຊິ່ງເອີ້ນວ່າແບບ OpenGL. ຖ້າທ່ານນຳເຂົ້"
"າ material ທີ່ສ້າງມາສຳລັບເອັນຈິນອື່ນ ມັນອາດຈະເປັນແບບ DirectX, ເຊິ່ງໃນ ກໍລະນີນັ້ນຕ້ອງໄດ້ແປງ "
"normal map ໂດຍການກັບດ້ານແກນ Y."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:431
#: ../../docs/tutorials/assets_pipeline/importing_images.rst:351
#: ../../docs/tutorials/assets_pipeline/importing_images.rst:460
msgid ""
"More information about normal maps (including a coordinate order table for "
"popular engines) can be found `here <http://wiki.polycount.com/wiki/"
"Normal_Map_Technical_Details>`__."
msgstr ""
"ສາມາດຫາຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບ normal maps (ລວມທັງຕາຕະລາງລຳດັບພິກັດສຳລັບເອັນຈິນຍອດນິຍົມ) ໄດ້ທີ່ "
"`ນີ້ <http://wiki.polycount.com/wiki/Normal_Map_Technical_Details>`__."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:438
msgid "Bent normal map"
msgstr "Bent normal map"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:440
msgid ""
"A bent normal map describes the average direction of ambient lighting. "
"Unlike a regular normal map, this is used to improve how a material reacts "
"to lighting rather than add surface detail."
msgstr ""
"Bent normal map ອະທິບາຍທິດທາງສະເລ່ຍຂອງແສງ ambient. ບໍ່ຄືກັບ normal map ທົ່ວໄປ, ສິ່ງນີ້ຖືກໃຊ້"
"ເພື່ອປັບປຸງວິທີທີ່ material ຕອບສະໜອງຕໍ່ແສງ ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນການເພີ່ມລາຍລະອຽດພື້ນຜິວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:444
msgid "This is achieved in two ways:"
msgstr "ສິ່ງນີ້ເຮັດໄດ້ສອງວິທີ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:446
msgid ""
"Indirect diffuse lighting is made to match global illumination more closely."
msgstr "ເຮັດໃຫ້ແສງ indirect diffuse ກົງກັບ global illumination ຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:447
msgid ""
"If specular occlusion is enabled, it is calculated using the bent normals "
"and ambient occlusion instead of just from ambient light. This includes "
"screen-space ambient occlusion (SSAO) and other sources of ambient occlusion."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເປີດໃຊ້ specular occlusion, ມັນຈະຖືກຄິດໄລ່ໂດຍໃຊ້ bent normals ແລະ ambient "
"occlusion ແທນທີ່ຈະມາຈາກ ambient light ພຽງຢ່າງດຽວ. ສິ່ງນີ້ລວມເຖິງ SSAO ແລະ ແຫຼ່ງອື່ນໆຂອງ "
"ambient occlusion."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:454
msgid ""
"Godot only uses the red and green channels of a bent normal map for better "
"compression and wider compatibility."
msgstr ""
"Godot ໃຊ້ສະເພາະຊ່ອງສີແດງ ແລະ ຂຽວຂອງ bent normal map ເພື່ອການບີບອັດທີ່ດີກວ່າ ແລະ ການຮອງຮັບ"
"ທີ່ກວ້າງຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:457
msgid ""
"When creating a bent normal map, there are three things required for it to "
"work correctly in Godot:"
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອສ້າງ bent normal map, ມີສາມຢ່າງທີ່ຈຳເປັນເພື່ອໃຫ້ມັນເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ຢ່າງຖືກຕ້ອງໃນ Godot:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:460
msgid "A **cosine distribution** of rays has to be used when baking."
msgstr "ຕ້ອງໃຊ້ **cosine distribution** ຂອງລັງສີເມື່ອເຮັດການ baking."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:461
msgid "The texture must be created in **tangent space**."
msgstr "Texture ຕ້ອງຖືກສ້າງໃນ **tangent space**."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:462
msgid ""
"The bent normal map needs to use the X+, Y+, and Z+ coordinates, this is "
"known as OpenGL style. If you've imported a material made to be used with "
"another engine it may be DirectX style, in which case the bent normal map "
"needs to be converted so its Y axis is flipped. This can be achieved by "
"setting the green channel under the **Channel Remap** section to **Inverted "
"Green** in the import dock."
msgstr ""
"Bent normal map ຕ້ອງໃຊ້ພິກັດ X+, Y+, ແລະ Z+, ເຊິ່ງເອີ້ນວ່າແບບ OpenGL. ຖ້າທ່ານນຳເຂົ້າ "
"material ທີ່ສ້າງມາສຳລັບເອັນຈິນອື່ນ ມັນອາດຈະເປັນແບບ DirectX, ເຊິ່ງໃນກໍລະນີນັ້ນ bent normal "
"map ຕ້ອງໄດ້ຖືກແປງໂດຍການກັບດ້ານແກນ Y. ສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ໂດຍການຕັ້ງຄ່າ ຊ່ອງສີຂຽວໃນສ່ວນ **Channel "
"Remap** ເປັນ **Inverted Green** ໃນແຖບ import."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:471
msgid ""
"A bent normal map is different from a regular normal map. The two are not "
"interchangeable."
msgstr ""
"Bent normal map ແຕກຕ່າງຈາກ normal map ປົກກະຕິ. ທັງສອງບໍ່ສາມາດໃຊ້ແທນກັນໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:475
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/visibility_ranges.rst:216
msgid "Rim"
msgstr "Rim (ແສງທີ່ຂອບ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:477
msgid ""
"Some fabrics have small micro-fur that causes light to scatter around it. "
"Godot emulates this with the *Rim* parameter. Unlike other rim lighting "
"implementations, which just use the emission channel, this one actually "
"takes light into account (no light means no rim). This makes the effect "
"considerably more believable."
msgstr ""
"ຜ້າບາງຊະນິດມີຂົນນ້ອຍໆທີ່ເຮັດໃຫ້ແສງກະຈາຍໄປທົ່ວ. Godot ຈຳລອງສິ່ງນີ້ດ້ວຍພາຣາມິເຕີ *Rim*. ບໍ່ຄືກັບວິທີການ"
"ເຮັດ rim lighting ອື່ນໆທີ່ໃຊ້ພຽງແຕ່ຊ່ອງ emission, ວິທີນີ້ມີການຄຳນຶງເຖິງ ແສງແທ້ໆ (ຖ້າບໍ່ມີແສງກໍຈະບໍ່"
"ມີ rim). ສິ່ງນີ້ເຮັດໃຫ້ເອັບເຟັກເບິ່ງສົມຈິງຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:484
msgid ""
"Rim size depends on roughness, and there is a special parameter to specify "
"how it must be colored. If *Tint* is ``0``, the color of the light is used "
"for the rim. If *Tint* is ``1``, then the albedo of the material is used. "
"Using intermediate values generally works best."
msgstr ""
"ຂະໜາດຂອງ Rim ຂຶ້ນກັບຄວາມຫຍາບ, ແລະ ມີພາຣາມິເຕີພິເສດເພື່ອລະບຸວ່າຈະໃຫ້ມັນມີສີແນວໃດ. ຖ້າ *Tint* ເ"
"ປັນ ``0``, ຈະໃຊ້ສີຂອງແສງສຳລັບ rim. ຖ້າ *Tint* ເປັນ ``1``, ຈະໃຊ້ສີ albedo ຂອງ "
"material. ການໃຊ້ຄ່າລະຫວ່າງກາງປົກກະຕິແລ້ວຈະໃຫ້ຜົນດີທີ່ສຸດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:490
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/visibility_ranges.rst:217
msgid "Clearcoat"
msgstr "Clearcoat (ການເຄືອບໃສ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:493
msgid ""
"The *Clearcoat* parameter is used to add a secondary pass of transparent "
"coat to the material. This is common in car paint and toys. In practice, "
"it's a smaller specular blob added on top of the existing material."
msgstr ""
"ພາຣາມິເຕີ *Clearcoat* ຖືກໃຊ້ເພື່ອເພີ່ມການເຄືອບໃສອີກຊັ້ນໜຶ່ງໃສ່ material. ສິ່ງນີ້ ພົບເຫັນໄດ້ທົ່ວໄປໃນສີລົ"
"ດ ແລະ ຂອງຫຼິ້ນ. ໃນທາງປະຕິບັດ, ມັນຄື specular blob ຂະໜາດນ້ອຍ ທີ່ເພີ່ມເຂົ້າໄປເທິງ material ທີ່ມີ"
"ຢູ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:500
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/visibility_ranges.rst:218
msgid "Anisotropy"
msgstr "Anisotropy (ຄວາມບໍ່ຄົງທີ່ຂອງທິດທາງ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:503
msgid ""
"This changes the shape of the specular blob and aligns it to tangent space. "
"Anisotropy is commonly used with hair, or to make materials such as brushed "
"aluminum more realistic. It works especially well when combined with "
"flowmaps."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະປ່ຽນຮູບຮ່າງຂອງ specular blob ແລະ ຈັດວາງໃຫ້ກົງກັບ tangent space. Anisotropy ມັກຈະ"
"ຖືກໃຊ້ກັບເສັ້ນຜົມ, ຫຼື ເພື່ອເຮັດໃຫ້ material ເຊັ່ນ ອາລູມີນຽມຂັດ (brushed aluminum) ເບິ່ງສົມຈິງຫຼາຍຂຶ້"
"ນ. ມັນໃຊ້ໄດ້ດີເປັນພິເສດເມື່ອໃຊ້ຮ່ວມກັບ flowmaps."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:510
msgid "Ambient Occlusion"
msgstr "Ambient Occlusion (ການບັງແສງແວດລ້ອມ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:512
msgid ""
"It is possible to specify a baked ambient occlusion map. This map affects "
"how much ambient light reaches each surface of the object (it does not "
"affect direct light by default). While it is possible to use Screen-Space "
"Ambient Occlusion (SSAO) to generate ambient occlusion, nothing beats the "
"quality of a well-baked AO map. It is recommended to bake ambient occlusion "
"whenever possible."
msgstr ""
"ສາມາດກຳນົດ AO map ທີ່ເຮັດການ baked ມາແລ້ວໄດ້. map ນີ້ມີຜົນຕໍ່ປະລິມານແສງ ambient ທີ່ຈະເຂົ້າເຖິງແ"
"ຕ່ລະພື້ນຜິວຂອງວັດຖຸ (ໂດຍເລີ່ມຕົ້ນມັນຈະບໍ່ມີຜົນຕໍ່ແສງໂດຍກົງ). ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າ ຈະສາມາດໃຊ້ SSAO ເພື່ອສ້າງ AO "
"ໄດ້, ແຕ່ບໍ່ມີຫຍັງຈະສູ້ຄຸນນະພາບຂອງ AO map ທີ່ baked ມາຢ່າງດີໄດ້. ແນະນຳໃຫ້ bake ambient "
"occlusion ທຸກຄັ້ງທີ່ເຮັດໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:521
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/visibility_ranges.rst:219
msgid "Height"
msgstr "Height (ຄວາມສູງ/ຄວາມເລິກ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:523
msgid ""
"Setting a height map on a material produces a ray-marched search to emulate "
"the proper displacement of cavities along the view direction. This only "
"creates an illusion of depth, and does not add real geometry — for a height "
"map shape used for physics collision (such as terrain), "
"see :ref:`class_HeightMapShape3D`. It may not work for complex objects, but "
"it produces a realistic depth effect for textures. For best results, "
"*Height* should be used together with normal mapping."
msgstr ""
"ການຕັ້ງ height map ໃນ material ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດການຄົ້ນຫາແບບ ray-marched ເພື່ອຈຳລອງ ການແທນ"
"ທີ່ (displacement) ຂອງສ່ວນທີ່ເປັນຫຼຸມຕາມທິດທາງການເບິ່ງ. ສິ່ງນີ້ສ້າງພຽງແຕ່ ພາບລວງຕາຂອງຄວາມເລິກ ແ"
"ລະ ບໍ່ໄດ້ເພີ່ມເລຂາຄະນິດແທ້ໆ — ສຳລັບ height map ທີ່ໃຊ້ສຳລັບ ການຕຳທາງຟີຊິກ (ເຊັ່ນ ພື້ນທີ່), ໃຫ້ເບິ່ງ "
":ref:`class_HeightMapShape3D`. ມັນອາດຈະ ໃຊ້ບໍ່ໄດ້ດີກັບວັດຖຸທີ່ຊັບຊ້ອນ, ແຕ່ມັນໃຫ້ເອັບເຟັກຄວາມເລິກ"
"ທີ່ສົມຈິງສຳລັບ texture. ເພື່ອໃຫ້ໄດ້ຜົນດີທີ່ສຸດ, ຄວນໃຊ້ *Height* ຮ່ວມກັບ normal mapping."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:534
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/visibility_ranges.rst:220
msgid "Subsurface Scattering"
msgstr "Subsurface Scattering (ການກະຈາຍແສງໃຕ້ຜິວ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:536
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_antialiasing.rst:91
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/3d_antialiasing.rst:124
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/resolution_scaling.rst:188
msgid ""
"*This is only available in the Forward+ renderer, not the Mobile or "
"Compatibility renderers.*"
msgstr ""
"*ສິ່ງນີ້ມີໃຫ້ສະເພາະໃນ Forward+ renderer ເທົ່ານັ້ນ, ບໍ່ມີໃນ Mobile ຫຼື Compatibility "
"renderer.*"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:539
msgid ""
"This effect emulates light that penetrates an object's surface, is "
"scattered, and then comes out. It is useful to create realistic skin, "
"marble, colored liquids, etc."
msgstr ""
"ເອັບເຟັກນີ້ຈຳລອງແສງທີ່ຊຶມຜ່ານພື້ນຜິວຂອງວັດຖຸ, ມີການກະຈາຍຕົວ, ແລ້ວສະທ້ອນອອກມາ. ມັນມີປະໂຫຍດໃນການສ້າ"
"ງຜິວໜັງທີ່ສົມຈິງ, ຫີນອ່ອນ, ຂອງແຫຼວທີ່ມີສີ ແລະ ອື່ນໆ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:546
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/visibility_ranges.rst:221
msgid "Back Lighting"
msgstr "ແສງດ້ານຫຼັງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:548
msgid ""
"This controls how much light from the lit side (visible to light) is "
"transferred to the dark side (opposite from the light). This works well for "
"thin objects such as plant leaves, grass, human ears, etc."
msgstr ""
"ສ່ວນນີ້ຄວບຄຸມປະລິມານແສງຈາກດ້ານທີ່ຖືກແສງ (ດ້ານທີ່ເບິ່ງເຫັນແສງ) ສົ່ງຜ່ານໄປຍັງດ້ານມືດ (ດ້ານກົງກັນຂ້າມກັບແສ"
"ງ). ມັນໃຊ້ໄດ້ດີກັບວັດຖຸທີ່ບາງ ເຊັ່ນ: ໃບໄມ້, ຫຍ້າ, ຫູມະນຸດ ແລະ ອື່ນໆ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:555
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/visibility_ranges.rst:222
msgid "Refraction"
msgstr "ການຫັກເຫ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:557
msgid ""
"When refraction is enabled, Godot attempts to fetch information from behind "
"the object being rendered. This allows distorting the transparency in a way "
"similar to refraction in real life."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອເປີດໃຊ້ການຫັກເຫ, Godot ຈະພະຍາຍາມດຶງເອົາຂໍ້ມູນຈາກດ້ານຫຼັງຂອງວັດຖຸທີ່ກຳລັງສະແດງຜົນ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ກ"
"ານບິດເບືອນຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສໃນລັກສະນະທີ່ຄ້າຍຄືກັບການຫັກເຫຂອງແສງໃນຊີວິດຈິງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:561
msgid ""
"Remember to use a transparent albedo texture (or reduce the albedo color's "
"alpha channel) to make refraction visible, as refraction relies on "
"transparency to have a visible effect."
msgstr ""
"ຢ່າລືມໃຊ້ພື້ນຜິວ (texture) albedo ແບບໂປ່ງໃສ (ຫຼື ຫຼຸດຄ່າ alpha ຂອງສີ albedo ລົງ) ເພື່ອໃຫ້ເບິ່ງເຫັ"
"ນການຫັກເຫໄດ້, ເພາະການຫັກເຫຕ້ອງອາໄສຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສຈຶ່ງຈະສະແດງເອັບເຟັກອອກມາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:565
msgid ""
"Refraction also takes the material roughness into account. Higher roughness "
"values will make the objects behind the refraction look blurrier, which "
"simulates real life behavior. If you can't see behind the object when "
"refraction is enabled and albedo transparency is reduced, decrease the "
"material's **Roughness** value."
msgstr ""
"ການຫັກເຫຍັງຄຳນຶງເຖິງຄວາມຫຍາບ (roughness) ຂອງວັດສະດຸນຳ. ຄ່າຄວາມຫຍາບທີ່ສູງຂຶ້ນຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ວັດຖຸທີ່ຢູ່ເ"
"ບື້ອງຫຼັງການຫັກເຫເບິ່ງມົວລົງ, ເຊິ່ງເປັນການຈຳລອງພຶດຕິກຳໃນຊີວິດຈິງ. ຖ້າເຈົ້າບໍ່ສາມາດເບິ່ງເຫັນດ້ານຫຼັງຂອງວັດຖຸ"
"ໄດ້ເມື່ອເປີດການຫັກເຫ ແລະ ຫຼຸດຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ albedo ລົງແລ້ວ, ໃຫ້ຫຼຸດຄ່າ **Roughness** ຂອງວັດສະດຸລົ"
"ງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:571
msgid ""
"A normal map can optionally be specified in the **Refraction Texture** "
"property to allow distorting the refraction's direction on a per-pixel basis."
msgstr ""
"ສາມາດກຳນົດ normal map ໃນຄຸນສົມບັດ **Refraction Texture** ເພື່ອບິດເບືອນທິດທາງການຫັກເຫໃນແ"
"ຕ່ລະພິກເຊວໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:578
msgid ""
"Refraction is implemented as a screen-space effect and forces the material "
"to be transparent. This makes the effect relatively fast, but this results "
"in some limitations:"
msgstr ""
"ການຫັກເຫຖືກສ້າງຂຶ້ນເປັນເອັບເຟັກແບບ screen-space ແລະ ບັງຄັບໃຫ້ວັດສະດຸມີຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ. ສິ່ງນີ້ເຮັດໃຫ້ເອັ"
"ບເຟັກເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ໄວ, ແຕ່ກໍມີຂໍ້ຈຳກັດບາງຢ່າງ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:582
msgid ""
":ref:`Transparency sorting "
"<doc_3d_rendering_limitations_transparency_sorting>` issues may occur."
msgstr ""
"ອາດເກີດບັນຫາ :ref:`ການຈັດລຽງຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ "
"<doc_3d_rendering_limitations_transparency_sorting>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:584
msgid ""
"The refractive material cannot refract onto itself, or onto other "
"transparent materials. A refractive material behind another transparent "
"material will be invisible."
msgstr ""
"ວັດສະດຸທີ່ມີການຫັກເຫບໍ່ສາມາດຫັກເຫໃສ່ຕົວມັນເອງ ຫຼື ໃສ່ວັດສະດຸໂປ່ງໃສອື່ນໆໄດ້. ວັດສະດຸຫັກເຫທີ່ຢູ່ເບື້ອງຫຼັງວັດສະດຸ"
"ໂປ່ງໃສອື່ນຈະເບິ່ງບໍ່ເຫັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:587
msgid ""
"Off-screen objects cannot appear in the refraction. This is most noticeable "
"with high refraction strength values."
msgstr ""
"ວັດຖຸທີ່ຢູ່ນອກໜ້າຈໍຈະບໍ່ປາກົດໃນການຫັກເຫ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະເຫັນໄດ້ຊັດເຈນເມື່ອກຳນົດຄ່າຄວາມເຂັ້ມຂອງການຫັກເຫໄວ້ສູງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:589
msgid ""
"Opaque materials in front of the refractive material will appear to have "
"\"refracted\" edges, even though they shouldn't."
msgstr ""
"ວັດສະດຸທຶບແສງທີ່ຢູ່ທາງໜ້າວັດສະດຸຫັກເຫຈະປາກົດມີຂອບທີ່ \"ຫັກເຫ\", ທັງໆທີ່ມັນບໍ່ຄວນຈະເປັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:593
msgid "Detail"
msgstr "ລາຍລະອຽດ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:595
msgid ""
"Godot allows using secondary albedo and normal maps to generate a detail "
"texture, which can be blended in many ways. By combining this with secondary "
"UV or triplanar modes, many interesting textures can be achieved."
msgstr ""
"Godot ອະນຸຍາດໃຫ້ໃຊ້ albedo ແລະ normal map ສໍາຮອງເພື່ອສ້າງພື້ນຜິວລາຍລະອຽດ (detail "
"texture), ເຊິ່ງສາມາດປະສົມປະສານໄດ້ຫຼາຍຮູບແບບ. ເມື່ອໃຊ້ຮ່ວມກັບໂໝດ UV ສໍາຮອງ ຫຼື triplanar, ຈະ"
"ສາມາດສ້າງພື້ນຜິວທີ່ໜ້າສົນໃຈໄດ້ຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:601
msgid "There are several settings that control how detail is used."
msgstr "ມີການຕັ້ງຄ່າຫຼາຍຢ່າງທີ່ຄວບຄຸມວິທີການໃຊ້ລາຍລະອຽດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:603
msgid ""
"Mask: The detail mask is a black and white image used to control where the "
"blending takes place on a texture. White is for the detail textures, Black "
"is for the regular material textures, different shades of gray are for "
"partial blending of the material textures and detail textures."
msgstr ""
"Mask: detail mask ແມ່ນຮູບພາບຂາວດຳທີ່ໃຊ້ເພື່ອຄວບຄຸມບ່ອນທີ່ຈະເກີດການປະສົມ (blending) ໃສ່ພື້ນຜິ"
"ວ. ສີຂາວແມ່ນສຳລັບພື້ນຜິວລາຍລະອຽດ, ສີດຳແມ່ນສຳລັບພື້ນຜິວວັດສະດຸປົກກະຕິ, ສ່ວນສີເທີົາໃນລະດັບຕ່າງໆ ແມ່ນສຳ"
"ລັບການປະສົມບາງສ່ວນລະຫວ່າງວັດສະດຸປົກກະຕິ ແລະ ລາຍລະອຽດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:608
msgid ""
"Blend Mode: These four modes control how the textures are blended together."
msgstr "Blend Mode: ສີ່ໂໝດນີ້ຄວບຄຸມວິທີການປະສົມພື້ນຜິວເຂົ້າກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:610
msgid ""
"Mix: Combines pixel values of both textures. At black, only show the "
"material texture, at white, only show the detail texture. Values of gray "
"create a smooth blend between the two."
msgstr ""
"Mix: ປະສົມຄ່າພິກເຊວຂອງທັງສອງພື້ນຜິວເຂົ້າກັນ. ບ່ອນທີ່ເປັນສີດຳຈະສະແດງແຕ່ພື້ນຜິວວັດສະດຸ, ບ່ອນທີ່ເປັນສີຂາວຈ"
"ະສະແດງແຕ່ພື້ນຜິວລາຍລະອຽດ. ຄ່າສີເທີົາຈະສ້າງການປະສົມທີ່ນຸ້ມນວນລະຫວ່າງທັງສອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:614
msgid ""
"Add: Adds pixel values of one Texture with the other. Unlike mix mode both "
"textures are completely mixed at white parts of a mask and not at gray "
"parts. The original texture is mostly unchanged at black"
msgstr ""
"Add: ບວກຄ່າພິກເຊວຂອງພື້ນຜິວໜຶ່ງເຂົ້າກັບອີກອັນໜຶ່ງ. ຕ່າງຈາກໂໝດ mix, ທັງສອງພື້ນຜິວຈະຖືກປະສົມເຂົ້າກັນທັງໝົ"
"ດໃນສ່ວນສີຂາວຂອງ mask ແລະ ບໍ່ປະສົມໃນສ່ວນສີເທີົາ. ພື້ນຜິວເດີມຈະເກືອບບໍ່ປ່ຽນແປງໃນສ່ວນສີດຳ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:618
msgid ""
"Sub: Subtracts pixel values of one texture with the other. The second "
"texture is completely subtracted at white parts of a mask with only a little "
"subtraction in black parts, gray parts being different levels of subtraction "
"based on the exact texture."
msgstr ""
"Sub: ລົບຄ່າພິກເຊວຂອງພື້ນຜິວໜຶ່ງອອກຈາກອີກອັນໜຶ່ງ. ພື້ນຜິວທີສອງຈະຖືກລົບອອກທັງໝົດໃນສ່ວນສີຂາວຂອງ mask ແ"
"ລະ ລົບອອກພຽງເລັກນ້ອຍໃນສ່ວນສີດຳ, ສ່ວນສີເທີົາຈະມີລະດັບການລົບທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນໄປຕາມລັກສະນະຂອງພື້ນຜິວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:623
msgid ""
"Mul: Multiplies the RGB channel numbers for each pixel from the top texture "
"with the values for the corresponding pixel from the bottom texture."
msgstr ""
"Mul: ຄູນຄ່າຊ່ອງ RGB ຂອງແຕ່ລະພິກເຊວຈາກພື້ນຜິວເທິງ ເຂົ້າກັບຄ່າພິກເຊວທີ່ກົງກັນຈາກພື້ນຜິວລຸ່ມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:626
msgid ""
"Albedo: This is where you put an albedo texture you want to blend. If "
"nothing is in this slot it will be interpreted as white by default."
msgstr ""
"Albedo: ແມ່ນບ່ອນທີ່ເຈົ້າໃສ່ພື້ນຜິວ albedo ທີ່ຕ້ອງການປະສົມ. ຖ້າບໍ່ມີຫຍັງຢູ່ໃນຊ່ອງນີ້ ມັນຈະຖືກກຳນົດໃຫ້ເປັນສີຂ"
"າວໂດຍຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:629
msgid ""
"Normal: This is where you put a normal texture you want to blend. If nothing "
"is in this slot it will be interpreted as a flat normal map. This can still "
"be used even if the material does not have normal map enabled."
msgstr ""
"Normal: ແມ່ນບ່ອນທີ່ເຈົ້າໃສ່ພື້ນຜິວ normal ທີ່ຕ້ອງການປະສົມ. ຖ້າບໍ່ມີຫຍັງຢູ່ໃນຊ່ອງນີ້ ມັນຈະຖືກກຳນົດໃຫ້ເປັນ "
"normal map ແບບຮາບພຽງ. ສ່ວນນີ້ຍັງສາມາດໃຊ້ໄດ້ເຖິງວ່າວັດສະດຸຈະບໍ່ໄດ້ເປີດໃຊ້ normal map ກໍຕາມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:634
msgid "UV1 and UV2"
msgstr "UV1 ແລະ UV2"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:636
msgid ""
"Godot supports two UV channels per material. Secondary UV is often useful "
"for ambient occlusion or emission (baked light). UVs can be scaled and "
"offset, which is useful when using repeating textures."
msgstr ""
"Godot ຮອງຮັບສອງຊ່ອງ UV ຕໍ່ໜຶ່ງວັດສະດຸ. UV ສໍາຮອງມັກຈະມີປະໂຫຍດສຳລັບ ambient occlusion ຫຼື "
"emission (ແສງທີ່ຖືກ bake ມາ). UV ສາມາດປັບຂະໜາດ (scale) ແລະ ຕຳແໜ່ງ (offset) ໄດ້, ເຊິ່ງ"
"ມີປະໂຫຍດຫຼາຍເມື່ອໃຊ້ພື້ນຜິວທີ່ມີການວາງຊ້ຳ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:643
msgid "Triplanar Mapping"
msgstr "Triplanar Mapping"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:645
msgid ""
"Triplanar mapping is supported for both UV1 and UV2. This is an alternative "
"way to obtain texture coordinates, sometimes called \"Autotexture\". "
"Textures are sampled in X, Y and Z and blended by the normal. Triplanar "
"mapping can be performed in either world space or object space."
msgstr ""
"Triplanar mapping ຮອງຮັບທັງ UV1 ແລະ UV2. ນີ້ແມ່ນວິທີທາງເລືອກໃນການສ້າງພິກັດພື້ນຜິວ, ບາງຄັ້ງເອີ້ນ"
"ວ່າ \"Autotexture\". ພື້ນຜິວຈະຖືກສຸ່ມຕົວຢ່າງໃນແກນ X, Y ແລະ Z ແລ້ວປະສົມເຂົ້າກັນດ້ວຍ normal. "
"Triplanar mapping ສາມາດເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ທັງໃນ world space ຫຼື object space."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:650
msgid ""
"In the image below, you can see how all primitives share the same material "
"with world triplanar, so the brick texture continues smoothly between them."
msgstr ""
"ໃນຮູບລຸ່ມນີ້, ເຈົ້າຈະເຫັນວ່າທຸກ primitives ໃຊ້ວັດສະດຸດຽວກັນກັບ world triplanar, ເຮັດໃຫ້ພື້ນຜິວຮູບດິ"
"ນຈີ່ມີຄວາມຕໍ່ເນື່ອງກັນຢ່າງນຸ້ມນວນລະຫວ່າງພວກມັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:656
msgid "World Triplanar"
msgstr "World Triplanar"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:658
msgid ""
"When using triplanar mapping, it is computed in object local space. This "
"option makes it use world space instead."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອໃຊ້ triplanar mapping, ປົກກະຕິມັນຈະຖືກຄິດໄລ່ໃນ object local space. ແຕ່ຕົວເລືອກນີ້ຈະເຮັດ"
"ໃຫ້ມັນໃຊ້ world space ແທນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:664
msgid "Sampling"
msgstr "ການສຸ່ມຕົວຢ່າງ (Sampling)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:667
#: ../../docs/tutorials/audio/audio_effects.rst:180
msgid "Filter"
msgstr "ຟິວເຕີ (Filter)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:669
msgid ""
"The filtering method for the textures used by the material. See :ref:`this "
"page<class_BaseMaterial3D_property_texture_filter>` for a full list of "
"options and their description."
msgstr ""
"ວິທີການກັ່ນຕອງ (filtering) ສຳລັບພື້ນຜິວທີ່ວັດສະດຸໃຊ້. ເບິ່ງ :ref:`ໜ້າ"
"ນີ້<class_BaseMaterial3D_property_texture_filter>` ສຳລັບລາຍການຕົວເລືອກທັງໝົດ ແລະ ຄຳອ"
"ະທິບາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:673
msgid "Repeat"
msgstr "ການວາງຊ້ຳ (Repeat)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:675
msgid ""
"if the textures used by the material repeat, and how they repeat. "
"See :ref:`this page<class_BaseMaterial3D_property_texture_repeat>` for a "
"full list of options and their description."
msgstr ""
"ກຳນົດວ່າພື້ນຜິວທີ່ວັດສະດຸໃຊ້ຈະມີການວາງຊ້ຳຫຼືບໍ່ ແລະ ຈະຊ້ຳແນວໃດ. ເບິ່ງ :ref:`ໜ້າ"
"ນີ້<class_BaseMaterial3D_property_texture_repeat>` ສຳລັບລາຍການຕົວເລືອກທັງໝົດ ແລະ ຄຳອ"
"ະທິບາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:679
msgid "Shadows"
msgstr "ເງົາ (Shadows)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:682
msgid "Disable Receive Shadows"
msgstr "ປິດການຮັບເງົາ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:684
msgid ""
"Makes the object not receive any kind of shadow that would otherwise be cast "
"onto it."
msgstr "ເຮັດໃຫ້ວັດຖຸບໍ່ຮັບເງົາທຸກຊະນິດທີ່ຈະມາຕົກກະທົບໃສ່ມັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:688
msgid "Shadow to Opacity"
msgstr "Shadow to Opacity"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:690
#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/spatial_shader.rst:88
msgid ""
"Lighting modifies the alpha so shadowed areas are opaque and non-shadowed "
"areas are transparent. Useful for overlaying shadows onto a camera feed in "
"AR."
msgstr ""
"ການໃຫ້ແສງຈະໄປປັບຄ່າ alpha ເຮັດໃຫ້ສ່ວນທີ່ເປັນເງົາມີຄວາມທຶບແສງ ແລະ ສ່ວນທີ່ບໍ່ມີເງົາມີຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ. ມີປະ"
"ໂຫຍດໃນການວາງເງົາທັບລົງໃນພາບຈາກກ້ອງໃນລະບົບ AR."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:694
msgid "Billboard"
msgstr "Billboard"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:697
msgid "Billboard Mode"
msgstr "ໂໝດ Billboard"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:699
msgid ""
"Enables billboard mode for drawing materials. This controls how the object "
"faces the camera:"
msgstr ""
"ເປີດໃຊ້ໂໝດ billboard ສຳລັບວັດສະດຸ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຄວບຄຸມວິທີທີ່ວັດຖຸຈະຫັນໜ້າໄປຫາກ້ອງ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:702
msgid "**Disabled:** Billboard mode is disabled."
msgstr "**Disabled:** ປິດໃຊ້ໂໝດ Billboard."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:703
msgid ""
"**Enabled:** Billboard mode is enabled. The object's -Z axis will always "
"face the camera's viewing plane."
msgstr ""
"**Enabled:** ເປີດໃຊ້ໂໝດ Billboard. ແກນ -Z ຂອງວັດຖຸຈະຫັນໜ້າໄປຫາລະນາບການເບິ່ງຂອງກ້ອງສະເ"
"ໝີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:705
msgid ""
"**Y-Billboard:** The object's X axis will always be aligned with the "
"camera's viewing plane."
msgstr ""
"**Y-Billboard:** ແກນ X ຂອງວັດຖຸຈະຢູ່ໃນແນວດຽວກັບລະນາບການເບິ່ງຂອງກ້ອງສະເໝີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:706
msgid ""
"**Particle Billboard:** Most suited for particle systems, because it allows "
"specifying :ref:`flipbook animation "
"<doc_process_material_properties_animation>`."
msgstr ""
"**Particle Billboard:** ເໝາະສົມທີ່ສຸດສຳລັບລະບົບພາກທິເຄິນ (particle systems), ເພາະມັນອະ"
"ນຸຍາດໃຫ້ກຳນົດ :ref:`flipbook animation "
"<doc_process_material_properties_animation>` ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:711
msgid ""
"The **Particles Anim** section is only visible when the billboard mode is "
"**Particle Billboard**."
msgstr ""
"ສ່ວນ **Particles Anim** ຈະປາກົດໃຫ້ເຫັນກໍຕໍ່ເມື່ອໂໝດ billboard ຖືກຕັ້ງເປັນ **Particle "
"Billboard**."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:714
msgid "Billboard Keep Scale"
msgstr "Billboard Keep Scale"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:716
msgid "Enables scaling a mesh in billboard mode."
msgstr "ອະນຸຍາດໃຫ້ປັບຂະໜາດ (scale) ຂອງ mesh ໃນໂໝດ billboard."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:721
msgid "Grow"
msgstr "ການຂະຫຍາຍຕົວ (Grow)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:723
msgid "Grows the object vertices in the direction pointed by their normals:"
msgstr "ຂະຫຍາຍຈຸດ vertex ຂອງວັດຖຸໄປຕາມທິດທາງຂອງ normal ຂອງພວກມັນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:727
msgid ""
"This is commonly used to create cheap outlines. Add a second material pass, "
"make it black and unshaded, reverse culling (Cull Front), and add some grow:"
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງນີ້ມັກຖືກໃຊ້ເພື່ອສ້າງຂອບ (outlines) ແບບປະຢັດຊັບພະຍາກອນ. ໂດຍການເພີ່ມ material pass ທີສອ"
"ງ, ເຮັດໃຫ້ເປັນສີດຳ ແລະ ບໍ່ມີແສງ (unshaded), ກັບຄືນການຄັດອອກ (Cull Front), ແລະ ເພີ່ມຄ່າ "
"grow ໜ້ອຍໜຶ່ງ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:734
msgid ""
"For Grow to work as expected, the mesh must have connected faces with shared "
"vertices, or \"smooth shading\". If the mesh has disconnected faces with "
"unique vertices, or \"flat shading\", the mesh will appear to have gaps when "
"using Grow."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອໃຫ້ Grow ເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ຕາມທີ່ຄາດໄວ້, mesh ຕ້ອງມີພື້ນຜິວທີ່ເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ກັນດ້ວຍ vertex ດຽວກັນ, ຫຼື ໃຊ້ "
"\"smooth shading\". ຖ້າ mesh ມີພື້ນຜິວທີ່ແຍກກັນດ້ວຍ vertex ສະເພາະ, ຫຼື ໃຊ້ \"flat "
"shading\", mesh ຈະປາກົດໃຫ້ເຫັນເປັນຊ່ອງວ່າງເມື່ອໃຊ້ Grow."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:738
msgid ""
"Note that in Godot 4.5 onwards, stencil buffer-based outlines are available "
"using the **Outline** :ref:`stencil mode "
"<doc_standard_material_3d_stencil>`. This can be used as an alternative to "
"Grow for outlines."
msgstr ""
"ໝາຍເຫດ: ຕັ້ງແຕ່ Godot 4.5 ເປັນຕົ້ນໄປ, ສາມາດໃຊ້ການສ້າງຂອບດ້ວຍ stencil buffer ຜ່ານ "
":ref:`stencil mode <doc_standard_material_3d_stencil>` **Outline**. ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດໃ"
"ຊ້ເປັນທາງເລືອກແທນ Grow ສຳລັບການສ້າງຂອບໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:746
msgid "Fixed Size"
msgstr "Fixed Size (ຂະໜາດຄົງທີ່)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:748
msgid ""
"This causes the object to be rendered at the same size no matter the "
"distance. This is useful mostly for indicators (no depth test and high "
"render priority) and some types of billboards."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງນີ້ເຮັດໃຫ້ວັດຖຸຖືກສະແດງຜົນໃນຂະໜາດດຽວກັນສະເໝີ ບໍ່ວ່າຈະຢູ່ໄກປານໃດກໍຕາມ. ສ່ວນຫຼາຍແມ່ນມີປະໂຫຍດສຳລັບເ"
"ຄື່ອງໝາຍບອກຕຳແໜ່ງ (ທີ່ບໍ່ມີ depth test ແລະ ມີ render priority ສູງ) ແລະ billboard ບາງປະເ"
"ພດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:753
msgid "Use Point Size"
msgstr "ໃຊ້ Point Size"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:755
msgid ""
"This option is only effective when the geometry rendered is made of points "
"(generally it's made of triangles when imported from 3D modeling software). "
"If so, then those points can be resized (see below)."
msgstr ""
"ຕົວເລືອກນີ້ຈະມີຜົນກໍຕໍ່ເມື່ອ geometry ທີ່ສະແດງຜົນຖືກສ້າງຂຶ້ນຈາກຈຸດ (point) (ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປແລ້ວມັນຈະຖືກສ້າງຂຶ້"
"ນຈາກຮູບສາມແຈເມື່ອນຳເຂົ້າຈາກຊອບແວສ້າງແບບຈຳລອງ 3D). ຖ້າເປັນແບບນັ້ນ, ຈຸດເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນຈະສາມາດປັບຂະໜາດ"
"ໄດ້ (ເບິ່ງລຸ່ມນີ້)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:760
msgid "Point Size"
msgstr "Point Size"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:762
msgid "When drawing points, specify the point size in pixels."
msgstr "ເມື່ອແຕ້ມຈຸດ, ໃຫ້ກຳນົດຂະໜາດຂອງຈຸດເປັນພິກເຊວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:765
msgid "Use Particle Trails"
msgstr "ໃຊ້ Particle Trails"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:770
msgid ""
"If true, enables parts of the shader required for GPUParticles3D trails to "
"function. This also requires using a mesh with appropriate skinning, such as "
"RibbonTrailMesh or TubeTrailMesh. Enabling this feature outside of materials "
"used in GPUParticles3D meshes will break material rendering."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເລືອກເປັນ true, ຈະເປີດໃຊ້ສ່ວນຂອງ shader ທີ່ຈຳເປັນສຳລັບໃຫ້ GPUParticles3D trails ເຮັດວຽ"
"ກໄດ້. ສິ່ງນີ້ຍັງຕ້ອງໃຊ້ mesh ທີ່ມີການ skinning ທີ່ເໝາະສົມ ເຊັ່ນ: RibbonTrailMesh ຫຼື "
"TubeTrailMesh. ການເປີດໃຊ້ຄຸນສົມບັດນີ້ກັບວັດສະດຸທີ່ບໍ່ໄດ້ໃຊ້ໃນ GPUParticles3D meshes ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ກາ"
"ນສະແດງຜົນວັດສະດຸຜິດພາດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:776
msgid "Use Z Clip Scale"
msgstr "ໃຊ້ Z Clip Scale"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:778
msgid ""
"Scales the object being rendered towards the camera to avoid clipping into "
"things like walls. This is intended to be used for objects that are fixed "
"with respect to the camera like player arms, tools, etc. Lighting and "
"shadows will continue to work correctly when this setting is adjusted, but "
"screen-space effects like SSAO and SSR may break with lower scales. "
"Therefore, try to keep this setting as close to 1.0 as possible."
msgstr ""
"ປັບຂະໜາດວັດຖຸທີ່ກຳລັງສະແດງຜົນໃຫ້ເຂົ້າມາຫາກ້ອງ ເພື່ອຫຼີກລ່ຽງການທະລຸ (clipping) ເຂົ້າໄປໃນສິ່ງຂອງຕ່າງ"
"ໆ ເຊັ່ນ ຝາ. ສິ່ງນີ້ອອກແບບມາເພື່ອໃຊ້ກັບວັດຖຸທີ່ຄົງທີ່ເມື່ອທຽບກັບກ້ອງ ເຊັ່ນ: ແຂນຂອງຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນ, ເຄື່ອງມື ແລະ ອື່ນ"
"ໆ. ແສງ ແລະ ເງົາຈະຍັງເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ຢ່າງຖືກຕ້ອງເມື່ອປັບການຕັ້ງຄ່ານີ້, ແຕ່ເອັບເຟັກແບບ screen-space ເຊັ່"
"ນ SSAO ແລະ SSR ອາດຈະຜິດພາດເມື່ອໃຊ້ scale ທີ່ຕໍ່າ. ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ພະຍາຍາມຮັກສາຄ່ານີ້ໃຫ້ໃກ້ຄຽງກັບ 1.0 ຫຼ"
"າຍທີ່ສຸດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:786
msgid "Use FOV Override"
msgstr "ໃຊ້ FOV Override"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:788
msgid "Overrides the ``Camera3D``'s field of view angle (in degrees)."
msgstr ""
"ຂ້າມຄ່າ (Override) ມຸມເບິ່ງ (field of view) ຂອງ ``Camera3D`` (ເປັນອົງສາ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:792
msgid ""
"This behaves as if the field of view is set on a ``Camera3D`` with "
"``Camera3D.keep_aspect`` set to ``Camera3D.KEEP_HEIGHT``. Additionally, it "
"may not look correct on a non-perspective camera where the field of view "
"setting is ignored."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະເຮັດວຽກຄືກັບວ່າຄ່າ field of view ຖືກຕັ້ງໄວ້ໃນ ``Camera3D`` ໂດຍທີ່ "
"``Camera3D.keep_aspect`` ຖືກຕັ້ງເປັນ ``Camera3D.KEEP_HEIGHT``. ນອກຈາກນັ້ນ, ມັນອາດຈະເ"
"ບິ່ງບໍ່ຖືກຕ້ອງໃນກ້ອງທີ່ບໍ່ແມ່ນ perspective ເຊິ່ງຄ່າ field of view ຈະຖືກລະເລີຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:798
msgid "Proximity and Distance Fade"
msgstr "Proximity ແລະ Distance Fade"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:800
msgid ""
"Godot allows materials to fade by proximity to each other as well as "
"depending on the distance from the viewer. Proximity fade is useful for "
"effects such as soft particles or a mass of water with a smooth blending to "
"the shores."
msgstr ""
"Godot ອະນຸຍາດໃຫ້ວັດສະດຸຄ່ອຍໆຈາງຫາຍໄປ (fade) ຕາມຄວາມໃກ້ຊິດລະຫວ່າງກັນ ແລະ ຕາມໄລຍະຫ່າງຈາກຜູ້"
"ເບິ່ງ. Proximity fade ມີປະໂຫຍດສຳລັບເອັບເຟັກ ເຊັ່ນ: ພາກທິເຄິນທີ່ນຸ້ມນວນ (soft particles) ຫຼື ມ"
"ວນນ້ຳທີ່ມີການປະສົມປະສານຢ່າງນຸ້ມນວນເຂົ້າກັບຊາຍຝັ່ງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:806
msgid ""
"Distance fade is useful for light shafts or indicators that are only present "
"after a given distance."
msgstr ""
"Distance fade ມີປະໂຫຍດສຳລັບລຳແສງ ຫຼື ເຄື່ອງໝາຍບອກຕຳແໜ່ງທີ່ຈະປາກົດໃຫ້ເຫັນຫຼັງຈາກໄລຍະຫ່າງທີ່ກຳນົດ"
"ເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:809
msgid ""
"Keep in mind enabling proximity fade or distance fade with **Pixel Alpha** "
"mode enables alpha blending. Alpha blending is more GPU-intensive and can "
"cause transparency sorting issues. Alpha blending also disables many "
"material features such as the ability to cast shadows."
msgstr ""
"ຈົ່ງຈື່ໄວ້ວ່າການເປີດໃຊ້ proximity fade ຫຼື distance fade ດ້ວຍໂໝດ **Pixel Alpha** ຈະເປັນກາ"
"ນເປີດໃຊ້ alpha blending. Alpha blending ຈະໃຊ້ GPU ຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນ ແລະ ອາດເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດບັນຫາການຈັດ"
"ລຽງຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ. ນອກຈາກນັ້ນ Alpha blending ຍັງປິດໃຊ້ງານຄຸນສົມບັດຂອງວັດສະດຸຫຼາຍຢ່າງ ເຊັ່ນ ຄວາມສ"
"າມາດໃນການສ້າງເງົາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:816
msgid ""
"To hide a character when they get too close to the camera, consider using "
"**Pixel Dither** or better, **Object Dither** (which is even faster than "
"**Pixel Dither**)."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອເຊື່ອງຕົວລະຄອນເມື່ອພວກເຂົາເຂົ້າໃກ້ກ້ອງເກີນໄປ, ໃຫ້ພິຈາລະນາໃຊ້ **Pixel Dither** ຫຼື ໃຫ້ດີກວ່ານັ້ນ"
"ຄື **Object Dither** (ເຊິ່ງເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ໄວກວ່າ **Pixel Dither**)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:820
msgid ""
"**Pixel Alpha** mode: The actual transparency of a pixel of the object "
"changes with distance to the camera. This is the most effect, but forces the "
"material into the transparency pipeline (which leads, for example, to no "
"shadows)."
msgstr ""
"ໂໝດ **Pixel Alpha**: ຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສຕົວຈິງຂອງພິກເຊວວັດຖຸຈະປ່ຽນແປງຕາມໄລຍະຫ່າງຈາກກ້ອງ. ນີ້ແມ່ນວິທີ"
"ທີ່ໃຫ້ຜົນດີທີ່ສຸດ, ແຕ່ຈະບັງຄັບໃຫ້ວັດສະດຸເຂົ້າສູ່ transparency pipeline (ເຊິ່ງເຮັດໃຫ້ ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ ບໍ່ມີເງົ"
"າ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:826
msgid ""
"**Pixel Dither** mode: What this does is sort of approximate the "
"transparency by only having a fraction of the pixels rendered."
msgstr ""
"ໂໝດ **Pixel Dither**: ສິ່ງທີ່ມັນເຮັດຄືການປະມານຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສໂດຍການສະແດງຜົນພຽງແຕ່ບາງສ່ວນຂອງພິກ"
"ເຊວເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:831
msgid ""
"**Object Dither** mode: Like the previous mode, but the calculated "
"transparency is the same across the entire object's surface."
msgstr ""
"ໂໝດ **Object Dither**: ຄ້າຍຄືກັບໂໝດກ່ອນໜ້ານີ້, ແຕ່ຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສທີ່ຄິດໄລ່ໄດ້ຈະຄືກັນຕະຫຼອດທົ່ວພື້ນຜິວຂອງ"
"ວັດຖຸ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:839
msgid "Stencil"
msgstr "Stencil"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:841
msgid ""
"Since Godot 4.5, Godot allows materials to make use of the stencil buffer. "
"This feature is commonly used to create outlines and X-ray effects, which "
"can be useful to highlight objects, especially behind walls."
msgstr ""
"ຕັ້ງແຕ່ Godot 4.5, Godot ອະນຸຍາດໃຫ້ວັດສະດຸໃຊ້ງານ stencil buffer ໄດ້. ຄຸນສົມບັດນີ້ມັກຖືກໃຊ້ເພື່ອສ້"
"າງຂອບ (outlines) ແລະ ເອັບເຟັກ X-ray, ເຊິ່ງມີປະໂຫຍດໃນການເນັ້ນວັດຖຸ ໂດຍສະເພາະວັດຖຸທີ່ຢູ່ຫຼັງຝາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:845
msgid ""
"The **Outline** and **X-Ray** modes assign a preconfigured stencil material "
"in the material's **Next Pass** property. The **Custom** mode can be used "
"for advanced effects."
msgstr ""
"ໂໝດ **Outline** ແລະ **X-Ray** ຈະກຳນົດວັດສະດຸ stencil ທີ່ຕັ້ງຄ່າໄວ້ລ່ວງໜ້າໃນຄຸນສົມບັດ "
"**Next Pass** ຂອງວັດສະດຸ. ສ່ວນໂໝດ **Custom** ສາມາດໃຊ້ສຳລັບເອັບເຟັກລະດັບສູງໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:851
msgid ""
"Materials that write to the stencil buffer are always drawn in the "
"transparent pass, so they are subject to the usual :ref:`transparency "
"limitations <doc_3d_rendering_limitations_transparency_sorting>`."
msgstr ""
"ວັດສະດຸທີ່ຂຽນລົງໃນ stencil buffer ຈະຖືກແຕ້ມໃນ transparent pass ສະເໝີ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນພວກມັນຈຶ່ງຢູ່ພາຍ"
"ໃຕ້ :ref:`ຂໍ້ຈຳກັດຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ <doc_3d_rendering_limitations_transparency_sorting>` "
"ປົກກະຕິ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:857
msgid ""
"Like with the :ref:`Grow property <ref_standard_material_3d_grow>`, for the "
"stencil outline to work as expected, the mesh must have connected faces with "
"shared vertices, or \"smooth shading\". If the mesh has disconnected faces "
"with unique vertices, or \"flat shading\", the mesh will appear to have gaps "
"when using a stencil outline."
msgstr ""
"ເຊັ່ນດຽວກັບ :ref:`ຄຸນສົມບັດ Grow <ref_standard_material_3d_grow>`, ເພື່ອໃຫ້ stencil "
"outline ເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ຕາມທີ່ຄາດໄວ້, mesh ຕ້ອງມີພື້ນຜິວທີ່ເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ກັນດ້ວຍ vertex ດຽວກັນ, ຫຼື ໃຊ້ "
"\"smooth shading\". ຖ້າ mesh ມີພື້ນຜິວທີ່ແຍກກັນດ້ວຍ vertex ສະເພາະ, ຫຼື ໃຊ້ \"flat "
"shading\", mesh ຈະປາກົດໃຫ້ເຫັນເປັນຊ່ອງວ່າງເມື່ອໃຊ້ stencil outline."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:863
msgid ""
"Stencil outlines render similarly to the Grow property, but won't look "
"identical in every scenario, especially when intersections with opaque "
"surfaces are involved."
msgstr ""
"Stencil outlines ຈະສະແດງຜົນຄ້າຍຄືກັບຄຸນສົມບັດ Grow, ແຕ່ຈະບໍ່ເບິ່ງຄືກັນໃນທຸກສະຖານະການ, ໂດຍສະເ"
"ພາະເມື່ອມີການຕັດກັນກັບພື້ນຜິວທີ່ທຶບແສງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:867
msgid "Material Settings"
msgstr "ການຕັ້ງຄ່າວັດສະດຸ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:870
msgid "Render priority"
msgstr "Render priority (ລຳດັບການສະແດງຜົນ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:872
msgid ""
"The rendering order of objects can be changed, although this is mostly "
"useful for transparent objects (or opaque objects that perform depth draw "
"but no color draw, such as cracks on the floor)."
msgstr ""
"ລຳດັບການສະແດງຜົນຂອງວັດຖຸສາມາດປ່ຽນແປງໄດ້, ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າມັນຈະມີປະໂຫຍດຫຼາຍທີ່ສຸດສຳລັບວັດຖຸໂປ່ງໃສ (ຫຼື ວັ"
"ດຖຸທຶບແສງທີ່ເຮັດການ depth draw ແຕ່ບໍ່ມີ color draw ເຊັ່ນ ຮອຍແຕກເທິງພື້ນ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:876
msgid ""
"Objects are sorted by an opaque/transparent queue, "
"then :ref:`render_priority<class_Material_property_render_priority>`, with "
"higher priority being drawn later. Transparent objects are also sorted by "
"depth."
msgstr ""
"ວັດຖຸຈະຖືກຈັດລຽງຕາມຄິວ opaque/transparent, ຈາກນັ້ນແມ່ນ "
":ref:`render_priority<class_Material_property_render_priority>`, ໂດຍຄ່າ "
"priority ທີ່ສູງກວ່າຈະຖືກແຕ້ມທີຫຼັງ. ວັດຖຸໂປ່ງໃສຍັງຖືກຈັດລຽງຕາມຄວາມເລິກ (depth) ນຳ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:879
msgid ""
"Depth testing overrules priority. Priority alone cannot force opaque objects "
"to be drawn over each other."
msgstr ""
"Depth testing ຈະມີອຳນາດເໜືອກວ່າ priority. ພຽງແຕ່ priority ຢ່າງດຽວບໍ່ສາມາດບັງຄັບໃຫ້ວັດຖຸທຶບ"
"ແສງ ແຕ້ມທັບກັນໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:882
msgid "Next Pass"
msgstr "Next Pass"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:884
msgid ""
"Setting :ref:`next_pass<class_Material_property_next_pass>` on a material "
"will cause an object to be rendered again with that next material."
msgstr ""
"ການຕັ້ງຄ່າ :ref:`next_pass<class_Material_property_next_pass>` ໃນວັດສະດຸ ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ວັດ"
"ຖຸ ຖືກສະແດງຜົນອີກຄັ້ງດ້ວຍວັດສະດຸຖັດໄປນັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:887
msgid ""
"Materials are sorted by an opaque/transparent queue, "
"then :ref:`render_priority<class_Material_property_render_priority>`, with "
"higher priority being drawn later."
msgstr ""
"ວັດສະດຸຈະຖືກຈັດລຽງຕາມຄິວ opaque/transparent, ຈາກນັ້ນແມ່ນ "
":ref:`render_priority<class_Material_property_render_priority>`, ໂດຍຄ່າ "
"priority ທີ່ສູງກວ່າຈະຖືກແຕ້ມທີຫຼັງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/standard_material_3d.rst:892
msgid ""
"Depth will test equal between both materials unless the grow setting or "
"other vertex transformations are used. Multiple transparent passes should "
"use :ref:`render_priority<class_Material_property_render_priority>` to "
"ensure correct ordering."
msgstr ""
"ຄ່າ Depth ຈະຖືກທົດສອບໃຫ້ເທົ່າກັນລະຫວ່າງທັງສອງວັດສະດຸ ນອກຈາກວ່າຈະມີການໃຊ້ການຕັ້ງຄ່າ grow ຫຼື ການແ"
"ປງ vertex ອື່ນໆ. ການໃຊ້ transparent passes ຫຼາຍອັນຄວນໃຊ້ "
":ref:`render_priority<class_Material_property_render_priority>` ເພື່ອໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າລຳ"
"ດັບຖືກຕ້ອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:4
msgid "3D lights and shadows"
msgstr "ແສງ ແລະ ເງົາ 3D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:9
msgid ""
"Light sources emit light that mixes with the materials and produces a "
"visible result. Light can come from several types of sources in a scene:"
msgstr ""
"ແຫຼ່ງກຳເນີດແສງຈະປ່ອຍແສງທີ່ໄປປະສົມກັບວັດສະດຸ ແລະ ສ້າງຜົນລັບທີ່ເບິ່ງເຫັນໄດ້. ແສງສາມາດມາຈາກ ແຫຼ່ງກຳເນີ"
"ດຫຼາຍປະເພດໃນສາກ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:12
msgid ""
"From the material itself, in the form of the emission color (though it does "
"not affect nearby objects unless baked or screen-space indirect lighting is "
"enabled)."
msgstr ""
"ຈາກຕົວວັດສະດຸເອງ, ໃນຮູບແບບຂອງສີ emission (ເຖິງວ່າມັນຈະບໍ່ມີຜົນຕໍ່ວັດຖຸໃກ້ຄຽງ ນອກຈາກວ່າຈະມີການ "
"bake ຫຼື ເປີດໃຊ້ screen-space indirect lighting)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:14
msgid "Light nodes: DirectionalLight3D, OmniLight3D and SpotLight3D."
msgstr "ໂນດແສງ (Light nodes): DirectionalLight3D, OmniLight3D ແລະ SpotLight3D."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:15
msgid ""
"Ambient light in the :ref:`Environment <class_Environment>` "
"or :ref:`doc_reflection_probes`."
msgstr ""
"ແສງສະພາບແວດລ້ອມ (Ambient light) ໃນ :ref:`Environment <class_Environment>` ຫຼື "
":ref:`doc_reflection_probes`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:17
msgid ""
"Global illumination (:ref:`LightmapGI "
"<doc_using_lightmap_gi>`, :ref:`VoxelGI <doc_using_voxel_gi>` or :ref:`SDFGI "
"<doc_using_sdfgi>`)."
msgstr ""
"ການໃຫ້ແສງທົ່ວໂລກ (Global illumination): (:ref:`LightmapGI "
"<doc_using_lightmap_gi>`, :ref:`VoxelGI <doc_using_voxel_gi>` ຫຼື :ref:`SDFGI "
"<doc_using_sdfgi>`)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:20
msgid ""
"The emission color is a material property. You can read more about it in "
"the :ref:`doc_standard_material_3d` tutorial."
msgstr ""
"ສີ emission ແມ່ນຄຸນສົມບັດຂອງວັດສະດຸ. ເຈົ້າສາມາດອ່ານເພີ່ມເຕີມໄດ້ໃນບົດຮຽນ "
":ref:`doc_standard_material_3d`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:25
msgid ""
"You can compare various types of lights in action using the `3D Lights and "
"Shadows demo project <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/"
"tree/master/3d/lights_and_shadows>`__."
msgstr ""
"ເຈົ້າສາມາດປຽບທຽບແສງປະເພດຕ່າງໆໃນການເຮັດວຽກຕົວຈິງໄດ້ໂດຍໃຊ້ `3D Lights and Shadows demo "
"project <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/3d/"
"lights_and_shadows>`__."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:29
msgid "Light nodes"
msgstr "ໂນດແສງ (Light nodes)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:31
msgid ""
"There are three types of light "
"nodes: :ref:`class_DirectionalLight3D`, :ref:`class_OmniLight3D` "
"and :ref:`class_SpotLight3D`. Let's take a look at the common parameters for "
"lights:"
msgstr ""
"ໂນດແສງມີ 3 ປະເພດຄື: :ref:`class_DirectionalLight3D`, :ref:`class_OmniLight3D` ແ"
"ລະ :ref:`class_SpotLight3D`. ມາເບິ່ງພາລາມິເຕີທົ່ວໄປຂອງແສງ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:37
msgid "Each property has a specific function:"
msgstr "ແຕ່ລະຄຸນສົມບັດມີໜ້າທີ່ສະເພາະດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:39
msgid "**Color:** Base color for emitted light."
msgstr "**Color:** ສີພື້ນຖານຂອງແສງທີ່ປ່ອຍອອກມາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:40
msgid ""
"**Energy:** Energy multiplier. This is useful for saturating lights or "
"working with :ref:`doc_high_dynamic_range`."
msgstr ""
"**Energy:** ຕົວຄູນພະລັງງານ. ສິ່ງນີ້ມີປະໂຫຍດໃນການເຮັດໃຫ້ແສງອີ່ມຕົວ ຫຼື ເຮັດວຽກກັບ "
":ref:`doc_high_dynamic_range`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:41
msgid ""
"**Indirect Energy:** Secondary multiplier used with indirect light (light "
"bounces). This works with :ref:`doc_using_lightmap_gi`, VoxelGI or SDFGI."
msgstr ""
"**Indirect Energy:** ຕົວຄູນສໍາຮອງທີ່ໃຊ້ກັບແສງທາງອ້ອມ (ແສງສະທ້ອນ). ສິ່ງນີ້ເຮັດວຽກຮ່ວມກັບ "
":ref:`doc_using_lightmap_gi`, VoxelGI ຫຼື SDFGI."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:42
msgid ""
"**Volumetric Fog Energy:** Secondary multiplier used with volumetric fog. "
"This only has an effect when volumetric fog is enabled."
msgstr ""
"**Volumetric Fog Energy:** ຕົວຄູນສໍາຮອງທີ່ໃຊ້ກັບໝອກບໍລິມາດ (volumetric fog). ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະມີຜົນກໍ"
"ຕໍ່ເມື່ອເປີດໃຊ້ volumetric fog ເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:43
msgid ""
"**Negative:** Light becomes subtractive instead of additive. It's sometimes "
"useful to manually compensate some dark corners."
msgstr ""
"**Negative:** ແສງຈະກາຍເປັນແບບລົບແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນແບບບວກ. ບາງຄັ້ງມັນມີປະໂຫຍດໃນການປັບ ຊົດເຊີຍບາງ"
"ມຸມມືດດ້ວຍຕົວເອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:44
msgid ""
"**Specular:** Affects the intensity of the specular blob in objects affected "
"by this light. At zero, this light becomes a pure diffuse light."
msgstr ""
"**Specular:** ສົ່ງຜົນຕໍ່ຄວາມເຂັ້ມຂອງຈຸດສະທ້ອນ (specular blob) ໃນວັດຖຸທີ່ຖືກແສງນີ້ກະທົບ. ຖ້າຕັ້ງເປັ"
"ນສູນ, ແສງນີ້ຈະກາຍເປັນແສງແບບ diffuse ບໍລິສຸດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:45
msgid ""
"**Bake Mode:** Sets the bake mode for the light. "
"See :ref:`doc_using_lightmap_gi`."
msgstr ""
"**Bake Mode:** ກຳນົດໂໝດການ bake ສຳລັບແສງ. ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_using_lightmap_gi`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:46
msgid ""
"**Cull Mask:** Objects that are in the selected layers below will be "
"affected by this light. Note that objects disabled via this cull mask will "
"still cast shadows. If you don't want disabled objects to cast shadows, "
"adjust the **Cast Shadow** property on the GeometryInstance3D to the desired "
"value."
msgstr ""
"**Cull Mask:** ວັດຖຸທີ່ຢູ່ໃນເລເຢີ (layers) ທີ່ເລືອກຈະຖືກກະທົບໂດຍແສງນີ້. ໝາຍເຫດ: ວັດຖຸທີ່ຖືກປິດຜ່າ"
"ນ cull mask ນີ້ຈະຍັງຄົງສ້າງເງົາຢູ່. ຖ້າເຈົ້າບໍ່ຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ວັດຖຸທີ່ຖືກປິດ ສ້າງເງົາ, ໃຫ້ປັບຄຸນສົມບັດ **Cast "
"Shadow** ໃນ GeometryInstance3D ເປັນຄ່າທີ່ຕ້ອງການ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:53
msgid ""
"See :ref:`doc_physical_light_and_camera_units` if you wish to use real world "
"units to configure your lights' intensity and color temperature."
msgstr ""
"ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_physical_light_and_camera_units` ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການໃຊ້ຫົວໜ່ວຍໃນໂລກຕົວຈິງ ເພື່"
"ອຕັ້ງຄ່າຄວາມເຂັ້ມຂອງແສງ ແລະ ອຸນຫະພູມສີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:57
msgid "Light number limits"
msgstr "ຂໍ້ຈຳກັດຈຳນວນແສງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:59
msgid ""
"When using the Forward+ renderer, Godot uses a *clustering* approach for "
"real-time lighting. As many lights as desired can be added (as long as "
"performance allows). However, there's still a default limit of 512 "
"*clustered elements* that can be present in the current camera view. A "
"clustered element is an omni light, a spot light, a :ref:`decal "
"<doc_using_decals>` or a :ref:`reflection probe <doc_reflection_probes>`. "
"This limit can be increased by adjusting :ref:`Max Clustered "
"Elements<class_ProjectSettings_property_rendering/limits/cluster_builder/"
"max_clustered_elements>` in **Project Settings > Rendering > Limits > "
"Cluster Builder**."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອໃຊ້ Forward+ renderer, Godot ຈະໃຊ້ວິທີ *clustering* ສຳລັບການໃຫ້ແສງແບບ real-"
"time. ສາມາດເພີ່ມແສງໄດ້ຫຼາຍຕາມທີ່ຕ້ອງການ (ຕາບໃດທີ່ປະສິດທິພາບຍັງຮັບໄຫວ). ຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ຍັງມີ ຂີດຈຳ"
"ກັດເລີ່ມຕົ້ນຢູ່ທີ່ 512 *clustered elements* ທີ່ສາມາດປາກົດໃນມຸມມອງກ້ອງປັດຈຸບັນ. clustered "
"element ແມ່ນ omni light, spot light, :ref:`decal <doc_using_decals>` ຫຼື "
":ref:`reflection probe <doc_reflection_probes>`. ຂີດຈຳກັດນີ້ສາມາດເພີ່ມໄດ້ໂດຍການປັບ "
":ref:`Max Clustered Elements<class_ProjectSettings_property_rendering/limits/"
"cluster_builder/max_clustered_elements>` ໃນ **Project Settings > Rendering > "
"Limits > Cluster Builder**."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:68
msgid ""
"When using the Mobile renderer, there is a limitation of 8 OmniLights + 8 "
"SpotLights per mesh resource. There is also a limit of 256 OmniLights + 256 "
"SpotLights that can be rendered in the current camera view. These limits "
"currently cannot be changed."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອໃຊ້ Mobile renderer, ຈະມີຂໍ້ຈຳກັດຢູ່ທີ່ 8 OmniLights + 8 SpotLights ຕໍ່ໜຶ່ງຊັບພະຍາກອນ "
"mesh. ນອກຈາກນັ້ນຍັງມີຂໍ້ຈຳກັດ 256 OmniLights + 256 SpotLights ທີ່ສາມາດສະແດງຜົນໃນມຸມມອງກ້ອ"
"ງປັດຈຸບັນ. ຂໍ້ຈຳກັດເຫຼົ່ານີ້ໃນປັດຈຸບັນຍັງບໍ່ສາມາດປ່ຽນແປງໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:72
msgid ""
"When using the Compatibility renderer, up to 8 OmniLights + 8 SpotLights can "
"be rendered per mesh resource. This limit can be increased in the advanced "
"Project Settings by adjusting :ref:`Max Renderable "
"Elements<class_ProjectSettings_property_rendering/limits/opengl/"
"max_renderable_elements>` and/or :ref:`Max Lights per "
"Object<class_ProjectSettings_property_rendering/limits/opengl/"
"max_lights_per_object>` in **Rendering > Limits > OpenGL**, at the cost of "
"performance and longer shader compilation times. The limit can also be "
"decreased to reduce shader compilation times and improve performance "
"slightly."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອໃຊ້ Compatibility renderer, ສາມາດສະແດງຜົນໄດ້ສູງສຸດ 8 OmniLights + 8 SpotLights "
"ຕໍ່ mesh. ຂີດຈຳກັດນີ້ສາມາດເພີ່ມໄດ້ໃນການຕັ້ງຄ່າ Project Settings ລະດັບສູງ ໂດຍການປັບ "
":ref:`Max Renderable Elements<class_ProjectSettings_property_rendering/"
"limits/opengl/max_renderable_elements>` ແລະ/ຫຼື :ref:`Max Lights per "
"Object<class_ProjectSettings_property_rendering/limits/opengl/"
"max_lights_per_object>` ໃນ **Rendering > Limits > OpenGL**, ແຕ່ຈະຕ້ອງແລກດ້ວຍປະສິດ"
"ທິພາບ ແລະ ເວລາໃນການ compile shader ທີ່ດົນຂຶ້ນ. ຂີດຈຳກັດນີ້ຍັງສາມາດຫຼຸດລົງໄດ້ເພື່ອຫຼຸດເວລາ "
"compile shader ແລະ ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ປະສິດທິພາບດີຂຶ້ນເລັກນ້ອຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:81
msgid ""
"With all rendering methods, up to 8 DirectionalLights can be visible at a "
"time. However, each additional DirectionalLight with shadows enabled will "
"reduce the effective shadow resolution of each DirectionalLight. This is "
"because directional shadow atlas is shared between all lights."
msgstr ""
"ໃນທຸກວິທີການສະແດງຜົນ, ສາມາດເບິ່ງເຫັນ DirectionalLights ໄດ້ສູງສຸດ 8 ອັນໃນເວລາດຽວກັນ. ຢ່າງໃດ"
"ກໍຕາມ, ແຕ່ລະ DirectionalLight ທີ່ເພີ່ມເຂົ້າມາພ້ອມກັບເປີດໃຊ້ເງົາ ຈະໄປຫຼຸດຄວາມລະອຽດເງົາ ຂອງ "
"DirectionalLight ແຕ່ລະອັນລົງ. ນີ້ເປັນຍ້ອນວ່າ directional shadow atlas ຖືກໃຊ້ຮ່ວມກັນລະຫວ່າງ"
"ແສງທັງໝົດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:86
msgid ""
"If the rendering limit is exceeded, lights will start popping in and out "
"during camera movement, which can be distracting. Enabling **Distance Fade** "
"on light nodes can help reduce this issue while also improving performance. "
"Splitting your meshes into smaller portions can also help, especially for "
"level geometry (which also improves culling efficiency)."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເກີນຂີດຈຳກັດການສະແດງຜົນ, ແສງຈະເລີ່ມປາກົດ ແລະ ຫາຍໄປໃນລະຫວ່າງທີ່ກ້ອງເຄື່ອນໄຫວ, ເຊິ່ງອາດຈະລົບກ"
"ວນສາຍຕາ. ການເປີດໃຊ້ **Distance Fade** ໃນໂນດແສງສາມາດຊ່ວຍຫຼຸດບັນຫານີ້ ພ້ອມທັງປັບປຸງປະສິດທິພາບ"
"ນຳ. ການແບ່ງ mesh ຂອງທ່ານອອກເປັນສ່ວນນ້ອຍໆກໍສາມາດຊ່ວຍໄດ້, ໂດຍສະເພາະສຳລັບ geometry ຂອງສາ"
"ກ (ເຊິ່ງຍັງຊ່ວຍເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບການ culling)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:92
msgid ""
"If you need to render more lights than possible in a given renderer, "
"consider using :ref:`baked lightmaps <doc_using_lightmap_gi>` with lights' "
"bake mode set to **Static**. This allows lights to be fully baked, which "
"also makes them much faster to render. You can also use emissive materials "
"with any :ref:`global illumination "
"<doc_introduction_to_global_illumination>` technique as a replacement for "
"light nodes that emit light over a large area."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການສະແດງຜົນແສງຫຼາຍກວ່າທີ່ renderer ຈະຮັບໄຫວ, ໃຫ້ພິຈາລະນາໃຊ້ :ref:`baked "
"lightmaps <doc_using_lightmap_gi>` ໂດຍຕັ້ງ bake mode ຂອງແສງເປັນ **Static**. ສິ່ງນີ້ຊ່"
"ວຍໃຫ້ແສງຖືກ bake ທັງໝົດ, ເຊິ່ງເຮັດໃຫ້ສະແດງຜົນໄດ້ໄວຂຶ້ນຫຼາຍ. ເຈົ້າຍັງສາມາດໃຊ້ ວັດສະດຸແບບ "
"emissive ຮ່ວມກັບເຕັກນິກ :ref:`global illumination "
"<doc_introduction_to_global_illumination>` ໃດໜຶ່ງ ເພື່ອໃຊ້ແທນໂນດແສງທີ່ປ່ອຍແສງໄປທົ່ວພື້ນທີ່ກ"
"ວ້າງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:100
#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/internal_rendering_architecture.rst:525
msgid "Shadow mapping"
msgstr "ການເຮັດແຜນຜັງເງົາ (Shadow mapping)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:102
msgid ""
"Lights can optionally cast shadows. This gives them greater realism (light "
"does not reach occluded areas), but it can incur a bigger performance cost. "
"There is a list of generic shadow parameters, each also has a specific "
"function:"
msgstr ""
"ແສງສາມາດເລືອກໃຫ້ສ້າງເງົາໄດ້. ສິ່ງນີ້ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ມີຄວາມສົມຈິງຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນ (ແສງຈະບໍ່ໄປຮອດພື້ນທີ່ທີ່ຖືກບັງ), ແຕ່ມັນກໍຕ້ອ"
"ງແລກດ້ວຍການໃຊ້ຊັບພະຍາກອນທີ່ສູງຂຶ້ນ. ນີ້ແມ່ນລາຍການພາລາມິເຕີເງົາທົ່ວໄປ, ເຊິ່ງແຕ່ລະອັນມີໜ້າທີ່ສະເພາະດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:106
msgid "**Enabled:** Check to enable shadow mapping in this light."
msgstr "**Enabled:** ໝາຍເລືອກເພື່ອເປີດໃຊ້ shadow mapping ໃນແສງນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:107
msgid ""
"**Opacity:** Areas occluded are darkened by this opacity factor. Shadows are "
"fully opaque by default, but this can be changed to make shadows translucent "
"for a given light."
msgstr ""
"**Opacity:** ພື້ນທີ່ທີ່ຖືກບັງຈະຖືກເຮັດໃຫ້ມືດລົງດ້ວຍຄ່າ opacity ນີ້. ໂດຍປົກກະຕິເງົາຈະທຶບແສງ ທັງໝົດ, ແ"
"ຕ່ສາມາດປ່ຽນຄ່ານີ້ເພື່ອເຮັດໃຫ້ເງົາຂອງແສງນັ້ນໆມີຄວາມໂປ່ງແສງໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:110
msgid ""
"**Bias:** When this parameter is too low, self-shadowing occurs. When too "
"high, shadows separate from the casters. Tweak to what works best for you."
msgstr ""
"**Bias:** ຖ້າພາລາມິເຕີນີ້ຕໍ່າເກີນໄປ, ຈະເກີດເງົາທັບຕົວເອງ (self-shadowing). ຖ້າສູງເກີນໄປ, ເງົາ"
"ຈະແຍກອອກຈາກວັດຖຸທີ່ສ້າງເງົາ. ໃຫ້ປັບຄ່າທີ່ເໝາະສົມກັບວຽກຂອງທ່ານ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:112
msgid ""
"**Normal Bias:** When this parameter is too low, self-shadowing occurs. When "
"too high, shadows appear misaligned from the casters. Tweak to what works "
"best for you."
msgstr ""
"**Normal Bias:** ຖ້າພາລາມິເຕີນີ້ຕໍ່າເກີນໄປ, ຈະເກີດເງົາທັບຕົວເອງ. ຖ້າສູງເກີນໄປ, ເງົາຈະເບິ່ງຄືບໍ່ຕົງກັ"
"ບວັດຖຸທີ່ສ້າງເງົາ. ໃຫ້ປັບຄ່າທີ່ເໝາະສົມກັບວຽກຂອງທ່ານ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:114
msgid ""
"**Transmittance Bias:** When this parameter is too low, self-shadowing "
"occurs on materials that have transmittance enabled. When too high, shadows "
"will not affect materials that have transmittance enabled consistently. "
"Tweak to what works best for you."
msgstr ""
"**Transmittance Bias:** ຖ້າພາລາມິເຕີນີ້ຕໍ່າເກີນໄປ, ຈະເກີດເງົາທັບຕົວເອງໃນວັດສະດຸທີ່ເປີດໃຊ້ "
"transmittance. ຖ້າສູງເກີນໄປ, ເງົາຈະບໍ່ສົ່ງຜົນຕໍ່ວັດສະດຸທີ່ເປີດໃຊ້ transmittance ຢ່າງສະໝໍ່າສະເໝີ. ໃ"
"ຫ້ປັບຄ່າທີ່ເໝາະສົມກັບວຽກຂອງທ່ານ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:118
msgid ""
"**Reverse Cull Face:** Some scenes work better when shadow mapping is "
"rendered with face-culling inverted."
msgstr ""
"**Reverse Cull Face:** ບາງສາກຈະເບິ່ງດີກວ່າເມື່ອ shadow mapping ຖືກສະແດງຜົນ ໂດຍການກັບດ້າ"
"ນການຄັດອອກ (face-culling inverted)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:120
msgid ""
"**Blur:** Multiplies the shadow blur radius for this light. This works with "
"both traditional shadow mapping and contact-hardening shadows (lights with "
"**Angular Distance** or **Size** greater than ``0.0``). Higher values result "
"in softer shadows, which will also appear to be more temporally stable for "
"moving objects. The downside of increasing shadow blur is that it will make "
"the grainy pattern used for filtering more noticeable. See "
"also :ref:`doc_lights_and_shadows_shadow_filter_mode`."
msgstr ""
"**Blur:** ຄູນລັດສະໝີຄວາມມົວຂອງເງົາສຳລັບແສງນີ້. ສິ່ງນີ້ເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ທັງກັບ shadow mapping ແບບດັ້ງເດີ"
"ມ ແລະ contact-hardening shadows (ແສງທີ່ມີ **Angular Distance** ຫຼື **Size** ສູງກວ່າ "
"``0.0``). ຄ່າທີ່ສູງຂຶ້ນຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເງົານຸ້ມນວນຂຶ້ນ, ເຊິ່ງຈະເບິ່ງມີຄວາມສະຖຽນຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນສຳລັບວັດຖຸທີ່ເຄື່ອນໄຫວ. ຂໍ້"
"ເສຍຂອງການເພີ່ມ shadow blur ແມ່ນມັນຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ລວດລາຍເມັດຊາຍ (grainy pattern) ທີ່ໃຊ້ໃນການກັ່ນ"
"ຕອງ ເຫັນໄດ້ຊັດເຈນຂຶ້ນ. ເບິ່ງເພີ່ມເຕີມທີ່ "
":ref:`doc_lights_and_shadows_shadow_filter_mode`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:127
msgid ""
"**Caster Mask:** Shadows are only cast by objects in these layers. Note that "
"this mask does not affect which objects shadows are cast *onto*."
msgstr ""
"**Caster Mask:** ເງົາຈະຖືກສ້າງຂຶ້ນຈາກວັດຖຸທີ່ຢູ່ໃນເລເຢີເຫຼົ່ານີ້ເທົ່ານັ້ນ. ໝາຍເຫດ: mask ນີ້ບໍ່ມີຜົນຕໍ່ວັດຖຸທີ່"
"ເງົາຈະໄປ *ຕົກໃສ່*."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:133
msgid "Tweaking shadow bias"
msgstr "ການປັບແຕ່ງ shadow bias"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:135
msgid ""
"Below is an image of what tweaking bias looks like. Default values work for "
"most cases, but in general, it depends on the size and complexity of "
"geometry."
msgstr ""
"ລຸ່ມນີ້ແມ່ນຮູບພາບສະແດງໃຫ້ເຫັນຜົນຂອງການປັບ bias. ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນໃຊ້ໄດ້ດີໃນເກືອບທຸກກໍລະນີ, ແຕ່ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປແລ້ວ "
"ມັນຂຶ້ນກັບຂະໜາດ ແລະ ຄວາມຊັບຊ້ອນຂອງ geometry."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:138
msgid ""
"If the **Shadow Bias** or **Shadow Normal Bias** is set too low for a given "
"light, the shadow will be \"smeared\" onto the objects. This will cause the "
"light's intended appearance to darken, and is called *shadow acne*:"
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າຕັ້ງ **Shadow Bias** ຫຼື **Shadow Normal Bias** ຕໍ່າເກີນໄປສຳລັບແສງນັ້ນໆ, ເງົາຈະ \"ເລິ"
"ະ\" ລົງເທິງວັດຖຸ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ຮູບລັກສະນະຂອງແສງທີ່ຕ້ອງການເບິ່ງມືດລົງ, ເຊິ່ງເອີ້ນວ່າ *shadow acne*:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:144
msgid ""
"On the other hand, if the **Shadow Bias** or **Shadow Normal Bias** is set "
"too high for a given light, the shadow may appear to be disconnected from "
"the object. This is called *peter-panning*:"
msgstr ""
"ໃນທາງກົງກັນຂ້າມ, ຖ້າຕັ້ງ **Shadow Bias** ຫຼື **Shadow Normal Bias** ສູງເກີນໄປ, ເງົາອາດຈະ"
"ປາກົດຄືກັບວ່າຫຼຸດອອກຈາກວັດຖຸ. ສິ່ງນີ້ເອີ້ນວ່າ *peter-panning* (ເງົາລອຍ):"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:150
msgid ""
"In general, increasing **Shadow Normal Bias** is preferred over increasing "
"**Shadow Bias**. Increasing **Shadow Normal Bias** does not cause as much "
"peter-panning as increasing **Shadow Bias**, but it can still resolve most "
"shadow acne issues efficiently. The downside of increasing **Shadow Normal "
"Bias** is that it can make shadows appear thinner for certain objects."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປແລ້ວ, ການເພີ່ມ **Shadow Normal Bias** ແມ່ນດີກວ່າການເພີ່ມ **Shadow Bias**. ການເ"
"ພີ່ມ **Shadow Normal Bias** ບໍ່ເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດບັນຫາເງົາລອຍຫຼາຍເທົ່າກັບການເພີ່ມ **Shadow Bias**, "
"ແຕ່ມັນຍັງສາມາດແກ້ໄຂບັນຫາ shadow acne ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ໄດ້ຢ່າງມີປະສິດທິພາບ. ຂໍ້ເສຍຂອງການເພີ່ມ **Shadow "
"Normal Bias** ແມ່ນມັນອາດເຮັດໃຫ້ເງົາເບິ່ງບາງລົງສຳລັບວັດຖຸບາງຢ່າງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:156
msgid ""
"Any sort of bias issues can be fixed by :ref:`increasing the shadow map "
"resolution <doc_lights_and_shadows_balancing_performance_and_quality>`, at "
"the cost of decreased performance."
msgstr ""
"ບັນຫາ bias ທຸກປະເພດສາມາດແກ້ໄຂໄດ້ໂດຍ :ref:`ການເພີ່ມຄວາມລະອຽດຂອງ shadow map "
"<doc_lights_and_shadows_balancing_performance_and_quality>`, ແຕ່ຕ້ອງແລກດ້ວຍປະສິດທິ"
"ພາບທີ່ຫຼຸດລົງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:162
msgid ""
"Tweaking shadow mapping settings is an art – there are no \"one size fits "
"all\" settings. To achieve the best visuals, you may need to use different "
"shadow bias values on a per-light basis."
msgstr ""
"ການປັບແຕ່ງການຕັ້ງຄ່າ shadow mapping ແມ່ນສິລະປະຢ່າງໜຶ່ງ – ບໍ່ມີການຕັ້ງຄ່າໃດທີ່ \"ເໝາະສົມກັບທຸກຢ່າ"
"ງ\". ເພື່ອໃຫ້ໄດ້ພາບທີ່ດີທີ່ສຸດ, ທ່ານອາດຈະຕ້ອງໃຊ້ຄ່າ shadow bias ທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນໃນແຕ່ລະແສງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:166
msgid ""
"**Note on Appearance Changes**: When enabling shadows on a light, be aware "
"that the light's appearance might change compared to when it's rendered "
"without shadows in the compatibility renderer. Due to limitations with older "
"mobile devices, shadows are implemented using a multi-pass rendering "
"approach so lights with shadows are rendered in sRGB space instead of linear "
"space. This change in rendering space can sometimes drastically alter the "
"light's appearance. To achieve a similar appearance to an unshadowed light, "
"you may need to adjust the light's energy setting."
msgstr ""
"**ໝາຍເຫດກ່ຽວກັບການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງຮູບລັກສະນະ**: ເມື່ອເປີດໃຊ້ເງົາໃນແສງ, ໃຫ້ລະວັງວ່າ ຮູບລັກສະນະຂອງແສ"
"ງອາດຈະປ່ຽນແປງເມື່ອທຽບກັບຕອນທີ່ບໍ່ມີເງົາໃນ compatibility renderer. ເນື່ອງຈາກຂໍ້ຈຳກັດຂອງອຸປະກອນ"
"ມືຖືລຸ້ນເກົ່າ, ເງົາຖືກສ້າງຂຶ້ນດ້ວຍວິທີ multi-pass rendering ເຮັດໃຫ້ແສງທີ່ມີເງົາຖືກສະແດງຜົນໃນ sRGB "
"space ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນ linear space. ການປ່ຽນແປງ rendering space ນີ້ບາງຄັ້ງອາດເຮັດໃຫ້ຮູບລັກສະນ"
"ະຂອງແສງປ່ຽນໄປຫຼາຍ. ເພື່ອໃຫ້ໄດ້ຮູບລັກສະນະ ທີ່ໃກ້ຄຽງກັບແສງທີ່ບໍ່ມີເງົາ, ທ່ານອາດຈະຕ້ອງປັບການຕັ້ງຄ່າ "
"energy ຂອງແສງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:178
msgid ""
"This is the most common type of light and represents a light source very far "
"away (such as the sun). It is also the cheapest light to compute and should "
"be used whenever possible (although it's not the cheapest shadow-map to "
"compute, but more on that later)."
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ແມ່ນປະເພດແສງທີ່ພົບເລື້ອຍທີ່ສຸດ ແລະ ໃຊ້ແທນແຫຼ່ງກຳເນີດແສງທີ່ຢູ່ໄກຫຼາຍ (ເຊັ່ນ ດວງອາທິດ). ມັນຍັງເປັນແສງທີ່"
"ໃຊ້ຊັບພະຍາກອນໃນການຄິດໄລ່ໜ້ອຍທີ່ສຸດ ແລະ ຄວນໃຊ້ທຸກຄັ້ງທີ່ເປັນໄປໄດ້ (ເຖິງວ່າມັນຈະບໍ່ແມ່ນ shadow-map ທີ່ປ"
"ະຢັດທີ່ສຸດໃນການຄິດໄລ່, ແຕ່ຈະເວົ້າເຖິງເລື່ອງນັ້ນທີຫຼັງ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:183
msgid ""
"Directional light models an infinite number of parallel light rays covering "
"the whole scene. The directional light node is represented by a big arrow "
"which indicates the direction of the light rays. However, the position of "
"the node does not affect the lighting at all and can be anywhere."
msgstr ""
"Directional light ຈຳລອງລັງສີແສງແບບຂະໜານຈຳນວນມະຫາສານທີ່ປົກຄຸມທົ່ວສາກ. ໂນດ directional "
"light ຈະສະແດງດ້ວຍລູກສອນຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ເຊິ່ງບອກທິດທາງຂອງລັງສີແສງ. ຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ຕຳແໜ່ງຂອງໂນດຈະບໍ່ມີ"
"ຜົນຕໍ່ການໃຫ້ແສງເລີຍ ແລະ ສາມາດຢູ່ບ່ອນໃດກໍໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:190
msgid ""
"Every face whose front-side is hit by the light rays is lit, while the "
"others stay dark. Unlike most other light types, directional lights don't "
"have specific parameters."
msgstr ""
"ທຸກໆດ້ານທີ່ດ້ານໜ້າຖືກລັງສີແສງກະທົບຈະຖືກສ່ອງສະຫວ່າງ, ໃນຂະນະທີ່ດ້ານອື່ນໆຈະມືດ. ຕ່າງຈາກແສງປະເພດອື່ນໆສ່ວ"
"ນໃຫຍ່, directional lights ບໍ່ມີພາລາມິເຕີສະເພາະ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:194
msgid ""
"The directional light also offers an **Angular Distance** property, which "
"determines the light's angular size in degrees. Increasing this above "
"``0.0`` will make shadows softer at greater distances from the caster, while "
"also affecting the sun's appearance in procedural sky materials. This is "
"called a *contact-hardening* shadow (also known as PCSS)."
msgstr ""
"Directional light ຍັງມີຄຸນສົມບັດ **Angular Distance**, ເຊິ່ງກຳນົດຂະໜາດມຸມຂອງແສງເປັນອົງສ"
"າ. ການເພີ່ມຄ່ານີ້ໃຫ້ສູງກວ່າ ``0.0`` ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເງົານຸ້ມນວນຂຶ້ນເມື່ອຢູ່ໄກຈາກວັດຖຸສ້າງເງົາ, ພ້ອມທັງສົ່ງຜົນຕໍ່ຮູບ"
"ລັກສະນະຂອງດວງອາທິດໃນວັດສະດຸທ້ອງຟ້າ (procedural sky materials). ສິ່ງນີ້ເອີ້ນວ່າ *contact-"
"hardening* shadow (ຫຼື ຮູ້ຈັກກັນໃນຊື່ PCSS)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:200
msgid ""
"For reference, the angular distance of the Sun viewed from the Earth is "
"approximately ``0.5``. This kind of shadow is expensive, so check the "
"recommendations in :ref:`doc_lights_and_shadows_pcss_recommendations` if "
"setting this value above ``0.0`` on lights with shadows enabled."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບການອ້າງອີງ, ມຸມຂອງດວງອາທິດເມື່ອເບິ່ງຈາກໂລກແມ່ນປະມານ ``0.5``. ເງົາຊະນິດນີ້ ໃຊ້ຊັບພະຍາກອນສູ"
"ງ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນໃຫ້ກວດເບິ່ງຄຳແນະນຳໃນ :ref:`doc_lights_and_shadows_pcss_recommendations` ຖ້"
"າຈະຕັ້ງຄ່ານີ້ໃຫ້ສູງກວ່າ ``0.0`` ໃນແສງທີ່ເປີດໃຊ້ເງົາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:206
msgid "Directional shadow mapping"
msgstr "Directional shadow mapping"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:208
msgid ""
"To compute shadow maps, the scene is rendered (only depth) from an "
"orthogonal point of view that covers the whole scene (or up to the max "
"distance). There is, however, a problem with this approach because objects "
"closer to the camera receive low-resolution shadows that may appear blocky."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອຄິດໄລ່ shadow maps, ສາກຈະຖືກສະແດງຜົນ (ສະເພາະຄວາມເລິກ) ຈາກມຸມມອງ orthogonal ທີ່ປົກຄຸມ"
"ທົ່ວສາກ (ຫຼື ຈົນຮອດໄລຍະຫ່າງສູງສຸດ). ຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ວິທີນີ້ມີບັນຫາຄື ວັດຖຸທີ່ຢູ່ ໃກ້ກ້ອງຈະໄດ້ຮັບເງົາທີ່ມີຄວາມລະ"
"ອຽດຕໍ່າ ເຊິ່ງອາດເບິ່ງເປັນເມັດຫຼ່ຽມໆ (blocky)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:213
msgid ""
"To fix this, a technique named *Parallel Split Shadow Maps* (PSSM) is used. "
"This splits the view frustum in 2 or 4 areas. Each area gets its own shadow "
"map. This allows small areas close to the viewer to have the same shadow "
"resolution as a huge, far-away area. When shadows are enabled for "
"DirectionalLight3D, the default shadow mode is PSSM with 4 splits. In "
"scenarios where an object is large enough to appear in all four splits, it "
"results in increased draw calls. Specifically, such an object will be "
"rendered five times in total: once for each of the four shadow splits and "
"once for the final scene rendering. This can impact performance, "
"understanding this behavior is important for optimizing your scene and "
"managing performance expectations."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອແກ້ໄຂບັນຫານີ້, ເຕັກນິກທີ່ຊື່ວ່າ *Parallel Split Shadow Maps* (PSSM) ຈຶ່ງຖືກນຳມາໃຊ້. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະ"
"ແບ່ງ view frustum ອອກເປັນ 2 ຫຼື 4 ສ່ວນ. ແຕ່ລະສ່ວນຈະມີ shadow map ຂອງມັນເອງ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ພື້ນ"
"ທີ່ນ້ອຍໆທີ່ຢູ່ໃກ້ຜູ້ເບິ່ງ ມີຄວາມລະອຽດເງົາເທົ່າກັບພື້ນທີ່ກວ້າງໃຫຍ່ທີ່ຢູ່ໄກອອກໄປ. ເມື່ອເປີດໃຊ້ເງົາສຳລັບ "
"DirectionalLight3D, ໂໝດເງົາເລີ່ມຕົ້ນແມ່ນ PSSM ແບບ 4 ສ່ວນ. ໃນກໍລະນີທີ່ວັດຖຸມີຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ພໍທີ່ຈະປາກົ"
"ດໃນທັງ 4 ສ່ວນ, ມັນຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ draw calls ເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນ. ໂດຍສະເພາະ, ວັດຖຸດັ່ງກ່າວຈະຖືກສະແດງຜົນທັງໝົດ "
"5 ຄັ້ງ: 4 ຄັ້ງສຳລັບແຕ່ລະ shadow split ແລະ ອີກ 1 ຄັ້ງສຳລັບການສະແດງຜົນສາກສຸດທ້າຍ. ສິ່ງນີ້ອາດສົ່ງຜົນ"
"ຕໍ່ປະສິດທິພາບ, ການເຂົ້າໃຈ ພຶດຕິກຳນີ້ຈຶ່ງສຳຄັນສຳລັບການປັບແຕ່ງ (optimize) ສາກຂອງທ່ານ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:225
msgid "With this, shadows become more detailed:"
msgstr "ດ້ວຍວິທີນີ້, ເງົາຈະມີລາຍລະອຽດຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:229
msgid "To control PSSM, a number of parameters are exposed:"
msgstr "ເພື່ອຄວບຄຸມ PSSM, ມີພາລາມິເຕີຫຼາຍຢ່າງທີ່ເປີດໃຫ້ປັບແຕ່ງ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:233
msgid ""
"Each split distance is controlled relative to the camera far (or shadow "
"**Max Distance** if greater than ``0.0``). ``0.0`` is the eye position and "
"``1.0`` is where the shadow ends at a distance. Splits are in-between. "
"Default values generally work well, but tweaking the first split a bit is "
"common to give more detail to close objects (like a character in a third-"
"person game)."
msgstr ""
"ໄລຍະຫ່າງຂອງແຕ່ລະ split ຈະຖືກຄວບຄຸມໂດຍທຽບກັບ camera far (ຫຼື shadow **Max Distance** "
"ຖ້າສູງກວ່າ ``0.0``). ``0.0`` ແມ່ນຕຳແໜ່ງສາຍຕາ ແລະ ``1.0`` ແມ່ນຈຸດທີ່ເງົາສິ້ນສຸດ. Splits ຈະຢູ່"
"ລະຫວ່າງກາງ. ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນແມ່ນໃຊ້ໄດ້ດີ, ແຕ່ການປັບ split ທຳອິດເລັກນ້ອຍ ແມ່ນເລື່ອງປົກກະຕິ ເພື່ອໃ"
"ຫ້ລາຍລະອຽດຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນກັບວັດຖຸທີ່ຢູ່ໃກ້ (ເຊັ່ນ ຕົວລະຄອນໃນເກມມຸມມອງບຸກຄົນທີສາມ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:239
msgid ""
"Always make sure to set a shadow **Max Distance** according to what the "
"scene needs. A lower maximum distance will result in better-looking shadows "
"and better performance, as fewer objects will need to be included in shadow "
"rendering. You can also adjust **Fade Start** to control how aggressive the "
"shadow fade-out should be at a distance. For scenes where the **Max "
"Distance** fully covers the scene at any given camera position, you can "
"increase **Fade Start** to ``1.0`` to prevent the shadow from fading at a "
"distance. This should not be done in scenes where **Max Distance** doesn't "
"fully cover the scene, as the shadow will appear to be suddenly cut off at a "
"distance."
msgstr ""
"ໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈສະເໝີວ່າໄດ້ຕັ້ງຄ່າ shadow **Max Distance** ຕາມຄວາມຈຳເປັນຂອງສາກ. ໄລຍະຫ່າງສູງສຸດທີ່ຕໍ່າ"
"ລົງຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເງົາເບິ່ງດີຂຶ້ນ ແລະ ປະສິດທິພາບດີຂຶ້ນ, ເພາະວັດຖຸທີ່ຈະ ຖືກນຳມາສະແດງຜົນເງົາມີໜ້ອຍລົງ. ທ່ານຍັງສ"
"າມາດປັບ **Fade Start** ເພື່ອຄວບຄຸມຄວາມໜັກເບົາ ຂອງການຈາງຫາຍຂອງເງົາໃນໄລຍະໄກ. ສຳລັບສາກທີ່ "
"**Max Distance** ປົກຄຸມທົ່ວສາກຢູ່ແລ້ວ ບໍ່ວ່າກ້ອງຈະຢູ່ໃສ, ທ່ານສາມາດເພີ່ມ **Fade Start** ເປັນ "
"``1.0`` ເພື່ອປ້ອງກັນບໍ່ໃຫ້ເງົາຈາງຫາຍ. ແຕ່ບໍ່ຄວນເຮັດໃນສາກທີ່ **Max Distance** ບໍ່ໄດ້ປົກຄຸມທົ່ວສາກ, "
"ເພາະເງົາຈະປາກົດຄືກັບວ່າ ຖືກຕັດອອກຢ່າງກະທັນຫັນໃນໄລຍະໄກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:249
msgid ""
"Sometimes, the transition between a split and the next can look bad. To fix "
"this, the **Blend Splits** option can be turned on, which sacrifices detail "
"and performance in exchange for smoother transitions:"
msgstr ""
"ບາງຄັ້ງ, ຮອຍຕໍ່ລະຫວ່າງ split ຫນຶ່ງໄປຫາອີກອັນຫນຶ່ງອາດຈະເບິ່ງບໍ່ດີ. ເພື່ອແກ້ໄຂບັນຫານີ້, ສາມາດເປີດຕົວເລືອ"
"ກ **Blend Splits**, ເຊິ່ງຈະຕ້ອງແລກດ້ວຍລາຍລະອຽດ ແລະ ປະສິດທິພາບ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ໄດ້ຮອຍຕໍ່ທີ່ນຸ້ມນວນຂຶ້ນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:255
msgid ""
"The **Shadow > Normal Bias** parameter can be used to fix special cases of "
"self-shadowing when objects are perpendicular to the light. The only "
"downside is that it makes the shadow a bit thinner. Consider increasing "
"**Shadow > Normal Bias** before increasing **Shadow > Bias** in most "
"situations."
msgstr ""
"ພາລາມິເຕີ **Shadow > Normal Bias** ສາມາດໃຊ້ເພື່ອແກ້ໄຂກໍລະນີພິເສດຂອງ self-shadowing ເມື່ອ"
"ວັດຖຸຕັ້ງສາກກັບແສງ. ຂໍ້ເສຍພຽງຢ່າງດຽວແມ່ນມັນເຮັດໃຫ້ເງົາບາງລົງເລັກນ້ອຍ. ໃນເກືອບທຸກສະຖານະການ, ຄວນພິ"
"ຈາລະນາເພີ່ມ **Shadow > Normal Bias** ກ່ອນທີ່ຈະເພີ່ມ **Shadow > Bias**."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:260
msgid ""
"Lastly, **Pancake Size** is a property that can be adjusted to fix missing "
"shadows when using large objects with unsubdivided meshes. Only change this "
"value if you notice missing shadows that are not related to shadow biasing "
"issues."
msgstr ""
"ສຸດທ້າຍ, **Pancake Size** ແມ່ນຄຸນສົມບັດທີ່ສາມາດປັບເພື່ອແກ້ໄຂບັນຫາເງົາຫາຍ ເມື່ອໃຊ້ວັດຖຸຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ທີ່"
"ມີ mesh ແບບບໍ່ມີການແບ່ງສ່ວນ (unsubdivided). ໃຫ້ປ່ຽນຄ່ານີ້ ກໍຕໍ່ເມື່ອທ່ານສັງເກດເຫັນວ່າເງົາຫາຍໄປໂດຍທີ່"
"ບໍ່ກ່ຽວກັບບັນຫາ shadow bias ເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:268
msgid "Omni light"
msgstr "Omni light (ແສງຮອບທິດທາງ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:270
msgid ""
"Omni light is a point source that emits light spherically in all directions "
"up to a given radius."
msgstr ""
"Omni light ແມ່ນແຫຼ່ງກຳເນີດແສງແບບຈຸດທີ່ປ່ອຍແສງເປັນຮູບຊົງກົມໄປທຸກທິດທາງ ຕາມລັດສະໝີທີ່ກຳນົດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:275
msgid ""
"In real life, light attenuation is an inverse function, which means omni "
"lights don't have a radius. This is a problem because it means computing "
"several omni lights would become demanding."
msgstr ""
"ໃນຊີວິດຈິງ, ການຫຼຸດຜ່ອນຂອງແສງ (attenuation) ເປັນຟັງຊັນຜົກຜັນ, ເຊິ່ງໝາຍຄວາມວ່າ ແສງຮອບທິດທາງຈະ"
"ບໍ່ມີລັດສະໝີສິ້ນສຸດ. ນີ້ເປັນບັນຫາເພາະການຄິດໄລ່ omni lights ຫຼາຍອັນ ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ໃຊ້ຊັບພະຍາກອນຫຼາຍເກີນໄ"
"ປ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:278
msgid ""
"To solve this, a **Range** parameter is introduced together with an "
"attenuation function."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອແກ້ໄຂບັນຫານີ້, ຈຶ່ງມີການນຳໃຊ້ພາລາມິເຕີ **Range** ຮ່ວມກັບຟັງຊັນ attenuation."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:282
msgid ""
"These two parameters allow tweaking how this works visually in order to find "
"aesthetically pleasing results."
msgstr ""
"ພາລາມິເຕີທັງສອງນີ້ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສາມາດປັບແຕ່ງການເຮັດວຽກຂອງແສງ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ໄດ້ຜົນລັບທາງສາຍຕາທີ່ສວຍງາມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:286
msgid ""
"A **Size** parameter is also available in OmniLight3D. Increasing this value "
"will make the light fade out slower and shadows appear blurrier when far "
"away from the caster. This can be used to simulate area lights to an extent. "
"This is called a *contact-hardening* shadow (also known as PCSS). This kind "
"of shadow is expensive, so check the recommendations "
"in :ref:`doc_lights_and_shadows_pcss_recommendations` if setting this value "
"above ``0.0`` on lights with shadows enabled."
msgstr ""
"ພາລາມິເຕີ **Size** ຍັງມີໃຫ້ໃຊ້ໃນ OmniLight3D. ການເພີ່ມຄ່ານີ້ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ແສງຈາງຫາຍຊ້າລົງ ແລະ ເງົາ"
"ເບິ່ງມົວຂຶ້ນເມື່ອຢູ່ໄກຈາກວັດຖຸສ້າງເງົາ. ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດໃຊ້ເພື່ອຈຳລອງ area lights ໄດ້ ໃນລະດັບໜຶ່ງ. ນີ້ເອີ້ນວ່"
"າ *contact-hardening* shadow (ຫຼື PCSS). ເງົາຊະນິດນີ້ໃຊ້ ຊັບພະຍາກອນສູງ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນໃຫ້ກວດເບິ່ງຄຳ"
"ແນະນຳໃນ :ref:`doc_lights_and_shadows_pcss_recommendations` ຖ້າຈະຕັ້ງຄ່ານີ້ໃຫ້ສູງກວ່າ "
"``0.0`` ໃນແສງທີ່ເປີດໃຊ້ເງົາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:297
msgid "Omni shadow mapping"
msgstr "Omni shadow mapping"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:299
msgid ""
"Omni light shadow mapping is relatively straightforward. The main issue that "
"needs to be considered is the algorithm used to render it."
msgstr ""
"ການເຮັດ shadow mapping ສຳລັບ omni light ແມ່ນຂ້ອນຂ້າງເຂົ້າໃຈງ່າຍ. ບັນຫາຫຼັກທີ່ ຕ້ອງຄຳນຶງເຖິງແມ່"
"ນອັລກໍລິທຶມທີ່ໃຊ້ໃນການສະແດງຜົນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:302
msgid ""
"Omni Shadows can be rendered as either **Dual Paraboloid** or **Cube** "
"mapped. **Dual Paraboloid** renders quickly, but can cause deformations, "
"while **Cube** is more correct, but slower. The default is **Cube**, but "
"consider changing it to **Dual Paraboloid** for lights where it doesn't make "
"much of a visual difference."
msgstr ""
"ເງົາຂອງ Omni ສາມາດສະແດງຜົນໄດ້ທັງແບບ **Dual Paraboloid** ຫຼື **Cube** mapping. "
"**Dual Paraboloid** ຈະສະແດງຜົນໄດ້ໄວ ແຕ່ອາດເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດການບິດບ້ຽວ, ໃນຂະນະທີ່ **Cube** ຈະມີ"
"ຄວາມຖືກຕ້ອງກວ່າແຕ່ຊ້າກວ່າ. ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນແມ່ນ **Cube**, ແຕ່ຄວນພິຈາລະນາປ່ຽນເປັນ **Dual "
"Paraboloid** ສຳລັບແສງທີ່ການປ່ຽນແປງນີ້ບໍ່ສົ່ງຜົນກະທົບຕໍ່ສາຍຕາຫຼາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:310
msgid ""
"If the objects being rendered are mostly irregular and subdivided, Dual "
"Paraboloid is usually enough. In any case, as these shadows are cached in a "
"shadow atlas (more on that at the end), it may not make a difference in "
"performance for most scenes."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າວັດຖຸທີ່ສະແດງຜົນສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ມີຮູບຮ່າງບໍ່ສະໝໍ່າສະເໝີ ແລະ ຖືກແບ່ງສ່ວນ (subdivided), ແບບ Dual "
"Paraboloid ກໍພຽງພໍແລ້ວ. ຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ເນື່ອງຈາກເງົາເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຖືກເກັບໄວ້ໃນ shadow atlas (ເຊິ່ງຈະເວົ້"
"າເຖິງໃນຕອນທ້າຍ), ມັນອາດຈະບໍ່ເຮັດໃຫ້ປະສິດທິພາບແຕກຕ່າງກັນຫຼາຍໃນເກືອບທຸກສາກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:315
msgid ""
"Omni lights with shadows enabled can make use of projectors. The projector "
"texture will *multiply* the light's color by the color at a given point on "
"the texture. As a result, lights will usually appear to be darker once a "
"projector texture is assigned; you can increase **Energy** to compensate for "
"this."
msgstr ""
"Omni lights ທີ່ເປີດໃຊ້ເງົາສາມາດໃຊ້ງານ projectors ໄດ້. ພື້ນຜິວ (texture) ຂອງ projector ຈ"
"ະໄປ *ຄູນ* ກັບສີຂອງແສງ ຕາມສີໃນແຕ່ລະຈຸດຂອງພື້ນຜິວ. ຜົນທີ່ໄດ້ຄື ແສງມັກຈະເບິ່ງມືດລົງ ເມື່ອມີການໃສ່ "
"projector texture; ທ່ານສາມາດເພີ່ມ **Energy** ເພື່ອຊົດເຊີຍສ່ວນນີ້ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:320
msgid ""
"Omni light projector textures require a special 360° panorama mapping, "
"similar to :ref:`class_PanoramaSkyMaterial` textures."
msgstr ""
"Projector textures ສຳລັບ omni light ຕ້ອງການການເຮັດ mapping ແບບພາໂນຣາມາ 360 ອົງສາ "
"ແບບພິເສດ, ເຊິ່ງຄ້າຍຄືກັບພື້ນຜິວ :ref:`class_PanoramaSkyMaterial`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:323
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:368
msgid "With the projector texture below, the following result is obtained:"
msgstr "ດ້ວຍ projector texture ລຸ່ມນີ້, ຈະໄດ້ຜົນລັບດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:331
msgid ""
"If you've acquired omni projectors in the form of cubemap images, you can "
"use `this web-based conversion tool <https://danilw.github.io/GLSL-howto/"
"cubemap_to_panorama_js/cubemap_to_panorama.html>`__ to convert them to a "
"single panorama image."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເຈົ້າໄດ້ omni projectors ມາໃນຮູບແບບ cubemap, ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ `ເຄື່ອງມືແປງຜ່ານເວັບນີ້ "
"<https://danilw.github.io/GLSL-howto/cubemap_to_panorama_js/"
"cubemap_to_panorama.html>`__ ເພື່ອແປງພວກມັນໃຫ້ເປັນຮູບພາໂນຣາມາດ່ຽວໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:338
msgid "Spot light"
msgstr "Spot light (ແສງສ່ອງສະເພາະຈຸດ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:340
msgid ""
"Spot lights are similar to omni lights, except they emit light only into a "
"cone (or \"cutoff\"). They are useful to simulate flashlights, car lights, "
"reflectors, spots, etc. This type of light is also attenuated towards the "
"opposite direction it points to."
msgstr ""
"Spot lights ຄ້າຍຄືກັບ omni lights, ແຕ່ຈະປ່ອຍແສງອອກມາເປັນຮູບຊົງຈວຍ (cone) ເທົ່ານັ້ນ. ພວກມັນ"
"ມີປະໂຫຍດໃນການຈຳລອງໄຟສາຍ, ໄຟລົດ, ໄຟສະປອດໄລ້ ແລະ ອື່ນໆ. ແສງປະເພດນີ້ ຍັງມີການຫຼຸດຜ່ອນຂອງແສງໄ"
"ປໃນທິດທາງກົງກັນຂ້າມກັບທີ່ມັນສ່ອງໄປນຳ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:345
msgid ""
"Spot lights share the same **Range**, **Attenuation** and **Size** as "
"OmniLight3D, and add two extra parameters:"
msgstr ""
"Spot lights ໃຊ້ພາລາມິເຕີ **Range**, **Attenuation** ແລະ **Size** ຄືກັນກັບ "
"OmniLight3D, ແຕ່ເພີ່ມພາລາມິເຕີພິເສດອີກສອງອັນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:348
msgid "**Angle:** The aperture angle of the light."
msgstr "**Angle:** ມຸມກວ້າງຂອງລຳແສງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:349
msgid ""
"**Angle Attenuation:** The cone attenuation, which helps soften the cone "
"borders."
msgstr ""
"**Angle Attenuation:** ການຫຼຸດຜ່ອນແສງໃນຮູບຊົງຈວຍ, ເຊິ່ງຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ຂອບຂອງລຳແສງນຸ້ມນວນຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:352
msgid "Spot shadow mapping"
msgstr "Spot shadow mapping"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:354
msgid ""
"Spots feature the same parameters as omni lights for shadow mapping. "
"Rendering spot shadow maps is significantly faster compared to omni lights, "
"as only one shadow texture needs to be rendered (instead of rendering 6 "
"faces, or 2 in dual paraboloid mode)."
msgstr ""
"Spot lights ມີພາລາມິເຕີສຳລັບ shadow mapping ຄືກັນກັບ omni lights. ແຕ່ການສະແດງຜົນ spot "
"shadow maps ຈະໄວຂຶ້ນກວ່າຫຼາຍເມື່ອທຽບກັບ omni lights, ເພາະຕ້ອງສະແດງຜົນ shadow texture ພ"
"ຽງອັນດຽວ (ແທນທີ່ຈະຕ້ອງສະແດງຜົນທັງ 6 ດ້ານ, ຫຼື 2 ດ້ານໃນໂໝດ dual paraboloid)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:359
msgid ""
"Spot lights with shadows enabled can make use of projectors. The projector "
"texture will *multiply* the light's color by the color at a given point on "
"the texture. As a result, lights will usually appear to be darker once a "
"projector texture is assigned; you can increase **Energy** to compensate for "
"this."
msgstr ""
"Spot lights ທີ່ເປີດໃຊ້ເງົາສາມາດໃຊ້ງານ projectors ໄດ້. Projector texture ຈະໄປ *ຄູນ* ກັບ"
"ສີຂອງແສງ ຕາມສີໃນແຕ່ລະຈຸດຂອງພື້ນຜິວ. ຜົນທີ່ໄດ້ຄື ແສງມັກຈະເບິ່ງມືດລົງ ເມື່ອມີການໃສ່ projector "
"texture; ທ່ານສາມາດເພີ່ມ **Energy** ເພື່ອຊົດເຊີຍສ່ວນນີ້ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:364
msgid ""
"Unlike omni light projectors, a spot light projector texture doesn't need to "
"follow a special format to look correct. It will be mapped in a way similar "
"to a :ref:`decal <doc_using_decals>`."
msgstr ""
"ຕ່າງຈາກ omni light projectors, spot light projector texture ບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງໃຊ້ຮູບແບບ ພິ"
"ເສດເພື່ອໃຫ້ເບິ່ງຖືກຕ້ອງ. ມັນຈະຖືກເຮັດ mapping ໃນລັກສະນະທີ່ຄ້າຍຄືກັບ :ref:`decal "
"<doc_using_decals>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:376
msgid ""
"Spot lights with wide angles will have lower-quality shadows than spot "
"lights with narrow angles, as the shadow map is spread over a larger "
"surface. At angles wider than 89 degrees, spot light shadows will stop "
"working entirely. If you need shadows for wider lights, use an omni light "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Spot lights ທີ່ມີມຸມກວ້າງຈະມີຄຸນນະພາບເງົາຕໍ່າກວ່າ spot lights ທີ່ມີມຸມແຄບ, ເພາະ shadow map ຈ"
"ະຖືກແຜ່ອອກໄປທົ່ວພື້ນທີ່ທີ່ໃຫຍ່ກວ່າ. ທີ່ມຸມກວ້າງກວ່າ 89 ອົງສາ, ເງົາຂອງ spot light ຈະຢຸດເຮັດວຽກທັງໝົ"
"ດ. ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການເງົາສຳລັບແສງທີ່ກວ້າງກວ່ານັ້ນ, ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ omni light ແທນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:385
msgid "Area light"
msgstr "Area light (ແສງແບບພື້ນທີ່)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:387
msgid ""
"Sometimes, you want lighting to come from a large area instead of a single "
"point. Area lights are useful for simulating soft, diffuse lighting, such as "
"light coming from a window or a lit billboard."
msgstr ""
"ບາງຄັ້ງ, ທ່ານຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ແສງມາຈາກພື້ນທີ່ກວ້າງແທນທີ່ຈະມາຈາກຈຸດດຽວ. Area lights ມີປະໂຫຍດ ໃນການຈ"
"ຳລອງແສງທີ່ນຸ້ມນວນ ແລະ ກະຈາຍຕົວ (diffuse), ເຊັ່ນ ແສງທີ່ມາຈາກປ່ອງຢ້ຽມ ຫຼື ປ້າຍໂຄສະນາທີ່ມີໄຟສ່ອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:391
msgid ""
"Godot provides the :ref:`class_AreaLight3D` node for this purpose, which "
"emits light from a rectangular area. The node only emits light and has no "
"other visual representation in the scene. The screenshots below use "
"a :ref:`class_Sprite3D` node as a child of the area light for visualization "
"purposes."
msgstr ""
"Godot ມີໂນດ :ref:`class_AreaLight3D` ສຳລັບຈຸດປະສົງນີ້, ເຊິ່ງຈະປ່ອຍແສງອອກມາຈາກພື້ນທີ່ ຮູບສີ່ຫຼ່ຽ"
"ມຜືນຜ້າ. ໂນດນີ້ຈະປ່ອຍແຕ່ແສງເທົ່ານັ້ນ ແລະ ບໍ່ມີການສະແດງຜົນທາງສາຍຕາອື່ນໆໃນສາກ. ຮູບຕົວຢ່າງລຸ່ມນີ້ໃຊ້ໂນດ "
":ref:`class_Sprite3D` ເປັນໂນດລູກຂອງ area light ເພື່ອໃຫ້ ເບິ່ງເຫັນຕຳແໜ່ງໄດ້ງ່າຍຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:398
msgid ""
"This type of light is the most expensive to render in real-time. It should "
"be used sparingly, especially when shadows are enabled. Consider using them "
"only for cinematics or when targeting high-end devices."
msgstr ""
"ແສງປະເພດນີ້ແມ່ນໃຊ້ຊັບພະຍາກອນສູງສຸດໃນການສະແດງຜົນແບບ real-time. ຄວນໃຊ້ຢ່າງປະຢັດ, ໂດຍສະເພາະ"
"ເມື່ອເປີດໃຊ້ເງົາ. ຄວນພິຈາລະນາໃຊ້ສະເພາະໃນສາກຄລິບວິດີໂອ (cinematics) ຫຼື ເມື່ອເນັ້ນກຸ່ມຜູ້ໃຊ້ທີ່ໃຊ້ອຸປະກ"
"ອນສະເປັກສູງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:402
msgid ""
"In Forward+, as soon as one area light is visible in the view frustum, it "
"incurs an additional performance cost on **all** rendered objects in the "
"scene, even those that are not reached by an area light. This tradeoff "
"allows for a greater number of area lights to be rendered (clustered "
"lighting)."
msgstr ""
"ໃນ Forward+, ທັນທີທີ່ມີ area light ປາກົດໃນ view frustum, ມັນຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດການໃຊ້ ຊັບພະຍາກອ"
"ນເພີ່ມເຕີມກັບ **ທຸກໆ** ວັດຖຸທີ່ສະແດງຜົນໃນສາກ, ເຖິງວ່າວັດຖຸນັ້ນຈະບໍ່ຖືກ area light ສ່ອງໄປຮອດກໍຕາມ. "
"ສິ່ງນີ້ເປັນຂໍ້ແລກປ່ຽນເພື່ອໃຫ້ສາມາດສະແດງຜົນ area lights ໄດ້ເປັນຈຳນວນຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນ (clustered "
"lighting)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:408
msgid ""
"In Mobile and Compatibility, only objects that are reached by an area light "
"incur an additional performance cost."
msgstr ""
"ໃນ Mobile ແລະ Compatibility, ຈະມີແຕ່ຄ່າໃຊ້ຈ່າຍຊັບພະຍາກອນເພີ່ມເຕີມສະເພາະກັບວັດຖຸ ທີ່ area "
"light ສ່ອງໄປຮອດເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:411
msgid ""
"Area lights can also cast shadows, with variable penumbra simulated "
"using :ref:`PCSS <doc_lights_and_shadows_pcss_recommendations>` by default. "
"The size of this penumbra can be controlled with the Light3D **Size** "
"property. This effect can be quite demanding, so it can be turned off by "
"setting **Size** to ``0.0``."
msgstr ""
"Area lights ສາມາດສ້າງເງົາໄດ້ຄືກັນ, ໂດຍມີການຈຳລອງຂອບເງົາ (penumbra) ທີ່ປ່ຽນແປງໄດ້ ຜ່ານ "
":ref:`PCSS <doc_lights_and_shadows_pcss_recommendations>` ໂດຍຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ. ຂະໜາດຂອ"
"ງຂອບເງົານີ້ສາມາດຄວບຄຸມໄດ້ດ້ວຍຄຸນສົມບັດ **Size** ຂອງ Light3D. ເອັບເຟັກນີ້ ຂ້ອນຂ້າງໃຊ້ຊັບພະຍາກອນ"
"ສູງ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນສາມາດປິດໄດ້ໂດຍການຕັ້ງຄ່າ **Size** ເປັນ ``0.0``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:419
msgid ""
"Shadows cast by an area light may look incorrect if the object casting "
"shadows doesn't have enough subdivisions and it's very close to the area "
"light. This is the same limitation as Dual Paraboloid shadow mode on an omni "
"light."
msgstr ""
"ເງົາທີ່ສ້າງຈາກ area light ອາດຈະເບິ່ງບໍ່ຖືກຕ້ອງ ຖ້າວັດຖຸທີ່ສ້າງເງົາບໍ່ມີການແບ່ງສ່ວນ (subdivisions) ທີ່"
"ພຽງພໍ ແລະ ຢູ່ໃກ້ກັບ area light ຫຼາຍເກີນໄປ. ນີ້ແມ່ນຂໍ້ຈຳກັດດຽວກັນກັບໂໝດເງົາ Dual Paraboloid ໃ"
"ນ omni light."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:427
msgid ""
"Since area lights are difficult to simulate in a real-time rasterized "
"renderer, they come with a number of limitations."
msgstr ""
"ເນື່ອງຈາກ area lights ເປັນເລື່ອງຍາກໃນການຈຳລອງໃນ real-time rasterized renderer, ພວກ"
"ມັນຈຶ່ງມາພ້ອມກັບຂໍ້ຈຳກັດຫຼາຍຢ່າງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:430
msgid ""
"For small light sources, you will likely get better results when using point "
"lights. Shadows from area lights are crude approximations, as they are "
"calculated as if they were point lights, and may appear to be distorted at "
"the edges. To get a better result, make sure the meshes in the light's range "
"are sufficiently subdivided."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບແຫຼ່ງກຳເນີດແສງຂະໜາດນ້ອຍ, ທ່ານອາດຈະໄດ້ຜົນລັບທີ່ດີກວ່າເມື່ອໃຊ້ point lights. ເງົາຈາກ area "
"lights ເປັນພຽງການປະມານແບບຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ເພາະພວກມັນຖືກຄິດໄລ່ຄືກັບວ່າ ເປັນ point lights, ແລະ ອ"
"າດຈະປາກົດການບິດບ້ຽວຢູ່ບໍລິເວນຂອບ. ເພື່ອໃຫ້ໄດ້ຜົນລັບທີ່ດີຂຶ້ນ, ໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າ mesh ທີ່ຢູ່ໃນໄລຍະຂອງແສງມີການແ"
"ບ່ງສ່ວນ (subdivided) ທີ່ພຽງພໍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:436
msgid ""
"Area lights suffer from light leaking on the backside of geometry closely in "
"front of them at grazing angles, so be careful with where you place them."
msgstr ""
"Area lights ມັກຈະມີບັນຫາແສງຮົ່ວ (light leaking) ໄປທາງດ້ານຫຼັງຂອງ geometry ທີ່ຢູ່ທາງໜ້າ ໃນມຸ"
"ມແຄບໆ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນຈົ່ງລະມັດລະວັງໃນການວາງຕຳແໜ່ງຂອງພວກມັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:439
msgid ""
"Lastly, not all material features are fully supported; area lights are "
"practically limited to Lambertian diffuse and GGX specular shading, while "
"anisotropic materials will appear as if isotropic. Vertex shading is also "
"not implemented for area lights."
msgstr ""
"ສຸດທ້າຍ, ບໍ່ແມ່ນທຸກຄຸນສົມບັດຂອງວັດສະດຸທີ່ຈະຖືກຮອງຮັບທັງໝົດ; ໃນທາງປະຕິບັດແລ້ວ area lights ຈະຖືກຈຳກັດ"
"ຢູ່ແຕ່ Lambertian diffuse ແລະ GGX specular shading, ໃນຂະນະທີ່ ວັດສະດຸແບບ "
"anisotropic ຈະປາກົດຄືກັບວ່າເປັນ isotropic. ນອກຈາກນັ້ນ Vertex shading ກໍຍັງບໍ່ທັນໄດ້ຖືກນຳມາໃ"
"ຊ້ກັບ area lights ເທື່ອ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:444
msgid ""
"Area lights emit light in a rectangular area defined by the **Area > Size** "
"property (not to be confused with the generic Light3D **Size** property). To "
"get a physically accurate result, you should resize this area to match the "
"size of the real-life light source you are trying to simulate. For example, "
"if you are simulating a 1-meter neon tube that is 10 centimeters wide, set "
"the area size to ``(1, 0.1)`` and adjust the energy accordingly."
msgstr ""
"Area lights ປ່ອຍແສງໃນພື້ນທີ່ຮູບສີ່ຫຼ່ຽມຜືນຜ້າທີ່ກຳນົດໂດຍຄຸນສົມບັດ **Area > Size** (ຢ່າສັບສົນກັບຄຸນສົມ"
"ບັດ **Size** ທົ່ວໄປຂອງ Light3D). ເພື່ອໃຫ້ໄດ້ຜົນລັບທີ່ຖືກຕ້ອງ ຕາມຫຼັກຟີຊິກ, ທ່ານຄວນປັບຂະໜາດພື້ນທີ່ນີ້ໃຫ້"
"ກົງກັບຂະໜາດຂອງແຫຼ່ງກຳເນີດແສງໃນໂລກຕົວຈິງ ທີ່ທ່ານກຳລັງຈຳລອງ. ຕົວຢ່າງ: ຖ້າທ່ານກຳລັງຈຳລອງຫຼອດໄຟນີອອ"
"ນຍາວ 1 ແມັດ ແລະ ກວ້າງ 10 ຊັງຕີແມັດ, ໃຫ້ຕັ້ງຄ່າ area size ເປັນ ``(1, 0.1)`` ແລະ ປັບຄ່າ "
"energy ໃຫ້ເໝາະສົມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:451
msgid ""
"By default, the light's energy is normalized: the larger the area, the "
"weaker the light. This allows you to change the area size without needing to "
"adjust the energy to compensate, which is useful for animation. You can "
"disable this behavior by unchecking **Area > Normalize Energy** if you want "
"the energy to be independent of the area size."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ພະລັງງານຂອງແສງຈະຖືກເຮັດໃຫ້ເປັນຄ່າປົກກະຕິ (normalized): ຍິ່ງພື້ນທີ່ໃຫຍ່ ແສງກໍຍິ່ງອ່ອນ"
"ລົງ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ທ່ານປ່ຽນຂະໜາດພື້ນທີ່ໄດ້ໂດຍບໍ່ຕ້ອງໄປປັບ energy ເພື່ອຊົດເຊີຍ, ເຊິ່ງມີປະໂຫຍດສຳລັບການເຮັດ"
"ອານິເມຊັນ. ທ່ານສາມາດປິດພຶດຕິກຳນີ້ໄດ້ໂດຍການຍົກເລີກການໝາຍ **Area > Normalize Energy** ຖ້າທ່າ"
"ນຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ energy ເປັນອິດສະຫຼະຈາກຂະໜາດພື້ນທີ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:457
msgid ""
"The rectangular area can optionally be textured. This can be effectively "
"used to change the light's shape into any 2D shape, or tint it in different "
"colors. The texture's alpha channel is treated as black (no light coming "
"through). The area light's texture will be visible in reflections according "
"to the surface's roughness. This behavior is different from omni/spot "
"projectors, as it does not project the texture directly onto all diffuse "
"lighting."
msgstr ""
"ພື້ນທີ່ຮູບສີ່ຫຼ່ຽມຜືນຜ້າສາມາດໃສ່ພື້ນຜິວ (texture) ໄດ້. ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດໃຊ້ເພື່ອປ່ຽນຮູບຮ່າງ ຂອງແສງໃຫ້ເປັນຮູບ "
"2D ໃດໆກໍໄດ້, ຫຼື ຍ້ອມສີໃຫ້ເປັນສີຕ່າງໆ. ຊ່ອງ alpha ຂອງພື້ນຜິວ ຈະຖືກຖືວ່າເປັນສີດຳ (ບໍ່ມີແສງຜ່ານ). ພື້ນຜິວ"
"ຂອງ area light ຈະເບິ່ງເຫັນໄດ້ໃນການສະທ້ອນ ຕາມຄວາມຫຍາບ (roughness) ຂອງພື້ນຜິວ. ພຶດຕິກຳນີ້ແຕ"
"ກຕ່າງຈາກ omni/spot projectors, ເພາະມັນບໍ່ໄດ້ສາຍພື້ນຜິວລົງໃສ່ diffuse lighting ທັງໝົດໂດຍກົ"
"ງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:464
msgid ""
"When using a textures that are transparent or black toward the edges, you "
"might want to leave a gap of a few pixels to make sure the texture is "
"blurred smoothly."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອໃຊ້ພື້ນຜິວທີ່ມີຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ ຫຼື ມີສີດຳບໍລິເວນຂອບ, ທ່ານອາດຈະຕ້ອງການເວັ້ນໄລຍະຫ່າງ ສອງສາມພິກເຊວ ເພື່ອ"
"ໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າພື້ນຜິວຈະມົວເຂົ້າກັນຢ່າງນຸ້ມນວນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:472
msgid ""
"Changing the area light's texture at runtime can be expensive, especially if "
"the texture is large."
msgstr ""
"ການປ່ຽນພື້ນຜິວຂອງ area light ໃນລະຫວ່າງການເຮັດວຽກ (runtime) ສາມາດໃຊ້ຊັບພະຍາກອນສູງ, ໂດຍສ"
"ະເພາະຖ້າພື້ນຜິວນັ້ນມີຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:475
msgid ""
"To reduce the performance impact of switching textures at runtime, make sure "
"each dimension of an area texture is either a multiple of 128 pixels, or a "
"power of two. This removes the need for a scaling pass, which slows down "
"texture changes. The textures don't necessarily have to be square to be "
"optimal. Examples of optimal texture sizes include 32×64, 128×128, and "
"256×384."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອຫຼຸດຜົນກະທົບຕໍ່ປະສິດທິພາບໃນການສະຫຼັບພື້ນຜິວໃນ runtime, ໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າແຕ່ລະດ້ານ ຂອງ area "
"texture ມີຂະໜາດເປັນພະຫຸຄູນຂອງ 128 ພິກເຊວ, ຫຼື ເປັນເລກກຳລັງຂອງສອງ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະຊ່ວຍຫຼຸດຄວາມຈຳເປັນໃ"
"ນການເຮັດ scaling pass, ເຊິ່ງເຮັດໃຫ້ການປ່ຽນພື້ນຜິວຊ້າລົງ. ພື້ນຜິວບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງເປັນຮູບຈະຕຸລັດສະເໝີໄປ. "
"ຕົວຢ່າງຂອງຂະໜາດພື້ນຜິວທີ່ເໝາະສົມ ລວມມີ 32×64, 128×128, ແລະ 256×384."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:482
msgid "Textured area lights are not supported in the Compatibility renderer."
msgstr ""
"Area lights ແບບມີພື້ນຜິວ (Textured) ຍັງບໍ່ຮອງຮັບໃນ Compatibility renderer."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:487
msgid "Shadow atlas"
msgstr "Shadow atlas"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:489
msgid ""
"Unlike Directional lights, which have their own shadow texture, omni and "
"spot lights are assigned to slots of a shadow atlas. This atlas can be "
"configured in the advanced Project Settings (**Rendering > Lights And "
"Shadows > Positional Shadow**)."
msgstr ""
"ຕ່າງຈາກ Directional lights ທີ່ມີ shadow texture ຂອງຕົວເອງ, omni ແລະ spot lights ຈະ"
"ຖືກກຳນົດໃຫ້ຢູ່ໃນຊ່ອງ (slots) ຂອງ shadow atlas. atlas ນີ້ສາມາດຕັ້ງຄ່າໄດ້ໃນ Project "
"Settings ລະດັບສູງ (**Rendering > Lights And Shadows > Positional Shadow**)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:493
msgid ""
"The resolution applies to the whole shadow atlas. This atlas is divided into "
"four quadrants:"
msgstr ""
"ຄວາມລະອຽດຈະຖືກໃຊ້ກັບ shadow atlas ທັງໝົດ. atlas ນີ້ຖືກແບ່ງອອກເປັນ 4 ສ່ວນ (quadrants):"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:497
msgid ""
"Each quadrant can be subdivided to allocate any number of shadow maps; the "
"following is the default subdivision:"
msgstr ""
"ແຕ່ລະສ່ວນສາມາດຖືກແບ່ງອອກເປັນສ່ວນຍ່ອຍເພື່ອຈັດສັນຈຳນວນ shadow maps ໄດ້ຕາມຕ້ອງການ; ລຸ່ມນີ້ແມ່ນການແ"
"ບ່ງສ່ວນຍ່ອຍເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:501
msgid "The shadow atlas allocates space as follows:"
msgstr "ແຜນຜັງເງົາ (Shadow atlas) ຈັດສັນພື້ນທີ່ດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:503
msgid ""
"The biggest shadow map size (when no subdivision is used) represents a light "
"the size of the screen (or bigger)."
msgstr ""
"ຂະໜາດ shadow map ທີ່ໃຫຍ່ທີ່ສຸດ (ເມື່ອບໍ່ມີການແບ່ງສ່ວນຍ່ອຍ) ຈະໃຊ້ແທນແສງ ທີ່ມີຂະໜາດເທົ່າໜ້າຈໍ (ຫຼື ໃຫຍ່ກ"
"ວ່າ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:504
msgid ""
"Subdivisions (smaller maps) represent shadows for lights that are further "
"away from view and proportionally smaller."
msgstr ""
"ການແບ່ງສ່ວນຍ່ອຍ (ແຜນຜັງຂະໜາດນ້ອຍລົງ) ຈະໃຊ້ແທນເງົາສຳລັບແສງທີ່ຢູ່ໄກຈາກ ມຸມມອງ ແລະ ມີຂະໜາດນ້ອຍລົງ"
"ຕາມສັດສ່ວນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:506
msgid "Every frame, the following procedure is performed for all lights:"
msgstr "ໃນທຸກໆເຟຣມ, ຂັ້ນຕອນຕໍ່ໄປນີ້ຈະຖືກປະຕິບັດສຳລັບແສງທັງໝົດ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:508
msgid ""
"Check if the light is on a slot of the right size. If not, re-render it and "
"move it to a larger/smaller slot."
msgstr ""
"ກວດເບິ່ງວ່າແສງຢູ່ໃນຊ່ອງ (slot) ທີ່ມີຂະໜາດຖືກຕ້ອງຫຼືບໍ່. ຖ້າບໍ່, ໃຫ້ສະແດງຜົນໃໝ່ ແລ້ວຍ້າຍມັນໄປຍັງຊ່ອງທີ່ໃຫຍ່"
"ຂຶ້ນ ຫຼື ນ້ອຍລົງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:509
msgid ""
"Check if any object affecting the shadow map has changed. If it did, re-"
"render the light."
msgstr ""
"ກວດເບິ່ງວ່າມີວັດຖຸໃດໜຶ່ງທີ່ສົ່ງຜົນຕໍ່ shadow map ປ່ຽນແປງຫຼືບໍ່. ຖ້າມີ, ໃຫ້ສະແດງຜົນແສງໃໝ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:510
msgid ""
"If neither of the above has happened, nothing is done, and the shadow is "
"left untouched."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າບໍ່ມີສິ່ງໃດໃນສອງຂໍ້ຂ້າງເທິງເກີດຂຶ້ນ, ຈະບໍ່ມີການເຮັດຫຍັງ ແລະ ປ່ອຍເງົາໄວ້ຄືເກົ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:512
msgid ""
"If the slots in a quadrant are full, lights are pushed back to smaller "
"slots, depending on size and distance. If all slots in all quadrants are "
"full, some lights will not be able to render shadows even if shadows are "
"enabled on them."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າຊ່ອງໃນ quadrant ໃດໜຶ່ງເຕັມ, ແສງຈະຖືກດັນກັບໄປຍັງຊ່ອງທີ່ນ້ອຍກວ່າ, ຂຶ້ນກັບ ຂະໜາດ ແລະ ໄລຍະຫ່າງ. "
"ຖ້າທຸກຊ່ອງໃນທຸກ quadrants ເຕັມ, ແສງບາງອັນຈະບໍ່ສາມາດ ສະແດງຜົນເງົາໄດ້ ເຖິງວ່າຈະເປີດໃຊ້ເງົາໃນແສງ"
"ນັ້ນໆແລ້ວກໍຕາມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:516
msgid ""
"The default shadow allocation strategy allows rendering up to 88 lights with "
"shadows enabled in the camera frustum (4 + 4 + 16 + 64):"
msgstr ""
"ກົນລະຍຸດການຈັດສັນເງົາເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ ອະນຸຍາດໃຫ້ສະແດງຜົນແສງໄດ້ສູງສຸດ 88 ອັນ ທີ່ເປີດໃຊ້ເງົາ ໃນ camera "
"frustum (4 + 4 + 16 + 64):"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:519
msgid "The first and most detailed quadrant can store 4 shadows."
msgstr "ສ່ວນສີ່ທຳອິດ ແລະ ມີລາຍລະອຽດສູງສຸດ ສາມາດເກັບເງົາໄດ້ 4 ອັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:520
msgid "The second quadrant can store 4 other shadows."
msgstr "ສ່ວນສີ່ທີສອງ ສາມາດເກັບເງົາອື່ນໆໄດ້ອີກ 4 ອັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:521
msgid "The third quadrant can store 16 shadows, with less detail."
msgstr "ສ່ວນສີ່ທີສາມ ສາມາດເກັບເງົາໄດ້ 16 ອັນ, ທີ່ມີລາຍລະອຽດໜ້ອຍລົງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:522
msgid ""
"The fourth and least detailed quadrant can store 64 shadows, with even less "
"detail."
msgstr ""
"ສ່ວນສີ່ທີສີ່ ແລະ ມີລາຍລະອຽດໜ້ອຍທີ່ສຸດ ສາມາດເກັບເງົາໄດ້ 64 ອັນ, ທີ່ມີລາຍລະອຽດໜ້ອຍລົງໄປອີກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:524
msgid ""
"Using a higher number of shadows per quadrant allows supporting a greater "
"amount of total lights with shadows enabled, while also improving "
"performance (as shadows will be rendered at a lower resolution for each "
"light). However, increasing the number of shadows per quadrant comes at the "
"cost of lower shadow quality."
msgstr ""
"ການໃຊ້ຈຳນວນເງົາຕໍ່ quadrant ທີ່ສູງຂຶ້ນ ຈະຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ຮອງຮັບຈຳນວນແສງທີ່ເປີດໃຊ້ເງົາໄດ້ຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນ, ພ້ອມທັງປັບປຸງ"
"ປະສິດທິພາບ (ເນື່ອງຈາກເງົາຈະຖືກສະແດງຜົນໃນຄວາມລະອຽດທີ່ຕໍ່າລົງສຳລັບແຕ່ລະແສງ). ຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ການເພີ່"
"ມຈຳນວນເງົາຕໍ່ quadrant ຈະຕ້ອງແລກດ້ວຍຄຸນນະພາບເງົາທີ່ຕໍ່າລົງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:530
msgid ""
"In some cases, you may want to use a different allocation strategy. For "
"example, in a top-down game where all lights are around the same size, you "
"may want to set all quadrants to have the same subdivision so that all "
"lights have shadows of similar quality level."
msgstr ""
"ໃນບາງກໍລະນີ, ທ່ານອາດຈະຕ້ອງການໃຊ້ກົນລະຍຸດການຈັດສັນທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນ. ຕົວຢ່າງ: ໃນເກມມຸມມອງຈາກເທິງລົງລຸ່"
"ມ (top-down) ທີ່ແສງທັງໝົດມີຂະໜາດໃກ້ຄຽງກັນ, ທ່ານອາດຈະ ຕ້ອງການຕັ້ງຄ່າທຸກ quadrants ໃຫ້ມີການແບ່ງ"
"ສ່ວນຍ່ອຍຄືກັນ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ແສງທັງໝົດມີເງົາ ໃນລະດັບຄຸນນະພາບດຽວກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:538
#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/volumetric_fog.rst:133
msgid "Balancing performance and quality"
msgstr "ການສ້າງຄວາມສົມດຸນລະຫວ່າງປະສິດທິພາບ ແລະ ຄຸນນະພາບ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:540
msgid ""
"Shadow rendering is a critical topic in 3D rendering performance. It's "
"important to make the right choices here to avoid creating bottlenecks."
msgstr ""
"ການສະແດງຜົນເງົາແມ່ນຫົວຂໍ້ທີ່ສຳຄັນໃນປະສິດທິພາບການສະແດງຜົນ 3D. ມັນສຳຄັນຫຼາຍທີ່ ຈະຕ້ອງເລືອກໃຫ້ຖືກຕ້ອງເ"
"ພື່ອຫຼີກລ່ຽງການເກີດຄໍຂວດ (bottlenecks)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:543
msgid ""
"Directional shadow quality settings can be changed at runtime by calling the "
"appropriate :ref:`class_RenderingServer` methods."
msgstr ""
"ການຕັ້ງຄ່າຄຸນນະພາບເງົາ Directional ສາມາດປ່ຽນແປງໄດ້ໃນ runtime ໂດຍການເອີ້ນໃຊ້ ເມທອດ "
":ref:`class_RenderingServer` ທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:546
msgid ""
"Positional (omni/spot) shadow quality settings can be changed at runtime on "
"the root :ref:`class_Viewport`."
msgstr ""
"ການຕັ້ງຄ່າຄຸນນະພາບເງົາ Positional (omni/spot) ສາມາດປ່ຽນແປງໄດ້ໃນ runtime ຜ່ານ root "
":ref:`class_Viewport`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:550
msgid "Shadow map size"
msgstr "ຂະໜາດ Shadow map"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:552
msgid ""
"High shadow resolutions result in sharper shadows, but at a significant "
"performance cost. It should also be noted that *sharper shadows are not "
"always more realistic*. In most cases, this should be kept at its default "
"value of ``4096`` or decreased to ``2048`` for low-end GPUs."
msgstr ""
"ຄວາມລະອຽດເງົາທີ່ສູງຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ໄດ້ເງົາທີ່ຄົມຊັດ, ແຕ່ຕ້ອງແລກດ້ວຍການໃຊ້ຊັບພະຍາກອນທີ່ສູງຫຼາຍ. ນອກຈາກນັ້ນຄວ"
"ນສັງເກດວ່າ *ເງົາທີ່ຄົມຊັດກວ່າ ບໍ່ໄດ້ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າຈະສົມຈິງກວ່າສະເໝີໄປ*. ໃນເກືອບທຸກກໍລະນີ, ຄວນຕັ້ງຄ່ານີ້ໄວ້ທີ່"
"ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ ``4096`` ຫຼື ຫຼຸດລົງເປັນ ``2048`` ສຳລັບ GPU ສະເປັກຕໍ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:557
msgid ""
"If positional shadows become too blurry after decreasing the shadow map "
"size, you can counteract this by adjusting the :ref:`shadow atlas "
"<doc_lights_and_shadows_shadow_atlas>` quadrants to contain fewer shadows. "
"This will allow each shadow to be rendered at a higher resolution."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເງົາ positional ເບິ່ງມົວເກີນໄປຫຼັງຈາກຫຼຸດຂະໜາດ shadow map ລົງ, ທ່ານສາມາດແກ້ໄຂ ໂດຍການປັບ "
":ref:`shadow atlas <doc_lights_and_shadows_shadow_atlas>` quadrants ໃຫ້ເກັບເງົາໜ້"
"ອຍລົງ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ແຕ່ລະເງົາຖືກສະແດງຜົນໃນຄວາມລະອຽດທີ່ສູງຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:565
msgid "Shadow filter mode"
msgstr "ໂໝດການກັ່ນຕອງເງົາ (Shadow filter mode)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:567
msgid ""
"Several shadow map quality settings can be chosen here. The default **Soft "
"Low** is a good balance between performance and quality for scenes with "
"detailed textures, as the texture detail will help make the dithering "
"pattern less noticeable."
msgstr ""
"ມີການຕັ້ງຄ່າຄຸນນະພາບ shadow map ຫຼາຍຢ່າງໃຫ້ເລືອກ. ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ **Soft Low** ແມ່ນ ຈຸດສົມດຸນທີ່ດີລະຫ"
"ວ່າງປະສິດທິພາບ ແລະ ຄຸນນະພາບສຳລັບສາກທີ່ມີພື້ນຜິວ (textures) ທີ່ມີລາຍລະອຽດ, ເພາະລາຍລະອຽດພື້ນຜິວຈ"
"ະຊ່ວຍເຮັດໃຫ້ລວດລາຍ dithering ເບິ່ງເຫັນໄດ້ຍາກຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:571
msgid ""
"However, in projects with less detailed textures, the shadow dithering "
"pattern may be more visible. To hide this pattern, you can either "
"enable :ref:`doc_3d_antialiasing_taa`, :ref:`doc_3d_antialiasing_fsr2`, :ref:`doc_3d_antialiasing_fxaa`, "
"or increase the shadow filter quality to **Soft Medium** or higher."
msgstr ""
"ຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ໃນໂປຣເຈັກທີ່ມີພື້ນຜິວລາຍລະອຽດໜ້ອຍ, ລວດລາຍ shadow dithering ອາດຈະ ເຫັນໄດ້ຊັດເຈ"
"ນຂຶ້ນ. ເພື່ອເຊື່ອງລວດລາຍນີ້, ທ່ານສາມາດເປີດໃຊ້ :ref:`doc_3d_antialiasing_taa`, "
":ref:`doc_3d_antialiasing_fsr2`, :ref:`doc_3d_antialiasing_fxaa`, ຫຼື ເພີ່ມ ຄຸນນະພ"
"າບ shadow filter ເປັນ **Soft Medium** ຫຼື ສູງກວ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:577
msgid ""
"The **Soft Very Low** setting will automatically decrease shadow blur to "
"make artifacts from the low sample count less visible. Conversely, the "
"**Soft High** and **Soft Ultra** settings will automatically increase shadow "
"blur to better make use of the increased sample count."
msgstr ""
"ການຕັ້ງຄ່າ **Soft Very Low** ຈະຫຼຸດ shadow blur ລົງໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ ເພື່ອເຮັດໃຫ້ ຈຸດບົກພ່ອງ "
"(artifacts) ຈາກການສຸ່ມຕົວຢ່າງທີ່ຕໍ່າເຫັນໄດ້ຍາກຂຶ້ນ. ໃນທາງກົງກັນຂ້າມ, ການຕັ້ງຄ່າ **Soft High** ແ"
"ລະ **Soft Ultra** ຈະເພີ່ມ shadow blur ໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ໃຊ້ປະໂຫຍດຈາກຈຳນວນການສຸ່ມຕົວຢ່"
"າງທີ່ເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນໄດ້ດີກວ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:585
msgid "16-bits versus 32-bit"
msgstr "16-ບິດ ທຽບກັບ 32-ບິດ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:587
msgid ""
"By default, Godot uses 16-bit depth textures for shadow map rendering. This "
"is recommended in most cases as it performs better without a noticeable "
"difference in quality."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, Godot ຈະໃຊ້ depth textures ແບບ 16-ບິດ ສຳລັບການສະແດງຜົນ shadow map. ສິ່ງ"
"ນີ້ແມ່ນແນະນຳໃນເກືອບທຸກກໍລະນີ ເພາະມັນເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ໄວກວ່າໂດຍທີ່ຄຸນນະພາບ ບໍ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນຫຼາຍຈົນສັງເກດໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:591
msgid ""
"If **16 Bits** is disabled, 32-bit depth textures will be used instead. This "
"can result in less artifacting in large scenes and large lights with shadows "
"enabled. However, the difference is often barely visible, yet this can have "
"a significant performance cost."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າປິດ **16 Bits**, ຈະມີການໃຊ້ depth textures ແບບ 32-ບິດ ແທນ. ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດ ຫຼຸດການເກີດ "
"artifacts ໃນສາກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ ແລະ ແສງຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ທີ່ເປີດໃຊ້ເງົາ. ຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ຄວາມແຕກຕ່າງມັກຈະເຫັ"
"ນໄດ້ຍາກຫຼາຍ, ແຕ່ອາດຈະຕ້ອງແລກດ້ວຍປະສິດທິພາບທີ່ຫຼຸດລົງຢ່າງຊັດເຈນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:597
msgid "Light/shadow distance fade"
msgstr "Light/shadow distance fade (ການຈາງຫາຍຂອງແສງ/ເງົາຕາມໄລຍະຫ່າງ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:599
msgid ""
"OmniLight3D and SpotLight3D offer several properties to hide distant lights. "
"This can improve performance significantly in large scenes with dozens of "
"lights or more."
msgstr ""
"OmniLight3D ແລະ SpotLight3D ມີຄຸນສົມບັດຫຼາຍຢ່າງເພື່ອເຊື່ອງແສງທີ່ຢູ່ໄກ. ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດປັບປຸງປະສິດທິພາບ"
"ໄດ້ຢ່າງຫຼວງຫຼາຍໃນສາກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ທີ່ມີແສງເປັນສິບ ຫຼື ຫຼາຍກວ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:603
msgid ""
"**Enabled:** Controls whether distance fade (a form of :abbr:`LOD (Level of "
"Detail)`) is enabled. The light will fade out over **Begin + Length**, after "
"which it will be culled and not sent to the shader at all. Use this to "
"reduce the number of active lights in a scene and thus improve performance."
msgstr ""
"**Enabled:** ຄວບຄຸມການເປີດໃຊ້ distance fade (ຮູບແບບໜຶ່ງຂອງ :abbr:`LOD (Level of "
"Detail)`). ແສງຈະຄ່ອຍໆຈາງຫາຍໄປໃນໄລຍະ **Begin + Length**, ຫຼັງຈາກນັ້ນມັນຈະຖືກຄັດອອກ "
"(culled) ແລະ ບໍ່ຖືກສົ່ງໄປໃຫ້ shader ເລີຍ. ໃຊ້ສິ່ງນີ້ເພື່ອຫຼຸດຈຳນວນແສງທີ່ເຮັດວຽກໃນສາກ ແລະ ຊ່ວຍເພີ່ມປ"
"ະສິດທິພາບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:607
msgid ""
"**Begin:** The distance from the camera at which the light begins to fade "
"away (in 3D units)."
msgstr "**Begin:** ໄລຍະຫ່າງຈາກກ້ອງທີ່ແສງເລີ່ມຈາງຫາຍໄປ (ເປັນຫົວໜ່ວຍ 3D)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:609
msgid ""
"**Shadow:** The distance from the camera at which the shadow begins to fade "
"away (in 3D units). This can be used to fade out shadows sooner compared to "
"the light, further improving performance. Only available if shadows are "
"enabled for the light."
msgstr ""
"**Shadow:** ໄລຍະຫ່າງຈາກກ້ອງທີ່ເງົາເລີ່ມຈາງຫາຍໄປ (ເປັນຫົວໜ່ວຍ 3D). ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດ ໃຊ້ເພື່ອເຮັດໃຫ້ເງົ"
"າຈາງຫາຍໄວຂຶ້ນເມື່ອທຽບກັບແສງ, ເພື່ອເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບໃຫ້ດີຂຶ້ນ. ໃຊ້ໄດ້ສະເພາະຖ້າແສງນັ້ນເປີດໃຊ້ເງົາເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:612
msgid ""
"**Length:** The distance over which the light and shadow fades (in 3D "
"units). The light becomes slowly more transparent over this distance and is "
"completely invisible at the end. Higher values result in a smoother fade-out "
"transition, which is more suited when the camera moves fast."
msgstr ""
"**Length:** ໄລຍະທາງທີ່ແສງ ແລະ ເງົາຈະໃຊ້ໃນການຈາງຫາຍ (ເປັນຫົວໜ່ວຍ 3D). ແສງຈະຄ່ອຍໆໂປ່ງໃສຂຶ້"
"ນໃນໄລຍະທາງນີ້ ແລະ ຈະຫາຍໄປທັງໝົດໃນຕອນທ້າຍ. ຄ່າທີ່ສູງຂຶ້ນ ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ການປ່ຽນແປງນຸ້ມນວນຂຶ້ນ, ເຊິ່ງເໝາະ"
"ສົມເມື່ອກ້ອງເຄື່ອນໄຫວໄວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:620
msgid "PCSS recommendations"
msgstr "ຄຳແນະນຳສຳລັບ PCSS"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:622
msgid ""
"Percentage-closer soft shadows (PCSS) provide a more realistic shadow "
"mapping appearance, with the penumbra size varying depending on the distance "
"between the caster and the surface receiving the shadow. This comes at a "
"high performance cost, especially for directional lights."
msgstr ""
"Percentage-closer soft shadows (PCSS) ໃຫ້ຮູບລັກສະນະ shadow mapping ທີ່ສົມຈິງກວ່າ, ໂດຍ"
"ຂະໜາດຂອງຂອບເງົາ (penumbra) ຈະປ່ຽນແປງຕາມໄລຍະຫ່າງລະຫວ່າງວັດຖຸສ້າງເງົາ ແລະ ພື້ນຜິວທີ່ຮັບເງົາ. ສິ່"
"ງນີ້ມາພ້ອມກັບຄ່າໃຊ້ຈ່າຍຊັບພະຍາກອນທີ່ສູງ, ໂດຍສະເພາະສຳລັບ directional lights."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:627
msgid "To avoid performance issues, it's recommended to:"
msgstr "ເພື່ອຫຼີກລ່ຽງບັນຫາປະສິດທິພາບ, ແນະນຳໃຫ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:629
msgid ""
"Only use a handful of lights with PCSS shadows enabled at a given time. The "
"effect is generally most visible on large, bright lights. Secondary light "
"sources that are more faint usually don't benefit much from using PCSS "
"shadows."
msgstr ""
"ໃຊ້ແສງທີ່ເປີດເງົາແບບ PCSS ພຽງແຕ່ບໍ່ເທົ່າໃດອັນໃນເວລາດຽວກັນ. ເອັບເຟັກນີ້ມັກຈະ ເຫັນໄດ້ຊັດເຈນທີ່ສຸດໃນແສງ"
"ຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ ແລະ ສະຫວ່າງ. ແຫຼ່ງກຳເນີດແສງສໍາຮອງທີ່ ບໍ່ຄ່ອຍສະຫວ່າງມັກຈະບໍ່ໄດ້ຮັບຜົນປະໂຫຍດຫຼາຍຈາກການໃ"
"ຊ້ PCSS."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:633
msgid ""
"Provide a setting for users to disable PCSS shadows. On directional lights, "
"this can be done by setting the DirectionalLight3D's "
"``light_angular_distance`` property to ``0.0`` in a script. On positional "
"lights, this can be done by setting the OmniLight3D or SpotLight3D's "
"``light_size`` property to ``0.0`` in a script."
msgstr ""
"ມີການຕັ້ງຄ່າໃຫ້ຜູ້ໃຊ້ສາມາດປິດເງົາ PCSS ໄດ້. ສຳລັບ directional lights, ສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ ໂດຍການຕັ້ງ"
"ຄ່າຄຸນສົມບັດ ``light_angular_distance`` ຂອງ DirectionalLight3D ເປັນ ``0.0`` ໃນສະຄຣິ"
"ບ. ສຳລັບ positional lights, ສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ໂດຍການຕັ້ງຄ່າຄຸນສົມບັດ ``light_size`` ຂອງ "
"OmniLight3D ຫຼື SpotLight3D ເປັນ ``0.0`` ໃນສະຄຣິບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:640
msgid "Projector filter mode"
msgstr "ໂໝດການກັ່ນຕອງ Projector (Projector filter mode)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:642
msgid ""
"The way projectors are rendered also has an impact on performance. The "
"**Rendering > Textures > Light Projectors > Filter** advanced project "
"setting lets you control how projector textures should be filtered. "
"**Nearest/Linear** do not use mipmaps, which makes them faster to render. "
"However, projectors will look grainy at distance. **Nearest/Linear Mipmaps** "
"will look smoother at a distance, but projectors will look blurry when "
"viewed from oblique angles. This can be resolved by using **Nearest/Linear "
"Mipmaps Anisotropic**, which is the highest-quality mode, but also the most "
"expensive."
msgstr ""
"ວິທີທີ່ projectors ຖືກສະແດງຜົນຍັງສົ່ງຜົນກະທົບຕໍ່ປະສິດທິພາບນຳ. ການຕັ້ງຄ່າໂປຣເຈັກ ລະດັບສູງ "
"**Rendering > Textures > Light Projectors > Filter** ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ທ່ານຄວບຄຸມ ວິທີການກັ່ນຕອ"
"ງ projector textures. **Nearest/Linear** ບໍ່ໃຊ້ mipmaps, ເຊິ່ງເຮັດໃຫ້ ສະແດງຜົນໄດ້ໄວຂຶ້"
"ນ. ແຕ່ projectors ຈະເບິ່ງຄືເປັນເມັດໆ (grainy) ໃນໄລຍະໄກ. **Nearest/Linear Mipmaps** "
"ຈະເບິ່ງນຸ້ມນວນຂຶ້ນໃນໄລຍະໄກ, ແຕ່ຈະເບິ່ງມົວເມື່ອ ເບິ່ງຈາກມຸມອຽງ. ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດແກ້ໄຂໄດ້ໂດຍໃຊ້ "
"**Nearest/Linear Mipmaps Anisotropic**, ເຊິ່ງເປັນໂໝດທີ່ມີຄຸນນະພາບສູງສຸດ ແຕ່ກໍໃຊ້ຊັບພະຍາກອນ"
"ຫຼາຍທີ່ສຸດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/lights_and_shadows.rst:651
msgid ""
"If your project has a pixel art style, consider setting the filter to one of "
"the **Nearest** values so that projectors use nearest-neighbor filtering. "
"Otherwise, stick to **Linear**."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າໂປຣເຈັກຂອງທ່ານເປັນສະໄຕລ໌ pixel art, ໃຫ້ພິຈາລະນາຕັ້ງຄ່າ filter ເປັນຄ່າ **Nearest** ໜຶ່ງໃດ"
"ໜຶ່ງ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ projectors ໃຊ້ການກັ່ນຕອງແບບ nearest-neighbor. ຖ້າບໍ່ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ **Linear** "
"ຕາມເດີມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/using_decals.rst:4
msgid "Using decals"
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ດີຄໍ (Decals)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/using_decals.rst:8
msgid ""
"Decals are only supported in the Forward+ and Mobile renderers, not the "
"Compatibility renderer."
msgstr ""
"ດີຄໍ (Decals) ຮອງຮັບສະເພາະໃນ Forward+ ແລະ Mobile renderers ເທົ່ານັ້ນ, ບໍ່ຮອງຮັບໃນ "
"Compatibility renderer."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/using_decals.rst:11
msgid ""
"If using the Compatibility renderer, consider using Sprite3D as an "
"alternative for projecting decals onto (mostly) flat surfaces."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າໃຊ້ Compatibility renderer, ໃຫ້ພິຈາລະນາໃຊ້ Sprite3D ເປັນທາງເລືອກໃນການວາງດີຄໍ ລົງເທິງພື້"
"ນຜິວທີ່ (ສ່ວນຫຼາຍ) ຮາບພຽງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/using_decals.rst:14
msgid ""
"Decals are projected textures that apply on opaque or transparent surfaces "
"in 3D. This projection happens in real-time and doesn't rely on mesh "
"generation. This allows you to move decals every frame with only a small "
"performance impact, even when applied on complex meshes."
msgstr ""
"ດີຄໍ ແມ່ນພື້ນຜິວ (textures) ທີ່ຖືກສາຍລົງໃສ່ວັດຖຸ 3D ບໍ່ວ່າຈະເປັນພື້ນຜິວແບບທຶບແສງ ຫຼື ໂປ່ງແສງ. ການສາຍນີ້"
"ເກີດຂຶ້ນແບບ real-time ແລະ ບໍ່ໄດ້ອາໄສການສ້າງ mesh ໃໝ່. ສິ່ງນີ້ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ທ່ານ ສາມາດເຄື່ອນຍ້າຍດີຄໍໄດ້ໃນທຸ"
"ກໆເຟຣມໂດຍສົ່ງຜົນກະທົບຕໍ່ປະສິດທິພາບພຽງເລັກນ້ອຍ, ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າ ຈະໃຊ້ກັບ mesh ທີ່ມີຄວາມຊັບຊ້ອນກໍຕາມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/using_decals.rst:19
msgid ""
"While decals cannot add actual geometry detail onto the projected surface, "
"decals can still make use of physically-based rendering to provide similar "
"properties to full-blown :abbr:`PBR (Physically-Based Rendering)` materials."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງວ່າດີຄໍຈະບໍ່ສາມາດເພີ່ມລາຍລະອຽດ geometry ຕົວຈິງລົງໃນພື້ນຜິວທີ່ຖືກສາຍໄດ້, ແຕ່ດີຄໍຍັງສາມາດໃຊ້ "
"physically-based rendering ເພື່ອໃຫ້ຄຸນສົມບັດທີ່ຄ້າຍຄືກັບ ວັດສະດຸ :abbr:`PBR (Physically-"
"Based Rendering)` ແບບເຕັມຮູບແບບໄດ້."

