msgid "Example VRS density map texture, simulating foveated rendering"
msgstr "ຕົວຢ່າງ VRS density map texture, ຈຳລອງ foveated rendering"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/variable_rate_shading.rst:166
msgid ""
"There are no size or aspect ratio requirements for the VRS density texture. "
"However, there is no benefit to using a VRS density map that is larger than "
"the viewport resolution divided by the GPU's *tile size*. The tile size is "
"what determines the smallest area of pixels where the shading density can be "
"changed separately from other tiles. On most GPUs, this tile size is 8×8 "
"pixels. You can view the tile size by running Godot with the ``--verbose`` "
"command line argument, as it's printed in the VRS debugging information."
msgstr ""
"ບໍ່ມີຂໍ້ກຳນົດເລື່ອງຂະໜາດ ຫຼື ອັດຕາສ່ວນ (aspect ratio) ສຳລັບ VRS density texture. ແນວໃດກໍຕາ"
"ມ, ມັນບໍ່ມີປະໂຫຍດຫຍັງທີ່ຈະໃຊ້ density map ທີ່ມີຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ກວ່າ ຄວາມລະອຽດໜ້າຈໍຫານດ້ວຍ *tile "
"size* ຂອງ GPU. tile size ແມ່ນສິ່ງທີ່ກຳນົດພື້ນທີ່ ພິກເຊລທີ່ນ້ອຍທີ່ສຸດທີ່ສາມາດປ່ຽນຄວາມລະອຽດການໃຫ້ເງົາ"
"ແຍກຈາກສ່ວນອື່ນໄດ້. ໃນ GPU ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່, tile size ນີ້ແມ່ນ 8×8 ພິກເຊລ. ເຈົ້າສາມາດເບິ່ງ tile "
"size ໄດ້ໂດຍການ ເປີດ Godot ດ້ວຍ ``--verbose`` ເພາະມັນຈະສະແດງໃນຂໍ້ມູນ debug ຂອງ VRS."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/variable_rate_shading.rst:174
msgid ""
"Therefore, sticking to a relatively low resolution such as 256×256 (square) "
"or 480×270 (16:9) is recommended. Depending on your use cases, a square "
"texture may be more suited compared to a texture that matches the most "
"common viewport aspect ratio in your project (such as 16:9)."
msgstr ""
"ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ຈຶ່ງແນະນຳໃຫ້ໃຊ້ຄວາມລະອຽດທີ່ຂ້ອນຂ້າງຕ່ຳ ເຊັ່ນ 256×256 (ສີ່ຫຼ່ຽມ) ຫຼື 480×270 (16:9). ຂຶ້ນຢູ່ກັ"
"ບການໃຊ້ງານ, ເທັກເຈີຮູບສີ່ຫຼ່ຽມອາດຈະເໝາະສົມກວ່າເທັກເຈີທີ່ມີອັດຕາສ່ວນ ກົງກັບໜ້າຈໍເກມ (ເຊັ່ນ 16:9)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/variable_rate_shading.rst:181
msgid ""
"When using variable rate shading, you can use a negative :ref:`texture "
"mipmap LOD bias <doc_resolution_scaling_mipmap_bias>` to reduce blurriness "
"in areas with reduced shading rate."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອໃຊ້ VRS, ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ຄ່າລົບສຳລັບ :ref:`texture mipmap LOD bias "
"<doc_resolution_scaling_mipmap_bias>` ເພື່ອຫຼຸດຄວາມເບີໃນບໍລິເວນທີ່ຫຼຸດອັດຕາການໃຫ້ເງົາລົງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/variable_rate_shading.rst:185
msgid ""
"Note that the texture LOD bias is set globally, so this will also affect "
"areas of the viewport with full shading rate. Don't use values that are too "
"low, or textures will appear grainy."
msgstr ""
"ໝາຍເຫດວ່າ texture LOD bias ຖືກຕັ້ງຄ່າແບບທົ່ວໂລກ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນມັນຈະມີຜົນຕໍ່ບໍລິເວນໜ້າຈໍ ທີ່ມີອັດຕາການໃຫ້ເງົາ"
"ເຕັມນຳ. ຢ່າໃຊ້ຄ່າທີ່ຕ່ຳເກີນໄປ ບໍ່ດັ່ງນັ້ນເທັກເຈີຈະເບິ່ງເປັນເມັດໆ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/variable_rate_shading.rst:190
msgid "Performance comparison"
msgstr "ການປຽບທຽບປະສິດທິພາບ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/variable_rate_shading.rst:192
msgid ""
"To give an idea of how much VRS can improve performance in theory, here's a "
"performance comparison with the textured example scene shown at the top of "
"this page. The VRS density map example present on this page is used."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອໃຫ້ເຫັນພາບວ່າ VRS ສາມາດເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບໄດ້ຫຼາຍປານໃດໃນທາງທິດສະດີ, ນີ້ແມ່ນການປຽບທຽບ ກັບສາກຕົວ"
"ຢ່າງທີ່ມີເທັກເຈີທີ່ສະແດງຢູ່ດ້ານເທິງ. ໂດຍໃຊ້ VRS density map ຕົວຢ່າງໃນໜ້ານີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/3d/variable_rate_shading.rst:196
msgid ""
"Results were captured on a GeForce RTX 4090 with the NVIDIA 525.60.11 driver."
