msgstr ""
"Cubic Bezier interpolation ເຮັດວຽກຄືກັນໃນ 3D, ພຽງແຕ່ໃຊ້ ``Vector3`` ແທນ "
"``Vector2``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:171
msgid "Adding control points"
msgstr "ການເພີ່ມຈຸດຄວບຄຸມ (control points)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:173
msgid ""
"Building upon Cubic Bezier, we can change the way two of the points work to "
"control the shape of our curve freely. Instead of having ``p0``, ``p1``, "
"``p2`` and ``p3``, we will store them as:"
msgstr ""
"ຈາກ Cubic Bezier, ພວກເຮົາສາມາດປ່ຽນວິທີທີ່ສອງຈຸດເຮັດວຽກເພື່ອຄວບຄຸມຮູບຮ່າງຂອງເສັ້ນໂຄ້ງໄດ້ຢ່າງອິດສະ"
"ຫຼະ. ແທນທີ່ຈະມີ ``p0``, ``p1``, ``p2`` ແລະ ``p3``, ພວກເຮົາຈະເກັບພວກມັນໄວ້ດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:177
msgid "``point0 = p0``: Is the first point, the source"
msgstr "``point0 = p0``: ແມ່ນຈຸດທຳອິດ, ເປັນຈຸດເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ (source)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:178
msgid "``control0 = p1 - p0``: Is a vector relative to the first control point"
msgstr "``control0 = p1 - p0``: ແມ່ນເວກເຕີທີ່ທຽບກັບຈຸດຄວບຄຸມທຳອິດ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:179
msgid ""
"``control1 = p3 - p2``: Is a vector relative to the second control point"
msgstr "``control1 = p3 - p2``: ແມ່ນເວກເຕີທີ່ທຽບກັບຈຸດຄວບຄຸມທີສອງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:180
msgid "``point1 = p3``: Is the second point, the destination"
msgstr "``point1 = p3``: ແມ່ນຈຸດທີສອງ, ເປັນຈຸດປາຍທາງ (destination)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:182
msgid ""
"This way, we have two points and two control points which are relative "
"vectors to the respective points. If you've used graphics or animation "
"software before, this might look familiar:"
msgstr ""
"ດ້ວຍວິທີນີ້, ພວກເຮົາຈະມີສອງຈຸດ ແລະ ສອງຈຸດຄວບຄຸມເຊິ່ງເປັນເວກເຕີທຽບກັບຈຸດນັ້ນໆ. ຖ້າເຈົ້າເຄີຍໃຊ້ຊອບແວຣ໌ກ"
"ຣາຟິກ ຫຼື ແອນິເມຊັນມາກ່ອນ, ສິ່ງນີ້ອາດຈະເບິ່ງຄືຄຸ້ນໆຕາ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:188
msgid ""
"This is how graphics software presents Bezier curves to the users, and how "
"they work and look in Godot."
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ແມ່ນວິທີທີ່ຊອບແວຣ໌ກຣາຟິກສະແດງເສັ້ນໂຄ້ງ Bezier ໃຫ້ຜູ້ໃຊ້ເຫັນ, ແລະ ແມ່ນວິທີທີ່ພວກມັນເຮັດວຽກ ແລະ ສະແດ"
"ງອອກໃນ Godot."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:192
msgid "Curve2D, Curve3D, Path and Path2D"
msgstr "Curve2D, Curve3D, Path ແລະ Path2D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:194
msgid ""
"There are two objects that contain curves: :ref:`Curve3D <class_Curve3D>` "
"and :ref:`Curve2D <class_Curve2D>` (for 3D and 2D respectively)."
msgstr ""
"ມີສອງວັດຖຸທີ່ບັນຈຸເສັ້ນໂຄ້ງຄື: :ref:`Curve3D <class_Curve3D>` ແລະ :ref:`Curve2D "
"<class_Curve2D>` (ສຳລັບ 3D ແລະ 2D ຕາມລຳດັບ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:196
msgid ""
"They can contain several points, allowing for longer paths. It is also "
"possible to set them to nodes: :ref:`Path3D <class_Path3D>` and :ref:`Path2D "
"<class_Path2D>` (also for 3D and 2D respectively):"
msgstr ""
"ພວກມັນສາມາດບັນຈຸຫຼາຍຈຸດ, ເຮັດໃຫ້ສ້າງເສັ້ນທາງທີ່ຍາວຂຶ້ນໄດ້. ມັນຍັງເປັນໄປໄດ້ທີ່ຈະຕັ້ງຄ່າພວກມັນໃຫ້ກັບໂນດ: "
":ref:`Path3D <class_Path3D>` ແລະ :ref:`Path2D <class_Path2D>` (ສຳລັບ 3D ແລະ "
"2D ຕາມລຳດັບ):"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:200
msgid ""
"Using them, however, may not be completely obvious, so following is a "
"description of the most common use cases for Bezier curves."
msgstr ""
"ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ການໃຊ້ພວກມັນອາດຈະບໍ່ຄ່ອຍຈະແຈ້ງປານໃດ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນຕໍ່ໄປນີ້ແມ່ນຄຳອະທິບາຍກ່ຽວກັບກໍລະນີການໃຊ້ງາ"
"ນທີ່ພົບເລື້ອຍທີ່ສຸດສຳລັບເສັ້ນໂຄ້ງ Bezier."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:203
msgid "Evaluating"
msgstr "ການປະເມີນຄ່າ (Evaluating)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:205
msgid ""
"Only evaluating them may be an option, but in most cases it's not very "
"useful. The big drawback with Bezier curves is that if you traverse them at "
"constant speed, from ``t = 0`` to ``t = 1``, the actual interpolation will "
"*not* move at constant speed. The speed is also an interpolation between the "
"distances between points ``p0``, ``p1``, ``p2`` and ``p3`` and there is not "
"a mathematically simple way to traverse the curve at constant speed."
msgstr ""
"ການປະເມີນຄ່າພວກມັນຢ່າງດຽວອາດຈະເປັນທາງເລືອກໜຶ່ງ, ແຕ່ໃນກໍລະນີສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ມັນບໍ່ຄ່ອຍມີປະໂຫຍດຫຼາຍ. ຂໍ້ເສຍໃ"
"ຫຍ່ຂອງເສັ້ນໂຄ້ງ Bezier ແມ່ນຖ້າເຈົ້າເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄປຕາມພວກມັນດ້ວຍຄວາມໄວຄົງທີ່, ຈາກ ``t = 0`` ຫາ ``t "
"= 1``, ການ interpolation ຕົວຈິງຈະ *ບໍ່* ເຄື່ອນທີ່ດ້ວຍຄວາມໄວຄົງທີ່. ຄວາມໄວນັ້ນຍັງເປັນການ "
"interpolation ລະຫວ່າງໄລຍະຫ່າງຂອງຈຸດ ``p0``, ``p1``, ``p2`` ແລະ ``p3`` ແລະ ບໍ່ມີວິທີທາ"
"ງຄະນິດສາດທີ່ງ່າຍໆໃນການເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄປຕາມເສັ້ນໂຄ້ງດ້ວຍຄວາມໄວຄົງທີ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:207
msgid "Let's do an example with the following pseudocode:"
msgstr "ລອງມາເບິ່ງຕົວຢ່າງດ້ວຍ pseudocode ດັ່ງຕໍ່ໄປນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:230
msgid ""
"As you can see, the speed (in pixels per second) of the circle varies, even "
"though ``t`` is increased at constant speed. This makes beziers difficult to "
"use for anything practical out of the box."
msgstr ""
"ດັ່ງທີ່ເຈົ້າເຫັນ, ຄວາມໄວ (ເປັນພິກເຊວຕໍ່ວິນາທີ) ຂອງວົງມົນຈະແຕກຕ່າງກັນ, ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າ ``t`` ຈະເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນດ້ວ"
"ຍຄວາມໄວຄົງທີ່ກໍຕາມ. ສິ່ງນີ້ເຮັດໃຫ້ bezier ຍາກທີ່ຈະນຳໃຊ້ໃນທາງປະຕິບັດໄດ້ທັນທີໂດຍບໍ່ມີການປັບແຕ່ງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:235
msgid ""
"Drawing beziers (or objects based on the curve) is a very common use case, "
"but it's also not easy. For pretty much any case, Bezier curves need to be "
"converted to some sort of segments. This is normally difficult, however, "
"without creating a very high amount of them."
msgstr ""
"ການແຕ້ມ bezier (ຫຼື ວັດຖຸທີ່ອີງໃສ່ເສັ້ນໂຄ້ງ) ແມ່ນກໍລະນີການໃຊ້ງານທີ່ພົບເລື້ອຍຫຼາຍ, ແຕ່ມັນກໍບໍ່ແມ່ນເລື່ອງງ່າ"
"ຍ. ເກືອບທຸກກໍລະນີ, ເສັ້ນໂຄ້ງ Bezier ຕ້ອງຖືກແປງເປັນສ່ວນໆ (segments). ໂດຍປົກກະຕິແລ້ວມັນຈະຍາກ ຖ້"
"າຈະເຮັດໂດຍບໍ່ສ້າງຈຳນວນສ່ວນທີ່ຫຼາຍເກີນໄປ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:237
msgid ""
"The reason is that some sections of a curve (specifically, corners) may "
"require considerable amounts of points, while other sections may not:"
msgstr ""
"ເຫດຜົນແມ່ນຍ້ອນວ່າບາງສ່ວນຂອງເສັ້ນໂຄ້ງ (ໂດຍສະເພາະສ່ວນທີ່ເປັນມຸມ) ອາດຈະຕ້ອງການຈຳນວນຈຸດທີ່ຫຼາຍ, ໃນຂ"
"ະນະທີ່ສ່ວນອື່ນໆອາດຈະບໍ່ຕ້ອງການ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:241
msgid ""
"Additionally, if both control points were ``0, 0`` (remember they are "
"relative vectors), the Bezier curve would just be a straight line (so "
"drawing a high amount of points would be wasteful)."
msgstr ""
"ນອກຈາກນັ້ນ, ຖ້າຈຸດຄວບຄຸມທັງສອງເປັນ ``0, 0`` (ຈື່ໄວ້ວ່າພວກມັນແມ່ນເວກເຕີທຽບເຄຽງ), ເສັ້ນໂຄ້ງ "
"Bezier ກໍຈະເປັນພຽງເສັ້ນຊື່ (ດັ່ງນັ້ນການແຕ້ມຈຸດຈຳນວນຫຼາຍຈຶ່ງເປັນການສິ້ນເປືອງ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:243
msgid ""
"Before drawing Bezier curves, *tessellation* is required. This is often done "
"with a recursive or divide and conquer function that splits the curve until "
"the curvature amount becomes less than a certain threshold."
msgstr ""
"ກ່ອນທີ່ຈະແຕ້ມເສັ້ນໂຄ້ງ Bezier, ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງເຮັດ *tessellation* ກ່ອນ. ສິ່ງນີ້ມັກຈະເຮັດດ້ວຍຟັງຊັນ "
"recursive ຫຼື divide and conquer ທີ່ແບ່ງເສັ້ນໂຄ້ງອອກຈົນກວ່າລະດັບຄວາມໂຄ້ງຈະໜ້ອຍກວ່າເກນທີ່ກຳນົດໄ"
"ວ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:245
msgid ""
"The *Curve* classes provide this via the :ref:`Curve2D.tessellate() "
"<class_Curve2D_method_tessellate>` function (which receives optional "
"``stages`` of recursion and angle ``tolerance`` arguments). This way, "
"drawing something based on a curve is easier."
msgstr ""
"ຄລາສ *Curve* ມີຟັງຊັນນີ້ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ຜ່ານ :ref:`Curve2D.tessellate() "
"<class_Curve2D_method_tessellate>` (ເຊິ່ງຮັບພາຣາມິເຕີເສີມຄື ``stages`` ຂອງ "
"recursion ແລະ ມຸມ ``tolerance``). ດ້ວຍວິທີນີ້, ການແຕ້ມບາງສິ່ງທີ່ອີງໃສ່ເສັ້ນໂຄ້ງຈຶ່ງງ່າຍຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:249
msgid "Traversal"
msgstr "ການເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄປຕາມເສັ້ນ (Traversal)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:251
msgid ""
"The last common use case for the curves is to traverse them. Because of what "
"was mentioned before regarding constant speed, this is also difficult."
msgstr ""
"ກໍລະນີການໃຊ້ງານທົ່ວໄປສຸດທ້າຍສຳລັບເສັ້ນໂຄ້ງແມ່ນການເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄປຕາມພວກມັນ. ເນື່ອງຈາກສິ່ງທີ່ໄດ້ກ່າວມາກ່ອນໜ້ານີ້"
"ກ່ຽວກັບຄວາມໄວຄົງທີ່, ສິ່ງນີ້ຈຶ່ງຍາກເຊັ່ນກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:253
msgid ""
"To make this easier, the curves need to be *baked* into equidistant points. "
"This way, they can be approximated with regular interpolation (which can be "
"improved further with a cubic option). To do this, just use "
"the :ref:`Curve3D.sample_baked()<class_Curve3D_method_sample_baked>` method "
"together "
"with :ref:`Curve2D.get_baked_length()<class_Curve2D_method_get_baked_length>`. "
"The first call to either of them will bake the curve internally."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອໃຫ້ສິ່ງນີ້ງ່າຍຂຶ້ນ, ເສັ້ນໂຄ້ງຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງຖືກ *baked* (ອົບ) ໃຫ້ເປັນຈຸດທີ່ມີໄລຍະຫ່າງເທົ່າກັນ. ດ້ວຍວິທີນີ້, ພ"
"ວກມັນສາມາດປະມານຄ່າໄດ້ດ້ວຍ interpolation ປົກກະຕິ (ເຊິ່ງສາມາດປັບປຸງໃຫ້ດີຂຶ້ນດ້ວຍຕົວເລືອກ cubic)"
". ເພື່ອເຮັດສິ່ງນີ້, ພຽງແຕ່ໃຊ້ເມທອດ :ref:`Curve3D.sample_baked()"
"<class_Curve3D_method_sample_baked>` ຮ່ວມກັບ :ref:`Curve2D.get_baked_length()"
"<class_Curve2D_method_get_baked_length>`. ການເອີ້ນໃຊ້ຄັ້ງທຳອິດຈະເຮັດການ bake ເສັ້ນໂຄ້ງພ"
"າຍໃນໃຫ້ໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:256
msgid ""
"Traversal at constant speed, then, can be done with the following pseudo-"
"code:"
msgstr ""
"ຈາກນັ້ນ, ການເຄື່ອນທີ່ດ້ວຍຄວາມໄວຄົງທີ່ສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ດ້ວຍ pseudo-code ດັ່ງຕໍ່ໄປນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/beziers_and_curves.rst:277
msgid "And the output will, then, move at constant speed:"
msgstr "ແລະ ຜົນໄດ້ຮັບຈະເຄື່ອນທີ່ດ້ວຍຄວາມໄວຄົງທີ່:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/random_number_generation.rst:4
msgid "Random number generation"
msgstr "ການສ້າງຕົວເລກສຸ່ມ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/random_number_generation.rst:6
msgid ""
"Many games rely on randomness to implement core game mechanics. This page "
"guides you through common types of randomness and how to implement them in "
"Godot."
msgstr ""
"ເກມຈຳນວນຫຼາຍອາໄສການສຸ່ມເພື່ອສ້າງລະບົບຫຼັກຂອງເກມ. ໜ້ານີ້ຈະແນະນຳເຈົ້າກ່ຽວກັບການສຸ່ມປະເພດຕ່າງໆທີ່ພົບເລື້"
"ອຍ ແລະ ວິທີການນຳໃຊ້ພວກມັນໃນ Godot."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/random_number_generation.rst:10
msgid ""
"After giving you a brief overview of useful functions that generate random "
"numbers, you will learn how to get random elements from arrays, "
"dictionaries, and how to use a noise generator in GDScript. Lastly, we'll "
"take a look at cryptographically secure random number generation and how it "
"differs from typical random number generation."
msgstr ""
"ຫຼັງຈາກໃຫ້ພາບລວມສັ້ນໆກ່ຽວກັບຟັງຊັນທີ່ມີປະໂຫຍດໃນການສ້າງຕົວເລກສຸ່ມແລ້ວ, ເຈົ້າຈະໄດ້ຮຽນຮູ້ວິທີການສຸ່ມເອົາຂໍ້ມູນ"
"ຈາກ array, dictionary, ແລະ ວິທີການໃຊ້ noise generator ໃນ GDScript. ສຸດທ້າຍ, ພວກເຮົາ"
"ຈະມາເບິ່ງການສ້າງຕົວເລກສຸ່ມທີ່ມີຄວາມປອດໄພທາງການເຂົ້າລະຫັດ (cryptographically secure) ແລະ ວ່"
"າມັນແຕກຕ່າງຈາກການສຸ່ມທົ່ວໄປແນວໃດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/random_number_generation.rst:18
msgid ""
"Computers cannot generate \"true\" random numbers. Instead, they rely on "
"`pseudorandom number generators <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Pseudorandom_number_generator>`__ (PRNGs)."
msgstr ""
"ຄອມພິວເຕີບໍ່ສາມາດສ້າງຕົວເລກສຸ່ມ \"ແທ້ໆ\" ໄດ້. ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນແນວນັ້ນ, ພວກມັນອາໄສ `pseudorandom "
"number generators <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Pseudorandom_number_generator>`__ (PRNGs)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/random_number_generation.rst:22
msgid ""
"Godot internally uses the `PCG Family <https://www.pcg-random.org/>`__ of "
"pseudorandom number generators."
msgstr ""
"Godot ໃຊ້ `PCG Family <https://www.pcg-random.org/>`__ ຂອງຕົວສ້າງຕົວເລກສຸ່ມທຽມພາຍໃ"
"ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/random_number_generation.rst:26
msgid "Global scope versus RandomNumberGenerator class"
msgstr "Global scope ທຽບກັບ ຄລາສ RandomNumberGenerator"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/random_number_generation.rst:28
msgid ""
"Godot exposes two ways to generate random numbers: via *global scope* "
"methods or using the :ref:`class_RandomNumberGenerator` class."
msgstr ""
"Godot ມີສອງວິທີໃນການສ້າງຕົວເລກສຸ່ມຄື: ຜ່ານເມທອດໃນ *global scope* ຫຼື ໃຊ້ຄລາສ "
":ref:`class_RandomNumberGenerator`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/random_number_generation.rst:31
msgid ""
"Global scope methods are easier to set up, but they don't offer as much "
"control."
msgstr ""
"ເມທອດໃນ Global scope ນັ້ນຕັ້ງຄ່າງ່າຍກວ່າ, ແຕ່ພວກມັນບໍ່ມີການຄວບຄຸມຫຼາຍປານໃດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/random_number_generation.rst:33
msgid ""
"RandomNumberGenerator requires more code to use, but allows creating "
"multiple instances, each with their own seed and state."
msgstr ""
"RandomNumberGenerator ຕ້ອງໃຊ້ໂຄ້ດຫຼາຍກວ່າ, ແຕ່ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສ້າງໄດ້ຫຼາຍ instance, ເຊິ່ງແຕ່ລະອັນມີ "
"seed ແລະ state ຂອງຕົນເອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/random_number_generation.rst:36
msgid ""
"This tutorial uses global scope methods, except when the method only exists "
"in the RandomNumberGenerator class."
msgstr ""
"ບົດຮຽນນີ້ຈະໃຊ້ເມທອດ global scope, ຍົກເວັ້ນເມື່ອເມທອດນັ້ນມີຢູ່ໃນຄລາສ RandomNumberGenerator ເ"
"ທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/random_number_generation.rst:40
msgid "The randomize() method"
msgstr "ເມທອດ randomize()"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/random_number_generation.rst:44
msgid ""
"Since Godot 4.0, the random seed is automatically set to a random value when "
"the project starts. This means you don't need to call ``randomize()`` in "
"``_ready()`` anymore to ensure that results are random across project runs. "
"However, you can still use ``randomize()`` if you want to use a specific "
"seed number, or generate it using a different method."
msgstr ""
"ຕັ້ງແຕ່ Godot 4.0 ເປັນຕົ້ນມາ, random seed ຈະຖືກຕັ້ງເປັນຄ່າສຸ່ມໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດເມື່ອໂປຣເຈັກເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ. ນີ້"
"ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າເຈົ້າບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງເອີ້ນໃຊ້ ``randomize()`` ໃນ ``_ready()`` ອີກຕໍ່ໄປເພື່ອໃຫ້ໝັ້ນໃຈວ່າຜົນ"
"ໄດ້ຮັບຈະສຸ່ມທຸກຄັ້ງທີ່ລັນໂປຣເຈັກ. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ເຈົ້າຍັງສາມາດໃຊ້ ``randomize()`` ໄດ້ຖ້າຕ້ອງການໃຊ້ເລ"
"ກ seed ທີ່ເຈາະຈົງ ຫຼື ສ້າງມັນດ້ວຍວິທີອື່ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/random_number_generation.rst:50
msgid ""
"In global scope, you can find a :ref:`randomize() "
"<class_@GlobalScope_method_randomize>` method. **This method should be "
"called only once when your project starts to initialize the random seed.** "
"Calling it multiple times is unnecessary and may impact performance "
"negatively."
msgstr ""
"ໃນ global scope, ເຈົ້າຈະພົບເມທອດ :ref:`randomize() "
"<class_@GlobalScope_method_randomize>`. **ເມທອດນີ້ຄວນຖືກເອີ້ນໃຊ້ພຽງແຕ່ຄັ້ງດຽວເມື່ອໂປຣເຈັກ"
"ເລີ່ມຕົ້ນເພື່ອຕັ້ງຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນໃຫ້ກັບ random seed.** ການເອີ້ນໃຊ້ມັນຫຼາຍຄັ້ງແມ່ນບໍ່ຈຳເປັນ ແລະ ອາດຈະສົ່ງຜົນເສ"
"ຍຕໍ່ປະສິດທິພາບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/random_number_generation.rst:55
msgid ""
"Putting it in your main scene script's ``_ready()`` method is a good choice:"
msgstr ""
"ການວາງມັນໄວ້ໃນເມທອດ ``_ready()`` ຂອງສະຄຣິບໃນສາກຫຼັກ (main scene) ແມ່ນທາງເລືອກທີ່ດີ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/random_number_generation.rst:70
msgid ""
"You can also set a fixed random seed instead using :ref:`seed() "
"<class_@GlobalScope_method_seed>`. Doing so will give you *deterministic* "
"results across runs:"
msgstr ""
"ເຈົ້າຍັງສາມາດຕັ້ງຄ່າ random seed ໃຫ້ຄົງທີ່ໄດ້ໂດຍໃຊ້ :ref:`seed() "
"<class_@GlobalScope_method_seed>`. ການເຮັດແບບນີ້ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ໄດ້ຜົນໄດ້ຮັບທີ່ *ຄາດການໄດ້* "
"(deterministic) ໃນທຸກໆຄັ້ງທີ່ລັນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/math/random_number_generation.rst:91
msgid ""
"When using the RandomNumberGenerator class, you should call ``randomize()`` "
"on the instance since it has its own seed:"
msgstr ""
