msgstr ""
"ຕົວຢ່າງທີ່ກ້າວໜ້າກວ່າເຊິ່ງໃຊ້ WebSocket ສຳລັບການສົ່ງສັນຍານລະຫວ່າງ peers ແລະ "
":ref:`WebRTCMultiplayerPeer <class_WebRTCMultiplayerPeer>` ແມ່ນມີໃຫ້ໃຊ້ໃນ `godot "
"demo projects <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects>`_ ພາຍໃຕ້ "
"`networking/webrtc_signaling`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/index.rst:11
msgid ""
"Godot follows a balanced performance philosophy. In the performance world, "
"there are always tradeoffs, which consist of trading speed for usability and "
"flexibility. Some practical examples of this are:"
msgstr ""
"Godot ຍຶດຖືປັດຊະຍາປະສິດທິພາບທີ່ສົມດຸນ. ໃນໂລກຂອງປະສິດທິພາບ, ມັນມີສິ່ງທີ່ຕ້ອງແລກປ່ຽນສະເໝີ, ເຊິ່ງປະກອບ"
"ມີການແລກປ່ຽນຄວາມໄວເພື່ອຄວາມງ່າຍໃນການໃຊ້ງານ ແລະ ຄວາມຍືດຍຸ່ນ. ຕົວຢ່າງຕົວຈິງບາງອັນມີດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/index.rst:15
msgid ""
"Rendering large amounts of objects efficiently is easy, but when a large "
"scene must be rendered, it can become inefficient. To solve this, visibility "
"computation must be added to the rendering. This makes rendering less "
"efficient, but at the same time, fewer objects are rendered. Therefore, the "
"overall rendering efficiency is improved."
msgstr ""
"ການເຣັນເດີວັດຖຸຈຳນວນຫຼາຍໃຫ້ມີປະສິດທິພາບນັ້ນແມ່ນງ່າຍ, ແຕ່ເມື່ອຕ້ອງເຣັນເດີສາກທີ່ມີຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່, ມັນອາດຈະກາ"
"ຍເປັນວ່າບໍ່ມີປະສິດທິພາບ. ເພື່ອແກ້ໄຂບັນຫານີ້, ຕ້ອງມີການເພີ່ມການຄຳນວນການເບິ່ງເຫັນ (Visibility "
"computation) ເຂົ້າໃນການເຣັນເດີ. ສິ່ງນີ້ເຮັດໃຫ້ການເຣັນເດີມີປະສິດທິພາບຫຼຸດລົງໃນຕົວມັນເອງ, ແຕ່ໃນຂະນະດ"
"ຽວກັນ, ວັດຖຸທີ່ຈະຖືກເຣັນເດີກໍມີໜ້ອຍລົງ. ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ປະສິດທິພາບການເຣັນເດີໂດຍລວມຈຶ່ງດີຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/index.rst:21
msgid ""
"Configuring the properties of every material for every object that needs to "
"be rendered is also slow. To solve this, objects are sorted by material to "
"reduce the costs. At the same time, sorting has a cost."
msgstr ""
"ການກຳນົດຄຸນສົມບັດຂອງທຸກໆ ວັດສະດຸ (Material) ໃຫ້ກັບທຸກໆ ວັດຖຸທີ່ຕ້ອງເຣັນເດີນັ້ນກໍຊ້າຄືກັນ. ເພື່ອແກ້ໄຂບັນຫ"
"ານີ້, ວັດຖຸຕ່າງໆ ຈະຖືກຈັດລຽງຕາມວັດສະດຸເພື່ອຫຼຸດຕົ້ນທຶນການປະມວນຜົນ. ໃນຂະນະດຽວກັນ, ການຈັດລຽງເອງກໍມີຕົ້"
"ນທຶນໃນການປະມວນຜົນເຊັ່ນກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/index.rst:25
msgid ""
"In 3D physics, a similar situation happens. The best algorithms to handle "
"large amounts of physics objects (such as SAP) are slow at insertion/removal "
"of objects and raycasting. Algorithms that allow faster insertion and "
"removal, as well as raycasting, will not be able to handle as many active "
"objects."
msgstr ""
"ໃນດ້ານຟີຊິກ 3D, ສະຖານະການທີ່ຄ້າຍຄືກັນກໍເກີດຂຶ້ນ. ຂັ້ນຕອນການປະມວນຜົນ (Algorithm) ທີ່ດີທີ່ສຸດໃນການຈັດ"
"ການກັບວັດຖຸຟີຊິກຈຳນວນຫຼາຍ (ເຊັ່ນ SAP) ຈະຊ້າໃນການເພີ່ມ/ລົບວັດຖຸ ແລະ ການເຮັດ Raycasting. ສ່ວນ "
"Algorithm ທີ່ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ການເພີ່ມ ແລະ ລົບວັດຖຸ ລວມເຖິງການເຮັດ Raycasting ໄວຂຶ້ນ, ກໍຈະບໍ່ສາມາດຈັດການ"
"ກັບວັດຖຸທີ່ມີການເຄື່ອນໄຫວໄດ້ຈຳນວນຫຼາຍຄືກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/index.rst:31
msgid ""
"And there are many more examples of this! Game engines strive to be general-"
"purpose in nature. Balanced algorithms are always favored over algorithms "
"that might be fast in some situations and slow in others, or algorithms that "
"are fast but are more difficult to use."
msgstr ""
"ແລະ ຍັງມີຕົວຢ່າງອີກຫຼາຍຢ່າງ! ເກມເອນຈິນ (Game engines) ພະຍາຍາມອອກແບບມາເພື່ອໃຊ້ງານທົ່ວໄປ. "
"Algorithm ທີ່ສົມດຸນມັກຈະຖືກເລືອກໃຊ້ຫຼາຍກວ່າ Algorithm ທີ່ອາດຈະໄວໃນບາງສະຖານະການແຕ່ຊ້າໃນສະຖານ"
"ະການອື່ນ, ຫຼື Algorithm ທີ່ໄວແຕ່ໃຊ້ງານຍາກກວ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/index.rst:36
msgid ""
"Godot is not an exception to this. While it is designed to have backends "
"swappable for different algorithms, the default backends prioritize balance "
"and flexibility over performance."
msgstr ""
"Godot ກໍບໍ່ແມ່ນຂໍ້ຍົກເວັ້ນ. ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າມັນຖືກອອກແບບມາໃຫ້ສາມາດປ່ຽນແປງ Backend ເພື່ອໃຊ້ Algorithm "
"ທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນໄດ້, ແຕ່ Backend ມາດຕະຖານຈະໃຫ້ຄວາມສຳຄັນກັບຄວາມສົມດຸນ ແລະ ຄວາມຍືດຍຸ່ນຫຼາຍກວ່າປະສິດ"
"ທິພາບພຽງຢ່າງດຽວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/index.rst:40
msgid ""
"With this clear, the aim of this tutorial section is to explain how to get "
"the maximum performance out of Godot. While the tutorials can be read in any "
"order, it is a good idea to start from :ref:`doc_general_optimization`."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອເຂົ້າໃຈແນວນັ້ນແລ້ວ, ຈຸດປະສົງຂອງບົດຮຽນພາກນີ້ແມ່ນເພື່ອອະທິບາຍວິທີການດຶງປະສິດທິພາບສູງສຸດອອກມາຈາກ "
"Godot. ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າບົດຮຽນສາມາດອ່ານລຽງລຳດັບໃດກໍໄດ້, ແຕ່ມັນເປັນການດີທີ່ຈະເລີ່ມຕົ້ນຈາກ "
":ref:`doc_general_optimization`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/index.rst:45
msgid "Common"
msgstr "ທົ່ວໄປ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/index.rst:55
msgid "CPU"
msgstr "CPU"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/index.rst:64
msgid "GPU"
msgstr "GPU"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/index.rst:86
#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:204
#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:11
#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:7
msgid "Threads"
msgstr "ເທຣດ (Threads)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:4
msgid "General optimization tips"
msgstr "ເຄັດລັບການປັບແຕ່ງປະສິດທິພາບທົ່ວໄປ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:9
msgid ""
"In an ideal world, computers would run at infinite speed. The only limit to "
"what we could achieve would be our imagination. However, in the real world, "
"it's all too easy to produce software that will bring even the fastest "
"computer to its knees."
msgstr ""
"ໃນໂລກທີ່ສົມບູນແບບ, ຄອມພິວເຕີຈະເຮັດວຽກດ້ວຍຄວາມໄວທີ່ບໍ່ມີຂີດຈຳກັດ. ສິ່ງດຽວທີ່ຈຳກັດຄວາມສຳເລັດຂອງພວກເຮົ"
"າກໍຄືຈິນຕະນາການ. ເຖິງຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ໃນໂລກຕົວຈິງ, ມັນງ່າຍເກີນໄປທີ່ຈະສ້າງຊອບແວທີ່ເຮັດໃຫ້ແມ່ນແຕ່ຄອມພິວເ"
"ຕີທີ່ໄວທີ່ສຸດກໍຍັງເຮັດວຽກບໍ່ໄຫວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:14
msgid ""
"Thus, designing games and other software is a compromise between what we "
"would like to be possible, and what we can realistically achieve while "
"maintaining good performance."
msgstr ""
"ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ການອອກແບບເກມ ແລະ ຊອບແວອື່ນໆ ຈຶ່ງເປັນການຫາຈຸດສົມດຸນລະຫວ່າງສິ່ງທີ່ພວກເຮົາຢາກໃຫ້ເປັນໄປໄດ້ ກັ"
"ບສິ່ງທີ່ພວກເຮົາສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ແທ້ໃນຂະນະທີ່ຍັງຮັກສາປະສິດທິພາບທີ່ດີໄວ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:18
msgid "To achieve the best results, we have two approaches:"
msgstr "ເພື່ອໃຫ້ໄດ້ຜົນລັດທີ່ດີທີ່ສຸດ, ພວກເຮົາມີສອງແນວທາງ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:20
msgid "Work faster."
msgstr "ເຮັດວຽກໃຫ້ໄວຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:21
msgid "Work smarter."
msgstr "ເຮັດວຽກໃຫ້ສະຫຼາດຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:23
msgid "And preferably, we will use a blend of the two."
msgstr "ແລະ ຖ້າເປັນໄປໄດ້, ພວກເຮົາຈະໃຊ້ທັງສອງຢ່າງປະສົມປະສານກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:26
msgid "Smoke and mirrors"
msgstr "ພາບລວງຕາ (Smoke and mirrors)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:28
msgid ""
"Part of working smarter is recognizing that, in games, we can often get the "
"player to believe they're in a world that is far more complex, interactive, "
"and graphically exciting than it really is. A good programmer is a magician, "
"and should strive to learn the tricks of the trade while trying to invent "
"new ones."
msgstr ""
"ສ່ວນໜຶ່ງຂອງການເຮັດວຽກໃຫ້ສະຫຼາດຂຶ້ນຄືການຮັບຮູ້ວ່າ ໃນເກມ, ພວກເຮົາມັກຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນເຊື່ອວ່າເຂົາເຈົ້າຢູ່ໃນໂລ"
"ກທີ່ມີຄວາມຊັບຊ້ອນ, ມີການຕອບໂຕ້ ແລະ ມີກຣາບຟິກທີ່ໜ້າຕື່ນເຕັ້ນກວ່າຄວາມເປັນຈິງຫຼາຍ. ໂປຣແກຣມເມີທີ່ດີກໍຄືກັບນັກ"
"ມາຍາກົນ, ແລະ ຄວນພະຍາຍາມຮຽນຮູ້ເຄັດລັບຕ່າງໆ ພ້ອມທັງຄິດຄົ້ນເຄັດລັບໃໝ່ໆ ຂຶ້ນມາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:34
msgid "The nature of slowness"
msgstr "ທຳມະຊາດຂອງຄວາມຊ້າ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:36
msgid ""
"To the outside observer, performance problems are often lumped together. But "
"in reality, there are several different kinds of performance problems:"
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບຜູ້ສັງເກດການພາຍນອກ, ບັນຫາປະສິດທິພາບມັກຈະຖືກເບິ່ງລວມໆ ກັນ. ແຕ່ໃນຄວາມເປັນຈິງ, ມັນມີບັນຫາປະສິດ"
"ທິພາບຫຼາຍຮູບແບບທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:39
msgid ""
"A slow process that occurs every frame, leading to a continuously low frame "
"rate."
msgstr ""
"ຂະບວນການທີ່ຊ້າເຊິ່ງເກີດຂຶ້ນໃນທຸກໆ ເຟຣມ (Frame), ສົ່ງຜົນໃຫ້ອັດຕາເຟຣມ (Frame rate) ຕ່ຳຢ່າງຕໍ່ເນື່ອ"
"ງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:41
msgid ""
"An intermittent process that causes \"spikes\" of slowness, leading to "
"stalls."
msgstr ""
"ຂະບວນການທີ່ເກີດຂຶ້ນບາງຄັ້ງຄາວເຊິ່ງເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດຄວາມຊ້າແບບກະທັນຫັນ (Spikes), ສົ່ງຜົນໃຫ້ເກມຢຸດສະງັກ ຫຼື "
"ຄ້າງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:43
msgid ""
"A slow process that occurs outside of normal gameplay, for instance, when "
"loading a level."
msgstr ""
"ຂະບວນການທີ່ຊ້າເຊິ່ງເກີດຂຶ້ນນອກການຫຼິ້ນເກມປົກກະຕິ, ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ, ໃນເວລາໂຫຼດດ່ານ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:46
msgid "Each of these are annoying to the user, but in different ways."
msgstr ""
"ແຕ່ລະຢ່າງເຫຼົ່ານີ້ລ້ວນແຕ່ສ້າງຄວາມລຳຄານໃຫ້ກັບຜູ້ໃຊ້, ແຕ່ໃນຮູບແບບທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:49
#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:7
msgid "Measuring performance"
msgstr "ການວັດແທກປະສິດທິພາບ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:51
msgid ""
"Probably the most important tool for optimization is the ability to measure "
"performance - to identify where bottlenecks are, and to measure the success "
"of our attempts to speed them up."
msgstr ""
"ອາດຈະເວົ້າໄດ້ວ່າເຄື່ອງມືທີ່ສຳຄັນທີ່ສຸດສຳລັບການປັບແຕ່ງປະສິດທິພາບແມ່ນຄວາມສາມາດໃນການວັດແທກປະສິດທິພາ"
"ບ - ເພື່ອລະບຸວ່າຈຸດຄໍຂວດ (Bottlenecks) ຢູ່ໃສ, ແລະ ເພື່ອວັດແທກຄວາມສຳເລັດຂອງຄວາມພະຍາຍາມໃນກາ"
"ນເພີ່ມຄວາມໄວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:55
msgid "There are several methods of measuring performance, including:"
msgstr "ມັນມີຫຼາຍວິທີໃນການວັດແທກປະສິດທິພາບ, ລວມທັງ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:57
msgid "Putting a start/stop timer around code of interest."
msgstr "ການໃສ່ເຄື່ອງຈັບເວລາເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ/ຢຸດ (Timer) ອ້ອມຮອບໂຄດທີ່ສົນໃຈ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:58
msgid "Using the :ref:`Godot profiler <doc_the_profiler>`."
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ :ref:`Godot profiler <doc_the_profiler>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:59
msgid "Using :ref:`external CPU profilers <doc_using_cpp_profilers>`."
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ :ref:`ເຄື່ອງມືວິເຄາະ CPU ພາຍນອກ <doc_using_cpp_profilers>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:60
msgid ""
"Using external GPU profilers/debuggers such as `NVIDIA Nsight Graphics "
"<https://developer.nvidia.com/nsight-graphics>`__, `Radeon GPU Profiler "
"<https://gpuopen.com/rgp/>`__, `PIX <https://devblogs.microsoft.com/pix/"
"download/>`__ (Direct3D 12 only), `Xcode <https://developer.apple.com/"
"documentation/xcode/optimizing-gpu-performance>`__ (Metal only), or `Arm "
"Performance Studio <https://developer.arm.com/Tools%20and%20Software/"
"Arm%20Performance%20Studio>`__."
msgstr ""
"ການໃຊ້ເຄື່ອງມືວິເຄາະ/ກວດສອບ GPU ພາຍນອກ ເຊັ່ນ `NVIDIA Nsight Graphics <https://"
"developer.nvidia.com/nsight-graphics>`__, `Radeon GPU Profiler <https://"
"gpuopen.com/rgp/>`__, `PIX <https://devblogs.microsoft.com/pix/download/>`__ "
"(ສະເພາະ Direct3D 12), `Xcode <https://developer.apple.com/documentation/"
"xcode/optimizing-gpu-performance>`__ (ສະເພາະ Metal), ຫຼື `Arm Performance "
"Studio <https://developer.arm.com/Tools%20and%20Software/"
"Arm%20Performance%20Studio>`__."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:66
msgid ""
"Checking the frame rate (with V-Sync disabled). Third-party utilities such "
"as `RivaTuner Statistics Server <https://www.guru3d.com/files-details/rtss-"
"rivatuner-statistics-server-download.html>`__ (Windows), `Special K <https://"
"www.special-k.info/>`__ (Windows), or `MangoHud <https://github.com/"
"flightlessmango/MangoHud>`__ (Linux) can also be useful here."
msgstr ""
"ການກວດສອບອັດຕາເຟຣມ (ໂດຍປິດ V-Sync). ໂປຣແກຣມເສີມຈາກພາຍນອກເຊັ່ນ `RivaTuner "
"Statistics Server <https://www.guru3d.com/files-details/rtss-rivatuner-"
"statistics-server-download.html>`__ (Windows), `Special K <https://"
"www.special-k.info/>`__ (Windows), ຫຼື `MangoHud <https://github.com/"
"flightlessmango/MangoHud>`__ (Linux) ກໍມີປະໂຫຍດໃນສ່ວນນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:71
msgid ""
"Using an unofficial `debug menu add-on <https://github.com/godot-extended-"
"libraries/godot-debug-menu>`__."
msgstr ""
"ການໃຊ້ `debug menu add-on <https://github.com/godot-extended-libraries/godot-"
"debug-menu>`__ ທີ່ບໍ່ເປັນທາງການ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:73
msgid ""
"Be very aware that the relative performance of different areas can vary on "
"different hardware. It's often a good idea to measure timings on more than "
"one device. This is especially the case if you're targeting mobile devices."
msgstr ""
"ຄວນລະວັງໄວ້ວ່າປະສິດທິພາບໃນສ່ວນຕ່າງໆ ອາດແຕກຕ່າງກັນໄປຕາມຮາດແວແຕ່ລະຊະນິດ. ມັນມັກຈະເປັນການດີທີ່ຈະວັ"
"ດແທກເວລາໃນອຸປະກອນຫຼາຍກວ່າໜຶ່ງເຄື່ອງ. ໂດຍສະເພາະຢ່າງຍິ່ງຖ້າທ່ານກຳລັງເນັ້ນໃສ່ອຸປະກອນມືຖື."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:80
msgid ""
"CPU profilers are often the go-to method for measuring performance. However, "
"they don't always tell the whole story."
msgstr ""
"ເຄື່ອງມືວິເຄາະ CPU ມັກຈະເປັນວິທີຫຼັກໃນການວັດແທກປະສິດທິພາບ. ເຖິງຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ພວກມັນບໍ່ໄດ້ບອກເລື່ອງລາ"
"ວທັງໝົດສະເໝີໄປ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:83
msgid ""
"Bottlenecks are often on the GPU, \"as a result\" of instructions given by "
"the CPU."
msgstr "ຈຸດຄໍຂວດມັກຈະຢູ່ທີ່ GPU, ເຊິ່ງເປັນ \"ຜົນມາຈາກ\" ຄຳສັ່ງທີ່ໃຫ້ໂດຍ CPU."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:85
msgid ""
"Spikes can occur in the operating system processes (outside of Godot) \"as a "
"result\" of instructions used in Godot (for example, dynamic memory "
"allocation)."
msgstr ""
"ການກະຕຸກ (Spikes) ສາມາດເກີດຂຶ້ນໃນຂະບວນການຂອງລະບົບປະຕິບັດການ (ນອກ Godot) ເຊິ່ງເປັນ \"ຜົນມ"
"າຈາກ\" ຄຳສັ່ງທີ່ໃຊ້ໃນ Godot (ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ, ການຈອງໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳແບບໄດນາມິກ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:87
msgid ""
"You may not always be able to profile specific devices like a mobile phone "
"due to the initial setup required."
msgstr ""
"ທ່ານອາດຈະບໍ່ສາມາດວິເຄາະອຸປະກອນສະເພາະບາງຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ ໂທລະສັບມືຖື ໄດ້ສະເໝີໄປ ເນື່ອງຈາກການຕັ້ງຄ່າເບື້ອງ"
"ຕົ້ນທີ່ຈຳເປັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:89
msgid ""
"You may have to solve performance problems that occur on hardware you don't "
"have access to."
msgstr ""
"ທ່ານອາດຈະຕ້ອງແກ້ໄຂບັນຫາປະສິດທິພາບທີ່ເກີດຂຶ້ນໃນຮາດແວທີ່ທ່ານບໍ່ມີສິດເຂົ້າເຖິງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:92
msgid ""
"As a result of these limitations, you often need to use detective work to "
"find out where bottlenecks are."
msgstr ""
"ເນື່ອງຈາກຂໍ້ຈຳກັດເຫຼົ່ານີ້, ທ່ານມັກຈະຕ້ອງໃຊ້ວຽກງານການສືບສວນເພື່ອຊອກຫາວ່າຈຸດຄໍຂວດຢູ່ໃສ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:96
msgid "Detective work"
msgstr "ວຽກງານການສືບສວນ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:98
msgid ""
"Detective work is a crucial skill for developers (both in terms of "
"performance, and also in terms of bug fixing). This can include hypothesis "
"testing, and binary search."
msgstr ""
"ວຽກງານການສືບສວນແມ່ນທັກສະທີ່ສຳຄັນສຳລັບນັກພັດທະນາ (ທັງໃນດ້ານປະສິດທິພາບ ແລະ ການແກ້ໄຂບັກ). ສິ່ງນີ້ສາ"
"ມາດລວມເຖິງການທົດສອບສົມມຸດຕິຖານ ແລະ ການຄົ້ນຫາແບບໄບນາຣີ (Binary search)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:103
msgid "Hypothesis testing"
msgstr "ການທົດສອບສົມມຸດຕິຖານ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:105
msgid ""
"Say, for example, that you believe sprites are slowing down your game. You "
"can test this hypothesis by:"
msgstr ""
"ສົມມຸດວ່າ, ຕົວຢ່າງ, ທ່ານເຊື່ອວ່າ Sprite ກຳລັງເຮັດໃຫ້ເກມຂອງທ່ານຊ້າລົງ. ທ່ານສາມາດທົດສອບສົມມຸດຕິຖານນີ້"
"ໄດ້ໂດຍ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:108
msgid "Measuring the performance when you add more sprites, or take some away."
msgstr "ການວັດແທກປະສິດທິພາບເມື່ອທ່ານເພີ່ມ Sprite ເຂົ້າໄປ ຫຼື ເອົາບາງສ່ວນອອກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:110
msgid ""
"This may lead to a further hypothesis: does the size of the sprite determine "
"the performance drop?"
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງນີ້ອາດຈະນຳໄປສູ່ສົມມຸດຕິຖານຕໍ່ໄປ: ຂະໜາດຂອງ Sprite ເປັນຕົວຄັດສິນການຕົກຕ່ຳຂອງປະສິດທິພາບຫຼືບໍ່?"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:113
msgid ""
"You can test this by keeping everything the same, but changing the sprite "
"size, and measuring performance."
msgstr ""
"ທ່ານສາມາດທົດສອບສິ່ງນີ້ໄດ້ໂດຍການຮັກສາທຸກຢ່າງໃຫ້ຄືເກົ່າ, ແຕ່ປ່ຽນຂະໜາດຂອງ Sprite ແລະ ວັດແທກປະສິດທິພ"
"າບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:117
msgid "Binary search"
msgstr "ການຄົ້ນຫາແບບໄບນາຣີ (Binary search)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:119
msgid ""
"If you know that frames are taking much longer than they should, but you're "
"not sure where the bottleneck lies. You could begin by commenting out "
"approximately half the routines that occur on a normal frame. Has the "
"performance improved more or less than expected?"
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າທ່ານຮູ້ວ່າແຕ່ລະເຟຣມໃຊ້ເວລາດົນກວ່າທີ່ຄວນຈະເປັນ, ແຕ່ທ່ານບໍ່ແນ່ໃຈວ່າຈຸດຄໍຂວດຢູ່ໃສ. ທ່ານສາມາດເລີ່ມຕົ້ນໂດຍ"
"ການປິດ (Comment out) ປະມານເຄິ່ງໜຶ່ງຂອງຂະບວນການທີ່ເກີດຂຶ້ນໃນເຟຣມປົກກະຕິ. ປະສິດທິພາບດີຂຶ້ນຫຼາຍ ຫຼື "
"ໜ້ອຍກວ່າທີ່ຄາດໄວ້ບໍ່?"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:124
msgid ""
"Once you know which of the two halves contains the bottleneck, you can "
"repeat this process until you've pinned down the problematic area."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອທ່ານຮູ້ວ່າເຄິ່ງໃດໃນສອງສ່ວນນັ້ນມີຈຸດຄໍຂວດ, ທ່ານສາມາດເຮັດຊ້ຳຂະບວນການນີ້ຈົນກວ່າທ່ານຈະລະບຸພື້ນທີ່ທີ່ມີບັນຫາ"
"ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:128
msgid "Profilers"
msgstr "ເຄື່ອງມືວິເຄາະປະສິດທິພາບ (Profilers)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:130
msgid ""
"Profilers allow you to time your program while running it. Profilers then "
"provide results telling you what percentage of time was spent in different "
"functions and areas, and how often functions were called."
msgstr ""
"Profilers ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ທ່ານສາມາດຈັບເວລາໂປຣແກຣມຂອງທ່ານໃນຂະນະທີ່ມັນກຳລັງເຮັດວຽກ. ຈາກນັ້ນ "
"Profilers ຈະໃຫ້ຜົນລັດທີ່ບອກທ່ານວ່າໃຊ້ເວລາຈັກເປີເຊັນໃນຟັງຊັນ ແລະ ພື້ນທີ່ຕ່າງໆ, ແລະ ຟັງຊັນຕ່າງໆ ຖືກຮຽ"
"ກໃຊ້ເລື້ອຍປານໃດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:134
msgid ""
"This can be very useful both to identify bottlenecks and to measure the "
"results of your improvements. Sometimes, attempts to improve performance can "
"backfire and lead to slower performance. **Always use profiling and timing "
"to guide your efforts.**"
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງນີ້ມີປະໂຫຍດຫຼາຍທັງໃນການລະບຸຈຸດຄໍຂວດ ແລະ ການວັດແທກຜົນລັດຂອງການປັບປຸງຂອງທ່ານ. ບາງຄັ້ງ, ຄວາມພະ"
"ຍາຍາມໃນການປັບປຸງປະສິດທິພາບອາດຈະສົ່ງຜົນກົງກັນຂ້າມ ແລະ ເຮັດໃຫ້ປະສິດທິພາບຊ້າລົງ. **ຈົ່ງໃຊ້ການວິເຄາະ "
"(Profiling) ແລະ ການຈັບເວລາ (Timing) ເພື່ອເປັນແນວທາງໃນການເຮັດວຽກສະເໝີ.**"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:139
msgid ""
"For more info about using Godot's built-in profiler, "
"see :ref:`doc_the_profiler`."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບການໃຊ້ profiler ທີ່ມາກັບ Godot, ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_the_profiler`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:142
msgid "Principles"
msgstr "ຫຼັກການ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:144
msgid "`Donald Knuth <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Knuth>`__ said:"
msgstr "`Donald Knuth <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Knuth>`__ ກ່າວວ່າ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:146
msgid ""
"*Programmers waste enormous amounts of time thinking about, or worrying "
"about, the speed of noncritical parts of their programs, and these attempts "
"at efficiency actually have a strong negative impact when debugging and "
"maintenance are considered. We should forget about small efficiencies, say "
"about 97% of the time: premature optimization is the root of all evil. Yet "
"we should not pass up our opportunities in that critical 3%.*"
msgstr ""
"*ໂປຣແກຣມເມີເສຍເວລາຈຳນວນມະຫາສານໄປກັບການຄິດ ຫຼື ກັງວົນກ່ຽວກັບຄວາມໄວຂອງສ່ວນທີ່ບໍ່ສຳຄັນໃນໂປຣແກຣມ"
"ຂອງພວກເຂົາ, ແລະ ຄວາມພະຍາຍາມໃນການເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຕົວຈິງແລ້ວສົ່ງຜົນກະທົບທາງລົບຢ່າງຮຸນແຮງເມື່ອ"
"ພິຈາລະນາເຖິງການກວດສອບຂໍ້ຜິດພາດ (Debugging) ແລະ ການບຳລຸງຮັກສາ. ພວກເຮົາຄວນລືມກ່ຽວກັບການປັບແ"
"ຕ່ງປະສິດທິພາບເລັກໆ ໜ້ອຍໆ, ປະມານ 97% ຂອງເວລາທັງໝົດ: ການປັບແຕ່ງປະສິດທິພາບກ່ອນເວລາອັນຄວນ "
"(Premature optimization) ແມ່ນຮາກເຫງົ້າຂອງຄວາມຊົ່ວຮ້າຍທັງປວງ. ແຕ່ເຖິງຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ ພວກເຮົາກໍບໍ່"
"ຄວນປ່ອຍໂອກາດໃນສ່ວນ 3% ທີ່ສຳຄັນນັ້ນໄປ.*"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:153
msgid "The messages are very important:"
msgstr "ຂໍ້ຄວາມເຫຼົ່ານີ້ສຳຄັນຫຼາຍ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:155
msgid ""
"Developer time is limited. Instead of blindly trying to speed up all aspects "
"of a program, we should concentrate our efforts on the aspects that really "
"matter."
msgstr ""
"ເວລາຂອງນັກພັດທະນາມີຈຳກັດ. ແທນທີ່ຈະພະຍາຍາມເລັ່ງຄວາມໄວໃນທຸກພາກສ່ວນຂອງໂປຣແກຣມແບບບໍ່ລືມຫູລືມຕາ, "
"ພວກເຮົາຄວນເນັ້ນຄວາມພະຍາຍາມໃສ່ໃນສ່ວນທີ່ສຳຄັນແທ້ໆ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:158
msgid ""
"Efforts at optimization often end up with code that is harder to read and "
"debug than non-optimized code. It is in our interests to limit this to areas "
"that will really benefit."
msgstr ""
"ຄວາມພະຍາຍາມໃນການປັບແຕ່ງປະສິດທິພາບມັກຈະລົງທ້າຍດ້ວຍໂຄດທີ່ອ່ານຍາກ ແລະ ແກ້ໄຂບັກໄດ້ຍາກກວ່າໂຄດທີ່ບໍ່ໄດ້"
"ປັບແຕ່ງ. ມັນເປັນຜົນປະໂຫຍດຂອງພວກເຮົາທີ່ຈະຈຳກັດສິ່ງນີ້ໄວ້ສະເພາະໃນພື້ນທີ່ທີ່ຈະໄດ້ຮັບຜົນປະໂຫຍດແທ້ໆ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:162
msgid ""
"Just because we *can* optimize a particular bit of code, it doesn't "
"necessarily mean that we *should*. Knowing when and when not to optimize is "
"a great skill to develop."
msgstr ""
"ພຽງແຕ່ຍ້ອນວ່າພວກເຮົາ *ສາມາດ* ປັບແຕ່ງໂຄດສ່ວນໃດສ່ວນໜຶ່ງໄດ້, ມັນກໍບໍ່ໄດ້ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າພວກເຮົາ *ຄວນ* ເຮັ"
"ດສະເໝີໄປ. ການຮູ້ວ່າເມື່ອໃດຄວນ ແລະ ເມື່ອໃດບໍ່ຄວນປັບແຕ່ງແມ່ນທັກສະທີ່ດີທີ່ຄວນພັດທະນາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:166
msgid ""
"One misleading aspect of the quote is that people tend to focus on the "
"subquote *\"premature optimization is the root of all evil\"*. While "
"*premature* optimization is (by definition) undesirable, performant software "
"is the result of performant design."
msgstr ""
"ແງ່ມຸມໜຶ່ງທີ່ອາດເຮັດໃຫ້ເຂົ້າໃຈຜິດຈາກຄຳເວົ້າຂ້າງເທິງແມ່ນຄົນມັກຈະເນັ້ນໃສ່ຄຳເວົ້າຍ່ອຍທີ່ວ່າ *\"ການປັບແຕ່ງປະສິດ"
"ທິພາບກ່ອນເວລາອັນຄວນ ແມ່ນຮາກເຫງົ້າຂອງຄວາມຊົ່ວຮ້າຍທັງປວງ\"*. ໃນຂະນະທີ່ການປັບແຕ່ງ *ກ່ອນເວລາອັນຄວ"
"ນ* ເປັນສິ່ງທີ່ບໍ່ເພິ່ງປະສົງ, ແຕ່ຊອບແວທີ່ມີປະສິດທິພາບສູງແມ່ນຜົນມາຈາກການອອກແບບທີ່ມີປະສິດທິພາບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:172
msgid "Performant design"
msgstr "ການອອກແບບທີ່ມີປະສິດທິພາບ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:174
msgid ""
"The danger with encouraging people to ignore optimization until necessary, "
"is that it conveniently ignores that the most important time to consider "
"performance is at the design stage, before a key has even hit a keyboard. If "
"the design or algorithms of a program are inefficient, then no amount of "
"polishing the details later will make it run fast. It may run *faster*, but "
"it will never run as fast as a program designed for performance."
msgstr ""
"ອັນຕະລາຍຂອງການສະໜັບສະໜູນໃຫ້ຄົນເມີນເສີຍຕໍ່ການປັບແຕ່ງປະສິດທິພາບຈົນກວ່າຈະຈຳເປັນ ຄືມັນເປັນການເມີນເສີຍຕໍ່"
"ຄວາມຈິງທີ່ວ່າເວລາທີ່ສຳຄັນທີ່ສຸດໃນການພິຈາລະນາປະສິດທິພາບແມ່ນຂັ້ນຕອນການອອກແບບ, ກ່ອນທີ່ນິ້ວມືຈະແຕະຄີບອດຊ້"
"ຳ. ຖ້າການອອກແບບ ຫຼື algorithm ຂອງໂປຣແກຣມບໍ່ມີປະສິດທິພາບ, ກໍບໍ່ມີການຂັດເກົາລາຍລະອຽດໃດໆ ໃນພາຍ"
"ຫຼັງທີ່ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ມັນເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ໄວ. ມັນອາດຈະເຮັດວຽກ *ໄວຂຶ້ນ*, ແຕ່ມັນຈະບໍ່ມີວັນເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ໄວເທົ່າກັບໂປຣແກຣ"
"ມທີ່ຖືກອອກແບບມາເພື່ອປະສິດທິພາບແຕ່ທຳອິດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:181
msgid ""
"This tends to be far more important in game or graphics programming than in "
"general programming. A performant design, even without low-level "
"optimization, will often run many times faster than a mediocre design with "
"low-level optimization."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງນີ້ມັກຈະສຳຄັນຫຼາຍໃນການຂຽນເກມ ຫຼື ໂປຣແກຣມກຣາບຟິກ ຫຼາຍກວ່າການຂຽນໂປຣແກຣມທົ່ວໄປ. ການອອກແບບທີ່"
"ມີປະສິດທິພາບ, ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຈະບໍ່ມີການປັບແຕ່ງໃນລະດັບຕ່ຳ (Low-level), ມັກຈະເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ໄວກວ່າການອອກແ"
"ບບທົ່ວໄປທີ່ມີການປັບແຕ່ງລະດັບຕ່ຳຫຼາຍເທົ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:187
msgid "Incremental design"
msgstr "ການອອກແບບແບບຄ່ອຍເປັນຄ່ອຍໄປ (Incremental design)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:189
msgid ""
"Of course, in practice, unless you have prior knowledge, you are unlikely to "
"come up with the best design the first time. Instead, you'll often make a "
"series of versions of a particular area of code, each taking a different "
"approach to the problem, until you come to a satisfactory solution. It's "
"important not to spend too much time on the details at this stage until you "
"have finalized the overall design. Otherwise, much of your work will be "
"thrown out."
msgstr ""
"ແນ່ນອນວ່າ, ໃນທາງປະຕິບັດ, ນອກຈາກວ່າທ່ານຈະມີຄວາມຮູ້ມາກ່ອນ, ມັນຍາກທີ່ທ່ານຈະຄິດການອອກແບບທີ່ດີທີ່ສຸດອອກ"
"ມາໄດ້ໃນຄັ້ງທຳອິດ. ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນແນວນັ້ນ, ທ່ານມັກຈະສ້າງໂຄດໃນສ່ວນນັ້ນອອກມາຫຼາຍໆ ເວີຊັນ, ໂດຍແຕ່ລະເວີຊັນ"
"ໃຊ້ແນວທາງທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນໃນການແກ້ໄຂບັນຫາ, ຈົນກວ່າທ່ານຈະໄດ້ວິທີແກ້ໄຂທີ່ໜ້າພໍໃຈ. ມັນສຳຄັນທີ່ຈະບໍ່ເສຍເວລາກັບ"
"ລາຍລະອຽດຫຼາຍເກີນໄປໃນຂັ້ນຕອນນີ້ ຈົນກວ່າທ່ານຈະໄດ້ການອອກແບບໂດຍລວມທີ່ແນ່ນອນ. ບໍ່ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ວຽກສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ຂ"
"ອງທ່ານອາດຈະຖືກຖິ້ມໄປລ້າໆ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:196
msgid ""
"It's difficult to give general guidelines for performant design because this "
"is so dependent on the problem. One point worth mentioning though, on the "
"CPU side, is that modern CPUs are nearly always limited by memory bandwidth. "
"This has led to a resurgence in data-oriented design, which involves "
"designing data structures and algorithms for *cache locality* of data and "
"linear access, rather than jumping around in memory."
msgstr ""
"ມັນຍາກທີ່ຈະໃຫ້ຄຳແນະນຳທົ່ວໄປສຳລັບການອອກແບບທີ່ມີປະສິດທິພາບ ເພາະມັນຂຶ້ນຢູ່ກັບບັນຫາເປັນຫຼັກ. ເຖິງຢ່າງໃດກໍຕ"
"າມ, ຈຸດໜຶ່ງທີ່ຄວນກ່າວເຖິງໃນດ້ານ CPU ແມ່ນ CPU ໃນປັດຈຸບັນເກືອບທັງໝົດຈະຖືກຈຳກັດໂດຍ Memory "
"bandwidth. ສິ່ງນີ້ໄດ້ນຳໄປສູ່ການກັບມາຂອງການອອກແບບທີ່ເນັ້ນຂໍ້ມູນເປັນຫຼັກ (Data-oriented design), "
"ເຊິ່ງກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັບການອອກແບບໂຄງສ້າງຂໍ້ມູນ ແລະ Algorithm ເພື່ອໃຫ້ຂໍ້ມູນຢູ່ໃກ້ກັນໃນແຄຊ (Cache "
"locality) ແລະ ການເຂົ້າເຖິງແບບເສັ້ນຊື່ (Linear access), ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນການໂດດໄປມາໃນໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈ"
"ຳ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:204
msgid "The optimization process"
msgstr "ຂະບວນການປັບແຕ່ງປະສິດທິພາບ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:206
msgid ""
"Assuming we have a reasonable design, and taking our lessons from Knuth, our "
"first step in optimization should be to identify the biggest bottlenecks - "
"the slowest functions, the low-hanging fruit."
msgstr ""
"ສົມມຸດວ່າພວກເຮົາມີການອອກແບບທີ່ເໝາະສົມແລ້ວ, ແລະ ຖອດຖອນບົດຮຽນຈາກ Knuth, ຂັ້ນຕອນທຳອິດໃນການປັບແ"
"ຕ່ງຂອງພວກເຮົາຄວນຈະແມ່ນການລະບຸຈຸດຄໍຂວດທີ່ໃຫຍ່ທີ່ສຸດ - ຟັງຊັນທີ່ຊ້າທີ່ສຸດ, ເຊິ່ງເປັນສ່ວນທີ່ແກ້ໄຂງ່າຍ ແລະ ໄດ້"
"ຜົນໄວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:210
msgid ""
"Once we've successfully improved the speed of the slowest area, it may no "
"longer be the bottleneck. So we should test/profile again and find the next "
"bottleneck on which to focus."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອພວກເຮົາປັບປຸງຄວາມໄວຂອງພື້ນທີ່ທີ່ຊ້າທີ່ສຸດໄດ້ສຳເລັດແລ້ວ, ມັນອາດຈະບໍ່ແມ່ນຈຸດຄໍຂວດອີກຕໍ່ໄປ. ດັ່ງນັ້ນພວກເຮົາ"
"ຄວນທົດສອບ/ວິເຄາະອີກຄັ້ງ ແລະ ຊອກຫາຈຸດຄໍຂວດຕໍ່ໄປທີ່ຈະຕ້ອງເນັ້ນໃສ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:214
msgid "The process is thus:"
msgstr "ຂະບວນການຈຶ່ງເປັນດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:216
msgid "Profile / Identify bottleneck."
msgstr "ວິເຄາະ (Profile) / ລະບຸຈຸດຄໍຂວດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:217
msgid "Optimize bottleneck."
msgstr "ປັບແຕ່ງຈຸດຄໍຂວດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:218
msgid "Return to step 1."
msgstr "ກັບໄປຂັ້ນຕອນທີ 1."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:221
msgid "Optimizing bottlenecks"
msgstr "ການປັບແຕ່ງຈຸດຄໍຂວດ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:223
msgid ""
"Some profilers will even tell you which part of a function (which data "
"accesses, calculations) are slowing things down."
msgstr ""
"Profilers ບາງໂຕຈະບອກທ່ານເຖິງຂັ້ນວ່າສ່ວນໃດຂອງຟັງຊັນ (ການເຂົ້າເຖິງຂໍ້ມູນໃດ, ການຄຳນວນໃດ) ທີ່ກຳລັງ"
"ເຮັດໃຫ້ສິ່ງຕ່າງໆ ຊ້າລົງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:226
msgid ""
"As with design, you should concentrate your efforts first on making sure the "
"algorithms and data structures are the best they can be. Data access should "
"be local (to make best use of CPU cache), and it can often be better to use "
"compact storage of data (again, always profile to test results). Often, you "
"precalculate heavy computations ahead of time. This can be done by "
"performing the computation when loading a level, by loading a file "
"containing precalculated data, or by storing the results of complex "
"calculations into a script constant and reading its value."
msgstr ""
"ເຊັ່ນດຽວກັບການອອກແບບ, ທ່ານຄວນເນັ້ນຄວາມພະຍາຍາມຂອງທ່ານກ່ອນອື່ນໝົດໃນການເຮັດໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າ "
"Algorithm ແລະ ໂຄງສ້າງຂໍ້ມູນນັ້ນດີທີ່ສຸດເທົ່າທີ່ຈະເປັນໄປໄດ້. ການເຂົ້າເຖິງຂໍ້ມູນຄວນຢູ່ໃກ້ກັນ (ເພື່ອໃຊ້ປະໂຫຍດ"
"ສູງສຸດຈາກ CPU cache), ແລະ ມັນມັກຈະດີກວ່າທີ່ຈະໃຊ້ການຈັດເກັບຂໍ້ມູນແບບກະທັດຮັດ (ຢ່າລືມວິເຄາະເພື່ອທົດສອ"
"ບຜົນລັດສະເໝີ). ຫຼາຍຄັ້ງ, ທ່ານສາມາດຄຳນວນສິ່ງທີ່ໜັກໆ ໄວ້ລ່ວງໜ້າ. ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ໂດຍການຄຳນວນໃນເວລ"
"າໂຫຼດດ່ານ, ໂດຍການໂຫຼດໄຟລ໌ທີ່ມີຂໍ້ມູນທີ່ຄຳນວນໄວ້ແລ້ວ, ຫຼື ໂດຍການເກັບຜົນລັດຂອງການຄຳນວນທີ່ຊັບຊ້ອນໄວ້ໃນຄ່າ"
"ຄົງທີ່ (Constant) ຂອງສະຄຣິບ ແລະ ອ່ານຄ່ານັ້ນມາໃຊ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:235
msgid ""
"Once algorithms and data are good, you can often make small changes in "
"routines which improve performance. For instance, you can move some "
"calculations outside of loops or transform nested ``for`` loops into non-"
"nested loops. (This should be feasible if you know a 2D array's width or "
"height in advance.)"
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອ Algorithm ແລະ ຂໍ້ມູນດີແລ້ວ, ທ່ານມັກຈະສາມາດປ່ຽນແປງເລັກໆ ໜ້ອຍໆ ໃນຂະບວນການເພື່ອເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພ"
"າບ. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ, ທ່ານສາມາດຍ້າຍບາງການຄຳນວນອອກມານອກ Loop ຫຼື ປ່ຽນ Loop ``for`` ທີ່ຊ້ອນກັນໃຫ້"
"ເປັນ Loop ທີ່ບໍ່ຊ້ອນກັນ. (ສິ່ງນີ້ເປັນໄປໄດ້ຖ້າທ່ານຮູ້ຄວາມກວ້າງ ຫຼື ຄວາມສູງຂອງ Array 2D ລ່ວງໜ້າ.)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:240
msgid ""
"Always retest your timing/bottlenecks after making each change. Some changes "
"will increase speed, others may have a negative effect. Sometimes, a small "
"positive effect will be outweighed by the negatives of more complex code, "
"and you may choose to leave out that optimization."
msgstr ""
"ຈົ່ງທົດສອບເວລາ/ຈຸດຄໍຂວດຂອງທ່ານຄືນໃໝ່ຫຼັງຈາກການປ່ຽນແປງແຕ່ລະຄັ້ງສະເໝີ. ການປ່ຽນແປງບາງຢ່າງຈະເພີ່ມຄວາ"
"ມໄວ, ສ່ວນຢ່າງອື່ນອາດຈະສົ່ງຜົນທາງລົບ. ບາງຄັ້ງ, ຜົນກະທົບທາງບວກເລັກໆ ໜ້ອຍໆ ອາດຈະບໍ່ຄຸ້ມຄ່າກັບຂໍ້ເສຍຂອງ"
"ໂຄດທີ່ຊັບຊ້ອນຂຶ້ນ, ແລະ ທ່ານອາດຈະເລືອກທີ່ຈະບໍ່ໃຊ້ການປັບແຕ່ງນັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:246
msgid "Appendix"
msgstr "ພາກຜະໜວກ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:249
msgid "Bottleneck math"
msgstr "ຄະນິດສາດຂອງຈຸດຄໍຂວດ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:251
msgid ""
"The proverb *\"a chain is only as strong as its weakest link\"* applies "
"directly to performance optimization. If your project is spending 90% of the "
"time in function ``A``, then optimizing ``A`` can have a massive effect on "
"performance."
msgstr ""
"ສຸພາສິດທີ່ວ່າ *\"ໂສ້ຈະແຂງແຮງເທົ່າກັບຂໍ້ທີ່ອ່ອນແອທີ່ສຸດຂອງມັນ\"* ສາມາດນຳມາໃຊ້ໄດ້ໂດຍກົງກັບການປັບແຕ່ງປະສິ"
"ດທິພາບ. ຖ້າໂປຣເຈັກຂອງທ່ານໃຊ້ເວລາ 90% ຢູ່ໃນຟັງຊັນ ``A``, ການປັບແຕ່ງ ``A`` ຈະສົ່ງຜົນກະທົບຢ່າງມະ"
"ຫາສານຕໍ່ປະສິດທິພາບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:267
msgid ""
"In this example, improving this bottleneck ``A`` by a factor of 9× decreases "
"overall frame time by 5× while increasing frames per second by 5×."
msgstr ""
"ໃນຕົວຢ່າງນີ້, ການປັບປຸງຈຸດຄໍຂວດ ``A`` ໃຫ້ດີຂຶ້ນ 9 ເທົ່າ ຈະຊ່ວຍຫຼຸດເວລາຂອງແຕ່ລະເຟຣມໂດຍລວມລົງ 5 ເທົ່"
"າ ໃນຂະນະທີ່ເພີ່ມຈຳນວນເຟຣມຕໍ່ວິນາທີ (FPS) ຂຶ້ນ 5 ເທົ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:270
msgid ""
"However, if something else is running slowly and also bottlenecking your "
"project, then the same improvement can lead to less dramatic gains:"
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ຖ້າມີສິ່ງອື່ນທີ່ເຮັດວຽກຊ້າ ແລະ ເປັນຈຸດຄໍຂວດໃຫ້ກັບໂປຣເຈັກຂອງທ່ານຄືກັນ, ການປັບປຸງໃນແບບ"
"ດຽວກັນນັ້ນອາດຈະໃຫ້ຜົນລັດທີ່ບໍ່ໂດດເດັ່ນປານໃດ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:285
msgid ""
"In this example, even though we have hugely optimized function ``A``, the "
"actual gain in terms of frame rate is quite small."
msgstr ""
"ໃນຕົວຢ່າງນີ້, ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າພວກເຮົາຈະປັບແຕ່ງຟັງຊັນ ``A`` ຢ່າງມະຫາສານ, ແຕ່ຜົນທີ່ໄດ້ຮັບໃນແງ່ຂອງອັດຕາເຟຣ"
"ມນັ້ນມີໜ້ອຍຫຼາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:288
msgid ""
"In games, things become even more complicated because the CPU and GPU run "
"independently of one another. Your total frame time is determined by the "
"slower of the two."
msgstr ""
"ໃນເກມ, ສິ່ງຕ່າງໆ ຈະຍິ່ງຊັບຊ້ອນຂຶ້ນ ເພາະ CPU ແລະ GPU ເຮັດວຽກແຍກກັນ. ເວລາເຟຣມທັງໝົດຂອງທ່ານຈະຖື"
"ກກຳນົດໂດຍຕົວທີ່ເຮັດວຽກຊ້າກວ່າໃນສອງຕົວນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.rst:304
msgid ""
"In this example, we optimized the CPU hugely again, but the frame time "
"didn't improve because we are GPU-bottlenecked."
msgstr ""
"ໃນຕົວຢ່າງນີ້, ພວກເຮົາປັບແຕ່ງ CPU ຢ່າງມະຫາສານອີກຄັ້ງ, ແຕ່ເວລາເຟຣມບໍ່ໄດ້ດີຂຶ້ນເລີຍ ເພາະວ່າພວກເຮົາກຳລັ"
"ງຕິດຈຸດຄໍຂວດທີ່ GPU."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:4
msgid "Optimization using Servers"
msgstr "ການປັບແຕ່ງປະສິດທິພາບໂດຍໃຊ້ ເຊີເວີ (Servers)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:6
msgid ""
"Engines like Godot provide increased ease of use thanks to their high-level "
"constructs and features. Most of them are accessed and used via "
"the :ref:`scene system <doc_scene_tree>`. Using nodes and resources "
"simplifies project organization and asset management in complex games."
msgstr ""
"ເອນຈິນ (Engine) ຄື Godot ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ໃຊ້ງານໄດ້ງ່າຍຂຶ້ນຍ້ອນໂຄງສ້າງ ແລະ ຟີເຈີໃນລະດັບສູງ (High-"
"level). ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ແມ່ນຖືກເຂົ້າເຖິງ ແລະ ໃຊ້ງານຜ່ານ :ref:`ລະບົບສາກ (Scene system) "
"<doc_scene_tree>`. ການໃຊ້ ໂນດ (Nodes) ແລະ ຊັບພະຍາກອນ (Resources) ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ການຈັດການໂ"
"ປຣເຈັກ ແລະ ສິ່ງຂອງຕ່າງໆ ໃນເກມທີ່ຊັບຊ້ອນເປັນເລື່ອງງ່າຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:11
msgid "There are several drawbacks to this:"
msgstr "ແຕ່ສິ່ງນີ້ກໍມີຂໍ້ເສຍບາງຢ່າງ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:13
msgid "There is an extra layer of complexity."
msgstr "ມັນມີຊັ້ນຄວາມຊັບຊ້ອນເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:14
msgid "Performance is lower than when using simple APIs directly."
msgstr "ປະສິດທິພາບຕ່ຳກວ່າການໃຊ້ API ແບບງ່າຍໆ ໂດຍກົງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:15
msgid ""
"It is not possible to :ref:`use multiple threads "
"<doc_using_multiple_threads>` to control them."
msgstr ""
"ບໍ່ສາມາດ :ref:`ໃຊ້ຫຼາຍເທຣດ (Multiple threads) <doc_using_multiple_threads>` ເພື່ອຄວ"
"ບຄຸມພວກມັນໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:17
msgid "More memory is needed."
msgstr "ຕ້ອງການໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:19
msgid ""
"In most cases, this is not really a problem. Godot is well-optimized, and "
"most operations are handled with signals, which means no polling is "
"required. Still, sometimes, we want to extract better performance from the "
"hardware when other avenues of optimization have been exhausted. For "
"example, dealing with tens of thousands of instances for something that "
"needs to be processed every frame can be a bottleneck."
msgstr ""
"ໃນກໍລະນີສ່ວນໃຫຍ່, ສິ່ງນີ້ບໍ່ແມ່ນບັນຫາແທ້ໆ. Godot ຖືກປັບແຕ່ງມາເປັນຢ່າງດີ, ແລະ ການເຮັດວຽກສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ແມ່ນຖື"
"ກຈັດການດ້ວຍສັນຍານ (Signals), ເຊິ່ງໝາຍຄວາມວ່າບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງມີການກວດສອບ (Polling) ຕະຫຼອດເວລ"
"າ. ເຖິງຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ບາງຄັ້ງພວກເຮົາຕ້ອງການດຶງປະສິດທິພາບຈາກຮາດແວໃຫ້ໄດ້ຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນເມື່ອວິທີການປັບແຕ່ງອື່ນ"
"ໆ ຖືກໃຊ້ໝົດແລ້ວ. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ, ການຈັດການກັບ Instance ຫຼາຍໝື່ນໂຕສຳລັບບາງສິ່ງທີ່ຕ້ອງປະມວນຜົນທຸກໆ ເຟຣ"
"ມກໍອາດກາຍເປັນຈຸດຄໍຂວດໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:26
msgid ""
"This type of situation makes programmers regret they are using a game engine "
"and wish they could go back to a more handcrafted, low-level implementation "
"of game code."
msgstr ""
"ສະຖານະການແບບນີ້ເຮັດໃຫ້ໂປຣແກຣມເມີຮູ້ສຶກເສຍດາຍທີ່ໃຊ້ເກມເອນຈິນ ແລະ ຢາກກັບໄປຂຽນໂຄດເກມໃນລະດັບຕ່ຳ "
"(Low-level) ທີ່ປັບແຕ່ງເອງກັບມືຫຼາຍກວ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:30
msgid "Still, Godot is designed to work around this problem."
msgstr "ແຕ່ຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, Godot ຖືກອອກແບບມາເພື່ອແກ້ໄຂບັນຫານີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:34
msgid ""
"You can see how using low-level servers works in action using the `Bullet "
"Shower demo project <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/"
"master/2d/bullet_shower>`__."
msgstr ""
"ທ່ານສາມາດເບິ່ງການເຮັດວຽກຂອງເຊີເວີລະດັບຕ່ຳໄດ້ໃນ `Bullet Shower demo project <https://"
"github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/2d/bullet_shower>`__."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:38
msgid "Servers"
msgstr "ເຊີເວີ (Servers)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:40
msgid ""
"One of the most interesting design decisions for Godot is the fact that the "
"whole scene system is *optional*. While it is not possible to compile it "
"out, it can be completely bypassed."
msgstr ""
"ໜຶ່ງໃນການຕັດສິນໃຈອອກແບບທີ່ໜ້າສົນໃຈທີ່ສຸດຂອງ Godot ແມ່ນຄວາມຈິງທີ່ວ່າລະບົບສາກ (Scene system) ທັງໝົ"
"ດນັ້ນເປັນ *ທາງເລືອກ*. ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຈະບໍ່ສາມາດຕັດມັນອອກຈາກການ Compile ໄດ້, ແຕ່ມັນສາມາດຖືກຂ້າມໄປໄ"
"ດ້ທັງໝົດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:44
msgid ""
"At the core, Godot uses the concept of Servers. They are low-level APIs to "
"control rendering, physics, sound, etc. The scene system is built on top of "
"them and uses them directly. The most common servers are:"
msgstr ""
"ໃນລະດັບແກນກາງ, Godot ໃຊ້ແນວຄິດຂອງ ເຊີເວີ (Servers). ພວກມັນແມ່ນ API ລະດັບຕ່ຳເພື່ອຄວບຄຸມການ"
"ເຣັນເດີ, ຟີຊິກ, ສຽງ ແລະ ອື່ນໆ. ລະບົບສາກຖືກສ້າງຂຶ້ນມາເທິງພວກມັນ ແລະ ໃຊ້ງານພວກມັນໂດຍກົງ. ເຊີເວີທີ່ໃ"
"ຊ້ເລື້ອຍທີ່ສຸດແມ່ນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:48
msgid ":ref:`class_RenderingServer`: Handles everything related to graphics."
msgstr ":ref:`class_RenderingServer`: ຈັດການທຸກຢ່າງທີ່ກ່ຽວກັບກຣາບຟິກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:49
msgid ":ref:`class_PhysicsServer3D`: Handles everything related to 3D physics."
msgstr ":ref:`class_PhysicsServer3D`: ຈັດການທຸກຢ່າງທີ່ກ່ຽວກັບຟີຊິກ 3D."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:50
msgid ":ref:`class_PhysicsServer2D`: Handles everything related to 2D physics."
msgstr ":ref:`class_PhysicsServer2D`: ຈັດການທຸກຢ່າງທີ່ກ່ຽວກັບຟີຊິກ 2D."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:51
msgid ":ref:`class_AudioServer`: Handles everything related to audio."
msgstr ":ref:`class_AudioServer`: ຈັດການທຸກຢ່າງທີ່ກ່ຽວກັບສຽງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:53
msgid ""
"Explore their APIs, and you will realize that all the functions provided are "
"low-level implementations of everything Godot allows you to do using nodes."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອສຶກສາ API ຂອງພວກມັນ, ທ່ານຈະເຫັນວ່າຟັງຊັນທັງໝົດທີ່ມີໃຫ້ນັ້ນແມ່ນການເຮັດວຽກໃນລະດັບຕ່ຳຂອງທຸກສິ່ງທີ່ "
"Godot ອະນຸຍາດໃຫ້ທ່ານເຮັດໂດຍການໃຊ້ໂນດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:57
msgid "RIDs"
msgstr "RID"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:59
msgid ""
"The key to using servers is understanding Resource ID (:ref:`RID "
"<class_RID>`) objects. These are opaque handles to the server "
"implementation. They are allocated and freed manually. Almost every function "
"in the servers requires RIDs to access the actual resource."
msgstr ""
"ກະແຈສຳຄັນໃນການໃຊ້ງານເຊີເວີແມ່ນການເຂົ້າໃຈກ່ຽວກັບວັດຖຸ Resource ID (:ref:`RID <class_RID>"
"`). ພວກມັນແມ່ນຕົວຈັດການ (Handles) ທີ່ໃຊ້ເຂົ້າເຖິງການເຮັດວຽກພາຍໃນເຊີເວີ. ພວກມັນຈະຖືກຈອງ ແລະ ປ່"
"ອຍໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳດ້ວຍຕົນເອງ (Manually). ເກືອບທຸກຟັງຊັນໃນເຊີເວີຕ້ອງການ RID ເພື່ອເຂົ້າເຖິງຊັບພະຍາກອນ"
"ຕົວຈິງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:64
msgid ""
"Most Godot nodes and resources contain these RIDs from the servers "
"internally, and they can be obtained with different functions. In fact, "
"anything that inherits :ref:`Resource <class_Resource>` can be directly "
"casted to an RID. Not all resources contain an RID, though: in such cases, "
"the RID will be empty. The resource can then be passed to server APIs as an "
"RID."
msgstr ""
"ໂນດ ແລະ ຊັບພະຍາກອນສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ຂອງ Godot ຈະເກັບ RID ເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຈາກເຊີເວີໄວ້ພາຍໃນ, ແລະ ສາມາດດຶງມາໄ"
"ດ້ດ້ວຍຟັງຊັນຕ່າງໆ. ທີ່ຈິງແລ້ວ, ສິ່ງໃດກໍຕາມທີ່ສືບທອດມາຈາກ :ref:`Resource <class_Resource>` ສາ"
"ມາດຖືກປ່ຽນໃຫ້ເປັນ RID ໄດ້ໂດຍກົງ. ເຖິງຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ບໍ່ແມ່ນທຸກຊັບພະຍາກອນທີ່ຈະມີ RID: ໃນກໍລະນີນັ້ນ, "
"RID ຈະວ່າງເປົ່າ. ຈາກນັ້ນຊັບພະຍາກອນສາມາດຖືກສົ່ງໄປໃຫ້ API ຂອງເຊີເວີໃນຮູບແບບຂອງ RID ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:72
msgid ""
"Resources are reference-counted (see :ref:`RefCounted <class_RefCounted>`), "
"and references to a resource's RID are *not* counted when determining "
"whether the resource is still in use. Make sure to **keep a reference** to "
"the resource outside the server. Otherwise, both the resource and its RID "
"will be erased."
msgstr ""
"ຊັບພະຍາກອນຈະມີການນັບຈຳນວນການອ້າງອີງ (ເບິ່ງ :ref:`RefCounted <class_RefCounted>`), ແຕ່"
"ການອ້າງອີງເຖິງ RID ຂອງຊັບພະຍາກອນນັ້ນຈະ *ບໍ່* ຖືກນັບລວມໃນເວລາພິຈາລະນາວ່າຍັງມີການໃຊ້ງານຊັບພະຍາກ"
"ອນຢູ່ຫຼືບໍ່. ຕ້ອງໝັ້ນໃຈວ່າໄດ້ **ເກັບການອ້າງອີງ (Reference)** ຂອງຊັບພະຍາກອນນັ້ນໄວ້ທາງນອກເຊີເວີ. ບໍ່ດັ່"
"ງນັ້ນ, ທັງຊັບພະຍາກອນ ແລະ RID ຂອງມັນຈະຖືກລຶບໄປ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:77
msgid "For nodes, there are many functions available:"
msgstr "ສຳລັບໂນດ, ມັນມີຫຼາຍຟັງຊັນໃຫ້ໃຊ້ງານ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:79
msgid ""
"For CanvasItem, the :ref:`CanvasItem.get_canvas_item() "
"<class_CanvasItem_method_get_canvas_item>` method will return the canvas "
"item RID in the server."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບ CanvasItem, ວິທີການ :ref:`CanvasItem.get_canvas_item() "
"<class_CanvasItem_method_get_canvas_item>` ຈະສົ່ງຄືນ RID ຂອງ canvas item ໃນເຊີເວີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:81
msgid ""
"For CanvasLayer, the :ref:`CanvasLayer.get_canvas() "
"<class_CanvasLayer_method_get_canvas>` method will return the canvas RID in "
"the server."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບ CanvasLayer, ວິທີການ :ref:`CanvasLayer.get_canvas() "
"<class_CanvasLayer_method_get_canvas>` ຈະສົ່ງຄືນ RID ຂອງ canvas ໃນເຊີເວີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:83
msgid ""
"For Viewport, the :ref:`Viewport.get_viewport_rid() "
"<class_Viewport_method_get_viewport_rid>` method will return the viewport "
"RID in the server."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບ Viewport, ວິທີການ :ref:`Viewport.get_viewport_rid() "
"<class_Viewport_method_get_viewport_rid>` ຈະສົ່ງຄືນ RID ຂອງ viewport ໃນເຊີເວີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:85
msgid ""
"For 2D, the :ref:`class_World2D` resource (obtainable in "
"the :ref:`class_Viewport` and :ref:`CanvasItem <class_CanvasItem>` nodes) "
"contains functions to get the *RenderingServer Canvas*, and the "
"*PhysicsServer2D Space*. This allows creating 2D objects directly with the "
"server API and using them."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບ 2D, ຊັບພະຍາກອນ :ref:`class_World2D` (ຫາໄດ້ໃນໂນດ :ref:`class_Viewport` ແລະ "
":ref:`CanvasItem <class_CanvasItem>`) ປະກອບມີຟັງຊັນສຳລັບດຶງ *RenderingServer "
"Canvas* ແລະ *PhysicsServer2D Space*. ສິ່ງນີ້ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສາມາດສ້າງວັດຖຸ 2D ຜ່ານ API ຂອງເຊີເວີໂດ"
"ຍກົງ ແລະ ໃຊ້ງານພວກມັນໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:89
msgid ""
"For 3D, the :ref:`class_World3D` resource (obtainable in "
"the :ref:`class_Viewport` and :ref:`class_Node3D` nodes) contains functions "
"to get the *RenderingServer Scenario*, and the *PhysicsServer Space*. This "
"allows creating 3D objects directly with the server API and using them."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບ 3D, ຊັບພະຍາກອນ :ref:`class_World3D` (ຫາໄດ້ໃນໂນດ :ref:`class_Viewport` ແລະ "
":ref:`class_Node3D`) ປະກອບມີຟັງຊັນສຳລັບດຶງ *RenderingServer Scenario* ແລະ "
"*PhysicsServer Space*. ສິ່ງນີ້ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສາມາດສ້າງວັດຖຸ 3D ຜ່ານ API ຂອງເຊີເວີໂດຍກົງ ແລະ ໃຊ້ງານພ"
"ວກມັນໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:93
msgid ""
"The :ref:`class_VisualInstance3D` class, allows getting the scenario "
"*instance* and *instance base* via the :ref:`VisualInstance3D.get_instance() "
"<class_VisualInstance3D_method_get_instance>` "
"and :ref:`VisualInstance3D.get_base() "
"<class_VisualInstance3D_method_get_base>` respectively."
msgstr ""
"ຄລາສ :ref:`class_VisualInstance3D` ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສາມາດດຶງ scenario *instance* ແລະ "
"*instance base* ຜ່ານ :ref:`VisualInstance3D.get_instance() "
"<class_VisualInstance3D_method_get_instance>` ແລະ "
":ref:`VisualInstance3D.get_base() <class_VisualInstance3D_method_get_base>` ຕ"
"າມລຳດັບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:97
msgid ""
"Try exploring the nodes and resources you are familiar with and find the "
"functions to obtain the server *RIDs*."
msgstr ""
"ລອງສຶກສາໂນດ ແລະ ຊັບພະຍາກອນທີ່ທ່ານຄຸ້ນເຄີຍ ແລະ ຊອກຫາຟັງຊັນເພື່ອດຶງຄ່າ *RID* ຂອງເຊີເວີອອກມາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:99
msgid ""
"It is not advised to control RIDs from objects that already have a node "
"associated. Instead, server functions should always be used for creating and "
"controlling new ones and interacting with the existing ones."
msgstr ""
"ບໍ່ແນະນຳໃຫ້ຄວບຄຸມ RID ຈາກວັດຖຸທີ່ມີໂນດເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ຢູ່ແລ້ວ. ແຕ່ຄວນໃຊ້ຟັງຊັນຂອງເຊີເວີສະເໝີສຳລັບການສ້າງ ແລະ "
"ຄວບຄຸມວັດຖຸໃໝ່ ຫຼື ໂຕ້ຕອບກັບວັດຖຸທີ່ມີຢູ່ແລ້ວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:103
msgid "Creating a sprite"
msgstr "ການສ້າງ Sprite"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:105
msgid ""
"This is an example of how to create a sprite from code and move it using the "
"low-level :ref:`class_CanvasItem` API."
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ແມ່ນຕົວຢ່າງວິທີການສ້າງ Sprite ຈາກໂຄດ ແລະ ເຄື່ອນຍ້າຍມັນໂດຍໃຊ້ API ລະດັບຕ່ຳຂອງ "
":ref:`class_CanvasItem`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:110
msgid ""
"When creating canvas items using the RenderingServer, you should reset "
"physics interpolation on the first frame "
"using :ref:`RenderingServer.canvas_item_reset_physics_interpolation() "
"<class_RenderingServer_method_canvas_item_reset_physics_interpolation>`. "
"This ensures proper synchronization between the rendering and physics "
"systems."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອສ້າງ canvas item ໂດຍໃຊ້ RenderingServer, ທ່ານຄວນຣີເຊັດ physics interpolation ໃນ"
"ເຟຣມທຳອິດໂດຍໃຊ້ :ref:`RenderingServer.canvas_item_reset_physics_interpolation"
"() <class_RenderingServer_method_canvas_item_reset_physics_interpolation>`. ສິ່"
"ງນີ້ຈະຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ການເຮັດວຽກລະຫວ່າງລະບົບການເຣັນເດີ ແລະ ຟີຊິກມີຄວາມກົງກັນ (Synchronization)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:115
msgid ""
"If this is not done, the canvas item may appear to teleport in when the "
"scene is loaded, rather than appearing directly at its intended location."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າບໍ່ເຮັດແນວນີ້, canvas item ອາດຈະປະກົດຂຶ້ນແບບຄືກັບການວາບ (Teleport) ເຂົ້າມາໃນເວລາໂຫຼດສາ"
"ກ, ແທນທີ່ຈະປະກົດຢູ່ໃນຕຳແໜ່ງທີ່ກຳນົດໄວ້ໂດຍກົງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:170
msgid ""
"The Canvas Item API in the server allows you to add draw primitives to it. "
"Once added, they can't be modified. The Item needs to be cleared and the "
"primitives re-added. This is not the case for setting the transform, which "
"can be done as many times as desired."
msgstr ""
"Canvas Item API ໃນເຊີເວີອະນຸຍາດໃຫ້ທ່ານເພີ່ມ Draw primitives ເຂົ້າໄປໄດ້. ເມື່ອເພີ່ມເຂົ້າໄປແລ້"
"ວ, ພວກມັນຈະບໍ່ສາມາດຖືກແກ້ໄຂໄດ້. ຖ້າຕ້ອງການປ່ຽນ ຕ້ອງລ້າງ (Clear) Item ນັ້ນອອກແລ້ວເພີ່ມ "
"primitives ເຂົ້າໄປໃໝ່. ແຕ່ສຳລັບການຕັ້ງຄ່າການປ່ຽນແປງຕຳແໜ່ງ (Transform) ນັ້ນສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ຫຼາຍຄັ້ງ"
"ຕາມທີ່ຕ້ອງການ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:175
msgid "Primitives are cleared this way:"
msgstr "Primitives ຈະຖືກລ້າງອອກດ້ວຍວິທີນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:188
msgid "Instantiating a Mesh into 3D space"
msgstr "ການສ້າງ Instance ຂອງ Mesh ເຂົ້າໃນພື້ນທີ່ 3D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:190
msgid ""
"The 3D APIs are different from the 2D ones, so the instantiation API must be "
"used."
msgstr ""
"API ຂອງ 3D ຈະແຕກຕ່າງຈາກ 2D, ດັ່ງນັ້ນຕ້ອງໃຊ້ API ສຳລັບການສ້າງ Instance ໂດຍສະເພາະ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:243
msgid "Creating a 2D RigidBody and moving a sprite with it"
msgstr "ການສ້າງ RigidBody 2D ແລະ ໃຊ້ຄູ່ກັບການເຄື່ອນຍ້າຍ Sprite"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:245
msgid ""
"This creates a :ref:`class_RigidBody2D` using "
"the :ref:`class_PhysicsServer2D` API, and moves a :ref:`class_CanvasItem` "
"when the body moves."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະສ້າງ :ref:`class_RigidBody2D` ໂດຍໃຊ້ API ຂອງ "
":ref:`class_PhysicsServer2D`, ແລະ ເຄື່ອນຍ້າຍ :ref:`class_CanvasItem` ໃນເວລາທີ່ວັດຖຸຟີ"
"ຊິກເຄື່ອນທີ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:328
msgid ""
"The 3D version should be very similar, as the 2D and 3D physics servers are "
"identical (using :ref:`class_RigidBody3D` and :ref:`class_PhysicsServer3D` "
"respectively)."
msgstr ""
"ເວີຊັນ 3D ຈະມີລັກສະນະຄ້າຍຄືກັນຫຼາຍ, ເນື່ອງຈາກເຊີເວີຟີຊິກ 2D ແລະ 3D ເຮັດວຽກຄືກັນ (ໂດຍໃຊ້ "
":ref:`class_RigidBody3D` ແລະ :ref:`class_PhysicsServer3D` ຕາມລຳດັບ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:333
msgid "Getting data from the servers"
msgstr "ການດຶງຂໍ້ມູນຈາກເຊີເວີ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:335
msgid ""
"Try to **never** request any information "
"from :ref:`class_RenderingServer`, :ref:`class_PhysicsServer2D`, "
"or :ref:`class_PhysicsServer3D` by calling functions unless you know what "
"you are doing. These servers will often run asynchronously for performance "
"and calling any function that returns a value will stall them and force them "
"to process anything pending until the function is actually called. This will "
"severely decrease performance if you call them every frame (and it won't be "
"obvious why)."
msgstr ""
"ພະຍາຍາມ **ຢ່າ** ຮ້ອງຂໍຂໍ້ມູນໃດໆ ຈາກ :ref:`class_RenderingServer`, "
":ref:`class_PhysicsServer2D`, ຫຼື :ref:`class_PhysicsServer3D` ດ້ວຍການຮຽກໃຊ້ຟັງຊັນ "
"ນອກຈາກວ່າທ່ານຈະຮູ້ແທ້ໆ ວ່າກຳລັງເຮັດຫຍັງຢູ່. ເຊີເວີເຫຼົ່ານີ້ມັກຈະເຮັດວຽກແບບບໍ່ພ້ອມກັນ "
"(Asynchronously) ເພື່ອປະສິດທິພາບ ແລະ ການຮຽກໃຊ້ຟັງຊັນໃດໆ ທີ່ສົ່ງຄືນຄ່າຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ພວກມັນຢຸດສະງັກ ແລ"
"ະ ຖືກບັງຄັບໃຫ້ປະມວນຜົນທຸກຢ່າງທີ່ຄ້າງຢູ່ຈົນກວ່າຟັງຊັນນັ້ນຈະຖືກຮຽກໃຊ້ແທ້ໆ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ປະສິດທິພາບຫຼຸດລົງຢ່າງ"
"ຮຸນແຮງຖ້າທ່ານຮຽກໃຊ້ພວກມັນທຸກເຟຣມ (ແລະ ມັນຈະບໍ່ຊັດເຈນວ່າຍ້ອນຫຍັງ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_servers.rst:343
msgid ""
"Because of this, most APIs in such servers are designed so it's not even "
"possible to request information back, until it's actual data that can be "
"saved."
msgstr ""
"ຍ້ອນເຫດນີ້, API ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ໃນເຊີເວີເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນຈຶ່ງຖືກອອກແບບມາໃຫ້ບໍ່ສາມາດຮ້ອງຂໍຂໍ້ມູນຄືນໄດ້ເລີຍ, ຈົນກວ່າຈະເປັນຂໍ້"
"ມູນຕົວຈິງທີ່ສາມາດບັນທຶກໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:4
msgid "CPU optimization"
msgstr "ການປັບແຕ່ງ CPU"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:9
msgid ""
"We have to know where the \"bottlenecks\" are to know how to speed up our "
"program. Bottlenecks are the slowest parts of the program that limit the "
"rate that everything can progress. Focusing on bottlenecks allows us to "
"concentrate our efforts on optimizing the areas which will give us the "
"greatest speed improvement, instead of spending a lot of time optimizing "
"functions that will lead to small performance improvements."
msgstr ""
"ພວກເຮົາຕ້ອງຮູ້ວ່າ \"ຈຸດຄໍຂວດ\" ຢູ່ໃສເພື່ອທີ່ຈະຮູ້ວິທີເລັ່ງຄວາມໄວຂອງໂປຣແກຣມ. ຈຸດຄໍຂວດແມ່ນສ່ວນທີ່ຊ້າທີ່ສຸດຂອ"
"ງໂປຣແກຣມທີ່ຈຳກັດຄວາມໄວໃນການເຮັດວຽກຂອງທຸກຢ່າງ. ການເນັ້ນໃສ່ຈຸດຄໍຂວດຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ພວກເຮົາສຸມຄວາມພະຍາຍາ"
"ມໃນການປັບແຕ່ງພື້ນທີ່ທີ່ຈະໃຫ້ຜົນການປັບປຸງຄວາມໄວສູງສຸດ, ແທນທີ່ຈະເສຍເວລາຫຼາຍໄປກັບການປັບແຕ່ງຟັງຊັນທີ່ໃຫ້ຜົນ"
"ການປັບປຸງປະສິດທິພາບພຽງເລັກນ້ອຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:16
msgid ""
"For the CPU, the easiest way to identify bottlenecks is to use a profiler."
msgstr "ສຳລັບ CPU, ວິທີທີ່ງ່າຍທີ່ສຸດໃນການລະບຸຈຸດຄໍຂວດແມ່ນການໃຊ້ profiler."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:19
msgid "CPU profilers"
msgstr "ເຄື່ອງມືວິເຄາະ CPU (CPU profilers)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:21
msgid ""
"Profilers run alongside your program and take timing measurements to work "
"out what proportion of time is spent in each function."
msgstr ""
"Profilers ເຮັດວຽກໄປພ້ອມກັບໂປຣແກຣມຂອງທ່ານ ແລະ ວັດແທກເວລາເພື່ອເບິ່ງວ່າເວລາສ່ວນໃດຖືກໃຊ້ໄປໃນແຕ່"
"ລະຟັງຊັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:24
msgid ""
"The Godot IDE conveniently has a built-in profiler. It does not run every "
"time you start your project: it must be manually started and stopped. This "
"is because, like most profilers, recording these timing measurements can "
"slow down your project significantly."
msgstr ""
"Godot IDE ມີ profiler ທີ່ມາກັບຕົວມັນເອງ ເຊິ່ງສະດວກຫຼາຍ. ມັນຈະບໍ່ເຮັດວຽກທຸກຄັ້ງທີ່ທ່ານເລີ່ມໂປຣເຈັກ: "
"ມັນຕ້ອງຖືກເປີດ ແລະ ປິດດ້ວຍຕົນເອງ. ນີ້ແມ່ນຍ້ອນວ່າ, ເຊັ່ນດຽວກັບ profiler ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່, ການບັນທຶກການວັດແ"
"ທກເວລາເຫຼົ່ານີ້ສາມາດເຮັດໃຫ້ໂປຣເຈັກຂອງທ່ານຊ້າລົງຢ່າງເຫັນໄດ້ຊັດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:29
msgid "After profiling, you can look back at the results for a frame."
msgstr "ຫຼັງຈາກການວິເຄາະ, ທ່ານສາມາດກັບມາເບິ່ງຜົນລັດສຳລັບແຕ່ລະເຟຣມໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:31
msgid "Screenshot of the Godot profiler"
msgstr "ພາບໜ້າຈໍຂອງ Godot profiler"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:35
msgid "Results of a profile of one of the demo projects."
msgstr "ຜົນລັດຂອງການວິເຄາະຈາກໜຶ່ງໃນໂປຣເຈັກຕົວຢ່າງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:37
msgid ""
"We can see the cost of built-in processes such as physics and audio, as well "
"as seeing the cost of our own scripting functions at the bottom."
msgstr ""
"ພວກເຮົາສາມາດເຫັນຕົ້ນທຶນການປະມວນຜົນຂອງຂະບວນການພາຍໃນເຊັ່ນ ຟີຊິກ ແລະ ສຽງ, ລວມທັງເຫັນຕົ້ນທຶນຂອງຟັ"
"ງຊັນສະຄຣິບຂອງພວກເຮົາເອງຢູ່ທາງລຸ່ມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:41
msgid ""
"Time spent waiting for various built-in servers may not be counted in the "
"profilers. This is a known bug."
msgstr ""
"ເວລາທີ່ໃຊ້ໃນການລໍຖ້າເຊີເວີພາຍໃນຕ່າງໆ ອາດຈະບໍ່ຖືກນັບລວມໃນ profiler. ນີ້ແມ່ນບັກທີ່ຮັບຮູ້ກັນຢູ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:44
msgid ""
"When a project is running slowly, you will often see an obvious function or "
"process taking a lot more time than others. This is your primary bottleneck, "
"and you can usually increase speed by optimizing this area."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອໂປຣເຈັກເຮັດວຽກຊ້າ, ທ່ານມັກຈະເຫັນຟັງຊັນ ຫຼື ຂະບວນການທີ່ຊັດເຈນເຊິ່ງໃຊ້ເວລາຫຼາຍກວ່າສ່ວນອື່ນໆ. ນີ້ຄືຈຸດ"
"ຄໍຂວດຫຼັກຂອງທ່ານ, ແລະ ໂດຍປົກກະຕິທ່ານສາມາດເພີ່ມຄວາມໄວໄດ້ໂດຍການປັບແຕ່ງພື້ນທີ່ນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:48
msgid ""
"For more info about using Godot's built-in profiler, "
"see :ref:`doc_debugger_panel`."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບການໃຊ້ profiler ທີ່ມາກັບ Godot, ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_debugger_panel`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:52
msgid "External profilers"
msgstr "ເຄື່ອງມືວິເຄາະພາຍນອກ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:54
msgid ""
"Although the Godot IDE profiler is very convenient and useful, sometimes you "
"need more power, and the ability to profile the Godot engine source code "
"itself."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າ Godot IDE profiler ຈະສະດວກ ແລະ ມີປະໂຫຍດຫຼາຍ, ແຕ່ບາງຄັ້ງທ່ານຕ້ອງການປະສິດທິພາບຫຼ"
"າຍກວ່ານັ້ນ, ແລະ ຄວາມສາມາດໃນການວິເຄາະຕົວຊອດໂຄດ (Source code) ຂອງ Godot engine ເອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:57
msgid ""
"You can :ref:`use a number of third-party C++ profilers "
"<doc_using_cpp_profilers>` to do this."
msgstr ""
"ທ່ານສາມາດ :ref:`ໃຊ້ເຄື່ອງມືວິເຄາະ C++ ຈາກພາຍນອກ <doc_using_cpp_profilers>` ເພື່ອເຮັດສິ່ງ"
"ນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:60
msgid "Screenshot of Callgrind"
msgstr "ພາບໜ້າຈໍຂອງ Callgrind"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:63
msgid "Example results from Callgrind, which is part of Valgrind."
msgstr "ຕົວຢ່າງຜົນລັດຈາກ Callgrind, ເຊິ່ງເປັນສ່ວນໜຶ່ງຂອງ Valgrind."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:65
msgid ""
"From the left, Callgrind is listing the percentage of time within a function "
"and its children (Inclusive), the percentage of time spent within the "
"function itself, excluding child functions (Self), the number of times the "
"function is called, the function name, and the file or module."
msgstr ""
"ຈາກທາງຊ້າຍ, Callgrind ຈະສະແດງລາຍການເປີເຊັນຂອງເວລາພາຍໃນຟັງຊັນ ແລະ ຟັງຊັນລູກຂອງມັນ "
"(Inclusive), ເປີເຊັນຂອງເວລາທີ່ໃຊ້ໃນຕົວຟັງຊັນເອງ ໂດຍບໍ່ລວມຟັງຊັນລູກ (Self), ຈຳນວນຄັ້ງທີ່ຟັງຊັນຖືກຮ"
"ຽກໃຊ້, ຊື່ຟັງຊັນ, ແລະ ໄຟລ໌ ຫຼື ໂມດູນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:70
msgid ""
"In this example, we can see nearly all time is spent under the "
"``Main::iteration()`` function. This is the master function in the Godot "
"source code that is called repeatedly. It causes frames to be drawn, physics "
"ticks to be simulated, and nodes and scripts to be updated. A large "
"proportion of the time is spent in the functions to render a canvas (66%), "
"because this example uses a 2D benchmark. Below this, we see that almost 50% "
"of the time is spent outside Godot code in ``libglapi`` and ``i965_dri`` "
"(the graphics driver). This tells us the a large proportion of CPU time is "
"being spent in the graphics driver."
msgstr ""
"ໃນຕົວຢ່າງນີ້, ພວກເຮົາເຫັນວ່າເກືອບທັງໝົດຂອງເວລາແມ່ນໃຊ້ໄປໃນຟັງຊັນ ``Main::iteration()``. ນີ້ຄືຟັງ"
"ຊັນຫຼັກໃນຊອດໂຄດຂອງ Godot ທີ່ຖືກຮຽກໃຊ້ຊ້ຳໆ. ມັນເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດການແຕ້ມເຟຣມ, ການຈຳລອງຟີຊິກ, ແລະ ການ"
"ອັບເດດໂນດ ແລະ ສະຄຣິບ. ເວລາສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ຖືກໃຊ້ໄປໃນຟັງຊັນສຳລັບການເຣັນເດີ canvas (66%), ເພາະວ່າຕົວ"
"ຢ່າງນີ້ໃຊ້ການທົດສອບແບບ 2D. ຖັດລົງມາ, ພວກເຮົາເຫັນວ່າເກືອບ 50% ຂອງເວລາແມ່ນໃຊ້ຢູ່ນອກໂຄດຂອງ "
"Godot ໃນ ``libglapi`` ແລະ ``i965_dri`` (ໄດຣເວີກຣາບຟິກ). ສິ່ງນີ້ບອກໃຫ້ພວກເຮົາຮູ້ວ່າເວລາສ່ວ"
"ນໃຫຍ່ຂອງ CPU ແມ່ນໃຊ້ໄປໃນໄດຣເວີກຣາບຟິກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:80
msgid ""
"This is actually an excellent example because, in an ideal world, only a "
"very small proportion of time would be spent in the graphics driver. This is "
"an indication that there is a problem with too much communication and work "
"being done in the graphics API. This specific profiling led to the "
"development of 2D batching, which greatly speeds up 2D rendering by reducing "
"bottlenecks in this area."
msgstr ""
"ອັນນີ້ເປັນຕົວຢ່າງທີ່ດີຫຼາຍ ເພາະວ່າໃນໂລກທີ່ສົມບູນແບບ, ເວລາພຽງເລັກນ້ອຍເທົ່ານັ້ນທີ່ຈະຖືກໃຊ້ໃນໄດຣເວີກຣາບຟິ"
"ກ. ສິ່ງນີ້ສະແດງໃຫ້ເຫັນວ່າມີບັນຫາກ່ຽວກັບການສື່ສານ ແລະ ວຽກງານທີ່ເຮັດໃນ graphics API ຫຼາຍເກີນໄປ. ກ"
"ານວິເຄາະສະເພາະນີ້ໄດ້ນຳໄປສູ່ການພັດທະນາລະບົບ 2D batching, ເຊິ່ງຊ່ວຍເລັ່ງຄວາມໄວໃນການເຣັນເດີ 2D "
"ຢ່າງມະຫາສານໂດຍການຫຼຸດຈຸດຄໍຂວດໃນພື້ນທີ່ນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:88
msgid "Manually timing functions"
msgstr "ການຈັບເວລາຟັງຊັນດ້ວຍຕົນເອງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:90
msgid ""
"Another handy technique, especially once you have identified the bottleneck "
"using a profiler, is to manually time the function or area under test. The "
"specifics vary depending on the language, but in GDScript, you would do the "
"following:"
msgstr ""
"ອີກເຕັກນິກໜຶ່ງທີ່ມີປະໂຫຍດ, ໂດຍສະເພາະເມື່ອທ່ານລະບຸຈຸດຄໍຂວດໄດ້ແລ້ວໂດຍໃຊ້ profiler, ແມ່ນການຈັບເວລາຟັ"
"ງຊັນ ຫຼື ພື້ນທີ່ທີ່ກຳລັງທົດສອບດ້ວຍຕົນເອງ. ລາຍລະອຽດຈະແຕກຕ່າງກັນໄປຕາມພາສາ, ແຕ່ໃນ GDScript, ທ່ານສ"
"າມາດເຮັດໄດ້ດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:116
msgid ""
"When manually timing functions, it is usually a good idea to run the "
"function many times (1,000 or more times), instead of just once (unless it "
"is a very slow function). The reason for doing this is that timers often "
"have limited accuracy. Moreover, CPUs will schedule processes in a haphazard "
"manner. Therefore, an average over a series of runs is more accurate than a "
"single measurement."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອຈັບເວລາຟັງຊັນດ້ວຍຕົນເອງ, ມັນມັກຈະເປັນການດີທີ່ຈະສັ່ງໃຫ້ຟັງຊັນເຮັດວຽກຫຼາຍໆ ຄັ້ງ (1,000 ຄັ້ງ ຫຼື ຫຼາຍກ"
"ວ່ານັ້ນ), ແທນທີ່ຈະເຮັດພຽງຄັ້ງດຽວ (ນອກຈາກວ່າມັນເປັນຟັງຊັນທີ່ຊ້າຫຼາຍ). ເຫດຜົນທີ່ເຮັດແນວນັ້ນແມ່ນຍ້ອນວ່າເຄື່ອ"
"ງຈັບເວລາມັກຈະມີຄວາມຊັດເຈນທີ່ຈຳກັດ. ນອກຈາກນັ້ນ, CPU ຈະຈັດລໍາດັບການປະມວນຜົນແບບສຸ່ມ. ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ຄ່າສະ"
"ເລ່ຍຈາກການເຮັດວຽກຫຼາຍໆ ຄັ້ງຈຶ່ງຊັດເຈນກວ່າການວັດແທກພຽງຄັ້ງດຽວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:122
msgid ""
"As you attempt to optimize functions, be sure to either repeatedly profile "
"or time them as you go. This will give you crucial feedback as to whether "
"the optimization is working (or not)."
msgstr ""
"ໃນຂະນະທີ່ທ່ານພະຍາຍາມປັບແຕ່ງຟັງຊັນ, ໃຫ້ໝັ້ນໃຈວ່າໄດ້ວິເຄາະ ຫຼື ຈັບເວລາພວກມັນຊ້ຳໆ ໃນຂະນະທີ່ເຮັດ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈ"
"ະໃຫ້ຂໍ້ມູນຕອບກັບທີ່ສຳຄັນວ່າການປັບແຕ່ງນັ້ນໄດ້ຜົນຫຼືບໍ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:127
msgid "Caches"
msgstr "ແຄຊ (Caches)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:129
msgid ""
"CPU caches are something else to be particularly aware of, especially when "
"comparing timing results of two different versions of a function. The "
"results can be highly dependent on whether the data is in the CPU cache or "
"not. CPUs don't load data directly from the system RAM, even though it's "
"huge in comparison to the CPU cache (several gigabytes instead of a few "
"megabytes). This is because system RAM is very slow to access. Instead, CPUs "
"load data from a smaller, faster bank of memory called cache. Loading data "
"from cache is very fast, but every time you try and load a memory address "
"that is not stored in cache, the cache must make a trip to main memory and "
"slowly load in some data. This delay can result in the CPU sitting around "
"idle for a long time, and is referred to as a \"cache miss\"."
msgstr ""
"CPU cache ແມ່ນສິ່ງທີ່ຕ້ອງລະວັງເປັນພິເສດ, ໂດຍສະເພາະເມື່ອປຽບທຽບຜົນການຈັບເວລາຂອງຟັງຊັນສອງເວີຊັນທີ່ແ"
"ຕກຕ່າງກັນ. ຜົນລັດອາດຈະຂຶ້ນຢູ່ກັບວ່າຂໍ້ມູນຢູ່ໃນ CPU cache ຫຼື ບໍ່. CPU ບໍ່ໄດ້ໂຫຼດຂໍ້ມູນໂດຍກົງຈາກ system "
"RAM, ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າມັນຈະໃຫຍ່ຫຼາຍເມື່ອທຽບກັບ CPU cache (ຫຼາຍກິກະໄບ ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນພຽງບໍ່ເທົ່າໃດເມກະໄບ)"
". ນີ້ແມ່ນຍ້ອນວ່າ system RAM ເຂົ້າເຖິງໄດ້ຊ້າຫຼາຍ. ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນແນວນັ້ນ, CPU ຈະໂຫຼດຂໍ້ມູນຈາກໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈ"
"ຳທີ່ນ້ອຍກວ່າ ແລະ ໄວກວ່າທີ່ເອີ້ນວ່າ cache. ການໂຫຼດຂໍ້ມູນຈາກ cache ແມ່ນໄວຫຼາຍ, ແຕ່ທຸກໆ ຄັ້ງທີ່ທ່ານພະຍາ"
"ຍາມໂຫຼດຕຳແໜ່ງໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳທີ່ບໍ່ໄດ້ເກັບໄວ້ໃນ cache, cache ຈະຕ້ອງເດີນທາງໄປຫາໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳຫຼັກ ແລະ ໂ"
"ຫຼດຂໍ້ມູນເຂົ້າມາຢ່າງຊ້າໆ. ຄວາມຊັກຊ້ານີ້ສາມາດເຮັດໃຫ້ CPU ວ່າງວຽກເປັນເວລາດົນ, ແລະ ເອີ້ນວ່າ \"cache "
"miss\"."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:141
msgid ""
"This means that the first time you run a function, it may run slowly because "
"the data is not in the CPU cache. The second and later times, it may run "
"much faster because the data is in the cache. Due to this, always use "
"averages when timing, and be aware of the effects of cache."
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າຄັ້ງທຳອິດທີ່ທ່ານສັ່ງໃຫ້ຟັງຊັນເຮັດວຽກ, ມັນອາດຈະຊ້າເພາະຂໍ້ມູນບໍ່ໄດ້ຢູ່ໃນ CPU cache. ຄັ້ງທີສອງ "
"ແລະ ຄັ້ງຕໍ່ໆ ໄປ, ມັນອາດຈະໄວຂຶ້ນຫຼາຍເພາະຂໍ້ມູນຢູ່ໃນ cache ແລ້ວ. ຍ້ອນເຫດນີ້, ຄວນໃຊ້ຄ່າສະເລ່ຍສະເໝີໃນກ"
"ານຈັບເວລາ, ແລະ ຄຳນຶງເຖິງຜົນກະທົບຂອງ cache."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:146
msgid ""
"Understanding caching is also crucial to CPU optimization. If you have an "
"algorithm (routine) that loads small bits of data from randomly spread out "
"areas of main memory, this can result in a lot of cache misses, a lot of the "
"time, the CPU will be waiting around for data instead of doing any work. "
"Instead, if you can make your data accesses localised, or even better, "
"access memory in a linear fashion (like a continuous list), then the cache "
"will work optimally and the CPU will be able to work as fast as possible."
msgstr ""
"ການເຂົ້າໃຈເລື່ອງ caching ແມ່ນສຳຄັນຫຼາຍຕໍ່ການປັບແຕ່ງ CPU. ຖ້າທ່ານມີ algorithm ທີ່ໂຫຼດຂໍ້ມູນນ້ອຍໆ ຈາ"
"ກພື້ນທີ່ຕ່າງໆ ໃນໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳຫຼັກແບບສຸ່ມ, ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະສົ່ງຜົນໃຫ້ເກີດ cache miss ຈຳນວນຫຼາຍ, ແລະ ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ແລ້"
"ວ CPU ຈະເສຍເວລາໄປກັບການລໍຖ້າຂໍ້ມູນແທນທີ່ຈະເຮັດວຽກ. ໃນທາງກົງກັນຂ້າມ, ຖ້າທ່ານສາມາດເຮັດໃຫ້ການເຂົ້າ"
"ເຖິງຂໍ້ມູນຢູ່ໃກ້ກັນ, ຫຼື ດີກວ່ານັ້ນຄືການເຂົ້າເຖິງໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳແບບເສັ້ນຊື່ (ຄືກັບລາຍການທີ່ຕໍ່ເນື່ອງກັນ), ຈາກນັ້ນ "
"cache ຈະເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ຢ່າງມີປະສິດທິພາບສູງສຸດ ແລະ CPU ຈະສາມາດເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ໄວທີ່ສຸດເທົ່າທີ່ຈະເປັນໄປໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:154
msgid ""
"Godot usually takes care of such low-level details for you. For example, the "
"Server APIs make sure data is optimized for caching already for things like "
"rendering and physics. Still, you should be especially aware of caching when "
"writing GDExtensions."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍປົກກະຕິ Godot ຈະຈັດການລາຍລະອຽດລະດັບຕ່ຳເຫຼົ່ານີ້ໃຫ້ທ່ານແລ້ວ. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ, Server API ຈະຮັບປະ"
"ກັນວ່າຂໍ້ມູນຖືກປັບແຕ່ງໃຫ້ເໝາະສົມກັບ caching ແລ້ວສຳລັບສິ່ງຕ່າງໆ ເຊັ່ນ ການເຣັນເດີ ແລະ ຟີຊິກ. ເຖິງຢ່າງໃດ"
"ກໍຕາມ, ທ່ານຄວນຄຳນຶງເຖິງເລື່ອງ caching ເປັນພິເສດເມື່ອຂຽນ GDExtensions."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:162
msgid ""
"Godot supports a number of different languages, and it is worth bearing in "
"mind that there are trade-offs involved. Some languages are designed for "
"ease of use at the cost of speed, and others are faster but more difficult "
"to work with."
msgstr ""
"Godot ຮອງຮັບພາສາທີ່ຫຼາກຫຼາຍ, ແລະ ມັນຄຸ້ມຄ່າທີ່ຈະຈື່ໄວ້ວ່າມັນມີສິ່ງທີ່ຕ້ອງແລກປ່ຽນ. ບາງພາສາຖືກອອກແບບມາໃ"
"ຫ້ໃຊ້ງ່າຍແຕ່ຕ້ອງແລກດ້ວຍຄວາມໄວ, ແລະ ພາສາອື່ນໆ ທີ່ໄວແຕ່ເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ຍາກກວ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:166
msgid ""
"Built-in engine functions run at the same speed regardless of the scripting "
"language you choose. If your project is making a lot of calculations in its "
"own code, consider moving those calculations to a faster language."
msgstr ""
"ຟັງຊັນພາຍໃນຂອງເອນຈິນຈະເຮັດວຽກດ້ວຍຄວາມໄວດຽວກັນ ບໍ່ວ່າທ່ານຈະເລືອກໃຊ້ພາສາສະຄຣິບໃດກໍຕາມ. ຖ້າໂປຣເ"
"ຈັກຂອງທ່ານມີການຄຳນວນຈຳນວນຫຼາຍໃນໂຄດຂອງທ່ານເອງ, ໃຫ້ພິຈາລະນາຍ້າຍການຄຳນວນເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນໄປຫາພາສາທີ່ໄວ"
"ກວ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:173
msgid ""
":ref:`GDScript <doc_gdscript>` is designed to be easy to use and iterate, "
"and is ideal for making many types of games. However, in this language, ease "
"of use is considered more important than performance. If you need to make "
"heavy calculations, consider moving some of your project to one of the other "
"languages."
msgstr ""
":ref:`GDScript <doc_gdscript>` ຖືກອອກແບບມາໃຫ້ໃຊ້ງານ ແລະ ປັບແຕ່ງໄດ້ງ່າຍ, ແລະ ເໝາະສົມສຳ"
"ລັບການສ້າງເກມຫຼາຍປະເພດ. ເຖິງຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ໃນພາສານີ້, ຄວາມງ່າຍໃນການໃຊ້ງານຖືກຖືວ່າສຳຄັນກວ່າປະສິດ"
"ທິພາບ. ຖ້າທ່ານຕ້ອງການຄຳນວນສິ່ງທີ່ໜັກໜ່ວງ, ໃຫ້ພິຈາລະນາຍ້າຍບາງສ່ວນຂອງໂປຣເຈັກໄປຫາພາສາອື່ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:182
msgid ""
":ref:`C# <doc_c_sharp>` is popular and has first-class support in Godot. It "
"offers a good compromise between speed and ease of use. Beware of possible "
"garbage collection pauses and leaks that can occur during gameplay, though. "
"A common approach to workaround issues with garbage collection is to use "
"*object pooling*, which is outside the scope of this guide."
msgstr ""
":ref:`C# <doc_c_sharp>` ເປັນທີ່ນິຍົມ ແລະ ໄດ້ຮັບການຮອງຮັບຢ່າງເຕັມທີ່ໃນ Godot. ມັນເປັນຈຸດສົມດຸນທີ່"
"ດີລະຫວ່າງຄວາມໄວ ແລະ ຄວາມງ່າຍໃນການໃຊ້ງານ. ແຕ່ຄວນລະວັງເລື່ອງການຢຸດຊົ່ວຄາວຈາກ Garbage "
"collection ແລະ ການຮົ່ວໄຫຼຂອງໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳ (Leaks) ທີ່ອາດເກີດຂຶ້ນໃນລະຫວ່າງການຫຼິ້ນເກມ. ວິທີທົ່ວໄປໃ"
"ນການແກ້ໄຂບັນຫາ Garbage collection ແມ່ນການໃຊ້ *object pooling*, ເຊິ່ງຢູ່ນອກຂອບເຂດຂອງຄູ່ມື"
"ນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:189
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/other_languages.rst:4
msgid "Other languages"
msgstr "ພາສາອື່ນໆ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:191
msgid ""
"Third parties provide support for several other languages, including `Rust "
"<https://github.com/godot-rust/gdext>`_."
msgstr ""
"ບຸກຄົນພາຍນອກມີການສະໜັບສະໜູນພາສາອື່ນໆ ອີກຫຼາຍພາສາ, ລວມທັງ `Rust <https://github.com/"
"godot-rust/gdext>`_."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:197
msgid ""
"Godot is written in C++. Using C++ will usually result in the fastest code. "
"However, on a practical level, it is the most difficult to deploy to end "
"users' machines on different platforms. Options for using C++ include "
"GDExtensions and :ref:`custom modules <doc_custom_modules_in_cpp>`."
msgstr ""
"Godot ຖືກຂຽນຂຶ້ນດ້ວຍ C++. ການໃຊ້ C++ ມັກຈະໃຫ້ໂຄດທີ່ໄວທີ່ສຸດ. ເຖິງຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ໃນທາງປະຕິບັດ, ມັນ"
"ເປັນພາສາທີ່ຍາກທີ່ສຸດໃນການນຳໃຊ້ (Deploy) ໄປຫາເຄື່ອງຂອງຜູ້ໃຊ້ໃນແພລັດຟອມຕ່າງໆ. ທາງເລືອກສຳລັບການໃ"
"ຊ້ C++ ລວມມີ GDExtensions ແລະ :ref:`custom modules <doc_custom_modules_in_cpp>"
"`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:206
msgid ""
"Consider using threads when making a lot of calculations that can run in "
"parallel to each other. Modern CPUs have multiple cores, each one capable of "
"doing a limited amount of work. By spreading work over multiple threads, you "
"can move further towards peak CPU efficiency."
msgstr ""
"ໃຫ້ພິຈາລະນາການໃຊ້ເທຣດ (Threads) ເມື່ອມີການຄຳນວນຈຳນວນຫຼາຍທີ່ສາມາດເຮັດວຽກຂະໜານກັນໄດ້. CPU ໃ"
"ນປັດຈຸບັນມີຫຼາຍແກນ (Cores), ເຊິ່ງແຕ່ລະແກນສາມາດເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ໃນຈຳນວນຈຳກັດ. ດ້ວຍການກະຈາຍວຽກໄປຍັງ"
"ຫຼາຍເທຣດ, ທ່ານສາມາດເຂົ້າໃກ້ປະສິດທິພາບສູງສຸດຂອງ CPU ໄດ້ຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:211
msgid ""
"The disadvantage of threads is that you have to be incredibly careful. As "
"each CPU core operates independently, they can end up trying to access the "
"same memory at the same time. One thread can be reading to a variable while "
"another is writing: this is called a *race condition*. Before you use "
"threads, make sure you understand the dangers and how to try and prevent "
"these race conditions. Threads can make debugging considerably more "
"difficult."
msgstr ""
"ຂໍ້ເສຍຂອງເທຣດແມ່ນທ່ານຕ້ອງລະມັດລະວັງເປັນຢ່າງສູງ. ເນື່ອງຈາກແຕ່ລະແກນ CPU ເຮັດວຽກແຍກກັນ, ພວກມັນອາ"
"ດຈະພະຍາຍາມເຂົ້າເຖິງໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳດຽວກັນໃນເວລາດຽວກັນ. ເທຣດໜຶ່ງອາດຈະກຳລັງອ່ານຄ່າຕົວປ່ຽນ ໃນຂະນະທີ່ອີ"
"ກເທຣດໜຶ່ງກຳລັງຂຽນ: ສິ່ງນີ້ເອີ້ນວ່າ *race condition*. ກ່ອນທີ່ທ່ານຈະໃຊ້ເທຣດ, ໃຫ້ໝັ້ນໃຈວ່າທ່ານເຂົ້າໃຈເ"
"ຖິງອັນຕະລາຍ ແລະ ວິທີການປ້ອງກັນ race condition ເຫຼົ່ານີ້. ເທຣດສາມາດເຮັດໃຫ້ການ Debug ຍາກຂຶ້ນກວ່"
"າເກົ່າຫຼາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:218
msgid "For more information on threads, see :ref:`doc_using_multiple_threads`."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບເທຣດ, ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_using_multiple_threads`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:221
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/scene_tree.rst:33
msgid "SceneTree"
msgstr "SceneTree"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:223
msgid ""
"Although Nodes are an incredibly powerful and versatile concept, be aware "
"that every node has a cost. Built-in functions such as ``_process()`` and "
"``_physics_process()`` propagate through the tree. This housekeeping can "
"reduce performance when you have a very large numbers of nodes (how many "
"exactly depends on the target platform and can range from thousands to tens "
"of thousands so ensure that you profile performance on all target platforms "
"during development)."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າ ໂນດ (Nodes) ຈະເປັນແນວຄິດທີ່ມີປະສິດທິພາບ ແລະ ຫຼາກຫຼາຍ, ແຕ່ໃຫ້ຮູ້ໄວ້ວ່າທຸກໆ ໂນດມີຕົ້ນທຶນກາ"
"ນປະມວນຜົນ. ຟັງຊັນພາຍໃນເຊັ່ນ ``_process()`` ແລະ ``_physics_process()`` ຈະສົ່ງຜ່ານໄປທົ່ວທັ"
"ງ Tree. ການຈັດການພາຍໃນນີ້ສາມາດຫຼຸດປະສິດທິພາບລົງໄດ້ເມື່ອທ່ານມີໂນດຈຳນວນມະຫາສານ (ຈຳນວນທີ່ແນ່ນອນຂຶ້"
"ນຢູ່ກັບແພລັດຟອມເປົ້າໝາຍ ແລະ ອາດມີຕັ້ງແຕ່ຫຼັກພັນໄປຫາຫຼັກໝື່ນ ດັ່ງນັ້ນໃຫ້ໝັ້ນໃຈວ່າໄດ້ວິເຄາະປະສິດທິພາບໃນທຸກແພລັ"
"ດຟອມໃນລະຫວ່າງການພັດທະນາ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:231
msgid ""
"Each node is handled individually in the Godot renderer. Therefore, a "
"smaller number of nodes with more in each can lead to better performance."
msgstr ""
"ແຕ່ລະໂນດຈະຖືກຈັດການແຍກກັນໃນຕົວເຣັນເດີຂອງ Godot. ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ການມີໂນດຈຳນວນໜ້ອຍລົງແຕ່ມີລາຍລະອຽດພາ"
"ຍໃນຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນ ສາມາດນຳໄປສູ່ປະສິດທິພາບທີ່ດີກວ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:234
msgid ""
"One quirk of the :ref:`SceneTree <class_SceneTree>` is that you can "
"sometimes get much better performance by removing nodes from the SceneTree, "
"rather than by pausing or hiding them. You don't have to delete a detached "
"node. You can for example, keep a reference to a node, detach it from the "
"scene tree using :ref:`Node.remove_child(node) "
"<class_Node_method_remove_child>`, then reattach it later "
"using :ref:`Node.add_child(node) <class_Node_method_add_child>`. This can be "
"very useful for adding and removing areas from a game, for example."
msgstr ""
"ຈຸດພິເສດຢ່າງໜຶ່ງຂອງ :ref:`SceneTree <class_SceneTree>` ແມ່ນບາງຄັ້ງທ່ານສາມາດໄດ້ຮັບປະສິດທິພາ"
"ບທີ່ດີກວ່າຫຼາຍໂດຍການເອົາໂນດອອກຈາກ SceneTree, ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນການຢຸດ (Pause) ຫຼື ເຊື່ອງ (Hide) ພ"
"ວກມັນ. ທ່ານບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງລຶບໂນດທີ່ແຍກອອກມາ. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ, ທ່ານສາມາດເກັບການອ້າງອີງເຖິງໂນດໄວ້, ແຍກມັ"
"ນອອກຈາກ SceneTree ໂດຍໃຊ້ :ref:`Node.remove_child(node) "
"<class_Node_method_remove_child>`, ແລ້ວນຳມາກັບຄືນໃສ່ໃໝ່ໃນພາຍຫຼັງໂດຍໃຊ້ "
":ref:`Node.add_child(node) <class_Node_method_add_child>`. ສິ່ງນີ້ມີປະໂຫຍດຫຼາຍສຳລັບກ"
"ານເພີ່ມ ແລະ ເອົາພື້ນທີ່ອອກຈາກເກມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:242
msgid ""
"You can avoid the SceneTree altogether by using Server APIs. For more "
"information, see :ref:`doc_using_servers`."
msgstr ""
"ທ່ານສາມາດຫຼີກລ່ຽງການໃຊ້ SceneTree ໄດ້ທັງໝົດໂດຍການໃຊ້ Server API. ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມ, ເບິ່ງ "
":ref:`doc_using_servers`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:248
msgid ""
"In some situations, physics can end up becoming a bottleneck. This is "
"particularly the case with complex worlds and large numbers of physics "
"objects."
msgstr ""
"ໃນບາງສະຖານະການ, ຟີຊິກອາດກາຍເປັນຈຸດຄໍຂວດໄດ້. ສິ່ງນີ້ມັກຈະເກີດຂຶ້ນກັບໂລກທີ່ມີຄວາມຊັບຊ້ອນ ແລະ ມີວັດຖຸຟີຊິ"
"ກຈຳນວນຫຼາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:251
msgid "Here are some techniques to speed up physics:"
msgstr "ນີ້ແມ່ນບາງເຕັກນິກເພື່ອເລັ່ງຄວາມໄວຟີຊິກ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:253
msgid ""
"Try using simplified versions of your rendered geometry for collision "
"shapes. Often, this won't be noticeable for end users, but can greatly "
"increase performance."
msgstr ""
"ລອງໃຊ້ຮູບຮ່າງທີ່ລຽບງ່າຍ (Simplified) ຂອງວັດຖຸທີ່ເຣັນເດີມາເຮັດເປັນ Collision shapes. ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ແ"
"ລ້ວ ຜູ້ໃຊ້ຈະບໍ່ສັງເກດເຫັນຄວາມແຕກຕ່າງ, ແຕ່ມັນສາມາດເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບໄດ້ຫຼາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:256
msgid ""
"Try removing objects from physics when they are out of view / outside the "
"current area, or reusing physics objects (maybe you allow 8 monsters per "
"area, for example, and reuse these)."
msgstr ""
"ລອງເອົາວັດຖຸອອກຈາກລະບົບຟີຊິກເມື່ອພວກມັນຢູ່ນອກສາຍຕາ / ນອກພື້ນທີ່ປັດຈຸບັນ, ຫຼື ການນຳວັດຖຸຟີຊິກມາກັບມາໃຊ້ໃ"
"ໝ່ (ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ ທ່ານອາດຈະກຳນົດໃຫ້ມີຜີ 8 ໂຕຕໍ່ພື້ນທີ່ ແລະ ໃຊ້ວັດຖຸເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນຊ້ຳ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:260
msgid ""
"Another crucial aspect to physics is the physics tick rate. In some games, "
"you can greatly reduce the tick rate, and instead of for example, updating "
"physics 60 times per second, you may update them only 30 or even 20 times "
"per second. This can greatly reduce the CPU load."
msgstr ""
"ອີກແງ່ມຸມໜຶ່ງທີ່ສຳຄັນຂອງຟີຊິກແມ່ນ Physics tick rate. ໃນບາງເກມ, ທ່ານສາມາດຫຼຸດ tick rate ລົງໄດ້"
"ຫຼາຍ, ແລະ ແທນທີ່ຈະອັບເດດຟີຊິກ 60 ຄັ້ງຕໍ່ວິນາທີ, ທ່ານອາດຈະອັບເດດພຽງແຕ່ 30 ຫຼື ແມ່ນແຕ່ 20 ຄັ້ງຕໍ່ວິນາ"
"ທີ. ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດຫຼຸດພາລະຂອງ CPU ໄດ້ຫຼາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:265
msgid ""
"The downside of changing physics tick rate is you can get jerky movement or "
"jitter when the physics update rate does not match the frames per second "
"rendered. Also, decreasing the physics tick rate will increase input lag. "
"It's recommended to stick to the default physics tick rate (60 Hz) in most "
"games that feature real-time player movement."
msgstr ""
"ຂໍ້ເສຍຂອງການປ່ຽນ physics tick rate ແມ່ນທ່ານອາດຈະເຫັນການເຄື່ອນທີ່ທີ່ກະຕຸກ ຫຼື ສັ່ນ (Jitter) ເມື່ອ"
"ອັດຕາການອັບເດດຟີຊິກບໍ່ກົງກັບເຟຣມທີ່ເຣັນເດີ. ນອກຈາກນັ້ນ, ການຫຼຸດ physics tick rate ຈະເພີ່ມອາການຊັ"
"ກຊ້າໃນການຕອບສະໜອງ (Input lag). ແນະນຳໃຫ້ໃຊ້ຄ່າເບື້ອງຕົ້ນ (60 Hz) ໃນເກມສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ທີ່ມີການເຄື່ອນທີ່"
"ຂອງຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນແບບເວລາຈິງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/cpu_optimization.rst:271
msgid ""
"The solution to jitter is to use *fixed timestep interpolation*, which "
"involves smoothing the rendered positions and rotations over multiple frames "
"to match the physics. Godot has built-in physics interpolation which you can "
"read about :ref:`here<doc_physics_interpolation>`. Performance-wise, "
"interpolation is a very cheap operation compared to running a physics tick. "
"It's orders of magnitude faster, so this can be a significant performance "
"win while also reducing jitter."
msgstr ""
"ວິທີແກ້ໄຂບັນຫາການສັ່ນ (Jitter) ແມ່ນການໃຊ້ *fixed timestep interpolation*, ເຊິ່ງກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັບ"
"ການເຮັດໃຫ້ຕຳແໜ່ງ ແລະ ການໝຸນທີ່ເຣັນເດີອອກມາມີຄວາມນຸ່ມນວນຂຶ້ນໃນຫຼາຍໆ ເຟຣມເພື່ອໃຫ້ກົງກັບຟີຊິກ. Godot "
"ມີລະບົບ physics interpolation ພາຍໃນເຊິ່ງທ່ານສາມາດອ່ານໄດ້ :ref:`ທີ່"
"ນີ້<doc_physics_interpolation>`. ໃນແງ່ຂອງປະສິດທິພາບ, interpolation ແມ່ນການເຮັດວຽກທີ່ມີຕົ້"
"ນທຶນຕ່ຳຫຼາຍເມື່ອທຽບກັບການປະມວນຜົນຟີຊິກ. ມັນໄວຫຼາຍກວ່າກັນຫຼາຍເທົ່າ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນສິ່ງນີ້ຈຶ່ງເປັນຜົນດີຕໍ່ປະສິດທິພາບ ແ"
"ລະ ຍັງຊ່ວຍຫຼຸດອາການສັ່ນໄດ້ນຳ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:4
msgid "GPU optimization"
msgstr "ການປັບແຕ່ງ GPU"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:9
msgid ""
"The demand for new graphics features and progress almost guarantees that you "
"will encounter graphics bottlenecks. Some of these can be on the CPU side, "
"for instance in calculations inside the Godot engine to prepare objects for "
"rendering. Bottlenecks can also occur on the CPU in the graphics driver, "
"which sorts instructions to pass to the GPU, and in the transfer of these "
"instructions. And finally, bottlenecks also occur on the GPU itself."
msgstr ""
"ຄວາມຕ້ອງການຟີເຈີກຣາບຟິກໃໝ່ໆ ແລະ ຄວາມກ້າວໜ້າມັກຈະຮັບປະກັນວ່າທ່ານຈະພົບກັບຈຸດຄໍຂວດທາງກຣາບຟິກ. ບາງ"
"ສ່ວນອາດເກີດຂຶ້ນຢູ່ຝ່າຍ CPU, ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນໃນການຄຳນວນພາຍໃນ Godot engine ເພື່ອຕຽມວັດຖຸສຳລັບການເຣັນ"
"ເດີ. ຈຸດຄໍຂວດຍັງສາມາດເກີດຂຶ້ນຢູ່ CPU ໃນສ່ວນຂອງໄດຣເວີກຣາບຟິກ, ເຊິ່ງຈັດລຽງຄຳສັ່ງເພື່ອສົ່ງໄປໃຫ້ GPU, ແ"
"ລະ ໃນການສົ່ງຜ່ານຄຳສັ່ງເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນ. ແລະ ສຸດທ້າຍ, ຈຸດຄໍຂວດກໍເກີດຂຶ້ນຢູ່ທີ່ຕົວ GPU ເອງນຳ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:16
msgid ""
"Where bottlenecks occur in rendering is highly hardware-specific. Mobile "
"GPUs in particular may struggle with scenes that run easily on desktop."
msgstr ""
"ຈຸດທີ່ເກີດຈຸດຄໍຂວດໃນການເຣັນເດີນັ້ນຂຶ້ນຢູ່ກັບຮາດແວສະເພາະ. ໂດຍສະເພາະ GPU ຂອງມືຖືອາດຈະເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ຍາກ"
"ກັບສາກທີ່ເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ງ່າຍໆ ໃນຄອມພິວເຕີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:19
msgid ""
"Understanding and investigating GPU bottlenecks is slightly different to the "
"situation on the CPU. This is because, often, you can only change "
"performance indirectly by changing the instructions you give to the GPU. "
"Also, it may be more difficult to take measurements. In many cases, the only "
"way of measuring performance is by examining changes in the time spent "
"rendering each frame."
msgstr ""
"ການເຂົ້າໃຈ ແລະ ການກວດສອບຈຸດຄໍຂວດຂອງ GPU ຈະແຕກຕ່າງຈາກ CPU ເລັກນ້ອຍ. ນີ້ແມ່ນຍ້ອນວ່າ, ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່"
"ແລ້ວ, ທ່ານສາມາດປ່ຽນແປງປະສິດທິພາບທາງອ້ອມໄດ້ໂດຍການປ່ຽນຄຳສັ່ງທີ່ທ່ານໃຫ້ກັບ GPU ເທົ່ານັ້ນ. ນອກຈາກນັ້"
"ນ, ມັນອາດຈະຍາກກວ່າໃນການວັດແທກ. ໃນຫຼາຍກໍລະນີ, ວິທີດຽວໃນການວັດແທກປະສິດທິພາບແມ່ນການກວດສອບການ"
"ປ່ຽນແປງຂອງເວລາທີ່ໃຊ້ໃນການເຣັນເດີແຕ່ລະເຟຣມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:26
msgid "Draw calls, state changes, and APIs"
msgstr "ການຮຽກໃຊ້ການແຕ້ມ (Draw calls), ການປ່ຽນສະຖານະ (State changes), ແລະ API"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:28
msgid ""
"The following section is not relevant to end-users, but is useful to provide "
"background information that is relevant in later sections."
msgstr ""
"ພາກສ່ວນຕໍ່ໄປນີ້ອາດຈະບໍ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັບຜູ້ໃຊ້ທົ່ວໄປ, ແຕ່ມີປະໂຫຍດໃນການໃຫ້ຂໍ້ມູນພື້ນຖານທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັບພາກສ່ວນຕໍ່ໆ ໄ"
"ປ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:31
msgid ""
"Godot sends instructions to the GPU via a graphics API (Vulkan, OpenGL, "
"OpenGL ES or WebGL). The communication and driver activity involved can be "
"quite costly, especially in OpenGL, OpenGL ES and WebGL. If we can provide "
"these instructions in a way that is preferred by the driver and GPU, we can "
"greatly increase performance."
msgstr ""
"Godot ສົ່ງຄຳສັ່ງໄປຫາ GPU ຜ່ານ Graphics API (Vulkan, OpenGL, OpenGL ES ຫຼື WebGL). ກາ"
"ນສື່ສານ ແລະ ການເຮັດວຽກຂອງໄດຣເວີທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງອາດຈະມີຕົ້ນທຶນສູງ, ໂດຍສະເພາະໃນ OpenGL, OpenGL "
"ES ແລະ WebGL. ຖ້າພວກເຮົາສາມາດໃຫ້ຄຳສັ່ງເຫຼົ່ານີ້ໃນຮູບແບບທີ່ໄດຣເວີ ແລະ GPU ມັກ, ພວກເຮົາຈະສາມາດເ"
"ພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບໄດ້ຢ່າງມະຫາສານ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:37
msgid ""
"Nearly every API command in OpenGL requires a certain amount of validation "
"to make sure the GPU is in the correct state. Even seemingly simple commands "
"can lead to a flurry of behind-the-scenes housekeeping. Therefore, the goal "
"is to reduce these instructions to a bare minimum and group together similar "
"objects as much as possible so they can be rendered together, or with the "
"minimum number of these expensive state changes."
msgstr ""
"ເກືອບທຸກຄຳສັ່ງ API ໃນ OpenGL ຕ້ອງການການກວດສອບ (Validation) ຈຳນວນໜຶ່ງເພື່ອໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າ GPU "
"ຢູ່ໃນສະຖານະທີ່ຖືກຕ້ອງ. ແມ່ນແຕ່ຄຳສັ່ງທີ່ເບິ່ງຄືວ່າງ່າຍກໍສາມາດນຳໄປສູ່ການຈັດການເບື້ອງຫຼັງທີ່ຫຼາກຫຼາຍ. ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ເ"
"ປົ້າໝາຍຄືການຫຼຸດຄຳສັ່ງເຫຼົ່ານີ້ໃຫ້ເຫຼືອໜ້ອຍທີ່ສຸດ ແລະ ຈັດກຸ່ມວັດຖຸທີ່ຄ້າຍຄືກັນເຂົ້າກັນໃຫ້ໄດ້ຫຼາຍທີ່ສຸດ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ພວກມັນຖືກ"
"ເຣັນເດີໄປພ້ອມກັນ, ຫຼື ໃຫ້ມີການປ່ຽນສະຖານະທີ່ສິ້ນເປືອງເຫຼົ່ານີ້ໜ້ອຍທີ່ສຸດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:45
msgid "2D batching"
msgstr "2D batching"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:47
msgid ""
"In 2D, the costs of treating each item individually can be prohibitively "
"high - there can easily be thousands of them on the screen. This is why 2D "
"*batching* is used. Multiple similar items are grouped together and rendered "
"in a batch, via a single draw call, rather than making a separate draw call "
"for each item. In addition, this means state changes, material and texture "
"changes can be kept to a minimum."
msgstr ""
"ໃນ 2D, ຕົ້ນທຶນຂອງການຈັດການແຕ່ລະລາຍການແຍກກັນອາດຈະສູງເກີນໄປ - ເພາະອາດມີວັດຖຸເປັນພັນໆ ໂຕໃນໜ້າ"
"ຈໍ. ນີ້ຄືເຫດຜົນທີ່ຕ້ອງໃຊ້ 2D *batching*. ວັດຖຸທີ່ຄ້າຍຄືກັນຫຼາຍໂຕຈະຖືກຈັດກຸ່ມເຂົ້າກັນ ແລະ ເຣັນເດີໃນຊຸດດຽ"
"ວ (Batch), ຜ່ານການຮຽກໃຊ້ການແຕ້ມ (Draw call) ພຽງຄັ້ງດຽວ, ແທນທີ່ຈະເຮັດແຍກກັນແຕ່ລະໂຕ. ນອກຈ"
"າກນັ້ນ, ສິ່ງນີ້ຍັງໝາຍຄວາມວ່າການປ່ຽນສະຖານະ, ການປ່ຽນວັດສະດຸ ແລະ ພື້ນຜິວ (Texture) ຈະຖືກຫຼຸດໃຫ້ເຫຼືອໜ້"
"ອຍທີ່ສຸດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:55
msgid "3D batching"
msgstr "3D batching"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:57
msgid ""
"In 3D, we still aim to minimize draw calls and state changes. However, it "
"can be more difficult to batch together several objects into a single draw "
"call. 3D meshes tend to comprise hundreds or thousands of triangles, and "
"combining large meshes in real-time is prohibitively expensive. The costs of "
"joining them quickly exceeds any benefits as the number of triangles grows "
"per mesh. A much better alternative is to **join meshes ahead of time** "
"(static meshes in relation to each other). This can be done by artists, or "
"programmatically within Godot using an add-on."
msgstr ""
"ໃນ 3D, ພວກເຮົາຍັງຄົງຕັ້ງເປົ້າໝາຍທີ່ຈະຫຼຸດ draw calls ແລະ ການປ່ຽນສະຖານະໃຫ້ໜ້ອຍທີ່ສຸດ. ເຖິງຢ່າງໃດກໍ"
"ຕາມ, ມັນອາດຈະຍາກກວ່າໃນການລວມວັດຖຸຫຼາຍໆ ໂຕເຂົ້າໃນ draw call ດຽວ. Mesh 3D ມັກຈະປະກອບດ້ວຍ"
"ສາມຫຼ່ຽມເປັນຮ້ອຍ ຫຼື ເປັນພັນ, ແລະ ການລວມ Mesh ຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ແບບເວລາຈິງແມ່ນສິ້ນເປືອງເກີນໄປ. ຕົ້ນທຶນໃນ"
"ການລວມພວກມັນຈະເກີນຜົນປະໂຫຍດຢ່າງວ່ອງໄວເມື່ອຈຳນວນສາມຫຼ່ຽມຕໍ່ Mesh ເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນ. ທາງເລືອກທີ່ດີກວ່າຫຼາຍແມ່"
"ນການ **ລວມ Mesh ໄວ້ລ່ວງໜ້າ** (Static meshes ທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັນ). ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ໂດຍສິລະປິນ, "
"ຫຼື ຜ່ານໂປຣແກຣມໃນ Godot ໂດຍໃຊ້ add-on."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:65
msgid ""
"There is also a cost to batching together objects in 3D. Several objects "
"rendered as one cannot be individually culled. An entire city that is off-"
"screen will still be rendered if it is joined to a single blade of grass "
"that is on screen. Thus, you should always take objects' locations and "
"culling into account when attempting to batch 3D objects together. Despite "
"this, the benefits of joining static objects often outweigh other "
"considerations, especially for large numbers of distant or low-poly objects."
msgstr ""
"ການລວມວັດຖຸເຂົ້າກັນໃນ 3D ກໍມີຕົ້ນທຶນເຊັ່ນກັນ. ວັດຖຸຫຼາຍໆ ໂຕທີ່ຖືກເຣັນເດີເປັນອັນດຽວກັນຈະບໍ່ສາມາດຖືກຄັດອອກ "
"(Culling) ແຍກກັນໄດ້. ເມືອງທັງເມືອງທີ່ຢູ່ນອກໜ້າຈໍຈະຍັງຄົງຖືກເຣັນເດີຢູ່ ຖ້າມັນຖືກລວມເຂົ້າກັບຫຍ້າພຽງໃບດຽວ"
"ທີ່ປະກົດຢູ່ໃນໜ້າຈໍ. ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ທ່ານຄວນຄຳນຶງເຖິງຕຳແໜ່ງຂອງວັດຖຸ ແລະ ການຄັດອອກ (Culling) ສະເໝີເມື່ອພະຍ"
"າຍາມລວມວັດຖຸ 3D ເຂົ້າກັນ. ເຖິງຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ຜົນປະໂຫຍດຂອງການລວມວັດຖຸຄົງທີ່ (Static objects) ມັ"
"ກຈະມີຫຼາຍກວ່າຂໍ້ເສຍ, ໂດຍສະເພາະສຳລັບວັດຖຸຈຳນວນຫຼາຍທີ່ຢູ່ໄກ ຫຼື ມີຄວາມລະອຽດຕ່ຳ (Low-poly)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:73
msgid ""
"For more information on 3D specific optimizations, "
"see :ref:`doc_optimizing_3d_performance`."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບການປັບແຕ່ງສະເພາະ 3D, ເບິ່ງ "
":ref:`doc_optimizing_3d_performance`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:77
msgid "Reuse shaders and materials"
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ Shaders ແລະ ວັດສະດຸ (Materials) ຊ້ຳ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:79
msgid ""
"The Godot renderer is a little different to what is out there. It's designed "
"to minimize GPU state changes as much as possible. :ref:`StandardMaterial3D "
"<class_StandardMaterial3D>` does a good job at reusing materials that need "
"similar shaders. If custom shaders are used, make sure to reuse them as much "
"as possible. Godot's priorities are:"
msgstr ""
"ຕົວເຣັນເດີຂອງ Godot ແຕກຕ່າງຈາກອັນອື່ນເລັກນ້ອຍ. ມັນຖືກອອກແບບມາເພື່ອຫຼຸດການປ່ຽນສະຖານະຂອງ GPU ໃຫ້"
"ໜ້ອຍທີ່ສຸດເທົ່າທີ່ຈະເປັນໄປໄດ້. :ref:`StandardMaterial3D <class_StandardMaterial3D>` ເຮັດ"
"ວຽກໄດ້ດີໃນການໃຊ້ວັດສະດຸຊ້ຳທີ່ຕ້ອງການ shader ທີ່ຄ້າຍຄືກັນ. ຖ້າໃຊ້ shader ທີ່ຂຽນເອງ, ໃຫ້ໝັ້ນໃຈວ່າໄດ້ໃຊ້"
"ພວກມັນຊ້ຳໃຫ້ໄດ້ຫຼາຍທີ່ສຸດ. ລຳດັບຄວາມສຳຄັນຂອງ Godot ແມ່ນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:85
msgid ""
"**Reusing Materials:** The fewer different materials in the scene, the "
"faster the rendering will be. If a scene has a huge amount of objects (in "
"the hundreds or thousands), try reusing the materials. In the worst case, "
"use atlases to decrease the amount of texture changes."
msgstr ""
"**ການໃຊ້ວັດສະດຸຊ້ຳ:** ຍິ່ງມີວັດສະດຸທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນໜ້ອຍເທົ່າໃດໃນສາກ, ການເຣັນເດີກໍຈະຍິ່ງໄວຂຶ້ນ. ຖ້າສາກມີວັດ"
"ຖຸຈຳນວນມະຫາສານ (ເປັນຮ້ອຍ ຫຼື ເປັນພັນ), ໃຫ້ລອງໃຊ້ວັດສະດຸຊ້ຳກັນ. ໃນກໍລະນີທີ່ແຍກກັນບໍ່ໄດ້ແທ້ໆ, ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ "
"Atlases ເພື່ອຫຼຸດຈຳນວນການປ່ຽນ texture."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:89
msgid ""
"**Reusing Shaders:** If materials can't be reused, at least try to reuse "
"shaders. Note: shaders are automatically reused between StandardMaterial3Ds "
"that share the same configuration (features that are enabled or disabled "
"with a check box) even if they have different parameters."
msgstr ""
"**ການໃຊ້ Shader ຊ້ຳ:** ຖ້າບໍ່ສາມາດໃຊ້ວັດສະດຸຊ້ຳໄດ້, ຢ່າງໜ້ອຍໃຫ້ພະຍາຍາມໃຊ້ shader ຊ້ຳ. ໝາຍເຫ"
"ດ: shader ຈະຖືກນຳມາໃຊ້ຊ້ຳໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດລະຫວ່າງ StandardMaterial3D ທີ່ໃຊ້ການຕັ້ງຄ່າດຽວກັນ (ຟີ"
"ເຈີທີ່ເປີດ ຫຼື ປິດດ້ວຍການຕິກເຄື່ອງໝາຍ) ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າພວກມັນຈະມີພາຣາມີເຕີທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນກໍຕາມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:95
msgid ""
"If a scene has, for example, 20,000 objects with 20,000 different materials "
"each, rendering will be slow. If the same scene has 20,000 objects, but only "
"uses 100 materials, rendering will be much faster."
msgstr ""
"ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ ຖ້າສາກມີວັດຖຸ 20,000 ໂຕ ໂດຍແຕ່ລະໂຕມີວັດສະດຸທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນ 20,000 ຢ່າງ, ການເຣັນເດີຈະຊ້"
"າ. ແຕ່ຖ້າສາກດຽວກັນນັ້ນມີ 20,000 ວັດຖຸ ແຕ່ໃຊ້ວັດສະດຸພຽງ 100 ຢ່າງ, ການເຣັນເດີຈະໄວຂຶ້ນຫຼາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:100
msgid "Pixel cost versus vertex cost"
msgstr "ຕົ້ນທຶນຂອງພິກເຊວ (Pixel) ທຽບກັບ ຕົ້ນທຶນຂອງເວີເທັກ (Vertex)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:102
msgid ""
"You may have heard that the lower the number of polygons in a model, the "
"faster it will be rendered. This is *really* relative and depends on many "
"factors."
msgstr ""
"ທ່ານອາດຈະເຄີຍໄດ້ຍິນວ່າ ຍິ່ງຈຳນວນໂພລີກອນ (Polygons) ໃນໂມເດວໜ້ອຍເທົ່າໃດ, ມັນກໍຈະຍິ່ງເຣັນເດີໄດ້ໄວຂຶ້"
"ນເທົ່ານັ້ນ. ສິ່ງນີ້ເປັນເລື່ອງທີ່ *ຂຶ້ນຢູ່ກັບ* ຫຼາຍປັດໄຈ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:105
msgid ""
"On a modern PC and console, vertex cost is low. GPUs originally only "
"rendered triangles. This meant that every frame:"
msgstr ""
"ໃນ PC ແລະ ຄອນໂຊນສະໄໝໃໝ່, ຕົ້ນທຶນຂອງ vertex ແມ່ນຕ່ຳ. ໃນເບື້ອງຕົ້ນ GPU ຈະເຣັນເດີພຽງແຕ່ສາມຫຼ່ຽມ"
"ເທົ່ານັ້ນ. ສິ່ງນີ້ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າທຸກໆ ເຟຣມ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:108
msgid "All vertices had to be transformed by the CPU (including clipping)."
msgstr ""
"Vertex ທັງໝົດຕ້ອງຖືກແປງຄ່າ (Transform) ໂດຍ CPU (ລວມທັງການຕັດສ່ວນເກີນ ຫຼື Clipping)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:109
msgid "All vertices had to be sent to the GPU memory from the main RAM."
msgstr "Vertex ທັງໝົດຕ້ອງຖືກສົ່ງໄປຍັງໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳຂອງ GPU ຈາກ RAM ຫຼັກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:111
msgid ""
"Nowadays, all this is handled inside the GPU, greatly increasing "
"performance. 3D artists usually have the wrong feeling about polycount "
"performance because 3D modeling software (such as Blender, 3ds Max, etc.) "
"need to keep geometry in CPU memory for it to be edited, reducing actual "
"performance. Game engines rely on the GPU more, so they can render many "
"triangles much more efficiently."
msgstr ""
"ໃນປັດຈຸບັນ, ທຸກຢ່າງນີ້ຖືກຈັດການພາຍໃນ GPU, ເຊິ່ງຊ່ວຍເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບໄດ້ຢ່າງມະຫາສານ. ສິລະປິນ 3D ມັກຈະ"
"ມີຄວາມຮູ້ສຶກທີ່ຜິດກ່ຽວກັບປະສິດທິພາບຂອງຈຳນວນໂພລີກອນ (Polycount) ເພາະວ່າຊອບແວອອກແບບ 3D (ເຊັ່ນ "
"Blender, 3ds Max ແລະ ອື່ນໆ) ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງເກັບຂໍ້ມູນຮູບຮ່າງໄວ້ໃນໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳຂອງ CPU ເພື່ອໃຫ້ສາມາດແ"
"ກ້ໄຂໄດ້, ເຊິ່ງເຮັດໃຫ້ປະສິດທິພາບຕົວຈິງຫຼຸດລົງ. ແຕ່ເກມເອນຈິນຈະເພິ່ງພາ GPU ຫຼາຍກວ່າ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນພວກມັນຈຶ່ງສາມ"
"າດເຣັນເດີສາມຫຼ່ຽມຈຳນວນຫຼາຍໄດ້ຢ່າງມີປະສິດທິພາບກວ່າຫຼາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:117
msgid ""
"On mobile devices, the story is different. PC and console GPUs are brute-"
"force monsters that can pull as much electricity as they need from the power "
"grid. Mobile GPUs are limited to a tiny battery, so they need to be a lot "
"more power efficient."
msgstr ""
"ໃນອຸປະກອນມືຖື, ເລື່ອງລາວຈະແຕກຕ່າງອອກໄປ. GPU ຂອງ PC ແລະ ຄອນໂຊນແມ່ນເໝືອນກັບສັດຮ້າຍທີ່ມີພະລັງມະ"
"ຫາສານ ເຊິ່ງສາມາດດຶງໄຟຟ້າຈາກແຫຼ່ງຈ່າຍໄດ້ຕາມທີ່ຕ້ອງການ. ແຕ່ GPU ຂອງມືຖືຖືກຈຳກັດດ້ວຍແບັດເຕີຣີນ້ອຍໆ, ດັ່"
"ງນັ້ນພວກມັນຈຶ່ງຕ້ອງປະຢັດພະລັງງານຫຼາຍກວ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:122
msgid ""
"To be more efficient, mobile GPUs attempt to avoid *overdraw*. Overdraw "
"occurs when the same pixel on the screen is being rendered more than once. "
"Imagine a town with several buildings. GPUs don't know what is visible and "
"what is hidden until they draw it. For example, a house might be drawn and "
"then another house in front of it (which means rendering happened twice for "
"the same pixel). PC GPUs normally don't care much about this and just throw "
"more pixel processors to the hardware to increase performance (which also "
"increases power consumption)."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອໃຫ້ມີປະສິດທິພາບຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນ, GPU ມືຖືຈະພະຍາຍາມຫຼີກລ່ຽງ *overdraw*. Overdraw ເກີດຂຶ້ນເມື່ອພິກເຊວດ"
"ຽວກັນໃນໜ້າຈໍຖືກເຣັນເດີຫຼາຍກວ່າໜຶ່ງຄັ້ງ. ຈິນຕະນາການເຖິງເມືອງທີ່ມີຕຶກຫຼາຍໆ ຫຼັງ. GPU ຈະບໍ່ຮູ້ວ່າອັນໃດເຫັນ ແລ"
"ະ ອັນໃດຖືກບັງ ຈົນກວ່າພວກມັນຈະແຕ້ມມັນອອກມາ. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ, ເຮືອນຫຼັງໜຶ່ງອາດຈະຖືກແຕ້ມ ແລ້ວມີເຮືອນອີກຫຼັງໜຶ່"
"ງມາແຕ້ມທັບທາງໜ້າ (ເຊິ່ງໝາຍຄວາມວ່າການເຣັນເດີເກີດຂຶ້ນສອງຄັ້ງສຳລັບພິກເຊວດຽວກັນ). ປົກກະຕິ GPU ຂອງ "
"PC ຈະບໍ່ຄ່ອຍສົນໃຈເລື່ອງນີ້ ແລະ ຈະໃຊ້ຕົວປະມວນຜົນພິກເຊວເພີ່ມເຂົ້າໄປໃນຮາດແວເພື່ອເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບ (ເຊິ່ງກໍເ"
"ພີ່ມການໃຊ້ພະລັງງານນຳ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:130
msgid ""
"Using more power is not an option on mobile so mobile devices use a "
"technique called *tile-based rendering* which divides the screen into a "
"grid. Each cell keeps the list of triangles drawn to it and sorts them by "
"depth to minimize *overdraw*. This technique improves performance and "
"reduces power consumption, but takes a toll on vertex performance. As a "
"result, fewer vertices and triangles can be processed for drawing."
msgstr ""
"ການໃຊ້ພະລັງງານຫຼາຍບໍ່ແມ່ນທາງເລືອກໃນມືຖື ດັ່ງນັ້ນອຸປະກອນມືຖືຈຶ່ງໃຊ້ເຕັກນິກທີ່ເອີ້ນວ່າ *tile-based "
"rendering* ເຊິ່ງແບ່ງໜ້າຈໍອອກເປັນຕາຕະລາງ (Grid). ແຕ່ລະຫ້ອງ (Cell) ຈະເກັບລາຍການຂອງສາມຫຼ່ຽມ"
"ທີ່ຖືກແຕ້ມໃສ່ນັ້ນ ແລະ ຈັດລຽງຕາມຄວາມເລິກເພື່ອຫຼຸດ *overdraw*. ເຕັກນິກນີ້ຊ່ວຍເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບ ແລະ ຫຼຸດກາ"
"ນໃຊ້ພະລັງງານ, ແຕ່ຕ້ອງແລກດ້ວຍປະສິດທິພາບຂອງ vertex. ສົ່ງຜົນໃຫ້ສາມາດປະມວນຜົນ vertex ແລະ ສາມຫຼ່"
"ຽມສຳລັບການແຕ້ມໄດ້ໜ້ອຍລົງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:137
msgid ""
"Additionally, tile-based rendering struggles when there are small objects "
"with a lot of geometry within a small portion of the screen. This forces "
"mobile GPUs to put a lot of strain on a single screen tile, which "
"considerably decreases performance as all the other cells must wait for it "
"to complete before displaying the frame."
msgstr ""
"ນອກຈາກນີ້, tile-based rendering ຍັງມີບັນຫາເມື່ອມີວັດຖຸນ້ອຍໆ ທີ່ມີລາຍລະອຽດຮູບຮ່າງຫຼາຍໆ ຢູ່ໃນພາກສ່ວ"
"ນນ້ອຍໆ ຂອງໜ້າຈໍ. ສິ່ງນີ້ບັງຄັບໃຫ້ GPU ມືຖືຕ້ອງເຮັດວຽກໜັກຫຼາຍໃນ tile ດຽວຂອງໜ້າຈໍ, ເຊິ່ງເຮັດໃຫ້ປະສິດທິພ"
"າບຫຼຸດລົງຢ່າງຫຼວງຫຼາຍ ເພາະຫ້ອງອື່ນໆ ທັງໝົດຕ້ອງລໍຖ້າມັນເຮັດວຽກໃຫ້ສຳເລັດກ່ອນຈະສະແດງເຟຣມໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:143
msgid ""
"To summarize, don't worry about vertex count on mobile, but **avoid "
"concentration of vertices in small parts of the screen**. If a character, "
"NPC, vehicle, etc. is far away (which means it looks tiny), use a smaller "
"level of detail (LOD) model. Even on desktop GPUs, it's preferable to avoid "
"having triangles smaller than the size of a pixel on screen."
msgstr ""
"ສະຫຼຸບແລ້ວ, ບໍ່ຕ້ອງກັງວົນກ່ຽວກັບຈຳນວນ vertex ໃນມືຖືເກີນໄປ, ແຕ່ **ໃຫ້ຫຼີກລ່ຽງການລວມຕົວຂອງ vertex "
"ໃນພື້ນທີ່ນ້ອຍໆ ຂອງໜ້າຈໍ**. ຖ້າຕົວລະຄອນ, NPC, ພາຫະນະ ແລະ ອື່ນໆ ຢູ່ໄກ (ເຊິ່ງໝາຍຄວາມວ່າມັນເບິ່ງຄືວ່ານ້"
"ອຍ), ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ໂມເດວທີ່ມີລະດັບຄວາມລະອຽດຕ່ຳກວ່າ (LOD). ແມ່ນແຕ່ໃນ GPU ຂອງຄອມພິວເຕີ, ກໍຄວນຫຼີກລ່ຽງກາ"
"ນມີສາມຫຼ່ຽມທີ່ນ້ອຍກວ່າຂະໜາດຂອງພິກເຊວໃນໜ້າຈໍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:149
msgid "Pay attention to the additional vertex processing required when using:"
msgstr "ໃຫ້ໃສ່ໃຈກັບການປະມວນຜົນ vertex ເພີ່ມເຕີມທີ່ຈຳເປັນເມື່ອໃຊ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:151
msgid "Skinning (skeletal animation)"
msgstr "Skinning (ແອນິເມຊັນໂຄງກະດູກ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:152
msgid "Morphs (shape keys)"
msgstr "Morphs (ເຊບຄີ - shape keys)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:153
msgid "Vertex-lit objects (common on mobile)"
msgstr "ວັດຖຸທີ່ໃຊ້ແສງລະດັບ vertex (ພົບເລື້ອຍໃນມືຖື)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:156
msgid "Pixel/fragment shaders and fill rate"
msgstr "ພິກເຊວ (Pixel)/ແຟຣກເມນ (Fragment) ເຊດເດີ ແລະ ອັດຕາການເຕີມ (Fill rate)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:158
msgid ""
"In contrast to vertex processing, the costs of fragment (per-pixel) shading "
"have increased dramatically over the years. Screen resolutions have "
"increased: the area of a 4K screen is 8,294,400 pixels, versus 307,200 for "
"an old 640×480 VGA screen. That is 27 times the area! Also, the complexity "
"of fragment shaders has exploded. Physically-based rendering requires "
"complex calculations for each fragment."
msgstr ""
"ໃນທາງກົງກັນຂ້າມກັບການປະມວນຜົນ vertex, ຕົ້ນທຶນຂອງ fragment (ຕໍ່ພິກເຊວ) shading ໄດ້ເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນຢ່າງ"
"ມະຫາສານໃນຊ່ວງຫຼາຍປີທີ່ຜ່ານມາ. ຄວາມລະອຽດຂອງໜ້າຈໍເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນ: ພື້ນທີ່ຂອງໜ້າຈໍ 4K ແມ່ນ 8,294,400 ພິກເຊ"
"ວ, ທຽບກັບ 307,200 ພິກເຊວສຳລັບໜ້າຈໍ VGA 640×480 ແບບເກົ່າ. ນັ້ນແມ່ນພື້ນທີ່ໃຫຍ່ກວ່າເຖິງ 27 ເທົ່າ! ນ"
"ອກຈາກນີ້, ຄວາມຊັບຊ້ອນຂອງ fragment shader ກໍເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນຢ່າງຫຼວງຫຼາຍ. ການເຣັນເດີຕາມຫຼັກຟີຊິກ "
"(Physically-based rendering) ຕ້ອງການການຄຳນວນທີ່ຊັບຊ້ອນສຳລັບແຕ່ລະ fragment."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:165
msgid ""
"You can test whether a project is fill rate-limited quite easily. Turn off V-"
"Sync to prevent capping the frames per second, then compare the frames per "
"second when running with a large window, to running with a very small "
"window. You may also benefit from similarly reducing your shadow map size if "
"using shadows. Usually, you will find the FPS increases quite a bit using a "
"small window, which indicates you are to some extent fill rate-limited. On "
"the other hand, if there is little to no increase in FPS, then your "
"bottleneck lies elsewhere."
msgstr ""
"ທ່ານສາມາດທົດສອບວ່າໂປຣເຈັກຖືກຈຳກັດດ້ວຍ fill rate ຫຼື ບໍ່ໄດ້ຢ່າງງ່າຍດາຍ. ໃຫ້ປິດ V-Sync ເພື່ອບໍ່ໃຫ້ຈຳ"
"ກັດ FPS, ຈາກນັ້ນປຽບທຽບ FPS ເມື່ອເປີດໜ້າຕ່າງໃຫຍ່ ກັບຕອນເປີດໜ້າຕ່າງນ້ອຍໆ. ທ່ານອາດຈະໄດ້ຮັບຜົນປະໂຫຍ"
"ດໃນການຫຼຸດຂະໜາດ shadow map ຖ້າໃຊ້ເງົາ. ໂດຍປົກກະຕິ, ທ່ານຈະເຫັນວ່າ FPS ເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນເລັກນ້ອຍເມື່ອໃຊ້ໜ້າ"
"ຕ່າງນ້ອຍ, ເຊິ່ງສະແດງໃຫ້ເຫັນວ່າທ່ານຖືກຈຳກັດດ້ວຍ fill rate ໃນລະດັບໃດໜຶ່ງ. ໃນທາງກົງກັນຂ້າມ, ຖ້າ "
"FPS ແທບບໍ່ເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນເລີຍ, ສະແດງວ່າຈຸດຄໍຂວດຂອງທ່ານຢູ່ບ່ອນອື່ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:174
msgid ""
"You can increase performance in a fill rate-limited project by reducing the "
"amount of work the GPU has to do. You can do this by simplifying the shader "
"(perhaps turn off expensive options if you are using "
"a :ref:`StandardMaterial3D <class_StandardMaterial3D>`), or reducing the "
"number and size of textures used. Also, when using shaded particles, "
"consider forcing vertex shading in their material to decrease the shading "
"cost."
msgstr ""
"ທ່ານສາມາດເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບໃນໂປຣເຈັກທີ່ຖືກຈຳກັດດ້ວຍ fill rate ໄດ້ໂດຍການຫຼຸດປະລິມານວຽກທີ່ GPU ຕ້ອງເ"
"ຮັດ. ທ່ານສາມາດເຮັດສິ່ງນີ້ໄດ້ໂດຍການເຮັດໃຫ້ shader ລຽບງ່າຍຂຶ້ນ (ບາງທີອາດປິດຕົວເລືອກທີ່ສິ້ນເປືອງຖ້າທ່ານໃ"
"ຊ້ :ref:`StandardMaterial3D <class_StandardMaterial3D>`), ຫຼື ຫຼຸດຈຳນວນ ແລະ ຂະໜາດຂ"
"ອງ texture ທີ່ໃຊ້. ນອກຈາກນີ້, ເມື່ອໃຊ້ particles ທີ່ມີແສງເງົາ, ໃຫ້ພິຈາລະນາບັງຄັບໃຊ້ vertex "
"shading ໃນວັດສະດຸຂອງພວກມັນເພື່ອຫຼຸດຕົ້ນທຶນ shading."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:183
msgid ""
"On supported hardware, :ref:`doc_variable_rate_shading` can be used to "
"reduce shading processing costs without impacting the sharpness of edges on "
"the final image."
msgstr ""
"ໃນຮາດແວທີ່ຮອງຮັບ, :ref:`doc_variable_rate_shading` ສາມາດໃຊ້ເພື່ອຫຼຸດຕົ້ນທຶນການປະມວນຜົນ "
"shading ໂດຍບໍ່ກະທົບຕໍ່ຄວາມຄົມຊັດຂອງຂອບໃນຮູບພາບສຸດທ້າຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:187
msgid ""
"**When targeting mobile devices, consider using the simplest possible "
"shaders you can reasonably afford to use.**"
msgstr ""
"**ເມື່ອເນັ້ນໃສ່ອຸປະກອນມືຖື, ໃຫ້ພິຈາລະນາໃຊ້ shader ທີ່ລຽບງ່າຍທີ່ສຸດເທົ່າທີ່ທ່ານຈະສາມາດໃຊ້ໄດ້.**"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:191
msgid "Reading textures"
msgstr "ການອ່ານພື້ນຜິວ (Textures)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:193
msgid ""
"The other factor in fragment shaders is the cost of reading textures. "
"Reading textures is an expensive operation, especially when reading from "
"several textures in a single fragment shader. Also, consider that filtering "
"may slow it down further (trilinear filtering between mipmaps, and "
"averaging). Reading textures is also expensive in terms of power usage, "
"which is a big issue on mobiles."
msgstr ""
"ອີກປັດໄຈໜຶ່ງໃນ fragment shader ແມ່ນຕົ້ນທຶນຂອງການອ່ານ texture. ການອ່ານ texture ແມ່ນການເຮັດ"
"ວຽກທີ່ສິ້ນເປືອງ, ໂດຍສະເພາະເມື່ອອ່ານຈາກຫຼາຍໆ texture ໃນ fragment shader ດຽວ. ນອກຈາກນີ້, ໃ"
"ຫ້ຄຳນຶງວ່າການກັ່ນຕອງ (Filtering) ອາດຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ມັນຊ້າລົງຕື່ມ (trilinear filtering ລະຫວ່າງ "
"mipmaps, ແລະ ການຫາຄ່າສະເລ່ຍ). ການອ່ານ texture ຍັງສິ້ນເປືອງໃນແງ່ຂອງການໃຊ້ພະລັງງານ, ເຊິ່ງເປັ"
"ນບັນຫາໃຫຍ່ໃນມືຖື."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:200
msgid ""
"**If you use third-party shaders or write your own shaders, try to use "
"algorithms that require as few texture reads as possible.**"
msgstr ""
"**ຖ້າທ່ານໃຊ້ shader ຈາກພາຍນອກ ຫຼື ຂຽນ shader ຂອງທ່ານເອງ, ໃຫ້ພະຍາຍາມໃຊ້ algorithm ທີ່ຕ້ອງ"
"ການການອ່ານ texture ໜ້ອຍທີ່ສຸດເທົ່າທີ່ຈະເປັນໄປໄດ້.**"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:204
msgid "Texture compression"
msgstr "ການບີບອັດພື້ນຜິວ (Texture compression)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:206
msgid ""
"By default, Godot compresses textures of 3D models when imported using video "
"RAM (VRAM) compression. Video RAM compression isn't as efficient in size as "
"PNG or JPG when stored, but increases performance enormously when drawing "
"large enough textures."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, Godot ຈະບີບອັດ texture ຂອງໂມເດວ 3D ເມື່ອນຳເຂົ້າ (Import) ໂດຍໃຊ້ການບີບອັດ "
"video RAM (VRAM). ການບີບອັດ Video RAM ອາດຈະບໍ່ມີປະສິດທິພາບໃນດ້ານຂະໜາດເທົ່າກັບ PNG ຫຼື JPG "
"ໃນເວລາຈັດເກັບ, ແຕ່ມັນຊ່ວຍເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບໄດ້ຢ່າງມະຫາສານເມື່ອແຕ້ມ texture ທີ່ມີຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ພໍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:211
msgid ""
"This is because the main goal of texture compression is bandwidth reduction "
"between memory and the GPU."
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ກໍຍ້ອນວ່າເປົ້າໝາຍຫຼັກຂອງການບີບອັດ texture ແມ່ນເພື່ອຫຼຸດຜ່ອນ bandwidth ລະຫວ່າງໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳ ແລະ "
"GPU."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:214
msgid ""
"In 3D, the shapes of objects depend more on the geometry than the texture, "
"so compression is generally not noticeable. In 2D, compression depends more "
"on shapes inside the textures, so the artifacts resulting from 2D "
"compression are more noticeable."
msgstr ""
"ໃນ 3D, ຮູບຮ່າງຂອງວັດຖຸຈະຂຶ້ນຢູ່ກັບຮູບຮ່າງເລຂາຄະນິດຫຼາຍກວ່າ texture, ດັ່ງນັ້ນໂດຍທົ່ວໄປແລ້ວການບີບອັດຈະ"
"ບໍ່ເປັນທີ່ສັງເກດເຫັນ. ແຕ່ໃນ 2D, ການບີບອັດຈະຂຶ້ນຢູ່ກັບຮູບຮ່າງພາຍໃນ texture ຫຼາຍກວ່າ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນຮອຍຕຳນິ "
"(Artifacts) ທີ່ເກີດຈາກການບີບອັດ 2D ຈຶ່ງສັງເກດເຫັນໄດ້ຊັດເຈນກວ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:219
msgid ""
"As a warning, most Android devices do not support texture compression of "
"textures with transparency (only opaque), so keep this in mind."
msgstr ""
"ຂໍ້ຄວນລະວັງ, ອຸປະກອນ Android ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ບໍ່ຮອງຮັບການບີບອັດ texture ທີ່ມີຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ "
"(Transparency) (ຮອງຮັບແຕ່ແບບທຶບແສງ ຫຼື Opaque), ດັ່ງນັ້ນໃຫ້ຈື່ຈຳເລື່ອງນີ້ໄວ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:229
msgid "Post-processing and shadows"
msgstr "ການປະມວນຜົນຫຼັງການເຣັນເດີ (Post-processing) ແລະ ເງົາ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:231
msgid ""
"Post-processing effects and shadows can also be expensive in terms of "
"fragment shading activity. Always test the impact of these on different "
"hardware."
msgstr ""
"ເອັບເຟັກ post-processing ແລະ ເງົາກໍສາມາດສິ້ນເປືອງໃນແງ່ຂອງ fragment shading. ໃຫ້ທົດສອບຜົນ"
"ກະທົບຂອງສິ່ງເຫຼົ່ານີ້ໃນຮາດແວທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນສະເໝີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:234
msgid ""
"**Reducing the size of shadowmaps can increase performance**, both in terms "
"of writing and reading the shadowmaps. On top of that, the best way to "
"improve performance of shadows is to turn shadows off for as many lights and "
"objects as possible. Smaller or distant OmniLights/SpotLights can often have "
"their shadows disabled with only a small visual impact."
msgstr ""
"**ການຫຼຸດຂະໜາດຂອງ shadowmaps ສາມາດເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບໄດ້**, ທັງໃນແງ່ຂອງການຂຽນ ແລະ ການອ່ານ "
"shadowmaps. ນອກຈາກນັ້ນ, ວິທີທີ່ດີທີ່ສຸດໃນການປັບປຸງປະສິດທິພາບຂອງເງົາແມ່ນການປິດການໃຊ້ເງົາສຳລັບດອກໄ"
"ຟ ແລະ ວັດຖຸໃຫ້ໄດ້ຫຼາຍທີ່ສຸດ. OmniLights/SpotLights ທີ່ມີຂະໜາດນ້ອຍ ຫຼື ຢູ່ໄກ ມັກຈະສາມາດປິດເງົາໄດ້ໂ"
"ດຍທີ່ມີຜົນກະທົບຕໍ່ພາບພຽງເລັກນ້ອຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:241
msgid "Transparency and blending"
msgstr "ຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ (Transparency) ແລະ ການປະສົມສີ (Blending)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:243
msgid ""
"Transparent objects present particular problems for rendering efficiency. "
"Opaque objects (especially in 3D) can be essentially rendered in any order "
"and the Z-buffer will ensure that only the front most objects get shaded. "
"Transparent or blended objects are different. In most cases, they cannot "
"rely on the Z-buffer and must be rendered in \"painter's order\" (i.e. from "
"back to front) to look correct."
msgstr ""
"ວັດຖຸໂປ່ງໃສສ້າງບັນຫາສະເພາະໃຫ້ກັບປະສິດທິພາບການເຣັນເດີ. ວັດຖຸທຶບແສງ (ໂດຍສະເພາະໃນ 3D) ສາມາດຖືກເ"
"ຣັນເດີໃນລຳດັບໃດກໍໄດ້ ແລະ Z-buffer ຈະຮັບປະກັນວ່າສະເພາະວັດຖຸທີ່ຢູ່ທາງໜ້າສຸດເທົ່ານັ້ນທີ່ຈະຖືກ shading. "
"ແຕ່ວັດຖຸໂປ່ງໃສ ຫຼື ວັດຖຸທີ່ມີການປະສົມສີນັ້ນຕ່າງອອກໄປ. ໃນຫຼາຍກໍລະນີ, ພວກມັນບໍ່ສາມາດເພິ່ງພາ Z-buffer ໄ"
"ດ້ ແລະ ຕ້ອງຖືກເຣັນເດີຕາມ \"ລຳດັບຂອງນັກແຕ້ມຮູບ\" (ຄື ຈາກຫຼັງມາໜ້າ) ເພື່ອໃຫ້ເບິ່ງຄືຄວາມຈິງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:250
msgid ""
"Transparent objects are also particularly bad for fill rate, because every "
"item has to be drawn even if other transparent objects will be drawn on top "
"later on."
msgstr ""
"ວັດຖຸໂປ່ງໃສຍັງສົ່ງຜົນເສຍຕໍ່ fill rate ເປັນພິເສດ, ເພາະວ່າທຸກໆ ລາຍການຕ້ອງຖືກແຕ້ມ ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຈະມີວັດຖຸ"
"ໂປ່ງໃສອື່ນໆ ມາແຕ້ມທັບທາງໜ້າໃນພາຍຫຼັງກໍຕາມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:254
msgid ""
"Opaque objects don't have to do this. They can usually take advantage of the "
"Z-buffer by writing to the Z-buffer only first, then only performing the "
"fragment shader on the \"winning\" fragment, the object that is at the front "
"at a particular pixel."
msgstr ""
"ວັດຖຸທຶບແສງບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງເຮັດແນວນັ້ນ. ພວກມັນມັກຈະໃຊ້ປະໂຫຍດຈາກ Z-buffer ໂດຍການຂຽນລົງໃນ Z-"
"buffer ກ່ອນ, ຈາກນັ້ນຈຶ່ງເຮັດ fragment shader ສະເພາະ fragment ທີ່ \"ຊະນະ\" ເທົ່ານັ້ນ, ເຊິ່ງກໍ"
"ຄືວັດຖຸທີ່ຢູ່ທາງໜ້າສຸດໃນພິກເຊວນັ້ນໆ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:259
msgid ""
"Transparency is particularly expensive where multiple transparent objects "
"overlap. It is usually better to use transparent areas as small as possible "
"to minimize these fill rate requirements, especially on mobile, where fill "
"rate is very expensive. Indeed, in many situations, rendering more complex "
"opaque geometry can end up being faster than using transparency to \"cheat\"."
msgstr ""
"ຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສຈະສິ້ນເປືອງເປັນພິເສດເມື່ອມີວັດຖຸໂປ່ງໃສຫຼາຍໆ ໂຕຊ້ອນທັບກັນ. ມັນມັກຈະດີກວ່າທີ່ຈະໃຊ້ພື້ນທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສໃຫ້"
"ມີຂະໜາດນ້ອຍທີ່ສຸດເທົ່າທີ່ຈະເປັນໄປໄດ້ເພື່ອຫຼຸດຄວາມຕ້ອງການ fill rate ເຫຼົ່ານີ້, ໂດຍສະເພາະໃນມືຖືທີ່ fill "
"rate ມີຄ່າສູງຫຼາຍ. ໃນຄວາມເປັນຈິງແລ້ວ, ໃນຫຼາຍສະຖານະການ, ການເຣັນເດີຮູບຮ່າງທຶບແສງທີ່ຊັບຊ້ອນກວ່າ ອາ"
"ດຈະຈົບລົງດ້ວຍຄວາມໄວທີ່ໄວກວ່າການໃຊ້ຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສເພື່ອ \"ຫຼອກຕາ\"."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:266
msgid "Multi-platform advice"
msgstr "ຄຳແນະນຳສຳລັບຫຼາຍແພລັດຟອມ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:268
msgid ""
"If you are aiming to release on multiple platforms, test *early* and test "
"*often* on all your platforms, especially mobile. Developing a game on "
"desktop but attempting to port it to mobile at the last minute is a recipe "
"for disaster."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າທ່ານຕັ້ງເປົ້າໝາຍທີ່ຈະປ່ອຍເກມໃນຫຼາຍແພລັດຟອມ, ໃຫ້ທົດສອບ *ແຕ່ຫົວທີ* ແລະ ທົດສອບ *ເລື້ອຍໆ* ໃນທຸກແພລັ"
"ດຟອມຂອງທ່ານ, ໂດຍສະເພາະມືຖື. ການພັດທະນາເກມໃນຄອມພິວເຕີ ແລ້ວພະຍາຍາມປ່ຽນໄປລົງມືຖືໃນນາທີສຸດທ້າຍແ"
"ມ່ນສູດສຳເລັດຂອງຄວາມລົ້ມລະລາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:272
msgid ""
"In general, you should design your game for the lowest common denominator, "
"then add optional enhancements for more powerful platforms. For example, you "
"may want to use the Compatibility rendering method for both desktop and "
"mobile platforms where you target both."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປ, ທ່ານຄວນອອກແບບເກມຂອງທ່ານສຳລັບສະເປັກທີ່ຕ່ຳທີ່ສຸດກ່ອນ, ຈາກນັ້ນຈຶ່ງເພີ່ມສິ່ງເສີມຕ່າງໆ ໃຫ້ກັບແພລັ"
"ດຟອມທີ່ແຮງກວ່າ. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ, ທ່ານອາດຈະຕ້ອງການໃຊ້ວິທີການເຣັນເດີແບບ Compatibility ສຳລັບທັງແພລັດ"
"ຟອມຄອມພິວເຕີ ແລະ ມືຖື ຖ້າທ່ານເນັ້ນໃສ່ທັງສອງຢ່າງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:278
msgid "Mobile/tiled renderers"
msgstr "ມືຖື/ຕົວເຣັນເດີແບບແບ່ງຫ້ອງ (Tiled renderers)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:280
msgid ""
"As described above, GPUs on mobile devices work in dramatically different "
"ways from GPUs on desktop. Most mobile devices use tile renderers. Tile "
"renderers split up the screen into regular-sized tiles that fit into super "
"fast cache memory, which reduces the number of read/write operations to the "
"main memory."
msgstr ""
"ຕາມທີ່ໄດ້ອະທິບາຍໄວ້ຂ້າງເທິງ, GPU ໃນອຸປະກອນມືຖືເຮັດວຽກໃນຮູບແບບທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງຈາກ GPU ໃນຄອມພິວເຕີຢ່າງສິ້"
"ນເຊີງ. ອຸປະກອນມືຖືສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ໃຊ້ tile renderers. Tile renderers ຈະແບ່ງໜ້າຈໍອອກເປັນຫ້ອງ "
"(Tiles) ຂະໜາດມາດຕະຖານທີ່ພໍດີກັບໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳ cache ທີ່ໄວຫຼາຍ, ເຊິ່ງຊ່ວຍຫຼຸດຈຳນວນການອ່ານ/ຂຽນໃນໜ່ວ"
"ຍຄວາມຈຳຫຼັກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/gpu_optimization.rst:285
msgid ""
"There are some downsides though. Tiled rendering can make certain techniques "
"much more complicated and expensive to perform. Tiles that rely on the "
"results of rendering in different tiles or on the results of earlier "
"operations being preserved can be very slow. Be very careful to test the "
"performance of shaders, viewport textures and post processing."
msgstr ""
"ແຕ່ມັນກໍມີຂໍ້ເສຍບາງຢ່າງ. Tiled rendering ສາມາດເຮັດໃຫ້ບາງເຕັກນິກມີຄວາມຊັບຊ້ອນ ແລະ ສິ້ນເປືອງຫຼາຍຂຶ້"
"ນໃນການເຮັດວຽກ. Tile ທີ່ຕ້ອງເພິ່ງພາຜົນລັດຂອງການເຣັນເດີໃນ tile ອື່ນ ຫຼື ເພິ່ງພາຜົນລັດຈາກການເຮັດວຽກ"
"ກ່ອນໜ້ານັ້ນອາດຈະຊ້າຫຼາຍ. ໃຫ້ລະມັດລະວັງເປັນຢ່າງສູງໃນການທົດສອບປະສິດທິພາບຂອງ shader, viewport "
"textures ແລະ post processing."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multimesh.rst:6
msgid "Optimization using MultiMeshes"
msgstr "ການປັບແຕ່ງປະສິດທິພາບໂດຍໃຊ້ MultiMeshes"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multimesh.rst:8
msgid ""
"For large amount of instances (in the thousands), that need to be constantly "
"processed (and certain amount of control needs to be retained), :ref:`using "
"servers directly <doc_using_servers>` is the recommended optimization."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບ instance ຈຳນວນຫຼາຍ (ເປັນພັນໆ), ທີ່ຕ້ອງຖືກປະມວນຜົນຕະຫຼອດເວລາ (ແລະ ຍັງຕ້ອງການການຄວບຄຸມ"
"ບາງຢ່າງ), :ref:`ການໃຊ້ເຊີເວີໂດຍກົງ <doc_using_servers>` ແມ່ນການປັບແຕ່ງທີ່ແນະນຳ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multimesh.rst:12
msgid ""
"When the amount of objects reach the hundreds of thousands or millions, none "
"of these approaches are efficient anymore. Still, depending on the "
"requirements, there is one more optimization possible."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອຈຳນວນວັດຖຸສູງເຖິງຫຼັກແສນ ຫຼື ຫຼັກລ້ານ, ແນວທາງເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຈະບໍ່ມີປະສິດທິພາບອີກຕໍ່ໄປ. ເຖິງຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ຂຶ້ນຢູ່"
"ກັບຄວາມຕ້ອງການ, ຍັງມີການປັບແຕ່ງອີກຢ່າງໜຶ່ງທີ່ເປັນໄປໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multimesh.rst:17
#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:179
msgid "MultiMeshes"
msgstr "MultiMeshes"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multimesh.rst:19
msgid ""
"A :ref:`MultiMesh<class_MultiMesh>` is a single draw primitive that can draw "
"up to millions of objects in one go. It's extremely efficient because it "
"uses the GPU hardware to do this."
msgstr ""
":ref:`MultiMesh<class_MultiMesh>` ແມ່ນ draw primitive ດຽວທີ່ສາມາດແຕ້ມວັດຖຸໄດ້ເຖິງຫຼັກລ້າ"
"ນໂຕໃນຄັ້ງດຽວ. ມັນມີປະສິດທິພາບສູງຫຼາຍເພາະມັນໃຊ້ຮາດແວຂອງ GPU ໃນການເຮັດສິ່ງນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multimesh.rst:22
msgid ""
"The only drawback is that there is no *screen* or *frustum* culling possible "
"for individual instances. This means, that millions of objects will be "
"*always* or *never* drawn, depending on the visibility of the whole "
"MultiMesh. It is possible to provide a custom visibility rect for them, but "
"it will always be *all-or-none* visibility."
msgstr ""
"ຂໍ້ເສຍພຽງຢ່າງດຽວແມ່ນບໍ່ສາມາດເຮັດການຄັດອອກ (Culling) ແບບແຍກແຕ່ລະ instance ໄດ້. ນີ້ໝາຍຄວາມວ່"
"າ, ວັດຖຸຫຼັກລ້ານໂຕຈະຖືກແຕ້ມ *ຕະຫຼອດເວລາ* ຫຼື *ບໍ່ຖືກແຕ້ມເລີຍ*, ຂຶ້ນຢູ່ກັບການເບິ່ງເຫັນຂອງ MultiMesh ທັ"
"ງໝົດ. ທ່ານສາມາດກຳນົດຂອບເຂດການເບິ່ງເຫັນ (Visibility rect) ແບບກຳນົດເອງໃຫ້ພວກມັນໄດ້, ແຕ່ມັນຈ"
"ະເປັນການເບິ່ງເຫັນແບບ *ທັງໝົດ ຫຼື ບໍ່ມີເລີຍ* ສະເໝີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multimesh.rst:27
msgid ""
"If the objects are simple enough (just a couple of vertices), this is "
"generally not much of a problem as most modern GPUs are optimized for this "
"use case. A workaround is to create several MultiMeshes for different areas "
"of the world."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າວັດຖຸນັ້ນລຽບງ່າຍພໍ (ມີພຽງບໍ່ເທົ່າໃດ vertex), ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປແລ້ວສິ່ງນີ້ຈະບໍ່ແມ່ນບັນຫາໃຫຍ່ ເພາະ GPU ສະໄໝໃ"
"ໝ່ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ຖືກປັບແຕ່ງມາສຳລັບກໍລະນີການໃຊ້ງານແບບນີ້ຢູ່ແລ້ວ. ວິທີແກ້ໄຂຄືການສ້າງ MultiMesh ຫຼາຍໆ ອັນສຳລັບ"
"ພື້ນທີ່ຕ່າງໆ ຂອງໂລກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multimesh.rst:31
msgid ""
"It is also possible to execute some logic inside the vertex shader (using "
"the ``INSTANCE_ID`` or ``INSTANCE_CUSTOM`` built-in constants). For an "
"example of animating thousands of objects in a MultiMesh, see "
"the :ref:`Animating thousands of fish <doc_animating_thousands_of_fish>` "
"tutorial. Information to the shader can be provided via textures (there are "
"floating-point :ref:`Image<class_Image>` formats which are ideal for this)."
msgstr ""
"ນອກຈາກນີ້ຍັງສາມາດສັ່ງໃຫ້ເຮັດວຽກບາງຢ່າງພາຍໃນ vertex shader ໄດ້ (ໂດຍໃຊ້ຄ່າຄົງທີ່ພາຍໃນ "
"``INSTANCE_ID`` ຫຼື ``INSTANCE_CUSTOM``). ສຳລັບຕົວຢ່າງການເຮັດແອນິເມຊັນໃຫ້ວັດຖຸເປັນພັນໆ ໂຕໃ"
"ນ MultiMesh, ເບິ່ງບົດຮຽນ :ref:`Animating thousands of fish "
"<doc_animating_thousands_of_fish>`. ຂໍ້ມູນສຳລັບ shader ສາມາດສົ່ງຜ່ານ texture ໄດ້ (ມັນມີ"
"ຮູບແບບ :ref:`Image<class_Image>` ແບບ floating-point ເຊິ່ງເໝາະສົມທີ່ສຸດສຳລັບວຽກນີ້)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multimesh.rst:37
msgid ""
"Another alternative is to use a GDExtension and C++, which should be "
"extremely efficient (it's possible to set the entire state for all objects "
"using linear memory via the :ref:`RenderingServer.multimesh_set_buffer() "
"<class_RenderingServer_method_multimesh_set_buffer>` function). This way, "
"the array can be created with multiple threads, then set in one call, "
"providing high cache efficiency."
msgstr ""
"ອີກທາງເລືອກໜຶ່ງແມ່ນການໃຊ້ GDExtension ແລະ C++, ເຊິ່ງຄວນຈະມີປະສິດທິພາບສູງສຸດ (ສາມາດຕັ້ງຄ່າສະຖາ"
"ນະທັງໝົດຂອງທຸກວັດຖຸໂດຍໃຊ້ໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳແບບເສັ້ນຊື່ຜ່ານຟັງຊັນ "
":ref:`RenderingServer.multimesh_set_buffer() "
"<class_RenderingServer_method_multimesh_set_buffer>`). ດ້ວຍວິທີນີ້, array ສາມາດຖືກສ້"
"າງຂຶ້ນດ້ວຍຫຼາຍເທຣດ, ຈາກນັ້ນຕັ້ງຄ່າໃນການຮຽກໃຊ້ຄັ້ງດຽວ, ເຊິ່ງຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ cache ເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ຢ່າງມີປະສິດທິພາບ"
"ສູງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multimesh.rst:43
msgid ""
"Finally, it's not required to have all MultiMesh instances visible. The "
"amount of visible ones can be controlled with "
"the :ref:`MultiMesh.visible_instance_count "
"<class_MultiMesh_property_visible_instance_count>` property. The typical "
"workflow is to allocate the maximum amount of instances that will be used, "
"then change the amount visible depending on how many are currently needed."
msgstr ""
"ສຸດທ້າຍ, ບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງໃຫ້ MultiMesh instance ທັງໝົດປະກົດໃຫ້ເຫັນ. ຈຳນວນທີ່ເຫັນໄດ້ສາມາດຄວບຄຸມໄດ້ດ້"
"ວຍຄຸນສົມບັດ :ref:`MultiMesh.visible_instance_count "
"<class_MultiMesh_property_visible_instance_count>`. ຂະບວນການເຮັດວຽກປົກກະຕິຄືການຈອ"
"ງຈຳນວນ instance ສູງສຸດທີ່ຈະໃຊ້, ຈາກນັ້ນປ່ຽນຈຳນວນທີ່ເບິ່ງເຫັນຕາມຄວາມຕ້ອງການໃນຂະນະນັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multimesh.rst:49
msgid "Multimesh example"
msgstr "ຕົວຢ່າງ MultiMesh"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multimesh.rst:51
msgid ""
"Here is an example of using a MultiMesh from code. Languages other than "
"GDScript may be more efficient for millions of objects, but for a few "
"thousands, GDScript should be fine."
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ແມ່ນຕົວຢ່າງການໃຊ້ MultiMesh ຈາກໂຄດ. ພາສາອື່ນໆ ທີ່ບໍ່ແມ່ນ GDScript ອາດຈະມີປະສິດທິພາບກວ່າສຳລັບ"
"ວັດຖຸຫຼັກລ້ານໂຕ, ແຕ່ສຳລັບວັດຖຸຫຼັກພັນໂຕ, GDScript ກໍຖືວ່າໃຊ້ໄດ້ດີແລ້ວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:4
msgid "Reducing stutter from shader (pipeline) compilations"
msgstr "ການຫຼຸດອາການກະຕຸກຈາກການ Compile ເຊດເດີ (ໄປ້ລາຍ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:8
msgid ""
"This page only applies to the Forward+ and Mobile renderers, not "
"Compatibility. Ubershaders and pipeline precompilation rely on functionality "
"only available in modern low-level graphics APIs (Vulkan, Direct3D 12, "
"Metal). The Compatibility renderer uses OpenGL 3.3, OpenGL ES 3.0, or WebGL "
"2.0 depending on the platform. These versions lack the functionality to "
"effectively implement ubershaders and pipeline precompilation."
msgstr ""
"ໜ້ານີ້ໃຊ້ໄດ້ກັບຕົວເຣັນເດີ Forward+ ແລະ Mobile ເທົ່ານັ້ນ, ບໍ່ລວມ Compatibility. Ubershaders ແ"
"ລະ ການ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍ (Pipeline) ໄວ້ລ່ວງໜ້າແມ່ນເພິ່ງພາການເຮັດວຽກທີ່ມີສະເພາະໃນ Graphics "
"API ລະດັບຕ່ຳສະໄໝໃໝ່ (Vulkan, Direct3D 12, Metal). ຕົວເຣັນເດີ Compatibility ໃຊ້ "
"OpenGL 3.3, OpenGL ES 3.0, ຫຼື WebGL 2.0 ຂຶ້ນຢູ່ກັບແພລັດຟອມ. ເວີຊັນເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຂາດຄວາມສາມາດໃນກາ"
"ນນຳໃຊ້ ubershaders ແລະ ການ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍໄວ້ລ່ວງໜ້າໄດ້ຢ່າງມີປະສິດທິພາບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:15
msgid ""
"To avoid shader stutters in Compatibility, you need to use the legacy "
"approach of preloading materials, shaders, and particles by displaying them "
"for at least one frame in the view frustum when the level is loading."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອຫຼີກລ່ຽງອາການກະຕຸກຂອງ shader ໃນ Compatibility, ທ່ານຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງໃຊ້ແນວທາງແບບເກົ່າຄືການໂຫຼ"
"ດວັດສະດຸ, shader ແລະ particles ໄວ້ລ່ວງໜ້າ ໂດຍການສະແດງພວກມັນຢ່າງໜ້ອຍໜຶ່ງເຟຣມໃນຂອບເຂດການເ"
"ບິ່ງ (View frustum) ໃນລະຫວ່າງທີ່ກຳລັງໂຫຼດດ່ານ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:19
msgid ""
"Pipeline compilation, also commonly known as shader compilation, is an "
"expensive operation required by the engine to be able to draw any kind of "
"content with the GPU."
msgstr ""
"ການ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍ (Pipeline compilation), ຫຼື ທີ່ເອີ້ນກັນທົ່ວໄປວ່າການ Compile shader, ແ"
"ມ່ນການເຮັດວຽກທີ່ມີຕົ້ນທຶນສູງທີ່ເອນຈິນຕ້ອງການເພື່ອໃຫ້ສາມາດແຕ້ມເນື້ອຫາໃດໆ ກໍຕາມດ້ວຍ GPU."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:23
msgid ""
"Flowchart showing the entire compilation process for a shader: VisualShader "
"and Standard Material to Godot Shading Language to GLSL to Intermediate "
"Format (SPIR-V) to Pipeline. Shader Compilation is the GLSL to Intermediate "
"Format step. Pipeline Compilation is the Intermediate Format to Pipeline "
"step."
msgstr ""
"ຜັງງານ (Flowchart) ສະແດງຂະບວນການ Compile ທັງໝົດສຳລັບ shader: ຈາກ VisualShader ແລ"
"ະ Standard Material ໄປຫາ Godot Shading Language ໄປຫາ GLSL ໄປຫາຮູບແບບລະຫວ່າງກາງ "
"(SPIR-V) ໄປຫາ Pipeline. ການ Compile Shader ແມ່ນຂັ້ນຕອນຈາກ GLSL ໄປຫາຮູບແບບລະຫວ່າງກາ"
"ງ. ການ Compile Pipeline ແມ່ນຂັ້ນຕອນຈາກຮູບແບບລະຫວ່າງກາງໄປຫາ Pipeline."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:27
msgid ""
"Shaders and materials in Godot go through several steps before they can be "
"run by the GPU."
msgstr ""
"Shader ແລະ ວັດສະດຸໃນ Godot ຕ້ອງຜ່ານຫຼາຍຂັ້ນຕອນກ່ອນທີ່ຈະສາມາດເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ດ້ວຍ GPU."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:30
msgid ""
"In more precise terms, *shader compilation* involves the translation of the "
"GLSL code that Godot generates into an intermediate format that can be "
"shared across systems (such as SPIR-V when using Vulkan). However, this "
"format can't be used by the GPU directly."
msgstr ""
"ໃນຄວາມໝາຍທີ່ຊັດເຈນກວ່າ, *ການ Compile shader* ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັບການແປໂຄດ GLSL ທີ່ Godot ສ້າງຂຶ້ນໃ"
"ຫ້ເປັນຮູບແບບລະຫວ່າງກາງ (Intermediate format) ທີ່ສາມາດໃຊ້ຮ່ວມກັນໄດ້ໃນຫຼາຍລະບົບ (ເຊັ່ນ SPIR-"
"V ເມື່ອໃຊ້ Vulkan). ເຖິງຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ຮູບແບບນີ້ຍັງບໍ່ສາມາດໃຊ້ໂດຍ GPU ໄດ້ໂດຍກົງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:35
msgid ""
"*Pipeline compilation* is the step where the GPU driver converts the "
"intermediate shader format (the result from shader compilation) to something "
"the GPU can actually use for rendering. Drivers usually keep a cache of "
"pipelines stored somewhere in the system to avoid repeating the process "
"every time a game is run. This cache is usually deleted when the driver is "
"updated."
msgstr ""
"*ການ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍ (Pipeline compilation)* ແມ່ນຂັ້ນຕອນທີ່ໄດຣເວີຂອງ GPU ແປງຮູບແບບ "
"shader ລະຫວ່າງກາງ (ຜົນລັດຈາກການ Compile shader) ໃຫ້ເປັນສິ່ງທີ່ GPU ສາມາດໃຊ້ໃນການເຣັນເດີໄດ້"
"ແທ້ໆ. ໄດຣເວີມັກຈະເກັບແຄຊ (Cache) ຂອງໄປ້ລາຍໄວ້ບ່ອນໃດບ່ອນໜຶ່ງໃນລະບົບເພື່ອຫຼີກລ່ຽງການເຮັດຂະບວນການ"
"ຊ້ຳທຸກຄັ້ງທີ່ເປີດເກມ. ແຄຊນີ້ມັກຈະຖືກລຶບອອກເມື່ອມີການອັບເດດໄດຣເວີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:41
msgid ""
"Pipelines contain more information than just the shader code, which means "
"that for each shader, there can be dozens of pipelines or more! This makes "
"it difficult for an engine to compile them ahead of time, both because it "
"would be very slow, and because it would take up a lot of memory. On top of "
"that, this step can only be performed on the user's system and it is very "
"tough to share the result between users unless they have the exact same "
"hardware and driver version."
msgstr ""
"ໄປ້ລາຍ (Pipelines) ປະກອບມີຂໍ້ມູນຫຼາຍກວ່າພຽງແຕ່ໂຄດ shader, ເຊິ່ງໝາຍຄວາມວ່າສຳລັບແຕ່ລະ "
"shader, ອາດຈະມີໄປ້ລາຍເປັນສິບ ຫຼື ຫຼາຍກວ່ານັ້ນ! ສິ່ງນີ້ເຮັດໃຫ້ເປັນເລື່ອງຍາກສຳລັບເອນຈິນທີ່ຈະ Compile ພ"
"ວກມັນໄວ້ລ່ວງໜ້າ, ທັງຍ້ອນວ່າມັນຈະຊ້າຫຼາຍ ແລະ ຍ້ອນວ່າມັນຈະກິນໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳຫຼາຍ. ນອກຈາກນັ້ນ, ຂັ້ນຕອນນີ້ສາ"
"ມາດເຮັດໄດ້ສະເພາະໃນເຄື່ອງຂອງຜູ້ໃຊ້ເທົ່ານັ້ນ ແລະ ມັນຍາກຫຼາຍທີ່ຈະແບ່ງປັນຜົນລັດລະຫວ່າງຜູ້ໃຊ້ ນອກຈາກວ່າພວກ"
"ເຂົາຈະມີຮາດແວ ແລະ ເວີຊັນໄດຣເວີທີ່ຄືກັນເປະ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:49
msgid ""
"Before Godot 4.4, there was no solution to pipeline compilation other than "
"generating them when an object shows up inside the camera's view, leading to "
"the infamous *shader stutter* or hitches that only occur during the first "
"playthrough. **With Godot 4.4, new mechanisms have been introduced to "
"mitigate stutters from pipeline compilation.**"
msgstr ""
"ກ່ອນ Godot 4.4, ບໍ່ມີວິທີແກ້ໄຂການ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍ ນອກຈາກການສ້າງພວກມັນເມື່ອມີວັດຖຸປະກົດຂຶ້ນໃນສາຍຕ"
"າຂອງກ້ອງ, ເຊິ່ງນຳໄປສູ່ອາການ *shader stutter* ຫຼື ອາການກະຕຸກທີ່ເກີດຂຶ້ນສະເພາະໃນການຫຼິ້ນຄັ້ງທຳອິ"
"ດ. **ດ້ວຍ Godot 4.4, ລະບົບໃໝ່ໄດ້ຖືກນຳເຂົ້າມາເພື່ອຫຼຸດຜ່ອນອາການກະຕຸກຈາກການ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍ.**"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:55
msgid ""
"**Ubershaders**: Godot makes use of specialization constants, a feature that "
"allows the driver to optimize a pipeline's code around a set of parameters "
"such as lighting, shadow quality, etc. Specialization constants are used to "
"optimize a shader by limiting unnecessary features. Changing a "
"specialization constant requires recompiling the pipeline. Ubershaders are a "
"special version of the shader that are able to change these constants while "
"rendering, which means Godot can precompile just one pipeline ahead of time "
"and compile the more optimized versions on the background during gameplay. "
"This reduces the amount of pipelines that need to be created significantly."
msgstr ""
"**Ubershaders**: Godot ໃຊ້ຄ່າຄົງທີ່ສະເພາະ (Specialization constants), ເຊິ່ງເປັນຟີເຈີທີ່ຊ່ວ"
"ຍໃຫ້ໄດຣເວີປັບແຕ່ງໂຄດຂອງໄປ້ລາຍຕາມພາຣາມີເຕີຕ່າງໆ ເຊັ່ນ ແສງສະຫວ່າງ, ຄຸນນະພາບເງົາ ແລະ ອື່ນໆ. ຄ່າຄົ"
"ງທີ່ສະເພາະຖືກໃຊ້ເພື່ອປັບແຕ່ງ shader ໂດຍການຈຳກັດຟີເຈີທີ່ບໍ່ຈຳເປັນ. ການປ່ຽນຄ່າຄົງທີ່ສະເພາະຈະຕ້ອງມີການ "
"Recompile ໄປ້ລາຍໃໝ່. Ubershaders ແມ່ນ shader ເວີຊັນພິເສດທີ່ສາມາດປ່ຽນແປງຄ່າຄົງທີ່ເຫຼົ່ານີ້ໄດ້ໃນຂະ"
"ນະທີ່ເຣັນເດີ, ເຊິ່ງໝາຍຄວາມວ່າ Godot ສາມາດ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍພຽງອັນດຽວໄວ້ລ່ວງໜ້າ ແລະ Compile ເ"
"ວີຊັນທີ່ຖືກປັບແຕ່ງດີກວ່າໃນເບື້ອງຫຼັງລະຫວ່າງການຫຼິ້ນ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຊ່ວຍຫຼຸດຈຳນວນໄປ້ລາຍທີ່ຕ້ອງສ້າງຂຶ້ນຢ່າງຫຼວງຫຼາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:64
msgid ""
"**Pipeline precompilation**: By using ubershaders, the engine can precompile "
"pipelines ahead of time in multiple places such as when meshes are loaded or "
"when nodes are added to the scene. By being part of the resource loading "
"process, pipelines can even be precompiled in multiple background threads if "
"possible during loading screens or even gameplay."
msgstr ""
"**Pipeline precompilation (ການ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍໄວ້ລ່ວງໜ້າ)**: ດ້ວຍການໃຊ້ "
"ubershaders, ເອນຈິນສາມາດ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍໄວ້ລ່ວງໜ້າໄດ້ໃນຫຼາຍບ່ອນ ເຊັ່ນ ເມື່ອໂຫຼດ mesh ຫຼື ເມື່ອເ"
"ພີ່ມໂນດເຂົ້າໃນສາກ. ໂດຍການເປັນສ່ວນໜຶ່ງຂອງຂະບວນການໂຫຼດຊັບພະຍາກອນ, ໄປ້ລາຍຍັງສາມາດຖືກ Compile "
"ລ່ວງໜ້າໃນຫຼາຍເທຣດເບື້ອງຫຼັງໄດ້ ຖ້າເປັນໄປໄດ້ໃນລະຫວ່າງໜ້າຈໍໂຫຼດ ຫຼື ແມ່ນແຕ່ໃນລະຫວ່າງການຫຼິ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:70
msgid ""
"Starting in Godot 4.4, Godot will detect which pipelines are needed and "
"precompile them at load-time. This detection system is mostly automatic, but "
"it relies on the RenderingServer seeing evidence of all shaders, meshes, or "
"rendering features at load-time. For example, if you load a mesh and shader "
"while the game is running, the pipeline for that mesh/shader combination "
"won't be compiled until the mesh/shader is loaded. Similarly, things like "
"enabling MSAA, or instancing a VoxelGI node while the game is running will "
"trigger pipeline recompilations."
msgstr ""
"ເລີ່ມຕັ້ງແຕ່ Godot 4.4, Godot ຈະກວດສອບວ່າໄປ້ລາຍໃດທີ່ຈຳເປັນ ແລະ Compile ພວກມັນໄວ້ລ່ວງໜ້າໃນເວ"
"ລາໂຫຼດ. ລະບົບກວດສອບນີ້ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ແມ່ນອັດຕະໂນມັດ, ແຕ່ມັນເພິ່ງພາ RenderingServer ທີ່ຕ້ອງເຫັນຫຼັກຖານຂອ"
"ງທຸກໆ shader, mesh ຫຼື ຟີເຈີການເຣັນເດີໃນເວລາໂຫຼດ. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ, ຖ້າທ່ານໂຫຼດ mesh ແລະ shader "
"ໃນຂະນະທີ່ເກມກຳລັງເຮັດວຽກ, ໄປ້ລາຍສຳລັບຄູ່ mesh/shader ນັ້ນຈະບໍ່ຖືກ Compile ຈົນກວ່າ mesh/"
"shader ຈະຖືກໂຫຼດ. ໃນທຳນອງດຽວກັນ, ສິ່ງຕ່າງໆ ເຊັ່ນ ການເປີດໃຊ້ MSAA, ຫຼື ການສ້າງ instance ຂອງ"
"ໂນດ VoxelGI ໃນຂະນະທີ່ເກມເຮັດວຽກ ຈະກະຕຸ້ນໃຫ້ເກີດການ Recompile ໄປ້ລາຍໃໝ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:80
msgid "Pipeline precompilation monitors"
msgstr "ຕົວຕິດຕາມການ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍລ່ວງໜ້າ (Pipeline precompilation monitors)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:84
msgid ""
"Compiling pipelines ahead of time is the main mechanism Godot uses to "
"mitigate shader stutters, but it's not a perfect solution. Being aware of "
"the situations that can lead to pipeline stutters can be very helpful, and "
"the workarounds are pretty straightforward compared to previous versions. "
"These workarounds may be less necessary over time with future versions of "
"Godot as more detection techniques are implemented."
msgstr ""
"ການ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍໄວ້ລ່ວງໜ້າແມ່ນກົນໄກຫຼັກທີ່ Godot ໃຊ້ເພື່ອຫຼຸດຜ່ອນອາການກະຕຸກຂອງ shader, ແຕ່ມັນກໍ"
"ບໍ່ແມ່ນວິທີແກ້ໄຂທີ່ສົມບູນແບບ. ການຮັບຮູ້ສະຖານະການທີ່ອາດນຳໄປສູ່ອາການກະຕຸກຂອງໄປ້ລາຍນັ້ນມີປະໂຫຍດຫຼາຍ, ແລ"
"ະ ວິທີແກ້ໄຂກໍຂ້ອນຂ້າງງ່າຍດາຍເມື່ອທຽບກັບເວີຊັນກ່ອນໆ. ວິທີແກ້ໄຂເຫຼົ່ານີ້ອາດຈະມີຄວາມຈຳເປັນໜ້ອຍລົງໃນອະນາຄົ"
"ດ ເມື່ອ Godot ເວີຊັນໃໝ່ໆ ມີເຕັກນິກການກວດສອບທີ່ດີຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:91
msgid ""
"The Godot debugger offers monitors for tracking the amount of pipelines "
"created by the game and the step that triggered their compilation. You can "
"keep an eye on these monitors as the game runs to identify potential sources "
"of shader stutters without having to wipe your driver cache every time you "
"wish to test. Sudden increases of these values outside of loading screens "
"can show up as hitches during gameplay the first time someone plays the game "
"on their system. **It is recommended you take a look at these monitors to "
"identify possible sources of stutter for your players**, as you might be "
"unable to experience them yourself without deleting your driver cache or "
"testing on a weaker system."
msgstr ""
"Debugger ຂອງ Godot ມີຕົວຕິດຕາມ (Monitors) ສຳລັບກວດສອບຈຳນວນໄປ້ລາຍທີ່ຖືກສ້າງຂຶ້ນໂດຍເກມ ແລ"
"ະ ຂັ້ນຕອນທີ່ກະຕຸ້ນໃຫ້ເກີດການ Compile. ທ່ານສາມາດຕິດຕາມຕົວວັດແທກເຫຼົ່ານີ້ໃນຂະນະທີ່ເກມເຮັດວຽກ ເພື່ອລະບຸ"
"ແຫຼ່ງທີ່ມາຂອງອາການກະຕຸກຂອງ shader ໂດຍບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງລ້າງແຄຊຂອງໄດຣເວີທຸກຄັ້ງທີ່ຕ້ອງການທົດສອບ. ການເ"
"ພີ່ມຂຶ້ນຢ່າງກະທັນຫັນຂອງຄ່າເຫຼົ່ານີ້ນອກໜ້າຈໍໂຫຼດ ອາດຈະສະແດງອອກມາເປັນອາການກະຕຸກໃນລະຫວ່າງການຫຼິ້ນຄັ້ງທຳອິ"
"ດໃນເຄື່ອງຂອງຜູ້ໃຊ້. **ແນະນຳໃຫ້ທ່ານກວດເບິ່ງຕົວຕິດຕາມເຫຼົ່ານີ້ເພື່ອລະບຸແຫຼ່ງທີ່ມາຂອງອາການກະຕຸກສຳລັບຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນຂອ"
"ງທ່ານ**, ເພາະວ່າທ່ານອາດຈະບໍ່ພົບອາການເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນດ້ວຍຕົນເອງ ຖ້າບໍ່ລຶບແຄຊໄດຣເວີ ຫຼື ທົດສອບໃນເຄື່ອງທີ່ສະເປັກ"
"ຕ່ຳກວ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:101
msgid "Screenshot of the Godot pipeline compilations monitor"
msgstr "ພາບໜ້າຈໍຂອງຕົວຕິດຕາມການ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍໃນ Godot"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:105
msgid "Pipeline compilations of one of the demo projects."
msgstr "ການ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍຈາກໜຶ່ງໃນໂປຣເຈັກຕົວຢ່າງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:107
msgid ""
"We can see the pipelines compiled during gameplay and verify which steps "
"could possibly cause stuttters. Note that these values will only increase "
"and never go down, as deleted pipelines are not tracked by these monitors "
"and pipelines may be erased and recreated during gameplay."
msgstr ""
"ພວກເຮົາສາມາດເຫັນໄປ້ລາຍທີ່ຖືກ Compile ໃນລະຫວ່າງການຫຼິ້ນ ແລະ ກວດສອບໄດ້ວ່າຂັ້ນຕອນໃດທີ່ອາດເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີ"
"ດອາການກະຕຸກ. ໝາຍເຫດວ່າຄ່າເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຈະເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນເທົ່ານັ້ນ ແລະ ບໍ່ມີວັນຫຼຸດລົງ, ເພາະໄປ້ລາຍທີ່ຖືກລຶບໄປຈະບໍ່ຖືກນັບໂ"
"ດຍຕົວຕິດຕາມເຫຼົ່ານີ້ ແລະ ໄປ້ລາຍອາດຖືກລຶບ ແລະ ສ້າງໃໝ່ໄດ້ໃນລະຫວ່າງການຫຼິ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:113
msgid ""
"**Canvas**: Compiled when drawing a 2D node. The engine does not currently "
"feature precompilation for 2D elements and stutters will show up when the 2D "
"node is drawn for the first time."
msgstr ""
"**Canvas**: ຖືກ Compile ເມື່ອແຕ້ມໂນດ 2D. ປັດຈຸບັນເອນຈິນຍັງບໍ່ມີຟີເຈີການ Compile ລ່ວງໜ້າສຳລັບອົງ"
"ປະກອບ 2D ແລະ ອາການກະຕຸກຈະປະກົດຂຶ້ນເມື່ອໂນດ 2D ຖືກແຕ້ມເປັນຄັ້ງທຳອິດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:116
msgid ""
"**Mesh**: Compiled as part of loading a 3D mesh and identifying what "
"pipelines can be precompiled from its properties. These can lead to stutters "
"if a mesh is loaded during gameplay, but they can be mitigated if the mesh "
"is loaded by using a background thread. **Modifiers that are part of nodes "
"such as material overrides can't be compiled on this step**."
msgstr ""
"**Mesh**: ຖືກ Compile ເປັນສ່ວນໜຶ່ງຂອງການໂຫຼດ mesh 3D ແລະ ການລະບຸວ່າໄປ້ລາຍໃດສາມາດ "
"Compile ລ່ວງໜ້າໄດ້ຈາກຄຸນສົມບັດຂອງມັນ. ສິ່ງນີ້ອາດນຳໄປສູ່ອາການກະຕຸກຖ້າ mesh ຖືກໂຫຼດລະຫວ່າງການຫຼິ້ນ, "
"ແຕ່ສາມາດຫຼຸດຜ່ອນໄດ້ຖ້າ mesh ຖືກໂຫຼດໂດຍໃຊ້ເທຣດເບື້ອງຫຼັງ. **Modifier ທີ່ເປັນສ່ວນໜຶ່ງຂອງໂນດ ເຊັ່ນ "
"material overrides ບໍ່ສາມາດຖືກ Compile ໃນຂັ້ນຕອນນີ້ໄດ້**."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:121
msgid ""
"**Surface**: Compiled when a frame is about to be drawn and 3D objects were "
"instanced on the scene tree for the first time. This can also include "
"compilation for nodes that aren't even visible on the scene tree. The "
"stutter will occur only on the first frame the node is added to the scene, "
"which won't result in an obvious stutter if it happens right after a loading "
"screen."
msgstr ""
"**Surface**: ຖືກ Compile ເມື່ອເຟຣມກຳລັງຈະຖືກແຕ້ມ ແລະ ວັດຖຸ 3D ຖືກສ້າງ instance ໃນ "
"scene tree ເປັນຄັ້ງທຳອິດ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຍັງລວມເຖິງການ Compile ສຳລັບໂນດທີ່ບໍ່ໄດ້ປະກົດໃຫ້ເຫັນໃນ scene "
"tree ນຳ. ອາການກະຕຸກຈະເກີດຂຶ້ນສະເພາະໃນເຟຣມທຳອິດທີ່ໂນດຖືກເພີ່ມເຂົ້າໃນສາກ, ເຊິ່ງຈະບໍ່ສົ່ງຜົນໃຫ້ເກີດອາ"
"ການກະຕຸກທີ່ຊັດເຈນ ຖ້າມັນເກີດຂຶ້ນທັນທີຫຼັງຈາກໜ້າຈໍໂຫຼດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:126
msgid ""
"**Draw**: Compiled on demand when a 3D object needs to be drawn and an "
"ubershader was not precompiled ahead of time. The engine is unable to "
"precompile this pipeline due to triggering a case that hasn't been covered "
"yet or a modification that was done to the engine's code. Leads to stutters "
"during gameplay. This is identical to Godot versions before 4.4. If you see "
"compilations here, please `let the developers know <https://github.com/"
"godotengine/godot/issues>`__ as this should never happen with the Ubershader "
"system. Make sure to attach a minimal reproduction project when doing so."
msgstr ""
"**Draw**: ຖືກ Compile ເມື່ອມີຄວາມຕ້ອງການແຕ້ມວັດຖຸ 3D ແລະ ubershader ບໍ່ໄດ້ຖືກ Compile ໄວ້ລ່"
"ວງໜ້າ. ເອນຈິນບໍ່ສາມາດ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍນີ້ລ່ວງໜ້າໄດ້ ເນື່ອງຈາກເກີດກໍລະນີທີ່ຍັງບໍ່ຖືກຄຸ້ມຄອງ ຫຼື ມີການແກ້ໄຂໂ"
"ຄດຂອງເອນຈິນ. ນຳໄປສູ່ອາການກະຕຸກລະຫວ່າງການຫຼິ້ນ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຄືກັນກັບ Godot ເວີຊັນກ່ອນ 4.4. ຖ້າທ່ານເຫັນກາ"
"ນ Compile ຢູ່ທີ່ນີ້, ກະລຸນາ `ແຈ້ງໃຫ້ນັກພັດທະນາຮູ້ <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/"
"issues>`__ ເພາະສິ່ງນີ້ບໍ່ຄວນເກີດຂຶ້ນກັບລະບົບ Ubershader. ໃຫ້ໝັ້ນໃຈວ່າໄດ້ແນບໂປຣເຈັກຕົວຢ່າງສຳລັບການ"
"ທົດສອບ (Minimal reproduction project) ເມື່ອແຈ້ງບັນຫາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:135
msgid ""
"**Specialization**: Compiled in the background during gameplay to optimize "
"the framerate. Unable to cause stutters, but may result in reduced "
"framerates if there are many happening per frame."
msgstr ""
"**Specialization**: ຖືກ Compile ໃນເບື້ອງຫຼັງລະຫວ່າງການຫຼິ້ນເພື່ອປັບແຕ່ງອັດຕາເຟຣມ. ບໍ່ເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດ"
"ອາການກະຕຸກ, ແຕ່ອາດສົ່ງຜົນໃຫ້ອັດຕາເຟຣມຫຼຸດລົງ ຖ້າມີການ Compile ເກີດຂຶ້ນຈຳນວນຫຼາຍໃນແຕ່ລະເຟຣມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:140
msgid "Pipeline precompilation features"
msgstr "ຟີເຈີການ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍລ່ວງໜ້າ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:142
msgid ""
"Godot offers a lot of rendering features that are not necessarily used by "
"every game. Unfortunately, pipeline precompilation can't know ahead of time "
"if a particular feature is used by a project. Some of these features can "
"only be detected when a user adds a node to the scene or toggles a "
"particular setting in the project or the environment. The pipeline "
"precompilation system will keep track of these features as they're "
"encountered for the first time and enable precompilation of them for any "
"meshes or surfaces that are created afterwards."
msgstr ""
"Godot ມີຟີເຈີການເຣັນເດີຫຼາຍຢ່າງທີ່ບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງຖືກໃຊ້ໃນທຸກໆ ເກມ. ໜ້າເສຍດາຍທີ່ການ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍລ່ວ"
"ງໜ້າບໍ່ສາມາດຮູ້ໄດ້ລ່ວງໜ້າວ່າຟີເຈີໃດໜຶ່ງຖືກໃຊ້ໃນໂປຣເຈັກຫຼືບໍ່. ບາງຟີເຈີເຫຼົ່ານີ້ສາມາດກວດພົບໄດ້ກໍຕໍ່ເມື່ອຜູ້ໃຊ້ເພີ່ມໂນ"
"ດເຂົ້າໃນສາກ ຫຼື ປ່ຽນການຕັ້ງຄ່າບາງຢ່າງໃນໂປຣເຈັກ ຫຼື ສະພາບແວດລ້ອມ (Environment). ລະບົບການ "
"Compile ໄປ້ລາຍລ່ວງໜ້າຈະຕິດຕາມຟີເຈີເຫຼົ່ານີ້ເມື່ອພົບພວກມັນເປັນຄັ້ງທຳອິດ ແລະ ເປີດໃຊ້ການ Compile ລ່ວງໜ້"
"າສຳລັບ mesh ຫຼື surface ໃດໆ ກໍຕາມທີ່ຖືກສ້າງຂຶ້ນຫຼັງຈາກນັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:150
msgid ""
"If your game makes use of these features, **make sure to have a scene that "
"uses them as early as possible** before loading the majority of the assets. "
"This scene can be very simple and will do the job as long as it uses the "
"features the game plans to use. It can even be rendered off-screen for at "
"least one frame if necessary, e.g. by covering it with "
"a :ref:`class_ColorRect` node or using a :ref:`class_SubViewport` located "
"outside the window bounds."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເກມຂອງທ່ານໃຊ້ຟີເຈີເຫຼົ່ານີ້, **ໃຫ້ໝັ້ນໃຈວ່າໄດ້ມີສາກທີ່ໃຊ້ພວກມັນໃຫ້ໄວທີ່ສຸດເທົ່າທີ່ຈະເປັນໄປໄດ້** ກ່ອນທີ່ຈະໂຫຼ"
"ດຊັບພະຍາກອນສ່ວນໃຫຍ່. ສາກນີ້ສາມາດລຽບງ່າຍຫຼາຍ ແລະ ຈະເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ຕາບໃດທີ່ມັນໃຊ້ຟີເຈີທີ່ເກມວາງແຜນຈະໃ"
"ຊ້. ມັນຍັງສາມາດຖືກເຣັນເດີຢູ່ນອກໜ້າຈໍຢ່າງໜ້ອຍໜຶ່ງເຟຣມໄດ້ຖ້າຈຳເປັນ, ເຊັ່ນ ໂດຍການບັງມັນດ້ວຍໂນດ "
":ref:`class_ColorRect` ຫຼື ໃຊ້ :ref:`class_SubViewport` ທີ່ຢູ່ນອກຂອບເຂດໜ້າຕ່າງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:157
msgid ""
"You should also keep in mind that changing any of these features during "
"gameplay will result in immediate stutters. Make sure to only change these "
"features from configuration screens if necessary and insert loading screens "
"and messages when the changes are applied."
msgstr ""
"ທ່ານຄວນຈື່ໄວ້ນຳວ່າການປ່ຽນແປງຟີເຈີເຫຼົ່ານີ້ໃນລະຫວ່າງການຫຼິ້ນຈະສົ່ງຜົນໃຫ້ເກີດອາການກະຕຸກທັນທີ. ໃຫ້ໝັ້ນໃຈວ່າໄດ້"
"ປ່ຽນແປງຟີເຈີເຫຼົ່ານີ້ສະເພາະຈາກໜ້າຈໍການຕັ້ງຄ່າຖ້າຈຳເປັນ ແລະ ໃສ່ໜ້າຈໍໂຫຼດ ຫຼື ຂໍ້ຄວາມແຈ້ງເຕືອນເມື່ອມີການນຳໃ"
"ຊ້ການປ່ຽນແປງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:162
msgid ""
"**MSAA Level**: Enabled when the level of 3D MSAA is changed on the project "
"settings. Unfortunately, different MSAA levels being used on different "
"viewports will lead to stutters as the engine only keeps track of one level "
"at a time to perform precompilation."
msgstr ""
"**MSAA Level**: ເປີດໃຊ້ເມື່ອລະດັບຂອງ 3D MSAA ຖືກປ່ຽນໃນການຕັ້ງຄ່າໂປຣເຈັກ. ໜ້າເສຍດາຍທີ່ການໃຊ້ລ"
"ະດັບ MSAA ທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນໃນ viewport ທີ່ຕ່າງກັນຈະນຳໄປສູ່ອາການກະຕຸກ ເພາະເອນຈິນຕິດຕາມໄດ້ພຽງລະດັບດ"
"ຽວໃນແຕ່ລະຄັ້ງເພື່ອເຮັດການ Compile ລ່ວງໜ້າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:166
msgid ""
"**Reflection Probes**: Enabled when a ReflectionProbe node is placed on the "
"scene."
msgstr "**Reflection Probes**: ເປີດໃຊ້ເມື່ອມີການວາງໂນດ ReflectionProbe ໃນສາກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:168
msgid ""
"**Separate Specular**: Enabled when using effects like sub-surface "
"scattering or a compositor effect that relies on sampling the specularity "
"directly off the screen."
msgstr ""
"**Separate Specular**: ເປີດໃຊ້ເມື່ອໃຊ້ເອັບເຟັກເຊັ່ນ sub-surface scattering ຫຼື "
"compositor effect ທີ່ເພິ່ງພາການເກັບຕົວຢ່າງຄວາມເງົາ (Specularity) ຈາກໜ້າຈໍໂດຍກົງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:171
msgid ""
"**Motion Vectors**: Enabled when using effects such as TAA, FSR2 or a "
"compositor effect that requires motion vectors (such as motion blur)."
msgstr ""
"**Motion Vectors**: ເປີດໃຊ້ເມື່ອໃຊ້ເອັບເຟັກເຊັ່ນ TAA, FSR2 ຫຼື compositor effect ທີ່ຕ້ອງກາ"
"ນ motion vectors (ເຊັ່ນ motion blur)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:173
msgid ""
"**Normal and Roughness**: Enabled when using SDFGI, VoxelGI, screen-space "
"reflections, SSAO, SSIL, or using the ``normal_roughness_buffer`` in a "
"custom shader or :ref:`class_CompositorEffect`."
msgstr ""
"**Normal and Roughness**: ເປີດໃຊ້ເມື່ອໃຊ້ SDFGI, VoxelGI, screen-space "
"reflections, SSAO, SSIL, ຫຼື ໃຊ້ ``normal_roughness_buffer`` ໃນ custom shader ຫຼື "
":ref:`class_CompositorEffect`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:176
msgid ""
"**Lightmaps**: Enabled when a LightmapGI node is placed on the scene and a "
"node uses a baked lightmap."
msgstr ""
"**Lightmaps**: ເປີດໃຊ້ເມື່ອມີການວາງໂນດ LightmapGI ໃນສາກ ແລະ ມີໂນດທີ່ໃຊ້ baked "
"lightmap."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:178
msgid "**VoxelGI**: Enabled when a VoxelGI node is placed on the scene."
msgstr "**VoxelGI**: ເປີດໃຊ້ເມື່ອມີການວາງໂນດ VoxelGI ໃນສາກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:179
msgid "**SDFGI**: Enabled when the WorldEnvironment enables SDFGI."
msgstr "**SDFGI**: ເປີດໃຊ້ເມື່ອ WorldEnvironment ເປີດໃຊ້ SDFGI."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:180
msgid "**Multiview**: Enabled for XR projects."
msgstr "**Multiview**: ເປີດໃຊ້ສຳລັບໂປຣເຈັກ XR."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:181
msgid ""
"**16/32-bit Shadows**: Enabled when the configuration of the depth precision "
"of shadowmaps is changed on the project settings."
msgstr ""
"**16/32-bit Shadows**: ເປີດໃຊ້ເມື່ອການຕັ້ງຄ່າຄວາມຊັດເຈນຂອງຄວາມເລິກ (Depth precision) ຂ"
"ອງ shadowmaps ຖືກປ່ຽນໃນການຕັ້ງຄ່າໂປຣເຈັກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:183
msgid ""
"**Omni Shadow Dual Paraboloid**: Enabled when an omni light casts shadows "
"and uses the dual paraboloid mode."
msgstr ""
"**Omni Shadow Dual Paraboloid**: ເປີດໃຊ້ເມື່ອ Omni light ສ້າງເງົາ ແລະ ໃຊ້ໂໝດ dual "
"paraboloid."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:185
msgid ""
"**Omni Shadow Cubemap**: Enabled when an omni light casts shadows and uses "
"the cubemap mode (which is the default)."
msgstr ""
"**Omni Shadow Cubemap**: ເປີດໃຊ້ເມື່ອ Omni light ສ້າງເງົາ ແລະ ໃຊ້ໂໝດ cubemap (ເຊິ່ງເປັນ"
"ຄ່າເບື້ອງຕົ້ນ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:188
msgid ""
"If you witness stutters during gameplay and the monitors report a sudden "
"increase in compilations during the **Surface** step, it is very likely a "
"feature was not enabled ahead of time. Ensuring that this effect is enabled "
"while loading your game will likely mitigate the issue."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າທ່ານພົບອາການກະຕຸກໃນລະຫວ່າງການຫຼິ້ນ ແລະ ຕົວຕິດຕາມລາຍງານການເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນຢ່າງກະທັນຫັນຂອງການ "
"Compile ໃນຂັ້ນຕອນ **Surface**, ມັນເປັນໄປໄດ້ສູງວ່າຟີເຈີໃດໜຶ່ງບໍ່ໄດ້ຖືກເປີດໃຊ້ໄວ້ລ່ວງໜ້າ. ການຮັບປະກັນ"
"ວ່າເອັບເຟັກນີ້ຖືກເປີດໃຊ້ໃນຂະນະທີ່ໂຫຼດເກມຈະຊ່ວຍຫຼຸດຜ່ອນບັນຫານີ້ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:194
msgid "Pipeline precompilation instancing"
msgstr "ການສ້າງ Instance ເພື່ອ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍລ່ວງໜ້າ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:196
msgid ""
"One common source of stutters in games is the fact that some effects are "
"only instanced on the scene because of interactions that only happen during "
"gameplay. For example, if you have a particle effect that is only added to "
"the scene through a script when a player does an action. Even if the scene "
"is preloaded, the engine might be unable to precompile the pipelines until "
"the effect is added to the scene at least once."
msgstr ""
"ແຫຼ່ງທີ່ມາທົ່ວໄປຂອງອາການກະຕຸກໃນເກມແມ່ນການທີ່ບາງເອັບເຟັກຖືກສ້າງ instance ໃນສາກສະເພາະຕອນທີ່ມີການ"
"ໂຕ້ຕອບລະຫວ່າງການຫຼິ້ນເທົ່ານັ້ນ. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ, ຖ້າທ່ານມີ particle effect ທີ່ຈະຖືກເພີ່ມເຂົ້າໃນສາກຜ່ານສະ"
"ຄຣິບເມື່ອຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນເຮັດບາງຢ່າງ. ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າສາກຈະຖືກໂຫຼດໄວ້ລ່ວງໜ້າແລ້ວ, ແຕ່ເອນຈິນອາດຈະບໍ່ສາມາດ Compile "
"ໄປ້ລາຍລ່ວງໜ້າໄດ້ ຈົນກວ່າເອັບເຟັກນັ້ນຈະຖືກເພີ່ມເຂົ້າໃນສາກຢ່າງໜ້ອຍໜຶ່ງຄັ້ງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:203
msgid ""
"Luckily, it's possible for Godot 4.4 and later to precompile these pipelines "
"as long as the scene is instantiated at least once on the scene, even if "
"it's completely invisible or outside of the camera's view."
msgstr ""
"ໂຊກດີທີ່ Godot 4.4 ແລະ ເວີຊັນຫຼັງຈາກນັ້ນ ສາມາດ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍເຫຼົ່ານີ້ລ່ວງໜ້າໄດ້ ຕາບໃດທີ່ສາກຖືກສ້າ"
"ງ instance ຢ່າງໜ້ອຍໜຶ່ງຄັ້ງໃນສາກ, ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າມັນຈະຖືກເຊື່ອງໄວ້ທັງໝົດ ຫຼື ຢູ່ນອກສາຍຕາຂອງກ້ອງກໍຕາມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:207
msgid "Screenshot of an example of a hidden Node for an effect"
msgstr "ພາບໜ້າຈໍຕົວຢ່າງຂອງໂນດທີ່ຖືກເຊື່ອງໄວ້ສຳລັບເອັບເຟັກ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:211
msgid ""
"Hidden bullet node attached to the player in one of the demo projects. This "
"helps the engine precompile the effect's pipelines ahead of time."
msgstr ""
"ໂນດລູກປືນທີ່ຖືກເຊື່ອງໄວ້ເຊິ່ງຕິດຢູ່ກັບຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນໃນໜຶ່ງໃນໂປຣເຈັກຕົວຢ່າງ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ເອນຈິນ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍຂອງເ"
"ອັບເຟັກໄວ້ລ່ວງໜ້າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:214
msgid ""
"If you're aware of any effects that are added to the scene dynamically "
"during gameplay and are seeing sudden increases on the compilations monitor "
"when these effects show up, a workaround is to attach a hidden version of "
"the effect somewhere that is guaranteed to show up."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າທ່ານຮູ້ວ່າມີເອັບເຟັກໃດທີ່ຖືກເພີ່ມເຂົ້າໃນສາກແບບໄດນາມິກລະຫວ່າງການຫຼິ້ນ ແລະ ເຫັນການເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນຢ່າງກະທັນຫັນໃ"
"ນຕົວຕິດຕາມການ Compile ເມື່ອເອັບເຟັກເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນປະກົດຂຶ້ນ, ວິທີແກ້ໄຂຄືການແນບເອັບເຟັກເວີຊັນທີ່ຖືກເຊື່ອງໄວ້ໃນບ່"
"ອນໃດບ່ອນໜຶ່ງທີ່ໝັ້ນໃຈວ່າມັນຈະປະກົດຂຶ້ນແນ່ນອນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:219
msgid ""
"For example, if the player character is able to cause some sort of "
"explosion, you can attach the effect as a child of the player as an "
"invisible node. Make sure to disable the script attached to the hidden node "
"or to hide any other nodes that could cause issues, which can be done by "
"enabling **Editable Children** on the node."
msgstr ""
"ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ, ຖ້າຕົວລະຄອນຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນສາມາດເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດການລະເບີດບາງຢ່າງ, ທ່ານສາມາດແນບເອັບເຟັກນັ້ນເປັນລູກ "
"(Child) ຂອງຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນໃນຮູບແບບໂນດທີ່ເບິ່ງບໍ່ເຫັນ. ໃຫ້ໝັ້ນໃຈວ່າໄດ້ປິດການເຮັດວຽກຂອງສະຄຣິບທີ່ຕິດຢູ່ກັບໂນດທີ່ເຊື່ອງ"
"ໄວ້ ຫຼື ເຊື່ອງໂນດອື່ນໆ ທີ່ອາດເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດບັນຫາ, ເຊິ່ງສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ໂດຍການເປີດໃຊ້ **Editable "
"Children** ໃນໂນດນັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:228
msgid "Shader baker"
msgstr "Shader baker (ຕົວອົບເຊດເດີ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:230
msgid ""
"Since Godot 4.5, you can choose to bake shaders on export to improve initial "
"startup time. This will generally not resolve existing stutters, but it will "
"reduce the time it takes to load the game for the first time. This is "
"especially the case when using Direct3D 12 or Metal, which have "
"significantly slower initial shader compilation times than Vulkan due to the "
"conversion step required. Godot's own shaders use GLSL and SPIR-V, but "
"Direct3D 12 and Metal use different formats."
msgstr ""
"ຕັ້ງແຕ່ Godot 4.5, ທ່ານສາມາດເລືອກທີ່ຈັກ bake shader ໃນເວລາ export ເພື່ອປັບປຸງເວລາເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ "
"(Startup time). ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປແລ້ວສິ່ງນີ້ຈະບໍ່ແກ້ໄຂອາການກະຕຸກທີ່ມີຢູ່, ແຕ່ມັນຈະຫຼຸດເວລາທີ່ໃຊ້ໃນການໂຫຼດເກມເ"
"ປັນຄັ້ງທຳອິດ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະເຫັນຜົນຊັດເຈນເມື່ອໃຊ້ Direct3D 12 ຫຼື Metal, ເຊິ່ງມີເວລາ Compile shader ເ"
"ບື້ອງຕົ້ນຊ້າກວ່າ Vulkan ຢ່າງຫຼວງຫຼາຍຍ້ອນຂັ້ນຕອນການແປງທີ່ຈຳເປັນ. Shader ຂອງ Godot ເອງໃຊ້ GLSL "
"ແລະ SPIR-V, ແຕ່ Direct3D 12 ແລະ Metal ໃຊ້ຮູບແບບທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:240
msgid ""
"The shader baker can only bake the source into the intermediate format (SPIR-"
"V for Vulkan, DXIL for Direct3D 12, MIL for Metal). It cannot bake the "
"intermediate format into the final pipeline, as this is dependent on the GPU "
"driver and the hardware."
msgstr ""
"Shader baker ສາມາດ bake ຊອດໂຄດໃຫ້ເປັນຮູບແບບລະຫວ່າງກາງເທົ່ານັ້ນ (SPIR-V ສຳລັບ Vulkan, "
"DXIL ສຳລັບ Direct3D 12, MIL ສຳລັບ Metal). ມັນບໍ່ສາມາດ bake ຮູບແບບລະຫວ່າງກາງໃຫ້ເປັນໄປ້ລາ"
"ຍສຸດທ້າຍໄດ້, ເພາະສິ່ງນີ້ຂຶ້ນຢູ່ກັບໄດຣເວີຂອງ GPU ແລະ ຮາດແວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:245
msgid ""
"The shader baker is not a replacement for pipeline precompilation, but it "
"aims to complement it."
msgstr ""
"Shader baker ບໍ່ແມ່ນສິ່ງທີ່ຈະມາປ່ຽນແທນການ Compile ໄປ້ລາຍລ່ວງໜ້າ, ແຕ່ມັນມີຈຸດປະສົງເພື່ອມາເສີມສ້າງກ"
"ານເຮັດວຽກຮ່ວມກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:248
msgid ""
"When enabled, the shader baker will bundle compiled shader code into the "
"PCK, which results in the shader compilation step being skipped entirely. "
"The downside is that exporting will take slightly longer. The PCK file will "
"be larger by a few megabytes."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອເປີດໃຊ້ງານ, shader baker ຈະລວມໂຄດ shader ທີ່ Compile ແລ້ວເຂົ້າໃນ PCK, ເຊິ່ງສົ່ງຜົນໃຫ້ຂັ້ນ"
"ຕອນການ Compile shader ຖືກຂ້າມໄປທັງໝົດ. ຂໍ້ເສຍຄືການ export ຈະໃຊ້ເວລາດົນຂຶ້ນເລັກນ້ອຍ ແລະ ໄຟ"
"ລ໌ PCK ຈະມີຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ຂຶ້ນປະມານບໍ່ເທົ່າໃດເມກະໄບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:253
msgid ""
"The shader baker is disabled by default, but you can enable it in each "
"export preset in the Export dialog by ticking the :ui:`Shader Baker > "
"Enabled` export option."
msgstr ""
"Shader baker ຖືກປິດໄວ້ໂດຍຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ແຕ່ທ່ານສາມາດເປີດໃຊ້ມັນໄດ້ໃນແຕ່ລະ export preset ໃນໜ້າຕ່າ"
"ງ Export ໂດຍການຕິກທີ່ຕົວເລືອກ :ui:`Shader Baker > Enabled`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:257
msgid ""
"Note that shader baking will only be able to export shaders for drivers "
"supported by the platform the editor is currently running on:"
msgstr ""
"ໝາຍເຫດວ່າການ bake shader ຈະສາມາດ export shader ໄດ້ສະເພາະໄດຣເວີທີ່ຮອງຮັບໂດຍແພລັດຟອມທີ່ "
"editor ກຳລັງເຮັດວຽກຢູ່ເທົ່ານັ້ນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:260
msgid ""
"The editor running on Windows can export shaders for Vulkan and Direct3D 12."
msgstr ""
"Editor ທີ່ເຮັດວຽກໃນ Windows ສາມາດ export shader ສຳລັບ Vulkan ແລະ Direct3D 12."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:261
msgid "The editor running on macOS can export shaders for Vulkan and Metal."
msgstr "Editor ທີ່ເຮັດວຽກໃນ macOS ສາມາດ export shader ສຳລັບ Vulkan ແລະ Metal."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:262
msgid "The editor running on Linux can export shaders for Vulkan only."
msgstr "Editor ທີ່ເຮັດວຽກໃນ Linux ສາມາດ export shader ສຳລັບ Vulkan ເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:263
msgid "The editor running on Android can export shaders for Vulkan only."
msgstr "Editor ທີ່ເຮັດວຽກໃນ Android ສາມາດ export shader ສຳລັບ Vulkan ເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:265
msgid ""
"The shader baker will only export shaders that match the ``rendering/"
"rendering_device/driver`` project setting for the target platform."
msgstr ""
"Shader baker ຈະ export ສະເພາະ shader ທີ່ກົງກັບການຕັ້ງຄ່າໂປຣເຈັກ ``rendering/"
"rendering_device/driver`` ສຳລັບແພລັດຟອມເປົ້າໝາຍເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:270
msgid ""
"The shader baker is only supported for the Forward+ and Mobile renderers. It "
"will have no effect if the project uses the Compatibility renderer, or for "
"users who make use of the Compatibility fallback due to their hardware not "
"supporting the Forward+ or Mobile renderer."
msgstr ""
"Shader baker ຮອງຮັບສະເພາະຕົວເຣັນເດີ Forward+ ແລະ Mobile ເທົ່ານັ້ນ. ມັນຈະບໍ່ມີຜົນຫຍັງຖ້າໂປຣເຈັ"
"ກໃຊ້ຕົວເຣັນເດີ Compatibility, ຫຼື ສຳລັບຜູ້ໃຊ້ທີ່ຕ້ອງໃຊ້ Compatibility fallback ຍ້ອນຮາດແວບໍ່ຮອງ"
"ຮັບຕົວເຣັນເດີ Forward+ ຫຼື Mobile."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:275
msgid ""
"This also means the shader baker is not supported on the web platform, as "
"the web platform only supports the Compatibility renderer."
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ຍັງໝາຍຄວາມວ່າ shader baker ຈະບໍ່ຮອງຮັບໃນແພລັດຟອມເວັບ, ເນື່ອງຈາກແພລັດຟອມເວັບຮອງຮັບພຽງແຕ່ຕົວ"
"ສະແດງຜົນແບບ Compatibility ເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.rst:278
msgid ""
"Additionally, the shader baker is not supported when exporting a project "
"using the ``--headless`` :ref:`command line argument "
"<doc_command_line_tutorial>`, as Godot cannot access the GPU when running in "
"headless mode."
msgstr ""
"ນອກຈາກນີ້, shader baker ຍັງບໍ່ຮອງຮັບເມື່ອສົ່ງອອກໂປຣເຈັກໂດຍໃຊ້ argument ``--headless`` ໃນ "
":ref:`command line <doc_command_line_tutorial>`, ເນື່ອງຈາກ Godot ບໍ່ສາມາດເຂົ້າເຖິງ "
"GPU ໄດ້ເມື່ອເຮັດວຽກໃນໂໝດ headless."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:-1
msgid "optimization"
msgstr "ການເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:7
msgid "Optimizing 3D performance"
msgstr "ການເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບໃຫ້ກັບ 3D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:10
msgid "Culling"
msgstr "ການຄັດອອກ (Culling)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:12
msgid ""
"Godot will automatically perform view frustum culling in order to prevent "
"rendering objects that are outside the viewport. This works well for games "
"that take place in a small area, however things can quickly become "
"problematic in larger levels."
msgstr ""
"Godot ຈະເຮັດການຄັດອອກຕາມຂອບເຂດການເບິ່ງ (view frustum culling) ໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ ເພື່ອປ້ອງກັ"
"ນການປະມວນຜົນວັດຖຸທີ່ຢູ່ນອກ viewport. ສິ່ງນີ້ເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ດີສຳລັບເກມທີ່ມີພື້ນທີ່ຂະໜາດນ້ອຍ, ແຕ່ມັນອາດຈະກາຍເ"
"ປັນບັນຫາໄດ້ໃນດ່ານທີ່ມີຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:20
msgid ""
"Walking around a town for example, you may only be able to see a few "
"buildings in the street you are in, as well as the sky and a few birds "
"flying overhead. As far as a naive renderer is concerned however, you can "
"still see the entire town. It won't just render the buildings in front of "
"you, it will render the street behind that, with the people on that street, "
"the buildings behind that. You quickly end up in situations where you are "
"attempting to render 10× or 100× more than what is visible."
msgstr ""
"ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ: ການຍ່າງອ້ອມເມືອງ, ເຈົ້າອາດຈະເຫັນພຽງແຕ່ຕຶກບໍ່ເທົ່າໃດຫຼັງໃນຖະໜົນທີ່ເຈົ້າຢູ່, ລວມທັງທ້ອງຟ້າ ແລ"
"ະ ນົກສອງສາມໂຕທີ່ບິນຢູ່ເທິງຫົວ. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ສຳລັບຕົວສະແດງຜົນແບບທົ່ວໄປ, ມັນຍັງຄິດວ່າເຈົ້າເຫັນເມືອງທັງເ"
"ມືອງ. ມັນຈະບໍ່ພຽງແຕ່ປະມວນຜົນຕຶກທີ່ຢູ່ຕໍ່ໜ້າເຈົ້າເທົ່ານັ້ນ, ແຕ່ມັນຈະປະມວນຜົນຖະໜົນທີ່ຢູ່ທາງຫຼັງ, ຜູ້ຄົນໃນຖະໜົນນັ້ນ "
"ແລະ ຕຶກທີ່ຢູ່ຖັດໄປອີກ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເຈົ້າຕົກຢູ່ໃນສະຖານະການທີ່ພະຍາຍາມປະມວນຜົນຫຼາຍກວ່າສິ່ງທີ່ເບິ່ງເຫັນແທ້ໆເ"
"ຖິງ 10 ເທົ່າ ຫຼື 100 ເທົ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:28
msgid ""
"Things aren't quite as bad as they seem, because the Z-buffer usually allows "
"the GPU to only fully shade the objects that are at the front. This is "
"called *depth prepass* and is enabled by default in Godot when using the "
"Forward+ or Compatibility rendering methods. However, unneeded objects are "
"still reducing performance."
msgstr ""
"ແຕ່ມັນກໍບໍ່ໄດ້ຮ້າຍແຮງຄືກັບທີ່ຄິດ, ເພາະວ່າ Z-buffer ມັກຈະຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ GPU ໃສ່ເງົາໃຫ້ກັບວັດຖຸທີ່ຢູ່ທາງໜ້າເທົ່ານັ້"
"ນ. ສິ່ງນີ້ເອີ້ນວ່າ *depth prepass* ແລະ ມັນຖືກເປີດໃຊ້ໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດໃນ Godot ເມື່ອໃຊ້ວິທີການສະແດງຜົ"
"ນແບບ Forward+ ຫຼື Compatibility. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ວັດຖຸທີ່ບໍ່ຈຳເປັນກໍຍັງເຮັດໃຫ້ປະສິດທິພາບຫຼຸດລົງຢູ່ດີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:34
msgid ""
"One way we can potentially reduce the amount to be rendered is to **take "
"advantage of occlusion**. Godot offers an approach to occlusion culling "
"using occluder nodes. See :ref:`doc_occlusion_culling` for instructions on "
"setting up occlusion culling in your scene."
msgstr ""
"ວິທີໜຶ່ງທີ່ພວກເຮົາສາມາດຫຼຸດຈຳນວນການປະມວນຜົນໄດ້ຄື **ການໃຊ້ປະໂຫຍດຈາກການບັງ (occlusion)**. "
"Godot ມີວິທີການຄັດອອກວັດຖຸທີ່ຖືກບັງ (occlusion culling) ໂດຍໃຊ້ occluder nodes. ເບິ່ງ "
":ref:`doc_occlusion_culling` ສຳລັບວິທີການຕັ້ງຄ່າ occlusion culling ໃນສາກຂອງທ່ານ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:41
msgid ""
"In some cases, you may have to adapt your level design to add more occlusion "
"opportunities. For example, you may have to add more walls to prevent the "
"player from seeing too far away, which would decrease performance due to the "
"lost opportunities for occlusion culling."
msgstr ""
"ໃນບາງກໍລະນີ, ເຈົ້າອາດຈະຕ້ອງປັບປ່ຽນການອອກແບບດ່ານເພື່ອເພີ່ມໂອກາດໃນການບັງວັດຖຸ. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ: ເຈົ້າອາ"
"ດຈະຕ້ອງເພີ່ມກຳແພງຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນເພື່ອປ້ອງກັນບໍ່ໃຫ້ຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນເບິ່ງເຫັນໄກເກີນໄປ, ເພາະການເບິ່ງເຫັນໄກຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ປະສິດທິພາ"
"ບຫຼຸດລົງຍ້ອນບໍ່ມີໂອກາດໃນການເຮັດ occlusion culling."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:47
msgid "Transparent objects"
msgstr "ວັດຖຸທີ່ມີຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:49
msgid ""
"Godot sorts objects by :ref:`Material <class_Material>` and :ref:`Shader "
"<class_Shader>` to improve performance. This, however, can not be done with "
"transparent objects. Transparent objects are rendered from back to front to "
"make blending with what is behind work. As a result, **try to use as few "
"transparent objects as possible**. If an object has a small section with "
"transparency, try to make that section a separate surface with its own "
"material."
msgstr ""
"Godot ຈະຈັດລຽງວັດຖຸຕາມ :ref:`Material <class_Material>` ແລະ :ref:`Shader "
"<class_Shader>` ເພື່ອເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບ. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ສິ່ງນີ້ບໍ່ສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ກັບວັດຖຸທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສ. ວັດຖຸທີ່ໂປ່ງ"
"ໃສຈະຖືກປະມວນຜົນຈາກທາງຫຼັງມາທາງໜ້າເພື່ອໃຫ້ການປະສົມ (blending) ກັບສິ່ງທີ່ຢູ່ທາງຫຼັງເຮັດວຽກໄດ້. ດັ່ງນັ້"
"ນ, **ພະຍາຍາມໃຊ້ວັດຖຸໂປ່ງໃສໃຫ້ໜ້ອຍທີ່ສຸດ**. ຖ້າວັດຖຸໃດໜຶ່ງມີສ່ວນນ້ອຍໆທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສ, ໃຫ້ລອງແຍກສ່ວນນັ້ນອອກເປັ"
"ນ surface ຕ່າງຫາກທີ່ມີ material ຂອງມັນເອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:57
msgid ""
"For more information, see the :ref:`GPU optimizations "
"<doc_gpu_optimization>` doc."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມ, ເບິ່ງເອກະສານ :ref:`GPU optimizations <doc_gpu_optimization>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:61
msgid "Level of detail (LOD)"
msgstr "ລະດັບລາຍລະອຽດ (LOD)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:63
msgid ""
"In some situations, particularly at a distance, it can be a good idea to "
"**replace complex geometry with simpler versions**. The end user will "
"probably not be able to see much difference. Consider looking at a large "
"number of trees in the far distance. There are several strategies for "
"replacing models at varying distance. You could use lower poly models, or "
"use transparency to simulate more complex geometry."
msgstr ""
"ໃນບາງສະຖານະການ, ໂດຍສະເພາະໃນໄລຍະໄກ, ມັນເປັນການດີທີ່ຈະ **ປ່ຽນຮູບຊົງທີ່ຊັບຊ້ອນດ້ວຍເວີຊັນທີ່ງ່າຍກວ່"
"າ**. ຜູ້ໃຊ້ທົ່ວໄປອາດຈະບໍ່ເຫັນຄວາມແຕກຕ່າງຫຼາຍປານໃດ. ລອງນຶກເຖິງການເບິ່ງຕົ້ນໄມ້ຈຳນວນຫຼວງຫຼາຍໃນໄລຍະໄ"
"ກ. ມີຫຼາຍກົນລະຍຸດໃນການປ່ຽນໂມເດວໃນໄລຍະທາງທີ່ຕ່າງກັນ. ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ໂມເດວທີ່ມີ poly ຕ່ຳ ຫຼື ໃຊ້ຄວາມ"
"ໂປ່ງໃສເພື່ອຈຳລອງຮູບຊົງທີ່ຊັບຊ້ອນກໍໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:70
msgid "Godot 4 offers several ways to control level of detail:"
msgstr "Godot 4 ມີຫຼາຍວິທີໃນການຄວບຄຸມລະດັບລາຍລະອຽດ (LOD):"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:72
msgid "An automatic approach on mesh import using :ref:`doc_mesh_lod`."
msgstr "ວິທີການແບບອັດຕະໂນມັດເມື່ອນຳເຂົ້າ mesh ໂດຍໃຊ້ :ref:`doc_mesh_lod`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:73
msgid ""
"A manual approach configured in the 3D node "
"using :ref:`doc_visibility_ranges`."
msgstr "ວິທີການແບບຕັ້ງຄ່າເອງໃນ 3D node ໂດຍໃຊ້ :ref:`doc_visibility_ranges`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:74
msgid ""
":ref:`Decals <doc_using_decals>` and :ref:`lights <doc_lights_and_shadows>` "
"can also benefit from level of detail using their respective **Distance "
"Fade** properties."
msgstr ""
":ref:`Decals <doc_using_decals>` ແລະ :ref:`lights <doc_lights_and_shadows>` ຍັ"
"ງສາມາດໃຊ້ປະໂຫຍດຈາກ LOD ໄດ້ໂດຍໃຊ້ຄຸນສົມບັດ **Distance Fade** ຂອງພວກມັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:78
msgid ""
"While they can be used independently, these approaches are most effective "
"when used together. For example, you can set up visibility ranges to hide "
"particle effects that are too far away from the player to notice. At the "
"same time, you can rely on mesh LOD to make the particle effect's meshes "
"rendered with less detail at a distance."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າພວກມັນສາມາດໃຊ້ແຍກກັນໄດ້, ແຕ່ວິທີການເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຈະມີປະສິດທິພາບທີ່ສຸດເມື່ອໃຊ້ຮ່ວມກັນ. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ: ເ"
"ຈົ້າສາມາດຕັ້ງຄ່າ visibility ranges ເພື່ອເຊື່ອງ particle effects ທີ່ຢູ່ໄກເກີນໄປຈົນຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນບໍ່ສັງເກດເຫັ"
"ນ. ໃນຂະນະດຽວກັນ, ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ mesh LOD ເພື່ອໃຫ້ mesh ຂອງ particle effect ປະມວນຜົນດ້ວຍ"
"ລາຍລະອຽດທີ່ໜ້ອຍລົງໃນໄລຍະໄກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:84
msgid ""
"Visibility ranges are also a good way to set up *impostors* for distant "
"geometry (see below)."
msgstr ""
"Visibility ranges ຍັງເປັນວິທີທີ່ດີໃນການຕັ້ງຄ່າ *impostors* ສຳລັບຮູບຊົງທີ່ຢູ່ໄກ (ເບິ່ງດ້ານລຸ່ມ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:88
msgid "Billboards and imposters"
msgstr "ບິວບອດ (Billboards) ແລະ ອິມໂພສເຕີ (Imposters)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:90
msgid ""
"The simplest version of using transparency to deal with LOD is billboards. "
"For example, you can use a single transparent quad to represent a tree at "
"distance. This can be very cheap to render, unless of course, there are many "
"trees in front of each other. In this case, transparency may start eating "
"into fill rate (for more information on fill rate, "
"see :ref:`doc_gpu_optimization`)."
msgstr ""
"ວິທີທີ່ງ່າຍທີ່ສຸດໃນການໃຊ້ຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສເພື່ອຈັດການກັບ LOD ຄື billboards. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ: ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ແຜ່ນ"
"ສີ່ຫຼ່ຽມໂປ່ງໃສ (quad) ພຽງແຜ່ນດຽວເພື່ອແທນຕົ້ນໄມ້ໃນໄລຍະໄກ. ສິ່ງນີ້ປະມວນຜົນໄດ້ໄວຫຼາຍ, ເວັ້ນເສຍແຕ່ວ່າມີຕົ້"
"ນໄມ້ຫຼາຍຕົ້ນຊ້ອນກັນ. ໃນກໍລະນີນັ້ນ, ຄວາມໂປ່ງໃສອາດຈະເລີ່ມກິນ fill rate (ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບ "
"fill rate, ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_gpu_optimization`)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:96
msgid ""
"An alternative is to render not just one tree, but a number of trees "
"together as a group. This can be especially effective if you can see an area "
"but cannot physically approach it in a game."
msgstr ""
"ອີກທາງເລືອກໜຶ່ງຄືການປະມວນຜົນບໍ່ແມ່ນແຕ່ຕົ້ນໄມ້ຕົ້ນດຽວ, ແຕ່ເປັນກຸ່ມຕົ້ນໄມ້ລວມກັນ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະມີປະສິດທິພາບຫຼາຍຖ້າເ"
"ຈົ້າສາມາດເຫັນພື້ນທີ່ໃດໜຶ່ງໄດ້ແຕ່ບໍ່ສາມາດເຂົ້າໄປໃກ້ມັນໄດ້ໃນເກມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:100
msgid ""
"You can make imposters by pre-rendering views of an object at different "
"angles. Or you can even go one step further, and periodically re-render a "
"view of an object onto a texture to be used as an imposter. At a distance, "
"you need to move the viewer a considerable distance for the angle of view to "
"change significantly. This can be complex to get working, but may be worth "
"it depending on the type of project you are making."
msgstr ""
"ເຈົ້າສາມາດສ້າງ imposters ໄດ້ໂດຍການປະມວນຜົນມຸມມອງຂອງວັດຖຸໃນມຸມຕ່າງໆໄວ້ລ່ວງໜ້າ. ຫຼື ເຈົ້າສາມາດເຮັ"
"ດໃຫ້ມັນກ້າວໄປອີກຂັ້ນໂດຍການປະມວນຜົນມຸມມອງຂອງວັດຖຸໃໝ່ເປັນໄລຍະໆລົງເທິງ texture ເພື່ອໃຊ້ເປັນ "
"imposter. ໃນໄລຍະໄກ, ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງເຄື່ອນທີ່ຜູ້ເບິ່ງໄປໃນໄລຍະທີ່ໄກພໍສົມຄວນເພື່ອໃຫ້ມຸມມອງປ່ຽນແປງຢ່າງຊັດເຈ"
"ນ. ສິ່ງນີ້ອາດຈະມີຄວາມຊັບຊ້ອນໃນການເຮັດໃຫ້ເຮັດວຽກໄດ້, ແຕ່ມັນອາດຈະຄຸ້ມຄ່າຂຶ້ນຢູ່ກັບປະເພດຂອງໂປຣເຈັກທີ່ເຈົ້າ"
"ກຳລັງສ້າງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:108
msgid "Use automatic instancing"
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ automatic instancing"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:110
msgid ""
"*This is only implemented in the Forward+ renderer, not Mobile or "
"Compatibility.*"
msgstr ""
"*ສິ່ງນີ້ມີໃຫ້ໃຊ້ສະເພາະໃນ Forward+ renderer ເທົ່ານັ້ນ, ບໍ່ມີໃນ Mobile ຫຼື Compatibility.*"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:112
msgid ""
"If you have many identical objects in your scene, you can use automatic "
"instancing to reduce the number of draw calls. This automatically happens "
"for MeshInstance3D nodes that use the same mesh and material: no manual "
"setup is required."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເຈົ້າມີວັດຖຸທີ່ຄືກັນຫຼາຍໆຢ່າງໃນສາກ, ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ automatic instancing ເພື່ອຫຼຸດຈຳນວນ draw "
"calls. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະເກີດຂຶ້ນໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດສຳລັບ MeshInstance3D nodes ທີ່ໃຊ້ mesh ແລະ material ອັ"
"ນດຽວກັນ: ບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງຕັ້ງຄ່າໃດໆ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:116
msgid ""
"For automatic instancing to be effective, the material must be opaque or "
"alpha-tested (alpha scissor or alpha hash). Alpha-blended or depth pre-pass "
"materials are never instanced this way. Instead, you must use MultiMesh as "
"described below."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອໃຫ້ automatic instancing ມີປະສິດທິພາບ, material ຕ້ອງເປັນແບບ opaque (ທຶບແສງ) ຫຼື "
"alpha-tested (alpha scissor ຫຼື alpha hash). ສ່ວນ material ແບບ Alpha-blended ຫຼື "
"depth pre-pass ຈະບໍ່ຖືກເຮັດ instancing ດ້ວຍວິທີນີ້. ແຕ່ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງໃຊ້ MultiMesh ຕາມທີ່ໄດ້ອະທິບາຍໄ"
"ວ້ດ້ານລຸ່ມແທນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:122
msgid "Use manual instancing (MultiMesh)"
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ manual instancing (MultiMesh)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:124
msgid ""
"If several identical objects have to be drawn in the same place or nearby, "
"try using :ref:`MultiMesh <class_MultiMesh>` instead. MultiMesh allows the "
"drawing of many thousands of objects at very little performance cost, making "
"it ideal for flocks, grass, particles, and anything else where you have "
"thousands of identical objects."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າຕ້ອງແຕ້ມວັດຖຸທີ່ຄືກັນຫຼາຍໆຢ່າງໃນບ່ອນດຽວກັນ ຫຼື ໃກ້ຄຽງກັນ, ໃຫ້ລອງໃຊ້ :ref:`MultiMesh "
"<class_MultiMesh>` ແທນ. MultiMesh ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສາມາດແຕ້ມວັດຖຸໄດ້ຫຼາຍພັນຢ່າງໂດຍໃຊ້ຊັບພະຍາກອນໜ້ອຍ"
"ຫຼາຍ, ເຊິ່ງເໝາະສຳລັບ ຝູງສັດ, ຫຍ້າ, particles ແລະ ສິ່ງອື່ນໆທີ່ມີວັດຖຸຄືກັນເປັນພັນໆຢ່າງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:130
msgid ""
"See also the :ref:`Using MultiMesh <doc_using_multimesh>` documentation."
msgstr "ເບິ່ງເອກະສານ :ref:`Using MultiMesh <doc_using_multimesh>` ເພີ່ມເຕີມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:133
msgid "Bake lighting"
msgstr "ການອົບແສງ (Bake lighting)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:135
msgid ""
"Lighting objects is one of the most costly rendering operations. Realtime "
"lighting, shadows (especially multiple lights), and :ref:`global "
"illumination <doc_introduction_to_global_illumination>` are especially "
"expensive. They may simply be too much for lower power mobile devices to "
"handle."
msgstr ""
"ການປະມວນຜົນແສງໃຫ້ກັບວັດຖຸເປັນວຽກທີ່ໜັກທີ່ສຸດຢ່າງໜຶ່ງ. ແສງແບບ Realtime, ເງົາ (ໂດຍສະເພາະແສງຫຼາຍໆ"
"ດວງ), ແລະ :ref:`global illumination <doc_introduction_to_global_illumination>"
"` ແມ່ນມີລາຄາທີ່ຕ້ອງຈ່າຍສູງ (expensive). ພວກມັນອາດຈະໜັກເກີນໄປສຳລັບອຸປະກອນມືຖືທີ່ມີປະສິດທິພາບຕ່ຳ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:140
msgid ""
"**Consider using baked lighting**, especially for mobile. This can look "
"fantastic, but has the downside that it will not be dynamic. Sometimes, this "
"is a tradeoff worth making."
msgstr ""
"**ໃຫ້ພິຈາລະນາໃຊ້ baked lighting**, ໂດຍສະເພາະສຳລັບມືຖື. ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດເຮັດໃຫ້ພາບເບິ່ງສວຍງາມຫຼາ"
"ຍ, ແຕ່ມີຂໍ້ເສຍຄືມັນຈະບໍ່ເປັນແບບ dynamic (ບໍ່ປ່ຽນແປງຕາມການເຄື່ອນໄຫວ). ບາງຄັ້ງ, ນີ້ກໍເປັນການແລກປ່ຽນທີ່"
"ຄຸ້ມຄ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:144
msgid ""
"See :ref:`doc_using_lightmap_gi` for instructions on using baked lightmaps. "
"For best performance, you should set lights' bake mode to **Static** as "
"opposed to the default **Dynamic**, as this will skip real-time lighting on "
"meshes that have baked lighting."
msgstr ""
"ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_using_lightmap_gi` ສຳລັບວິທີການໃຊ້ baked lightmaps. ເພື່ອປະສິດທິພາບສູງສຸ"
"ດ, ເຈົ້າຄວນຕັ້ງຄ່າ bake mode ຂອງແສງໃຫ້ເປັນ **Static** ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນ **Dynamic** (ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້"
"ນ), ເພາະສິ່ງນີ້ຈະຂ້າມການປະມວນຜົນແສງແບບ real-time ໃຫ້ກັບ meshes ທີ່ໄດ້ຮັບການອົບແສງໄວ້ແລ້ວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:149
msgid ""
"The downside of lights with the **Static** bake mode is that they can't cast "
"shadows onto meshes with baked lighting. This can make scenes with outdoor "
"environments and dynamic objects look flat. A good balance between "
"performance and quality is to keep **Dynamic** for "
"the :ref:`class_DirectionalLight3D` node, and use **Static** for most (if "
"not all) omni and spot lights."
msgstr ""
"ຂໍ້ເສຍຂອງແສງທີ່ມີ bake mode ແບບ **Static** ຄືພວກມັນບໍ່ສາມາດສ້າງເງົາລົງເທິງ meshes ທີ່ມີ "
"baked lighting ໄດ້. ສິ່ງນີ້ອາດຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ສາກທີ່ເປັນສະພາບແວດລ້ອມກາງແຈ້ງ ແລະ ວັດຖຸທີ່ເຄື່ອນໄຫວເບິ່ງແ"
"ປ (flat). ຄວາມສົມດຸນທີ່ດີລະຫວ່າງປະສິດທິພາບ ແລະ ຄຸນນະພາບຄືການໃຊ້ **Dynamic** ສຳລັບ "
":ref:`class_DirectionalLight3D` node, ແລະ ໃຊ້ **Static** ສຳລັບ omni ແລະ spot "
"lights ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ (ຫຼື ທັງໝົດ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:156
msgid "Animation and skinning"
msgstr "ແອນິເມຊັນ (Animation) ແລະ ສະກິນນິງ (Skinning)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:158
msgid ""
"Animation and vertex animation such as skinning and morphing can be very "
"expensive on some platforms. You may need to lower the polycount "
"considerably for animated models, or limit the number of them on screen at "
"any given time. You can also reduce the animation rate for distant or "
"occluded meshes, or pause the animation entirely if the player is unlikely "
"to notice the animation being stopped."
msgstr ""
"ແອນິເມຊັນ ແລະ ເວີເທັກແອນິເມຊັນ (vertex animation) ເຊັ່ນ: skinning ແລະ morphing ສາມາດກິ"
"ນຊັບພະຍາກອນຫຼາຍໃນບາງແພລັດຟອມ. ເຈົ້າອາດຈະຕ້ອງຫຼຸດຈຳນວນ poly ລົງຫຼາຍພໍສົມຄວນສຳລັບໂມເດວທີ່ມີແອນິເ"
"ມຊັນ, ຫຼື ຈຳກັດຈຳນວນຂອງພວກມັນໃນໜ້າຈໍ. ເຈົ້າຍັງສາມາດຫຼຸດອັດຕາການຫຼິ້ນແອນິເມຊັນສຳລັບ meshes ທີ່ຢູ່ໄກ "
"ຫຼື ຖືກບັງຢູ່, ຫຼື ຢຸດແອນິເມຊັນໄວ້ເລີຍຖ້າຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນບໍ່ສັງເກດເຫັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:165
msgid ""
"The :ref:`class_VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D` "
"and :ref:`class_VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D` nodes can be useful for this "
"purpose."
msgstr ""
"ໂນດ :ref:class_VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D ແລະ "
":ref:class_VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D ສາມາດເປັນປະໂຫຍດສຳລັບຈຸດປະສົງນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:169
msgid "Large worlds"
msgstr "ໂລກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:171
msgid ""
"If you are making large worlds, there are different considerations than what "
"you may be familiar with from smaller games."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເຈົ້າກຳລັງສ້າງໂລກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່, ຈະມີຂໍ້ຄວນພິຈາລະນາທີ່ຕ່າງຈາກເກມຂະໜາດນ້ອຍທີ່ເຈົ້າອາດຈະຄຸ້ນເຄີຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:174
msgid ""
"Large worlds may need to be built in tiles that can be loaded on demand as "
"you move around the world. This can prevent memory use from getting out of "
"hand, and also limit the processing needed to the local area."
msgstr ""
"ໂລກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ອາດຈະຕ້ອງຖືກສ້າງຂຶ້ນເປັນແຜ່ນ (tiles) ທີ່ສາມາດໂຫຼດໄດ້ຕາມຄວາມຕ້ອງການໃນຂະນະທີ່ເຈົ້າເຄື່"
"ອນທີ່ໄປທົ່ວໂລກ. ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດປ້ອງກັນບໍ່ໃຫ້ການໃຊ້ໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳ (memory) ເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນຫຼາຍເກີນໄປ, ແລະ ຍັງຈຳກັດ"
"ການປະມວນຜົນໃຫ້ຢູ່ສະເພາະພື້ນທີ່ໃກ້ຄຽງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/optimizing_3d_performance.rst:178
msgid ""
"There may also be rendering and physics glitches due to floating point error "
"in large worlds. This can be resolved "
"using :ref:`doc_large_world_coordinates`. If using large world coordinates "
"is not an option, you may be able to use techniques such as orienting the "
"world around the player (rather than the other way around), or shifting the "
"origin periodically to keep things centred around ``Vector3(0, 0, 0)``."
msgstr ""
"ອາດຈະມີຂໍ້ຜິດພາດໃນການສະແດງຜົນ ແລະ ຟີຊິກເນື່ອງຈາກ floating point error ໃນໂລກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່. ສິ່"
"ງນີ້ສາມາດແກ້ໄຂໄດ້ໂດຍໃຊ້ :ref:`doc_large_world_coordinates`. ຖ້າການໃຊ້ large world "
"coordinates ບໍ່ແມ່ນທາງເລືອກ, ເຈົ້າອາດຈະໃຊ້ເຕັກນິກຕ່າງໆ ເຊັ່ນ: ການປັບໃຫ້ໂລກເຄື່ອນທີ່ອ້ອມຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນ (ແທນທີ່"
"ຈະໃຫ້ຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນເຄື່ອນທີ່), ຫຼື ການຍ້າຍຈຸດກຳເນີດ (origin) ເປັນໄລຍະໆ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ສິ່ງຕ່າງໆຢູ່ໃກ້ກັບຈຸດ ``Vector3"
"(0, 0, 0)`` ສະເໝີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/index.rst:4
msgid "Animating thousands of objects"
msgstr "ການເຮັດແອນິເມຊັນໃຫ້ກັບວັດຖຸຫຼາຍພັນຢ່າງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:6
msgid "Animating thousands of fish with MultiMeshInstance3D"
msgstr "ການເຮັດແອນິເມຊັນໃຫ້ກັບປາຫຼາຍພັນໂຕດ້ວຍ MultiMeshInstance3D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:8
msgid ""
"This tutorial explores a technique used in the game `ABZU <https://"
"www.gdcvault.com/play/1024409/Creating-the-Art-of-ABZ>`_ for rendering and "
"animating thousands of fish using vertex animation and static mesh "
"instancing."
msgstr ""
"ບົດຮຽນນີ້ຈະສຳຫຼວດເຕັກນິກທີ່ໃຊ້ໃນເກມ `ABZU <https://www.gdcvault.com/play/1024409/"
"Creating-the-Art-of-ABZ>`_ ສຳລັບການປະມວນຜົນ ແລະ ເຮັດແອນິເມຊັນໃຫ້ກັບປາຫຼາຍພັນໂຕໂດຍໃຊ້ "
"vertex animation ແລະ static mesh instancing."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:12
msgid ""
"In Godot, this can be accomplished with a custom :ref:`Shader "
"<class_Shader>` and a :ref:`MultiMeshInstance3D "
"<class_MultiMeshInstance3D>`. Using the following technique you can render "
"thousands of animated objects, even on low-end hardware."
msgstr ""
"ໃນ Godot, ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ດ້ວຍ :ref:`Shader <class_Shader>` ທີ່ຂຽນຂຶ້ນເອງ ແລະ "
":ref:`MultiMeshInstance3D <class_MultiMeshInstance3D>`. ໂດຍການໃຊ້ເຕັກນິກຕໍ່ໄປນີ້ ເຈົ້າ"
"ສາມາດປະມວນຜົນວັດຖຸທີ່ມີແອນິເມຊັນໄດ້ຫຼາຍພັນຢ່າງ, ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຈະຢູ່ໃນຮາດແວຣ໌ທີ່ມີປະສິດທິພາບຕ່ຳກໍຕາມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:16
msgid ""
"We will start by animating one fish. Then, we will see how to extend that "
"animation to thousands of fish."
msgstr ""
"ພວກເຮົາຈະເລີ່ມຕົ້ນດ້ວຍການເຮັດແອນິເມຊັນໃຫ້ກັບປາໂຕດຽວກ່ອນ. ຈາກນັ້ນ, ພວກເຮົາຈະເບິ່ງວິທີການຂະຫຍາຍແອນິ"
"ເມຊັນນັ້ນໄປສູ່ປາຫຼາຍພັນໂຕ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:20
msgid "Animating one Fish"
msgstr "ການເຮັດແອນິເມຊັນໃຫ້ກັບປາໂຕດຽວ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:22
msgid ""
"We will start with a single fish. Load your fish model into "
"a :ref:`MeshInstance3D <class_MeshInstance3D>` and add a "
"new :ref:`ShaderMaterial <class_ShaderMaterial>`."
msgstr ""
"ພວກເຮົາຈະເລີ່ມຕົ້ນດ້ວຍປາໂຕດຽວ. ໃຫ້ໂຫຼດໂມເດວປາຂອງທ່ານລົງໃນ :ref:`MeshInstance3D "
"<class_MeshInstance3D>` ແລະ ເພີ່ມ :ref:`ShaderMaterial <class_ShaderMaterial>` "
"ໃໝ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:25
msgid ""
"Here is the fish we will be using for the example images, you can use any "
"fish model you like."
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ຄືປາທີ່ພວກເຮົາຈະໃຊ້ໃນຮູບພາບຕົວຢ່າງ, ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ໂມເດວປາແບບໃດກໍໄດ້ທີ່ເຈົ້າມັກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:29
msgid ""
"The fish model in this tutorial is made by `QuaterniusDev <https://"
"quaternius.com>`_ and is shared with a creative commons license. CC0 1.0 "
"Universal (CC0 1.0) Public Domain Dedication https://creativecommons.org/"
"publicdomain/zero/1.0/"
msgstr ""
"ໂມເດວປາໃນບົດຮຽນນີ້ສ້າງໂດຍ `QuaterniusDev <https://quaternius.com>`_ ແລະ ຖືກແບ່ງປັນພາ"
"ຍໃຕ້ໃບອະນຸຍາດ creative commons. CC0 1.0 Universal (CC0 1.0) Public Domain "
"Dedication https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:33
msgid ""
"Typically, you would use bones and a :ref:`Skeleton3D <class_Skeleton3D>` to "
"animate objects. However, bones are animated on the CPU and so you end "
"having to calculate thousands of operations every frame and it becomes "
"impossible to have thousands of objects. Using vertex animation in a vertex "
"shader, you avoid using bones and can instead calculate the full animation "
"in a few lines of code and completely on the GPU."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍປົກກະຕິແລ້ວ, ເຈົ້າຈະໃຊ້ກະດູກ (bones) ແລະ :ref:`Skeleton3D <class_Skeleton3D>` ເພື່ອ"
"ເຮັດແອນິເມຊັນໃຫ້ກັບວັດຖຸ. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ກະດູກຈະຖືກປະມວນຜົນໃນ CPU ດັ່ງນັ້ນເຈົ້າຈຶ່ງຕ້ອງຄຳນວນການເຮັດວຽ"
"ກຫຼາຍພັນຢ່າງໃນທຸກໆເຟຣມ ເຊິ່ງເຮັດໃຫ້ມັນເປັນໄປບໍ່ໄດ້ທີ່ຈະມີວັດຖຸຫຼາຍພັນຢ່າງ. ໂດຍການໃຊ້ vertex "
"animation ໃນ vertex shader, ເຈົ້າສາມາດຫຼີກລ່ຽງການໃຊ້ກະດູກ ແລະ ສາມາດຄຳນວນແອນິເມຊັນທັງໝົດໄ"
"ດ້ໃນລະຫັດບໍ່ເທົ່າໃດແຖວ ແລະ ປະມວນຜົນໃນ GPU ທັງໝົດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:39
msgid "The animation will be made of four key motions:"
msgstr "ແອນິເມຊັນຈະປະກອບດ້ວຍ 4 ການເຄື່ອນໄຫວຫຼັກ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:41
msgid "A side to side motion"
msgstr "ການເຄື່ອນໄຫວຊ້າຍ-ຂວາ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:42
msgid "A pivot motion around the center of the fish"
msgstr "ການເຄື່ອນໄຫວແບບໝູນຮອບຈຸດສູນກາງຂອງປາ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:43
msgid "A panning wave motion"
msgstr "ການເຄື່ອນໄຫວແບບຄື້ນທີ່ແລ່ນຜ່ານ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:44
msgid "A panning twist motion"
msgstr "ການເຄື່ອນໄຫວແບບບິດທີ່ແລ່ນຜ່ານ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:46
msgid ""
"All the code for the animation will be in the vertex shader with uniforms "
"controlling the amount of motion. We use uniforms to control the strength of "
"the motion so that you can tweak the animation in editor and see the results "
"in real time, without the shader having to recompile."
msgstr ""
"ລະຫັດທັງໝົດສຳລັບແອນິເມຊັນຈະຢູ່ໃນ vertex shader ໂດຍມີ uniforms ເປັນຕົວຄວບຄຸມປະລິມານການເຄື່ອນໄ"
"ຫວ. ພວກເຮົາໃຊ້ uniforms ເພື່ອຄວບຄຸມຄວາມແຮງຂອງການເຄື່ອນໄຫວ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ເຈົ້າສາມາດປັບແຕ່ງແອນິເມຊັນໃ"
"ນ editor ແລະ ເຫັນຜົນໄດ້ທັນທີ ໂດຍທີ່ shader ບໍ່ຕ້ອງ compile ໃໝ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:50
msgid ""
"All the motions will be made using cosine waves applied to ``VERTEX`` in "
"model space. We want the vertices to be in model space so that the motion is "
"always relative to the orientation of the fish. For example, side-to-side "
"will always move the fish back and forth in its left to right direction, "
"instead of on the ``x`` axis in the world orientation."
msgstr ""
"ການເຄື່ອນໄຫວທັງໝົດຈະສ້າງຂຶ້ນໂດຍໃຊ້ຄື້ນ cosine ທີ່ໃຊ້ກັບ ``VERTEX`` ໃນ model space. ພວກເຮົາຕ້ອ"
"ງການໃຫ້ vertices ຢູ່ໃນ model space ເພື່ອໃຫ້ການເຄື່ອນໄຫວທຽບກັບທິດທາງຂອງປາສະເໝີ. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່"
"ນ: ການເຄື່ອນໄຫວຊ້າຍ-ຂວາຈະຍ້າຍປາໄປມາໃນທິດທາງຊ້າຍ ແລະ ຂວາຂອງມັນເອງສະເໝີ, ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນຕາມແກ"
"ນ ``x`` ໃນທິດທາງຂອງໂລກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:55
msgid ""
"In order to control the speed of the animation, we will start by defining "
"our own time variable using ``TIME``."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອຄວບຄຸມຄວາມໄວຂອງແອນິເມຊັນ, ພວກເຮົາຈະເລີ່ມຕົ້ນດ້ວຍການກຳນົດຕົວປ່ຽນເວລາຂອງພວກເຮົາເອງໂດຍໃຊ້ "
"``TIME``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:62
msgid ""
"The first motion we will implement is the side to side motion. It can be "
"made by offsetting ``VERTEX.x`` by ``cos`` of ``TIME``. Each time the mesh "
"is rendered, all the vertices will move to the side by the amount of "
"``cos(time)``."
msgstr ""
"ການເຄື່ອນໄຫວທຳອິດທີ່ພວກເຮົາຈະເຮັດຄື ການເຄື່ອນໄຫວຊ້າຍ-ຂວາ. ມັນສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ໂດຍການປ່ຽນຄ່າ "
"(offset) ``VERTEX.x`` ດ້ວຍຄ່າ ``cos`` ຂອງ ``TIME``. ທຸກໆຄັ້ງທີ່ mesh ຖືກປະມວນຜົນ, "
"vertices ທັງໝົດຈະເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄປທາງຂ້າງຕາມຄ່າຂອງ ``cos(time)``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:71
msgid "The resulting animation should look something like this:"
msgstr "ແອນິເມຊັນທີ່ໄດ້ຄວນຈະເປັນປະມານນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:75
msgid ""
"Next, we add the pivot. Because the fish is centered at (0, 0), all we have "
"to do is multiply ``VERTEX`` by a rotation matrix for it to rotate around "
"the center of the fish."
msgstr ""
"ຕໍ່ໄປ, ພວກເຮົາຈະເພີ່ມການໝູນ (pivot). ເນື່ອງຈາກປາຢູ່ຈຸດສູນກາງ (0, 0), ສິ່ງທີ່ພວກເຮົາຕ້ອງເຮັດຄື ຄູນ "
"``VERTEX`` ດ້ວຍ matrix ການໝູນ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ມັນໝູນຮອບຈຸດສູນກາງຂອງປາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:78
msgid "We construct a rotation matrix like so:"
msgstr "ພວກເຮົາສ້າງ matrix ການໝູນດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:87
msgid ""
"And then we apply it in the ``x`` and ``z`` axes by multiplying it by "
"``VERTEX.xz``."
msgstr "ຈາກນັ້ນພວກເຮົາໃຊ້ກັບແກນ ``x`` ແລະ ``z`` ໂດຍການຄູນມັນດ້ວຍ ``VERTEX.xz``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:93
msgid "With only the pivot applied you should see something like this:"
msgstr "ເມື່ອໃຊ້ພຽງແຕ່ pivot ເຈົ້າຄວນຈະເຫັນບາງສິ່ງທີ່ເປັນແບບນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:97
msgid ""
"The next two motions need to pan down the spine of the fish. For that, we "
"need a new variable, ``body``. ``body`` is a float that is ``0`` at the tail "
"of the fish and ``1`` at its head."
msgstr ""
"ສອງການເຄື່ອນໄຫວຕໍ່ໄປຈະຕ້ອງແລ່ນໄປຕາມກະດູກສັນຫຼັງຂອງປາ. ສຳລັບສິ່ງນັ້ນ, ພວກເຮົາຕ້ອງການຕົວປ່ຽນໃໝ່ຄື "
"``body``. ``body`` ເປັນ float ທີ່ມີຄ່າເປັນ ``0`` ຢູ່ຫາງຂອງປາ ແລະ ``1`` ຢູ່ຫົວຂອງມັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:104
msgid ""
"The next motion is a cosine wave that moves down the length of the fish. To "
"make it move along the spine of the fish, we offset the input to ``cos`` by "
"the position along the spine, which is the variable we defined above, "
"``body``."
msgstr ""
"ການເຄື່ອນໄຫວຕໍ່ໄປຄືຄື້ນ cosine ທີ່ເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄປຕາມຄວາມຍາວຂອງປາ. ເພື່ອໃຫ້ມັນເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄປຕາມກະດູກສັນຫຼັງຂອງ"
"ປາ, ພວກເຮົາຈະ offset input ຂອງ ``cos`` ດ້ວຍຕຳແໜ່ງຕາມກະດູກສັນຫຼັງ, ເຊິ່ງກໍຄືຕົວປ່ຽນທີ່ພວກເຮົາກ"
"ຳນົດໄວ້ຂ້າງເທິງຄື ``body``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:113
msgid ""
"This looks very similar to the side to side motion we defined above, but in "
"this one, by using ``body`` to offset ``cos`` each vertex along the spine "
"has a different position in the wave making it look like a wave is moving "
"along the fish."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງນີ້ເບິ່ງຄືກັນຫຼາຍກັບການເຄື່ອນໄຫວຊ້າຍ-ຂວາທີ່ພວກເຮົາກຳນົດໄວ້ກ່ອນໜ້ານີ້, ແຕ່ໃນອັນນີ້, ໂດຍການໃຊ້ "
"``body`` ເພື່ອ offset ``cos`` ແຕ່ລະ vertex ຕາມກະດູກສັນຫຼັງຈະມີຕຳແໜ່ງໃນຄື້ນທີ່ຕ່າງກັນ ເຮັດໃຫ້ມັນ"
"ເບິ່ງຄືວ່າມີຄື້ນກຳລັງເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄປຕາມຕົວປາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:119
msgid ""
"The last motion is the twist, which is a panning roll along the spine. "
"Similarly to the pivot, we first construct a rotation matrix."
msgstr ""
"ການເຄື່ອນໄຫວສຸດທ້າຍຄືການບິດ (twist), ເຊິ່ງເປັນການໝູນແບບກິ້ງໄປຕາມກະດູກສັນຫຼັງ. ຄືກັນກັບ pivot, ພວ"
"ກເຮົາຈະສ້າງ matrix ການໝູນກ່ອນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:128
msgid ""
"We apply the rotation in the ``xy`` axes so that the fish appears to roll "
"around its spine. For this to work, the fish's spine needs to be centered on "
"the ``z`` axis."
msgstr ""
"ພວກເຮົາໃຊ້ການໝູນໃນແກນ ``xy`` ເພື່ອໃຫ້ປາເບິ່ງຄືວ່າມັນກິ້ງອ້ອມກະດູກສັນຫຼັງຂອງມັນ. ເພື່ອໃຫ້ສິ່ງນີ້ເຮັດວຽກໄ"
"ດ້, ກະດູກສັນຫຼັງຂອງປາຕ້ອງຢູ່ຈຸດສູນກາງໃນແກນ ``z``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:135
msgid "Here is the fish with twist applied:"
msgstr "ນີ້ຄືປາທີ່ໄດ້ໃຊ້ການ twist:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:139
msgid ""
"If we apply all these motions one after another, we get a fluid jelly-like "
"motion."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າພວກເຮົາໃຊ້ການເຄື່ອນໄຫວທັງໝົດນີ້ຕໍ່ໆກັນ, ພວກເຮົາຈະໄດ້ການເຄື່ອນໄຫວທີ່ລື່ນໄຫຼຄືກັບວຸ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:143
msgid ""
"Normal fish swim mostly with the back half of their body. Accordingly, we "
"need to limit the panning motions to the back half of the fish. To do this, "
"we create a new variable, ``mask``."
msgstr ""
"ປາປົກກະຕິຈະລອຍນ້ຳໂດຍໃຊ້ສ່ວນເຄິ່ງຫຼັງຂອງຮ່າງກາຍເປັນຫຼັກ. ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ພວກເຮົາຈຶ່ງຕ້ອງຈຳກັດການເຄື່ອນໄຫວໃຫ້ຢູ່"
"ສະເພາະສ່ວນເຄິ່ງຫຼັງຂອງປາ. ເພື່ອເຮັດສິ່ງນີ້, ພວກເຮົາຈະສ້າງຕົວປ່ຽນໃໝ່ຄື ``mask``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:146
msgid ""
"``mask`` is a float that goes from ``0`` at the front of the fish to ``1`` "
"at the end using ``smoothstep`` to control the point at which the transition "
"from ``0`` to ``1`` happens."
msgstr ""
"``mask`` ເປັນ float ທີ່ມີຄ່າຕັ້ງແຕ່ ``0`` ຢູ່ທາງໜ້າຂອງປາ ຫາ ``1`` ຢູ່ສ່ວນທ້າຍ ໂດຍໃຊ້ "
"``smoothstep`` ເພື່ອຄວບຄຸມຈຸດທີ່ການປ່ຽນຄ່າຈາກ ``0`` ຫາ ``1`` ເກີດຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:154
msgid "Below is an image of the fish with ``mask`` used as ``COLOR``:"
msgstr "ດ້ານລຸ່ມນີ້ຄືຮູບຂອງປາທີ່ໃຊ້ ``mask`` ເປັນ ``COLOR``:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:158
msgid ""
"For the wave, we multiply the motion by ``mask`` which will limit it to the "
"back half."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບຄື້ນ, ພວກເຮົາຈະຄູນການເຄື່ອນໄຫວດ້ວຍ ``mask`` ເຊິ່ງຈະຈຳກັດມັນໄວ້ທີ່ສ່ວນເຄິ່ງຫຼັງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:165
msgid ""
"In order to apply the mask to the twist, we use ``mix``. ``mix`` allows us "
"to mix the vertex position between a fully rotated vertex and one that is "
"not rotated. We need to use ``mix`` instead of multiplying ``mask`` by the "
"rotated ``VERTEX`` because we are not adding the motion to the ``VERTEX`` we "
"are replacing the ``VERTEX`` with the rotated version. If we multiplied that "
"by ``mask``, we would shrink the fish."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອໃຊ້ mask ກັບການ twist, ພວກເຮົາຈະໃຊ້ ``mix``. ``mix`` ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ພວກເຮົາປະສົມຕຳແໜ່ງ "
"vertex ລະຫວ່າງ vertex ທີ່ໝູນເຕັມທີ່ ແລະ vertex ທີ່ບໍ່ໄດ້ໝູນ. ພວກເຮົາຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງໃຊ້ ``mix`` ແທນກ"
"ານຄູນ ``mask`` ດ້ວຍ ``VERTEX`` ທີ່ໝູນແລ້ວ ເພາະວ່າພວກເຮົາບໍ່ໄດ້ເພີ່ມການເຄື່ອນໄຫວໃຫ້ກັບ "
"``VERTEX`` ແຕ່ພວກເຮົາກຳລັງແທນທີ່ ``VERTEX`` ດ້ວຍເວີຊັນທີ່ໝູນແລ້ວ. ຖ້າພວກເຮົາຄູນມັນດ້ວຍ "
"``mask`` ໂດຍກົງ, ປາຈະຫົດຕົວລົງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:176
msgid "Putting the four motions together gives us the final animation."
msgstr "ເມື່ອລວມທັງ 4 ການເຄື່ອນໄຫວເຂົ້າກັນ ພວກເຮົາກໍจะได้ແອນິເມຊັນສຸດທ້າຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:180
msgid ""
"Go ahead and play with the uniforms in order to alter the swim cycle of the "
"fish. You will find that you can create a wide variety of swim styles using "
"these four motions."
msgstr ""
"ລອງປັບຫຼິ້ນກັບ uniforms ເພື່ອປ່ຽນຮອບການລອຍຂອງປາ. ເຈົ້າຈະພົບວ່າເຈົ້າສາມາດສ້າງຮູບແບບການລອຍທີ່ຫຼາກຫຼ"
"າຍໂດຍໃຊ້ 4 ການເຄື່ອນໄຫວນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:184
msgid "Making a school of fish"
msgstr "ການສ້າງຝູງປາ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:186
msgid ""
"Godot makes it easy to render thousands of the same object using a "
"MultiMeshInstance3D node."
msgstr ""
"Godot ເຮັດໃຫ້ການປະມວນຜົນວັດຖຸແບບດຽວກັນຫຼາຍພັນຢ່າງເປັນເລື່ອງງ່າຍໂດຍໃຊ້ MultiMeshInstance3D "
"node."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:188
msgid ""
"A MultiMeshInstance3D node is created and used the same way you would make a "
"MeshInstance3D node. For this tutorial, we will name the MultiMeshInstance3D "
"node ``School``, because it will contain a school of fish."
msgstr ""
"MultiMeshInstance3D node ຖືກສ້າງ ແລະ ໃຊ້ງານໃນແບບດຽວກັນກັບການສ້າງ MeshInstance3D "
"node. ສຳລັບບົດຮຽນນີ້, ພວກເຮົາຈະຕັ້ງຊື່ MultiMeshInstance3D node ວ່າ ``School``, ເພາະວ່າມັ"
"ນຈະບັນຈຸຝູງປາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:192
msgid ""
"Once you have a MultiMeshInstance3D add a :ref:`MultiMesh "
"<class_MultiMesh>`, and to that MultiMesh add your :ref:`Mesh <class_Mesh>` "
"with the shader from above."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອເຈົ້າມີ MultiMeshInstance3D ແລ້ວ ໃຫ້ເພີ່ມ :ref:`MultiMesh <class_MultiMesh>`, ແລ"
"ະ ໃນ MultiMesh ນັ້ນໃຫ້ເພີ່ມ :ref:`Mesh <class_Mesh>` ຂອງເຈົ້າພ້ອມກັບ shader ຈາກທາງເທິງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:195
msgid ""
"MultiMeshes draw your Mesh with three additional per-instance properties: "
"Transform (rotation, translation, scale), Color, and Custom. Custom is used "
"to pass in 4 multi-use variables using a :ref:`Color <class_Color>`."
msgstr ""
"MultiMeshes ຈະແຕ້ມ Mesh ຂອງທ່ານດ້ວຍຄຸນສົມບັດເພີ່ມເຕີມ 3 ຢ່າງຕໍ່ແຕ່ລະ instance: Transform "
"(ການໝູນ, ການຍ້າຍ, ການຂະຫຍາຍ), Color, ແລະ Custom. Custom ຖືກໃຊ້ເພື່ອສົ່ງຕົວປ່ຽນທີ່ໃຊ້ງານໄດ້ຫຼ"
"າກຫຼາຍ 4 ຕົວໂດຍໃຊ້ :ref:`Color <class_Color>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:199
msgid ""
"``instance_count`` specifies how many instances of the mesh you want to "
"draw. For now, leave ``instance_count`` at ``0`` because you cannot change "
"any of the other parameters while ``instance_count`` is larger than ``0``. "
"We will set ``instance count`` in GDScript later."
msgstr ""
"``instance_count`` ລະບຸວ່າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການແຕ້ມ mesh ຈັກອັນ. ສຳລັບຕອນນີ້, ໃຫ້ປະ "
"``instance_count`` ໄວ້ທີ່ ``0`` ເພາະເຈົ້າບໍ່ສາມາດປ່ຽນພາລາມິເຕີອື່ນໆໄດ້ໃນຂະນະທີ່ "
"``instance_count`` ຫຼາຍກວ່າ ``0``. ພວກເຮົາຈະຕັ້ງຄ່າ ``instance count`` ໃນ GDScript "
"ໃນພາຍຫຼັງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:203
msgid ""
"``transform_format`` specifies whether the transforms used are 3D or 2D. For "
"this tutorial, select 3D."
msgstr ""
"``transform_format`` ລະບຸວ່າ transforms ທີ່ໃຊ້ເປັນ 3D ຫຼື 2D. ສຳລັບບົດຮຽນນີ້, ໃຫ້ເລືອກ 3D."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:205
msgid ""
"For both ``color_format`` and ``custom_data_format`` you can choose between "
"``None``, ``Byte``, and ``Float``. ``None`` means you won't be passing in "
"that data (either a per-instance ``COLOR`` variable, or ``INSTANCE_CUSTOM``) "
"to the shader. ``Byte`` means each number making up the color you pass in "
"will be stored with 8 bits while ``Float`` means each number will be stored "
"in a floating-point number (32 bits). ``Float`` is slower but more precise, "
"``Byte`` will take less memory and be faster, but you may see some visual "
"artifacts."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບທັງ ``color_format`` ແລະ ``custom_data_format`` ເຈົ້າສາມາດເລືອກລະຫວ່າງ "
"``None``, ``Byte``, ແລະ ``Float``. ``None`` ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າເຈົ້າຈະບໍ່ສົ່ງຂໍ້ມູນນັ້ນ (ບໍ່ວ່າຈະເປັນຕົ"
"ວປ່ຽນ ``COLOR`` ຕໍ່ instance, ຫຼື ``INSTANCE_CUSTOM``) ໄປຫາ shader. ``Byte`` ໝາຍຄວ"
"າມວ່າແຕ່ລະຕົວເລກທີ່ປະກອບເປັນສີຈະຖືກເກັບດ້ວຍ 8 bits ໃນຂະນະທີ່ ``Float`` ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າແຕ່ລະຕົວເລກ"
"ຈະຖືກເກັບເປັນ floating-point (32 bits). ``Float`` ຈະຊ້າກວ່າແຕ່ມີຄວາມຊັດເຈນກວ່າ, "
"``Byte`` ຈະໃຊ້ memory ໜ້ອຍກວ່າ ແລະ ໄວກວ່າ, ແຕ່ເຈົ້າອາດຈະເຫັນບາງຂໍ້ຜິດພາດທາງພາບ (visual "
"artifacts)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:212
msgid "Now, set ``instance_count`` to the number of fish you want to have."
msgstr "ຕອນນີ້, ໃຫ້ຕັ້ງ ``instance_count`` ຕາມຈຳນວນປາທີ່ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:214
msgid "Next we need to set the per-instance transforms."
msgstr "ຕໍ່ໄປພວກເຮົາຕ້ອງຕັ້ງຄ່າ transforms ໃຫ້ກັບແຕ່ລະ instance."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:216
msgid ""
"There are two ways to set per-instance transforms for MultiMeshes. The first "
"is entirely in editor and is described in the :ref:`MultiMeshInstance3D "
"tutorial <doc_using_multi_mesh_instance>`."
msgstr ""
"ມີ 2 ວິທີໃນການຕັ້ງຄ່າ per-instance transforms ສຳລັບ MultiMeshes. ວິທີທຳອິດຄືເຮັດໃນ "
"editor ທັງໝົດ ເຊິ່ງໄດ້ອະທິບາຍໄວ້ໃນ :ref:`MultiMeshInstance3D tutorial "
"<doc_using_multi_mesh_instance>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:219
msgid ""
"The second is to loop over all the instances and set their transforms in "
"code. Below, we use GDScript to loop over all the instances and set their "
"transform to a random position."
msgstr ""
"ວິທີທີສອງຄືການ loop ຜ່ານທຸກໆ instances ແລະ ຕັ້ງຄ່າ transforms ຂອງພວກມັນໃນ code. ດ້ານລຸ່ມ"
"ນີ້, ພວກເຮົາໃຊ້ GDScript ເພື່ອ loop ຜ່ານທຸກໆ instances ແລະ ຕັ້ງຄ່າ transform ຂອງພວກມັນໄປຍັ"
"ງຕຳແໜ່ງແບບສຸ່ມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:229
msgid ""
"Running this script will place the fish in random positions in a box around "
"the position of the MultiMeshInstance3D."
msgstr ""
"ການ run script ນີ້ຈະວາງປາໃນຕຳແໜ່ງແບບສຸ່ມພາຍໃນຂອບເຂດກ່ອງອ້ອມຮອບຕຳແໜ່ງຂອງ "
"MultiMeshInstance3D."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:232
msgid ""
"If performance is an issue for you, try running the scene with fewer fish."
msgstr "ຖ້າປະສິດທິພາບເປັນບັນຫາສຳລັບເຈົ້າ, ໃຫ້ລອງ run ສາກດ້ວຍຈຳນວນປາທີ່ໜ້ອຍລົງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:234
msgid ""
"Notice how all the fish are all in the same position in their swim cycle? It "
"makes them look very robotic. The next step is to give each fish a different "
"position in the swim cycle so the entire school looks more organic."
msgstr ""
"ສັງເກດບໍ່ວ່າປາທຸກໂຕຢູ່ໃນຕຳແໜ່ງດຽວກັນໃນຮອບການລອຍຂອງພວກມັນ? ມັນເຮັດໃຫ້ພວກມັນເບິ່ງຄືຫຸ່ນຍົນຫຼາຍ. ຂັ້ນຕອ"
"ນຕໍ່ໄປຄືການເຮັດໃຫ້ປາແຕ່ລະໂຕມີຕຳແໜ່ງໃນຮອບການລອຍທີ່ຕ່າງກັນ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ຝູງປາທັງໝົດເບິ່ງເປັນທຳມະຊາດຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:239
msgid "Animating a school of fish"
msgstr "ການເຮັດແອນິເມຊັນໃຫ້ຝູງປາ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:241
msgid ""
"One of the benefits of animating the fish using ``cos`` functions is that "
"they are animated with one parameter, ``time``. In order to give each fish a "
"unique position in the swim cycle, we only need to offset ``time``."
msgstr ""
"ໜຶ່ງໃນປະໂຫຍດຂອງການເຮັດແອນິເມຊັນປາໂດຍໃຊ້ຟັງຊັນ ``cos`` ຄືພວກມັນຖືກຄວບຄຸມດ້ວຍພາລາມິເຕີດຽວຄື "
"``time``. ເພື່ອໃຫ້ປາແຕ່ລະໂຕມີຕຳແໜ່ງທີ່ເປັນເອກະລັກໃນຮອບການລອຍ, ພວກເຮົາພຽງແຕ່ຕ້ອງ offset "
"``time`` ເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:245
msgid ""
"We do that by adding the per-instance custom value ``INSTANCE_CUSTOM`` to "
"``time``."
msgstr ""
"ພວກເຮົາເຮັດສິ່ງນັ້ນໂດຍການເພີ່ມຄ່າ custom ຕໍ່ instance ຄື ``INSTANCE_CUSTOM`` ເຂົ້າໃນ "
"``time``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:251
msgid ""
"Next, we need to pass a value into ``INSTANCE_CUSTOM``. We do that by adding "
"one line into the ``for`` loop from above. In the ``for`` loop we assign "
"each instance a set of four random floats to use."
msgstr ""
"ຕໍ່ໄປ, ພວກເຮົາຕ້ອງສົ່ງຄ່າເຂົ້າໃນ ``INSTANCE_CUSTOM``. ພວກເຮົາເຮັດໄດ້ໂດຍການເພີ່ມ code ແຖວໜຶ່ງເ"
"ຂົ້າໃນ ``for`` loop ຈາກຂ້າງເທິງ. ໃນ ``for`` loop ນັ້ນ, ພວກເຮົາຈະກຳນົດໃຫ້ແຕ່ລະ instance "
"ໄດ້ຮັບຄ່າ random float 4 ຕົວເພື່ອໃຊ້ງານ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:259
msgid ""
"Now the fish all have unique positions in the swim cycle. You can give them "
"a little more individuality by using ``INSTANCE_CUSTOM`` to make them swim "
"faster or slower by multiplying by ``TIME``."
msgstr ""
"ຕອນນີ້ປາທຸກໂຕຈະມີຕຳແໜ່ງທີ່ຕ່າງກັນໃນຮອບການລອຍ. ເຈົ້າສາມາດເພີ່ມຄວາມເປັນເອກະລັກໃຫ້ພວກມັນໄດ້ຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນໂດ"
"ຍການໃຊ້ ``INSTANCE_CUSTOM`` ເພື່ອເຮັດໃຫ້ພວກມັນລອຍໄວຂຶ້ນ ຫຼື ຊ້າລົງໂດຍການຄູນກັບ ``TIME``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:268
msgid ""
"You can even experiment with changing the per-instance color the same way "
"you changed the per-instance custom value."
msgstr ""
"ເຈົ້າສາມາດທົດລອງປ່ຽນສີຕໍ່ instance ໃນແບບດຽວກັບທີ່ເຈົ້າປ່ຽນຄ່າ custom ຕໍ່ instance ກໍໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:271
msgid ""
"One problem that you will run into at this point is that the fish are "
"animated, but they are not moving. You can move them by updating the per-"
"instance transform for each fish every frame. Although doing so will be "
"faster than moving thousands of MeshInstance3Ds per frame, it'll still "
"likely be slow."
msgstr ""
"ບັນຫາໜຶ່ງທີ່ເຈົ້າຈະພົບໃນຕອນນີ້ຄື ປາມີແອນິເມຊັນແລ້ວ ແຕ່ພວກມັນບໍ່ເຄື່ອນທີ່. ເຈົ້າສາມາດຍ້າຍພວກມັນໄດ້ໂດຍການອັບ"
"ເດດ per-instance transform ສຳລັບປາແຕ່ລະໂຕໃນທຸກໆເຟຣມ. ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າການເຮັດແບບນັ້ນຈະໄວກວ່າກ"
"ານຍ້າຍ MeshInstance3D ຫຼາຍພັນອັນຕໍ່ເຟຣມ, ແຕ່ມັນກໍຍັງມີໂອກາດທີ່ຈະຊ້າຢູ່ດີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/animating_thousands_of_fish.rst:276
msgid ""
"In the next tutorial we will cover how to use :ref:`GPUParticles3D "
"<class_GPUParticles3D>` to take advantage of the GPU and move each fish "
"around individually while still receiving the benefits of instancing."
msgstr ""
"ໃນບົດຮຽນຕໍ່ໄປ ພວກເຮົາຈະເວົ້າເຖິງວິທີການໃຊ້ :ref:`GPUParticles3D <class_GPUParticles3D>"
"` ເພື່ອໃຊ້ປະໂຫຍດຈາກ GPU ແລະ ຍ້າຍປາແຕ່ລະໂຕແຍກກັນ ໃນຂະນະທີ່ຍັງໄດ້ຮັບປະໂຫຍດຈາກການເຮັດ "
"instancing."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:6
msgid "Controlling thousands of fish with Particles"
msgstr "ການຄວບຄຸມປາຫຼາຍພັນໂຕດ້ວຍ Particles"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:8
msgid ""
"The problem with :ref:`MeshInstance3D <class_MeshInstance3D>` is that it is "
"expensive to update their transform array. It is great for placing many "
"static objects around the scene. But it is still difficult to move the "
"objects around the scene."
msgstr ""
"ບັນຫາຂອງ :ref:`MeshInstance3D <class_MeshInstance3D>` ຄືມັນກິນຊັບພະຍາກອນຫຼາຍໃນການອັບ"
"ເດດ transform array ຂອງພວກມັນ. ມັນເໝາະສຳລັບການວາງວັດຖຸຄົງທີ່ (static) ຈຳນວນຫຼາຍໄວ້ໃນສາ"
"ກ. ແຕ່ມັນຍັງຍາກທີ່ຈະຍ້າຍວັດຖຸເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນໄປມາໃນສາກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:12
msgid ""
"To make each instance move in an interesting way, we will use "
"a :ref:`GPUParticles3D <class_GPUParticles3D>` node. Particles take "
"advantage of GPU acceleration by computing and setting the per-instance "
"information in a :ref:`Shader <class_Shader>`."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອເຮັດໃຫ້ແຕ່ລະ instance ເຄື່ອນທີ່ໃນຮູບແບບທີ່ໜ້າສົນໃຈ, ພວກເຮົາຈະໃຊ້ :ref:`GPUParticles3D "
"<class_GPUParticles3D>` node. Particles ຈະໃຊ້ປະໂຫຍດຈາກການເລັ່ງຄວາມໄວດ້ວຍ GPU ໂດຍກ"
"ານຄຳນວນ ແລະ ຕັ້ງຄ່າຂໍ້ມູນ per-instance ໃນ :ref:`Shader <class_Shader>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:16
msgid ""
"First create a Particles node. Then, under \"Draw Passes\" set the "
"Particle's \"Draw Pass 1\" to your :ref:`Mesh <class_Mesh>`. Then under "
"\"Process Material\" create a new :ref:`ShaderMaterial "
"<class_ShaderMaterial>`."
msgstr ""
"ທຳອິດໃຫ້ສ້າງ Particles node. ຈາກນັ້ນ, ພາຍໃຕ້ \"Draw Passes\" ໃຫ້ຕັ້ງຄ່າ \"Draw Pass "
"1\" ຂອງ Particle ໃຫ້ເປັນ :ref:`Mesh <class_Mesh>` ຂອງທ່ານ. ຈາກນັ້ນພາຍໃຕ້ \"Process "
"Material\" ໃຫ້ສ້າງ :ref:`ShaderMaterial <class_ShaderMaterial>` ໃໝ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:20
msgid "Set the ``shader_type`` to ``particles``."
msgstr "ຕັ້ງຄ່າ ``shader_type`` ໃຫ້ເປັນ ``particles``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:26
msgid "Then add the following two functions:"
msgstr "ຈາກນັ້ນເພີ່ມ 2 ຟັງຊັນຕໍ່ໄປນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:50
msgid ""
"These functions come from the default :ref:`ParticleProcessMaterial "
"<class_ParticleProcessMaterial>`. They are used to generate a random number "
"from each particle's ``RANDOM_SEED``."
msgstr ""
"ຟັງຊັນເຫຼົ່ານີ້ມາຈາກ :ref:`ParticleProcessMaterial <class_ParticleProcessMaterial>` "
"ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ. ພວກມັນຖືກໃຊ້ເພື່ອສ້າງຕົວເລກແບບສຸ່ມຈາກ ``RANDOM_SEED`` ຂອງແຕ່ລະ particle."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:53
msgid ""
"A unique thing about particle shaders is that some built-in variables are "
"saved across frames. ``TRANSFORM``, ``COLOR``, and ``CUSTOM`` can all be "
"accessed in the shader of the mesh, and also in the particle shader the next "
"time it is run."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງທີ່ພິເສດກ່ຽວກັບ particle shaders ຄືຕົວປ່ຽນ built-in ບາງຕົວຈະຖືກບັນທຶກໄວ້ຂ້າມເຟຣມ. "
"``TRANSFORM``, ``COLOR``, ແລະ ``CUSTOM`` ທັງໝົດສາມາດເຂົ້າເຖິງໄດ້ໃນ shader ຂອງ "
"mesh, ແລະ ຍັງເຂົ້າເຖິງໄດ້ໃນ particle shader ໃນຄັ້ງຕໍ່ໄປທີ່ມັນເຮັດວຽກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:57
msgid ""
"Next, setup your ``start()`` function. Particles shaders contain a "
"``start()`` function and a ``process()`` function."
msgstr ""
"ຕໍ່ໄປ, ໃຫ້ຕັ້ງຄ່າຟັງຊັນ ``start()`` ຂອງທ່ານ. Particle shaders ຈະປະກອບດ້ວຍຟັງຊັນ ``start()"
"`` ແລະ ຟັງຊັນ ``process()``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:60
msgid ""
"The code in the ``start()`` function only runs when the particle system "
"starts. The code in the ``process()`` function will always run."
msgstr ""
"ລະຫັດໃນຟັງຊັນ ``start()`` ຈະເຮັດວຽກພຽງແຕ່ຕອນທີ່ລະບົບ particle ເລີ່ມຕົ້ນເທົ່ານັ້ນ. ສ່ວນລະຫັດໃນຟັງ"
"ຊັນ ``process()`` ຈະເຮັດວຽກຕະຫຼອດເວລາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:63
msgid ""
"We need to generate 4 random numbers: 3 to create a random position and one "
"for the random offset of the swim cycle."
msgstr ""
"ພວກເຮົາຕ້ອງສ້າງຕົວເລກສຸ່ມ 4 ຕົວ: 3 ຕົວສຳລັບສ້າງຕຳແໜ່ງແບບສຸ່ມ ແລະ ອີກ 1 ຕົວສຳລັບ offset ແບບສຸ່ມຂ"
"ອງຮອບການລອຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:66
msgid ""
"First, generate 4 seeds inside the ``start()`` function using the ``hash()`` "
"function provided above:"
msgstr ""
"ທຳອິດ, ໃຫ້ສ້າງ seed 4 ຕົວພາຍໃນຟັງຊັນ ``start()`` ໂດຍໃຊ້ຟັງຊັນ ``hash()`` ທີ່ໃຫ້ໄວ້ຂ້າງເທິງ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:75
msgid ""
"Then, use those seeds to generate random numbers using ``rand_from_seed``:"
msgstr ""
"ຈາກນັ້ນ, ໃຊ້ seed ເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນເພື່ອສ້າງຕົວເລກສຸ່ມໂດຍໃຊ້ ``rand_from_seed``:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:84
msgid ""
"Finally, assign ``position`` to ``TRANSFORM[3].xyz``, which is the part of "
"the transform that holds the position information."
msgstr ""
"ສຸດທ້າຍ, ໃຫ້ກຳນົດ ``position`` ໃຫ້ກັບ ``TRANSFORM[3].xyz``, ເຊິ່ງເປັນສ່ວນຂອງ transform "
"ທີ່ເກັບຂໍ້ມູນຕຳແໜ່ງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:91
msgid "Remember, all this code so far goes inside the ``start()`` function."
msgstr "ຢ່າລືມວ່າ, ລະຫັດທັງໝົດທີ່ຜ່ານມານີ້ແມ່ນຢູ່ພາຍໃນຟັງຊັນ ``start()``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:93
msgid ""
"The vertex shader for your mesh can stay the exact same as it was in the "
"previous tutorial."
msgstr ""
"Vertex shader ສຳລັບ mesh ຂອງທ່ານສາມາດໃຊ້ແບບເດີມໄດ້ເລີຍຄືກັບໃນບົດຮຽນກ່ອນໜ້ານີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:95
msgid ""
"Now you can move each fish individually each frame, either by adding to the "
"``TRANSFORM`` directly or by writing to ``VELOCITY``."
msgstr ""
"ຕອນນີ້ເຈົ້າສາມາດຍ້າຍປາແຕ່ລະໂຕແຍກກັນໃນແຕ່ລະເຟຣມໄດ້ແລ້ວ, ບໍ່ວ່າຈະເປັນການເພີ່ມຄ່າໃຫ້ກັບ "
"``TRANSFORM`` ໂດຍກົງ ຫຼື ການຂຽນຄ່າລົງໃນ ``VELOCITY``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:98
msgid ""
"Let's transform the fish by setting their ``VELOCITY`` in the ``start()`` "
"function."
msgstr "ລອງປ່ຽນແປງປາໂດຍການຕັ້ງຄ່າ ``VELOCITY`` ຂອງພວກມັນໃນຟັງຊັນ ``start()``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:104
msgid ""
"This is the most basic way to set ``VELOCITY`` every particle (or fish) will "
"have the same velocity."
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ຄືວິທີທີ່ງ່າຍທີ່ສຸດໃນການຕັ້ງຄ່າ ``VELOCITY`` ເຊິ່ງທຸກໆ particle (ຫຼື ປາ) ຈະມີຄວາມໄວເທົ່າກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:106
msgid ""
"Just by setting ``VELOCITY`` you can make the fish swim however you want. "
"For example, try the code below."
msgstr ""
"ພຽງແຕ່ການຕັ້ງຄ່າ ``VELOCITY`` ເຈົ້າກໍສາມາດເຮັດໃຫ້ປາລອຍໄປໃນແບບທີ່ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການໄດ້. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ: ລ"
"ອງໃຊ້ລະຫັດດ້ານລຸ່ມນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:113
msgid "This will give each fish a unique speed between ``2`` and ``10``."
msgstr "ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ປາແຕ່ລະໂຕມີຄວາມໄວທີ່ເປັນເອກະລັກລະຫວ່າງ ``2`` ຫາ ``10``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:115
msgid ""
"You can also let each fish change its velocity over time if you set the "
"velocity in the ``process()`` function."
msgstr ""
"ເຈົ້າຍັງສາມາດເຮັດໃຫ້ປາແຕ່ລະໂຕປ່ຽນຄວາມໄວຕາມເວລາໄດ້ ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕັ້ງຄ່າຄວາມໄວໃນຟັງຊັນ ``process()"
"``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:118
msgid ""
"If you used ``CUSTOM.y`` in the last tutorial, you can also set the speed of "
"the swim animation based on the ``VELOCITY``. Just use ``CUSTOM.y``."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເຈົ້າໃຊ້ ``CUSTOM.y`` ໃນບົດຮຽນທີ່ແລ້ວ, ເຈົ້າຍັງສາມາດຕັ້ງຄວາມໄວຂອງແອນິເມຊັນການລອຍຕາມຄ່າ "
"``VELOCITY`` ໄດ້. ພຽງແຕ່ໃຊ້ ``CUSTOM.y``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:125
msgid "This code gives you the following behavior:"
msgstr "ລະຫັດນີ້ຈະໃຫ້ພຶດຕິກຳດັ່ງຕໍ່ໄປນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/vertex_animation/controlling_thousands_of_fish.rst:129
msgid ""
"Using a ParticleProcessMaterial you can make the fish behavior as simple or "
"complex as you like. In this tutorial we only set Velocity, but in your own "
"Shaders you can also set ``COLOR``, rotation, scale (through ``TRANSFORM``). "
"Please refer to the :ref:`Particles Shader Reference <doc_particle_shader>` "
"for more information on particle shaders."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍການໃຊ້ ParticleProcessMaterial ເຈົ້າສາມາດເຮັດໃຫ້ພຶດຕິກຳຂອງປາງ່າຍ ຫຼື ຊັບຊ້ອນໄດ້ຕາມໃຈມັ"
"ກ. ໃນບົດຮຽນນີ້ພວກເຮົາຕັ້ງຄ່າພຽງແຕ່ Velocity, ແຕ່ໃນ Shaders ຂອງເຈົ້າເອງ ເຈົ້າສາມາດຕັ້ງຄ່າ "
"``COLOR``, ການໝູນ, ຂະໜາດ (ຜ່ານ ``TRANSFORM``) ໄດ້ຄືກັນ. ກະລຸນາເບິ່ງ :ref:`Particles "
"Shader Reference <doc_particle_shader>` ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບ particle shaders."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:4
msgid "Using multiple threads"
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ຫຼາຍ Threads"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:8
msgid ""
"For a list of multithreading primitives in C++, "
"see :ref:`doc_core_concurrency_types`."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບລາຍການ multithreading primitives ໃນ C++, ເບິ່ງ "
":ref:`doc_core_concurrency_types`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:13
msgid ""
"Threads allow simultaneous execution of code. It allows off-loading work "
"from the main thread."
msgstr ""
"Threads ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ການປະມວນຜົນລະຫັດເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ພ້ອມໆກັນ. ມັນຊ່ວຍແບ່ງເບົາວຽກອອກຈາກ main thread "
"(ເທຣດຫຼັກ) ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:16
msgid "Godot supports threads and provides many handy functions to use them."
msgstr "Godot ຮອງຮັບ threads ແລະ ມີຟັງຊັນທີ່ສະດວກຫຼາຍຢ່າງໃຫ້ໃຊ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:18
msgid ""
"If using other languages (C#, C++), it may be easier to use the threading "
"classes they support."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າໃຊ້ພາສາອື່ນ (C#, C++), ມັນອາດຈະງ່າຍກວ່າທີ່ຈະໃຊ້ threading classes ທີ່ພາສາເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນຮອງຮັບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:23
msgid ""
"Before using a built-in class in a thread, read :ref:`doc_thread_safe_apis` "
"first to check whether it can be safely used in a thread."
msgstr ""
"ກ່ອນທີ່ຈະໃຊ້ built-in class ໃນ thread, ໃຫ້ອ່ານ :ref:`doc_thread_safe_apis` ກ່ອນເພື່ອເບິ່"
"ງວ່າມັນສາມາດໃຊ້ໃນ thread ໄດ້ຢ່າງປອດໄພຫຼືບໍ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:27
msgid "Creating a Thread"
msgstr "ການສ້າງ Thread"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:29
msgid "To create a thread, use the following code:"
msgstr "ເພື່ອສ້າງ thread, ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ລະຫັດຕໍ່ໄປນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:138
msgid ""
"Your function will, then, run in a separate thread until it returns. Even if "
"the function has returned already, the thread must collect it, so "
"call :ref:`Thread.wait_to_finish()<class_Thread_method_wait_to_finish>`, "
"which will wait until the thread is done (if not done yet), then properly "
"dispose of it."
msgstr ""
"ຈາກນັ້ນ, ຟັງຊັນຂອງທ່ານຈະເຮັດວຽກໃນ thread ທີ່ແຍກຕ່າງຫາກຈົນກວ່າມັນຈະ return. ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຟັງຊັນຈ"
"ະ return ແລ້ວ, thread ກໍຍັງຕ້ອງໄດ້ຮັບການຈັດການ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນໃຫ້ເອີ້ນໃຊ້ "
":ref:`Thread.wait_to_finish()<class_Thread_method_wait_to_finish>`, ເຊິ່ງຈະລໍຖ້າຈົ"
"ນກວ່າ thread ຈະເຮັດວຽກສຳເລັດ (ຖ້າຍັງບໍ່ສຳເລັດ), ຈາກນັ້ນຈຶ່ງທຳລາຍ (dispose) ມັນຢ່າງຖືກຕ້ອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:145
msgid ""
"Creating threads is a slow operation, especially on Windows. To avoid "
"unnecessary performance overhead, make sure to create threads before heavy "
"processing is needed instead of creating threads just-in-time."
msgstr ""
"ການສ້າງ threads ເປັນການເຮັດວຽກທີ່ຊ້າ, ໂດຍສະເພາະໃນ Windows. ເພື່ອຫຼີກລ່ຽງການກິນຊັບພະຍາກອນທີ່ບໍ່"
"ຈຳເປັນ, ໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າໄດ້ສ້າງ threads ກ່ອນທີ່ຈະມີການປະມວນຜົນໜັກໆ ແທນທີ່ຈະສ້າງແບບ just-in-time."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:149
msgid ""
"For example, if you need multiple threads during gameplay, you can create "
"threads while the level is loading and only actually start processing with "
"them later on."
msgstr ""
"ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ: ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການຫຼາຍ threads ໃນລະຫວ່າງການຫຼິ້ນເກມ, ເຈົ້າສາມາດສ້າງ threads ໃນຂະນະ"
"ທີ່ກຳລັງໂຫຼດດ່ານ ແລະ ຄ່ອຍເລີ່ມປະມວນຜົນກັບພວກມັນໃນພາຍຫຼັງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:153
msgid ""
"Additionally, locking and unlocking of mutexes can also be an expensive "
"operation. Locking should be done carefully; avoid locking too often (or for "
"too long)."
msgstr ""
"ນອກຈາກນີ້, ການລັອກ (locking) ແລະ ປົດລັອກ (unlocking) ຂອງ mutexes ກໍເປັນວຽກທີ່ໜັກຄືກັນ. ກາ"
"ນລັອກຄວນເຮັດຢ່າງລະມັດລະວັງ; ຫຼີກລ່ຽງການລັອກເລື້ອຍເກີນໄປ (ຫຼື ດົນເກີນໄປ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:160
msgid "Mutexes"
msgstr "ມິວເທັກ (Mutexes)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:162
msgid ""
"Accessing objects or data from multiple threads is not always supported (if "
"you do it, it will cause unexpected behaviors or crashes). Read "
"the :ref:`doc_thread_safe_apis` documentation to understand which engine "
"APIs support multiple thread access."
msgstr ""
"ການເຂົ້າເຖິງວັດຖຸ ຫຼື ຂໍ້ມູນຈາກຫຼາຍ threads ບໍ່ໄດ້ຖືກຮອງຮັບສະເໝີໄປ (ຖ້າເຈົ້າເຮັດ, ມັນຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດພຶດຕິກ"
"ຳທີ່ບໍ່ຄາດຄິດ ຫຼື ເກມຄ້າງ/ຫຼົ້ມ). ໃຫ້ອ່ານເອກະສານ :ref:`doc_thread_safe_apis` ເພື່ອເຂົ້າໃຈວ່າ "
"engine APIs ໃດແດ່ທີ່ຮອງຮັບການເຂົ້າເຖິງຈາກຫຼາຍ threads."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:167
msgid ""
"When processing your own data or calling your own functions, as a rule, try "
"to avoid accessing the same data directly from different threads. You may "
"run into synchronization problems, as the data is not always updated between "
"CPU cores when modified. Always use a :ref:`Mutex<class_Mutex>` when "
"accessing a piece of data from different threads."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອປະມວນຜົນຂໍ້ມູນຂອງເຈົ້າເອງ ຫຼື ເອີ້ນໃຊ້ຟັງຊັນຂອງເຈົ້າເອງ, ຕາມຫຼັກການແລ້ວ, ໃຫ້ຫຼີກລ່ຽງການເຂົ້າເຖິງຂໍ້ມູນ"
"ດຽວກັນໂດຍກົງຈາກ threads ທີ່ຕ່າງກັນ. ເຈົ້າອາດຈະພົບກັບບັນຫາ synchronization, ເພາະວ່າຂໍ້ມູນບໍ່ໄດ້ຖື"
"ກອັບເດດລະຫວ່າງ CPU cores ສະເໝີໄປເມື່ອມີການແກ້ໄຂ. ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ :ref:`Mutex<class_Mutex>` ສະເໝີ"
"ເມື່ອເຂົ້າເຖິງຂໍ້ມູນຈາກ threads ທີ່ຕ່າງກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:173
msgid ""
"When calling :ref:`Mutex.lock()<class_Mutex_method_lock>`, a thread ensures "
"that all other threads will be blocked (put on suspended state) if they try "
"to *lock* the same mutex. When the mutex is unlocked by "
"calling :ref:`Mutex.unlock()<class_Mutex_method_unlock>`, the other threads "
"will be allowed to proceed with the lock (but only one at a time)."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອເອີ້ນໃຊ້ :ref:`Mutex.lock()<class_Mutex_method_lock>`, thread ນັ້ນຈະຮັບປະກັນວ່າ "
"threads ອື່ນໆທັງໝົດຈະຖືກບລັອກ (ຢູ່ໃນສະຖານະ suspended) ຖ້າພວກມັນພະຍາຍາມ *lock* mutex ດຽວ"
"ກັນ. ເມື່ອ mutex ຖືກປົດລັອກໂດຍການເອີ້ນໃຊ້ :ref:`Mutex.unlock()"
"<class_Mutex_method_unlock>`, thread ອື່ນໆຈຶ່ງຈະໄດ້ຮັບອະນຸຍາດໃຫ້ດຳເນີນການລັອກຕໍ່ໄດ້ (ແຕ່ເທື່ອ"
"ລະ thread ເທົ່ານັ້ນ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:179
msgid "Here is an example of using a Mutex:"
msgstr "ນີ້ຄືຕົວຢ່າງການໃຊ້ Mutex:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:304
msgid "Semaphores"
msgstr "ເຊມາຟໍ (Semaphores)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:306
msgid ""
"Sometimes you want your thread to work *\"on demand\"*. In other words, tell "
"it when to work and let it suspend when it isn't doing anything. For "
"this, :ref:`Semaphores<class_Semaphore>` are used. The "
"function :ref:`Semaphore.wait()<class_Semaphore_method_wait>` is used in the "
"thread to suspend it until some data arrives."
msgstr ""
"ບາງຄັ້ງເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ thread ຂອງເຈົ້າເຮັດວຽກ *\"ຕາມຄວາມຕ້ອງການ\"*. ເວົ້າອີກຢ່າງໜຶ່ງຄື ບອກໃຫ້ມັນ"
"ເຮັດວຽກເມື່ອຕ້ອງການ ແລະ ປ່ອຍໃຫ້ມັນຢຸດ (suspend) ເມື່ອມັນບໍ່ໄດ້ເຮັດຫຍັງ. ສຳລັບສິ່ງນີ້, ຈະໃຊ້ "
":ref:`Semaphores<class_Semaphore>`. ຟັງຊັນ :ref:`Semaphore.wait()"
"<class_Semaphore_method_wait>` ຖືກໃຊ້ໃນ thread ເພື່ອຢຸດມັນໄວ້ຈົນກວ່າຈະມີຂໍ້ມູນເຂົ້າມາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/using_multiple_threads.rst:312
msgid ""
"The main thread, instead, "
"uses :ref:`Semaphore.post()<class_Semaphore_method_post>` to signal that "
"data is ready to be processed:"
msgstr ""
"ສ່ວນ main thread ຈະໃຊ້ :ref:`Semaphore.post()<class_Semaphore_method_post>` ເພື່ອ"
"ສົ່ງສັນຍານວ່າຂໍ້ມູນພ້ອມທີ່ຈະຖືກປະມວນຜົນແລ້ວ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:4
msgid "Thread-safe APIs"
msgstr "APIs ທີ່ປອດໄພຕໍ່ Thread (Thread-safe)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:9
msgid ""
"Threads are used to balance processing power across CPUs and cores. Godot "
"supports multithreading, but not in the whole engine."
msgstr ""
"Threads ຖືກໃຊ້ເພື່ອສ້າງຄວາມສົມດຸນຂອງກຳລັງການປະມວນຜົນຜ່ານ CPUs ແລະ cores. Godot ຮອງຮັບ "
"multithreading, ແຕ່ບໍ່ແມ່ນໃນທຸກສ່ວນຂອງ engine."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:12
msgid ""
"Below is a list of ways multithreading can be used in different areas of "
"Godot."
msgstr ""
"ດ້ານລຸ່ມນີ້ຄືລາຍການວິທີການທີ່ multithreading ສາມາດນຳມາໃຊ້ໃນສ່ວນຕ່າງໆຂອງ Godot."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:15
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_differences.rst:29
msgid "Global scope"
msgstr "ຂອບເຂດທົ່ວໂລກ (Global scope)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:17
msgid ""
"Most :ref:`Global Scope<class_@GlobalScope>` singletons are thread-safe by "
"default. Accessing servers from threads is supported. However, for "
"the :ref:`rendering <doc_thread_safe_apis_rendering>` and :ref:`physics "
"<doc_thread_safe_apis_physics>` servers, thread-safe operation must be "
"enabled in the project settings first."
msgstr ""
"ສ່ວນຫຼາຍ :ref:`ຂອບເຂດທົ່ວໂລກ<class_@GlobalScope>` ຊິງເກິລຕັນ ແມ່ນປອດໄພຕໍ່ເທຣດໂດຍຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້"
"ນ. ການເຂົ້າເຖິງເຊີເວີຈາກເທຣດແມ່ນໄດ້ຮັບການຮອງຮັບ. ຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ສຳລັບເຊີເວີ :ref:`ການເຣັນເດີ "
"<doc_thread_safe_apis_rendering>` ແລະ :ref:`ຟີຊິກ "
"<doc_thread_safe_apis_physics>`, ການເຮັດວຽກແບບປອດໄພຕໍ່ເທຣດຕ້ອງໄດ້ຮັບການເປີດໃຊ້ງານໃນກາ"
"ນຕັ້ງຄ່າໂຄງການກ່ອນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:23
msgid ""
"This makes singletons ideal for code that creates dozens of thousands of "
"instances in servers and controls them from threads. Of course, it requires "
"a bit more code, as this is used directly and not within the scene tree."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງນີ້ເຮັດໃຫ້ singletons ເໝາະສຳລັບ code ທີ່ສ້າງ instances ຫຼາຍໝື່ນອັນໃນ servers ແລະ ຄວບຄຸມພ"
"ວກມັນຈາກ threads. ແນ່ນອນວ່າ ມັນຕ້ອງໃຊ້ code ຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນໜ້ອຍໜຶ່ງ ເພາະສິ່ງນີ້ຖືກໃຊ້ໂດຍກົງ ແລະ ບໍ່ໄດ້ຢູ່ພາຍ"
"ໃນ scene tree."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:28
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/scene_tree.rst:90
msgid "Scene tree"
msgstr "Scene tree"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:30
msgid ""
"Interacting with the active scene tree is **not** thread-safe. Make sure to "
"use mutexes when sending data between threads. If you want to call functions "
"or set properties from a thread, you may use :ref:`call_deferred "
"<class_Object_method_call_deferred>` or :ref:`set_deferred "
"<class_Object_method_set_deferred>`:"
msgstr ""
"ການໂຕ້ຕອບກັບ scene tree ທີ່ກຳລັງເຮັດວຽກຢູ່ແມ່ນ **ບໍ່** thread-safe. ໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າໄດ້ໃຊ້ "
"mutexes ເມື່ອສົ່ງຂໍ້ມູນລະຫວ່າງ threads. ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການເອີ້ນໃຊ້ຟັງຊັນ ຫຼື ຕັ້ງຄ່າຄຸນສົມບັດຈາກ thread, "
"ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ :ref:`call_deferred <class_Object_method_call_deferred>` ຫຼື "
":ref:`set_deferred <class_Object_method_set_deferred>`:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:50
msgid ""
"However, creating scene chunks (nodes in tree arrangement) outside the "
"active tree is fine. This way, parts of a scene can be built or instantiated "
"in a thread, then added in the main thread:"
msgstr ""
"ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ການສ້າງ scene chunks (nodes ທີ່ຈັດລຽງເປັນ tree) ຢູ່ນອກ active tree ແມ່ນສາມ"
"າດເຮັດໄດ້. ດ້ວຍວິທີນີ້, ບາງສ່ວນຂອງ scene ສາມາດຖືກສ້າງ ຫຼື instantiate ໃນ thread, ຈາກນັ້ນຈຶ່ງເ"
"ພີ່ມເຂົ້າໃນ main thread:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:69
msgid ""
"Still, this is only really useful if you have **one** thread loading data. "
"Attempting to load or create scene chunks from multiple threads may work, "
"but you risk resources (which are only loaded once in Godot) being tweaked "
"by the multiple threads, resulting in unexpected behaviors or crashes."
msgstr ""
"ແຕ່ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະມີປະໂຫຍດແທ້ໆກໍຕໍ່ເມື່ອເຈົ້າມີ thread **ດຽວ** ທີ່ໂຫຼດຂໍ້ມູນ. ການພະຍາຍາມໂຫຼດ ຫຼື ສ້າງ scene "
"chunks ຈາກຫຼາຍ threads ອາດຈະເຮັດວຽກໄດ້, ແຕ່ເຈົ້າຈະມີຄວາມສ່ຽງທີ່ resources (ເຊິ່ງໃນ Godot "
"ຈະຖືກໂຫຼດພຽງຄັ້ງດຽວ) ຖືກປ່ຽນແປງໂດຍຫຼາຍ threads ພ້ອມກັນ, ເຊິ່ງເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດພຶດຕິກຳທີ່ບໍ່ຄາດຄິດ ຫຼື ເກມຫຼົ້"
"ມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:74
msgid ""
"Only use more than one thread to generate scene data if you *really* know "
"what you are doing and you are sure that a single resource is not being used "
"or set in multiple ones. Otherwise, you are safer just using the servers API "
"(which is fully thread-safe) directly and not touching scene or resources."
msgstr ""
"ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ຫຼາຍກວ່າໜຶ່ງ thread ເພື່ອສ້າງ scene data ກໍຕໍ່ເມື່ອເຈົ້າຮູ້ສິ່ງທີ່ເຈົ້າກຳລັງເຮັດ *ແທ້ໆ* ແລະ ເຈົ້າໝັ້ນໃ"
"ຈວ່າ resource ດຽວນັ້ນບໍ່ໄດ້ຖືກໃຊ້ ຫຼື ຖືກຕັ້ງຄ່າໃນຫຼາຍບ່ອນພ້ອມກັນ. ຖ້າບໍ່ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ມັນຈະປອດໄພກວ່າຖ້າເຈົ້າໃ"
"ຊ້ servers API (ເຊິ່ງເປັນ thread-safe ເຕັມຮູບແບບ) ໂດຍກົງ ແລະ ບໍ່ໄປແຕະຕ້ອງ scene ຫຼື "
"resources."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:84
msgid ""
"Instancing nodes that render anything in 2D or 3D (such "
"as :ref:`class_Sprite2D` or :ref:`class_MeshInstance3D`) is *not* thread-"
"safe by default. To run the rendering driver on a separate thread, set "
"the :ref:`Rendering > Driver > Thread Model "
"<class_ProjectSettings_property_rendering/driver/threads/thread_model>` "
"project setting to **Separate**."
msgstr ""
"ການເຮັດ instancing nodes ທີ່ສະແດງຜົນ 2D ຫຼື 3D (ເຊັ່ນ: :ref:`class_Sprite2D` ຫຼື "
":ref:`class_MeshInstance3D`) ແມ່ນ *ບໍ່* thread-safe ໂດຍຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ. ເພື່ອ run "
"rendering driver ໃນ thread ທີ່ແຍກຕ່າງຫາກ, ໃຫ້ຕັ້ງຄ່າ project setting "
":ref:`Rendering > Driver > Thread Model "
"<class_ProjectSettings_property_rendering/driver/threads/thread_model>` ເປັນ "
"**Separate**."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:90
msgid ""
"Note that the **Separate** thread model has several known bugs, so it may "
"not be usable in all scenarios."
msgstr ""
"ໝາຍເຫດວ່າ thread model ແບບ **Separate** ຍັງມີ bugs ບາງຢ່າງທີ່ຮູ້ກັນຢູ່, ດັ່ງນັ້ນມັນອາດຈະບໍ່ສາມາ"
"ດໃຊ້ໄດ້ໃນທຸກສະຖານະການ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:95
msgid ""
"You should avoid calling functions involving direct interaction with the GPU "
"on other threads, such as creating new textures or modifying and retrieving "
"image data. These operations can lead to performance stalls because they "
"require synchronization with "
"the :ref:`RenderingServer<class_RenderingServer>`, as data needs to be "
"transmitted to or updated on the GPU."
msgstr ""
"ເຈົ້າຄວນຫຼີກລ່ຽງການເອີ້ນໃຊ້ຟັງຊັນທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັບການໂຕ້ຕອບໂດຍກົງກັບ GPU ໃນ thread ອື່ນ, ເຊັ່ນ: ການສ້າ"
"ງ textures ໃໝ່ ຫຼື ການແກ້ໄຂ ແລະ ດຶງຂໍ້ມູນຮູບພາບ. ການເຮັດວຽກເຫຼົ່ານີ້ສາມາດເຮັດໃຫ້ປະສິດທິພາບຢຸດສະງັ"
"ກ ເພາະພວກມັນຕ້ອງການ synchronization ກັບ "
":ref:`RenderingServer<class_RenderingServer>`, ເນື່ອງຈາກຂໍ້ມູນຕ້ອງຖືກສົ່ງໄປຫາ ຫຼື ອັບເດດໃ"
"ນ GPU."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:106
msgid ""
"Physics simulation is *not* thread-safe by default. To run the physics "
"servers on separate threads (making them thread-safe), enable the following "
"project settings:"
msgstr ""
"ການຈຳລອງຟີຊິກແມ່ນ *ບໍ່* thread-safe ໂດຍຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ. ເພື່ອ run physics servers ໃນ thread "
"ທີ່ແຍກຕ່າງຫາກ (ເພື່ອໃຫ້ພວກມັນເປັນ thread-safe), ໃຫ້ເປີດໃຊ້ project settings ຕໍ່ໄປນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:109
msgid ""
"**PhysicsServer2D:** :ref:`Physics > 2D > Run on Separate Thread "
"<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/2d/run_on_separate_thread>`."
msgstr ""
"**PhysicsServer2D:** :ref:`Physics > 2D > Run on Separate Thread "
"<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/2d/run_on_separate_thread>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:110
msgid ""
"**PhysicsServer3D:** :ref:`Physics > 3D > Run on Separate Thread "
"<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/3d/run_on_separate_thread>`."
msgstr ""
"**PhysicsServer3D:** :ref:`Physics > 3D > Run on Separate Thread "
"<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/3d/run_on_separate_thread>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:115
msgid ""
":ref:`NavigationServer2D<class_NavigationServer2D>` "
"and :ref:`NavigationServer3D<class_NavigationServer3D>` are both thread-safe "
"and thread-friendly."
msgstr ""
":ref:`NavigationServer2D<class_NavigationServer2D>` ແລະ "
":ref:`NavigationServer3D<class_NavigationServer3D>` ແມ່ນທັງ thread-safe ແລະ "
"thread-friendly."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:117
msgid ""
"The navigation-related query functions can be called by threads and run in "
"true parallel."
msgstr ""
"ຟັງຊັນການຄົ້ນຫາ (query) ທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັບ navigation ສາມາດຖືກເອີ້ນໂດຍ threads ແລະ ເຮັດວຽກແບບຂ"
"ະໜານ (parallel) ແທ້ໆໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:119
msgid ""
"By default, a conservative number of threads is supported running in true "
"parallel on navigation maps before additional threads have to wait for map "
"data access at a semaphore. To increase the number of threads that can run "
"simultaneously on map data, set :ref:`Navigation > Pathfinding > Max Threads "
"<class_ProjectSettings_property_navigation/pathfinding/max_threads>`."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ລະບົບຮອງຮັບຈຳນວນ threads ທີ່ເຮັດວຽກແບບຂະໜານແທ້ໆໃນ navigation maps ໃນລະດັ"
"ບໜຶ່ງ ກ່ອນທີ່ threads ເພີ່ມເຕີມຈະຕ້ອງລໍຖ້າການເຂົ້າເຖິງຂໍ້ມູນ map ທີ່ semaphore. ເພື່ອເພີ່ມຈຳນວນ "
"threads ທີ່ສາມາດເຮັດວຽກພ້ອມກັນໄດ້, ໃຫ້ຕັ້ງຄ່າ :ref:`Navigation > Pathfinding > Max "
"Threads <class_ProjectSettings_property_navigation/pathfinding/max_threads>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:124
msgid ""
"The navigation server-related resources like NavigationSourceGeometryData, "
"NavigationMesh, and NavigationPolygon are all thread-safe but not "
"necessarily thread-friendly. They use internal read-write locks for thread-"
"safety so editing the same resource (e.g. a single big navmesh) on multiple "
"threads at the same time can cause thread congestion."
msgstr ""
"Resources ທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັບ navigation server ເຊັ່ນ: NavigationSourceGeometryData, "
"NavigationMesh, ແລະ NavigationPolygon ແມ່ນ thread-safe ທັງໝົດ ແຕ່ບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງເປັນ "
"thread-friendly. ພວກມັນໃຊ້ read-write locks ພາຍໃນເພື່ອຄວາມປອດໄພ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນການແກ້ໄຂ "
"resource ດຽວກັນ (ເຊັ່ນ: navmesh ຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ອັນດຽວ) ຈາກຫຼາຍ threads ພ້ອມກັນອາດຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດ"
"ການຕິດຂັດຂອງ thread (thread congestion)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:127
msgid ""
"The navigation-related helper classes "
"like :ref:`AStar2D<class_AStar2D>`, :ref:`AStar3D<class_AStar3D>`, "
"and :ref:`AStarGrid2D<class_AStarGrid2D>` are **not** thread-safe. They can "
"be used with threads to some limited capacity, but using two or more threads "
"on the same AStar object causes corruption. For example, using a dedicated "
"background thread per AStar object to populate points or do queries works, "
"but two threads using the same AStar object would corrupt each other's data."
msgstr ""
"ຄລາສຊ່ວຍເຫຼືອທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັບການນຳທາງ ເຊັ່ນ :ref:`AStar2D<class_AStar2D>`, "
":ref:`AStar3D<class_AStar3D>`, ແລະ :ref:`AStarGrid2D<class_AStarGrid2D>` ແມ່ນ "
"**ບໍ່** ປອດໄພຕໍ່ເທຣດ. ພວກມັນສາມາດຖືກນຳໃຊ້ຮ່ວມກັບເທຣດໄດ້ໃນຂອບເຂດທີ່ຈຳກັດ, ແຕ່ການໃຊ້ສອງເທຣດ ຫຼື "
"ຫຼາຍກວ່ານັ້ນກັບອອບເຈັກ AStar ດຽວກັນຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ຂໍ້ມູນເສຍຫາຍ. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ, ການໃຊ້ເທຣດພື້ນຫຼັງສະເພາະຕໍ່ໜຶ່"
"ງອອບເຈັກ AStar ເພື່ອເພີ່ມຈຸດ ຫຼື ສອບຖາມຂໍ້ມູນແມ່ນສາມາດເຮັດວຽກໄດ້, ແຕ່ຫາກໃຊ້ສອງເທຣດກັບອອບເຈັກ "
"AStar ດຽວກັນ ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ຂໍ້ມູນຂອງກັນແລະກັນເສຍຫາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:133
msgid "GDScript arrays and dictionaries"
msgstr "GDScript arrays ແລະ dictionaries"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:135
msgid ""
"In GDScript, reading and writing elements from multiple threads is OK, but "
"anything that changes the container size (resizing, adding, or removing "
"elements) requires locking a :ref:`mutex "
"<doc_using_multiple_threads_mutexes>`."
msgstr ""
"ໃນ GDScript, ການອ່ານ ແລະ ຂຽນຂໍ້ມູນໃນ elements ຈາກຫຼາຍ threads ແມ່ນສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້, ແຕ່ສິ່ງໃ"
"ດກໍຕາມທີ່ປ່ຽນແປງຂະໜາດຂອງ container (ການປ່ຽນຂະໜາດ, ການເພີ່ມ, ຫຼື ການລົບ elements) ຕ້ອງມີກາ"
"ນລັອກ :ref:`mutex <doc_using_multiple_threads_mutexes>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:140
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_exports.rst:349
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:341
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/resources.rst:4
#: ../../docs/tutorials/ui/creating_applications.rst:882
#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/object_class.rst:351
#: ../../docs/engine_details/file_formats/tscn.rst:263
#: ../../docs/community/tutorials.rst:39
msgid "Resources"
msgstr "Resources"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/performance/thread_safe_apis.rst:142
msgid ""
"Modifying a unique resource from multiple threads is not supported. However, "
"handling references on multiple threads *is* supported. Hence loading "
"resources on a thread is as well - scenes, textures, meshes, etc - can be "
"loaded and manipulated on a thread and then added to the active scene on the "
"main thread. The limitation here is as described above: one must be careful "
"not to load the same resource from multiple threads at once. Therefore, it's "
"easiest to use **one** thread for loading and modifying resources, and then "
"the main thread for adding them."
msgstr ""
"ການແກ້ໄຂ unique resource ຈາກຫຼາຍ threads ແມ່ນບໍ່ຖືກຮອງຮັບ. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ການຈັດການ "
"references ໃນຫຼາຍ threads ແມ່ນ *ຖືກ* ຮອງຮັບ. ດັ່ງນັ້ນການໂຫຼດ resources ໃນ thread ກໍເຮັດໄ"
"ດ້ເຊັ່ນກັນ - scenes, textures, meshes, ແລະ ອື່ນໆ - ສາມາດຖືກໂຫຼດ ແລະ ຈັດການໃນ thread ແລ້"
"ວຈຶ່ງເພີ່ມເຂົ້າໃນ active scene ໃນ main thread. ຂໍ້ຈຳກັດຢູ່ທີ່ນີ້ຄືຕາມທີ່ໄດ້ອະທິບາຍໄວ້ຂ້າງເທິງ: ຕ້ອງລະ"
"ວັງບໍ່ໃຫ້ໂຫຼດ resource ດຽວກັນຈາກຫຼາຍ threads ພ້ອມກັນ. ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ວິທີທີ່ງ່າຍທີ່ສຸດຄືການໃຊ້ thread **ດ"
"ຽວ** ສຳລັບການໂຫຼດ ແລະ ແກ້ໄຂ resources, ແລ້ວຈຶ່ງໃຊ້ main thread ສຳລັບການເພີ່ມພວກມັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:4
msgid "Physics introduction"
msgstr "ບົດນຳກ່ຽວກັບຟີຊິກ (Physics)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:6
msgid ""
"In game development, you often need to know when two objects in the game "
"intersect or come into contact. This is known as **collision detection**. "
"When a collision is detected, you typically want something to happen. This "
"is known as **collision response**."
msgstr ""
"ໃນການພັດທະນາເກມ, ເຈົ້າມັກຈະຕ້ອງຮູ້ວ່າເມື່ອໃດວັດຖຸ 2 ຢ່າງໃນເກມຕັດກັນ ຫຼື ມາສຳຜັດກັນ. ສິ່ງນີ້ເອີ້ນວ່າ **ກ"
"ານກວດຈັບການຕຳ (collision detection)**. ເມື່ອກວດພົບການຕຳ, ໂດຍປົກກະຕິແລ້ວເຈົ້າຈະຕ້ອງການໃຫ້"
"ມີບາງຢ່າງເກີດຂຶ້ນ. ສິ່ງນີ້ເອີ້ນວ່າ **ການຕອບສະໜອງການຕຳ (collision response)**."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:11
msgid ""
"Godot offers a number of collision objects in 2D and 3D to provide both "
"collision detection and response. Trying to decide which one to use for your "
"project can be confusing. You can avoid problems and simplify development if "
"you understand how each works and what their pros and cons are."
msgstr ""
"Godot ມີ collision objects ຫຼາຍຮູບແບບທັງ 2D ແລະ 3D ເພື່ອໃຫ້ບໍລິການທັງການກວດຈັບ ແລະ ການຕອ"
"ບສະໜອງການຕຳ. ການຕັດສິນໃຈວ່າຈະໃຊ້ອັນໃດໃນໂປຣເຈັກຂອງທ່ານອາດຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ສັບສົນ. ທ່ານສາມາດຫຼີກລ່ຽງບັນ"
"ຫາ ແລະ ເຮັດໃຫ້ການພັດທະນາງ່າຍຂຶ້ນໄດ້ ຖ້າທ່ານເຂົ້າໃຈວ່າແຕ່ລະຢ່າງເຮັດວຽກແນວໃດ ແລະ ມີຂໍ້ດີຂໍ້ເສຍແນວໃດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:18
msgid "Godot's four collision object types"
msgstr "Collision object 4 ປະເພດຂອງ Godot"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:19
msgid "How each collision object works"
msgstr "ການເຮັດວຽກຂອງ collision object ແຕ່ລະຢ່າງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:20
msgid "When and why to choose one type over another"
msgstr "ຄວນເລືອກໃຊ້ປະເພດໃດໃນຕອນໃດ ແລະ ຍ້ອນຫຍັງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:22
msgid ""
"This document's examples will use 2D objects. Every 2D physics object and "
"collision shape has a direct equivalent in 3D and in most cases they work in "
"much the same way."
msgstr ""
"ຕົວຢ່າງໃນເອກະສານນີ້ຈະໃຊ້ວັດຖຸ 2D. ທຸກໆ 2D physics object ແລະ collision shape ຈະມີສິ່ງທີ່ຄືກັ"
"ນໃນ 3D ແລະ ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ແລ້ວພວກມັນຈະເຮັດວຽກໃນແບບດຽວກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:26
msgid ""
"Physics in Godot, regardless of physics engine, is **not** deterministic, "
"the nature of physics engine determinism is very complex and has to do with "
"many factors, this means physics is not guaranteed to run the same way for "
"seemingly identical situations."
msgstr ""
"ຟີຊິກໃນ Godot, ບໍ່ວ່າຈະໃຊ້ physics engine ໃດກໍຕາມ, ແມ່ນ **ບໍ່** ເປັນແບບ deterministic (ຄ"
"າດເດົາຜົນໄດ້ແນ່ນອນ), ທຳມະຊາດຂອງ physics engine determinism ແມ່ນມີຄວາມຊັບຊ້ອນຫຼາຍ ແລະ ຂຶ້"
"ນຢູ່ກັບຫຼາຍປັດໄຈ, ເຊິ່ງໝາຍຄວາມວ່າຟີຊິກບໍ່ໄດ້ຖືກຮັບປະກັນວ່າຈະເຮັດວຽກຄືກັນໃນສະຖານະການທີ່ເບິ່ງຄືວ່າຄືກັນທຸກປະ"
"ການ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:31
msgid "Collision objects"
msgstr "Collision objects"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:33
msgid ""
"Godot offers four kinds of collision objects which all "
"extend :ref:`CollisionObject2D <class_CollisionObject2D>`. The last three "
"listed below are physics bodies and additionally extend :ref:`PhysicsBody2D "
"<class_PhysicsBody2D>`."
msgstr ""
"Godot ມີ collision objects ຢູ່ 4 ປະເພດ ເຊິ່ງທັງໝົດຈະ extend ມາຈາກ "
":ref:`CollisionObject2D <class_CollisionObject2D>`. 3 ຢ່າງສຸດທ້າຍທີ່ລະບຸໄວ້ດ້ານລຸ່ມນີ້ແມ່"
"ນ physics bodies ແລະ ຍັງ extend ເພີ່ມເຕີມມາຈາກ :ref:`PhysicsBody2D "
"<class_PhysicsBody2D>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:36
msgid ":ref:`Area2D <class_Area2D>`"
msgstr ":ref:`Area2D <class_Area2D>`"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:37
msgid ""
"``Area2D`` nodes provide **detection** and **influence**. They can detect "
"when objects overlap and can emit signals when bodies enter or exit. An "
"``Area2D`` can also be used to override physics properties, such as gravity "
"or damping, in a defined area."
msgstr ""
"``Area2D`` nodes ໃຊ້ສຳລັບ **ການກວດຈັບ** ແລະ **ອິດທິພົນ**. ພວກມັນສາມາດກວດຈັບໄດ້ເມື່ອວັດຖຸຊ້ອ"
"ນທັບກັນ ແລະ ສາມາດສົ່ງສັນຍານ (signals) ເມື່ອວັດຖຸເຂົ້າມາ ຫຼື ອອກໄປ. ``Area2D`` ຍັງສາມາດໃຊ້ເພື່ອ"
"ຂຽນທັບ (override) ຄຸນສົມບັດຟີຊິກ ເຊັ່ນ: ແຮງດຶງດູດ (gravity) ຫຼື ການຫຼຸດແຮງສັ່ນສະເທືອນ "
"(damping) ໃນພື້ນທີ່ທີ່ກຳນົດໄວ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:42
msgid ":ref:`StaticBody2D <class_StaticBody2D>`"
msgstr ":ref:`StaticBody2D <class_StaticBody2D>`"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:43
msgid ""
"A static body is one that is not moved by the physics engine. It "
"participates in collision detection, but does not move in response to the "
"collision. They are most often used for objects that are part of the "
"environment or that do not need to have any dynamic behavior."
msgstr ""
"Static body ຄືວັດຖຸທີ່ບໍ່ໄດ້ຖືກຍ້າຍໂດຍ physics engine. ມັນມີສ່ວນຮ່ວມໃນການກວດຈັບການຕຳ, ແຕ່ຈະບໍ່ເ"
"ຄື່ອນທີ່ເພື່ອຕອບສະໜອງຕໍ່ການຕຳນັ້ນ. ພວກມັນມັກຈະຖືກໃຊ້ສຳລັບວັດຖຸທີ່ເປັນສ່ວນໜຶ່ງຂອງສະພາບແວດລ້ອມ ຫຼື ວັດຖຸທີ່ບໍ່ຕ້"
"ອງການພຶດຕິກຳແບບເຄື່ອນໄຫວໃດໆ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:48
msgid ":ref:`RigidBody2D <class_RigidBody2D>`"
msgstr ":ref:`RigidBody2D <class_RigidBody2D>`"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:49
msgid ""
"This is the node that implements simulated 2D physics. You do not control a "
"``RigidBody2D`` directly, but instead you apply forces to it (gravity, "
"impulses, etc.) and the physics engine calculates the resulting "
"movement. :ref:`Read more about using rigid bodies. <doc_rigid_body>`"
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ຄື node ທີ່ໃຊ້ຈຳລອງຟີຊິກ 2D. ເຈົ້າບໍ່ໄດ້ຄວບຄຸມ ``RigidBody2D`` ໂດຍກົງ, ແຕ່ເຈົ້າຈະໃຊ້ແຮງຕ່າງໆກັບ"
"ມັນ (ແຮງດຶງດູດ, ແຮງຜັກດັນ, ແລະ ອື່ນໆ) ແລ້ວ physics engine ຈະຄຳນວນການເຄື່ອນທີ່ທີ່ເກີດຂຶ້ນເອງ. "
":ref:`ອ່ານເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບການໃຊ້ rigid bodies. <doc_rigid_body>`"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:54
msgid ":ref:`CharacterBody2D <class_CharacterBody2D>`"
msgstr ":ref:`CharacterBody2D <class_CharacterBody2D>`"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:55
msgid ""
"A body that provides collision detection, but no physics. All movement and "
"collision response must be implemented in code."
msgstr ""
"ວັດຖຸທີ່ໃຫ້ການກວດຈັບການຕຳ ແຕ່ບໍ່ມີຟີຊິກໃນຕົວ. ການເຄື່ອນທີ່ ແລະ ການຕອບສະໜອງການຕຳທັງໝົດຕ້ອງຖືກຂຽນຂຶ້ນເ"
"ອງໃນ code."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:59
msgid "Physics material"
msgstr "ວັດສະດຸຟີຊິກ (Physics material)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:61
msgid ""
"Static bodies and rigid bodies can be configured to use "
"a :ref:`PhysicsMaterial <class_PhysicsMaterial>`. This allows adjusting the "
"friction and bounce of an object, and set if it's absorbent and/or rough."
msgstr ""
"Static bodies ແລະ rigid bodies ສາມາດຕັ້ງຄ່າໃຫ້ໃຊ້ :ref:`PhysicsMaterial "
"<class_PhysicsMaterial>` ໄດ້. ສິ່ງນີ້ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສາມາດປັບຄ່າຄວາມຝືດ (friction) ແລະ ການກະເດັນ "
"(bounce) ຂອງວັດຖຸໄດ້, ລວມທັງກຳນົດວ່າວັດຖຸມີຄວາມດູດຊັບ ຫຼື ຄວາມຊາ (rough) ຫຼື ບໍ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:66
msgid "Collision shapes"
msgstr "Collision shapes (ຮູບຊົງການຕຳ)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:68
msgid ""
"A physics body can hold any number of :ref:`Shape2D <class_Shape2D>` objects "
"as children. These shapes are used to define the object's collision bounds "
"and to detect contact with other objects."
msgstr ""
"Physics body ສາມາດບັນຈຸ :ref:`Shape2D <class_Shape2D>` objects ຈຳນວນເທົ່າໃດກໍໄດ້ເປັ"
"ນ node ລູກ. ຮູບຊົງເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຖືກໃຊ້ເພື່ອລະບຸຂອບເຂດການຕຳຂອງວັດຖຸ ແລະ ເພື່ອກວດຈັບການສຳຜັດກັບວັດຖຸອື່ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:72
msgid ""
"In order to detect collisions, at least one ``Shape2D`` must be assigned to "
"the object."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອໃຫ້ກວດຈັບການຕຳໄດ້, ຕ້ອງມີຢ່າງໜ້ອຍໜຶ່ງ ``Shape2D`` ຖືກກຳນົດໃຫ້ກັບວັດຖຸ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:75
msgid ""
"The most common way to assign a shape is by adding a :ref:`CollisionShape2D "
"<class_CollisionShape2D>` or :ref:`CollisionPolygon2D "
"<class_CollisionPolygon2D>` as a child of the object. These nodes allow you "
"to draw the shape directly in the editor workspace."
msgstr ""
"ວິທີທີ່ນິຍົມທີ່ສຸດໃນການກຳນົດຮູບຊົງຄື ການເພີ່ມ :ref:`CollisionShape2D "
"<class_CollisionShape2D>` ຫຼື :ref:`CollisionPolygon2D "
"<class_CollisionPolygon2D>` ເປັນ node ລູກຂອງວັດຖຸ. node ເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ເຈົ້າສາມາດແຕ້ມຮູບຊົງໄ"
"ດ້ໂດຍກົງໃນ editor workspace."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:79
msgid ""
"Be careful to never scale your collision shapes in the editor. The \"Scale\" "
"property in the Inspector should remain ``(1, 1)``. When changing the size "
"of the collision shape, you should always use the size handles, **not** the "
"``Node2D`` scale handles. Scaling a shape can result in unexpected collision "
"behavior."
msgstr ""
"ລະວັງຢ່າປັບຂະໜາດ (scale) collision shapes ຂອງທ່ານໃນ editor. ຄຸນສົມບັດ \"Scale\" ໃນ "
"Inspector ຄວນເປັນ ``(1, 1)`` ສະເໝີ. ເມື່ອປ່ຽນຂະໜາດຂອງ collision shape, ເຈົ້າຄວນໃຊ້ປຸ່ມປັ"
"ບຂະໜາດ (handles) ຂອງມັນສະເໝີ, **ບໍ່ແມ່ນ** handles ຂອງ ``Node2D``. ການ scale ຮູບຊົງອາ"
"ດຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດພຶດຕິກຳການຕຳທີ່ຜິດພາດໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:88
msgid "Physics process callback"
msgstr "Physics process callback"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:90
msgid ""
"The physics engine runs at a fixed rate (a default of 60 iterations per "
"second). This rate is typically different from the frame rate which "
"fluctuates based on what is rendered and available resources."
msgstr ""
"Physics engine ຈະເຮັດວຽກໃນອັດຕາທີ່ຄົງທີ່ (ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນຄື 60 ຄັ້ງຕໍ່ວິນາທີ). ອັດຕານີ້ມັກຈະຕ່າງຈາກ "
"frame rate ເຊິ່ງຈະປ່ຽນແປງຕາມສິ່ງທີ່ຖືກສະແດງຜົນ ແລະ ຊັບພະຍາກອນທີ່ມີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:94
msgid ""
"It is important that all physics related code runs at this fixed rate. "
"Therefore Godot differentiates :ref:`between physics and idle processing "
"<doc_idle_and_physics_processing>`. Code that runs each frame is called idle "
"processing and code that runs on each physics tick is called physics "
"processing. Godot provides two different callbacks, one for each of those "
"processing rates."
msgstr ""
"ມັນເປັນສິ່ງສຳຄັນທີ່ code ທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັບຟີຊິກທັງໝົດຕ້ອງເຮັດວຽກໃນອັດຕາຄົງທີ່ນີ້. ດັ່ງນັ້ນ Godot ຈຶ່ງແຍກຄວາມແຕ"
"ກຕ່າງລະຫວ່າງ :ref:`physics ແລະ idle processing "
"<doc_idle_and_physics_processing>`. code ທີ່ເຮັດວຽກໃນທຸກໆເຟຣມເອີ້ນວ່າ idle "
"processing ແລະ code ທີ່ເຮັດວຽກໃນທຸກໆ physics tick ເອີ້ນວ່າ physics processing. "
"Godot ມີ 2 callbacks ທີ່ຕ່າງກັນສຳລັບແຕ່ລະອັດຕາການປະມວນຜົນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:100
msgid ""
"The physics callback, :ref:`Node._physics_process() "
"<class_Node_private_method__physics_process>`, is called before each physics "
"step. Any code that needs to access a body's properties should be run in "
"here. This method will be passed a ``delta`` parameter, which is a floating-"
"point number equal to the time passed in *seconds* since the last step. When "
"using the default 60 Hz physics update rate, it will typically be equal to "
"``0.01666...`` (but not always, see below)."
msgstr ""
"Physics callback, :ref:`Node._physics_process() "
"<class_Node_private_method__physics_process>`, ຈະຖືກເອີ້ນກ່ອນແຕ່ລະຂັ້ນຕອນຟີຊິກ. code ໃ"
"ດກໍຕາມທີ່ຕ້ອງການເຂົ້າເຖິງຄຸນສົມບັດຂອງ body ຄວນຖືກ run ຢູ່ບ່ອນນີ້. method ນີ້ຈະໄດ້ຮັບພາລາມິເຕີ "
"``delta``, ເຊິ່ງເປັນຕົວເລກ floating-point ທີ່ມີຄ່າເທົ່າກັບເວລາທີ່ຜ່ານໄປເປັນ *ວິນາທີ* ນັບຕັ້ງແຕ່ຂັ້ນຕ"
"ອນຫຼ້າສຸດ. ເມື່ອໃຊ້ physics update rate 60 Hz ຕາມຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ໂດຍປົກກະຕິແລ້ວມັນຈະມີຄ່າເທົ່າກັບ "
"``0.01666...``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:109
msgid ""
"It's recommended to always use the ``delta`` parameter when relevant in your "
"physics calculations, so that the game behaves correctly if you change the "
"physics update rate or if the player's device can't keep up."
msgstr ""
"ແນະນຳໃຫ້ໃຊ້ພາລາມິເຕີ ``delta`` ສະເໝີເມື່ອມີການຄຳນວນຟີຊິກ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ເກມເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ຢ່າງຖືກຕ້ອງ ຖ້າເຈົ້າ"
"ປ່ຽນ physics update rate ຫຼື ຖ້າອຸປະກອນຂອງຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນປະມວນຜົນບໍ່ທັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:116
msgid "Collision layers and masks"
msgstr "Collision layers ແລະ masks"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:118
msgid ""
"One of the most powerful, but frequently misunderstood, collision features "
"is the collision layer system. This system allows you to build up complex "
"interactions between a variety of objects. The key concepts are **layers** "
"and **masks**. Each ``CollisionObject2D`` has 32 different physics layers it "
"can interact with."
msgstr ""
"ໜຶ່ງໃນຟີເຈີການຕຳທີ່ມີປະສິດທິພາບຫຼາຍ ແຕ່ມັກຈະຖືກເຂົ້າໃຈຜິດເລື້ອຍໆຄື ລະບົບ collision layer. ລະບົບນີ້ຊ່ວ"
"ຍໃຫ້ເຈົ້າສ້າງການໂຕ້ຕອບທີ່ຊັບຊ້ອນລະຫວ່າງວັດຖຸທີ່ຫຼາກຫຼາຍໄດ້. ແນວຄວາມຄິດຫຼັກຄື **layers** ແລະ "
"**masks**. ແຕ່ລະ ``CollisionObject2D`` ຈະມີ physics layers 32 ຊັ້ນທີ່ມັນສາມາດໂຕ້ຕອບໄ"
"ດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:124
msgid "Let's look at each of the properties in turn:"
msgstr "ລອງມາເບິ່ງແຕ່ລະຄຸນສົມບັດຕາມລຳດັບ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:126
msgid "collision_layer"
msgstr "collision_layer"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:127
msgid ""
"This describes the layers that the object appears **in**. By default, all "
"bodies are on layer ``1``."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງນີ້ບອກວ່າວັດຖຸນີ້ **ຢູ່** ໃນ layer ໃດ. ໂດຍຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ທຸກໆ bodies ຈະຢູ່ໃນ layer ``1``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:130
msgid "collision_mask"
msgstr "collision_mask"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:131
msgid ""
"This describes what layers the body will **scan** for collisions. If an "
"object isn't in one of the mask layers, the body will ignore it. By default, "
"all bodies scan layer ``1``."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງນີ້ບອກວ່າ body ນີ້ຈະ **ກວດສອບ (scan)** ການຕຳໃນ layer ໃດແດ່. ຖ້າວັດຖຸອື່ນບໍ່ໄດ້ຢູ່ໃນ layer ທີ່"
"ກຳນົດໄວ້ໃນ mask, body ນີ້ກໍຈະເມີນວັດຖຸນັ້ນໄປ. ໂດຍຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ທຸກໆ bodies ຈະກວດສອບ layer "
"``1``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:135
msgid ""
"These properties can be configured via code, or by editing them in the "
"Inspector."
msgstr ""
"ຄຸນສົມບັດເຫຼົ່ານີ້ສາມາດຕັ້ງຄ່າໄດ້ຜ່ານ code, ຫຼື ແກ້ໄຂພວກມັນໃນ Inspector."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:137
msgid ""
"Keeping track of what you're using each layer for can be difficult, so you "
"may find it useful to assign names to the layers you're using. Names can be "
"assigned in **Project Settings > Layer Names > 2D Physics**."
msgstr ""
"ການຈື່ວ່າແຕ່ລະ layer ໃຊ້ເຮັດຫຍັງອາດຈະເປັນເລື່ອງຍາກ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນເຈົ້າອາດຈະພົບວ່າມັນມີປະໂຫຍດຖ້າຕັ້ງຊື່ໃຫ້ກັບ "
"layers ທີ່ໃຊ້ຢູ່. ສາມາດຕັ້ງຊື່ໄດ້ໃນ **Project Settings > Layer Names > 2D Physics**."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:144
msgid "GUI example"
msgstr "ຕົວຢ່າງ GUI"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:146
msgid ""
"You have four node types in your game: Walls, Player, Enemy, and Coin. Both "
"Player and Enemy should collide with Walls. The Player node should detect "
"collisions with both Enemy and Coin, but Enemy and Coin should ignore each "
"other."
msgstr ""
"ເຈົ້າມີ node 4 ປະເພດໃນເກມ: Walls (ກຳແພງ), Player (ຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນ), Enemy (ສັດຕູ), ແລະ Coin (ຫຼ"
"ຽນ). ທັງ Player ແລະ Enemy ຄວນຕຳກັບ Walls. Player ຄວນກວດຈັບການຕຳກັບທັງ Enemy ແລະ "
"Coin, ແຕ່ Enemy ແລະ Coin ຄວນເມີນກັນແລະກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:151
msgid ""
"Start by naming layers 1-4 \"walls\", \"player\", \"enemies\", and \"coins\" "
"and place each node type in its respective layer using the \"Layer\" "
"property. Then set each node's \"Mask\" property by selecting the layers it "
"should interact with. For example, the Player's settings would look like "
"this:"
msgstr ""
"ເລີ່ມຕົ້ນໂດຍການຕັ້ງຊື່ layers 1-4 ວ່າ \"walls\", \"player\", \"enemies\", ແລະ "
"\"coins\" ແລະ ວາງ node ແຕ່ລະປະເພດລົງໃນ layer ຂອງມັນເອງໂດຍໃຊ້ຄຸນສົມບັດ \"Layer\". ຈາກ"
"ນັ້ນໃຫ້ຕັ້ງຄ່າ \"Mask\" ຂອງແຕ່ລະ node ໂດຍເລືອກ layer ທີ່ມັນຄວນຈະໂຕ້ຕອບນຳ. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ: ການຕັ້ງ"
"ຄ່າຂອງ Player ຈະເປັນແບບນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:162
msgid "Code example"
msgstr "ຕົວຢ່າງ Code"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:164
msgid ""
"In function calls, layers are specified as a bitmask. Where a function "
"enables all layers by default, the layer mask will be given as "
"``0xffffffff``. Your code can use binary, hexadecimal, or decimal notation "
"for layer masks, depending on your preference."
msgstr ""
"ໃນການເອີ້ນໃຊ້ຟັງຊັນ, layers ຈະຖືກລະບຸເປັນ bitmask. ຖ້າຟັງຊັນໃດໜຶ່ງເປີດໃຊ້ທຸກ layers ຕາມຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້"
"ນ, layer mask ຈະມີຄ່າເປັນ ``0xffffffff``. code ຂອງທ່ານສາມາດໃຊ້ເລກຖານສອງ, ຖານສິບຫົກ, "
"ຫຼື ຖານສິບ ສຳລັບ layer masks ໄດ້ຕາມຄວາມສະດວກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:169
msgid ""
"The code equivalent of the above example where layers 1, 3 and 4 were "
"enabled would be as follows:"
msgstr ""
"ລະຫັດທີ່ທຽບເທົ່າກັບຕົວຢ່າງຂ້າງເທິງ ບ່ອນທີ່ເລເຢີ 1, 3 ແລະ 4 ຖືກເປີດໃຊ້ງານ ຈະເປັນດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:197
msgid ""
"You can also set bits independently by calling "
"``set_collision_layer_value(layer_number, value)`` or "
"``set_collision_mask_value(layer_number, value)`` on any "
"given :ref:`CollisionObject2D <class_CollisionObject2D>` as follows:"
msgstr ""
"ເຈົ້າຍັງສາມາດຕັ້ງ bits ແຍກກັນໄດ້ໂດຍການເອີ້ນໃຊ້ ``set_collision_layer_value"
"(layer_number, value)`` ຫຼື ``set_collision_mask_value(layer_number, value)`` ໃ"
"ນ :ref:`CollisionObject2D <class_CollisionObject2D>` ໃດໜຶ່ງດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:209
msgid ""
"Export annotations can be used to export bitmasks in the editor with a user-"
"friendly GUI:"
msgstr ""
"Export annotations ສາມາດນຳມາໃຊ້ເພື່ອສົ່ງອອກ bitmasks ໄປຍັງ editor ດ້ວຍ GUI ທີ່ໃຊ້ງານງ່າ"
"ຍ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:215
msgid ""
"Additional export annotations are available for render and navigation "
"layers, in both 2D and 3D. "
"See :ref:`doc_gdscript_exports_exporting_bit_flags`."
msgstr ""
"ຍັງມີ export annotations ເພີ່ມເຕີມສຳລັບ render ແລະ navigation layers ທັງໃນ 2D ແລະ "
"3D. ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_gdscript_exports_exporting_bit_flags`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:218
msgid "Area2D"
msgstr "Area2D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:220
msgid ""
"Area nodes provide **detection** and **influence**. They can detect when "
"objects overlap and emit signals when bodies enter or exit. Areas can also "
"be used to override physics properties, such as gravity or damping, in a "
"defined area."
msgstr ""
"Area nodes ໃຊ້ສຳລັບ **ການກວດຈັບ** ແລະ **ອິດທິພົນ**. ພວກມັນສາມາດກວດຈັບໄດ້ເມື່ອວັດຖຸຊ້ອນທັບກັນ "
"ແລະ ສົ່ງສັນຍານເມື່ອ bodies ເຂົ້າມາ ຫຼື ອອກໄປ. Areas ຍັງສາມາດໃຊ້ເພື່ອ override ຄຸນສົມບັດຟີຊິກ ເຊັ່"
"ນ: gravity ຫຼື damping ໃນພື້ນທີ່ທີ່ກຳນົດໄວ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:225
msgid "There are three main uses for :ref:`Area2D <class_Area2D>`:"
msgstr "ມີ 3 ການໃຊ້ງານຫຼັກສຳລັບ :ref:`Area2D <class_Area2D>`:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:227
msgid "Overriding physics parameters (such as gravity) in a given region."
msgstr "ການ override ພາລາມິເຕີຟີຊິກ (ເຊັ່ນ gravity) ໃນພື້ນທີ່ໃດໜຶ່ງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:229
msgid ""
"Detecting when other bodies enter or exit a region or what bodies are "
"currently in a region."
msgstr ""
"ການກວດຈັບເມື່ອ bodies ອື່ນໆເຂົ້າມາ ຫຼື ອອກຈາກພື້ນທີ່ ຫຼື ກວດສອບວ່າ bodies ໃດແດ່ທີ່ຢູ່ໃນພື້ນທີ່ນັ້ນໃນຕອນ"
"ນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:231
msgid "Checking other areas for overlap."
msgstr "ການກວດສອບການຊ້ອນທັບກັບ areas ອື່ນໆ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:233
msgid "By default, areas also receive mouse and touchscreen input."
msgstr "ໂດຍຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, areas ຍັງສາມາດຮັບ input ຈາກເມົ້າ ແລະ ໜ້າຈໍສຳຜັດໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:236
msgid "StaticBody2D"
msgstr "StaticBody2D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:238
msgid ""
"A static body is one that is not moved by the physics engine. It "
"participates in collision detection, but does not move in response to the "
"collision. However, it can impart motion or rotation to a colliding body "
"**as if** it were moving, using its ``constant_linear_velocity`` and "
"``constant_angular_velocity`` properties."
msgstr ""
"Static body ຄືວັດຖຸທີ່ບໍ່ໄດ້ຖືກຍ້າຍໂດຍ physics engine. ມັນມີສ່ວນຮ່ວມໃນການກວດຈັບການຕຳ, ແຕ່ຈະບໍ່ເ"
"ຄື່ອນທີ່ເພື່ອຕອບສະໜອງຕໍ່ການຕຳນັ້ນ. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ມັນສາມາດສົ່ງຜົນຕໍ່ການເຄື່ອນທີ່ ຫຼື ການໝູນໃຫ້ກັບ body ທີ່ມາ"
"ຕຳ **ຄືກັບວ່າ** ມັນກຳລັງເຄື່ອນທີ່ຢູ່ ໂດຍໃຊ້ຄຸນສົມບັດ ``constant_linear_velocity`` ແລະ "
"``constant_angular_velocity``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:243
msgid ""
"``StaticBody2D`` nodes are most often used for objects that are part of the "
"environment or that do not need to have any dynamic behavior."
msgstr ""
"``StaticBody2D`` nodes ມັກຈະຖືກໃຊ້ສຳລັບວັດຖຸທີ່ເປັນສ່ວນໜຶ່ງຂອງສະພາບແວດລ້ອມ ຫຼື ວັດຖຸທີ່ບໍ່ຕ້ອງການພຶດ"
"ຕິກຳແບບເຄື່ອນໄຫວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:246
msgid "Example uses for ``StaticBody2D``:"
msgstr "ຕົວຢ່າງການໃຊ້ງານ ``StaticBody2D``:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:248
msgid "Platforms (including moving platforms)"
msgstr "ແທ່ນຢືນ (Platforms) (ລວມທັງແທ່ນຢືນທີ່ເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄດ້)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:249
msgid "Conveyor belts"
msgstr "ສາຍພານລຳລຽງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:250
msgid "Walls and other obstacles"
msgstr "ກຳແພງ ແລະ ສິ່ງກີດຂວາງອື່ນໆ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:253
msgid "RigidBody2D"
msgstr "RigidBody2D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:255
msgid ""
"This is the node that implements simulated 2D physics. You do not control "
"a :ref:`RigidBody2D <class_RigidBody2D>` directly. Instead, you apply forces "
"to it and the physics engine calculates the resulting movement, including "
"collisions with other bodies, and collision responses, such as bouncing, "
"rotating, etc."
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ຄື node ທີ່ໃຊ້ຈຳລອງຟີຊິກ 2D. ເຈົ້າບໍ່ໄດ້ຄວບຄຸມ :ref:`RigidBody2D <class_RigidBody2D>` ໂດ"
"ຍກົງ. ແຕ່ເຈົ້າຈະໃຊ້ແຮງຕ່າງໆກັບມັນ ແລ້ວ physics engine ຈະຄຳນວນການເຄື່ອນທີ່ທີ່ເກີດຂຶ້ນເອງ, ລວມທັງກ"
"ານຕຳກັບ bodies ອື່ນໆ ແລະ ການຕອບສະໜອງການຕຳ ເຊັ່ນ ການກະເດັນ, ການໝູນ, ແລະ ອື່ນໆ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:261
msgid ""
"You can modify a rigid body's behavior via properties such as \"Mass\", "
"\"Friction\", or \"Bounce\", which can be set in the Inspector."
msgstr ""
"ເຈົ້າສາມາດແກ້ໄຂພຶດຕິກຳຂອງ rigid body ໄດ້ຜ່ານຄຸນສົມບັດ ເຊັ່ນ \"Mass\" (ມວນສານ), "
"\"Friction\" (ຄວາມຝືດ), ຫຼື \"Bounce\" (ການກະເດັນ), ເຊິ່ງສາມາດຕັ້ງຄ່າໄດ້ໃນ Inspector."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:264
msgid ""
"The body's behavior is also affected by the world's properties, as set in "
"**Project Settings > Physics**, or by entering an :ref:`Area2D "
"<class_Area2D>` that is overriding the global physics properties."
msgstr ""
"ພຶດຕິກຳຂອງ body ຍັງໄດ້ຮັບຜົນກະທົບຈາກຄຸນສົມບັດຂອງໂລກ, ຕາມທີ່ຕັ້ງຄ່າໄວ້ໃນ **Project Settings > "
"Physics**, ຫຼື ໂດຍການເຂົ້າໄປໃນ :ref:`Area2D <class_Area2D>` ທີ່ມີການ override ຄຸນສົມບັດ"
"ຟີຊິກທົ່ວໂລກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:268
msgid ""
"When a rigid body is at rest and hasn't moved for a while, it goes to sleep. "
"A sleeping body acts like a static body, and its forces are not calculated "
"by the physics engine. The body will wake up when forces are applied, either "
"by a collision or via code."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອ rigid body ຢຸດນິ່ງ ແລະ ບໍ່ໄດ້ເຄື່ອນທີ່ມາໄລຍະໜຶ່ງ, ມັນຈະເຂົ້າສູ່ສະພາວະຫຼັບ (sleep). body ທີ່ຫຼັບຢູ່"
"ຈະເຮັດວຽກຄືກັບ static body, ແລະ physics engine ຈະບໍ່ຄຳນວນແຮງຕ່າງໆໃຫ້ກັບມັນ. body ຈະຕື່ນຂຶ້"
"ນເມື່ອມີແຮງມາກະທົບ, ບໍ່ວ່າຈະມາຈາກການຕຳ ຫຼື ຜ່ານ code."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:274
msgid "Using RigidBody2D"
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ RigidBody2D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:276
msgid ""
"One of the benefits of using a rigid body is that a lot of behavior can be "
"had \"for free\" without writing any code. For example, if you were making "
"an \"Angry Birds\"-style game with falling blocks, you would only need to "
"create RigidBody2Ds and adjust their properties. Stacking, falling, and "
"bouncing would automatically be calculated by the physics engine."
msgstr ""
"ໜຶ່ງໃນປະໂຫຍດຂອງການໃຊ້ rigid body ຄືເຈົ້າຈະໄດ້ພຶດຕິກຳຫຼາຍຢ່າງມາໃຊ້ແບບ \"ຟຣີໆ\" ໂດຍບໍ່ຕ້ອງຂຽນ "
"code ໃດໆ. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ: ຖ້າເຈົ້າກຳລັງສ້າງເກມແບບ \"Angry Birds\" ທີ່ມີບລັອກຕົກລົງມາ, ເຈົ້າພຽງແຕ່"
"ຕ້ອງສ້າງ RigidBody2Ds ແລະ ປັບຄຸນສົມບັດຂອງພວກມັນ. ການຊ້ອນກັນ, ການຕົກ, ແລະ ການກະເດັນຈະຖືກຄຳ"
"ນວນໂດຍ physics engine ໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:282
msgid ""
"However, if you do wish to have some control over the body, you should take "
"care - altering the ``position``, ``linear_velocity``, or other physics "
"properties of a rigid body can result in unexpected behavior. If you need to "
"alter any of the physics-related properties, you should use "
"the :ref:`_integrate_forces() "
"<class_RigidBody2D_private_method__integrate_forces>` callback instead of "
"``_physics_process()``. In this callback, you have access to the "
"body's :ref:`PhysicsDirectBodyState2D <class_PhysicsDirectBodyState2D>`, "
"which allows for safely changing properties and synchronizing them with the "
"physics engine."
msgstr ""
"ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການຄວບຄຸມ body ເອງບາງສ່ວນ, ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງລະວັງ - ການປ່ຽນແປງ "
"``position``, ``linear_velocity``, ຫຼື ຄຸນສົມບັດຟີຊິກອື່ນໆຂອງ rigid body ອາດຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດ"
"ພຶດຕິກຳທີ່ບໍ່ຄາດຄິດ. ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການແກ້ໄຂຄຸນສົມບັດທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັບຟີຊິກ, ເຈົ້າຄວນໃຊ້ callback "
":ref:`_integrate_forces() "
"<class_RigidBody2D_private_method__integrate_forces>` ແທນ ``_physics_process"
"()``. ໃນ callback ນີ້, ເຈົ້າສາມາດເຂົ້າເຖິງ :ref:`PhysicsDirectBodyState2D "
"<class_PhysicsDirectBodyState2D>` ຂອງ body, ເຊິ່ງຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສາມາດປ່ຽນແປງຄຸນສົມບັດໄດ້ຢ່າງປອດ"
"ໄພ ແລະ sync ພວກມັນກັບ physics engine ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:291
msgid "For example, here is the code for an \"Asteroids\" style spaceship:"
msgstr "ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ: ນີ້ຄື code ສຳລັບຍານອາວະກາດແບບເກມ \"Asteroids\":"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:346
msgid ""
"Note that we are not setting the ``linear_velocity`` or ``angular_velocity`` "
"properties directly, but rather applying forces (``thrust`` and ``torque``) "
"to the body and letting the physics engine calculate the resulting movement."
msgstr ""
"ໝາຍເຫດວ່າພວກເຮົາບໍ່ໄດ້ຕັ້ງຄ່າ ``linear_velocity`` ຫຼື ``angular_velocity`` ໂດຍກົງ, ແຕ່ເປັນ"
"ການໃຊ້ແຮງ (``thrust`` ແລະ ``torque``) ກັບ body ແລະ ປ່ອຍໃຫ້ physics engine ຄຳນວນກາ"
"ນເຄື່ອນທີ່ທີ່ເກີດຂຶ້ນເອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:350
msgid ""
"When a rigid body goes to sleep, the ``_integrate_forces()`` function will "
"not be called. To override this behavior, you will need to keep the body "
"awake by creating a collision, applying a force to it, or by disabling "
"the :ref:`can_sleep <class_RigidBody2D_property_can_sleep>` property. Be "
"aware that this can have a negative effect on performance."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອ rigid body ເຂົ້າສູ່ສະພາວະຫຼັບ, ຟັງຊັນ ``_integrate_forces()`` ຈະບໍ່ຖືກເອີ້ນໃຊ້. ເພື່ອ "
"override ພຶດຕິກຳນີ້, ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງເຮັດໃຫ້ body ຕື່ນຢູ່ສະເໝີໂດຍການສ້າງການຕຳ, ໃຊ້ແຮງກັບມັນ, ຫຼື ປິດຄຸນສົມບັ"
"ດ :ref:`can_sleep <class_RigidBody2D_property_can_sleep>`. ແຕ່ໃຫ້ຮູ້ໄວ້ວ່າສິ່ງນີ້ອາດຈະສົ່"
"ງຜົນເສຍຕໍ່ປະສິດທິພາບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:357
msgid "Contact reporting"
msgstr "ການລາຍງານການສຳຜັດ (Contact reporting)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:359
msgid ""
"By default, rigid bodies do not keep track of contacts, because this can "
"require a huge amount of memory if many bodies are in the scene. To enable "
"contact reporting, set the :ref:`max_contacts_reported "
"<class_RigidBody2D_property_max_contacts_reported>` property to a non-zero "
"value. The contacts can then be obtained "
"via :ref:`PhysicsDirectBodyState2D.get_contact_count() "
"<class_PhysicsDirectBodyState2D_method_get_contact_count>` and related "
"functions."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, rigid bodies ຈະບໍ່ຕິດຕາມການສຳຜັດ, ເພາະສິ່ງນີ້ອາດຈະຕ້ອງໃຊ້ memory ມະຫາສານຖ້າ"
"ມີ bodies ຈຳນວນຫຼາຍໃນສາກ. ເພື່ອເປີດໃຊ້ການລາຍງານການສຳຜັດ, ໃຫ້ຕັ້ງຄ່າ "
":ref:`max_contacts_reported "
"<class_RigidBody2D_property_max_contacts_reported>` ໃຫ້ເປັນຄ່າທີ່ບໍ່ແມ່ນສູນ. ຈາກນັ້ນສາມາ"
"ດດຶງຂໍ້ມູນການສຳຜັດໄດ້ຜ່ານ :ref:`PhysicsDirectBodyState2D.get_contact_count() "
"<class_PhysicsDirectBodyState2D_method_get_contact_count>` ແລະ ຟັງຊັນອື່ນໆທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອ"
"ງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:366
msgid ""
"Contact monitoring via signals can be enabled via the :ref:`contact_monitor "
"<class_RigidBody2D_property_contact_monitor>` property. "
"See :ref:`RigidBody2D <class_RigidBody2D>` for the list of available signals."
msgstr ""
"ການຕິດຕາມການສຳຜັດຜ່ານ signals ສາມາດເປີດໃຊ້ໄດ້ຜ່ານຄຸນສົມບັດ :ref:`contact_monitor "
"<class_RigidBody2D_property_contact_monitor>`. ເບິ່ງ :ref:`RigidBody2D "
"<class_RigidBody2D>` ສຳລັບລາຍການ signals ທີ່ມີໃຫ້ໃຊ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:373
msgid ""
":ref:`CharacterBody2D <class_CharacterBody2D>` bodies detect collisions with "
"other bodies, but are not affected by physics properties like gravity or "
"friction. Instead, they must be controlled by the user via code. The physics "
"engine will not move a character body."
msgstr ""
":ref:`CharacterBody2D <class_CharacterBody2D>` bodies ສາມາດກວດຈັບການຕຳກັບ "
"bodies ອື່ນໆໄດ້, ແຕ່ບໍ່ໄດ້ຮັບຜົນກະທົບຈາກຄຸນສົມບັດຟີຊິກ ເຊັ່ນ gravity ຫຼື friction. ແຕ່ພວກມັນຕ້ອງຖືກຄ"
"ວບຄຸມໂດຍຜູ້ໃຊ້ຜ່ານ code. physics engine ຈະບໍ່ເຄື່ອນຍ້າຍ character body ເອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:378
msgid ""
"When moving a character body, you should not set its ``position`` directly. "
"Instead, you use the ``move_and_collide()`` or ``move_and_slide()`` methods. "
"These methods move the body along a given vector, and it will instantly stop "
"if a collision is detected with another body. After the body has collided, "
"any collision response must be coded manually."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອເຄື່ອນຍ້າຍ character body, ເຈົ້າບໍ່ຄວນຕັ້ງຄ່າ ``position`` ຂອງມັນໂດຍກົງ. ແຕ່ເຈົ້າຄວນໃຊ້ "
"method ``move_and_collide()`` ຫຼື ``move_and_slide()``. method ເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຈະຍ້າຍ body ໄ"
"ປຕາມ vector ທີ່ກຳນົດໄວ້, ແລະ ມັນຈະຢຸດທັນທີຖ້າກວດພົບການຕຳກັບ body ອື່ນ. ຫຼັງຈາກ body ຕຳແລ້ວ, ກ"
"ານຕອບສະໜອງການຕຳໃດໆ ຕ້ອງຖືກຂຽນ code ຈັດການເອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:385
msgid "Character collision response"
msgstr "ການຕອບສະໜອງການຕຳຂອງ Character"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:387
msgid ""
"After a collision, you may want the body to bounce, to slide along a wall, "
"or to alter the properties of the object it hit. The way you handle "
"collision response depends on which method you used to move the "
"CharacterBody2D."
msgstr ""
"ຫຼັງຈາກການຕຳ, ເຈົ້າອາດຈະຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ body ກະເດັນ, ໄຖໄປຕາມກຳແພງ, ຫຼື ປ່ຽນແປງຄຸນສົມບັດຂອງວັດຖຸທີ່ມັ"
"ນໄປຕຳ. ວິທີທີ່ເຈົ້າຈັດການກັບການຕອບສະໜອງການຕຳແມ່ນຂຶ້ນຢູ່ກັບວ່າເຈົ້າໃຊ້ method ໃດໃນການເຄື່ອນຍ້າຍ "
"CharacterBody2D."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:392
msgid ":ref:`move_and_collide <class_PhysicsBody2D_method_move_and_collide>`"
msgstr ":ref:`move_and_collide <class_PhysicsBody2D_method_move_and_collide>`"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:394
msgid ""
"When using ``move_and_collide()``, the function returns "
"a :ref:`KinematicCollision2D <class_KinematicCollision2D>` object, which "
"contains information about the collision and the colliding body. You can use "
"this information to determine the response."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອໃຊ້ ``move_and_collide()``, ຟັງຊັນຈະ return :ref:`KinematicCollision2D "
"<class_KinematicCollision2D>` object, ເຊິ່ງບັນຈຸຂໍ້ມູນກ່ຽວກັບການຕຳ ແລະ body ທີ່ມາຕຳ. ເຈົ້າ"
"ສາມາດໃຊ້ຂໍ້ມູນນີ້ເພື່ອຕັດສິນໃຈການຕອບສະໜອງໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:399
msgid ""
"For example, if you want to find the point in space where the collision "
"occurred:"
msgstr "ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ: ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການຫາຈຸດໃນອາວະກາດທີ່ການຕຳເກີດຂຶ້ນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:432
msgid "Or to bounce off of the colliding object:"
msgstr "ຫຼື ເພື່ອກະເດັນອອກຈາກວັດຖຸທີ່ຕຳ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:465
msgid ":ref:`move_and_slide <class_CharacterBody2D_method_move_and_slide>`"
msgstr ":ref:`move_and_slide <class_CharacterBody2D_method_move_and_slide>`"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:467
msgid ""
"Sliding is a common collision response; imagine a player moving along walls "
"in a top-down game or running up and down slopes in a platformer. While it's "
"possible to code this response yourself after using ``move_and_collide()``, "
"``move_and_slide()`` provides a convenient way to implement sliding movement "
"without writing much code."
msgstr ""
"ການໄຖ (Sliding) ແມ່ນການຕອບສະໜອງການຕຳທີ່ພົບເລື້ອຍ; ລອງນຶກພາບຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນທີ່ເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄປຕາມກຳແພງໃນເກມມຸ"
"ມມອງຈາກດ້ານເທິງ ຫຼື ແລ່ນຂຶ້ນລົງທາງລາດຊັນໃນເກມ platformer. ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າເຈົ້າສາມາດຂຽນ code ຈັດກ"
"ານການຕອບສະໜອງນີ້ເອງໄດ້ຫຼັງຈາກໃຊ້ ``move_and_collide()``, ແຕ່ ``move_and_slide()`` ກໍມີ"
"ວິທີທີ່ສະດວກໃນການເຮັດການເຄື່ອນທີ່ແບບໄຖໂດຍບໍ່ຕ້ອງຂຽນ code ຫຼາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:473
msgid ""
"``move_and_slide()`` automatically includes the timestep in its calculation, "
"so you should **not** multiply the velocity vector by ``delta``. This does "
"**not** apply to ``gravity`` as it is an acceleration and is time dependent, "
"and needs to be scaled by ``delta``."
msgstr ""
"``move_and_slide()`` ຈະລວມ timestep ເຂົ້າໃນການຄຳນວນໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນເຈົ້າ **ບໍ່ຄວ"
"ນ** ຄູນ velocity vector ດ້ວຍ ``delta``. ແຕ່ສິ່ງນີ້ **ບໍ່ໃຊ້** ກັບ ``gravity`` ເພາະມັນເປັນຄ"
"ວາມເລັ່ງ ແລະ ຂຶ້ນຢູ່ກັບເວລາ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນມັນຈຶ່ງຕ້ອງຖືກຄູນດ້ວຍ ``delta``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:479
msgid ""
"For example, use the following code to make a character that can walk along "
"the ground (including slopes) and jump when standing on the ground:"
msgstr ""
"ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ: ໃຊ້ code ຕໍ່ໄປນີ້ເພື່ອສ້າງຕົວລະຄອນທີ່ສາມາດຍ່າງຕາມພື້ນ (ລວມທັງທາງລາດຊັນ) ແລະ ກະໂດດໄດ້"
"ເມື່ອຢືນຢູ່ເທິງພື້ນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.rst:555
msgid ""
"See :ref:`doc_kinematic_character_2d` for more details on using "
"``move_and_slide()``, including a demo project with detailed code."
msgstr ""
"ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_kinematic_character_2d` ສຳລັບລາຍລະອຽດເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບການໃຊ້ "
"``move_and_slide()``, ລວມທັງໂປຣເຈັກຕົວຢ່າງພ້ອມ code ຢ່າງລະອຽດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_jolt_physics.rst:4
msgid "Using Jolt Physics"
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ Jolt Physics"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_jolt_physics.rst:9
msgid ""
"The Jolt physics engine was added as an alternative to the existing Godot "
"Physics physics engine in 4.4. Jolt is developed by Jorrit Rouwe with a "
"focus on games and VR applications. Previously it was available as an "
"extension but is now built into Godot. By default, new projects will use it "
"as the physics engine."
msgstr ""
"Physics engine ຂອງ Jolt ຖືກເພີ່ມເຂົ້າມາເປັນທາງເລືອກແທນ Godot Physics ທີ່ມີຢູ່ແລ້ວໃນເວີຊັນ "
"4.4. Jolt ຖືກພັດທະນາໂດຍ Jorrit Rouwe ໂດຍເນັ້ນໃສ່ເກມ ແລະ ແອັບພລິເຄຊັນ VR. ກ່ອນໜ້ານີ້ມັນມີໃຫ້ໃ"
"ຊ້ເປັນ extension ແຕ່ຕອນນີ້ໄດ້ຖືກລວມເຂົ້າໃນ Godot ແລ້ວ. ໂດຍຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ໂປຣເຈັກໃໝ່ຈະໃຊ້ Jolt ເປັ"
"ນ physics engine."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_jolt_physics.rst:14
msgid ""
"The existing extension is now considered in maintenance mode. That means bug "
"fixes will be merged, and it will be kept compatible with new versions of "
"Godot until the built-in module has feature parity with the extension. The "
"only thing missing at this point is related joints, which you can read about "
"on this page. The extension can be found `here on GitHub <https://github.com/"
"godot-jolt/godot-jolt>`_ and in Godot's asset library."
msgstr ""
"ສ່ວນເສີມທີ່ມີຢູ່ຕອນນີ້ແມ່ນຖືວ່າຢູ່ໃນໂໝດບຳລຸງຮັກສາ. ນັ້ນໝາຍຄວາມວ່າການແກ້ໄຂບັກຈະຖືກຮວມເຂົ້າ, ແລະ ມັນຈະຖືກ"
"ຮັກສາໃຫ້ສາມາດເຂົ້າກັນໄດ້ກັບເວີຊັນໃໝ່ໆຂອງ Godot ຈົນກວ່າໂມດູນທີ່ມີມາໃຫ້ໃນຕົວຈະມີຄຸນສົມບັດທີ່ເທົ່າທຽມກັບສ່ວນ"
"ເສີມ. ສິ່ງດຽວທີ່ຍັງຂາດຢູ່ໃນຕອນນີ້ແມ່ນຂໍ້ຕໍ່ທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງ, ເຊິ່ງທ່ານສາມາດອ່ານກ່ຽວກັບມັນໄດ້ໃນໜ້ານີ້. ສ່ວນເສີມນີ້ສາມ"
"າດຊອກເຫັນໄດ້ `ທີ່ນີ້ເທິງ GitHub <https://github.com/godot-jolt/godot-jolt>`_ ແລະ ໃນຄັ"
"ງຊັບສິນຂອງ Godot."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_jolt_physics.rst:21
msgid ""
"To change the 3D physics engine to be Jolt Physics, set :ref:`Project "
"Settings > Physics > 3D > Physics "
"Engine<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/3D/Physics_Engine>` to ``Jolt "
"Physics``. Once you've done that, click the **Save & Restart** button. When "
"the editor opens again, 3D scenes should now be using Jolt for physics."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອປ່ຽນ 3D physics engine ໃຫ້ເປັນ Jolt Physics, ໃຫ້ຕັ້ງຄ່າ :ref:`Project Settings > "
"Physics > 3D > Physics Engine<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/3D/"
"Physics_Engine>` ເປັນ ``Jolt Physics``. ເມື່ອເຮັດແລ້ວ, ໃຫ້ຄລິກປຸ່ມ **Save & "
"Restart**. ເມື່ອ editor ເປີດຂຶ້ນມາໃໝ່, ສາກ 3D ກໍຈະເລີ່ມໃຊ້ Jolt ສຳລັບຟີຊິກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_jolt_physics.rst:27
msgid "Notable differences to Godot Physics"
msgstr "ຄວາມແຕກຕ່າງທີ່ສຳຄັນເມື່ອທຽບກັບ Godot Physics"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_jolt_physics.rst:29
msgid ""
"There are many differences between the existing Godot Physics engine and "
"Jolt."
msgstr "ມີຄວາມແຕກຕ່າງຫຼາຍຢ່າງລະຫວ່າງ Godot Physics ທີ່ມີຢູ່ ແລະ Jolt."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_jolt_physics.rst:32
msgid "Joint properties"
msgstr "ຄຸນສົມບັດຂອງ Joint"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_jolt_physics.rst:34
msgid ""
"The current interfaces for the 3D joint nodes don't quite line up with the "
"interface of Jolt's own joints. As such, there are a number of joint "
"properties that are not supported, mainly ones related to configuring the "
"joint's soft limits."
msgstr ""
"ອິນເຕີເຟດໃນປັດຈຸບັນສຳລັບໂນດຂໍ້ຕໍ່ 3D ແມ່ນບໍ່ຄ່ອຍກົງກັບອິນເຕີເຟດຂອງຂໍ້ຕໍ່ຂອງ Jolt ເອງ. ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ຈຶ່ງມີຄຸນສົມ"
"ບັດຂອງຂໍ້ຕໍ່ຈຳນວນໜຶ່ງທີ່ບໍ່ໄດ້ຮັບການຮອງຮັບ, ເຊິ່ງສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ແມ່ນສິ່ງທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັບການຕັ້ງຄ່າຂີດຈຳກັດແບບອ່ອນ "
"(soft limits) ຂອງຂໍ້ຕໍ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_jolt_physics.rst:38
msgid "The unsupported properties are:"
msgstr "ຄຸນສົມບັດທີ່ບໍ່ຮອງຮັບມີດັ່ງນີ້:"

