"(thread-safety), ລວມເຖິງການສະໜັບສະໜູນການຕັ້ງຄ່າ :ref:`Physics > 3D > Run On "
"Separate Thread<class_ProjectSettings_Property_physics/3d/"
"run_on_separate_thread>`. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ສ່ວນນີ້ຍັງບໍ່ທັນໄດ້ຮັບການທົດສອບຢ່າງລະອຽດ, ຈຶ່ງຄວນຖືວ່າເ"
"ປັນຄຸນສົມບັດໃນຂັ້ນທົດລອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/rigid_body.rst:4
msgid "Using RigidBody"
msgstr "ການນຳໃຊ້ RigidBody"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/rigid_body.rst:7
msgid "What is a rigid body?"
msgstr "ວັດຖຸແຂງ (Rigid body) ແມ່ນຫຍັງ?"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/rigid_body.rst:9
msgid ""
"A rigid body is one that is directly controlled by the physics engine in "
"order to simulate the behavior of physical objects. In order to define the "
"shape of the body, it must have one or more :ref:`Shape3D <class_Shape3D>` "
"objects assigned. Note that setting the position of these shapes will affect "
"the body's center of mass."
msgstr ""
"ວັດຖຸແຂງ (Rigid body) ແມ່ນວັດຖຸທີ່ຖືກຄວບຄຸມໂດຍກົງຈາກເອນຈິນຟີຊິກ ເພື່ອຈຳລອງພຶດຕິກຳຂອງວັດຖຸທາງກາຍະ"
"ພາບ. ເພື່ອກຳນົດຮູບຊົງຂອງວັດຖຸ, ມັນຈະຕ້ອງມີການກຳນົດວັດຖຸ :ref:`Shape3D <class_Shape3D>` ຢ່າງ"
"ໜ້ອຍໜຶ່ງອັນ ຫຼື ຫຼາຍກວ່ານັ້ນ. ໝາຍເຫດ: ການກຳນົດຕຳແໜ່ງຂອງຮູບຊົງເຫຼົ່ານີ້ ຈະສົ່ງຜົນກະທົບຕໍ່ຈຸດສູນກາງມວນ "
"(center of mass) ຂອງວັດຖຸ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/rigid_body.rst:13
msgid "How to control a rigid body"
msgstr "ວິທີການຄວບຄຸມວັດຖຸແຂງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/rigid_body.rst:15
msgid ""
"A rigid body's behavior can be altered by setting its properties, such as "
"mass and weight. A physics material needs to be added to the rigid body to "
"adjust its friction and bounce, and set if it's absorbent and/or rough. "
"These properties can be set in the Inspector or via code. "
"See :ref:`RigidBody3D <class_RigidBody3D>` and :ref:`PhysicsMaterial "
"<class_PhysicsMaterial>` for the full list of properties and their effects."
msgstr ""
"ພຶດຕິກຳຂອງວັດຖຸແຂງສາມາດປ່ຽນແປງໄດ້ໂດຍການຕັ້ງຄ່າຄຸນສົມບັດຂອງມັນ ເຊັ່ນ: ມວນ (mass) ແລະ ນ້ຳໜັກ "
"(weight). ຕ້ອງມີການເພີ່ມ physics material ໃຫ້ກັບວັດຖຸແຂງ ເພື່ອປັບຄ່າຄວາມຮືດ (friction) ແລ"
"ະ ຄວາມເດັ້ງ (bounce), ລວມທັງກຳນົດວ່າມັນເປັນວັດຖຸດູດຊຶມແຮງ ຫຼື ຫຍາບ. ຄຸນສົມບັດເຫຼົ່ານີ້ ສາມາດຕັ້ງຄ່າໄດ້"
"ໃນ Inspector ຫຼື ຜ່ານການຂຽນໂຄ້ດ. ເບິ່ງ :ref:`RigidBody3D <class_RigidBody3D>` ແລະ "
":ref:`PhysicsMaterial <class_PhysicsMaterial>` ສຳລັບລາຍຊື່ຄຸນສົມບັດທັງໝົດ ແລະ ຜົນກະທົບຂ"
"ອງພວກມັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/rigid_body.rst:21
msgid ""
"There are several ways to control a rigid body's movement, depending on your "
"desired application."
msgstr ""
"ມີຫຼາຍວິທີໃນການຄວບຄຸມການເຄື່ອນທີ່ຂອງວັດຖຸແຂງ, ຂຶ້ນຢູ່ກັບການນຳໃຊ້ທີ່ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/rigid_body.rst:23
msgid ""
"If you only need to place a rigid body once, for example to set its initial "
"location, you can use the methods provided by the :ref:`Node3D "
"<class_Node3D>` node, such as ``set_global_transform()`` or ``look_at()``. "
"However, these methods cannot be called every frame or the physics engine "
"will not be able to correctly simulate the body's state. As an example, "
"consider a rigid body that you want to rotate so that it points towards "
"another object. A common mistake when implementing this kind of behavior is "
"to use ``look_at()`` every frame, which breaks the physics simulation. "
"Below, we'll demonstrate how to implement this correctly."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການວາງຕຳແໜ່ງວັດຖຸແຂງພຽງຄັ້ງດຽວ ເຊັ່ນ: ການກຳນົດຕຳແໜ່ງເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ method ຈ"
"າກໂນດ :ref:`Node3D <class_Node3D>` ເຊັ່ນ ``set_global_transform()`` ຫຼື ``look_at"
"()``. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, method ເຫຼົ່ານີ້ບໍ່ສາມາດເອີ້ນໃຊ້ໃນທຸກໆ frame ໄດ້, ບໍ່ດັ່ງນັ້ນເອນຈິນຟີຊິກ ຈະບໍ່ສາມາດ"
"ຈຳລອງສະຖານະຂອງວັດຖຸໄດ້ຢ່າງຖືກຕ້ອງ. ຕົວຢ່າງ: ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການໝູນວັດຖຸແຂງໃຫ້ຫັນໄປຫາວັດຖຸອື່ນ, ຂໍ້ຜິດພາດທີ່"
"ພົບເລື້ອຍຄືການໃຊ້ ``look_at()`` ໃນທຸກໆ frame ເຊິ່ງຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ການຈຳລອງຟີຊິກຜິດພາດ. ຂ້າງລຸ່ມນີ້ ເຮົາ"
"ຈະສະແດງວິທີການເຮັດທີ່ຖືກຕ້ອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/rigid_body.rst:26
msgid ""
"The fact that you can't use ``set_global_transform()`` or ``look_at()`` "
"methods doesn't mean that you can't have full control of a rigid body. "
"Instead, you can control it by using the ``_integrate_forces()`` callback. "
"In this method, you can add *forces*, apply *impulses*, or set the "
"*velocity* in order to achieve any movement you desire."
msgstr ""
"ການທີ່ເຈົ້າບໍ່ສາມາດໃຊ້ method ``set_global_transform()`` ຫຼື ``look_at()`` ບໍ່ໄດ້ໝາຍຄວາມວ່"
"າເຈົ້າຈະຄວບຄຸມວັດຖຸແຂງບໍ່ໄດ້ເລີຍ. ໃນທາງກົງກັນຂ້າມ, ເຈົ້າສາມາດຄວບຄຸມມັນໄດ້ໂດຍການໃຊ້ callback "
"``_integrate_forces()``. ໃນ method ນີ້, ເຈົ້າສາມາດເພີ່ມ *ແຮງ (forces)*, ໃຊ້ *ແຮງດັນ "
"(impulses)*, ຫຼື ກຳນົດ *ຄວາມໄວ (velocity)* ເພື່ອໃຫ້ໄດ້ການເຄື່ອນທີ່ຕາມທີ່ຕ້ອງການ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/rigid_body.rst:29
msgid "The \"look at\" method"
msgstr "ວິທີການ \"look at\""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/rigid_body.rst:31
msgid ""
"As described above, using the Node3D's ``look_at()`` method can't be used "
"each frame to follow a target. Here is a custom ``look_at()`` method called "
"``look_follow()`` that will work with rigid bodies:"
msgstr ""
"ຕາມທີ່ໄດ້ອະທິບາຍໄວ້ຂ້າງເທິງ, ການໃຊ້ method ``look_at()`` ຂອງ Node3D ບໍ່ສາມາດໃຊ້ໃນທຸກ "
"frame ເພື່ອຕິດຕາມເປົ້າໝາຍໄດ້. ນີ້ຄື method ``look_at()`` ທີ່ສ້າງຂຶ້ນເອງ ເຊິ່ງເອີ້ນວ່າ "
"``look_follow()`` ທີ່ສາມາດໃຊ້ກັບວັດຖຸແຂງໄດ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/rigid_body.rst:80
msgid ""
"This method uses the rigid body's ``angular_velocity`` property to rotate "
"the body. The axis to rotate around is given by the cross product between "
"the current forward direction and the direction one wants to look in. The "
"``clamp`` is a simple method used to prevent the amount of rotation from "
"going past the direction which is wanted to be looked in, as the total "
"amount of rotation needed is given by the arccosine of the dot product. This "
"method can be used with ``axis_lock_angular_*`` as well. If more precise "
"control is needed, solutions such as ones relying on :ref:`class_Quaternion` "
"may be required, as discussed in :ref:`doc_using_transforms`."
msgstr ""
"ວິທີການນີ້ໃຊ້ຄຸນສົມບັດ ``angular_velocity`` ຂອງວັດຖຸແຂງເພື່ອໝຸນວັດຖຸ.\n"
"ແກນທີ່ຈະໝຸນອ້ອມແມ່ນໄດ້ມາຈາກຜົນຄູນໄຂວ່ລະຫວ່າງທິດທາງໄປທາງໜ້າໃນປະຈຸບັນ ແລະ ທິດທາງທີ່ຕ້ອງການຈະແນມໄ"
"ປ.\n"
"``clamp`` ແມ່ນວິທີການແບບງ່າຍດາຍທີ່ໃຊ້ເພື່ອປ້ອງກັນບໍ່ໃຫ້ປະລິມານການໝຸນກາຍທິດທາງທີ່ຕ້ອງການຈະແນມໄປ, ເ"
"ນື່ອງຈາກປະລິມານການໝຸນທັງໝົດທີ່ຕ້ອງການແມ່ນໄດ້ມາຈາກ arccosine ຂອງຜົນຄູນຈຸດ.\n"
"ວິທີການນີ້ສາມາດໃຊ້ກັບ ``axis_lock_angular_*`` ໄດ້ເຊັ່ນກັນ.\n"
"ຫາກຕ້ອງການການຄວບຄຸມທີ່ຊັດເຈນກວ່າ, ວິທີການແກ້ໄຂບັນຫາທີ່ອີງໃສ່ :ref:`class_Quaternion` ອາດຈະມີ"
"ຄວາມຈໍາເປັນ, ດັ່ງທີ່ມີການສົນທະນາໃນ :ref:`doc_using_transforms`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:4
msgid "Using Area2D"
msgstr "ການນຳໃຊ້ Area2D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:9
msgid ""
"Godot offers a number of collision objects to provide both collision "
"detection and response. Trying to decide which one to use for your project "
"can be confusing. You can avoid problems and simplify development if you "
"understand how each of them works and what their pros and cons are. In this "
"tutorial, we'll look at the :ref:`Area2D <class_Area2D>` node and show some "
"examples of how it can be used."
msgstr ""
"Godot ມີວັດຖຸການຕຳ (collision objects) ຫຼາຍຮູບແບບເພື່ອໃຊ້ໃນການກວດຫາການຕຳ ແລະ ການຕອບສະ"
"ໜອງ. ການຕັດສິນໃຈວ່າຈະໃຊ້ແບບໃດໃນໂຄງການຂອງເຈົ້າ ອາດເປັນເລື່ອງທີ່ສັບສົນ. ເຈົ້າສາມາດຫຼີກລ່ຽງບັນຫາ ແລ"
"ະ ເຮັດໃຫ້ການພັດທະນາງ່າຍຂຶ້ນ ຖ້າເຈົ້າເຂົ້າໃຈວ່າແຕ່ລະຢ່າງເຮັດວຽກແນວໃດ ແລະ ມີຂໍ້ດີຂໍ້ເສຍຄືແນວໃດ. ໃນບົດຮ"
"ຽນນີ້, ເຮົາຈະມາເບິ່ງໂນດ :ref:`Area2D <class_Area2D>` ແລະ ສະແດງຕົວຢ່າງການນຳໃຊ້ຂອງມັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:15
msgid ""
"This document assumes you're familiar with Godot's various physics bodies. "
"Please read :ref:`doc_physics_introduction` first."
msgstr ""
"ເອກະສານນີ້ສົມມຸດວ່າເຈົ້າຄຸ້ນເຄີຍກັບ physics body ຕ່າງໆຂອງ Godot ແລ້ວ. ກະລຸນາອ່ານ "
":ref:`doc_physics_introduction` ກ່ອນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:19
msgid "What is an area?"
msgstr "Area ແມ່ນຫຍັງ?"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:21
msgid ""
"An Area2D defines a region of 2D space. In this space you can detect "
"other :ref:`CollisionObject2D <class_CollisionObject2D>` nodes overlapping, "
"entering, and exiting. Areas also allow for overriding local physics "
"properties. We'll explore each of these functions below."
msgstr ""
"Area2D ກຳນົດບໍລິເວນຂອງພື້ນທີ່ 2D. ໃນພື້ນທີ່ນີ້ ເຈົ້າສາມາດກວດຫາໂນດ :ref:`CollisionObject2D "
"<class_CollisionObject2D>` ອື່ນໆ ທີ່ເຂົ້າມາຊ້ອນທັບ, ເຂົ້າມາ ຫຼື ອອກໄປໄດ້. Area ຍັງອະນຸຍາດໃຫ້ປ່"
"ຽນແປງ (override) ຄຸນສົມບັດຟີຊິກໃນບໍລິເວນນັ້ນໄດ້. ເຮົາຈະມາເບິ່ງແຕ່ລະຟັງຊັນເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຢູ່ຂ້າງລຸ່ມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:27
msgid "Area properties"
msgstr "ຄຸນສົມບັດຂອງ Area"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:29
msgid "Areas have many properties you can use to customize their behavior."
msgstr "Area ມີຫຼາຍຄຸນສົມບັດທີ່ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ເພື່ອປັບແຕ່ງພຶດຕິກຳຂອງມັນໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:33
msgid ""
"The ``Gravity``, ``Linear Damp``, and ``Angular Damp`` sections are used to "
"configure the area's physics override behavior. We'll look at how to use "
"those in the *Area influence* section below."
msgstr ""
"ສ່ວນຂອງ ``Gravity``, ``Linear Damp``, ແລະ ``Angular Damp`` ແມ່ນໃຊ້ເພື່ອຕັ້ງຄ່າພຶດຕິກຳກາ"
"ນປ່ຽນແປງຟີຊິກຂອງ area. ເຮົາຈະມາເບິ່ງວິທີການໃຊ້ພວກມັນໃນສ່ວນ *Area influence* ຢູ່ຂ້າງລຸ່ມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:37
msgid ""
"``Monitoring`` and ``Monitorable`` are used to enable and disable the area."
msgstr ""
"``Monitoring`` ແລະ ``Monitorable`` ແມ່ນໃຊ້ເພື່ອເປີດ ແລະ ປິດການເຮັດວຽກຂອງ area."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:39
msgid ""
"The ``Audio Bus`` section allows you to override audio in the area, for "
"example to apply an audio effect when the player moves through."
msgstr ""
"ສ່ວນ ``Audio Bus`` ອະນຸຍາດໃຫ້ເຈົ້າປ່ຽນແປງສຽງໃນ area ນັ້ນ, ຕົວຢ່າງ: ການໃສ່ເອັບເຟັກສຽງເມື່ອຕົວລ"
"ະຄອນຍ່າງຜ່ານ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:42
msgid ""
"Note that Area2D extends :ref:`CollisionObject2D <class_CollisionObject2D>`, "
"so it also provides properties inherited from that class. The ``Collision`` "
"section of ``CollisionObject2D`` is where you configure the area's collision "
"layer(s) and mask(s)."
msgstr ""
"ໝາຍເຫດ: Area2D ສືບທອດມາຈາກ :ref:`CollisionObject2D <class_CollisionObject2D>"
"`, ດັ່ງນັ້ນມັນຈຶ່ງມີຄຸນສົມບັດທີ່ສືບທອດມາຈາກຄລາດນັ້ນນຳ. ສ່ວນ ``Collision`` ຂອງ "
"``CollisionObject2D`` ແມ່ນບ່ອນທີ່ເຈົ້າຕັ້ງຄ່າ collision layer(s) ແລະ mask(s) ຂອງ area."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:48
msgid "Overlap detection"
msgstr "ການກວດຫາການຊ້ອນທັບ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:50
msgid ""
"Perhaps the most common use of Area2D nodes is for contact and overlap "
"detection. When you need to know that two objects have touched, but don't "
"need physical collision, you can use an area to notify you of the contact."
msgstr ""
"ບາງທີການນຳໃຊ້ Area2D ທີ່ພົບເລື້ອຍທີ່ສຸດແມ່ນການກວດຫາການສຳພັດ ແລະ ການຊ້ອນທັບ. ເມື່ອເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການຮູ້ວ່າ"
"ວັດຖຸສອງຢ່າງໄດ້ແຕະກັນແລ້ວ, ແຕ່ບໍ່ຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ມີການຕຳກັນທາງຟີຊິກ, ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ area ເພື່ອແຈ້ງເຕືອນເມື່ອ"
"ມີການສຳພັດໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:54
msgid ""
"For example, let's say we're making a coin for the player to pick up. The "
"coin is not a solid object - the player can't stand on it or push it - we "
"just want it to disappear when the player touches it."
msgstr ""
"ຕົວຢ່າງ: ສົມມຸດວ່າເຮົາກຳລັງສ້າງຫຼຽນໃຫ້ຕົວລະຄອນເກັບ. ຫຼຽນບໍ່ແມ່ນວັດຖຸແຂງ (solid) - ຕົວລະຄອນບໍ່ສາມາດ"
"ຢືນເທິງມັນ ຫຼື ຍູ້ມັນໄດ້ - ເຮົາພຽງແຕ່ຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ມັນຫາຍໄປເມື່ອຕົວລະຄອນມາແຕະມັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:58
msgid "Here's the node setup for the coin:"
msgstr "ນີ້ຄືການຕັ້ງຄ່າໂນດສຳລັບຫຼຽນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:62
msgid ""
"To detect the overlap, we'll connect the appropriate signal on the Area2D. "
"Which signal to use depends on the player's node type. If the player is "
"another area, use ``area_entered``. However, let's assume our player is a "
"``CharacterBody2D`` (and therefore a ``CollisionObject2D`` type), so we'll "
"connect the ``body_entered`` signal."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອການກວດຫາການຊ້ອນທັບ, ເຮົາຈະເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ signal ທີ່ເໝາະສົມໃນ Area2D. ຈະໃຊ້ signal ໃດນັ້ນແມ່ນຂຶ້"
"ນຢູ່ກັບປະເພດໂນດຂອງຕົວລະຄອນ. ຖ້າຕົວລະຄອນເປັນ area ອື່ນ, ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ ``area_entered``. ແຕ່ສົມມຸດວ່າ"
"ຕົວລະຄອນຂອງເຮົາເປັນ ``CharacterBody2D`` (ເຊິ່ງເປັນປະເພດ ``CollisionObject2D``), ເຮົາ"
"ຈຶ່ງຈະເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ signal ``body_entered``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:68
msgid ""
"If you're not familiar with using signals, see :ref:`doc_signals` for an "
"introduction."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເຈົ້າຍັງບໍ່ຄຸ້ນເຄີຍກັບການໃຊ້ signal, ກະລຸນາເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_signals` ສຳລັບການເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:91
msgid "Now our player can collect the coins!"
msgstr "ຕອນນີ້ຕົວລະຄອນຂອງເຮົາກໍສາມາດເກັບຫຼຽນໄດ້ແລ້ວ!"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:93
msgid "Some other usage examples:"
msgstr "ຕົວຢ່າງການນຳໃຊ້ອື່ນໆ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:95
msgid ""
"Areas are great for bullets and other projectiles that hit and deal damage, "
"but don't need any other physics such as bouncing."
msgstr ""
"Area ແມ່ນເໝາະສຳລັບລູກປືນ ຫຼື ວັດຖຸທີ່ຖືກຍິງອອກໄປທີ່ຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ຕຳແລ້ວສ້າງຄວາມເສຍຫາຍ, ແຕ່ບໍ່ຕ້ອງການຟີຊິກ"
"ອື່ນໆ ເຊັ່ນການເດັ້ງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:96
msgid ""
"Use a large circular area around an enemy to define its \"detect\" radius. "
"When the player is outside the area, the enemy can't \"see\" it."
msgstr ""
"ໃຊ້ area ຮູບວົງມົນຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ອ້ອມຮອບສັດຕູເພື່ອກຳນົດລັດສະໝີ \"ການກວດຫາ\". ເມື່ອຕົວລະຄອນຢູ່ນອກ "
"area, ສັດຕູຈະບໍ່ສາມາດ \"ເຫັນ\" ຕົວລະຄອນໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:97
msgid ""
"\"Security cameras\" - In a large level with multiple cameras, attach areas "
"to each camera and activate them when the player enters."
msgstr ""
"\"ກ້ອງວົງຈອນປິດ\" - ໃນດ່ານຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ທີ່ມີກ້ອງຫຼາຍຕົວ, ໃຫ້ຕິດ area ໃສ່ກ້ອງແຕ່ລະຕົວ ແລະ ເປີດໃຊ້ງານພ"
"ວກມັນເມື່ອຕົວລະຄອນຍ່າງເຂົ້າມາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:99
msgid ""
"See the :ref:`doc_your_first_2d_game` for an example of using Area2D in a "
"game."
msgstr "ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_your_first_2d_game` ສຳລັບຕົວຢ່າງການນຳໃຊ້ Area2D ໃນເກມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:102
msgid "Area influence"
msgstr "ອິດທິພົນຂອງ Area"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:104
msgid ""
"The second major use for area nodes is to alter physics. By default, the "
"area won't do this, but you can enable this with the ``Space Override`` "
"property. When areas overlap, they are processed in ``Priority`` order "
"(higher priority areas are processed first). There are four options for "
"override:"
msgstr ""
"ການນຳໃຊ້ຫຼັກຢ່າງທີສອງຂອງໂນດ area ຄືການປ່ຽນແປງຟີຊິກ. ໂດຍປົກກະຕິແລ້ວ area ຈະບໍ່ເຮັດສິ່ງນີ້, ແຕ່ເຈົ້າສ"
"າມາດເປີດໃຊ້ງານໄດ້ດ້ວຍຄຸນສົມບັດ ``Space Override``. ເມື່ອມີ area ຊ້ອນທັບກັນ, ພວກມັນຈະຖືກປະມວນ"
"ຜົນຕາມລຳດັບ ``Priority`` (area ທີ່ມີ priority ສູງກວ່າຈະຖືກປະມວນຜົນກ່ອນ). ມີສີ່ຕົວເລືອກສຳລັບກາ"
"ນ override:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:109
msgid ""
"*Combine* - The area adds its values to what has been calculated so far."
msgstr "*Combine* - area ຈະເພີ່ມຄ່າຂອງມັນເຂົ້າກັບຄ່າທີ່ຖືກຄິດໄລ່ມາແລ້ວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:110
msgid ""
"*Replace* - The area replaces physics properties, and lower priority areas "
"are ignored."
msgstr ""
"*Replace* - area ຈະແທນທີ່ຄຸນສົມບັດຟີຊິກ, ແລະ area ທີ່ມີ priority ຕ່ຳກວ່າຈະຖືກລະເລີຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:111
msgid ""
"*Combine-Replace* - The area adds its gravity/damping values to whatever has "
"been calculated so far (in priority order), ignoring any lower priority "
"areas."
msgstr ""
"*Combine-Replace* - area ຈະເພີ່ມຄ່າ gravity/damping ຂອງມັນເຂົ້າກັບຄ່າໃດໆທີ່ຖືກຄິດໄລ່ມາແລ້ວ "
"(ຕາມລຳດັບ priority), ແລະ ຈະລະເລີຍ area ທີ່ມີ priority ຕ່ຳກວ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:112
msgid ""
"*Replace-Combine* - The area replaces any gravity/damping calculated so far, "
"but keeps calculating the rest of the areas."
msgstr ""
"*Replace-Combine* - area ຈະແທນທີ່ຄ່າ gravity/damping ໃດໆທີ່ຄິດໄລ່ມາແລ້ວ, ແຕ່ຍັງຄົງຄິດໄລ່ "
"area ທີ່ເຫຼືອຕໍ່ໄປ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:114
msgid ""
"Using these properties, you can create very complex behavior with multiple "
"overlapping areas."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍການໃຊ້ຄຸນສົມບັດເຫຼົ່ານີ້, ເຈົ້າສາມາດສ້າງພຶດຕິກຳທີ່ຊັບຊ້ອນຫຼາຍດ້ວຍ area ຫຼາຍອັນທີ່ຊ້ອນທັບກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:117
msgid "The physics properties that can be overridden are:"
msgstr "ຄຸນສົມບັດຟີຊິກທີ່ສາມາດ override ໄດ້ມີດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:119
msgid "*Gravity* - Gravity's strength inside the area."
msgstr "*Gravity* - ຄວາມແຮງຂອງແຮງໂນ້ມຖ່ວງພາຍໃນ area."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:120
msgid "*Gravity Direction* - This vector does not need to be normalized."
msgstr "*Gravity Direction* - ເວກເຕີນີ້ບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງຖືກ normalized."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:121
msgid ""
"*Linear Damp* - How quickly objects stop moving - linear velocity lost per "
"second."
msgstr ""
"*Linear Damp* - ຄວາມໄວທີ່ວັດຖຸຈະຢຸດເຄື່ອນທີ່ - ຄືຄວາມໄວເສັ້ນຊື່ (linear velocity) ທີ່ເສຍໄປຕໍ່ວິນ"
"າທີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:122
msgid ""
"*Angular Damp* - How quickly objects stop spinning - angular velocity lost "
"per second."
msgstr ""
"*Angular Damp* - ຄວາມໄວທີ່ວັດຖຸຈະຢຸດໝູນ - ຄືຄວາມໄວເຊີງມຸມ (angular velocity) ທີ່ເສຍໄປຕໍ່ວິນ"
"າທີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:125
msgid "Point gravity"
msgstr "ແຮງໂນ້ມຖ່ວງແບບຈຸດ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:127
msgid ""
"The ``Gravity Point`` property allows you to create an \"attractor\". "
"Gravity in the area will be calculated towards a point, given by the ``Point "
"Center`` property. Values are relative to the Area2D, so for example using "
"``(0, 0)`` will attract objects to the center of the area."
msgstr ""
"ຄຸນສົມບັດ ``Gravity Point`` ອະນຸຍາດໃຫ້ເຈົ້າສ້າງ \"ຕົວດຶງດູດ (attractor)\". ແຮງໂນ້ມຖ່ວງໃນ "
"area ຈະຖືກຄິດໄລ່ໄປຫາຈຸດໃດໜຶ່ງ ທີ່ກຳນົດໂດຍຄຸນສົມບັດ ``Point Center``. ຄ່າຕ່າງໆແມ່ນທຽບກັບ "
"Area2D, ຕົວຢ່າງ: ການໃຊ້ ``(0, 0)`` ຈະດຶງດູດວັດຖຸເຂົ້າຫາຈຸດສູນກາງຂອງ area."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:133
#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:219
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_features.rst:106
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/build_system/cmake.rst:214
#: ../../docs/engine_details/development/compiling/compiling_with_dotnet.rst:159
msgid "Examples"
msgstr "ຕົວຢ່າງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:135
msgid ""
"The example project attached below has three areas demonstrating physics "
"override."
msgstr ""
"ໂຄງການຕົວຢ່າງທີ່ແນບມາຂ້າງລຸ່ມນີ້ມີ area ສາມອັນທີ່ສະແດງການເຮັດວຽກຂອງ physics override."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_area_2d.rst:140
msgid ""
"You can download this project here: `area_2d_starter.zip <https://github.com/"
"godotengine/godot-docs-project-starters/releases/download/latest-4.x/"
"area_2d_starter.zip>`_"
msgstr ""
"ເຈົ້າສາມາດດາວໂຫຼດໂຄງການນີ້ໄດ້ທີ່ນີ້: `area_2d_starter.zip <https://github.com/"
"godotengine/godot-docs-project-starters/releases/download/latest-4.x/"
"area_2d_starter.zip>`_"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:4
msgid "Using CharacterBody2D/3D"
msgstr "ການນຳໃຊ້ CharacterBody2D/3D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:9
msgid ""
"Godot offers several collision objects to provide both collision detection "
"and response. Trying to decide which one to use for your project can be "
"confusing. You can avoid problems and simplify development if you understand "
"how each of them works and what their pros and cons are. In this tutorial, "
"we'll look at the :ref:`CharacterBody2D <class_CharacterBody2D>` node and "
"show some examples of how to use it."
msgstr ""
"Godot ມີວັດຖຸການຕຳ (collision objects) ຫຼາຍຮູບແບບເພື່ອໃຊ້ໃນການກວດຫາການຕຳ ແລະ ການຕອບສະ"
"ໜອງ. ການຕັດສິນໃຈວ່າຈະໃຊ້ແບບໃດໃນໂຄງການຂອງເຈົ້າ ອາດເປັນເລື່ອງທີ່ສັບສົນ. ເເຈົ້າສາມາດຫຼີກລ່ຽງບັນຫາ ແ"
"ລະ ເຮັດໃຫ້ການພັດທະນາງ່າຍຂຶ້ນ ຖ້າເຈົ້າເຂົ້າໃຈວ່າແຕ່ລະຢ່າງເຮັດວຽກແນວໃດ ແລະ ມີຂໍ້ດີຂໍ້ເສຍຄືແນວໃດ. ໃນບົດ"
"ຮຽນນີ້, ເຮົາຈະມາເບິ່ງໂນດ :ref:`CharacterBody2D <class_CharacterBody2D>` ແລະ ສະແດງຕົ"
"ວຢ່າງການນຳໃຊ້ຂອງມັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:16
msgid ""
"While this document uses ``CharacterBody2D`` in its examples, the same "
"concepts apply in 3D as well."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າເອກະສານນີ້ຈະໃຊ້ ``CharacterBody2D`` ໃນຕົວຢ່າງ, ແຕ່ແນວຄິດດຽວກັນນີ້ກໍສາມາດນຳໃຊ້ໃນ "
"3D ໄດ້ເຊັ່ນກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:20
msgid "What is a character body?"
msgstr "Character body ແມ່ນຫຍັງ?"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:22
msgid ""
"``CharacterBody2D`` is for implementing bodies that are controlled via code. "
"Character bodies detect collisions with other bodies when moving, but are "
"not affected by engine physics properties, like gravity or friction. While "
"this means that you have to write some code to create their behavior, it "
"also means you have more precise control over how they move and react."
msgstr ""
"``CharacterBody2D`` ແມ່ນໃຊ້ສຳລັບສ້າງວັດຖຸທີ່ຖືກຄວບຄຸມຜ່ານການຂຽນໂຄ້ດ. Character body ຈະກວດ"
"ຫາການຕຳກັບວັດຖຸອື່ນໃນຂະນະເຄື່ອນທີ່, ແຕ່ຈະບໍ່ໄດ້ຮັບຜົນກະທົບຈາກຄຸນສົມບັດຟີຊິກຂອງເອນຈິນ ເຊັ່ນ ແຮງໂນ້ມຖ່ວງ "
"ຫຼື ຄວາມຮືດ. ເຖິງວ່ານີ້ຈະໝາຍຄວາມວ່າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງຂຽນໂຄ້ດເອງເພື່ອສ້າງພຶດຕິກຳຂອງມັນ, ແຕ່ມັນກໍໝາຍຄວາມວ່າເຈົ້າ"
"ຈະສາມາດຄວບຄຸມການເຄື່ອນທີ່ ແລະ ການຕອບສະໜອງຂອງມັນໄດ້ຢ່າງຊັດເຈນກວ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:28
msgid ""
"Despite its name ``CharacterBody2D``, it can also be used for other physics "
"objects that require precise manual movement logic and detailed collision "
"information, such as moving platforms or complex projectiles."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າມັນຈະຊື່ວ່າ ``CharacterBody2D``, ແຕ່ມັນກໍສາມາດໃຊ້ກັບວັດຖຸຟີຊິກອື່ນໆ ທີ່ຕ້ອງການການເຄື່ອນທີ່ແ"
"ບບກຳນົດເອງທີ່ຊັດເຈນ ແລະ ຂໍ້ມູນການຕຳທີ່ລະອຽດ ເຊັ່ນ: platform ທີ່ເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄດ້ ຫຼື ວັດຖຸທີ່ຖືກຍິງອອກໄປທີ່ມີຄວ"
"າມຊັບຊ້ອນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:32
msgid ""
"This document assumes you're familiar with Godot's various physics bodies. "
"Please read :ref:`doc_physics_introduction` first, for an overview of the "
"physics options."
msgstr ""
"ເອກະສານນີ້ສົມມຸດວ່າເຈົ້າຄຸ້ນເຄີຍກັບ physics body ຕ່າງໆຂອງ Godot ແລ້ວ. ກະລຸນາອ່ານ "
":ref:`doc_physics_introduction` ກ່ອນ ເພື່ອເບິ່ງພາບລວມຂອງຕົວເລືອກຕ່າງໆທາງຟີຊິກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:36
msgid ""
"A `CharacterBody2D` can be affected by gravity and other forces, but you "
"must calculate the movement in code. The physics engine will not move a "
"`CharacterBody2D`."
msgstr ""
"`CharacterBody2D` ສາມາດຖືກກະທົບໂດຍແຮງໂນ້ມຖ່ວງ ແລະ ແຮງອື່ນໆໄດ້, ແຕ່ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງຄິດໄລ່ການເຄື່ອນທີ່ນັ້"
"ນໃນໂຄ້ດເອງ. ເອນຈິນຟີຊິກຈະບໍ່ເຮັດໃຫ້ `CharacterBody2D` ເຄື່ອນທີ່ໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:41
msgid "Movement and collision"
msgstr "ການເຄື່ອນທີ່ ແລະ ການຕຳ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:43
msgid ""
"When moving a ``CharacterBody2D``, you should not set its ``position`` "
"property directly. Instead, you use the ``move_and_collide()`` or "
"``move_and_slide()`` methods. These methods move the body along a given "
"vector and detect collisions."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອເຮັດໃຫ້ ``CharacterBody2D`` ເຄື່ອນທີ່, ເຈົ້າບໍ່ຄວນກຳນົດຄຸນສົມບັດ ``position`` ຂອງມັນໂດຍກົ"
"ງ. ແຕ່ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ method ``move_and_collide()`` ຫຼື ``move_and_slide()`` ແທນ. method ເຫຼົ່"
"ານີ້ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ວັດຖຸເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄປຕາມເວກເຕີທີ່ກຳນົດ ແລະ ກວດຫາການຕຳໄປພ້ອມໆກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:47
msgid ""
"You should handle physics body movement in the ``_physics_process()`` "
"callback."
msgstr ""
"ເຈົ້າຄວນຈັດການການເຄື່ອນທີ່ຂອງ physics body ໃນ callback ``_physics_process()``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:49
msgid ""
"The two movement methods serve different purposes, and later in this "
"tutorial, you'll see examples of how they work."
msgstr ""
"ການປ່ຽນຮູບແບບກ່ອນໜ້າ ແລະ ປະຈຸບັນຈະຄືກັນ, ເຮັດໃຫ້ບໍ່ມີການເຄື່ອນໄຫວໃນຕອນເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:53
msgid "move_and_collide"
msgstr "move_and_collide"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:55
msgid ""
"This method takes one required parameter: a :ref:`Vector2 <class_Vector2>` "
"indicating the body's relative movement. Typically, this is your velocity "
"vector multiplied by the frame timestep (``delta``). If the engine detects a "
"collision anywhere along this vector, the body will immediately stop moving. "
"If this happens, the method will return a :ref:`KinematicCollision2D "
"<class_KinematicCollision2D>` object."
msgstr ""
"ວິທີການນີ້ຕ້ອງການໜຶ່ງພາຣາມິເຕີທີ່ຈໍາເປັນ: :ref:`Vector2 <class_Vector2>` ທີ່ບົ່ງບອກເຖິງການເຄື່ອນທີ່"
"ສໍາພັດຂອງວັດຖຸ. ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປແລ້ວ, ນີ້ແມ່ນເວັກເຕີຄວາມໄວຂອງທ່ານຄູນກັບໄລຍະເວລາຂອງເຟຣມ (``delta``)"
". ຫາກເຄື່ອງຈັກກວດພົບການຕໍາກັນຢູ່ບ່ອນໃດບ່ອນໜຶ່ງຕາມເວັກເຕີນີ້, ວັດຖຸຈະຢຸດການເຄື່ອນທີ່ທັນທີ. ຫາກສິ່ງນີ້ເກີດຂຶ້"
"ນ, ວິທີການນີ້ຈະສົ່ງຄືນອັອບເຈັກ :ref:`KinematicCollision2D <class_KinematicCollision2D>"
"`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:61
msgid ""
"``KinematicCollision2D`` is an object containing data about the collision "
"and the colliding object. Using this data, you can calculate your collision "
"response."
msgstr ""
"``KinematicCollision2D`` ແມ່ນວັດຖຸທີ່ປະກອບດ້ວຍຂໍ້ມູນກ່ຽວກັບການຕຳ ແລະ ວັດຖຸທີ່ມາຕຳ. ໂດຍການໃຊ້ຂໍ້"
"ມູນນີ້, ເຈົ້າສາມາດຄິດໄລ່ການຕອບສະໜອງຕໍ່ການຕຳໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:65
msgid ""
"``move_and_collide`` is most useful when you just want to move the body and "
"detect collision, but don't need any automatic collision response. For "
"example, if you need a bullet that ricochets off a wall, you can directly "
"change the angle of the velocity when you detect a collision. See below for "
"an example."
msgstr ""
"``move_and_collide`` ມີປະໂຫຍດທີ່ສຸດເມື່ອເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການພຽງແຕ່ໃຫ້ວັດຖຸເຄື່ອນທີ່ ແລະ ກວດຫາການຕຳ, ແຕ່"
"ບໍ່ຕ້ອງການການຕອບສະໜອງຕໍ່ການຕຳແບບອັດຕະໂນມັດ. ຕົວຢ່າງ: ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ລູກປືນເດັ້ງອອກຈາກກຳແພງ, "
"ເຈົ້າສາມາດປ່ຽນມຸມຂອງຄວາມໄວໄດ້ໂດຍກົງເມື່ອກວດພົບການຕຳ. ເບິ່ງຕົວຢ່າງໄດ້ຢູ່ຂ້າງລຸ່ມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:71
msgid "move_and_slide"
msgstr "move_and_slide"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:73
msgid ""
"The ``move_and_slide()`` method is intended to simplify the collision "
"response in the common case where you want one body to slide along the "
"other. It is especially useful in platformers or top-down games, for example."
msgstr ""
"ວິທີການ ``move_and_slide()`` ມີຈຸດປະສົງເພື່ອເຮັດໃຫ້ການຕອບສະໜອງຕໍ່ການຕຳງ່າຍຂຶ້ນ ໃນກໍລະນີທົ່ວໄປທີ່ເ"
"ຈົ້າຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ວັດຖຸໜຶ່ງເລື່ອນໄປຕາມອີກວັດຖຸໜຶ່ງ. ມັນມີປະໂຫຍດເປັນພິເສດໃນເກມແນວ platformer ຫຼື ເກມມຸມມ"
"ອງຈາກດ້ານເທິງ, ຕົວຢ່າງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:77
msgid ""
"When calling ``move_and_slide()``, the function uses a number of node "
"properties to calculate its slide behavior. These properties can be found in "
"the Inspector, or set in code."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອເອີ້ນໃຊ້ ``move_and_slide()``, ຟັງຊັນຈະໃຊ້ຄຸນສົມບັດຫຼາຍຢ່າງຂອງໂນດເພື່ອຄິດໄລ່ພຶດຕິກຳການສະໄ"
"ລ້. ຄຸນສົມບັດເຫຼົ່ານີ້ ສາມາດພົບໄດ້ໃນ Inspector ຫຼື ຕັ້ງຄ່າໃນໂຄ້ດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:81
msgid "``velocity`` - *default value:* ``Vector2( 0, 0 )``"
msgstr "``velocity`` - *ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ:* ``Vector2( 0, 0 )``"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:83
msgid ""
"This property represents the body's velocity vector in pixels per second. "
"``move_and_slide()`` will modify this value automatically when colliding."
msgstr ""
"ຄຸນສົມບັດນີ້ແທນເວກເຕີຄວາມໄວຂອງວັດຖຸໃນຫົວໜ່ວຍ ພິກເຊວຕໍ່ວິນາທີ. ``move_and_slide()`` ຈະປ່ຽນແປງຄ່"
"ານີ້ໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດເມື່ອມີການຕຳ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:86
msgid "``motion_mode`` - *default value:* ``MOTION_MODE_GROUNDED``"
msgstr "``motion_mode`` - *ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ:* ``MOTION_MODE_GROUNDED``"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:88
msgid ""
"This property is typically used to distinguish between side-scrolling and "
"top-down movement. When using the default value, you can use the "
"``is_on_floor()``, ``is_on_wall()``, and ``is_on_ceiling()`` methods to "
"detect what type of surface the body is in contact with, and the body will "
"interact with slopes. When using ``MOTION_MODE_FLOATING``, all collisions "
"will be considered \"walls\"."
msgstr ""
"ຄຸນສົມບັດນີ້ມັກຈະໃຊ້ເພື່ອແຍກລະຫວ່າງການເຄື່ອນທີ່ແບບ side-scrolling (ດ້ານຂ້າງ) ແລະ top-down (ຈາ"
"ກທາງເທິງ). ເມື່ອໃຊ້ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ method ``is_on_floor()``, ``is_on_wall()"
"``, ແລະ ``is_on_ceiling()`` ເພື່ອກວດຫາປະເພດຂອງພື້ນຜິວທີ່ວັດຖຸສຳພັດຢູ່, ແລະ ວັດຖຸຈະມີການຕອບໂຕ້"
"ກັບທາງລາດຊັນ (slopes). ເມື່ອໃຊ້ ``MOTION_MODE_FLOATING``, ການຕຳທັງໝົດຈະຖືກຖືວ່າເປັນ \"ກຳ"
"ແພງ (walls)\"."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:94
msgid "``up_direction`` - *default value:* ``Vector2( 0, -1 )``"
msgstr "``up_direction`` - *ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ:* ``Vector2( 0, -1 )``"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:96
msgid ""
"This property allows you to define what surfaces the engine should consider "
"being the floor. Its value lets you use the ``is_on_floor()``, "
"``is_on_wall()``, and ``is_on_ceiling()`` methods to detect what type of "
"surface the body is in contact with. The default value means that the top "
"side of horizontal surfaces will be considered \"ground\"."
msgstr ""
"ຄຸນສົມບັດນີ້ອະນຸຍາດໃຫ້ເຈົ້າກຳນົດວ່າພື້ນຜິວໃດທີ່ເອນຈິນຄວນຖືວ່າເປັນພື້ນ. ຄ່າຂອງມັນຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເຈົ້າໃຊ້ method "
"``is_on_floor()``, ``is_on_wall()``, ແລະ ``is_on_ceiling()`` ເພື່ອກວດຫາປະເພດພື້ນຜິ"
"ວທີ່ວັດຖຸສຳພັດຢູ່ໄດ້. ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນໝາຍເຖິງ ດ້ານເທິງຂອງພື້ນຜິວແນວນອນຈະຖືກຖືວ່າເປັນ \"ພື້ນ (ground)\"."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:102
