msgstr ""
"ລອງ run scene ນີ້ແລ້ວເຈົ້າຈະເຫັນວ່າ ``move_and_collide()`` ເຮັດວຽກຕາມທີ່ຄາດໄວ້, ໂດຍການເຄື່"
"ອນທີ່ວັດຖຸໄປຕາມເວກເຕີຄວາມໄວ. ຕອນນີ້ລອງມາເບິ່ງວ່າ ຈະເກີດຫຍັງຂຶ້ນເມື່ອເຈົ້າເພີ່ມສິ່ງກີດຂວາງ. ໃຫ້ເພີ່ມ "
":ref:`StaticBody2D <class_StaticBody2D>` ທີ່ມີຮູບຊົງການຕຳແບບສີ່ແຈ. ເພື່ອໃຫ້ເຫັນໄດ້ຊັດເຈນ, "
"ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ Sprite2D, Polygon2D, ຫຼື ເປີດໃຊ້ \"Visible Collision Shapes\" ຈາກເມນູ "
"\"Debug\"."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:282
msgid ""
"Run the scene again and try moving into the obstacle. You'll see that the "
"``CharacterBody2D`` can't penetrate the obstacle. However, try moving into "
"the obstacle at an angle and you'll find that the obstacle acts like glue - "
"it feels like the body gets stuck."
msgstr ""
"Run scene ອີກຄັ້ງແລ້ວລອງເຄື່ອນທີ່ເຂົ້າຫາສິ່ງກີດຂວາງ. ເຈົ້າຈະເຫັນວ່າ ``CharacterBody2D`` ບໍ່ສາມາດ"
"ຜ່ານສິ່ງກີດຂວາງໄປໄດ້. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ລອງເຄື່ອນທີ່ເຂົ້າຫາສິ່ງກີດຂວາງແບບສະຫຼຽງ (ທຳມຸມ) ແລ້ວເຈົ້າຈະພົບວ່າ"
"ສິ່ງກີດຂວາງເຮັດໜ້າທີ່ຄືກັບກາວ - ມັນຈະຮູ້ສຶກຄືກັບວ່າວັດຖຸຖືກຕິດຢູ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:286
msgid ""
"This happens because there is no *collision response*. "
"``move_and_collide()`` stops the body's movement when a collision occurs. We "
"need to code whatever response we want from the collision."
msgstr ""
"ເຫດການນີ້ເກີດຂຶ້ນຍ້ອນວ່າມັນບໍ່ມີ *ການຕອບສະໜອງຕໍ່ການຕຳ (collision response)*. "
"``move_and_collide()`` ຈະຢຸດການເຄື່ອນທີ່ຂອງວັດຖຸເມື່ອເກີດການຕຳ. ເຮົາຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງຂຽນໂຄ້ດເພື່ອສ້າງ"
"ການຕອບສະໜອງທີ່ເຮົາຕ້ອງການຈາກການຕຳນັ້ນເອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:290
msgid "Try changing the function to ``move_and_slide()`` and running again."
msgstr "ລອງປ່ຽນຟັງຊັນເປັນ ``move_and_slide()`` ແລ້ວ run ໃໝ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:292
msgid ""
"``move_and_slide()`` provides a default collision response of sliding the "
"body along the collision object. This is useful for a great many game types, "
"and may be all you need to get the behavior you want."
msgstr ""
"``move_and_slide()`` ຈະໃຫ້ການຕອບສະໜອງຕໍ່ການຕຳແບບເລີ່ມຕົ້ນໂດຍການສະໄລ້ (slide) ວັດຖຸໄປຕາມ"
"ວັດຖຸທີ່ມາຕຳ. ສິ່ງນີ້ມີປະໂຫຍດກັບເກມຫຼາຍປະເພດ, ແລະ ອາດເປັນພຽງສິ່ງດຽວທີ່ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການເພື່ອໃຫ້ໄດ້ພຶດຕິກຳທີ່ເ"
"ຈົ້າຕ້ອງການ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:297
msgid "Bouncing/reflecting"
msgstr "ການເດັ້ງ/ການສະທ້ອນ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:299
msgid ""
"What if you don't want a sliding collision response? For this example "
"(\"bounce_and_collide.tscn\" in the sample project), we have a character "
"shooting bullets and we want the bullets to bounce off the walls."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເຈົ້າບໍ່ຕ້ອງການການຕອບສະໜອງຕໍ່ການຕຳແບບສະໄລ້ເດ? ສຳລັບຕົວຢ່າງນີ້ "
"(\"bounce_and_collide.tscn\" ໃນໂຄງການຕົວຢ່າງ), ເຮົາມີຕົວລະຄອນທີ່ຍິງລູກປືນ ແລະ ເຮົາຕ້ອງການ"
"ໃຫ້ລູກປືນເດັ້ງອອກຈາກກຳແພງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:303
msgid ""
"This example uses three scenes. The main scene contains the Player and "
"Walls. The Bullet and Wall are separate scenes so that they can be instanced."
msgstr ""
"ຕົວຢ່າງນີ້ໃຊ້ສາມ scene. scene ຫຼັກປະກອບດ້ວຍ Player ແລະ Walls. ສ່ວນ Bullet ແລະ Wall ແມ່ນ"
"ແຍກເປັນ scene ຕ່າງຫາກເພື່ອໃຫ້ສາມາດສ້າງ instance ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:306
msgid ""
"The Player is controlled by the ``w`` and ``s`` keys for forward and back. "
"Aiming uses the mouse pointer. Here is the code for the Player, using "
"``move_and_slide()``:"
msgstr ""
"Player ຖືກຄວບຄຸມດ້ວຍປຸ່ມ ``w`` ແລະ ``s`` ເພື່ອເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄປທາງໜ້າ ແລະ ຖອຍຫຼັງ. ການເລັງເປົ້າແມ່ນໃ"
"ຊ້ mouse pointer. ນີ້ຄືໂຄ້ດສຳລັບ Player ໂດຍໃຊ້ ``move_and_slide()``:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:380
msgid "And the code for the Bullet:"
msgstr "ແລະ ນີ້ຄືໂຄ້ດສຳລັບ Bullet:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:441
msgid ""
"The action happens in ``_physics_process()``. After using "
"``move_and_collide()``, if a collision occurs, a ``KinematicCollision2D`` "
"object is returned (otherwise, the return is ``null``)."
msgstr ""
"ການເຮັດວຽກແມ່ນຢູ່ໃນ ``_physics_process()``. ຫຼັງຈາກໃຊ້ ``move_and_collide()``, ຖ້າເກີດ"
"ການຕຳຂຶ້ນ, ວັດຖຸ ``KinematicCollision2D`` ຈະຖືກສົ່ງຄືນມາ (ຖ້າບໍ່ດັ່ງນັ້ນ ຈະສົ່ງຄືນເປັນ ``null``)"
"."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:445
msgid ""
"If there is a returned collision, we use the ``normal`` of the collision to "
"reflect the bullet's ``velocity`` with the ``Vector2.bounce()`` method."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າມີການສົ່ງຄືນການຕຳມາ, ເຮົາຈະໃຊ້ຄ່າ ``normal`` ຂອງການຕຳເພື່ອສະທ້ອນຄວາມໄວ (velocity) ຂອງ"
"ລູກປືນດ້ວຍ method ``Vector2.bounce()``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:448
msgid ""
"If the colliding object (``collider``) has a ``hit`` method, we also call "
"it. In the example project, we've added a flashing color effect to the Wall "
"to demonstrate this."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າວັດຖຸທີ່ມາຕຳ (``collider``) ມີ method ``hit``, ເຮົາກໍຈະເອີ້ນໃຊ້ມັນຄືກັນ. ໃນໂຄງການຕົວຢ່າງ, "
"ເຮົາໄດ້ເພີ່ມເອັບເຟັກສີກະພິບໃສ່ Wall ເພື່ອສະແດງໃຫ້ເຫັນເຖິງການເຮັດວຽກນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:455
msgid "Platformer movement"
msgstr "ການເຄື່ອນທີ່ແບບ Platformer"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:457
msgid ""
"Let's try one more popular example: the 2D platformer. ``move_and_slide()`` "
"is ideal for quickly getting a functional character controller up and "
"running. If you've downloaded the sample project, you can find this in "
"\"platformer.tscn\"."
msgstr ""
"ລອງມາເບິ່ງຕົວຢ່າງຍອດນິຍົມອີກອັນໜຶ່ງຄື: ເກມ 2D platformer. ``move_and_slide()`` ແມ່ນເໝາະສົມ"
"ຫຼາຍສຳລັບການສ້າງລະບົບຄວບຄຸມຕົວລະຄອນ ໃຫ້ເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ຢ່າງວ່ອງໄວ. ຖ້າເຈົ້າໄດ້ດາວໂຫຼດໂຄງການຕົວຢ່າງແລ້"
"ວ, ເຈົ້າສາມາດພົບຕົວຢ່າງນີ້ໄດ້ໃນ \"platformer.tscn\"."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:461
msgid ""
"For this example, we'll assume you have a level made of one or more "
"``StaticBody2D`` objects. They can be any shape and size. In the sample "
"project, we're using :ref:`Polygon2D <class_Polygon2D>` to create the "
"platform shapes."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບຕົວຢ່າງນີ້, ເຮົາສົມມຸດວ່າເຈົ້າມີດ່ານທີ່ສ້າງຂຶ້ນຈາກວັດຖຸ ``StaticBody2D`` ໜຶ່ງອັນ ຫຼື ຫຼາຍກວ່ານັ້ນ. ພວ"
"ກມັນສາມາດມີຮູບຊົງ ແລະ ຂະໜາດໃດກໍໄດ້. ໃນໂຄງການຕົວຢ່າງ, ເຮົາໃຊ້ :ref:`Polygon2D "
"<class_Polygon2D>` ເພື່ອສ້າງຮູບຊົງຂອງ platform."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:465
msgid "Here's the code for the player body:"
msgstr "ນີ້ຄືໂຄ້ດສຳລັບ player body:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:525
msgid ""
"In this code we're using ``move_and_slide()`` as described above - to move "
"the body along its velocity vector, sliding along any collision surfaces "
"such as the ground or a platform. We're also using ``is_on_floor()`` to "
"check if a jump should be allowed. Without this, you'd be able to \"jump\" "
"in midair; great if you're making Flappy Bird, but not for a platformer game."
msgstr ""
"ໃນໂຄ້ດນີ້ ເຮົາກຳລັງໃຊ້ ``move_and_slide()`` ຕາມທີ່ໄດ້ອະທິບາຍໄວ້ຂ້າງເທິງ - ເພື່ອໃຫ້ວັດຖຸເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄປຕ"
"າມເວກເຕີຄວາມໄວ, ໂດຍສະໄລ້ໄປຕາມພື້ນຜິວ ທີ່ຕຳກັນ ເຊັ່ນ ພື້ນ ຫຼື platform. ເຮົາຍັງໃຊ້ "
"``is_on_floor()`` ເພື່ອກວດສອບວ່າຍອມໃຫ້ໂດດໄດ້ຫຼືບໍ່. ຖ້າບໍ່ມີການກວດສອບນີ້, ເຈົ້າຈະສາມາດ \"ໂດ"
"ດ\" ໃນອາກາດໄດ້; ເຊິ່ງມັນອາດຈະດີຖ້າເຈົ້າສ້າງເກມ Flappy Bird, ແຕ່ມັນບໍ່ເໝາະກັບເກມແນວ "
"platformer."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/using_character_body_2d.rst:531
msgid ""
"There is a lot more that goes into a complete platformer character: "
"acceleration, double-jumps, coyote-time, and many more. The code above is "
"just a starting point. You can use it as a base to expand into whatever "
"movement behavior you need for your own projects."
msgstr ""
"ຍັງມີອີກຫຼາຍຢ່າງໃນການສ້າງຕົວລະຄອນ platformer ທີ່ສົມບູນ: ເຊັ່ນ ຄວາມເລັ່ງ (acceleration), ການໂ"
"ດດສອງຊັ້ນ (double-jumps), coyote-time, ແລະ ອື່ນໆອີກຫຼາຍ. ໂຄ້ດຂ້າງເທິງນີ້ເປັນພຽງແຕ່ຈຸດເລີ່ມຕົ້ນເ"
"ທົ່ານັ້ນ. ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ມັນເປັນພື້ນຖານເພື່ອຂະຫຍາຍໄປສູ່ພຶດຕິກຳການເຄື່ອນທີ່ຕ່າງໆ ຕາມທີ່ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການສຳລັບໂຄງກ"
"ານຂອງເຈົ້າເອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/ray-casting.rst:4
msgid "Ray-casting"
msgstr "ການຍິງລຳແສງ (Ray-casting)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/ray-casting.rst:9
msgid ""
"One of the most common tasks in game development is casting a ray (or custom "
"shaped object) and checking what it hits. This enables complex behaviors, "
"AI, etc. to take place. This tutorial will explain how to do this in 2D and "
"3D."
msgstr ""
"ໜຶ່ງໃນວຽກທີ່ພົບເລື້ອຍທີ່ສຸດໃນການພັດທະນາເກມແມ່ນການຍິງລຳແສງ (ຫຼື ວັດຖຸທີ່ມີຮູບຊົງຕາມກຳນົດ) ແລະ ກວດເບິ່ງວ່"
"າມັນຕຳກັບຫຍັງ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສ້າງ ພຶດຕິກຳທີ່ຊັບຊ້ອນ, ລະບົບ AI, ແລະ ອື່ນໆໄດ້. ບົດຮຽນນີ້ຈະອະທິບາຍວິທີການເ"
"ຮັດສິ່ງນີ້ທັງໃນ 2D ແລະ 3D."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/ray-casting.rst:14
msgid ""
"Godot stores all the low-level game information in servers, while the scene "
"is only a frontend. As such, ray casting is generally a lower-level task. "
"For simple raycasts, nodes like :ref:`RayCast3D <class_RayCast3D>` "
"and :ref:`RayCast2D <class_RayCast2D>` will work, as they return every frame "
"what the result of a raycast is."
msgstr ""
"Godot ເກັບຂໍ້ມູນເກມໃນລະດັບຕ່ຳ (low-level) ໄວ້ໃນ servers, ໃນຂະນະທີ່ scene ເປັນພຽງແຕ່ສ່ວນໜ້"
"າ (frontend). ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ການຍິງລຳແສງ (ray casting) ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປແລ້ວຈຶ່ງເປັນວຽກໃນລະດັບຕ່ຳ. ສຳລັບ"
"ການຍິງລຳແສງແບບງ່າຍໆ, ໂນດເຊັ່ນ :ref:`RayCast3D <class_RayCast3D>` ແລະ "
":ref:`RayCast2D <class_RayCast2D>` ຈະເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ດີ, ເພາະພວກມັນຈະສົ່ງຄືນຜົນລັດຂອງການຍິງລຳ"
"ແສງໃນທຸກໆ frame."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/ray-casting.rst:21
msgid ""
"Many times, though, ray-casting needs to be a more interactive process so a "
"way to do this by code must exist."
msgstr ""
"ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ໃນຫຼາຍໆຄັ້ງ, ການຍິງລຳແສງຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງເປັນຂະບວນການທີ່ມີການໂຕ້ຕອບກັນຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນຈຶ່ງຕ້ອ"
"ງມີວິທີການເຮັດສິ່ງນີ້ຜ່ານໂຄ້ດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/ray-casting.rst:25
msgid "Space"
msgstr "Space"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/ray-casting.rst:27
msgid ""
"In the physics world, Godot stores all the low-level collision and physics "
"information in a *space*. The current 2d space (for 2D Physics) can be "
"obtained by accessing :ref:`CanvasItem.get_world_2d().space "
"<class_CanvasItem_method_get_world_2d>`. For 3D, "
"it's :ref:`Node3D.get_world_3d().space <class_Node3D_method_get_world_3d>`."
msgstr ""
"ໃນໂລກຂອງຟີຊິກ, Godot ຈະເກັບຂໍ້ມູນການຕຳ ແລະ ຟີຊິກລະດັບຕ່ຳທັງໝົດໄວ້ໃນ *space*. space 2D ປະຈຸບັ"
"ນ (ສຳລັບ 2D Physics) ສາມາດເຂົ້າເຖິງໄດ້ ຜ່ານ :ref:`CanvasItem.get_world_2d().space "
"<class_CanvasItem_method_get_world_2d>`. ສຳລັບ 3D ແມ່ນ "
":ref:`Node3D.get_world_3d().space <class_Node3D_method_get_world_3d>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/ray-casting.rst:33
msgid ""
"The resulting space :ref:`RID <class_RID>` can be used "
"in :ref:`PhysicsServer3D <class_PhysicsServer3D>` and :ref:`PhysicsServer2D "
"<class_PhysicsServer2D>` respectively for 3D and 2D."
msgstr ""
"ຄ່າ :ref:`RID <class_RID>` ຂອງ space ທີ່ໄດ້ມາ ສາມາດນຳໄປໃຊ້ໃນ "
":ref:`PhysicsServer3D <class_PhysicsServer3D>` ແລະ :ref:`PhysicsServer2D "
"<class_PhysicsServer2D>` ສຳລັບ 3D ແລະ 2D ຕາມລຳດັບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/ray-casting.rst:38
msgid "Accessing space"
msgstr "ການເຂົ້າເຖິງ space"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/ray-casting.rst:40
msgid ""
"Godot physics runs by default in the same thread as game logic, but may be "
"set to run on a separate thread to work more efficiently. Due to this, the "
"only time accessing space is safe is during "
"the :ref:`Node._physics_process() "
"<class_Node_private_method__physics_process>` callback. Accessing it from "
"outside this function may result in an error due to space being *locked*."
msgstr ""
"ຟີຊິກຂອງ Godot ໂດຍປົກກະຕິຈະເຮັດວຽກໃນ thread ດຽວກັບ logic ຂອງເກມ, ແຕ່ກໍສາມາດຕັ້ງຄ່າໃຫ້ເຮັດວ"
"ຽກໃນ thread ແຍກຕ່າງຫາກເພື່ອປະສິດທິພາບທີ່ດີກວ່າ. ດ້ວຍເຫດນີ້, ເວລາທີ່ປອດໄພທີ່ສຸດໃນການເຂົ້າເຖິງ "
"space ຄືໃນລະຫວ່າງ callback :ref:`Node._physics_process() "
"<class_Node_private_method__physics_process>`. ການເຂົ້າເຖິງຈາກນອກຟັງຊັນນີ້ອາດຈະເຮັດໃຫ້"
"ເກີດຂໍ້ຜິດພາດ ເນື່ອງຈາກ space ຖືກ *locked* ຢູ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/ray-casting.rst:47
msgid ""
"To perform queries into physics space, the :ref:`PhysicsDirectSpaceState2D "
