#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:113
msgid "How large world coordinates work"
msgstr "ພິກັດໂລກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ເຮັດວຽກແນວໃດ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:115
msgid ""
"Large world coordinates (also known as **double-precision physics**) "
"increase the precision level of all floating-point computations within the "
"engine."
msgstr ""
"ພິກັດໂລກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ (ຫຼື ເອີ້ນວ່າ **double-precision physics**) ຈະເພີ່ມລະດັບຄວາມຊັດເຈນຂອງກາ"
"ນຄຳນວນຕົວເລກຈຸດລອຍຕົວທັງໝົດພາຍໃນ engine."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:118
msgid ""
"By default, :ref:`class_float` is 64-bit in GDScript, "
"but :ref:`class_Vector2`, :ref:`class_Vector3` and :ref:`class_Vector4` are "
"32-bit. This means that the precision of vector types is much more limited. "
"To resolve this, we can increase the number of bits used to represent a "
"floating-point number in a Vector type. This results in an *exponential* "
"increase in precision, which means the final value is not just twice as "
"precise, but potentially thousands of times more precise at high values. The "
"maximum value that can be represented is also greatly increased by going "
"from a single-precision float to a double-precision float."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, :ref:`class_float` ໃນ GDScript ແມ່ນ 64-bit, ແຕ່ "
":ref:`class_Vector2`, :ref:`class_Vector3` ແລະ :ref:`class_Vector4` ແມ່ນ 32-"
"bit. ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າຄວາມຊັດເຈນຂອງປະເພດ vector ແມ່ນຈຳກັດຫຼາຍ. ເພື່ອແກ້ໄຂບັນຫານີ້, ພວກເຮົາສາມາດເ"
"ພີ່ມຈຳນວນ bits ທີ່ໃຊ້ແທນຕົວເລກຈຸດລອຍຕົວໃນ Vector ໄດ້. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະສົ່ງຜົນໃຫ້ຄວາມຊັດເຈນເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນແບບ *ທະ"
"ວີຄູນ (exponential)*, ເຊິ່ງໝາຍຄວາມວ່າຄ່າສຸດທ້າຍບໍ່ໄດ້ຊັດເຈນຂຶ້ນພຽງສອງເທົ່າ, ແຕ່ອາດຈະຊັດເຈນຂຶ້ນຫຼາຍ"
"ພັນເທົ່າໃນຄ່າທີ່ສູງໆ. ຄ່າສູງສຸດທີ່ສາມາດສະແດງໄດ້ກໍເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນຢ່າງຫຼວງຫຼາຍເຊັ່ນກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:128
msgid ""
"To avoid model snapping issues when far away from the world origin, Godot's "
"3D rendering engine will increase its precision for rendering operations "
"when large world coordinates are enabled. The shaders do not use double-"
"precision floats for performance reasons, but an `alternative solution "
"<https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/66178>`__ is used to emulate "
"double precision for rendering using single-precision floats."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອຫຼີກເວັ້ນບັນຫາໂມເດວມີອາການກະຕຸກ (snapping) ເມື່ອຢູ່ຫ່າງຈາກຈຸດເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, engine ການສະແດງຜົນ "
"3D ຂອງ Godot ຈະເພີ່ມຄວາມຊັດເຈນໃນການສະແດງຜົນເມື່ອເປີດໃຊ້ພິກັດໂລກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່. Shaders ຈະບໍ່ໃຊ້ເ"
"ລກຈຸດລອຍຕົວແບບ 64-bit ຍ້ອນເຫດຜົນດ້ານປະສິດທິພາບ, ແຕ່ຈະໃຊ້ `ວິທີການທາງເລືອກ <https://"
"github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/66178>`__ ເພື່ອຈຳລອງຄວາມລະອຽດຄູ່ໂດຍໃຊ້ເລກຈຸດລອຍຕົວ"
"ແບບຄວາມລະອຽດດ່ຽວແທນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:136
msgid ""
"Enabling large world coordinates comes with a performance and memory usage "
"penalty, especially on 32-bit CPUs. Only enable large world coordinates if "
"you actually need them."
msgstr ""
"ການເປີດໃຊ້ພິກັດໂລກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ຈະມີການແລກປ່ຽນກັບປະສິດທິພາບ ແລະ ການໃຊ້ໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳ, ໂດຍສະເພາະໃນ "
"CPU ແບບ 32-bit. ຄວນເປີດໃຊ້ພຽງແຕ່ເມື່ອເຈົ້າຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງໃຊ້ມັນແທ້ໆ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:140
msgid ""
"This feature is tailored towards mid-range/high-end desktop platforms. Large "
"world coordinates may not perform well on low-end mobile devices, unless you "
"take steps to reduce CPU usage with other means (such as decreasing the "
"number of physics ticks per second)."
msgstr ""
"ຟີເຈີນີ້ຖືກອອກແບບມາສຳລັບຄອມພິວເຕີລະດັບກາງຫາລະດັບສູງ. ພິກັດໂລກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ອາດຈະເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ບໍ່ດີໃນອຸປະກ"
"ອນມືຖືລະດັບຕໍ່າ, ນອກຈາກວ່າເຈົ້າຈະມີມາດຕະການຫຼຸດຜ່ອນການໃຊ້ CPU ດ້ວຍວິທີອື່ນ (ເຊັ່ນ: ການຫຼຸດຈຳນວນ "
"physics ticks ຕໍ່ວິນາທີ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:145
msgid ""
"On low-end platforms, an *origin shifting* approach can be used instead to "
"allow for large worlds without using double-precision physics and rendering. "
"Origin shifting works with single-precision floats, but it introduces more "
"complexity to game logic, especially in multiplayer games. Therefore, origin "
"shifting is not detailed on this page."
msgstr ""
"ໃນອຸປະກອນລະດັບຕໍ່າ, ສາມາດໃຊ້ວິທີ *origin shifting* (ການຍ້າຍຈຸດເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ) ແທນເພື່ອຮອງຮັບໂລກຂະໜ"
"າດໃຫຍ່ໂດຍບໍ່ຕ້ອງໃຊ້ຟີຊິກ ແລະ ການສະແດງຜົນແບບຄວາມລະອຽດຄູ່. Origin shifting ເຮັດວຽກກັບເລກຈຸດລ"
"ອຍຕົວຄວາມລະອຽດດ່ຽວໄດ້, ແຕ່ມັນຈະເພີ່ມຄວາມຊັບຊ້ອນໃຫ້ກັບ logic ຂອງເກມ, ໂດຍສະເພາະໃນເກມທີ່ຫຼິ້ນຫຼາຍ"
"ຄົນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:152
msgid "Who are large world coordinates for?"
msgstr "ພິກັດໂລກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ເໝາະສຳລັບໃຜ?"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:154
msgid ""
"Large world coordinates are typically required for 3D space or planetary-"
"scale simulation games. This extends to games that require supporting *very* "
"fast movement speeds, but also very slow *and* precise movements at times."
msgstr ""
"ພິກັດໂລກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ປົກກະຕິແລ້ວແມ່ນຈຳເປັນສຳລັບເກມອະວະກາດ 3D ຫຼື ເກມຈຳລອງລະດັບດາວເຄາະ. ລວມໄປເ"
"ຖິງເກມທີ່ຕ້ອງການຮອງຮັບຄວາມໄວໃນການເຄື່ອນທີ່ທີ່ *ໄວຫຼາຍ*, ແຕ່ໃນຂະນະດຽວກັນກໍຕ້ອງການການເຄື່ອນທີ່ທີ່ຊ້າຫຼາ"
"ຍ *ແລະ* ຊັດເຈນໃນບາງຄັ້ງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:158
msgid ""
"On the other hand, it's important to only use large world coordinates when "
"actually required (for performance reasons). Large world coordinates are "
"usually **not** required for:"
msgstr ""
"ໃນທາງກັບກັນ, ມັນສຳຄັນຫຼາຍທີ່ຈະໃຊ້ພິກັດໂລກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ເມື່ອຈຳເປັນແທ້ໆເທົ່ານັ້ນ (ຍ້ອນເຫດຜົນດ້ານປະສິດທິພາບ)"
". ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປແລ້ວພິກັດໂລກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ແມ່ນ **ບໍ່** ຈຳເປັນສຳລັບ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:162
msgid "2D games, as precision issues are usually less noticeable."
msgstr "ເກມ 2D, ເພາະວ່າບັນຫາຄວາມຊັດເຈນມັກຈະສັງເກດເຫັນໄດ້ຍາກກວ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:163
msgid "Games with small-scale or medium-scale worlds."
msgstr "ເກມທີ່ມີໂລກຂະໜາດນ້ອຍ ຫຼື ຂະໜາດກາງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:164
msgid ""
"Games with large worlds, but split into different levels with loading "
"sequences in between. You can center each level portion around the world "
"origin to avoid precision issues without a performance penalty."
msgstr ""
"ເກມທີ່ມີໂລກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ ແຕ່ຖືກແບ່ງອອກເປັນຫຼາຍສາກ (levels) ໂດຍມີການໂຫຼດຂັ້ນກາງ. ເຈົ້າສາມາດວາງແຕ່ລ"
"ະສ່ວນຂອງສາກໄວ້ທີ່ຈຸດເລີ່ມຕົ້ນຂອງໂລກເພື່ອຫຼີກເວັ້ນບັນຫາຄວາມຊັດເຈນໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:167
msgid ""
"Open world games with a *playable on-foot area* not exceeding 8192×8192 "
"meters (centered around the world origin). As shown in the above table, the "
"level of precision remains acceptable within that range, even for a first-"
"person game."
msgstr ""
"ເກມແນວ Open world ທີ່ມີ *ພື້ນທີ່ຫຼິ້ນດ້ວຍການຍ່າງ* ບໍ່ເກີນ 8192×8192 ແມັດ (ໂດຍມີຈຸດເລີ່ມຕົ້ນຢູ່ເຄິ່ງກາງ)"
". ດັ່ງທີ່ສະແດງໃນຕາຕະລາງຂ້າງເທິງ, ລະດັບຄວາມຊັດເຈນຍັງຖືວ່າຮັບໄດ້ໃນຂອບເຂດນັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:171
msgid ""
"**If in doubt**, you probably don't need to use large world coordinates in "
"your project. For reference, most modern AAA open world titles don't use a "
"large world coordinates system and still rely on single-precision floats for "
"both rendering and physics."
msgstr ""
"**ຫາກເຈົ້າຍັງບໍ່ແນ່ໃຈ**, ເຈົ້າອາດຈະຍັງບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງໃຊ້ພິກັດໂລກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ໃນໂປຣເຈັກຂອງເຈົ້າ. ເພື່ອເປັນຂໍ້"
"ມູນອ້າງອີງ, ເກມລະດັບ AAA ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ໃນປະຈຸບັນກໍບໍ່ໄດ້ໃຊ້ລະບົບພິກັດໂລກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່ ແລະ ຍັງຄົງອາໄສເລກຈຸດລ"
"ອຍຕົວຄວາມລະອຽດດ່ຽວທັງໃນການສະແດງຜົນ ແລະ ຟີຊິກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:177
msgid "Enabling large world coordinates"
msgstr "ການເປີດໃຊ້ພິກັດໂລກຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:179
msgid ""
"This process requires recompiling the editor and all export template "
"binaries you intend to use. If you only intend to export your project in "
"release mode, you can skip the compilation of debug export templates. In any "
"case, you'll need to compile an editor build so you can test your large "
"precision world without having to export the project every time."
msgstr ""
"ຂະບວນການນີ້ຮຽກຮ້ອງໃຫ້ມີການຄອມໄພລ໌ (recompile) editor ແລະ export templates ໃໝ່ທັງໝົດ. ຫ"
"າກເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການສົ່ງອອກໂປຣເຈັກໃນໂໝດ release ເທົ່ານັ້ນ, ເຈົ້າສາມາດຂ້າມການຄອມໄພລ໌ debug "
"templates ໄດ້. ແຕ່ໃນທຸກກໍລະນີ, ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງຄອມໄພລ໌ editor build ເພື່ອໃຫ້ສາມາດທົດສອບໂລກທີ່ມີຄວາມລ"
"ະອຽດສູງໄດ້ໂດຍບໍ່ຕ້ອງສົ່ງອອກໂປຣເຈັກທຸກຄັ້ງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:185
msgid ""
"See the :ref:`Compiling <toc-devel-compiling>` section for compiling "
"instructions for each target platform. You will need to add the "
"``precision=double`` SCons option when compiling the editor and export "
"templates."
msgstr ""
"ເບິ່ງພາກ :ref:`Compiling <toc-devel-compiling>` ສຳລັບຂັ້ນຕອນການຄອມໄພລ໌ໃນແຕ່ລະແພລດຟອ"
"ມ. ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງເພີ່ມຕົວເລືອກ ``precision=double`` ໃນ SCons ເມື່ອຄອມໄພລ໌ editor ແລະ export "
"templates."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:189
msgid ""
"The resulting binaries will be named with a ``.double`` suffix to "
"distinguish them from single-precision binaries (which lack any precision "
"suffix). You can then specify the binaries as custom export templates in "
"your project's export presets in the Export dialog."
msgstr ""
"ໄຟລ໌ binary ທີ່ໄດ້ຈະມີນາມສະກຸນ ``.double`` ຕໍ່ທ້າຍເພື່ອແຍກອອກຈາກຄວາມລະອຽດດ່ຽວ. ຈາກນັ້ນເຈົ້າສາ"
"ມາດລະບຸໄຟລ໌ເຫຼົ່ານີ້ເປັນ custom export templates ໃນການຕັ້ງຄ່າການສົ່ງອອກຂອງໂປຣເຈັກໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:195
msgid "Compatibility between single-precision and double-precision builds"
msgstr "ຄວາມເຂົ້າກັນໄດ້ລະຫວ່າງ build ແບບຄວາມລະອຽດດ່ຽວ ແລະ ຄວາມລະອຽດຄູ່"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:197
msgid ""
"When saving a *binary* resource using the :ref:`class_ResourceSaver` "
"singleton, a special flag is stored in the file if the resource was saved "
"using a build that uses double-precision numbers. As a result, all binary "
"resources will change on disk when you switch to a double-precision build "
"and save over them."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອບັນທຶກ resource ແບບ *binary* ໂດຍໃຊ້ :ref:`class_ResourceSaver`, ຈະມີ flag ພິເສດ"
"ຖືກເກັບໄວ້ໃນໄຟລ໌ຫາກ resource ນັ້ນຖືກບັນທຶກດ້ວຍ build ທີ່ໃຊ້ຄວາມລະອຽດຄູ່. ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ທຸກໆ binary "
"resource ຈະປ່ຽນແປງໃນດິສກ໌ເມື່ອເຈົ້າປ່ຽນໄປໃຊ້ build ຄວາມລະອຽດຄູ່ແລ້ວບັນທຶກທັບພວກມັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:202
msgid ""
"Both single-precision and double-precision builds support using "
"the :ref:`class_ResourceLoader` singleton on resources that use this special "
"flag. This means single-precision builds can load resources saved using "
"double-precision builds and vice versa. Text-based resources don't store a "
"double-precision flag, as they don't require such a flag for correct reading."
msgstr ""
"ທັງ build ຄວາມລະອຽດດ່ຽວ ແລະ ຄວາມລະອຽດຄູ່ລ້ວນແຕ່ຮອງຮັບການໃຊ້ "
":ref:`class_ResourceLoader` ກັບ resource ທີ່ມີ flag ພິເສດນີ້. ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າ build ຄວາມລະ"
"ອຽດດ່ຽວສາມາດໂຫຼດ resource ທີ່ບັນທຶກດ້ວຍຄວາມລະອຽດຄູ່ໄດ້ ແລະ ໃນທາງກັບກັນກໍໄດ້ເຊັ່ນກັນ. ສ່ວນ "
"resource ທີ່ເປັນ text ແມ່ນຈະບໍ່ມີການເກັບ flag ນີ້ໄວ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:209
msgid "Known incompatibilities"
msgstr "ຂໍ້ທີ່ບໍ່ເຂົ້າກັນທີ່ພົບ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:211
msgid ""
"In a networked multiplayer game, the server and all clients should be using "
"the same build type to ensure precision remains consistent across clients. "
"Using different build types *may* work, but various issues can occur."
msgstr ""
"ໃນເກມອອນລາຍ, ທັງ server ແລະ client ທັງໝົດຄວນໃຊ້ build ປະເພດດຽວກັນເພື່ອໃຫ້ຄວາມຊັດເຈນຄົງ"
"ທີ່. ການໃຊ້ build ຄົນລະປະເພດ *ອາດຈະ* ໃຊ້ໄດ້, ແຕ່ອາດຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດບັນຫາຫຼາຍຢ່າງຕາມມາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:214
msgid ""
"The GDExtension API changes in an incompatible way in double-precision "
"builds. This means extensions **must** be rebuilt to work with double-"
"precision builds. On the extension developer's end, the ``REAL_T_IS_DOUBLE`` "
"define is enabled when building a GDExtension with ``precision=double``. "
"``real_t`` can be used as an alias for ``float`` in single-precision builds, "
"and ``double`` in double-precision builds."
msgstr ""
"GDExtension API ຈະມີການປ່ຽນແປງໃນ build ຄວາມລະອຽດຄູ່. ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າ extension **ຕ້ອງ** "
"ຖືກ rebuild ໃໝ່. ສຳລັບຜູ້ພັດທະນາ extension, ຄ່າ ``REAL_T_IS_DOUBLE`` ຈະຖືກເປີດໃຊ້ເມື່ອ "
"build GDExtension ດ້ວຍ ``precision=double``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:224
msgid ""
"Since 3D rendering shaders don't actually use double-precision floats, there "
"are some limitations when it comes to 3D rendering precision:"
msgstr ""
"ເນື່ອງຈາກ shader ໃນການສະແດງຜົນ 3D ບໍ່ໄດ້ໃຊ້ເລກຈຸດລອຍຕົວແບບຄວາມລະອຽດຄູ່ແທ້ໆ, ຈຶ່ງມີຂໍ້ຈຳກັດບາງຢ່າ"
"ງກ່ຽວກັບຄວາມຊັດເຈນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:227
msgid ""
":ref:`Triplanar mapping <doc_standard_material_3d_triplanar_mapping>` "
"doesn't benefit from increased precision. Materials using triplanar mapping "
"will exhibit visible jittering when far away from the world origin."
msgstr ""
":ref:`Triplanar mapping <doc_standard_material_3d_triplanar_mapping>` ຈະບໍ່ໄດ້ຮັບ"
"ຜົນປະໂຫຍດຈາກຄວາມຊັດເຈນທີ່ເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນ. ວັດສະດຸ (Materials) ທີ່ໃຊ້ triplanar mapping ຈະເຫັນອາກາ"
"ນສັ່ນ (jittering) ເມື່ອຢູ່ຫ່າງຈາກຈຸດເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:230
msgid ""
":ref:`class_GPUParticles3D` nodes with **Local Coords** disabled will not "
"benefit from increased precision. This can cause visible particle snapping "
"to occur when far away from the world origin. Nodes with **Local Coords** "
"enabled, as well as :ref:`class_CPUParticles3D` nodes, will still benefit "
"from increased precision."
msgstr ""
"ໂນດ :ref:`class_GPUParticles3D` ທີ່ປິດ **Local Coords** ຈະບໍ່ໄດ້ຮັບຜົນປະໂຫຍດຈາກຄວາມຊັດ"
"ເຈນທີ່ເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນ. ສິ່ງນີ້ອາດເຮັດໃຫ້ເຫັນ particle ມີອາການກະຕຸກ. ສ່ວນໂນດທີ່ເປີດ **Local Coords** ແລ"
"ະ ໂນດ :ref:`class_CPUParticles3D` ຍັງຄົງໄດ້ຮັບຜົນປະໂຫຍດຢູ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:234
msgid ""
"Shaders using the ``skip_vertex_transform`` or ``world_vertex_coords`` "
"render modes don't benefit from increased precision."
msgstr ""
"Shaders ທີ່ໃຊ້ໂໝດ ``skip_vertex_transform`` ຫຼື ``world_vertex_coords`` ຈະບໍ່ໄດ້ຮັບຜົນປ"
"ະໂຫຍດຈາກຄວາມຊັດເຈນທີ່ເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:236
msgid ""
"In double-precision builds, world space coordinates in a shader "
"``fragment()`` function can't be reconstructed from view space, for example:"
msgstr ""
"ໃນ build ຄວາມລະອຽດຄູ່, ພິກັດ world space ໃນຟັງຊັນ ``fragment()`` ຂອງ shader ບໍ່ສາມາດສ້"
"າງຄືນໃໝ່ຈາກ view space ໄດ້, ຕົວຢ່າງ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:243
msgid ""
"Instead, calculate the world space coordinates in the ``vertex()`` function "
"and pass them using a :ref:`varying<doc_shading_language_varyings>`, for "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"ແທນທີ່ຈະເຮັດແບບນັ້ນ, ໃຫ້ຄຳນວນພິກັດ world space ໃນຟັງຊັນ ``vertex()`` ແລ້ວສົ່ງຄ່າຜ່ານ "
":ref:`varying<doc_shading_language_varyings>`, ຕົວຢ່າງ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/large_world_coordinates.rst:253
msgid ""
"2D rendering currently doesn't benefit from increased precision when large "
"world coordinates are enabled. This can cause visible model snapping to "
"occur when far away from the world origin (starting from a few million "
"pixels at typical zoom levels). 2D physics calculations will still benefit "
"from increased precision though."
msgstr ""
"ການສະແດງຜົນ 2D ໃນປະຈຸບັນຍັງບໍ່ໄດ້ຮັບຜົນປະໂຫຍດຈາກຄວາມຊັດເຈນທີ່ເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນ. ສິ່ງນີ້ອາດເຮັດໃຫ້ເຫັນໂມເດວມີອ"
"າການກະຕຸກເມື່ອຢູ່ຫ່າງຈາກຈຸດເລີ່ມຕົ້ນຫຼາຍໆ. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ການຄຳນວນຟີຊິກ 2D ຍັງຄົງໄດ້ຮັບຜົນປະໂຫຍດຈາກຄ"
"ວາມຊັດເຈນທີ່ເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນຢູ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/index.rst:6
msgid "Physics Interpolation"
msgstr "ການແຊກຂໍ້ມູນຟີຊິກ (Physics Interpolation)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_quick_start_guide.rst:6
msgid ""
"Turn on physics interpolation: :ref:`Project Settings > Physics > Common > "
"Physics Interpolation<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/common/"
"physics_interpolation>`"
msgstr ""
"ເປີດໃຊ້ physics interpolation: :ref:`Project Settings > Physics > Common > "
"Physics Interpolation<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/common/"
"physics_interpolation>`"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_quick_start_guide.rst:7
msgid ""
"Make sure you move objects and run your game logic in ``_physics_process()`` "
"rather than ``_process()``. This includes moving objects directly *and "
"indirectly* (by e.g. moving a parent, or using another mechanism to "
"automatically move nodes)."
msgstr ""
"ໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າເຈົ້າຍ້າຍວັດຖຸ ແລະ ໃຊ້ logic ຂອງເກມໃນ ``_physics_process()`` ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນ "
"``_process()``. ສິ່ງນີ້ລວມເຖິງການຍ້າຍວັດຖຸໂດຍກົງ *ແລະ ທາງອ້ອມ* (ເຊັ່ນ: ການຍ້າຍໂນດແມ່, ຫຼື ການ"
"ໃຊ້ກົນໄກອື່ນໆເພື່ອຍ້າຍໂນດໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_quick_start_guide.rst:11
msgid ""
"Be sure to "
"call :ref:`Node.reset_physics_interpolation<class_Node_method_reset_physics_interpolation>` "
"on nodes *after* you first position or teleport them, to prevent "
"\"streaking\"."
msgstr ""
"ຢ່າລືມເອີ້ນໃຊ້ "
":ref:`Node.reset_physics_interpolation<class_Node_method_reset_physics_interpolation>"
"` ໃນໂນດ *ຫຼັງຈາກ* ທີ່ເຈົ້າກຳນົດຕຳແໜ່ງທຳອິດ ຫຼື ວັດຖຸຖືກ teleport, ເພື່ອປ້ອງກັນອາການ \"ລາກຍາວ "
"(streaking)\"."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_quick_start_guide.rst:13
msgid ""
"Temporarily try setting :ref:`Project Settings > Physics > Common > Physics "
"Ticks per Second<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/common/"
"physics_ticks_per_second>` to 10 to see the difference with and without "
"interpolation."
msgstr ""
"ທົດລອງຕັ້ງຄ່າ :ref:`Project Settings > Physics > Common > Physics Ticks per "
"Second<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/common/"
"physics_ticks_per_second>` ເປັນ 10 ຊົ່ວຄາວ ເພື່ອເບິ່ງຄວາມແຕກຕ່າງລະຫວ່າງຕອນທີ່ເປີດ ແລະ ປິດ "
"interpolation."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:7
msgid "Physics ticks and rendered frames"
msgstr "Physics ticks ແລະ ເຟຣມການສະແດງຜົນ (rendered frames)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:9
msgid ""
"One key concept to understand in Godot is the distinction between physics "
"ticks (sometimes referred to as iterations or physics frames), and rendered "
"frames. The physics proceeds at a fixed tick rate (set in :ref:`Project "
"Settings > Physics > Common > Physics Tick per "
"Second<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/common/"
"physics_ticks_per_second>`), which defaults to 60 ticks per second."
msgstr ""
"ແນວຄິດທີ່ສຳຄັນຢ່າງໜຶ່ງໃນ Godot ຄືຄວາມແຕກຕ່າງລະຫວ່າງ physics ticks (ບາງຄັ້ງເອີ້ນວ່າ "
"iterations ຫຼື physics frames) ແລະ ເຟຣມການສະແດງຜົນ (rendered frames). ຟີຊິກຈະເຮັດວຽ"
"ກດ້ວຍອັດຕາຄົງທີ່ (ຕັ້ງຄ່າໄດ້ໃນ :ref:`Project Settings > Physics > Common > Physics "
"Tick per Second<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/common/"
"physics_ticks_per_second>`), ເຊິ່ງຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນແມ່ນ 60 ticks ຕໍ່ວິນາທີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:14
msgid ""
"However, the engine does not necessarily **render** at the same rate. "
"Although many monitors refresh at 60 Hz (cycles per second), many refresh at "
"completely different frequencies (e.g. 75 Hz, 144 Hz, 240 Hz or more). Even "
"though a monitor may be able to show a new frame e.g. 60 times a second, "
"there is no guarantee that the CPU and GPU will be able to *supply* frames "
"at this rate. For instance, when running with V-Sync, the computer may be "
"too slow for 60 and only reach the deadlines for 30 FPS, in which case the "
"frames you see will change at 30 FPS (resulting in stuttering)."
msgstr ""
"ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, engine ບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງ **ສະແດງຜົນ (render)** ໃນອັດຕາດຽວກັນ. ເຖິງວ່າຈໍພາບຫຼາຍລຸ້ນຈ"
"ະມີ refresh rate ທີ່ 60 Hz, ແຕ່ຫຼາຍລຸ້ນກໍມີຄວາມຖີ່ທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນ (ເຊັ່ນ 75 Hz, 144 Hz, 240 Hz "
"ຫຼື ຫຼາຍກວ່ານັ້ນ). ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຈໍພາບຈະສາມາດສະແດງເຟຣມໃໝ່ໄດ້ 60 ຄັ້ງຕໍ່ວິນາທີ, ແຕ່ກໍບໍ່ມີຫຍັງຮັບປະກັນວ່າ "
"CPU ແລະ GPU ຈະສາມາດ *ສົ່ງ* ເຟຣມໃຫ້ໄດ້ໃນອັດຕານັ້ນ. ຕົວຢ່າງ: ເມື່ອເປີດ V-Sync, ຄອມພິວເຕີອາດຈະ"
"ຊ້າເກີນໄປຈົນເຮັດໄດ້ພຽງ 30 FPS, ເຊິ່ງຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເຫັນພາບມີອາການກະຕຸກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:23
msgid ""
"But there is a problem here. What happens if the physics ticks do not "
"coincide with frames? What happens if the physics tick rate is out of phase "
"with the frame rate? Or worse, what happens if the physics tick rate is "
"*lower* than the rendered frame rate?"
msgstr ""
"ແຕ່ມັນມີບັນຫາຢູ່ບ່ອນນີ້. ຈະເກີດຫຍັງຂຶ້ນຖ້າ physics ticks ບໍ່ກົງກັບເຟຣມ? ຈະເກີດຫຍັງຂຶ້ນຖ້າອັດຕາ "
"physics tick ບໍ່ກົງຈັງຫວະກັບອັດຕາເຟຣມ? ຫຼື ຮ້າຍແຮງກວ່ານັ້ນ, ຈະເກີດຫຍັງຂຶ້ນຖ້າອັດຕາ physics "
"tick *ຕໍ່າກວ່າ* ອັດຕາເຟຣມການສະແດງຜົນ?"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:28
msgid ""
"This problem is easier to understand if we consider an extreme scenario. If "
"you set the physics tick rate to 10 ticks per second, in a simple game with "
"a rendered frame rate of 60 FPS. If we plot a graph of the positions of an "
"object against the rendered frames, you can see that the positions will "
"appear to \"jump\" every 1/10th of a second, rather than giving a smooth "
"motion. When the physics calculates a new position for a new object, it is "
"not rendered in this position for just one frame, but for 6 frames."
msgstr ""
"ບັນຫານີ້ຈະເຂົ້າໃຈໄດ້ງ່າຍຂຶ້ນຖ້າເຮົາເບິ່ງໃນກໍລະນີທີ່ຕ່າງກັນຫຼາຍໆ. ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕັ້ງ physics tick ເປັນ 10 "
"ticks ຕໍ່ວິນາທີ ໃນເກມທີ່ສະແດງຜົນ 60 FPS. ຖ້າເຮົາເບິ່ງຕຳແໜ່ງຂອງວັດຖຸທຽບກັບເຟຣມທີ່ສະແດງຜົນ, ເຈົ້າຈະ"
"ເຫັນວ່າຕຳແໜ່ງຈະ \"ໂດດ\" ທຸກໆ 1/10 ວິນາທີ ແທນທີ່ຈະເຄື່ອນທີ່ແບບຕໍ່ເນື່ອງ. ເມື່ອຟີຊິກຄຳນວນຕຳແໜ່ງໃໝ່, ມັ"
"ນຈະບໍ່ໄດ້ສະແດງໃນຕຳແໜ່ງນັ້ນພຽງເຟຣມດຽວ, ແຕ່ຈະຄ້າງຢູ່ບ່ອນເກົ່າເຖິງ 6 ເຟຣມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:38
msgid ""
"This jump can be seen in other combinations of tick / frame rate as "
"glitches, or jitter, caused by this staircasing effect due to the "
"discrepancy between physics tick time and rendered frame time."
msgstr ""
"ການໂດດນີ້ສາມາດເຫັນໄດ້ໃນການປະສົມປະສານອື່ນໆຂອງ tick / frame rate ເຊິ່ງສະແດງອອກມາໃນຮູບແບບຂ"
"ອງການກະຕຸກ (jitter), ທີ່ເກີດຈາກຜົນກະທົບແບບຂັ້ນໄດ ຍ້ອນຄວາມແຕກຕ່າງລະຫວ່າງເວລາຂອງ physics "
"tick ແລະ ເວລາຂອງເຟຣມການສະແດງຜົນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:43
msgid "What can we do about frames and ticks being out of sync?"
msgstr "ເຮົາສາມາດເຮັດແນວໃດໄດ້ແດ່ເມື່ອເຟຣມ ແລະ ticks ບໍ່ກົງກັນ?"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:46
msgid "Lock the tick / frame rate together?"
msgstr "ລັອກ tick / frame rate ໃຫ້ເຂົ້າກັນ?"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:48
msgid ""
"The most obvious solution is to get rid of the problem, by ensuring there is "
"a physics tick that coincides with every frame. This used to be the approach "
"on old consoles and fixed hardware computers. If you know that every player "
"will be using the same hardware, you can ensure it is fast enough to "
"calculate ticks and frames at e.g. 50 FPS, and you will be sure it will work "
"great for everybody."
msgstr ""
"ວິທີແກ້ໄຂທີ່ຊັດເຈນທີ່ສຸດຄືການກຳຈັດບັນຫານີ້ອອກໄປ ໂດຍການເຮັດໃຫ້ physics tick ກົງກັບທຸກໆເຟຣມ. ນີ້ເຄີຍເ"
"ປັນວິທີທີ່ໃຊ້ໃນເຄື່ອງເກມຄອນໂຊລສະໄໝກ່ອນ ຫຼື ຄອມພິວເຕີທີ່ມີຮາດແວຄົງທີ່. ຖ້າເຈົ້າຮູ້ວ່າຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນທຸກຄົນໃຊ້ຮາດແວດຽວກັ"
"ນ, ເຈົ້າສາມາດເຮັດໃຫ້ມັນໄວພໍທີ່ຈະຄຳນວນ ticks ແລະ ເຟຣມໃຫ້ກົງກັນໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:54
msgid ""
"However, modern games are often no longer made for fixed hardware. You will "
"often be planning to release on desktop computers, mobiles, and more. All of "
"which have huge variations in performance, as well as different monitor "
"refresh rates. We need to come up with a better way of dealing with the "
"problem."
msgstr ""
"ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ເກມສະໄໝໃໝ່ບໍ່ໄດ້ຖືກສ້າງມາສຳລັບຮາດແວທີ່ຕາຍຕົວອີກຕໍ່ໄປ. ເຈົ້າມັກຈະວາງແຜນທີ່ຈະປ່ອຍເກມໃນຄ"
"ອມພິວເຕີ, ມືຖື ແລະ ອື່ນໆ. ເຊິ່ງທັງໝົດນີ້ມີປະສິດທິພາບທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນຫຼາຍ ລວມເຖິງ refresh rate ຂອງຈໍພາບ"
"ກໍແຕກຕ່າງກັນ. ເຮົາຈຶ່ງຕ້ອງຫາວິທີທີ່ດີກວ່າໃນການຈັດການກັບບັນຫານີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:60
msgid "Adapt the tick rate?"
msgstr "ປັບອັດຕາ tick rate ຕາມສະພາບ?"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:62
msgid ""
"Instead of designing the game at a fixed physics tick rate, we could allow "
"the tick rate to scale according to the end user's hardware. We could for "
"example use a fixed tick rate that works for that hardware, or even vary the "
"duration of each physics tick to match a particular frame duration."
msgstr ""
"ແທນທີ່ຈະອອກແບບເກມດ້ວຍ physics tick rate ທີ່ຕາຍຕົວ, ເຮົາອາດຈະປ່ອຍໃຫ້ tick rate ປັບປ່ຽນຕາມ"
"ຮາດແວຂອງຜູ້ໃຊ້. ເຮົາອາດຈະໃຊ້ tick rate ທີ່ຄົງທີ່ເຊິ່ງເໝາະກັບຮາດແວນັ້ນໆ ຫຼື ແມ່ນແຕ່ປ່ຽນໄລຍະເວລາຂອງ"
"ແຕ່ລະ physics tick ໃຫ້ກົງກັບໄລຍະເວລາຂອງແຕ່ລະເຟຣມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:67
msgid ""
"This works, but there is a problem. Physics (*and game logic*, which is "
"often also run in the ``_physics_process``) work best and most consistently "
"when run at a **fixed**, predetermined tick rate. If you attempt to run a "
"racing game physics that has been designed for 60 TPS (ticks per second) at "
"e.g. 10 TPS, the physics will behave completely differently. Controls may be "
"less responsive, collisions / trajectories can be completely different. You "
"may test your game thoroughly at 60 TPS, then find it breaks on end users' "
"machines when it runs at a different tick rate."
msgstr ""
"ວິທີນີ້ໃຊ້ໄດ້, ແຕ່ມັນມີບັນຫາ. ຟີຊິກ (*ແລະ logic ຂອງເກມ* ເຊິ່ງມັກຈະໃຊ້ໃນ "
"``_physics_process``) ຈະເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ດີທີ່ສຸດ ແລະ ສະໝໍ່າສະເໝີທີ່ສຸດເມື່ອເຮັດວຽກໃນອັດຕາ **ຄົງທີ່** ທີ່"
"ກຳນົດໄວ້ລ່ວງໜ້າ. ຖ້າເຈົ້າພະຍາຍາມໃຊ້ຟີຊິກຂອງເກມແຂ່ງລົດທີ່ຖືກອອກແບບມາສຳລັບ 60 TPS ໃນອັດຕາ 10 "
"TPS, ຟີຊິກຈະເຮັດວຽກແຕກຕ່າງກັນຢ່າງສິ້ນເຊີງ. ການຄວບຄຸມອາດຈະຕອບສະໜອງຊ້າລົງ, ການຕຳ ຫຼື ເສັ້ນທາງກາ"
"ນເຄື່ອນທີ່ອາດຈະປ່ຽນໄປເລີຍ. ເຈົ້າອາດຈະທົດສອບເກມຢ່າງດີທີ່ 60 TPS ແລ້ວພົບວ່າມັນພັງເມື່ອໄປຫຼິ້ນໃນເຄື່ອງຂອງ"
"ຜູ້ໃຊ້ທີ່ໃຊ້ tick rate ອື່ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:76
msgid ""
"This can make quality assurance difficult with hard to reproduce bugs, "
"especially in AAA games where problems of this sort can be very costly. This "
"can also be problematic for multiplayer games for competitive integrity, as "
"running the game at certain tick rates may be more advantageous than others."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງນີ້ອາດເຮັດໃຫ້ການກວດສອບຄຸນນະພາບ (QA) ເຮັດໄດ້ຍາກ ຍ້ອນມີ bugs ທີ່ເກີດຂຶ້ນຊ້ຳໄດ້ຍາກ, ໂດຍສະເພາະໃ"
"ນເກມລະດັບ AAA. ນອກຈາກນີ້ຍັງອາດເປັນບັນຫາສຳລັບເກມອອນລາຍໃນເລື່ອງຂອງຄວາມຍຸດຕິທຳ ເພາະການໃຊ້ "
"tick rates ບາງອັນອາດຈະໄດ້ປຽບຫຼາຍກວ່າອັນອື່ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:82
msgid ""
"Lock the tick rate, but use interpolation to smooth frames in between "
"physics ticks"
msgstr ""
"ລັອກ tick rate, ແຕ່ໃຊ້ interpolation ເພື່ອເຮັດໃຫ້ເຟຣມລະຫວ່າງ physics ticks ນຸ້ມນວນຂຶ້ນ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:84
msgid ""
"This has become one of the most popular approaches to deal with the problem, "
"although it is optional and disabled by default."
msgstr ""
"ວິທີນີ້ໄດ້ກາຍເປັນໜຶ່ງໃນວິທີທີ່ໄດ້ຮັບຄວາມນິຍົມທີ່ສຸດໃນການຈັດການກັບບັນຫາ, ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າມັນຈະເປັນທາງເລືອກ ແລະ "
"ຖືກປິດໄວ້ໂດຍເລີ່ມຕົ້ນກໍຕາມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:87
msgid ""
"We have established that the most desirable physics/game logic arrangement "
"for consistency and predictability is a physics tick rate that is fixed at "
"design-time. The problem is the discrepancy between the physics position "
"recorded, and where we \"want\" a physics object to be shown on a frame to "
"give smooth motion."
msgstr ""
"ເຮົາໄດ້ຮູ້ແລ້ວວ່າການຈັດການຟີຊິກ/logic ຂອງເກມທີ່ດີທີ່ສຸດເພື່ອຄວາມສະໝໍ່າສະເໝີ ຄືການໃຊ້ physics tick "
"rate ທີ່ຄົງທີ່ຕາມທີ່ອອກແບບໄວ້. ແຕ່ບັນຫາຄືຄວາມແຕກຕ່າງລະຫວ່າງຕຳແໜ່ງຟີຊິກທີ່ຖືກບັນທຶກໄວ້ ແລະ ຕຳແໜ່ງທີ່ເຮົ"
"າ \"ຕ້ອງການ\" ໃຫ້ວັດຖຸສະແດງໃນເຟຣມເພື່ອໃຫ້ເຫັນການເຄື່ອນທີ່ທີ່ນຸ້ມນວນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:92
msgid ""
"The answer turns out to be simple, but can be a little hard to get your head "
"around at first."
msgstr "ຄຳຕອບນັ້ນງ່າຍດາຍ, ແຕ່ອາດຈະເຂົ້າໃຈຍາກເລັກນ້ອຍໃນຕອນທຳອິດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:95
msgid ""
"Instead of keeping track of just the current position of a physics object in "
"the engine, we keep track of *both the current position of the object, and "
"the previous position* on the previous physics tick."
msgstr ""
"ແທນທີ່ຈະຕິດຕາມພຽງແຕ່ຕຳແໜ່ງປັດຈຸບັນຂອງວັດຖຸຟີຊິກໃນ engine, ເຮົາຈະຕິດຕາມ *ທັງຕຳແໜ່ງປັດຈຸບັນ ແລະ ຕຳ"
"ແໜ່ງກ່ອນໜ້າ* ໃນ physics tick ທີ່ຜ່ານມາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:99
msgid ""
"Why do we need the previous position *(in fact the entire transform, "
"including rotation and scaling)*? By using a little math magic, we can use "
"**interpolation** to calculate what the transform of the object would be "
"between those two points, in our ideal world of smooth continuous movement."
msgstr ""
"ເປັນຫຍັງເຮົາຈຶ່ງຕ້ອງມີຕຳແໜ່ງກ່ອນໜ້າ *(ໃນຄວາມເປັນຈິງແມ່ນ transform ທັງໝົດ, ລວມທັງການໝູນ ແລະ ການ"
"ປັບຂະໜາດ)*? ໂດຍການໃຊ້ຄະນິດສາດເລັກນ້ອຍ, ເຮົາສາມາດໃຊ້ **interpolation** ເພື່ອຄຳນວນວ່າ "
"transform ຂອງວັດຖຸຄວນຈະເປັນແນວໃດລະຫວ່າງສອງຈຸດນັ້ນ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ເກີດການເຄື່ອນທີ່ທີ່ນຸ້ມນວນ ແລະ ຕໍ່ເນື່ອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:107
msgid "Linear interpolation"
msgstr "ການແຊກຂໍ້ມູນແບບເສັ້ນຊື່ (Linear interpolation)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:109
msgid ""
"The simplest way to achieve this is linear interpolation, or lerping, which "
"you may have used before."
msgstr ""
"ວິທີທີ່ງ່າຍທີ່ສຸດທີ່ຈະເຮັດສິ່ງນີ້ຄືການໃຊ້ linear interpolation ຫຼື lerping, ເຊິ່ງເຈົ້າອາດຈະເຄີຍໃຊ້້ມາກ່ອ"
"ນແລ້ວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:112
msgid ""
"Let us consider only the position, and a situation where we know that the "
"previous physics tick X coordinate was 10 units, and the current physics "
"tick X coordinate is 30 units."
msgstr ""
"ລອງພິຈາລະນາສະເພາະຕຳແໜ່ງ, ໃນກໍລະນີທີ່ເຮົາຮູ້ວ່າພິກັດ X ຂອງ physics tick ກ່ອນໜ້າຄື 10 ໜ່ວຍ, ແລ"
"ະ ພິກັດ X ຂອງ physics tick ປັດຈຸບັນຄື 30 ໜ່ວຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:116
msgid ""
"Although the maths is explained here, you do not have to worry about the "
"details, as this step will be performed for you. Under the hood, Godot may "
"use more complex forms of interpolation, but linear interpolation is the "
"easiest in terms of explanation."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຈະມີການອະທິບາຍຄະນິດສາດຢູ່ບ່ອນນີ້, ແຕ່ເຈົ້າບໍ່ຕ້ອງກັງວົນກ່ຽວກັບລາຍລະອຽດ, ເພາະວ່າຂັ້ນຕອນນີ້ຈະຖື"
"ກຈັດການໃຫ້ໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ. ພາຍໃນລະບົບ, Godot ອາດຈະໃຊ້ interpolation ທີ່ຊັບຊ້ອນກວ່ານີ້, ແຕ່ "
"linear interpolation ແມ່ນເຂົ້າໃຈໄດ້ງ່າຍທີ່ສຸດໃນການອະທິບາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:122
msgid "The physics interpolation fraction"
msgstr "ສ່ວນເສດສ່ວນການແຊກຂໍ້ມູນຟີຊິກ (physics interpolation fraction)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:124
msgid ""
"If our physics ticks are happening 10 times per second (for this example), "
"what happens if our rendered frame takes place at time 0.12 seconds? We can "
"do some math to figure out where the object would be to obtain a smooth "
"motion between the two ticks."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າ physics ticks ຂອງເຮົາເກີດຂຶ້ນ 10 ຄັ້ງຕໍ່ວິນາທີ (ສຳລັບຕົວຢ່າງນີ້), ຈະເກີດຫຍັງຂຶ້ນຖ້າເຟຣມທີ່ສະແດງຜົ"
"ນເກີດຂຶ້ນໃນເວລາ 0.12 ວິນາທີ? ເຮົາສາມາດໃຊ້ຄະນິດສາດເພື່ອຫາວ່າວັດຖຸຄວນຈະຢູ່ໃສເພື່ອໃຫ້ການເຄື່ອນທີ່ລະຫວ່າ"
"ງສອງ ticks ນັ້ນນຸ້ມນວນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:129
msgid ""
"First of all, we have to calculate how far through the physics tick we want "
"the object to be. If the last physics tick took place at 0.1 seconds, we are "
"0.02 seconds *(0.12 - 0.1)* through a tick that we know will take 0.1 "
"seconds (10 ticks per second). The fraction through the tick is thus:"
msgstr ""
"ກ່ອນອື່ນໝົດ, ເຮົາຕ້ອງຄຳນວນວ່າວັດຖຸຄວນຈະຢູ່ຈຸດໃດໃນລະຫວ່າງ physics tick. ຖ້າ physics tick ຫຼ້າສຸ"
"ດເກີດຂຶ້ນທີ່ 0.1 ວິນາທີ, ຕອນນີ້ເຮົາຜ່ານມາແລ້ວ 0.02 ວິນາທີ *(0.12 - 0.1)* ຈາກໄລຍະເວລາຂອງ "
"tick ທັງໝົດທີ່ເຮົາຮູ້ວ່າຄື 0.1 ວິນາທີ (10 ticks ຕໍ່ວິນາທີ). ດັ່ງນັ້ນ ເສດສ່ວນ (fraction) ຄື:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:139
msgid ""
"This is called the **physics interpolation fraction**, and is handily "
"calculated for you by Godot. It can be retrieved on any frame by "
"calling :ref:`Engine.get_physics_interpolation_fraction<class_Engine_method_get_physics_interpolation_fraction>`."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງນີ້ເອີ້ນວ່າ **physics interpolation fraction**, ເຊິ່ງ Godot ຄຳນວນໃຫ້ເຈົ້າຢ່າງສະດວກ. ເຈົ້"
"າສາມາດດຶງຄ່ານີ້ໄດ້ໃນທຸກໆເຟຣມໂດຍການເອີ້ນໃຊ້ "
":ref:`Engine.get_physics_interpolation_fraction<class_Engine_method_get_physics_interpolation_fraction>"
"`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:143
msgid "Calculating the interpolated position"
msgstr "ການຄຳນວນຕຳແໜ່ງທີ່ແຊກຂໍ້ມູນແລ້ວ (interpolated position)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:145
msgid ""
"Once we have the interpolation fraction, we can insert it into a standard "
"linear interpolation equation. The X coordinate would thus be:"
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອເຮົາໄດ້ເສດສ່ວນ interpolation ແລ້ວ, ເຮົາສາມາດນຳໄປແທນໃນສົມຜົນ linear interpolation "
"ມາດຕະຖານໄດ້. ດັ່ງນັ້ນ ພິກັດ X ຈະເປັນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:152
msgid "So substituting our ``x_prev`` as 10, and ``x_curr`` as 30:"
msgstr "ໂດຍການແທນຄ່າ ``x_prev`` ເປັນ 10, ແລະ ``x_curr`` ເປັນ 30:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:160
msgid "Let's break that down:"
msgstr "ລອງມາແຍກລາຍລະອຽດເບິ່ງ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:162
msgid ""
"We know the X starts from the coordinate on the previous tick (``x_prev``) "
"which is 10 units."
msgstr ""
"ເຮົາຮູ້ວ່າ X ເລີ່ມຕົ້ນຈາກພິກັດໃນ tick ກ່ອນໜ້າ (``x_prev``) ເຊິ່ງຄື 10 ໜ່ວຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:164
msgid ""
"We know that after the full tick, the difference between the current tick "
"and the previous tick will have been added (``x_curr - x_prev``) (which is "
"20 units)."
msgstr ""
"ເຮົາຮູ້ວ່າຫຼັງຈາກຈົບ tick, ສ່ວນຕ່າງລະຫວ່າງ tick ປັດຈຸບັນ ແລະ tick ກ່ອນໜ້າຈະຖືກບວກເພີ່ມເຂົ້າໄປ "
"(``x_curr - x_prev``) (ເຊິ່ງຄື 20 ໜ່ວຍ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:166
msgid ""
"The only thing we need to vary is the proportion of this difference we add, "
"according to how far we are through the physics tick."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງດຽວທີ່ເຮົາຕ້ອງປ່ຽນແປງຄືສັດສ່ວນຂອງສ່ວນຕ່າງນີ້ທີ່ເຮົາຈະບວກເພີ່ມເຂົ້າໄປ, ຕາມໄລຍະເວລາທີ່ເຮົາຜ່ານມາໃນ "
"physics tick."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:169
msgid ""
"Although this example interpolates the position, the same thing can be done "
"with the rotation and scale of objects. It is not necessary to know the "
"details as Godot will do all this for you."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຕົວຢ່າງນີ້ຈະແຊກຂໍ້ມູນສະເພາະຕຳແໜ່ງ, ແຕ່ສິ່ງດຽວກັນນີ້ກໍສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ກັບການໝູນ ແລະ ການປັບຂະໜາ"
"ດຂອງວັດຖຸ. ເຈົ້າບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງຮູ້ລາຍລະອຽດ ເພາະ Godot ຈະຈັດການທຸກຢ່າງໃຫ້ເອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:174
msgid "Smoothed transformations between physics ticks?"
msgstr "ການປ່ຽນແປງຮູບຮ່າງທີ່ນຸ້ມນວນລະຫວ່າງ physics ticks?"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:176
msgid ""
"Putting all this together shows that it should be possible to have a nice "
"smooth estimation of the transform of objects between the current and "
"previous physics tick."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອຮວມທຸກຢ່າງເຂົ້າກັນແລ້ວ, ມັນຈະຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ເຮົາສາມາດຄາດຄະເນ transform ຂອງວັດຖຸລະຫວ່າງ physics "
"tick ປັດຈຸບັນ ແລະ ກ່ອນໜ້າໄດ້ຢ່າງນຸ້ມນວນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:180
msgid ""
"But wait, you may have noticed something. If we are interpolating between "
"the current and previous ticks, we are not estimating the position of the "
"object *now*, we are estimating the position of the object in the past. To "
"be exact, we are estimating the position of the object *between 1 and 2 "
"ticks* into the past."
msgstr ""
"ແຕ່ລໍຖ້າກ່ອນ, ເຈົ້າອາດຈະສັງເກດເຫັນບາງຢ່າງ. ຖ້າເຮົາແຊກຂໍ້ມູນລະຫວ່າງ tick ປັດຈຸບັນ ແລະ ກ່ອນໜ້າ, ເຮົາ"
"ບໍ່ໄດ້ຄາດຄະເນຕຳແໜ່ງຂອງວັດຖຸໃນ *ຕອນນີ້*, ແຕ່ເຮົາກຳລັງຄາດຄະເນຕຳແໜ່ງຂອງວັດຖຸໃນອະດີດ. ເວົ້າໃຫ້ຊັດເຈນ"
"ກໍຄື, ເຮົາກຳລັງຄາດຄະເນຕຳແໜ່ງຂອງວັດຖຸທີ່ຢ້ອນຫຼັງໄປ *ລະຫວ່າງ 1 ຫາ 2 ticks*."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:186
msgid "In the past"
msgstr "ໃນອະດີດ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:188
msgid ""
"What does this mean? This scheme does work, but it does mean we are "
"effectively introducing a delay between what we see on the screen, and where "
"the objects *should* be."
msgstr ""
"ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າແນວໃດ? ວິທີນີ້ໃຊ້ໄດ້ຜົນ, ແຕ່ມັນໝາຍຄວາມວ່າເຮົາກຳລັງເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດຄວາມຫຼ້າຊ້າ (delay) ລະຫວ່າ"
"ງສິ່ງທີ່ເຮົາເຫັນໃນຈໍ ກັບສິ່ງທີ່ວັດຖຸ *ຄວນ* ຈະເປັນແທ້ໆ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:192
msgid ""
"In practice, most people won't notice this delay, or rather, it is typically "
"not *objectionable*. There are already significant delays involved in games, "
"we just don't typically notice them. The most significant effect is there "
"can be a slight delay to input, which can be a factor in fast twitch games. "
"In some of these fast input situations, you may wish to turn off physics "
"interpolation and use a different scheme, or use a high tick rate, which "
"mitigates these delays."
msgstr ""
"ໃນທາງປະຕິບັດ, ຄົນສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ຈະບໍ່ສັງເກດເຫັນຄວາມຫຼ້າຊ້ານີ້, ຫຼື ເວົ້າອີກຢ່າງໜຶ່ງຄື ມັນບໍ່ແມ່ນເລື່ອງທີ່ *ຍອມຮັບບໍ່ໄ"
"ດ້*. ໃນເກມມີຄວາມຫຼ້າຊ້າຫຼາຍຢ່າງທີ່ເກີດຂຶ້ນຢູ່ແລ້ວ ໂດຍທີ່ເຮົາບໍ່ຮູ້ຕົວ. ຜົນກະທົບທີ່ເຫັນໄດ້ຊັດເຈນທີ່ສຸດຄືອາດຈະມີຄວ"
"າມຫຼ້າຊ້າເລັກນ້ອຍໃນການຕອບສະໜອງຕໍ່ input, ເຊິ່ງອາດຈະເປັນບັນຫາໃນເກມທີ່ຕ້ອງການຄວາມໄວສູງ. ໃນບາງກໍ"
"ລະນີ, ເຈົ້າອາດຈະຕ້ອງການປິດ physics interpolation ແລ້ວໃຊ້ວິທີອື່ນ ຫຼື ໃຊ້ tick rate ທີ່ສູງຂຶ້ນເພື່ອ"
"ຫຼຸດຜ່ອນຄວາມຫຼ້າຊ້າເຫຼົ່ານີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:200
msgid "Why look into the past? Why not predict the future?"
msgstr "ເປັນຫຍັງຕ້ອງເບິ່ງອະດີດ? ເປັນຫຍັງບໍ່ທຳນາຍອະນາຄົດ?"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:202
msgid ""
"There is an alternative to this scheme, which is: instead of interpolating "
"between the previous and current tick, we use maths to *extrapolate* into "
"the future. We try to predict where the object *will be*, rather than show "
"it where it was. This can be done and may be offered as an option in future, "
"but there are some significant downsides:"
msgstr ""
"ມັນມີວິທີທາງເລືອກຄື: ແທນທີ່ຈະແຊກຂໍ້ມູນລະຫວ່າງ tick ກ່ອນໜ້າ ແລະ ປັດຈຸບັນ, ເຮົາໃຊ້ຄະນິດສາດເພື່ອ *ຄາດກ"
"ານ (extrapolate)* ໄປໃນອະນາຄົດ. ເຮົາພະຍາຍາມທຳນາຍວ່າວັດຖຸ *ຈະໄປຢູ່ໃສ*, ແທນທີ່ຈະສະແດງບ່ອນທີ່"
"ມັນເຄີຍຢູ່. ວິທີນີ້ສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ ແລະ ອາດຈະມີໃຫ້ເລືອກໃນອະນາຄົດ, ແຕ່ມັນມີຂໍ້ເສຍທີ່ສຳຄັນຄື:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:208
msgid ""
"The prediction may not be correct, especially when an object collides with "
"another object during the physics tick."
msgstr ""
"ການທຳນາຍອາດຈະບໍ່ຖືກຕ້ອງ, ໂດຍສະເພາະເມື່ອວັດຖຸໄປຕຳກັບວັດຖຸອື່ນໃນລະຫວ່າງ physics tick."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:210
msgid ""
"Where a prediction was incorrect, the object may extrapolate into an "
"\"impossible\" position, like inside a wall."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອການທຳນາຍຜິດພາດ, ວັດຖຸອາດຈະເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄປຢູ່ໃນຕຳແໜ່ງທີ່ \"ເປັນໄປບໍ່ໄດ້\", ເຊັ່ນ: ເຂົ້າໄປໃນກຳແພງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:212
msgid ""
"Providing the movement speed is slow, these incorrect predictions may not be "
"too much of a problem."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າຄວາມໄວໃນການເຄື່ອນທີ່ຊ້າ, ການທຳນາຍທີ່ຜິດພາດເຫຼົ່ານີ້ອາດຈະບໍ່ແມ່ນບັນຫາໃຫຍ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:214
msgid ""
"When a prediction was incorrect, the object may have to jump or snap back "
"onto the corrected path. This can be visually jarring."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອການທຳນາຍຜິດພາດ, ວັດຖຸອາດຈະຕ້ອງໂດດ ຫຼື snap ກັບຄືນໄປຫາເສັ້ນທາງທີ່ຖືກຕ້ອງ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເຫັນພາ"
"ບທີ່ກະຕຸກ ແລະ ບໍ່ສະບາຍຕາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:218
msgid "Fixed timestep interpolation"
msgstr "ການແຊກຂໍ້ມູນແບບໄລຍະເວລາຄົງທີ່ (Fixed timestep interpolation)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:220
msgid ""
"In Godot this whole system is referred to as physics interpolation, but you "
"may also hear it referred to as **\"fixed timestep interpolation\"**, as it "
"is interpolating between objects moved with a fixed timestep (physics ticks "
"per second). In some ways the second term is more accurate, because it can "
"also be used to interpolate objects that are not driven by physics."
msgstr ""
"ໃນ Godot ລະບົບທັງໝົດນີ້ເອີ້ນວ່າ physics interpolation, ແຕ່ເຈົ້າອາດຈະເຄີຍໄດ້ຍິນຄົນເອີ້ນວ່າ "
"**\"fixed timestep interpolation\"**, ເພາະວ່າມັນເປັນການແຊກຂໍ້ມູນລະຫວ່າງວັດຖຸທີ່ເຄື່ອນທີ່ດ້ວຍ "
"timestep ທີ່ຄົງທີ່. ໃນບາງແງ່ມຸມ ຄຳສັບທີສອງອາດຈະຊັດເຈນກວ່າ ເພາະມັນຍັງສາມາດໃຊ້ເພື່ອແຊກຂໍ້ມູນວັດຖຸທີ່ບໍ່ໄ"
"ດ້ຖືກຄວບຄຸມດ້ວຍຟີຊິກໄດ້ອີກດ້ວຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/physics_interpolation_introduction.rst:226
msgid ""
"Although physics interpolation is usually a good choice, there are "
"exceptions where you may choose not to use Godot's built-in physics "
"interpolation (or use it in a limited fashion). An example category is "
"internet multiplayer games. Multiplayer games often receive tick or timing "
"based information from other players or a server and these may not coincide "
"with local physics ticks, so a custom interpolation technique can often be a "
"better fit."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າ physics interpolation ມັກຈະເປັນທາງເລືອກທີ່ດີ, ແຕ່ກໍມີຂໍ້ຍົກເວັ້ນທີ່ເຈົ້າອາດຈະເລືອກບໍ່ໃຊ້ "
"interpolation ທີ່ຕິດຕາມາຂອງ Godot (ຫຼື ໃຊ້ໃນແບບທີ່ຈຳກັດ). ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ ເກມອອນລາຍຫຼິ້ນຫຼາຍຄົນ. ເ"
"ກມເຫຼົ່ານີ້ມັກຈະໄດ້ຮັບຂໍ້ມູນ tick ຫຼື ເວລາຈາກຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນຄົນອື່ນ ຫຼື ຈາກ server ເຊິ່ງຂໍ້ມູນເຫຼົ່ານີ້ອາດຈະບໍ່ກົງກັບ "
"physics ticks ໃນເຄື່ອງຂອງເຮົາ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນການໃຊ້ເຕັກນິກ interpolation ທີ່ຂຽນຂຶ້ນເອງມັກຈະເໝາະສົມກ"
"ວ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:4
msgid "Using physics interpolation"
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ physics interpolation"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:6
msgid ""
"How do we incorporate physics interpolation into a Godot game? Are there any "
"caveats?"
msgstr ""
"ເຮົາຈະເອົາ physics interpolation ມາໃຊ້ໃນເກມ Godot ໄດ້ແນວໃດ? ແລະ ມີຂໍ້ຄວນລະວັງຫຍັງແດ່?"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:9
msgid ""
"We have tried to make the system as easy to use as possible, and many "
"existing games will work with few changes. That said there are some "
"situations which require special treatment, and these will be described."
msgstr ""
"ພວກເຮົາໄດ້ພະຍາຍາມເຮັດໃຫ້ລະບົບນີ້ໃຊ້ງ່າຍທີ່ສຸດເທົ່າທີ່ຈະເປັນໄປໄດ້, ແລະ ເກມຫຼາຍໆເກມທີ່ມີຢູ່ກໍຈະສາມາດໃຊ້ໄດ້"
"ໂດຍມີການປ່ຽນແປງພຽງເລັກນ້ອຍ. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ມັນມີບາງສະຖານະການທີ່ຕ້ອງການການຈັດການເປັນພິເສດ ເຊິ່ງພ"
"ວກເຮົາຈະອະທິບາຍໃນຕໍ່ໜ້າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:14
msgid "Turn on the physics interpolation setting"
msgstr "ເປີດການຕັ້ງຄ່າ physics interpolation"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:16
msgid ""
"The first step is to turn on physics interpolation in :ref:`Project Settings "
"> Physics > Common > Physics "
"Interpolation<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/common/"
"physics_interpolation>` You can now run your game."
msgstr ""
"ຂັ້ນຕອນທຳອິດຄືການເປີດ physics interpolation ໃນ :ref:`Project Settings > Physics > "
"Common > Physics Interpolation<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/common/"
"physics_interpolation>` ຈາກນັ້ນເຈົ້າກໍສາມາດລອງຫຼິ້ນເກມໄດ້ເລີຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:20
msgid ""
"It is likely that nothing looks hugely different, particularly if you are "
"running physics at 60 TPS or a multiple of it. However, quite a bit more is "
"happening behind the scenes."
msgstr ""
"ມັນອາດຈະເບິ່ງຄືວ່າບໍ່ມີຫຍັງປ່ຽນແປງຫຼາຍ, ໂດຍສະເພາະຖ້າເຈົ້າໃຊ້ຟີຊິກທີ່ 60 TPS ຫຼື ສູງກວ່ານັ້ນ. ແນວໃດກໍຕາ"
"ມ, ມັນມີຫຼາຍຢ່າງເກີດຂຶ້ນເບື້ອງຫຼັງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:26
msgid ""
"To convert an existing game to use interpolation, it is highly recommended "
"that you temporarily set :ref:`Project Settings > Physics > Common > Physics "
"Tick per Second<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/common/"
"physics_ticks_per_second>` to a low value such as ``10``, which will make "
"interpolation problems more obvious."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອແປງເກມທີ່ມີຢູ່ໃຫ້ມາໃຊ້ interpolation, ພວກເຮົາແນະນຳໃຫ້ເຈົ້າຕັ້ງຄ່າ :ref:`Project "
"Settings > Physics > Common > Physics Tick per "
"Second<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/common/"
"physics_ticks_per_second>` ເປັນຄ່າຕໍ່າໆ ເຊັ່ນ ``10`` ຊົ່ວຄາວ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ເຫັນບັນຫາຂອງ "
"interpolation ໄດ້ຊັດເຈນຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:32
msgid "Move (almost) all game logic from _process to _physics_process"
msgstr "ຍ້າຍ logic ເກມ (ເກືອບ) ທັງໝົດຈາກ _process ໄປໄວ້ໃນ _physics_process"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:34
msgid ""
"The most fundamental requirement for physics interpolation (which you may be "
"doing already) is that you should be moving and performing game logic on "
"your objects within ``_physics_process`` (which runs at a physics tick) "
"rather than ``_process`` (which runs on a rendered frame). This means your "
"scripts should typically be doing the bulk of their processing within "
"``_physics_process``, including responding to input and AI."
msgstr ""
"ຂໍ້ກຳນົດພື້ນຖານທີ່ສຸດສຳລັບ physics interpolation (ເຊິ່ງເຈົ້າອາດຈະເຮັດຢູ່ແລ້ວ) ຄື ເຈົ້າຄວນເຄື່ອນທີ່ ແລ"
"ະ ໃຊ້ logic ຂອງເກມໃນ ``_physics_process`` (ເຊິ່ງເຮັດວຽກຕາມ physics tick) ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັ"
"ນ ``_process`` (ເຊິ່ງເຮັດວຽກຕາມເຟຣມການສະແດງຜົນ). ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າ script ຂອງເຈົ້າສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ຄວນ"
"ຈະເຮັດວຽກໃນ ``_physics_process``, ລວມທັງການຕອບສະໜອງຕໍ່ input ແລະ AI."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:41
msgid ""
"Setting the transform of objects only within physics ticks allows the "
"automatic interpolation to deal with transforms *between* physics ticks, and "
"ensures the game will run the same whatever machine it is run on. As a "
"bonus, this also reduces CPU usage if the game is rendering at high FPS, "
"since AI logic (for example) will no longer run on every rendered frame."
msgstr ""
"ການກຳນົດ transform ຂອງວັດຖຸສະເພາະໃນ physics ticks ຈະຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ interpolation ອັດຕະໂນມັດ"
"ສາມາດຈັດການກັບ transform *ລະຫວ່າງ* physics ticks ໄດ້, ແລະ ຮັບປະກັນວ່າເກມຈະເຮັດວຽກຄືກັນບໍ່"
"ວ່າຈະຫຼິ້ນໃນເຄື່ອງໃດກໍຕາມ. ນອກຈາກນີ້, ມັນຍັງຊ່ວຍຫຼຸດຜ່ອນການໃຊ້ CPU ຫາກເກມສະແດງຜົນດ້ວຍ FPS ສູງ ເພ"
"າະ logic AI (ຕົວຢ່າງ) ຈະບໍ່ຕ້ອງເຮັດວຽກໃນທຸກໆເຟຣມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:47
msgid ""
"If you attempt to set the transform of interpolated objects *outside* the "
"physics tick, the calculations for the interpolated position will be "
"incorrect, and you will get jitter. This jitter may not be visible on your "
"machine, but it *will* occur for some players. For this reason, setting the "
"transform of interpolated objects should be avoided outside of the physics "
"tick. Godot will attempt to produce warnings in the editor if this case is "
"detected."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເຈົ້າພະຍາຍາມກຳນົດ transform ຂອງວັດຖຸທີ່ຖືກແຊກຂໍ້ມູນ *ຢູ່ນອກ* physics tick, ການຄຳນວນຕຳແໜ່ງ"
"ທີ່ຖືກແຊກຂໍ້ມູນຈະຜິດພາດ ແລະ ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດອາການສັ່ນ (jitter). ອາການສັ່ນນີ້ອາດຈະບໍ່ເຫັນໃນເຄື່ອງຂອງເຈົ້"
"າ, ແຕ່ມັນ *ຈະ* ເກີດຂຶ້ນກັບຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນບາງຄົນ. ດ້ວຍເຫດນີ້, ຄວນຫຼີກເວັ້ນການກຳນົດ transform ຂອງວັດຖຸຢູ່ນອກ "
"physics tick. Godot ຈະພະຍາຍາມສະແດງຄຳເຕືອນໃນ editor ຫາກກວດພົບກໍລະນີນັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:55
msgid ""
"This is only a *soft rule*. There are some occasions where you might want to "
"teleport objects outside of the physics tick (for instance when starting a "
"level, or respawning objects). Still, in general, you should be applying "
"transforms from the physics tick."
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ເປັນພຽງ *ກົດເກນທົ່ວໄປ*. ມັນມີບາງໂອກາດທີ່ເຈົ້າອາດຈະຕ້ອງການ teleport ວັດຖຸຢູ່ນອກ physics "
"tick (ຕົວຢ່າງ ເມື່ອເລີ່ມສາກໃໝ່ ຫຼື ເມື່ອເກີດໃໝ່). ແຕ່ໂດຍລວມແລ້ວ ເຈົ້າຄວນໃຊ້ transform ຈາກ "
"physics tick ເປັນຫຼັກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:62
msgid "Ensure that all indirect movement happens during physics ticks"
msgstr "ໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າການເຄື່ອນທີ່ທາງອ້ອມທັງໝົດເກີດຂຶ້ນໃນລະຫວ່າງ physics ticks"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:64
msgid ""
"Consider that in Godot, nodes can be moved not just directly in your own "
"scripts, but also by automatic methods such as tweening, animation, and "
"navigation. All these methods should also have their timing set to operate "
"on the physics tick rather than each frame (\"idle\"), **if** you are using "
"them to move objects (*these methods can also be used to control properties "
"that are not interpolated*)."
msgstr ""
"ໃນ Godot, ໂນດສາມາດເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄດ້ບໍ່ພຽງແຕ່ຜ່ານ script ໂດຍກົງ, ແຕ່ຍັງຜ່ານວິທີອັດຕະໂນມັດ ເຊັ່ນ "
"tweening, animation, ແລະ navigation. ວິທີການທັງໝົດເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຄວນຖືກຕັ້ງຄ່າເວລາໃຫ້ເຮັດວຽກໃນ "
"physics tick ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນແຕ່ລະເຟຣມ (\"idle\"), **ຫາກ** ເຈົ້າໃຊ້ມັນເພື່ອຍ້າຍວັດຖຸ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:70
msgid ""
"Also consider that nodes can be moved not just by moving themselves, but "
"also by moving parent nodes in the :ref:`SceneTree<class_SceneTree>`. The "
"movement of parents should therefore also only occur during physics ticks."
msgstr ""
"ນອກຈາກນີ້ ໂນດຍັງສາມາດເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄດ້ໂດຍການຍ້າຍໂນດແມ່ໃນ :ref:`SceneTree<class_SceneTree>`. "
"ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ການເຄື່ອນທີ່ຂອງໂນດແມ່ກໍຄວນເກີດຂຶ້ນສະເພາະໃນລະຫວ່າງ physics ticks ເຊັ່ນກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:75
msgid "Choose a physics tick rate"
msgstr "ເລືອກອັດຕາ physics tick rate"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:77
msgid ""
"When using physics interpolation, the rendering is decoupled from physics, "
"and you can choose any value that makes sense for your game. You are no "
"longer limited to values that are multiples of the user's monitor refresh "
"rate (for stutter-free gameplay if the target FPS is reached)."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອໃຊ້ physics interpolation, ການສະແດງຜົນຈະຖືກແຍກອອກຈາກຟີຊິກ, ແລະ ເຈົ້າສາມາດເລືອກຄ່າໃດ"
"ກໍໄດ້ທີ່ເໝາະສົມກັບເກມຂອງເຈົ້າ. ເຈົ້າບໍ່ໄດ້ຖືກຈຳກັດໃຫ້ໃຊ້ຄ່າທີ່ເປັນຕົວຄູນຂອງ refresh rate ຂອງຈໍພາບອີກຕໍ່ໄ"
"ປ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:82
msgid "As a rough guide:"
msgstr "ຄຳແນະນຳໂດຍສັງເຂບ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:1
msgid "Low tick rates (10-30)"
msgstr "Tick rates ຕໍ່າ (10-30)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:1
msgid "Medium tick rates (30-60)"
msgstr "Tick rates ກາງ (30-60)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:1
msgid "High tick rates (60+)"
msgstr "Tick rates ສູງ (60+)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:1
msgid "Better CPU performance"
msgstr "ປະສິດທິພາບ CPU ທີ່ດີກວ່າ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:1
msgid "Good physics behavior in complex scenes"
msgstr "ພຶດຕິກຳຟີຊິກທີ່ດີໃນສາກທີ່ຊັບຊ້ອນ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:1
msgid "Good with fast physics"
msgstr "ດີກັບຟີຊິກທີ່ເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄວ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:1
msgid "Add some delay to input"
msgstr "ເພີ່ມຄວາມຫຼ້າຊ້າໃຫ້ກັບ input ເລັກນ້ອຍ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:1
msgid "Good for first person games"
msgstr "ດີສຳລັບເກມມຸມມອງບຸກຄົນທີໜຶ່ງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:1
msgid "Good for racing games"
msgstr "ດີສຳລັບເກມແຂ່ງລົດ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:1
msgid "Simple physics behaviour"
msgstr "ພຶດຕິກຳຟີຊິກແບບງ່າຍໆ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:92
msgid ""
"You can always change the tick rate as you develop, it is as simple as "
"changing the project setting."
msgstr ""
"ເຈົ້າສາມາດປ່ຽນອັດຕາ tick rate ໄດ້ຕະຫຼອດເວລາໃນລະຫວ່າງການພັດທະນາ, ພຽງແຕ່ເຂົ້າໄປປ່ຽນໃນການຕັ້ງຄ່"
"າໂປຣເຈັກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:96
msgid "Call ``reset_physics_interpolation()`` when teleporting objects"
msgstr "ເອີ້ນໃຊ້ ``reset_physics_interpolation()`` ເມື່ອ teleport ວັດຖຸ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:98
msgid ""
"Most of the time, interpolation is what you want between two physics ticks. "
"However, there is one situation in which it may *not* be what you want. That "
"is when you are initially placing objects, or moving them to a new location. "
"Here, you don't want a smooth motion between where the object was (e.g. the "
"origin) and the initial position - you want an instantaneous move."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ແລ້ວ, interpolation ຄືສິ່ງທີ່ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການລະຫວ່າງສອງ physics ticks. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, "
"ມັນມີສະຖານະການໜຶ່ງທີ່ມັນອາດຈະ *ບໍ່* ແມ່ນສິ່ງທີ່ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການ. ນັ້ນຄືຕອນທີ່ເຈົ້າວາງວັດຖຸໃນຕຳແໜ່ງເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ ຫຼື ຍ້າ"
"ຍພວກມັນໄປຕຳແໜ່ງໃໝ່ທັນທີ. ໃນຈຸດນີ້ ເຈົ້າບໍ່ຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ເຫັນການເຄື່ອນທີ່ທີ່ນຸ້ມນວນລະຫວ່າງບ່ອນເກົ່າກັບບ່ອນໃໝ່ - "
"ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ມັນຍ້າຍໄປທັນທີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:104
msgid ""
"The solution to this is to call "
"the :ref:`Node.reset_physics_interpolation<class_Node_method_reset_physics_interpolation>` "
"function. What this function does under the hood is set the internally "
"stored *previous transform* of the object to be equal to the *current "
"transform*. This ensures that when interpolating between these two equal "
"transforms, there will be no movement."
msgstr ""
"ວິທີແກ້ໄຂຄືການເອີ້ນໃຊ້ຟັງຊັນ "
":ref:`Node.reset_physics_interpolation<class_Node_method_reset_physics_interpolation>"
"`. ສິ່ງທີ່ຟັງຊັນນີ້ເຮັດກໍຄືການກຳນົດໃຫ້ *transform ກ່ອນໜ້າ* ທີ່ຖືກເກັບໄວ້ເທົ່າກັບ *transform ປັດຈຸບັນ*. "
"ສິ່ງນີ້ຮັບປະກັນວ່າເມື່ອມີການແຊກຂໍ້ມູນລະຫວ່າງສອງຄ່າທີ່ເທົ່າກັນນີ້, ຈະບໍ່ມີການເຄື່ອນທີ່ເກີດຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:110
msgid ""
"Even if you forget to call this, it will usually not be a problem in most "
"situations (especially at high tick rates). This is something you can easily "
"leave to the polishing phase of your game. The worst that will happen is "
"seeing a streaking motion for a frame or so when you move them - you will "
"know when you need it!"
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າເຈົ້າຈະລືມເອີ້ນໃຊ້ມັນ, ປົກກະຕິແລ້ວກໍຈະບໍ່ເປັນບັນຫາໃນສະຖານະການສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ (ໂດຍສະເພາະໃນ "
"tick rates ທີ່ສູງ). ສິ່ງນີ້ເປັນເລື່ອງທີ່ເຈົ້າສາມາດເກັບໄວ້ເຮັດໃນຂັ້ນຕອນການເກັບລາຍລະອຽດຂອງເກມໄດ້. ສິ່ງ"
"ທີ່ຮ້າຍແຮງທີ່ສຸດທີ່ຈະເກີດຂຶ້ນກໍຄືການເຫັນວັດຖຸເຄື່ອນທີ່ແບບລາກຍາວພຽງເຟຣມດຽວເມື່ອເຈົ້າຍ້າຍມັນ - ເຈົ້າຈະຮູ້ເອງເ"
"ມື່ອເຫັນວ່າມັນຈຳເປັນ!"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:116
msgid "There are actually two ways to use ``reset_physics_interpolation()``:"
msgstr "ໃນຄວາມເປັນຈິງມີສອງວິທີໃນການໃຊ້ ``reset_physics_interpolation()``:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:118
msgid "*Standing start (e.g. player)*"
msgstr "*ການເລີ່ມຕົ້ນແບບຢູ່ກັບທີ່ (ເຊັ່ນ: ຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນ)*"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:120
#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:128
msgid "Set the initial transform"
msgstr "ກຳນົດ transform ເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:121
#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:129
msgid "Call ``reset_physics_interpolation()``"
msgstr "ເອີ້ນໃຊ້ ``reset_physics_interpolation()``"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:123
msgid ""
"The previous and current transforms will be identical, resulting in no "
"initial movement."
msgstr ""
"ຟັງຊັນ ``_exit_tree()`` ຈະຖືກເອີ້ນໃຊ້ ເມື່ອປລັກອິນຖືກປິດໃຊ້ງານ. ຖ້າໜ້າຈໍຫຼັກຍັງມີຢູ່, ພວກເຮົາຈະເອີ້ນໃ"
"ຊ້ ``queue_free()`` ເພື່ອຄືນໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈໍາໃຫ້ອິນສະແຕນຊ໌ (instance) ແລະ ລຶບມັນອອກຈາກໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈໍ"
"າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:126
msgid "*Moving start (e.g. bullet)*"
msgstr "*ການເລີ່ມຕົ້ນແບບເຄື່ອນທີ່ (ເຊັ່ນ: ລູກປືນ)*"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:130
msgid "Immediately set the transform expected after the first tick of motion"
msgstr "ກຳນົດ transform ທີ່ຄາດໄວ້ຫຼັງຈາກ tick ທຳອິດຂອງການເຄື່ອນທີ່ທັນທີ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:132
msgid ""
"The previous transform will be the starting position, and the current "
"transform will act as though a tick of simulation has already taken place. "
"This will immediately start moving the object, instead of having a tick "
"delay standing still."
msgstr ""
"ການປ່ຽນຮູບແບບກ່ອນໜ້າຈະເປັນຕຳແໜ່ງເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ແລະ ການປ່ຽນຮູບແບບປັດຈຸບັນຈະເຮັດຄືກັບວ່າບາດກ້າວໜຶ່ງຂອງການ"
"ຈຳລອງໄດ້ເກີດຂຶ້ນແລ້ວ.\n"
"ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ວັດຖຸເລີ່ມເຄື່ອນທີ່ທັນທີ, ແທນທີ່ຈະມີການຊັກຊ້າໜຶ່ງບາດກ້າວໃນການຢຸດນິ່ງຢູ່ກັບທີ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:136
msgid ""
"Make sure you set the transform and call ``reset_physics_interpolation()`` "
"in the correct order as shown above, otherwise you will see unwanted "
"\"streaking\"."
msgstr ""
"ໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າເຈົ້າກຳນົດ transform ແລະ ເອີ້ນໃຊ້ ``reset_physics_interpolation()`` ຕາມລຳດັບ"
"ທີ່ຖືກຕ້ອງດັ່ງທີ່ສະແດງຂ້າງເທິງ, ຖ້າບໍ່ດັ່ງນັ້ນເຈົ້າຈະເຫັນອາການ \"ລາກຍາວ\" ທີ່ບໍ່ຕ້ອງການ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:141
msgid "Testing and debugging tips"
msgstr "ເຄັດລັບການທົດສອບ ແລະ ການແກ້ໄຂ bug"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:143
msgid ""
"Even if you intend to run physics at 60 TPS, in order to thoroughly test "
"your interpolation and get the smoothest gameplay, it is highly recommended "
"to temporarily set the physics tick rate to a low value such as 10 TPS."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າເຈົ້າຈະຕັ້ງໃຈໃຊ້ຟີຊິກທີ່ 60 TPS, ແຕ່ເພື່ອທົດສອບ interpolation ໃຫ້ລະອຽດ ແລະ ໃຫ້ໄດ້ການຫຼິ້"
"ນເກມທີ່ນຸ້ມນວນທີ່ສຸດ, ພວກເຮົາແນະນຳໃຫ້ຕັ້ງ physics tick rate ເປັນຄ່າຕໍ່າໆ ເຊັ່ນ 10 TPS ຊົ່ວຄາວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:147
msgid ""
"The gameplay may not work perfectly, but it should enable you to more easily "
"see cases where you should be "
"calling :ref:`Node.reset_physics_interpolation<class_Node_method_reset_physics_interpolation>`, "
"or where you should be using your own custom interpolation on e.g. "
"a :ref:`Camera3D<class_Camera3D>`. Once you have these cases fixed, you can "
"set the physics tick rate back to the desired setting."
msgstr ""
"ການຫຼິ້ນເກມອາດຈະບໍ່ສົມບູນແບບ, ແຕ່ມັນຈະຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ເຈົ້າເຫັນກໍລະນີທີ່ເຈົ້າຄວນເອີ້ນໃຊ້ "
":ref:`Node.reset_physics_interpolation<class_Node_method_reset_physics_interpolation>"
"` ຫຼື ກໍລະນີທີ່ເຈົ້າຄວນໃຊ້ interpolation ທີ່ຂຽນຂຶ້ນເອງ ເຊັ່ນໃນ "
":ref:`Camera3D<class_Camera3D>`. ເມື່ອເຈົ້າແກ້ໄຂກໍລະນີເຫຼົ່ານີ້ແລ້ວ, ເຈົ້າກໍສາມາດຕັ້ງ physics "
"tick rate ກັບຄືນສູ່ຄ່າທີ່ຕ້ອງການໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:153
msgid ""
"The other great advantage to testing at a low tick rate is you can often "
"notice other game systems that are synchronized to the physics tick and "
"creating glitches which you may want to work around. Typical examples "
"include setting animation blend values, which you may decide to set in "
"``_process()`` and interpolate manually."
msgstr ""
"ຂໍ້ດີອີກຢ່າງຂອງການທົດສອບດ້ວຍ tick rate ຕໍ່າຄື ເຈົ້າມັກຈະສັງເກດເຫັນລະບົບອື່ນໆຂອງເກມທີ່ເຮັດວຽກກົງກັບ "
"physics tick ແລະ ເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດອາການກະຕຸກ ເຊິ່ງເຈົ້າອາດຈະຕ້ອງການແກ້ໄຂ. ຕົວຢ່າງທົ່ວໄປຄືການກຳນົດຄ່"
"າ animation blend, ເຊິ່ງເຈົ້າອາດຈະຕັດສິນໃຈໄປຕັ້ງໃນ ``_process()`` ແລະ ແຊກຂໍ້ມູນດ້ວຍຕົນເອງແ"
"ທນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:160
msgid ""
"In 2D, the position of visible collision shapes shown by the :menu:`Debug > "
"Visible Collision Shapes` option **will** take physics interpolation into "
"account."
msgstr ""
"ໃນ 2D, ຕຳແໜ່ງຂອງຮູບຮ່າງການຕຳທີ່ສະແດງຜ່ານຕົວເລືອກ :menu:`Debug > Visible Collision "
"Shapes` **ຈະ** ນຳເອົາ physics interpolation ມາຄຳນວນນຳ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/using_physics_interpolation.rst:164
msgid ""
"By contrast, in 3D, the position of visible collision shapes **will not** "
"take physics interpolation into account. This means the visible collision "
"shapes can appear to move less smoothly and appear slightly in front of the "
"object's visual representation when the object is moving. This is not a bug, "
"but a consequence of how physics interpolation is implemented in 3D."
msgstr ""
"ໃນທາງກົງກັນຂ້າມ, ໃນ 3D, ຕຳແໜ່ງຂອງຮູບຮ່າງການຕຳທີ່ສະແດງໃຫ້ເຫັນ **ຈະບໍ່** ນຳເອົາ physics "
"interpolation ມາຄຳນວນນຳ. ສິ່ງນີ້ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າຮູບຮ່າງການຕຳອາດຈະເບິ່ງຄືວ່າເຄື່ອນທີ່ບໍ່ນຸ້ມນວນ ແລະ ອາດ"
"ຈະປະກົດຢູ່ທາງໜ້າຂອງວັດຖຸເລັກນ້ອຍໃນຂະນະທີ່ວັດຖຸກຳລັງເຄື່ອນທີ່. ນີ້ບໍ່ແມ່ນ bug, ແຕ່ເປັນຜົນມາຈາກວິທີການເຮັດວ"
"ຽກຂອງ physics interpolation ໃນ 3D."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:4
msgid "Advanced physics interpolation"
msgstr "ການແຊກຂໍ້ມູນຟີຊິກລະດັບສູງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:6
msgid ""
"Although the previous instructions will give satisfactory results in a lot "
"of games, in some cases you will want to go a stage further to get the best "
"possible results and the smoothest possible experience."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຄຳແນະນຳກ່ອນໜ້ານີ້ຈະໃຫ້ຜົນລັດທີ່ໜ້າພໍໃຈໃນຫຼາຍເກມ, ແຕ່ໃນບາງກໍລະນີເຈົ້າອາດຈະຕ້ອງການໄປອີກຂັ້ນໜຶ່"
"ງເພື່ອໃຫ້ໄດ້ຜົນລັດທີ່ດີທີ່ສຸດ ແລະ ປະສົບການທີ່ນຸ້ມນວນທີ່ສຸດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:11
msgid "Exceptions to automatic physics interpolation"
msgstr "ຂໍ້ຍົກເວັ້ນສຳລັບ automatic physics interpolation"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:13
msgid ""
"Even with physics interpolation active, there may be some local situations "
"where you would benefit from disabling automatic interpolation for "
"a :ref:`Node<class_Node>` (or branch of "
"the :ref:`SceneTree<class_SceneTree>`), and have the finer control of "
"performing interpolation manually."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຈະເປີດໃຊ້ physics interpolation ຢູ່, ແຕ່ອາດຈະມີບາງສະຖານະການທີ່ການປິດ "
"interpolation ອັດຕະໂນມັດສຳລັບ :ref:`Node<class_Node>` ບາງອັນຈະມີປະໂຫຍດຫຼາຍກວ່າ, ເພື່ອໃ"
"ຫ້ເຈົ້າສາມາດຄວບຄຸມການແຊກຂໍ້ມູນດ້ວຍຕົນເອງໄດ້ລະອຽດຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:18
msgid ""
"This is possible using "
"the :ref:`Node.physics_interpolation_mode<class_Node_property_physics_interpolation_mode>` "
"property which is present in all Nodes. If you for example, turn off "
"interpolation for a Node, the children will recursively also be affected (as "
"they default to inheriting the parent setting). This means you can easily "
"disable interpolation for an entire subscene."
msgstr ""
"ເຈົ້າສາມາດເຮັດສິ່ງນີ້ໄດ້ໂດຍໃຊ້ property "
":ref:`Node.physics_interpolation_mode<class_Node_property_physics_interpolation_mode>"
"` ທີ່ມີຢູ່ໃນທຸກໆໂນດ. ຕົວຢ່າງ: ຖ້າເຈົ້າປິດ interpolation ສຳລັບໂນດໃດໜຶ່ງ, ໂນດລູກຂອງມັນກໍຈະຖືກປິດໄປນ"
"ຳ (ເພາະພວກມັນຈະສືບທອດການຕັ້ງຄ່າຈາກໂນດແມ່ໂດຍເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ). ສິ່ງນີ້ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າເຈົ້າສາມາດປິດ "
"interpolation ສຳລັບທັງສາກຍ່ອຍໄດ້ຢ່າງງ່າຍດາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:26
msgid ""
"It is worth noting that, both in 2D and 3D, physics interpolation is "
"performed on the **local transform** of each instance. During rendering, "
"interpolated local transforms are passed down to children."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງທີ່ຄວນຮູ້ຄື, ທັງໃນ 2D ແລະ 3D, physics interpolation ຈະຖືກເຮັດໃນ **local "
"transform** ຂອງແຕ່ລະ instance. ໃນລະຫວ່າງການສະແດງຜົນ, local transforms ທີ່ຖືກແຊກຂໍ້ມູນແ"
"ລ້ວຈະຖືກສົ່ງຕໍ່ໄປໃຫ້ໂນດລູກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:30
msgid ""
"This means that if a parent has ``physics_interpolation_mode`` set to "
"``On``, but the child is set to ``Off``, the child will still be "
"interpolated if the parent is moving. *Only the child's local transform is "
"uninterpolated.* Controlling the on / off behavior of nodes therefore "
"requires some thought and planning."
msgstr ""
"ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າ ຖ້າໂນດແມ່ຖືກຕັ້ງ ``physics_interpolation_mode`` ເປັນ ``On``, ແຕ່ໂນດລູກຖືກຕັ້ງເ"
"ປັນ ``Off``, ໂນດລູກກໍຍັງຈະຖືກແຊກຂໍ້ມູນຢູ່ຫາກໂນດແມ່ເຄື່ອນທີ່. *ມີພຽງແຕ່ local transform ຂອງໂນດລູ"
"ກເທົ່ານັ້ນທີ່ບໍ່ໄດ້ຖືກແຊກຂໍ້ມູນ.* ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ການຄວບຄຸມການເປີດ/ປິດ ຂອງໂນດຈຶ່ງຕ້ອງມີການວາງແຜນໃຫ້ດີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:36
msgid ""
"The most common situation where you may want to perform your own "
"interpolation is Cameras."
msgstr ""
"ສະຖານະການທີ່ພົບເລື້ອຍທີ່ສຸດທີ່ເຈົ້າອາດຈະຕ້ອງການເຮັດ interpolation ດ້ວຍຕົນເອງຄື ກ້ອງ (Cameras)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:42
msgid ""
"In many cases, a :ref:`Camera3D<class_Camera3D>` can use automatic "
"interpolation just like any other node. However, for best results, "
"especially at low physics tick rates, it is recommended that you take a "
"manual approach to camera interpolation."
msgstr ""
"ໃນຫຼາຍໆກໍລະນີ, :ref:`Camera3D<class_Camera3D>` ສາມາດໃຊ້ interpolation ອັດຕະໂນມັດໄດ້ຄື"
"ກັບໂນດອື່ນໆ. ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ເພື່ອໃຫ້ໄດ້ຜົນລັດທີ່ດີທີ່ສຸດ, ໂດຍສະເພາະໃນ tick rates ທີ່ຕໍ່າ, ພວກເຮົາແນະນ"
"ຳໃຫ້ໃຊ້ວິທີການຈັດການ interpolation ຂອງກ້ອງດ້ວຍຕົນເອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:46
msgid ""
"This is because viewers are very sensitive to camera movement. For instance, "
"a Camera3D that realigns slightly every 1/10th of a second (at 10tps tick "
"rate) will often be noticeable. You can get a much smoother result by moving "
"the camera each frame in ``_process``, and following an interpolated target "
"manually."
msgstr ""
"ເພາະວ່າຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນຈະມີຄວາມອ່ອນໄຫວຕໍ່ການເຄື່ອນທີ່ຂອງກ້ອງຫຼາຍ. ຕົວຢ່າງ: Camera3D ທີ່ປັບຕຳແໜ່ງໃໝ່ເລັກນ້ອຍທຸກ"
"ໆ 1/10 ວິນາທີ (ທີ່ 10tps) ມັກຈະສັງເກດເຫັນໄດ້ຊັດເຈນ. ເຈົ້າສາມາດເຮັດໃຫ້ມັນນຸ້ມນວນຂຶ້ນໄດ້ໂດຍການຍ້າຍກ້"
"ອງໃນທຸກໆເຟຣມໃນ ``_process``, ແລະ ໃຫ້ມັນຕິດຕາມເປົ້າໝາຍທີ່ຖືກແຊກຂໍ້ມູນແລ້ວດ້ວຍຕົນເອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:52
msgid "Manual camera interpolation"
msgstr "ການແຊກຂໍ້ມູນກ້ອງດ້ວຍຕົນເອງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:55
msgid "Ensure the camera is using global coordinate space"
msgstr "ໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າກ້ອງໃຊ້ພື້ນທີ່ພິກັດແບບ global (global coordinate space)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:57
msgid ""
"The very first step when performing manual camera interpolation is to make "
"sure the Camera3D transform is specified in *global space* rather than "
"inheriting the transform of a moving parent. This is because feedback can "
"occur between the movement of a parent node of a Camera3D and the movement "
"of the camera Node itself, which can mess up the interpolation."
msgstr ""
"ຂັ້ນຕອນທຳອິດໃນການເຮັດ interpolation ຂອງກ້ອງດ້ວຍຕົນເອງຄື ຕ້ອງໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າ transform ຂອງ "
"Camera3D ຖືກກຳນົດໃນ *global space* ແທນທີ່ຈະສືບທອດມາຈາກໂນດແມ່ທີ່ກຳລັງເຄື່ອນທີ່. ເພາະວ່າການເຄື່"
"ອນທີ່ຂອງໂນດແມ່ ແລະ ການເຄື່ອນທີ່ຂອງໂນດກ້ອງເອງອາດຈະສົ່ງຜົນກະທົບຕໍ່ກັນ ແລະ ເຮັດໃຫ້ interpolation "
"ຜິດພາດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:63
msgid "There are two ways of doing this:"
msgstr "ມີສອງວິທີໃນການເຮັດສິ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:65
msgid ""
"Move the Camera3D so it is independent on its own branch, rather than being "
"a child of a moving object."
msgstr ""
"ຍ້າຍ Camera3D ໃຫ້ຢູ່ແຍກເປັນອິດສະຫຼະໃນ branch ຂອງມັນເອງ, ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນໂນດລູກຂອງວັດຖຸທີ່ກຳລັງເຄື່ອນ"
"ທີ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:69
msgid ""
"Call :ref:`Node3D.top_level<class_Node3D_property_top_level>` and set this "
"to ``true``, which will make the Camera ignore the transform of its parent."
msgstr ""
"ເອີ້ນໃຊ້ :ref:`Node3D.top_level<class_Node3D_property_top_level>` ແລະ ຕັ້ງເປັນ "
"``true``, ເຊິ່ງຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ກ້ອງລະເລີຍ transform ຂອງໂນດແມ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:72
msgid "Typical example"
msgstr "ຕົວຢ່າງທົ່ວໄປ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:74
msgid ""
"A typical example of a custom approach is to use the ``look_at`` function in "
"the Camera3D every frame in ``_process()`` to look at a target node (such as "
"the player)."
msgstr ""
"ຕົວຢ່າງທົ່ວໄປຄືການໃຊ້ຟັງຊັນ ``look_at`` ໃນ Camera3D ທຸກໆເຟຣມໃນ ``_process()`` ເພື່ອເບິ່ງໄປ"
"ທີ່ໂນດເປົ້າໝາຍ (ເຊັ່ນ: ຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:77
msgid ""
"But there is a problem. If we use the traditional ``get_global_transform()`` "
"on a Camera3D \"target\" node, this transform will only focus the Camera3D "
"on the target *at the current physics tick*. This is *not* what we want, as "
"the camera will jump about on each physics tick as the target moves. Even "
"though the camera may be updated each frame, this does not help give smooth "
"motion if the *target* is only changing each physics tick."
msgstr ""
"ແຕ່ມີບັນຫາຢູ່ຢ່າງໜຶ່ງ. ຖ້າພວກເຮົາໃຊ້ ``get_global_transform()`` ແບບດັ້ງເດີມກັບ node \"ເປົ້າໝາ"
"ຍ\" ຂອງ Camera3D, ການແປງຄ່າ (transform) ນີ້ຈະໂຟກັດ Camera3D ໄປທີ່ເປົ້າໝາຍ *ໃນຊ່ວງ "
"physics tick ປັດຈຸບັນ* ເທົ່ານັ້ນ. ນີ້ *ບໍ່ແມ່ນ* ສິ່ງທີ່ພວກເຮົາຕ້ອງການ, ເພາະກ້ອງຈະມີການກະຕຸກໃນແຕ່ລະ "
"physics tick ເມື່ອເປົ້າໝາຍເຄື່ອນທີ່. ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າກ້ອງຈະຖືກອັບເດດໃນທຸກໆເຟຣມ (frame), ແຕ່ມັນກໍບໍ່ໄດ້ຊ່"
"ວຍໃຫ້ການເຄື່ອນໄຫວລຽບງ່າຍ ຖ້າຫາກວ່າ *ເປົ້າໝາຍ* ປ່ຽນແປງສະເພາະໃນແຕ່ລະ physics tick."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:85
msgid "get_global_transform_interpolated()"
msgstr "get_global_transform_interpolated()"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:87
msgid ""
"What we really want to focus the camera on, is not the position of the "
"target on the physics tick, but the *interpolated* position, i.e. the "
"position at which the target will be rendered."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງທີ່ເຮົາຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ກ້ອງໂຟກັດແທ້ໆ ບໍ່ແມ່ນຕຳແໜ່ງຂອງເປົ້າໝາຍໃນ physics tick, ແຕ່ເປັນຕຳແໜ່ງທີ່ *ຖືກແຊ"
"ກຂໍ້ມູນ (interpolated)* ແລ້ວ, ເຊິ່ງກໍຄືຕຳແໜ່ງທີ່ເປົ້າໝາຍຈະຖືກສະແດງຜົນແທ້ໆ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:91
msgid ""
"We can do this using "
"the :ref:`Node3D.get_global_transform_interpolated<class_Node3D_method_get_global_transform_interpolated>` "
"function. This acts exactly like "
"getting :ref:`Node3D.global_transform<class_Node3D_property_global_transform>` "
"but it gives you the *interpolated* transform (during a ``_process()`` call)."
msgstr ""
"ເຮົາສາມາດເຮັດສິ່ງນີ້ໄດ້ໂດຍໃຊ້ຟັງຊັນ "
":ref:`Node3D.get_global_transform_interpolated<class_Node3D_method_get_global_transform_interpolated>"
"`. ມັນເຮັດວຽກຄືກັນກັບການດຶງຄ່າ "
":ref:`Node3D.global_transform<class_Node3D_property_global_transform>` ແຕ່ມັນຈະ"
"ໃຫ້ຄ່າ transform ທີ່ *ຖືກແຊກຂໍ້ມູນ* ແລ້ວ (ເມື່ອເອີ້ນໃຊ້ໃນ ``_process()``)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:95
msgid ""
"``get_global_transform_interpolated()`` should only be used once or twice "
"for special cases such as cameras. It should **not** be used all over the "
"place in your code (both for performance reasons, and to give correct "
"gameplay)."
msgstr ""
"``get_global_transform_interpolated()`` ຄວນຖືກໃຊ້ພຽງແຕ່ຄັ້ງ ຫຼື ສອງຄັ້ງໃນກໍລະນີພິເສດ ເຊັ່ນ "
"ກ້ອງ. **ບໍ່ຄວນ** ໃຊ້ມັນໄປທົ່ວໃນ code ຂອງເຈົ້າ (ທັງຍ້ອນເຫດຜົນດ້ານປະສິດທິພາບ ແລະ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ການຫຼິ້ນເກມ"
"ຖືກຕ້ອງ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:100
msgid ""
"Aside from exceptions like the camera, in most cases, your game logic should "
"be in ``_physics_process()``. In game logic you should be calling "
"``get_global_transform()`` or ``get_transform()``, which will give the "
"current physics transform (in global or local space respectively), which is "
"usually what you will want for gameplay code."
msgstr ""
"ນອກຈາກຂໍ້ຍົກເວັ້ນຄືກ້ອງແລ້ວ, ໃນກໍລະນີສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ logic ຂອງເກມຄວນຢູ່ໃນ ``_physics_process()``. "
"ໃນ logic ເກມ ເຈົ້າຄວນເອີ້ນໃຊ້ ``get_global_transform()`` ຫຼື ``get_transform()`` ເພື່ອ"
"ໃຫ້ໄດ້ transform ຂອງຟີຊິກປັດຈຸບັນ ເຊິ່ງເປັນສິ່ງທີ່ຄວນໃຊ້ສຳລັບ code ຂອງເກມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:107
msgid "Example manual camera script"
msgstr "ຕົວຢ່າງ script ຂອງກ້ອງແບບ manual"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:109
msgid ""
"Here is an example of a simple fixed camera which follows an interpolated "
"target:"
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ແມ່ນຕົວຢ່າງຂອງກ້ອງທີ່ຢູ່ກັບທີ່ແບບງ່າຍໆ ເຊິ່ງຕິດຕາມເປົ້າໝາຍທີ່ຖືກແຊກຂໍ້ມູນແລ້ວ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:141
msgid "Mouse look"
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ເມົາສ໌ເບິ່ງ (Mouse look)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:143
msgid ""
"Mouse look is a very common way of controlling cameras. But there is a "
"problem. Unlike keyboard input which can be sampled periodically on the "
"physics tick, mouse move events can come in continuously. The camera will be "
"expected to react and follow these mouse movements on the next frame, rather "
"than waiting until the next physics tick."
msgstr ""
"Mouse look ແມ່ນວິທີທີ່ພົບເລື້ອຍຫຼາຍໃນການຄວບຄຸມກ້ອງ. ແຕ່ມັນມີບັນຫາ. ຕ່າງຈາກ input ຂອງຄີບອດທີ່ສາມາ"
"ດກວດສອບເປັນໄລຍະໆໃນ physics tick ໄດ້, ເຫດການການເຄື່ອນທີ່ຂອງເມົາສ໌ (mouse move events) "
"ສາມາດສົ່ງເຂົ້າມາໄດ້ຕະຫຼອດເວລາ. ກ້ອງຄວນຈະຕອບສະໜອງ ແລະ ຕິດຕາມການເຄື່ອນທີ່ຂອງເມົາສ໌ໃນເຟຣມຖັດໄປທັ"
"ນທີ, ແທນທີ່ຈະຕ້ອງລໍຖ້າຈົນກວ່າຈະເຖິງ physics tick ຖັດໄປ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:149
msgid ""
"In this situation, it can be better to disable physics interpolation for the "
"camera node "
"(using :ref:`Node.physics_interpolation_mode<class_Node_property_physics_interpolation_mode>`) "
"and directly apply the mouse input to the camera rotation, rather than apply "
"it in ``_physics_process``."
msgstr ""
"ໃນສະຖານະການນີ້, ມັນອາດຈະດີກວ່າທີ່ຈະປິດການນຳໃຊ້ physics interpolation ສຳລັບ node ກ້ອງຖ່າຍຮູ"
"ບ (ໂດຍໃຊ້ "
":ref:`Node.physics_interpolation_mode<class_Node_property_physics_interpolation_mode>"
"`) ແລະ ນຳໃຊ້ input ຈາກເມົ້າໃສ່ການໝູນຂອງກ້ອງໂດຍກົງ, ແທນທີ່ຈະນຳໃຊ້ມັນໃນ "
"``_physics_process``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:154
msgid ""
"Sometimes, especially with cameras, you will want to use a combination of "
"interpolation and non-interpolation:"
msgstr ""
"ບາງຄັ້ງ, ໂດຍສະເພາະກັບກ້ອງຖ່າຍຮູບ, ເຈົ້າອາດຈະຕ້ອງການໃຊ້ການປະສົມປະສານລະຫວ່າງການເຮັດ "
"interpolation ແລະ ບໍ່ເຮັດ interpolation:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:157
msgid ""
"A first person camera may position the camera at a player location (perhaps "
"using :ref:`Node3D.get_global_transform_interpolated<class_Node3D_method_get_global_transform_interpolated>`), "
"but control the Camera rotation from mouse look *without* interpolation."
msgstr ""
"ກ້ອງຖ່າຍຮູບແບບບຸກຄົນທີໜຶ່ງອາດຈະກຳນົດຕຳແໜ່ງກ້ອງໄວ້ທີ່ຕຳແໜ່ງຂອງຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນ (ອາດຈະໃຊ້ "
":ref:`Node3D.get_global_transform_interpolated<class_Node3D_method_get_global_transform_interpolated>"
"`), ແຕ່ຄວບຄຸມການໝູນຂອງກ້ອງຈາກການເບິ່ງດ້ວຍເມົ້າ *ໂດຍບໍ່ມີ* interpolation."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:160
msgid ""
"A third person camera may similarly determine the look at (target location) "
"of the camera "
"using :ref:`Node3D.get_global_transform_interpolated<class_Node3D_method_get_global_transform_interpolated>`, "
"but position the camera using mouse look *without* interpolation."
msgstr ""
"ກ້ອງຖ່າຍຮູບແບບບຸກຄົນທີສາມອາດຈະກຳນົດການເບິ່ງໄປທີ່ (ຕຳແໜ່ງເປົ້າໝາຍ) ຂອງກ້ອງໃນລັກສະນະດຽວກັນໂດຍໃຊ້ "
":ref:`Node3D.get_global_transform_interpolated<class_Node3D_method_get_global_transform_interpolated>"
"`, ແຕ່ກຳນົດຕຳແໜ່ງກ້ອງໂດຍໃຊ້ການເບິ່ງດ້ວຍເມົ້າ *ໂດຍບໍ່ມີ* interpolation."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:164
msgid ""
"There are many permutations and variations of camera types, but it should be "
"clear that in many cases, disabling automatic physics interpolation and "
"handling this yourself can give a better result."
msgstr ""
"ມີຮູບແບບ ແລະ ການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງປະເພດກ້ອງຖ່າຍຮູບຫຼາຍຢ່າງ, ແຕ່ມັນຄວນຈະຈະແຈ້ງວ່າໃນຫຼາຍໆກໍລະນີ, ການປິດ"
"ການນຳໃຊ້ automatic physics interpolation ແລະ ຈັດການດ້ວຍຕົວເຈົ້າເອງສາມາດໃຫ້ຜົນລັບທີ່ດີກວ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:169
msgid "Disabling interpolation on other nodes"
msgstr "ການປິດການນຳໃຊ້ interpolation ໃນ node ອື່ນໆ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:171
msgid ""
"Although cameras are the most common example, there are a number of cases "
"when you may wish other nodes to control their own interpolation, or be non-"
"interpolated. Consider for example, a player in a top view game whose "
"rotation is controlled by mouse look. Disabling physics rotation allows the "
"player rotation to match the mouse in real-time."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າກ້ອງຖ່າຍຮູບຈະເປັນຕົວຢ່າງທີ່ພົບເລື້ອຍທີ່ສຸດ, ແຕ່ກໍມີຫຼາຍກໍລະນີທີ່ເຈົ້າອາດຈະຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ node ອື່ນໆຄວ"
"ບຄຸມ interpolation ຂອງພວກມັນເອງ, ຫຼື ບໍ່ໃຫ້ມີການເຮັດ interpolation. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ, ຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນໃນເກມ"
"ມຸມເບິ່ງຈາກດ້ານເທິງ (top view) ທີ່ການໝູນຖືກຄວບຄຸມໂດຍການເບິ່ງດ້ວຍເມົ້າ. ການປິດການນຳໃຊ້ physics "
"rotation ຈະຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ການໝູນຂອງຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນກົງກັບເມົ້າແບບ real-time."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:181
msgid ""
"Although most visual Nodes follow the single Node single visual instance "
"paradigm, MultiMeshes can control several instances from the same Node. "
"Therefore, they have some extra functions for controlling interpolation "
"functionality on a *per-instance* basis. You should explore these functions "
"if you are using interpolated MultiMeshes."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າ Node ທີ່ສະແດງຜົນສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ຈະໃຊ້ຮູບແບບ Node ດຽວຕໍ່ instance ດຽວ, ແຕ່ MultiMeshes "
"ສາມາດຄວບຄຸມໄດ້ຫຼາຍ instances ຈາກ Node ດຽວກັນ. ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ພວກມັນຈຶ່ງມີຟັງຊັນເພີ່ມເຕີມສຳລັບການຄວບຄຸ"
"ມການເຮັດວຽກຂອງ interpolation ໃນຮູບແບບ *ແຕ່ລະ instance*. ເເຈົ້າຄວນສຶກສາຟັງຊັນເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຖ້າເຈົ້າ"
"ກຳລັງໃຊ້ MultiMeshes ທີ່ມີ interpolation."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:187
msgid ":ref:`MultiMesh.reset_instance_physics_interpolation<class_MultiMesh_method_reset_instance_physics_interpolation>`"
msgstr ""
":ref:`MultiMesh.reset_instance_physics_interpolation<class_MultiMesh_method_reset_instance_physics_interpolation>"
"`"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:188
msgid ":ref:`MultiMesh.set_buffer_interpolated<class_MultiMesh_method_set_buffer_interpolated>`"
msgstr ""
":ref:`MultiMesh.set_buffer_interpolated<class_MultiMesh_method_set_buffer_interpolated>"
"`"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/advanced_physics_interpolation.rst:190
msgid ""
"Full details are in the :ref:`MultiMesh<class_MultiMesh>` documentation."
msgstr "ລາຍລະອຽດທັງໝົດມີຢູ່ໃນເອກະສານຂອງ :ref:`MultiMesh<class_MultiMesh>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/2d_and_3d_physics_interpolation.rst:4
msgid "2D and 3D physics interpolation"
msgstr "ການເຮັດ Physics interpolation ແບບ 2D ແລະ 3D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/2d_and_3d_physics_interpolation.rst:6
msgid ""
"Generally 2D and 3D physics interpolation work in very similar ways. "
"However, there are a few differences, which will be described here."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປແລ້ວ physics interpolation ແບບ 2D ແລະ 3D ຈະເຮັດວຽກໃນລັກສະນະທີ່ຄ້າຍຄືກັນຫຼາຍ. ຢ່າ"
"ງໃດກໍຕາມ, ຍັງມີບາງຈຸດທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນ, ເຊິ່ງຈະຖືກອະທິບາຍຢູ່ທີ່ນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/2d_and_3d_physics_interpolation.rst:10
msgid "2D Particles"
msgstr "Particles ແບບ 2D"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/2d_and_3d_physics_interpolation.rst:12
msgid ""
"Currently only ``CPUParticles2D`` are supported for physics interpolation in "
"2D. It is recommended to use a physics tick rate of at least 20-30 ticks per "
"second to keep particles looking fluid."
msgstr ""
"ໃນປັດຈຸບັນມີພຽງແຕ່ ``CPUParticles2D`` ເທົ່ານັ້ນທີ່ຮອງຮັບ physics interpolation ໃນ 2D. ແນະ"
"ນຳໃຫ້ໃຊ້ physics tick rate ຢ່າງໜ້ອຍ 20-30 ticks ຕໍ່ວິນາທີ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ particles ເບິ່ງມີຄວາມຕໍ່ເນື່"
"ອງ (fluid)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/2d_and_3d_physics_interpolation.rst:16
msgid ""
"``Particles2D`` (GPU particles) are not yet interpolated, so for now it is "
"recommended to convert to ``CPUParticles2D`` (but keep a backup of your "
"``Particles2D`` in case we get these working)."
msgstr ""
"``Particles2D`` (GPU particles) ຍັງບໍ່ທັນມີການເຮັດ interpolation, ດັ່ງນັ້ນໃນເວລານີ້ຈຶ່ງແນະນ"
"ຳໃຫ້ປ່ຽນໄປໃຊ້ ``CPUParticles2D`` (ແຕ່ໃຫ້ເກັບສຳເນົາ ``Particles2D`` ຂອງເຈົ້າໄວ້ ໃນກໍລະນີທີ່ພ"
"ວກເຮົາເຮັດໃຫ້ມັນໃຊ້ງານໄດ້ໃນອະນາຄົດ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/2d_and_3d_physics_interpolation.rst:21
msgid "Other"
msgstr "ອື່ນໆ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/2d_and_3d_physics_interpolation.rst:23
msgid ""
"``get_global_transform_interpolated()`` is currently only available for 3D."
msgstr ""
"ໃນປັດຈຸບັນ ``get_global_transform_interpolated()`` ສາມາດໃຊ້ໄດ້ສະເພາະ 3D ເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/2d_and_3d_physics_interpolation.rst:24
msgid "``MultiMeshes`` are supported in both 2D and 3D."
msgstr "``MultiMeshes`` ຮອງຮັບທັງໃນ 2D ແລະ 3D."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/interpolation/2d_and_3d_physics_interpolation.rst:25
msgid ""
"Physics interpolation in 2D is implemented on the server side, which means "
"it's effective on physics bodies created using :ref:`low-level servers "
"<doc_using_servers>`. In contrast, physics interpolation in 3D is "
"implemented on the scene side. This means it does not affect physics bodies "
"created using servers. These must be interpolated manually instead. See the "
"`pull request description <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/"
"104269>`__ for the rationale on this design decision."
msgstr ""
"Physics interpolation ໃນ 2D ແມ່ນຖືກຕິດຕັ້ງຢູ່ຝັ່ງ server, ເຊິ່ງໝາຍຄວາມວ່າມັນມີຜົນກັບ physics "
"bodies ທີ່ສ້າງຂຶ້ນໂດຍໃຊ້ :ref:`low-level servers <doc_using_servers>`. ໃນທາງກົງກັນຂ້າ"
"ມ, physics interpolation ໃນ 3D ແມ່ນຖືກຕິດຕັ້ງຢູ່ຝັ່ງ scene. ນີ້ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າມັນຈະບໍ່ມີຜົນກັບ "
"physics bodies ທີ່ສ້າງຂຶ້ນໂດຍໃຊ້ servers. ສິ່ງເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຕ້ອງໄດ້ຮັບການເຮັດ interpolation ດ້ວຍຕົວເອ"
"ງແທນ. ເບິ່ງ `ລາຍລະອຽດຂອງ pull request <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/"
"pull/104269>`__ ສຳລັບເຫດຜົນໃນການຕັດສິນໃຈອອກແບບນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:4
msgid "Troubleshooting physics issues"
msgstr "ການແກ້ໄຂບັນຫາທາງດ້ານ physics"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:6
msgid ""
"When working with a physics engine, you may encounter unexpected results."
msgstr "ເມື່ອເຮັດວຽກກັບ physics engine, ເຈົ້າອາດຈະພົບກັບຜົນລັບທີ່ບໍ່ຄາດຄິດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:8
msgid ""
"While many of these issues can be resolved through configuration, some of "
"them are the result of engine bugs. For known issues related to the physics "
"engine, see `open physics-related issues on GitHub <https://github.com/"
"godotengine/godot/issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3Atopic%3Aphysics>`__. "
"Looking through `closed issues <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues?"
"q=+is%3Aclosed+is%3Aissue+label%3Atopic%3Aphysics>`__ can also help answer "
"questions related to physics engine behavior."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຫຼາຍໆບັນຫາເຫຼົ່ານີ້ສາມາດແກ້ໄຂໄດ້ຜ່ານການຕັ້ງຄ່າ, ແຕ່ບາງຢ່າງກໍເປັນຜົນມາຈາກ bug ຂອງ "
"engine. ສຳລັບບັນຫາທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັບ physics engine ທີ່ຖືກພົບແລ້ວ, ໃຫ້ເບິ່ງທີ່ `open physics-"
"related issues on GitHub <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/"
"issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3Atopic%3Aphysics>`__. ການຄົ້ນຫາໃນ `closed "
"issues <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/"
"issues?q=+is%3Aclosed+is%3Aissue+label%3Atopic%3Aphysics>`__ ສາມາດຊ່ວຍຕອບຄຳຖາມ"
"ກ່ຽວກັບພຶດຕິກຳຂອງ physics engine ໄດ້ເຊັ່ນກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:17
msgid "Objects are passing through each other at high speeds"
msgstr "ວັດຖຸທະລຸຜ່ານກັນເມື່ອມີຄວາມໄວສູງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:19
msgid ""
"This is known as *tunneling*. Enabling **Continuous CD** (Continuous "
"Collision Detection) in the RigidBody properties can sometimes resolve this "
"issue. If this does not help, there are other solutions you can try:"
msgstr ""
"ບັນຫານີ້ເອີ້ນວ່າ *tunneling*. ການເປີດໃຊ້ **Continuous CD** (Continuous Collision "
"Detection) ໃນຄຸນສົມບັດຂອງ RigidBody ບາງຄັ້ງສາມາດແກ້ໄຂບັນຫານີ້ໄດ້. ຖ້າມັນບໍ່ຊ່ວຍ, ຍັງມີວິທີອື່ນທີ່ເຈົ້າ"
"ສາມາດທົດລອງໄດ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:23
msgid ""
"Make your static collision shapes thicker. For example, if you have a thin "
"floor that the player can't get below in some way, you can make the collider "
"thicker than the floor's visual representation."
msgstr ""
"ເຮັດໃຫ້ static collision shapes ຂອງເຈົ້າໜາຂຶ້ນ. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ, ຖ້າເຈົ້າມີພື້ນທີ່ບາງໆ ທີ່ຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນບໍ່ສາມາດລ"
"ອດລົງໄປທາງລຸ່ມໄດ້, ເຈົ້າສາມາດເຮັດໃຫ້ collider ໜາກວ່າຮູບຮ່າງທີ່ເບິ່ງເຫັນຂອງພື້ນໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:26
msgid ""
"Modify your fast-moving object's collision shape depending on its movement "
"speed. The faster the object moves, the larger the collision shape should "
"extend outside of the object to ensure it can collide with thin walls more "
"reliably."
msgstr ""
"ປັບປ່ຽນ collision shape ຂອງວັດຖຸທີ່ເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄວຕາມຄວາມໄວຂອງມັນ. ຍິ່ງວັດຖຸເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄວເທົ່າໃດ, "
"collision shape ກໍຄວນຈະຂະຫຍາຍອອກໄປນອກວັດຖຸຫຼາຍເທົ່ານັ້ນ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າມັນຈະຕຳກັບຝາບາງໆ ໄດ້ຢ່"
"າງຖືກຕ້ອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:30
msgid ""
"Increase :ref:`Physics Ticks per "
"Second<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/common/"
"physics_ticks_per_second>` in the advanced Project Settings. While this has "
"other benefits (such as more stable simulation and reduced input lag), this "
"increases CPU utilization and may not be viable for mobile/web platforms. "
"Multipliers of the default value of ``60`` (such as ``120``, ``180`` or "
"``240``) should be preferred for a smooth appearance on most displays."
msgstr ""
"ເພີ່ມ :ref:`Physics Ticks per Second<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/"
"common/physics_ticks_per_second>` ໃນການຕັ້ງຄ່າ Project Settings ຂັ້ນສູງ. ເຖິງວ່າມັນຈະມີ"
"ປະໂຫຍດອື່ນໆ (ເຊັ່ນ: ການຈຳລອງທີ່ໝັ້ນຄົງຂຶ້ນ ແລະ ຫຼຸດ input lag), ແຕ່ວິທີນີ້ຈະເພີ່ມການໃຊ້ CPU ແລະ ອາ"
"ດຈະບໍ່ເໝາະສົມສຳລັບ platform ມືຖື ຫຼື ເວັບ. ຄວນເລືອກໃຊ້ຕົວຄູນຂອງຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ ``60`` (ເຊັ່ນ "
"``120``, ``180`` ຫຼື ``240``) ເພື່ອໃຫ້ການສະແດງຜົນເບິ່ງມີຄວາມຕໍ່ເນື່ອງໃນໜ້າຈໍສ່ວນໃຫຍ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:38
msgid "Stacked objects are unstable and wobbly"
msgstr "ວັດຖຸທີ່ວາງຊ້ອນກັນມີຄວາມບໍ່ໝັ້ນຄົງ ແລະ ສັ່ນ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:40
msgid ""
"Despite seeming like a simple problem, stable RigidBody simulation with "
"stacked objects is difficult to implement in a physics engine. This is "
"caused by integrating forces going against each other. The more stacked "
"objects are present, the stronger the forces will be against each other. "
"This eventually causes the simulation to become wobbly, making the objects "
"unable to rest on top of each other without moving."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງວ່າຈະເບິ່ງຄືເປັນບັນຫາງ່າຍໆ, ແຕ່ການຈຳລອງ RigidBody ໃຫ້ໝັ້ນຄົງເມື່ອວາງວັດຖຸຊ້ອນກັນນັ້ນແມ່ນເຮັດໄດ້ຍາ"
"ກໃນ physics engine. ນີ້ເກີດຈາກການລວມແຮງ (integrating forces) ທີ່ຕ້ານກັນ. ຍິ່ງມີວັດຖຸຊ້ອນກັນ"
"ຫຼາຍເທົ່າໃດ, ແຮງທີ່ຕ້ານກັນກໍຈະຍິ່ງແຮງຂຶ້ນ. ໃນທີ່ສຸດມັນຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ການຈຳລອງສັ່ນ ແລະ ເຮັດໃຫ້ວັດຖຸບໍ່ສາມາດວາງ"
"ຊ້ອນກັນໄດ້ໂດຍບໍ່ເຄື່ອນທີ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:47
msgid ""
"Increasing the physics simulation rate can help alleviate this issue. To do "
"so, increase :ref:`Physics Ticks per "
"Second<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/common/"
"physics_ticks_per_second>` in the advanced Project Settings. Note that "
"increases CPU utilization and may not be viable for mobile/web platforms. "
"Multipliers of the default value of ``60`` (such as ``120``, ``180`` or "
"``240``) should be preferred for a smooth appearance on most displays."
msgstr ""
"ການເພີ່ມອັດຕາການຈຳລອງ physics ສາມາດຊ່ວຍຫຼຸດຜ່ອນບັນຫານີ້ໄດ້. ໂດຍການເພີ່ມ :ref:`Physics "
"Ticks per Second<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/common/"
"physics_ticks_per_second>` ໃນການຕັ້ງຄ່າ Project Settings ຂັ້ນສູງ. ສັງເກດວ່າວິທີນີ້ຈະເພີ່ມກາ"
"ນໃຊ້ CPU ແລະ ອາດຈະບໍ່ເໝາະສົມສຳລັບ platform ມືຖື ຫຼື ເວັບ. ຄວນເລືອກໃຊ້ຕົວຄູນຂອງຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ "
"``60`` (ເຊັ່ນ ``120``, ``180`` ຫຼື ``240``) ເພື່ອໃຫ້ການສະແດງຜົນເບິ່ງມີຄວາມຕໍ່ເນື່ອງໃນໜ້າຈໍສ່ວນໃ"
"ຫຍ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:54
msgid ""
"In 3D, switching the physics engine from the default GodotPhysics to Jolt "
"can also improve stability. See :ref:`doc_using_jolt_physics` for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"ໃນ 3D, ການປ່ຽນ physics engine ຈາກ GodotPhysics ທີ່ເປັນຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນໄປເປັນ Jolt ກໍສາມາດປັບປຸ"
"ງຄວາມໝັ້ນຄົງໄດ້. ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_using_jolt_physics` ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:58
msgid "Scaled physics bodies or collision shapes do not collide correctly"
msgstr ""
"Physics bodies ຫຼື collision shapes ທີ່ຖືກປັບຂະໜາດ (scale) ຕຳກັນບໍ່ຖືກຕ້ອງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:60
msgid ""
"Godot does not currently support scaling of physics bodies or collision "
"shapes. As a workaround, change the collision shape's extents instead of "
"changing its scale. If you want the visual representation's scale to change "
"as well, change the scale of the underlying visual representation (Sprite2D, "
"MeshInstance3D, …) and change the collision shape's extents separately. Make "
"sure the collision shape is not a child of the visual representation in this "
"case."
msgstr ""
"ປັດຈຸບັນ Godot ຍັງບໍ່ຮອງຮັບການປັບ scale ຂອງ physics bodies ຫຼື collision shapes. ເພື່ອແກ້ໄ"
"ຂ, ໃຫ້ປ່ຽນຄ່າ extents ຂອງ collision shape ແທນການປ່ຽນ scale. ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ຂະໜາດທີ່ເບິ່"
"ງເຫັນປ່ຽນນຳ, ໃຫ້ປ່ຽນ scale ຂອງ node ທີ່ສະແດງຜົນ (ເຊັ່ນ Sprite2D, MeshInstance3D, …) ແລ"
"ະ ປ່ຽນ extents ຂອງ collision shape ແຍກຕ່າງຫາກ. ໃນກໍລະນີນີ້, ໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າ collision "
"shape ບໍ່ໄດ້ເປັນ child ຂອງ node ທີ່ສະແດງຜົນນັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:67
msgid ""
"Since resources are shared by default, you'll have to make the collision "
"shape resource unique if you don't want the change to be applied to all "
"nodes using the same collision shape resource in the scene. This can be done "
"in two ways:"
msgstr ""
"ເນື່ອງຈາກ resource ຖືກໃຊ້ຮ່ວມກັນໂດຍຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງເຮັດໃຫ້ collision shape resource ນັ້ນ"
"ເປັນ unique ຖ້າເຈົ້າບໍ່ຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ການປ່ຽນແປງມີຜົນກັບ node ທັງໝົດທີ່ໃຊ້ resource ດຽວກັນໃນ scene. "
"ເຊິ່ງສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ສອງວິທີ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:71
msgid ""
"In the editor, by clicking :menu:`Make Unique` in the CollisionShape "
"resource dropdown in the inspector, then changing its size."
msgstr ""
"ໃນ editor, ໂດຍການຄລິກທີ່ :menu:`Make Unique` ໃນລາຍການເລືອກ CollisionShape "
"resource ຢູ່ໃນ inspector, ແລ້ວຈຶ່ງປ່ຽນຂະໜາດຂອງມັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:73
msgid ""
"In a script, by calling ``duplicate()`` in a script on the collision shape "
"resource *before* changing its size."
msgstr ""
"ໃນ script, ໂດຍການເອີ້ນໃຊ້ ``duplicate()`` ໃສ່ collision shape resource *ກ່ອນ* ທີ່ຈະປ່"
"ຽນຂະໜາດຂອງມັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:77
msgid "Thin objects are wobbly when resting on the floor"
msgstr "ວັດຖຸບາງໆ ມີການສັ່ນເມື່ອວາງຢູ່ເທິງພື້ນ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:79
msgid "This can be due to one of two causes:"
msgstr "ສິ່ງນີ້ອາດຈະເກີດຈາກສອງສາເຫດ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:81
msgid "The floor's collision shape is too thin."
msgstr "Collision shape ຂອງພື້ນບາງເກີນໄປ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:82
msgid "The RigidBody's collision shape is too thin."
msgstr "Collision shape ຂອງ RigidBody ບາງເກີນໄປ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:84
msgid ""
"In the first case, this can be alleviated by making the floor's collision "
"shape thicker. For example, if you have a thin floor that the player can't "
"get below in some way, you can make the collider thicker than the floor's "
"visual representation."
msgstr ""
"ໃນກໍລະນີທຳອິດ, ສາມາດແກ້ໄຂໄດ້ໂດຍການເຮັດໃຫ້ collision shape ຂອງພື້ນໜາຂຶ້ນ. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ, ຖ້າເຈົ້າ"
"ມີພື້ນບາງໆ ທີ່ຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນບໍ່ສາມາດລອດລົງໄປທາງລຸ່ມໄດ້, ເຈົ້າສາມາດເຮັດໃຫ້ collider ໜາກວ່າຮູບຮ່າງທີ່ເບິ່ງເຫັນຂອງ"
"ພື້ນໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:89
msgid ""
"In the second case, this can usually only be resolved by increasing the "
"physics simulation rate (as making the shape thicker would cause a "
"disconnect between the RigidBody's visual representation and its collision)."
msgstr ""
"ໃນກໍລະນີທີສອງ, ປົກກະຕິແລ້ວຈະແກ້ໄຂໄດ້ພຽງແຕ່ການເພີ່ມອັດຕາການຈຳລອງ physics ເທົ່ານັ້ນ (ເພາະວ່າການເ"
"ຮັດໃຫ້ shape ໜາຂຶ້ນຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ຮູບຮ່າງທີ່ເບິ່ງເຫັນຂອງ RigidBody ກັບ collider ຂອງມັນບໍ່ກົງກັນ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:93
msgid ""
"In both cases, increasing the physics simulation rate can also help "
"alleviate this issue. To do so, increase :ref:`Physics Ticks per "
"Second<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/common/"
"physics_ticks_per_second>` in the advanced Project Settings. Note that this "
"increases CPU utilization and may not be viable for mobile/web platforms. "
"Multipliers of the default value of ``60`` (such as ``120``, ``180`` or "
"``240``) should be preferred for a smooth appearance on most displays."
msgstr ""
"ໃນທັງສອງກໍລະນີ, ການເພີ່ມອັດຕາການຈຳລອງ physics ກໍສາມາດຊ່ວຍຫຼຸດຜ່ອນບັນຫານີ້ໄດ້. ໂດຍການເພີ່ມ "
":ref:`Physics Ticks per Second<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/common/"
"physics_ticks_per_second>` ໃນການຕັ້ງຄ່າ Project Settings ຂັ້ນສູງ. ສັງເກດວ່າວິທີນີ້ຈະເພີ່ມກາ"
"ນໃຊ້ CPU ແລະ ອາດຈະບໍ່ເໝາະສົມສຳລັບ platform ມືຖື ຫຼື ເວັບ. ຄວນເລືອກໃຊ້ຕົວຄູນຂອງຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ "
"``60`` (ເຊັ່ນ ``120``, ``180`` ຫຼື ``240``) ເພື່ອໃຫ້ການສະແດງຜົນເບິ່ງມີຄວາມຕໍ່ເນື່ອງໃນໜ້າຈໍສ່ວນໃ"
"ຫຍ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:103
msgid "Cylinder collision shapes are unstable"
msgstr "Collision shapes ຮູບຊົງກະບອກ (Cylinder) ບໍ່ໝັ້ນຄົງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:105
msgid ""
"Switching the physics engine from the default GodotPhysics to Jolt should "
"make cylinder collision shapes more reliable. "
"See :ref:`doc_using_jolt_physics` for more information."
msgstr ""
"ການປ່ຽນ physics engine ຈາກ GodotPhysics ໄປເປັນ Jolt ຈະຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ cylinder collision "
"shapes ມີຄວາມໝັ້ນຄົງຂຶ້ນ. ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_using_jolt_physics` ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:109
msgid ""
"During the transition from Bullet to GodotPhysics in Godot 4, cylinder "
"collision shapes had to be reimplemented from scratch. However, cylinder "
"collision shapes are one of the most difficult shapes to support, which is "
"why many other physics engines don't provide any support for them. There are "
"several known bugs with cylinder collision shapes currently."
msgstr ""
"ໃນຊ່ວງທີ່ມີການປ່ຽນຈາກ Bullet ໄປເປັນ GodotPhysics ໃນ Godot 4, cylinder collision "
"shapes ຕ້ອງໄດ້ຖືກຂຽນຂຶ້ນໃໝ່ທັງໝົດ. ຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ຮູບຊົງກະບອກແມ່ນໜຶ່ງໃນຮູບຊົງທີ່ຮອງຮັບໄດ້ຍາກທີ່ສຸດ, ເຊິ່ງ"
"ເປັນເຫດຜົນທີ່ physics engines ອື່ນໆຈຳນວນຫຼາຍບໍ່ຮອງຮັບຮູບຊົງນີ້. ປັດຈຸບັນຍັງມີ bug ຫຼາຍຢ່າງທີ່ພົບໃນ "
"cylinder collision shapes."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:115
msgid ""
"If you are sticking to GodotPhysics, we recommend using box or capsule "
"collision shapes for characters for now. Boxes generally provide the best "
"reliability, but have the downside of making the character take more space "
"diagonally. Capsule collision shapes do not have this downside, but their "
"shape can make precision platforming more difficult."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການໃຊ້ GodotPhysics ຕໍ່ໄປ, ພວກເຮົາແນະນຳໃຫ້ໃຊ້ box ຫຼື capsule collision "
"shapes ສຳລັບຕົວລະຄອນໃນເວລານີ້. ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປແລ້ວ Box ຈະມີຄວາມໝັ້ນຄົງທີ່ສຸດ, ແຕ່ມີຂໍ້ເສຍຄືເຮັດໃຫ້ຕົວລະຄອ"
"ນໃຊ້ພື້ນທີ່ໃນແນວສະຫຼຽງຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນ. Capsule ຈະບໍ່ມີຂໍ້ເສຍນີ້, ແຕ່ຮູບຊົງຂອງມັນອາດຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ການໂດດໃນແນວ "
"platform ທີ່ຕ້ອງການຄວາມຊັດເຈນເຮັດໄດ້ຍາກຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:122
msgid "VehicleBody simulation is unstable, especially at high speeds"
msgstr "ການຈຳລອງ VehicleBody ບໍ່ໝັ້ນຄົງ, ໂດຍສະເພາະເມື່ອມີຄວາມໄວສູງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:124
msgid ""
"When a physics body moves at a high speed, it travels a large distance "
"between each physics step. For instance, when using the 1 unit = 1 meter "
"convention in 3D, a vehicle moving at 360 km/h will travel 100 units per "
"second. With the default physics simulation rate of 60 Hz, the vehicle moves "
"by ~1.67 units each physics tick. This means that small objects may be "
"ignored entirely by the vehicle (due to tunneling), but also that the "
"simulation has little data to work with in general at such a high speed."
msgstr ""
"ເມື່ອ physics body ເຄື່ອນທີ່ດ້ວຍຄວາມໄວສູງ, ມັນຈະເຄື່ອນທີ່ເປັນໄລຍະທາງທີ່ໄກໃນລະຫວ່າງແຕ່ລະ "
"physics step. ຕົວຢ່າງເຊັ່ນ, ຖ້າໃຊ້ 1 unit = 1 meter ໃນ 3D, ລົດທີ່ແລ່ນດ້ວຍຄວາມໄວ 360 km/"
"h ຈະເຄື່ອນທີ່ 100 units ຕໍ່ວິນາທີ. ດ້ວຍອັດຕາການຈຳລອງ physics ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນທີ່ 60 Hz, ລົດຈະເຄື່ອນທີ່ປ"
"ະມານ 1.67 units ໃນແຕ່ລະ physics tick. ນີ້ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າວັດຖຸນ້ອຍໆ ອາດຈະຖືກລົດແລ່ນທະລຸຜ່ານໄປເລີ"
"ຍ (ຍ້ອນ tunneling), ແລະ ຍັງໝາຍຄວາມວ່າການຈຳລອງມີຂໍ້ມູນໜ້ອຍເກີນໄປທີ່ຈະປະມວນຜົນໃນຄວາມໄວສູງຂະໜ"
"າດນັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:132
msgid ""
"Fast-moving vehicles can benefit a lot from an increased physics simulation "
"rate. To do so, increase :ref:`Physics Ticks per "
"Second<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/common/"
"physics_ticks_per_second>` in the advanced Project Settings. Note that this "
"increases CPU utilization and may not be viable for mobile/web platforms. "
"Multipliers of the default value of ``60`` (such as ``120``, ``180`` or "
"``240``) should be preferred for a smooth appearance on most displays."
msgstr ""
"ລົດທີ່ເຄື່ອນທີ່ໄວຈະໄດ້ຮັບປະໂຫຍດຫຼາຍຈາກການເພີ່ມອັດຕາການຈຳລອງ physics. ໂດຍການເພີ່ມ "
":ref:`Physics Ticks per Second<class_ProjectSettings_property_physics/common/"
"physics_ticks_per_second>` ໃນການຕັ້ງຄ່າ Project Settings ຂັ້ນສູງ. ສັງເກດວ່າວິທີນີ້ຈະເພີ່ມກາ"
"ນໃຊ້ CPU ແລະ ອາດຈະບໍ່ເໝາະສົມສຳລັບ platform ມືຖື ຫຼື ເວັບ. ຄວນເລືອກໃຊ້ຕົວຄູນຂອງຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ "
"``60`` (ເຊັ່ນ ``120``, ``180`` ຫຼື ``240``) ເພື່ອໃຫ້ການສະແດງຜົນເບິ່ງມີຄວາມຕໍ່ເນື່ອງໃນໜ້າຈໍສ່ວນໃ"
"ຫຍ່."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:142
msgid "Collision results in bumps when an object moves across tiles"
msgstr "ເກີດການກະແທກ (bumps) ເມື່ອວັດຖຸເຄື່ອນທີ່ຜ່ານ tiles ຕ່າງໆ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:144
msgid ""
"This is a known issue in the physics engine caused by the object bumping on "
"a shape's edges, even though that edge is covered by another shape. This can "
"occur in both 2D and 3D."
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ແມ່ນບັນຫາທີ່ຮູ້ກັນດີໃນ physics engine ທີ່ເກີດຈາກວັດຖຸໄປຕຳກັບຂອບຂອງຮູບຊົງ, ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຂອບນັ້ນຈະຖືກປົ"
"ກຄຸມດ້ວຍຮູບຊົງອື່ນແລ້ວກໍຕາມ. ສິ່ງນີ້ສາມາດເກີດຂຶ້ນໄດ້ທັງໃນ 2D ແລະ 3D."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:148
msgid ""
"The best way to work around this issue is to create a \"composite\" "
"collider. This means that instead of individual tiles having their "
"collision, you create a single collision shape representing the collision "
"for a group of tiles. Typically, you should split composite colliders on a "
"per-island basis (which means each group of touching tiles gets its own "
"collider)."
msgstr ""
"ວິທີທີ່ດີທີ່ສຸດໃນການແກ້ໄຂບັນຫານີ້ຄືການສ້າງ collider ແບບ \"composite\". ນີ້ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າແທນທີ່ຈະໃຫ້ແຕ່"
"ລະ tile ມີ collider ຂອງໃຜຂອງມັນ, ເຈົ້າຄວນສ້າງ collision shape ອັນດຽວທີ່ເປັນຕົວແທນຂອງກຸ່ມ "
"tiles. ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປແລ້ວ, ເຈົ້າຄວນແຍກ composite colliders ຕາມກຸ່ມ tiles ທີ່ຢູ່ຕິດກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:154
msgid ""
"Using a composite collider can also improve physics simulation performance "
"in certain cases. However, since the composite collision shape is much more "
"complex, this may not be a net performance win in all cases."
msgstr ""
"ການໃຊ້ composite collider ຍັງສາມາດຊ່ວຍປັບປຸງປະສິດທິພາບການຈຳລອງ physics ໃນບາງກໍລະນີ. ຢ່າ"
"ງໃດກໍຕາມ, ເນື່ອງຈາກ composite collision shape ມີຄວາມຊັບຊ້ອນກວ່າ, ມັນອາດຈະບໍ່ໄດ້ຊ່ວຍເລື່ອງປະ"
"ສິດທິພາບສະເໝີໄປໃນທຸກກໍລະນີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:160
msgid ""
"In Godot 4.5 and later, creating a composite collider is automatically done "
"when using a TileMapLayer node. The chunk size (``16`` tiles on each axis by "
"default) can be set using the **Physics Quadrant Size** property in the "
"TileMapLayer inspector. Larger values provide more reliable collision, at "
"the cost of slower updates when the TileMap is changed."
msgstr ""
"ໃນ Godot 4.5 ແລະ ລຸ້ນໃໝ່ກວ່າ, ການສ້າງ composite collider ຈະຖືກເຮັດໃຫ້ໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດເມື່ອໃ"
"ຊ້ node TileMapLayer. ຂະໜາດຂອງ chunk (ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນຄື ``16`` tiles ໃນແຕ່ລະແກນ) ສາມາດຕັ້ງ"
"ຄ່າໄດ້ໂດຍໃຊ້ຄຸນສົມບັດ **Physics Quadrant Size** ໃນ inspector ຂອງ TileMapLayer. ຄ່າທີ່ໃ"
"ຫຍ່ຂຶ້ນຈະໃຫ້ການຕຳທີ່ໝັ້ນຄົງຂຶ້ນ, ແຕ່ຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ການອັບເດດຊ້າລົງເມື່ອມີການປ່ຽນແປງ TileMap."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:167
msgid "Framerate drops when an object touches another object"
msgstr "Framerate ຕົກເມື່ອວັດຖຸໜຶ່ງໄປຕຳກັບອີກວັດຖຸໜຶ່ງ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:169
msgid ""
"This is likely due to one of the objects using a collision shape that is too "
"complex. Convex collision shapes should use a number of shapes as low as "
"possible for performance reasons. When relying on Godot's automatic "
"generation, it's possible that you ended up with dozens if not hundreds of "
"shapes created for a single convex shape collision resource."
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ອາດຈະເກີດຈາກການທີ່ວັດຖຸໃດໜຶ່ງໃຊ້ collision shape ທີ່ຊັບຊ້ອນເກີນໄປ. Convex collision "
"shapes ຄວນໃຊ້ຈຳນວນຮູບຊົງໃຫ້ໜ້ອຍທີ່ສຸດເທົ່າທີ່ຈະເຮັດໄດ້ເພື່ອປະສິດທິພາບ. ເມື່ອໃຊ້ການສ້າງແບບອັດຕະໂນມັດຂອ"
"ງ Godot, ເປັນໄປໄດ້ວ່າເຈົ້າອາດຈະໄດ້ຮູບຊົງເປັນສິບ ຫຼື ເປັນຮ້ອຍອັນສຳລັບ convex shape collision ພ"
"ຽງອັນດຽວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:175
msgid ""
"In some cases, replacing a convex collider with a couple of primitive "
"collision shapes (box, sphere, or capsule) can deliver better performance."
msgstr ""
"ໃນບາງກໍລະນີ, ການປ່ຽນຈາກ convex collider ໄປເປັນ primitive collision shapes ຈຳນວນໜຶ່"
"ງ (box, sphere, ຫຼື capsule) ສາມາດໃຫ້ປະສິດທິພາບທີ່ດີກວ່າ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:178
msgid ""
"This issue can also occur with StaticBodies that use very detailed trimesh "
"(concave) collisions. In this case, use a simplified representation of the "
"level geometry as a collider. Not only this will improve physics simulation "
"performance significantly, but this can also improve stability by letting "
"you remove small fixtures and crevices from being considered by collision."
msgstr ""
"ບັນຫານີ້ຍັງສາມາດເກີດຂຶ້ນກັບ StaticBodies ທີ່ໃຊ້ trimesh (concave) collisions ທີ່ມີລາຍລະອຽດຫຼ"
"າຍເກີນໄປ. ໃນກໍລະນີນີ້, ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ຮູບຮ່າງທີ່ງ່າຍດາຍຂອງສາກ (level geometry) ເປັນ collider ແທນ. ສິ່"
"ງນີ້ບໍ່ພຽງແຕ່ຈະປັບປຸງປະສິດທິພາບການຈຳລອງ physics ໃຫ້ດີຂຶ້ນຢ່າງເຫັນໄດ້ຊັດ, ແຕ່ຍັງຊ່ວຍເພີ່ມຄວາມໝັ້ນຄົງໂດຍ"
"ການຕັດລາຍລະອຽດນ້ອຍໆ ແລະ ຊອກຫຼືບຕ່າງໆ ອອກຈາກການຄຳນວນການຕຳ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:184
msgid ""
"In 3D, switching the physics engine from the default GodotPhysics to Jolt "
"can also improve performance. See :ref:`doc_using_jolt_physics` for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"ໃນ 3D, ການປ່ຽນ physics engine ຈາກ GodotPhysics ໄປເປັນ Jolt ກໍສາມາດປັບປຸງປະສິດທິພາບໄ"
"ດ້. ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_using_jolt_physics` ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:188
msgid ""
"Framerate suddenly drops to a very low value beyond a certain amount of "
"physics simulation"
msgstr ""
"Framerate ຕົກລົງຢ່າງກະທັນຫັນຈົນຕ່ຳຫຼາຍ ເມື່ອມີການຈຳລອງ physics ເກີນຂີດຈຳກັດ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:190
msgid ""
"This occurs because the physics engine can't keep up with the expected "
"simulation rate. In this case, the framerate will start dropping, but the "
"engine is only allowed to simulate a certain number of physics steps per "
"rendered frame. This snowballs into a situation where framerate keeps "
"dropping until it reaches a very low framerate (typically 1-2 FPS) and is "
"called the *physics spiral of death*."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງນີ້ເກີດຂຶ້ນຍ້ອນ physics engine ບໍ່ສາມາດປະມວນຜົນໄດ້ທັນຕາມອັດຕາການຈຳລອງທີ່ກຳນົດໄວ້. ໃນກໍລະນີນີ້, "
"framerate ຈະເລີ່ມຕົກ, ແຕ່ engine ຖືກກຳນົດໃຫ້ຈຳລອງ physics ໄດ້ພຽງແຕ່ຈຳນວນຮອບໃດໜຶ່ງຕໍ່ "
"frame ທີ່ສະແດງຜົນ. ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະລາມໄປເລື້ອຍໆ ຈົນກວ່າ framerate ຈະຕົກລົງຮອດຈຸດທີ່ຕ່ຳຫຼາຍ (ປົກກະຕິຄື 1-"
"2 FPS) ເຊິ່ງເອີ້ນວ່າ *physics spiral of death*."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:197
msgid ""
"To avoid this, you should check for situations in your project that can "
"cause excessive number of physics simulations to occur at the same time (or "
"with excessively complex collision shapes). If these situations cannot be "
"avoided, you can increase the **Max Physics Steps per Frame** project "
"setting and/or reduce **Physics Ticks per Second** to alleviate this."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອຫຼີກລ່ຽງບັນຫານີ້, ເຈົ້າຄວນກວດສອບສະຖານະການໃນ project ທີ່ອາດຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດການຈຳລອງ "
"physics ຈຳນວນມະຫາສານໃນເວລາດຽວກັນ (ຫຼື ໃຊ້ collision shapes ທີ່ຊັບຊ້ອນເກີນໄປ). ຖ້າບໍ່ສາມາດ"
"ຫຼີກລ່ຽງໄດ້, ເຈົ້າສາມາດເພີ່ມຄ່າ **Max Physics Steps per Frame** ໃນ project settings ແລ"
"ະ/ຫຼື ຫຼຸດ **Physics Ticks per Second** ເພື່ອບັນເທົາບັນຫານີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:204
msgid "Physics simulation is unreliable when far away from the world origin"
msgstr "ການຈຳລອງ physics ບໍ່ແນ່ນອນເມື່ອຢູ່ໄກຈາກຈຸດເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ (world origin)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/physics/troubleshooting_physics_issues.rst:206
msgid ""
"This is caused by floating-point precision errors, which become more "
"pronounced as the physics simulation occurs further away from the world "
"origin. This issue also affects rendering, which results in wobbly camera "
"movement when far away from the world origin. "
"See :ref:`doc_large_world_coordinates` for more information."
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ເກີດຈາກຂໍ້ຜິດພາດຂອງຄວາມລະອຽດ floating-point ເຊິ່ງຈະເຫັນໄດ້ຊັດເຈນຂຶ້ນເມື່ອການຈຳລອງ "
"physics ເກີດຂຶ້ນໃນຕຳແໜ່ງທີ່ຫ່າງໄກຈາກ world origin ຫຼາຍໆ. ບັນຫານີ້ຍັງສົ່ງຜົນກະທົບຕໍ່ການສະແດງຜົນ, "
"ເຮັດໃຫ້ກ້ອງຖ່າຍຮູບມີການສັ່ນເມື່ອຢູ່ໄກຈາກຈຸດເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ. ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_large_world_coordinates` ສ"
"ຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/index.rst:6
msgid ""
"Godot supports both running the editor and exporting projects on several "
"platforms. Usage of the engine is generally similar across platforms, but "
"there are some platform-specific considerations, which are covered in this "
"section."
msgstr ""
"Godot ຮອງຮັບທັງການໃຊ້ editor ແລະ ການ export project ໃນຫຼາຍ platform. ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປແລ້ວກາ"
"ນໃຊ້ engine ຈະຄ້າຍຄືກັນໃນທຸກ platform, ແຕ່ກໍມີບາງຂໍ້ຄວນລະວັງສະເພາະຂອງແຕ່ລະ platform ເຊິ່ງຈະ"
"ຖືກອະທິບາຍໃນສ່ວນນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/index.rst:12
msgid ""
"For platform-specific versions of the editor, "
"see :ref:`doc_using_the_xr_editor`, :ref:`doc_using_the_android_editor`, "
"and :ref:`doc_using_the_web_editor`. For exporting to specific platforms, "
"see the :ref:`doc_export_index` section."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບ editor ລຸ້ນສະເພາະ platform, ໃຫ້ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_using_the_xr_editor`, "
":ref:`doc_using_the_android_editor`, ແລະ :ref:`doc_using_the_web_editor`. ສຳລັ"
"ບການ export ໄປຍັງ platform ຕ່າງໆ, ໃຫ້ເບິ່ງທີ່ສ່ວນ :ref:`doc_export_index`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:4
msgid "Wayland/X11"
msgstr "Wayland/X11"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:9
msgid ""
"One of the important components of any operating system is its display "
"server. Windows and macOS only provide one option, Linux however has two, "
"X11 and Wayland."
msgstr ""
"ໜຶ່ງໃນສ່ວນປະກອບທີ່ສຳຄັນຂອງລະບົບປະຕິບັດການໃດໜຶ່ງກໍຄື display server. Windows ແລະ macOS ມີໃຫ້ເ"
"ລືອກພຽງຢ່າງດຽວ, ແຕ່ Linux ຊ້ຳພັດມີສອງຢ່າງ ຄື X11 ແລະ Wayland."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:12
msgid ""
"X11 is an older standard and is currently being gradually phased out by the "
"majority of linux distributions in favor of supporting Wayland, which has "
"been developed as a replacement. Applications running on X11 can still work "
"when a distribution is using Wayland thanks to a compatibility layer known "
"as Xwayland."
msgstr ""
"X11 ແມ່ນມາດຕະຖານເກົ່າ ແລະ ປັດຈຸບັນກຳລັງຖືກປ່ຽນແທນໂດຍ Linux distribution ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ເພື່ອໄປໃຊ້ "
"Wayland ທີ່ຖືກພັດທະນາຂຶ້ນມາແທນ. ແອັບພລິເຄຊັນທີ່ເຮັດວຽກໃນ X11 ຍັງຄົງສາມາດໃຊ້ງານໄດ້ໃນ "
"distribution ທີ່ໃຊ້ Wayland ຜ່ານ layer ທີ່ຊ່ວຍໃນການເຮັດວຽກຮ່ວມກັນທີ່ເອີ້ນວ່າ Xwayland."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:17
msgid ""
"Godot's support is still a work in progress, so for now X11 remains the "
"default setting for game projects, that will likely change in a future "
"version."
msgstr ""
"ການຮອງຮັບຂອງ Godot ຍັງຢູ່ໃນຊ່ວງການພັດທະນາ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນໃນເວລານີ້ X11 ຈຶ່ງຍັງເປັນຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນສຳລັບ "
"project ເກມ, ເຊິ່ງອາດຈະມີການປ່ຽນແປງໃນລຸ້ນຕໍ່ໄປ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:21
msgid "When to use Wayland"
msgstr "ເວລາໃດຄວນໃຊ້ Wayland"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:23
msgid ""
"If you're an engine developer who wants to help improve support, or if you "
"think Xwayland might be causing visual glitches in your exported project for "
"whatever reason, then we would recommend using Wayland. But outside of that "
"it's recommended to stick with X11 for now. It's important to note that "
"while X11 applications can run on Wayland, the reverse is not true."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າເຈົ້າເປັນຜູ້ພັດທະນາ engine ທີ່ຕ້ອງການຊ່ວຍປັບປຸງການຮອງຮັບ, ຫຼື ຖ້າເຈົ້າຄິດວ່າ Xwayland ອາດຈະເຮັດໃ"
"ຫ້ເກີດບັນຫາທາງດ້ານການສະແດງຜົນໃນ project ທີ່ export ອອກໄປ, ພວກເຮົາແນະນຳໃຫ້ໃຊ້ Wayland. ແ"
"ຕ່ຖ້ານອກເໜືອຈາກນັ້ນ, ແນະນຳໃຫ້ໃຊ້ X11 ໄປກ່ອນ. ສິ່ງທີ່ສຳຄັນຄື ເຖິງວ່າແອັບ X11 ຈະສາມາດໃຊ້ງານໃນ "
"Wayland ໄດ້, ແຕ່ແອັບ Wayland ບໍ່ສາມາດໃຊ້ງານໃນ X11 ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:29
msgid ""
"As of January 2026 most popular distributions are using Wayland by default, "
"including, but not limited to, the following:"
msgstr ""
"ມາຮອດເດືອນມັງກອນ 2026, distribution ທີ່ໄດ້ຮັບຄວາມນິຍົມສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ແມ່ນໃຊ້ Wayland ເປັນຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້"
"ນ, ເຊິ່ງລວມມີ (ແຕ່ບໍ່ຈຳກັດພຽງແຕ່):"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:32
msgid "SteamOS"
msgstr "SteamOS"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:33
msgid "Bazzite"
msgstr "Bazzite"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:34
msgid "CachyOS"
msgstr "CachyOS"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:35
#: ../../docs/engine_details/development/compiling/compiling_for_linuxbsd.rst:105
#: ../../docs/engine_details/development/compiling/compiling_for_linuxbsd.rst:565
#: ../../docs/engine_details/development/compiling/compiling_for_linuxbsd.rst:631
#: ../../docs/engine_details/development/debugging/vulkan/vulkan_validation_layers.rst:82
msgid "Fedora"
msgstr "Fedora"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:36
msgid "Fedora Silverblue"
msgstr "Fedora Silverblue"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:37
msgid "Ubuntu"
msgstr "Ubuntu"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:38
msgid "OpenSuse"
msgstr "OpenSuse"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:40
msgid ""
"Keep in mind that for some distributions, like Ubuntu, users may have "
"changed the display server to X11 manually themselves."
msgstr ""
"ຢ່າລືມວ່າໃນບາງ distribution ເຊັ່ນ Ubuntu, ຜູ້ໃຊ້ອາດຈະມີການປ່ຽນ display server ໄປເປັນ "
"X11 ດ້ວຍຕົວເອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:44
msgid "Changing the setting"
msgstr "ການປ່ຽນແປງການຕັ້ງຄ່າ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:46
msgid ""
"To change your display server to Wayland click on :menu:`Project > project "
"settings`, from here, go to :button:`Display Server` and change "
"the :button:`driver.linuxbsd` option to ``wayland``."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອປ່ຽນ display server ຂອງເຈົ້າໃຫ້ເປັນ Wayland ໃຫ້ຄລິກທີ່ :menu:`Project > project "
"settings`, ຈາກນັ້ນໄປທີ່ :button:`Display Server` ແລະ ປ່ຽນຕົວເລືອກ "
":button:`driver.linuxbsd` ໃຫ້ເປັນ ``wayland``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:51
msgid "Disabling Libdecor loading"
msgstr "ການປິດການໂຫຼດ Libdecor"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/linux/wayland_x11.rst:53
msgid ""
"Libdecor loading on Wayland has some quirks and it may be useful to disable "
"it depending on your situation. To do that you need to set the "
"``GODOT_WAYLAND_DISABLE_LIBDECOR`` environment variable to ``1`` like this:"
msgstr ""
"ການໂຫຼດ Libdecor ໃນ Wayland ອາດຈະມີບາງບັນຫາເລັກນ້ອຍ ແລະ ມັນອາດຈະມີປະໂຫຍດຖ້າປິດການນຳໃຊ້ມັ"
"ນຕາມສະຖານະການຂອງເຈົ້າ. ເພື່ອເຮັດແນວນັ້ນ ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງຕັ້ງຄ່າ environment variable "
"``GODOT_WAYLAND_DISABLE_LIBDECOR`` ໃຫ້ເປັນ ``1`` ແບບນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:4
msgid "Godot Android library"
msgstr "Godot Android library"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:6
msgid ""
"The Godot Engine for Android platforms is designed to be used as an `Android "
"library <https://developer.android.com/studio/projects/android-library>`_. "
"This architecture enables several key features on Android platforms:"
msgstr ""
"Godot Engine ສຳລັບ platform Android ຖືກອອກແບບມາເພື່ອໃຊ້ເປັນ `Android library "
"<https://developer.android.com/studio/projects/android-library>`_. ໂຄງສ້າງນີ້ຊ່ວຍ"
"ໃຫ້ສາມາດໃຊ້ງານຄຸນສົມບັດທີ່ສຳຄັນໃນ platform Android ໄດ້ຫຼາຍຢ່າງ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:9
msgid ""
"Ability to integrate the Gradle build system within the Godot Editor, which "
"provides the ability to leverage more components from the Android ecosystem "
"such as libraries and tools"
msgstr ""
"ຄວາມສາມາດໃນການລວມລະບົບ Gradle build ເຂົ້າໃນ Godot Editor, ເຊິ່ງຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສາມາດນຳໃຊ້ສ່ວນປະ"
"ກອບຕ່າງໆ ຈາກລະບົບຂອງ Android ໄດ້ຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນ ເຊັ່ນ library ແລະ ເຄື່ອງມືຕ່າງໆ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:11
msgid "Ability to make the engine portable and embeddable:"
msgstr ""
"ຄວາມສາມາດໃນການເຮັດໃຫ້ engine ສາມາດພົກພາ ແລະ ຝັງ (embed) ເຂົ້າໃນລະບົບອື່ນໄດ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:13
msgid ""
"Key in enabling the port of the Godot Editor to Android and mobile XR devices"
msgstr ""
"ເປັນຈຸດສຳຄັນທີ່ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສາມາດນຳ Godot Editor ໄປໃຊ້ໃນ Android ແລະ ອຸປະກອນ mobile XR ໄດ້"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:14
msgid ""
"Key in allowing the integration and reuse of Godot's capabilities within "
"existing codebase"
msgstr ""
"ເປັນຈຸດສຳຄັນທີ່ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສາມາດລວມ ແລະ ນຳໃຊ້ຄວາມສາມາດຂອງ Godot ຄືນໃໝ່ໃນ codebase ທີ່ມີຢູ່ແລ້ວ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:16
msgid ""
"Below we describe some of the use-cases and scenarios this architecture "
"enables."
msgstr ""
"ດ້ານລຸ່ມນີ້ພວກເຮົາຈະອະທິບາຍບາງກໍລະນີການນຳໃຊ້ ແລະ ສະຖານະການທີ່ໂຄງສ້າງນີ້ຮອງຮັບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:19
msgid "Using the Godot Android library"
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ Godot Android library"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:21
msgid ""
"The Godot Android library is packaged as an AAR archive file and hosted on "
"`MavenCentral <https://central.sonatype.com/artifact/org.godotengine/"
"godot>`_ along with `its documentation <https://javadoc.io/doc/"
"org.godotengine/godot/latest/index.html>`_."
msgstr ""
"Godot Android library ຖືກຈັດລວມເປັນໄຟລ໌ AAR ແລະ ຝາກໄວ້ທີ່ `MavenCentral <https://"
"central.sonatype.com/artifact/org.godotengine/godot>`_ ພ້ອມກັບ `ເອກະສານແນະນຳ "
"<https://javadoc.io/doc/org.godotengine/godot/latest/index.html>`_."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:23
msgid ""
"It provides access to Godot APIs and capabilities on Android platforms for "
"the following non-exhaustive use-cases."
msgstr ""
"ມັນຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ເຂົ້າເຖິງ Godot APIs ແລະ ຄວາມສາມາດຕ່າງໆ ໃນ platform Android ສຳລັບກໍລະນີນຳໃຊ້ດັ່ງ"
"ຕໍ່ໄປນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:26
#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_plugin.rst:4
msgid "Godot Android plugins"
msgstr "Godot Android plugins"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:28
msgid ""
"Android plugins are powerful tools to extend the capabilities of the Godot "
"Engine by tapping into the functionality provided by Android platforms and "
"ecosystem."
msgstr ""
"Android plugins ແມ່ນເຄື່ອງມືທີ່ມີປະສິດທິພາບໃນການຂະຫຍາຍຄວາມສາມາດຂອງ Godot Engine ໂດຍການ"
"ເຂົ້າເຖິງການເຮັດວຽກຕ່າງໆ ທີ່ມີໃນ platform ແລະ ລະບົບຂອງ Android."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:31
msgid ""
"An Android plugin is an Android library with a dependency on the Godot "
"Android library which the plugin uses to integrate into the engine's "
"lifecycle and to access Godot APIs, granting it powerful capabilities such "
"as GDExtension support which allows to update / mod the engine behavior as "
"needed."
msgstr ""
"Android plugin ແມ່ນ Android library ທີ່ມີການເຊື່ອມໂຍງກັບ Godot Android library ເຊິ່ງ "
"plugin ຈະໃຊ້ເພື່ອລວມເຂົ້າກັບ lifecycle ຂອງ engine ແລະ ເຂົ້າເຖິງ Godot APIs, ເຮັດໃຫ້ມັນມີຄວ"
"າມສາມາດສູງ ເຊັ່ນ ການຮອງຮັບ GDExtension ທີ່ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສາມາດອັບເດດ ຫຼື ປັບປ່ຽນ (mod) ພຶດຕິກຳຂອງ "
"engine ໄດ້ຕາມຕ້ອງການ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:35
msgid ""
"For more information, see :ref:`Godot Android plugins <doc_android_plugin>`."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມ, ໃຫ້ເບິ່ງ :ref:`Godot Android plugins <doc_android_plugin>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:38
msgid "Embedding Godot in existing Android projects"
msgstr "ການຝັງ Godot ເຂົ້າໃນ project Android ທີ່ມີຢູ່ແລ້ວ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:40
msgid ""
"The Godot Engine can be embedded within existing Android applications or "
"libraries, allowing developers to leverage mature and battle-tested code and "
"libraries better suited to a specific task."
msgstr ""
"Godot Engine ສາມາດຖືກຝັງເຂົ້າໃນແອັບພລິເຄຊັນ ຫຼື library ຂອງ Android ທີ່ມີຢູ່ແລ້ວ, ເຊິ່ງຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ຜູ້ພັ"
"ດທະນາສາມາດນຳໃຊ້ code ແລະ library ທີ່ຜ່ານການທົດສອບມາຢ່າງດີ ແລະ ເໝາະສົມກັບວຽກສະເພາະຢ່າງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:43
msgid ""
"The hosting component is responsible for driving the engine lifecycle via "
"Godot's Android APIs. These APIs can also be used to provide bidirectional "
"communication between the host and the embedded Godot instance allowing for "
"greater control over the desired experience."
msgstr ""
"ສ່ວນປະກອບທີ່ເປັນຕົວໂຮສ (host) ຈະມີໜ້າທີ່ໃນການຄວບຄຸມ lifecycle ຂອງ engine ຜ່ານ Godot's "
"Android APIs. API ເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຍັງສາມາດໃຊ້ເພື່ອສື່ສານແບບສອງທາງລະຫວ່າງຕົວໂຮສ ແລະ Godot "
"instance ທີ່ຖືກຝັງຢູ່ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ສາມາດຄວບຄຸມໄດ້ຕາມທີ່ຕ້ອງການ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:47
msgid ""
"We showcase how this is done using a sample Android app that embeds the "
"Godot Engine as an Android view, and uses it to render 3D glTF models."
msgstr ""
"ພວກເຮົາຈະສະແດງໃຫ້ເຫັນວິທີການເຮັດສິ່ງນີ້ໂດຍໃຊ້ແອັບ Android ຕົວຢ່າງທີ່ຝັງ Godot Engine ເປັນ "
"Android view, ແລະ ໃຊ້ມັນເພື່ອສະແດງຜົນ (render) ໂມເດວ 3D glTF."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:50
msgid ""
"The `GLTF Viewer <https://github.com/m4gr3d/Godot-Android-Samples/tree/"
"master/apps/gltf_viewer>`_ sample app uses an `Android RecyclerView "
"component <https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/views/layout/"
"recyclerview>`_ to create a list of glTF items, populated from `Kenney's "
"Food Kit pack <https://kenney.nl/assets/food-kit>`_. When an item on the "
"list is selected, the app's logic interacts with the embedded Godot Engine "
"to render the selected glTF item as a 3D model."
msgstr ""
"ແອັບຕົວຢ່າງ `GLTF Viewer <https://github.com/m4gr3d/Godot-Android-Samples/tree/"
"master/apps/gltf_viewer>`_ ໃຊ້ `Android RecyclerView component <https://"
"developer.android.com/develop/ui/views/layout/recyclerview>`_ ເພື່ອສ້າງລາຍການຂອ"
"ງ glTF, ເຊິ່ງດຶງຂໍ້ມູນມາຈາກ `Kenney's Food Kit pack <https://kenney.nl/assets/food-"
"kit>`_. ເມື່ອມີການເລືອກລາຍການ, logic ຂອງແອັບຈະຕິດຕໍ່ກັບ Godot Engine ທີ່ຝັງຢູ່ເພື່ອ render ໂມ"
"ເດວ 3D ຂອງໄຟລ໌ glTF ທີ່ຖືກເລືອກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:56
msgid ""
"The sample app source code can be found `on GitHub <https://github.com/"
"m4gr3d/Godot-Android-Samples/tree/master/apps/gltf_viewer>`_. Follow the "
"instructions on `its README <https://github.com/m4gr3d/Godot-Android-Samples/"
"blob/master/apps/gltf_viewer/README.md>`_ to build and install it."
msgstr ""
"Source code ຂອງແອັບຕົວຢ່າງສາມາດເບິ່ງໄດ້ທີ່ `on GitHub <https://github.com/m4gr3d/"
"Godot-Android-Samples/tree/master/apps/gltf_viewer>`_. ໃຫ້ເຮັດຕາມຄຳແນະນຳໃນ `ໄຟ"
"ລ໌ README ຂອງມັນ <https://github.com/m4gr3d/Godot-Android-Samples/blob/master/"
"apps/gltf_viewer/README.md>`_ ເພື່ອ build ແລະ ຕິດຕັ້ງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:59
msgid "Below we break-down the steps used to create the GLTF Viewer app."
msgstr "ດ້ານລຸ່ມນີ້ແມ່ນຂັ້ນຕອນຕ່າງໆ ໃນການສ້າງແອັບ GLTF Viewer."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:63
msgid ""
"Currently only a single instance of the Godot Engine is supported per "
"process. You can configure the process the Android Activity runs under using "
"the `android:process attribute <https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/"
"manifest/activity-element#proc>`_."
msgstr ""
"ປັດຈຸບັນຮອງຮັບ Godot Engine ພຽງແຕ່ instance ດຽວຕໍ່ໜຶ່ງ process ເທົ່ານັ້ນ. ເເຈົ້າສາມາດຕັ້ງຄ່າ "
"process ທີ່ Android Activity ຈະເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ໂດຍໃຊ້ `android:process attribute "
"<https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/manifest/activity-element#proc>"
"`_."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:68
msgid ""
"Automatic resizing / orientation configuration events are not supported and "
"may cause a crash. You can disable those events:"
msgstr ""
"ການປັບຂະໜາດ / ປ່ຽນທິດທາງ (orientation) ແບບອັດຕະໂນມັດແມ່ນຍັງບໍ່ຮອງຮັບ ແລະ ອາດຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ແອັບຄ້"
"າງໄດ້. ເຈົ້າສາມາດປິດ event ເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນໄດ້ໂດຍ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:71
msgid ""
"By locking to a specific orientation using the `android:screenOrientation "
"attribute <https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/manifest/activity-"
"element#screen>`_."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍການລັອກໃຫ້ເປັນທິດທາງໃດໜຶ່ງໂດຍໃຊ້ `android:screenOrientation attribute <https://"
"developer.android.com/guide/topics/manifest/activity-element#screen>`_."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/android/android_library.rst:72
msgid ""
"By declaring that the Activity will handle these configuration events using "
"the `android:configChanges attribute <https://developer.android.com/guide/"
"topics/manifest/activity-element#config>`_."
msgstr ""
"ໂດຍການກຳນົດວ່າ Activity ຈະເປັນຕົວຈັດການ config events ເຫຼົ່ານີ້ເອງ ໂດຍໃຊ້ "
"`android:configChanges attribute <https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/"
"manifest/activity-element#config>`_."

