#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:94
msgid ""
"These types can also be put inside :ref:`arrays "
"<doc_shading_language_arrays>` or :ref:`structs "
"<doc_shading_language_structs>`, which are also usable as function "
"parameters or return values. Arrays can be used as uniforms, but structs "
"cannot."
msgstr ""
"ປະເພດເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຍັງສາມາດໃສ່ພາຍໃນ :ref:`arrays <doc_shading_language_arrays>` ຫຼື "
":ref:`structs <doc_shading_language_structs>`, ເຊິ່ງສາມາດໃຊ້ເປັນ parameter ຂອງຟັງຊັ"
"ນ ຫຼື ຄ່າສົ່ງຄືນໄດ້. Arrays ສາມາດໃຊ້ເປັນ uniforms ໄດ້, ແຕ່ structs ບໍ່ສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:100
msgid ""
"Local variables are not initialized to a default value such as ``0.0``. If "
"you use a variable without assigning it first, it will contain whatever "
"value was already present at that memory location, and unpredictable visual "
"glitches will appear. However, uniforms and varyings are initialized to a "
"default value."
msgstr ""
"ຕົວປ່ຽນ Local ຈະບໍ່ຖືກຕັ້ງຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນເປັນຄ່າໃດໜຶ່ງເຊັ່ນ ``0.0``. ຖ້າທ່ານໃຊ້ຕົວປ່ຽນໂດຍທີ່ບໍ່ໄດ້ກຳນົດຄ່າໃຫ້ມັນ"
"ກ່ອນ, ມັນຈະເກັບຄ່າໃດກໍຕາມທີ່ມີຢູ່ໃນຕຳແໜ່ງໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳນັ້ນ, ແລະ ຈະເກີດພາບຜິດປົກກະຕິທີ່ຄາດເດົາບໍ່ໄດ້. ເຖິງ"
"ຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, uniforms ແລະ varyings ຈະຖືກຕັ້ງຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນໃຫ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:109
msgid ""
"The shading language supports the same comment syntax as used in C# and C++, "
"using ``//`` for single-line comments and ``/* */`` for multi-line comments:"
msgstr ""
"Shading language ຮອງຮັບຮູບແບບການຂຽນຄຳອະທິບາຍ (comment) ຄືກັນກັບທີ່ໃຊ້ໃນ C# ແລະ C++, ໂດ"
"ຍໃຊ້ ``//`` ສຳລັບຄຳອະທິບາຍແຖວດຽວ ແລະ ``/* */`` ສຳລັບຄຳອະທິບາຍຫຼາຍແຖວ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:124
msgid ""
"Additionally, you can use documentation comments that are displayed in the "
"inspector when hovering a shader parameter. Documentation comments are "
"currently only supported when placed immediately above a ``uniform`` "
"declaration. These documentation comments only support the **multiline** "
"comment syntax (even if used on a single line) and must use **two** leading "
"asterisks (``/**``) instead of just one (``/*``):"
msgstr ""
"ນອກຈາກນີ້, ທ່ານຍັງສາມາດໃຊ້ documentation comments ເຊິ່ງຈະສະແດງໃນ inspector ເມື່ອເອົາມາວ"
"ໄປວາງໄວ້ເທິງ shader parameter. ປັດຈຸບັນ Documentation comments ແມ່ນຮອງຮັບສະເພາະເມື່ອວາ"
"ງໄວ້ເທິງການປະກາດ ``uniform`` ທັນທີເທົ່ານັ້ນ. Documentation comments ເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຮອງຮັບສະເພາະຮູບ"
"ແບບຄຳອະທິບາຍ **ຫຼາຍແຖວ** (ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຈະໃຊ້ໃນແຖວດຽວກໍຕາມ) ແລະ ຕ້ອງໃຊ້ເຄື່ອງໝາຍດອກຈັນ **ສອ"
"ງ** ອັນນຳໜ້າ (``/**``) ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນອັນດຽວ (``/*``):"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:144
msgid ""
"The asterisks on the follow-up lines are not required, but are recommended "
"as per the :ref:`doc_shaders_style_guide`. These asterisks are automatically "
"stripped by the inspector, so they won't appear in the tooltip."
msgstr ""
"ເຄື່ອງໝາຍດອກຈັນໃນແຖວຖັດໄປນັ້ນບໍ່ໄດ້ຖືກບັງຄັບ, ແຕ່ແນະນຳໃຫ້ໃສ່ຕາມ "
":ref:`doc_shaders_style_guide`. ເຄື່ອງໝາຍດອກຈັນເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຈະຖືກຕັດອອກໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດໃນ "
"inspector, ດັ່ງນັ້ນພວກມັນຈະບໍ່ປາກົດໃນ tooltip."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:151
msgid ""
"Just like GLSL ES 3.0, implicit casting between scalars and vectors of the "
"same size but different type is not allowed. Casting of types of different "
"size is also not allowed. Conversion must be done explicitly via "
"constructors."
msgstr ""
"ຄືກັນກັບ GLSL ES 3.0, ການແປງປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນ (implicit casting) ລະຫວ່າງ scalars ແລະ "
"vectors ທີ່ມີຂະໜາດດຽວກັນແຕ່ຄົນລະປະເພດນັ້ນແມ່ນບໍ່ອະນຸຍາດ. ການແປງປະເພດທີ່ມີຂະໜາດຕ່າງກັນກໍບໍ່ອະນຸຍາດເ"
"ຊັ່ນກັນ. ການແປງຕ້ອງເຮັດຢ່າງຊັດເຈນຜ່ານ constructors."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:163
msgid ""
"Default integer constants are signed, so casting is always needed to convert "
"to unsigned:"
msgstr ""
"ຄ່າຄົງທີ່ເລກຖ້ວນເລີ່ມຕົ້ນແມ່ນແບບມີເຄື່ອງໝາຍ, ດັ່ງນັ້ນການແປງປະເພດຈຶ່ງຈຳເປັນສະເໝີເພື່ອປ່ຽນເປັນແບບບໍ່ມີເຄື່ອງໝ"
"າຍ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:173
msgid "Members"
msgstr "ສະມາຊິກ"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:175
msgid ""
"Individual scalar members of vector types are accessed via the \"x\", \"y\", "
"\"z\" and \"w\" members. Alternatively, using \"r\", \"g\", \"b\" and \"a\" "
"also works and is equivalent. Use whatever fits best for your needs."
msgstr ""
"ແຕ່ລະສະມາຊິກ scalar ຂອງປະເພດເວັກເຕີສາມາດເຂົ້າເຖິງໄດ້ຜ່ານສະມາຊິກ \"x\", \"y\", \"z\" ແລ"
"ະ \"w\". ອີກທາງເລືອກໜຶ່ງ, ການໃຊ້ \"r\", \"g\", \"b\" ແລະ \"a\" ກໍສາມາດໃຊ້ໄດ້ ແລະ ມີຄ່າເ"
"ທົ່າກັນ. ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ສິ່ງໃດກໍຕາມທີ່ເໝາະສົມກັບຄວາມຕ້ອງການຂອງທ່ານທີ່ສຸດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:179
msgid ""
"For matrices, use the ``m[column][row]`` indexing syntax to access each "
"scalar, or ``m[column]`` to access a vector by column index. For example, "
"for accessing the y-component of the translation from a mat4 transform "
"matrix (4th column, 2nd line) you use ``m[3][1]`` or ``m[3].y``."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບມາທຣິກ, ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ຮູບແບບ ``m[column][row]`` ເພື່ອເຂົ້າເຖິງແຕ່ລະ scalar, ຫຼື "
"``m[column]`` ເພື່ອເຂົ້າເຖິງເວັກເຕີຕາມລຳດັບຖັນ. ຕົວຢ່າງ, ສຳລັບການເຂົ້າເຖິງ y-component ຂອງກາ"
"ນແປງຕຳແໜ່ງຈາກ mat4 transform matrix (ຖັນທີ 4, ແຖວທີ 2) ໃຫ້ທ່ານໃຊ້ ``m[3][1]`` ຫຼື "
"``m[3].y``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:184
msgid "Constructing"
msgstr "ການສ້າງ (Constructing)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:186
msgid "Construction of vector types must always pass:"
msgstr "ການສ້າງປະເພດເວັກເຕີຕ້ອງມີການສົ່ງຄ່າສະເໝີ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:198
msgid ""
"Construction of matrix types requires vectors of the same dimension as the "
"matrix, interpreted as columns. You can also build a diagonal matrix using "
"``matx(float)`` syntax. Accordingly, ``mat4(1.0)`` is an identity matrix."
msgstr ""
"ການສ້າງປະເພດມາທຣິກຕ້ອງການເວັກເຕີທີ່ມີມິຕິດຽວກັນກັບມາທຣິກ, ເຊິ່ງຈະຖືກຕີຄວາມໝາຍເປັນຖັນ. ທ່ານຍັງສາມາດ"
"ສ້າງ diagonal matrix ໄດ້ໂດຍໃຊ້ຮູບແບບ ``matx(float)``. ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ``mat4(1.0)`` ຈຶ່ງເປັນ "
"identity matrix."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:208
msgid ""
"Matrices can also be built from a matrix of another dimension. There are two "
"rules:"
msgstr "ມາທຣິກຍັງສາມາດສ້າງຈາກມາທຣິກຂອງມິຕິອື່ນໄດ້. ມີສອງກົດຄື:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:211
msgid ""
"1. If a larger matrix is constructed from a smaller matrix, the additional "
"rows and columns are set to the values they would have in an identity "
"matrix. 1. If a smaller matrix is constructed from a larger matrix, the top, "
"left submatrix of the larger matrix is used."
msgstr ""
"1. ຖ້າມາດທຣິກທີ່ໃຫຍ່ກວ່າຖືກສ້າງຈາກມາທຣິກທີ່ນ້ອຍກວ່າ, ແຖວ ແລະ ຖັນທີ່ເພີ່ມເຂົ້າມາຈະຖືກຕັ້ງຄ່າໃຫ້ເປັນຄ່າຄືກັບ"
"ໃນ identity matrix. 1. ຖ້າມາດທຣິກທີ່ນ້ອຍກວ່າຖືກສ້າງຈາກມາທຣິກທີ່ໃຫຍ່ກວ່າ, ສ່ວນຍ່ອຍດ້ານເທິງຊ້າຍຂອ"
"ງມາທຣິກທີ່ໃຫຍ່ກວ່າຈະຖືກນຳມາໃຊ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:223
msgid "Swizzling"
msgstr "ການສະລັບອົງປະກອບ (Swizzling)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:225
msgid ""
"It is possible to obtain any combination of components in any order, as long "
"as the result is another vector type (or scalar). This is easier shown than "
"explained:"
msgstr ""
"ເຮົາສາມາດນຳອົງປະກອບໃດໆມາລວມກັນໃນລຳດັບໃດກໍໄດ້, ຕາບໃດທີ່ຜົນໄດ້ຮັບຍັງເປັນປະເພດເວັກເຕີອື່ນ (ຫຼື "
"scalar). ສິ່ງນີ້ສະແດງໃຫ້ເຫັນໄດ້ງ່າຍກວ່າການອະທິບາຍ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:243
#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_godot_shaders.rst:116
msgid "Precision"
msgstr "ຄວາມຊັດເຈນ (Precision)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:245
msgid ""
"It is possible to add precision modifiers to datatypes; use them for "
"uniforms, variables, arguments and varyings:"
msgstr ""
"ເຮົາສາມາດເພີ່ມ precision modifiers ໃຫ້ກັບປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນໄດ້; ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ພວກມັນກັບ uniforms, ຕົວປ່ຽນ, "
"arguments ແລະ varyings:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:255
msgid ""
"Using lower precision for some operations can speed up the math involved (at "
"the cost of less precision). This is rarely needed in the vertex processor "
"function (where full precision is needed most of the time), but is often "
"useful in the fragment processor."
msgstr ""
"ການໃຊ້ຄວາມຊັດເຈນທີ່ຕໍ່າລົງໃນບາງການປະຕິບັດການສາມາດຊ່ວຍເລັ່ງການຄຳນວນທາງຄະນິດສາດໄດ້ (ແຕ່ຕ້ອງແລກມ"
"າກັບຄວາມຊັດເຈນທີ່ໜ້ອຍລົງ). ສິ່ງນີ້ບໍ່ຄ່ອຍຈຳເປັນໃນຟັງຊັນ vertex processor, ແຕ່ມັກຈະມີປະໂຫຍດໃນ "
"fragment processor."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:260
msgid ""
"Some architectures (mainly mobile) can benefit significantly from this, but "
"there are downsides such as the additional overhead of conversion between "
"precisions. Refer to the documentation of the target architecture for "
"further information. In many cases, mobile drivers cause inconsistent or "
"unexpected behavior and it is best to avoid specifying precision unless "
"necessary."
msgstr ""
"ສະຖາປັດຕະຍະກຳບາງຢ່າງ (ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ແມ່ນມືຖື) ສາມາດໄດ້ຮັບປະໂຫຍດຢ່າງຫຼວງຫຼາຍຈາກສິ່ງນີ້, ແຕ່ກໍມີຂໍ້ເສຍເຊັ່"
"ນ: overhead ເພີ່ມເຕີມໃນການແປງລະຫວ່າງລະດັບຄວາມຊັດເຈນ. ໃຫ້ເບິ່ງເອກະສານຂອງສະຖາປັດຕະຍະກຳເປົ້າ"
"ໝາຍສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມ. ໃນຫຼາຍກໍລະນີ, mobile drivers ອາດຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດພຶດຕິກຳທີ່ບໍ່ຄົງທີ່, ດັ່ງນັ້ນຈຶ່ງເປັ"
"ນການດີທີ່ສຸດທີ່ຈະຫຼີກລ່ຽງການລະບຸຄວາມຊັດເຈນ ຍົກເວັ້ນໃນກໍລະນີທີ່ຈຳເປັນແທ້ໆ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:271
msgid "Arrays are containers for multiple variables of a similar type."
msgstr "Arrays ແມ່ນບ່ອນເກັບຕົວປ່ຽນຫຼາຍຕົວທີ່ມີປະເພດຄ້າຍຄືກັນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:274
msgid "Local arrays"
msgstr "Local arrays"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:276
msgid ""
"Local arrays are declared in functions. They can use all of the allowed "
"datatypes, except samplers. The array declaration follows a C-style syntax: "
"``[const] + [precision] + typename + identifier + [array size]``."
msgstr ""
"Local arrays ຖືກປະກາດໃນຟັງຊັນ. ພວກມັນສາມາດໃຊ້ປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນທີ່ອະນຸຍາດໄດ້ທັງໝົດ, ຍົກເວັ້ນ "
"samplers. ການປະກາດ array ຈະໃຊ້ຮູບແບບຄືກັບພາສາ C: ``[const] + [precision] + "
"typename + identifier + [array size]``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:286
msgid "They can be initialized at the beginning like:"
msgstr "ພວກມັນສາມາດຖືກຕັ້ງຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນໄດ້ຄື:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:298
msgid ""
"You can declare multiple arrays (even with different sizes) in one "
"expression:"
msgstr "ທ່ານສາມາດປະກາດຫຼາຍ arrays (ເຖິງແມ່ນຈະມີຂະໜາດຕ່າງກັນ) ໃນນິພົດດຽວ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:308
msgid "To access an array element, use the indexing syntax:"
msgstr "ເພື່ອເຂົ້າເຖິງອົງປະກອບຂອງ array, ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ຮູບແບບການໃສ່ດັດຊະນີ (indexing):"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:318
msgid ""
"Arrays also have a built-in function ``.length()`` (not to be confused with "
"the built-in ``length()`` function). It doesn't accept any parameters and "
"will return the array's size."
msgstr ""
"Arrays ຍັງມີຟັງຊັນ built-in ``.length()`` (ຢ່າສັບສົນກັບຟັງຊັນ built-in ``length()``). ມັ"
"ນບໍ່ຮັບ parameters ໃດໆ ແລະ ຈະສົ່ງຄືນຂະໜາດຂອງ array."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:331
msgid ""
"If you use an index either below 0 or greater than array size - the shader "
"will crash and break rendering. To prevent this, use ``length()``, ``if``, "
"or ``clamp()`` functions to ensure the index is between 0 and the array's "
"length. Always carefully test and check your code. If you pass a constant "
"expression or a number, the editor will check its bounds to prevent this "
"crash."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າທ່ານໃຊ້ດັດຊະນີທີ່ຕໍ່າກວ່າ 0 ຫຼື ໃຫຍ່ກວ່າຂະໜາດຂອງ array - shader ຈະຄ້າງ ແລະ ການ rendering "
"ຈະຢຸດເຮັດວຽກ. ເພື່ອປ້ອງກັນສິ່ງນີ້, ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ຟັງຊັນ ``length()``, ``if``, ຫຼື ``clamp()`` ເພື່ອຮັບປະ"
"ກັນວ່າດັດຊະນີຢູ່ລະຫວ່າງ 0 ຫາ ຄວາມຍາວຂອງ array. ໃຫ້ກວດສອບ ແລະ ທົດສອບໂຄ້ດຂອງທ່ານຢ່າງລະມັດລະວັ"
"ງສະເໝີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:339
msgid "Global arrays"
msgstr "Global arrays"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:341
msgid ""
"You can declare arrays in global space as either ``const`` or ``uniform``:"
msgstr ""
"ທ່ານສາມາດປະກາດ arrays ໃນ global space ໃຫ້ເປັນແບບ ``const`` ຫຼື ``uniform`` ໄດ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:356
msgid ""
"Global arrays use the same syntax as local arrays, except with a ``const`` "
"or ``uniform`` added to their declaration. Note that uniform arrays can't "
"have a default value."
msgstr ""
"Global arrays ໃຊ້ຮູບແບບດຽວກັນກັບ local arrays, ຍົກເວັ້ນແຕ່ມີການເພີ່ມ ``const`` ຫຼື "
"``uniform`` ເຂົ້າໃນການປະກາດ. ໝາຍເຫດວ່າ uniform arrays ບໍ່ສາມາດມີຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:363
msgid ""
"Use the ``const`` keyword before the variable declaration to make that "
"variable immutable, which means that it cannot be modified. All basic types, "
"except samplers can be declared as constants. Accessing and using a constant "
"value is slightly faster than using a uniform. Constants must be initialized "
"at their declaration."
msgstr ""
"ໃຊ້ຄຳສຳຄັນ ``const`` ກ່ອນການປະກາດຕົວປ່ຽນເພື່ອເຮັດໃຫ້ຕົວປ່ຽນນັ້ນບໍ່ສາມາດປ່ຽນແປງໄດ້ (immutable)"
". ປະເພດພື້ນຖານທັງໝົດ ຍົກເວັ້ນ samplers ສາມາດປະກາດເປັນ constants ໄດ້. ການເຂົ້າເຖິງ ແລະ ການ"
"ໃຊ້ຄ່າ constant ຈະໄວສກວ່າການໃຊ້ uniform ເລັກນ້ອຍ. Constants ຕ້ອງຖືກກຳນົດຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນໃນຕອນປະ"
"ກາດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:377
msgid ""
"Constants cannot be modified and additionally cannot have hints, but "
"multiple of them (if they have the same type) can be declared in a single "
"expression e.g"
msgstr ""
"Constants ບໍ່ສາມາດຖືກປ່ຽນແປງໄດ້ ແລະ ຍັງບໍ່ສາມາດມີ hints ໄດ້, ແຕ່ສາມາດປະກາດຫຼາຍຕົວ (ຖ້າພວກມັນ"
"ມີປະເພດດຽວກັນ) ໃນນິພົດດຽວໄດ້ ເຊັ່ນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:384
msgid "Similar to variables, arrays can also be declared with ``const``."
msgstr "ຄືກັນກັບຕົວປ່ຽນ, arrays ກໍສາມາດປະກາດດ້ວຍ ``const`` ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:394
msgid ""
"Constants can be declared both globally (outside of any function) or locally "
"(inside a function). Global constants are useful when you want to have "
"access to a value throughout your shader that does not need to be modified. "
"Like uniforms, global constants are shared between all shader stages, but "
"they are not accessible outside of the shader."
msgstr ""
"Constants ສາມາດປະກາດໄດ້ທັງແບບ global ຫຼື ແບບ local. Global constants ມີປະໂຫຍດເມື່ອທ່າ"
"ນຕ້ອງການເຂົ້າເຖິງຄ່າໃດໜຶ່ງຕະຫຼອດທັງ shader ໂດຍທີ່ຄ່ານັ້ນບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງມີການປ່ຽນແປງ. ຄືກັນກັບ "
"uniforms, global constants ຈະຖືກໃຊ້ຮ່ວມກັນລະຫວ່າງທຸກໆ shader stages, ແຕ່ພວກມັນບໍ່ສາມາດເ"
"ຂົ້າເຖິງໄດ້ຈາກພາຍນອກ shader."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:406
msgid ""
"Constants of the ``float`` type must be initialized using ``.`` notation "
"after the decimal part or by using the scientific notation. The optional "
"``f`` post-suffix is also supported."
msgstr ""
"Constants ປະເພດ ``float`` ຕ້ອງຖືກກຳນົດຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນໂດຍໃຊ້ເຄື່ອງໝາຍຈຸດ ``.`` ຫຼັງຈາກສ່ວນເລກທົດສ"
"ະນິຍົມ ຫຼື ໂດຍການໃຊ້ scientific notation. ນອກຈາກນີ້ຍັງຮອງຮັບການໃສ່ ``f`` ຕໍ່ທ້າຍນຳອີກ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:416
msgid ""
"Constants of the ``uint`` (unsigned int) type must have a ``u`` suffix to "
"differentiate them from signed integers. Alternatively, this can be done by "
"using the ``uint(x)`` built-in conversion function."
msgstr ""
"Constants ປະເພດ ``uint`` ຕ້ອງມີ ``u`` ຕໍ່ທ້າຍເພື່ອແຍກພວກມັນອອກຈາກເລກຖ້ວນແບບມີເຄື່ອງໝາຍ. ອີ"
"ກທາງເລືອກໜຶ່ງແມ່ນສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ໂດຍການໃຊ້ຟັງຊັນ built-in conversion ``uint(x)``."

