#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:551
#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shader_functions.rst:61
msgid ""
"The `GLSL Language Specification <http://www.opengl.org/registry/doc/"
"GLSLangSpec.4.30.6.pdf>`_ says under section 5.10 Vector and Matrix "
"Operations:"
msgstr ""
"`GLSL Language Specification <http://www.opengl.org/registry/doc/"
"GLSLangSpec.4.30.6.pdf>`_ ກ່າວໄວ້ໃນພາກສ່ວນ 5.10 Vector and Matrix Operations ວ່າ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:553
#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shader_functions.rst:63
msgid ""
"With a few exceptions, operations are component-wise. Usually, when an "
"operator operates on a vector or matrix, it is operating independently on "
"each component of the vector or matrix, in a component-wise fashion. [...] "
"The exceptions are matrix multiplied by vector, vector multiplied by matrix, "
"and matrix multiplied by matrix. These do not operate component-wise, but "
"rather perform the correct linear algebraic multiply."
msgstr ""
"ຍົກເວັ້ນບາງກໍລະນີ, ການປະຕິບັດການຈະເປັນແບບ component-wise. ໂດຍປົກກະຕິແລ້ວ, ເມື່ອຕົວດຳເນີນການເ"
"ຮັດວຽກກັບເວັກເຕີ ຫຼື ມາທຣິກ, ມັນຈະເຮັດວຽກຢ່າງເປັນເອກະລາດໃນແຕ່ລະອົງປະກອບນັ້ນໆ. [...] ຂໍ້ຍົກເວັ້ນ"
"ຄື: ມາທຣິກຄູນກັບເວັກເຕີ, ເວັກເຕີຄູນກັບມາທຣິກ, ແລະ ມາທຣິກຄູນກັບມາທຣິກ. ສິ່ງເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຈະບໍ່ເຮັດວຽກແບບ "
"component-wise, ແຕ່ຈະເຮັດການຄູນຕາມຫຼັກການຄະນິດສາດ linear algebraic ທີ່ຖືກຕ້ອງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:560
msgid "Flow control"
msgstr "ການຄວບຄຸມລຳດັບການເຮັດວຽກ (Flow control)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:562
msgid "Godot Shading language supports the most common types of flow control:"
msgstr ""
"Godot Shading language ຮອງຮັບການຄວບຄຸມລຳດັບການເຮັດວຽກປະເພດທີ່ໃຊ້ທົ່ວໄປທີ່ສຸດ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:613
msgid ""
"Keep in mind that in modern GPUs, an infinite loop can exist and can freeze "
"your application (including editor). Godot can't protect you from this, so "
"be careful not to make this mistake!"
msgstr ""
"ຂໍໃຫ້ຈື່ໄວ້ວ່າໃນ GPU ສະໄໝໃໝ່, loop ທີ່ບໍ່ມີວັນສິ້ນສຸດສາມາດເຮັດໃຫ້ແອັບພລິເຄຊັນຂອງທ່ານ (ລວມເຖິງ "
"editor) ຄ້າງໄດ້. Godot ບໍ່ສາມາດປ້ອງກັນທ່ານຈາກສິ່ງນີ້ໄດ້, ດັ່ງນັ້ນຈົ່ງລະມັດລະວັງ!"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:617
msgid ""
"Also, when comparing floating-point values against a number, make sure to "
"compare them against a *range* instead of an exact number."
msgstr ""
"ນອກຈາກນີ້, ເມື່ອປຽບທຽບຄ່າເລກທົດສະນິຍົມກັບຕົວເລກ, ໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າໄດ້ປຽບທຽບພວກມັນກັບ *ຊ່ວງ* (range) "
"ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນຕົວເລກທີ່ແນ່ນອນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:620
msgid ""
"A comparison like ``if (value == 0.3)`` may not evaluate to ``true``. "
"Floating-point math is often approximate and can defy expectations. It can "
"also behave differently depending on the hardware."
msgstr ""
"ການປຽບທຽບເຊັ່ນ ``if (value == 0.3)`` ອາດຈະບໍ່ສົ່ງຜົນເປັນ ``true``. ຄະນິດສາດເລກທົດສະນິຍົມມັ"
"ກຈະເປັນຄ່າປະມານ ແລະ ອາດຈະບໍ່ເປັນໄປຕາມທີ່ຄາດໄວ້. ມັນຍັງອາດຈະເຮັດວຽກແຕກຕ່າງກັນໄປຕາມຮາດແວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:624
msgid "**Don't** do this."
msgstr "**ຢ່າ** ເຮັດແບບນີ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:635
msgid ""
"Instead, always perform a range comparison with an epsilon value. The larger "
"the floating-point number (and the less precise the floating-point number), "
"the larger the epsilon value should be."
msgstr ""
"ແທນທີ່ຈະເຮັດແນວນັ້ນ, ໃຫ້ທຳການປຽບທຽບຊ່ວງດ້ວຍຄ່າ epsilon ສະເໝີ. ຍິ່ງເລກທົດສະນິຍົມມີຄ່າໃຫຍ່ເທົ່າໃດ, "
"ຄ່າ epsilon ກໍຄວນຈະໃຫຍ່ຂຶ້ນເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:646
msgid ""
"See `floating-point-gui.de <https://floating-point-gui.de/>`__ for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"ເບິ່ງ `floating-point-gui.de <https://floating-point-gui.de/>`__ ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:650
msgid "Discarding"
msgstr "ການຍົກເລີກ (Discarding)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:652
msgid ""
"Fragment, light, and custom functions (called from fragment or light) can "
"use the ``discard`` keyword. If used, the fragment is discarded and nothing "
"is written."
msgstr ""
"ຟັງຊັນ Fragment, light, ແລະ custom functions ສາມາດໃຊ້ຄຳສຳຄັນ ``discard`` ໄດ້. ຖ້າຖືກ"
"ໃຊ້, fragment ນັ້ນຈະຖືກຍົກເລີກ ແລະ ບໍ່ມີສິ່ງໃດຖືກຂຽນລົງໄປ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:655
msgid ""
"Beware that ``discard`` has a performance cost when used, as it will prevent "
"the depth prepass from being effective on any surfaces using the shader. "
"Also, a discarded pixel still needs to be rendered in the vertex shader, "
"which means a shader that uses ``discard`` on all of its pixels is still "
"more expensive to render compared to not rendering any object in the first "
"place."
msgstr ""
"ຈົ່ງລະວັງວ່າ ``discard`` ມີຄ່າໃຊ້ຈ່າຍທາງດ້ານປະສິດທິພາບເມື່ອຖືກໃຊ້. ນອກຈາກນີ້, ພິກເຊວທີ່ຖືກຍົກເລີກຍັງຄົ"
"ງຕ້ອງໄດ້ຮັບການ render ໃນ vertex shader, ເຊິ່ງໝາຍຄວາມວ່າ shader ທີ່ໃຊ້ ``discard`` ກັບທຸກ"
"ໆພິກເຊວຂອງມັນກໍຍັງມີຄ່າໃຊ້ຈ່າຍໃນການ render ທີ່ແພງກວ່າເມື່ອທຽບກັບການບໍ່ render ວັດຖຸໃດໆເລີຍແຕ່ທຳອິ"
"ດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:664
msgid ""
"It is possible to define functions in a Godot shader. They use the following "
"syntax:"
msgstr "ເຮົາສາມາດກຳນົດຟັງຊັນໃນ Godot shader ໄດ້. ພວກມັນຈະໃຊ້ຮູບແບບດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:680
msgid ""
"You can only use functions that have been defined above (higher in the "
"editor) the function from which you are calling them. Redefining a function "
"that has already been defined above (or is a built-in function name) will "
"cause an error."
msgstr ""
"ທ່ານສາມາດໃຊ້ໄດ້ສະເພາະຟັງຊັນທີ່ຖືກກຳນົດໄວ້ຂ້າງເທິງຂອງຟັງຊັນທີ່ທ່ານກຳລັງເອີ້ນໃຊ້ເທົ່ານັ້ນ. ການກຳນົດຟັງຊັນຊ້ຳ"
"ກັບຟັງຊັນທີ່ຖືກກຳນົດໄວ້ແລ້ວຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດຂໍ້ຜິດພາດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:684
msgid "Function arguments can have special qualifiers:"
msgstr "Arguments ຂອງຟັງຊັນສາມາດມີ qualifiers ພິເສດໄດ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:686
msgid "**in**: Means the argument is only for reading (default)."
msgstr "**in**: ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າ argument ແມ່ນສຳລັບການອ່ານເທົ່ານັ້ນ (ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:687
msgid "**out**: Means the argument is only for writing."
msgstr "**out**: ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າ argument ແມ່ນສຳລັບການຂຽນເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:688
msgid "**inout**: Means the argument is fully passed via reference."
msgstr "**inout**: ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າ argument ຈະຖືກສົ່ງຜ່ານແບບອ້າງອີງຢ່າງເຕັມຮູບແບບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:689
msgid ""
"**const**: Means the argument is a constant and cannot be changed, may be "
"combined with **in** qualifier."
msgstr "**const**: ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າ argument ແມ່ນຄ່າຄົງທີ່ ແລະ ບໍ່ສາມາດປ່ຽນແປງໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:692
msgid "Example below:"
msgstr "ຕົວຢ່າງລຸ່ມນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:700
msgid ""
"Function overloading is supported. You can define multiple functions with "
"the same name, but different arguments. Note that `implicit casting "
"<Casting_>`_ in overloaded function calls is not allowed, such as from "
"``int`` to ``float`` (``1`` to ``1.0``)."
msgstr ""
"ການເຮັດ Function overloading ແມ່ນຮອງຮັບ. ທ່ານສາມາດກຳນົດຫຼາຍຟັງຊັນທີ່ມີຊື່ດຽວກັນ ແຕ່ມີ "
"arguments ຕ່າງກັນໄດ້. ໝາຍເຫດວ່າ implicit casting ໃນການເອີ້ນໃຊ້ overloaded function ນັ້"
"ນແມ່ນບໍ່ອະນຸຍາດ, ເຊັ່ນຈາກ ``int`` ເປັນ ``float``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:720
#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_godot_shaders.rst:59
msgid "Varyings"
msgstr "Varyings"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:722
msgid ""
"To send data from the vertex to the fragment (or light) processor function, "
"*varyings* are used. They are set for every primitive vertex in the *vertex "
"processor*, and the value is interpolated for every pixel in the *fragment "
"processor*."
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອສົ່ງຂໍ້ມູນຈາກ vertex ໄປຫາ fragment (ຫຼື light) processor function, ເຮົາຈະໃຊ້ "
"*varyings*. ພວກມັນຈະຖືກຕັ້ງຄ່າສຳລັບທຸກໆ primitive vertex ໃນ *vertex processor*, ແລະ "
"ຄ່າຂອງພວກມັນຈະຖືກ interpolated ສຳລັບທຸກໆພິກເຊວໃນ *fragment processor*."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:744
msgid "Varying can also be an array:"
msgstr "Varying ຍັງສາມາດເປັນ array ໄດ້ນຳ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:761
msgid ""
"It's also possible to send data from *fragment* to *light* processors using "
"*varying* keyword. To do so you can assign it in the *fragment* and later "
"use it in the *light* function."
msgstr ""
"ນອກຈາກນີ້ຍັງສາມາດສົ່ງຂໍ້ມູນຈາກ *fragment* ໄປຫາ *light* processors ໄດ້ໂດຍການໃຊ້ຄຳສຳຄັນ "
"*varying*. ເພື່ອເຮັດແນວນັ້ນ ທ່ານສາມາດກຳນົດຄ່າໃຫ້ມັນໃນ *fragment* ແລະ ຈາກນັ້ນກໍນຳໄປໃຊ້ໃນຟັງຊັ"
"ນ *light* ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:777
msgid ""
"Note that varying may not be assigned in custom functions or a *light "
"processor* function like:"
msgstr ""
"ໝາຍເຫດວ່າ varying ອາດຈະບໍ່ສາມາດກຳນົດຄ່າໃນ custom functions ຫຼື ຟັງຊັນ *light "
"processor* ໄດ້ເຊັ່ນ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:797
msgid ""
"This limitation was introduced to prevent incorrect usage before "
"initialization."
msgstr ""
"ຂໍ້ຈຳກັດນີ້ຖືກນຳເຂົ້າມາເພື່ອປ້ອງກັນການໃຊ້ງານທີ່ບໍ່ຖືກຕ້ອງກ່ອນການຕັ້ງຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:800
msgid "Interpolation qualifiers"
msgstr "Interpolation qualifiers"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:802
msgid ""
"Certain values are interpolated during the shading pipeline. You can modify "
"how these interpolations are done by using *interpolation qualifiers*."
msgstr ""
"ບາງຄ່າຈະຖືກ interpolated ໃນລະຫວ່າງ shading pipeline. ທ່ານສາມາດປັບປ່ຽນວິທີການ "
"interpolations ເຫຼົ່ານີ້ໄດ້ໂດຍການໃຊ້ *interpolation qualifiers*."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:819
msgid "There are two possible interpolation qualifiers:"
msgstr "ມີ interpolation qualifiers ທີ່ເປັນໄປໄດ້ຢູ່ສອງຢ່າງ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:822
msgid "Qualifier"
msgstr "Qualifier"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:824
msgid "**flat**"
msgstr "**flat**"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:824
msgid "The value is not interpolated."
msgstr "ຄ່າຈະບໍ່ຖືກ interpolated."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:826
msgid "**smooth**"
msgstr "**smooth**"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:826
msgid ""
"The value is interpolated in a perspective-correct fashion. This is the "
"default."
msgstr ""
"ຄ່າຈະຖືກ interpolated ໃນຮູບແບບ perspective-correct. ນີ້ແມ່ນຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:832
#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/your_first_shader/your_first_3d_shader.rst:231
msgid "Uniforms"
msgstr "Uniforms"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:834
msgid ""
"Passing values to shaders is possible with *uniforms*, which are defined in "
"the global scope of the shader, outside of functions. When a shader is later "
"assigned to a material, the uniforms will appear as editable parameters in "
"the material's inspector. Uniforms can't be written from within the shader. "
"Any :ref:`data type <doc_shading_language_data_types>` except for ``void`` "
"can be a uniform."
msgstr ""
"ການສົ່ງຄ່າເຂົ້າໄປໃນ shaders ສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ດ້ວຍ *uniforms*, ເຊິ່ງຖືກກຳນົດໃນ global scope ຂອ"
"ງ shader, ນອກຟັງຊັນ. ເມື່ອ shader ຖືກນຳໄປໃຊ້ກັບ material, uniforms ຈະປາກົດເປັນ "
"parameters ທີ່ແກ້ໄຂໄດ້ໃນ inspector. Uniforms ບໍ່ສາມາດຖືກຂຽນຈາກພາຍໃນ shader ໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:848
msgid ""
"You can set uniforms in the editor in the material's inspector. Alternately, "
"you can set them :ref:`from code "
"<doc_shading_language_setting_uniforms_from_code>`."
msgstr ""
"ທ່ານສາມາດຕັ້ງຄ່າ uniforms ໃນ inspector. ຫຼື ອີກທາງເລືອກໜຶ່ງ, ທ່ານສາມາດຕັ້ງຄ່າພວກມັນ :ref:`ຈາ"
"ກໂຄ້ດ <doc_shading_language_setting_uniforms_from_code>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:852
msgid "Uniform hints"
msgstr "Uniform hints"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:854
msgid ""
"Godot provides optional uniform hints to make the compiler understand what "
"the uniform is used for, and how the editor should allow users to modify it."
msgstr ""
"Godot ມີ uniform hints ທີ່ເປັນທາງເລືອກເພື່ອຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ compiler ເຂົ້າໃຈວ່າ uniform ນັ້ນຖືກໃຊ້ເພື່ອຫ"
"ຍັງ, ແລະ editor ຄວນຈະອະນຸຍາດໃຫ້ຜູ້ໃຊ້ປັບປ່ຽນມັນແນວໃດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:866
msgid "Uniforms can also be assigned default values:"
msgstr "Uniforms ຍັງສາມາດຖືກກຳນົດຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນໄດ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:875
msgid ""
"Note that when adding a default value and a hint, the default value goes "
"after the hint."
msgstr "ໝາຍເຫດວ່າເມື່ອເພີ່ມຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ ແລະ hint, ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນຈະຢູ່ຖັດຈາກ hint."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:877
msgid "Full list of uniform hints below:"
msgstr "ລາຍການ Uniform hints ທັງໝົດຢູ່ລຸ່ມນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:880
msgid "Hint"
msgstr "Hint"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:882
msgid "**vec3, vec4**"
msgstr "**vec3, vec4**"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:882
#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:888
msgid "source_color"
msgstr "source_color"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:882
msgid "Used as color."
msgstr "ໃຊ້ເປັນສີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:884
msgid "hint_enum(\"String1\", \"String2\")"
msgstr "hint_enum(\"String1\", \"String2\")"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:884
msgid "Displays int input as a dropdown widget in the editor."
msgstr "ສະແດງ int input ເປັນ dropdown widget ໃນ editor."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:886
msgid "**int, float**"
msgstr "**int, float**"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:886
msgid "hint_range(min, max[, step])"
msgstr "hint_range(min, max[, step])"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:886
msgid "Restricted to values in a range (with min/max/step)."
msgstr "ຈຳກັດຄ່າໃນຊ່ວງໃດໜຶ່ງ (ມີ min/max/step)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:888
msgid "Used as albedo color."
msgstr "ໃຊ້ເປັນສີ albedo."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:890
msgid "hint_normal"
msgstr "hint_normal"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:890
msgid "Used as normalmap."
msgstr "ໃຊ້ເປັນ normalmap."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:892
msgid "hint_default_white"
msgstr "hint_default_white"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:892
msgid "As value or albedo color, default to opaque white."
msgstr "ເປັນຄ່າ ຫຼື ສີ albedo, ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນແມ່ນສີຂາວທີ່ທຶບແສງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:894
msgid "hint_default_black"
msgstr "hint_default_black"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:894
msgid "As value or albedo color, default to opaque black."
msgstr "ເປັນຄ່າ ຫຼື ສີ albedo, ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນແມ່ນສີດຳທີ່ທຶບແສງ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:896
msgid "hint_default_transparent"
msgstr "hint_default_transparent"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:896
msgid "As value or albedo color, default to transparent black."
msgstr "ເປັນຄ່າ ຫຼື ສີ albedo, ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນແມ່ນສີດຳທີ່ໂປ່ງໃສ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:898
msgid "hint_anisotropy"
msgstr "hint_anisotropy"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:898
msgid "As flowmap, default to right."
msgstr "ເປັນ flowmap, ຄ່າເລີ່ມຕົ້ນແມ່ນໄປທາງຂວາ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:900
msgid "hint_roughness[_r, _g, _b, _a, _normal, _gray]"
msgstr "hint_roughness[_r, _g, _b, _a, _normal, _gray]"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:900
msgid ""
"Used for roughness limiter on import (attempts reducing specular aliasing). "
"``_normal`` is a normal map that guides the roughness limiter, with "
"roughness increasing in areas that have high-frequency detail."
msgstr ""
"ໃຊ້ສຳລັບ roughness limiter ໃນຕອນ import. ``_normal`` ແມ່ນ normal map ທີ່ຊ່ວຍກຳນົດ "
"roughness limiter, ໂດຍ roughness ຈະເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນໃນບໍລິເວນທີ່ມີລາຍລະອຽດຄວາມຖີ່ສູງ."

