"You can access ``int`` values as a readable dropdown widget using the "
"``hint_enum`` uniform:"
msgstr ""
"ທ່ານສາມາດເຂົ້າເຖິງຄ່າ ``int`` ໃນຮູບແບບ dropdown widget ທີ່ອ່ານງ່າຍໂດຍການໃຊ້ "
"``hint_enum`` uniform:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:924
msgid ""
"You can assign explicit values to the ``hint_enum`` uniform using colon "
"syntax similar to GDScript:"
msgstr ""
"ທ່ານສາມາດກຳນົດຄ່າທີ່ຊັດເຈນໃຫ້ກັບ ``hint_enum`` uniform ໄດ້ໂດຍການໃຊ້ colon syntax ຄ້າຍຄືກັບ"
"ໃນ GDScript:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:930
msgid ""
"The value will be stored as an integer, corresponding to the index of the "
"selected option (i.e. ``0``, ``1``, or ``2``) or the value assigned by colon "
"syntax (i.e. ``30``, ``60``, or ``200``). When setting the value with "
"``set_shader_parameter()``, you must use the integer value, not the "
"``String`` name."
msgstr ""
"ຄ່າຈະຖືກເກັບເປັນເລກຖ້ວນ, ເຊິ່ງກົງກັບດັດຊະນີຂອງຕົວເລືອກທີ່ຖືກເລືອກ ຫຼື ຄ່າທີ່ຖືກກຳນົດໂດຍ colon "
"syntax. ເມື່ອຕັ້ງຄ່າດ້ວຍ ``set_shader_parameter()``, ທ່ານຕ້ອງໃຊ້ຄ່າເລກຖ້ວນ, ບໍ່ແມ່ນຊື່ "
"``String``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:937
msgid "Using ``source_color``"
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ ``source_color``"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:939
msgid ""
"Any texture which contains *sRGB color data* requires a ``source_color`` "
"hint in order to be correctly sampled. This is because Godot renders in "
"linear color space, but some textures contain sRGB color data. If this hint "
"is not used, the texture will appear washed out."
msgstr ""
"Texture ໃດໆກໍຕາມທີ່ມີ *sRGB color data* ຈະຕ້ອງມີ ``source_color`` hint ເພື່ອໃຫ້ສາມາດສຸ່ມ"
"ຕົວຢ່າງໄດ້ຢ່າງຖືກຕ້ອງ. ສິ່ງນີ້ເປັນເພາະວ່າ Godot ທຳການ render ໃນ linear color space, ແຕ່ "
"textures ບາງອັນມີຂໍ້ມູນສີແບບ sRGB. ຖ້າບໍ່ໃຊ້ hint ນີ້, texture ຈະປາກົດເປັນສີຈືດໆ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:944
msgid ""
"Albedo and color textures should typically have a ``source_color`` hint. "
"Normal, roughness, metallic, and height textures typically do not need a "
"``source_color`` hint."
msgstr ""
"Albedo ແລະ color textures ປົກກະຕິແລ້ວຄວນຈະມີ ``source_color`` hint. ສ່ວນ Normal, "
"roughness, metallic, ແລະ height textures ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປແລ້ວແມ່ນບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງມີ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:948
msgid ""
"Using ``source_color`` hint is required in the Forward+ and Mobile "
"renderers, and in ``canvas_item`` shaders when :ref:`HDR "
"2D<class_ProjectSettings_property_rendering/viewport/hdr_2d>` is enabled. "
"The ``source_color`` hint is optional for the Compatibility renderer, and "
"for ``canvas_item`` shaders if ``HDR 2D`` is disabled. However, it is "
"recommended to always use the ``source_color`` hint, because it works even "
"if you change renderers or disable ``HDR 2D``."
msgstr ""
"ການໃຊ້ ``source_color`` hint ແມ່ນຈຳເປັນໃນ Forward+ ແລະ Mobile renderers. ເຖິງຢ່າງໃ"
"ດກໍຕາມ, ແນະນຳໃຫ້ໃຊ້ ``source_color`` hint ສະເໝີ ເພາະວ່າມັນຈະເຮັດວຽກໄດ້ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າທ່ານຈະປ່ຽ"
"ນ renderers ກໍຕາມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:956
msgid "Uniform groups"
msgstr "ກຸ່ມຂອງ Uniform (Uniform groups)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:958
msgid ""
"To group multiple uniforms in a section in the inspector, you can use a "
"``group_uniform`` keyword like this:"
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອຈັດກຸ່ມຂອງ uniforms ຫຼາຍອັນເຂົ້າໃນສ່ວນດຽວກັນໃນ inspector, ທ່ານສາມາດໃຊ້ຄຳສຳຄັນ "
"``group_uniform`` ໄດ້ດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:966
msgid "You can close the group by using:"
msgstr "ທ່ານສາມາດປິດກຸ່ມໄດ້ໂດຍການໃຊ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:972
msgid ""
"The syntax also supports subgroups (it's not mandatory to declare the base "
"group before this):"
msgstr "ຮູບແບບນີ້ຍັງຮອງຮັບ subgroups (ບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງປະກາດ base group ກ່ອນ):"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:981
msgid "Global uniforms"
msgstr "Global uniforms"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:983
msgid ""
"Sometimes, you want to modify a parameter in many different shaders at once. "
"With a regular uniform, this takes a lot of work as all these shaders need "
"to be tracked and the uniform needs to be set for each of them. Global "
"uniforms allow you to create and update uniforms that will be available in "
"all shaders, in every shader type (``canvas_item``, ``spatial``, "
"``particles``, ``sky`` and ``fog``)."
msgstr ""
"ບາງຄັ້ງ, ທ່ານຕ້ອງການປ່ຽນແປງ parameter ໃນຫຼາຍໆ shaders ພ້ອມກັນ. Global uniforms ຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ທ່"
"ານສາມາດສ້າງ ແລະ ອັບເດດ uniforms ທີ່ຈະມີໃຫ້ໃຊ້ໃນທຸກໆ shaders, ໃນທຸກໆ shader type."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:990
msgid ""
"Global uniforms are especially useful for environmental effects that affect "
"many objects in a scene, like having foliage bend when the player is nearby, "
"or having objects move with the wind."
msgstr ""
"Global uniforms ມີປະໂຫຍດຫຼາຍສຳລັບເອຟເຟັກສິ່ງແວດລ້ອມທີ່ສົ່ງຜົນຕໍ່ຫຼາຍວັດຖຸໃນສາກ, ເຊັ່ນ: ການເຮັດໃຫ້ໃ"
"ບໄມ້ເໜັງຕີງເມື່ອຜູ້ຫຼິ້ນຢູ່ໃກ້ໆ, ຫຼື ການເຮັດໃຫ້ວັດຖຸເຄື່ອນໄຫວຕາມລົມ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:994
msgid ""
"*Global uniforms* are not the same as *global scope* for an individual "
"shader. While regular uniforms are defined outside of shader functions and "
"are therefore the global scope of the shader, global uniforms are global to "
"all shaders in the entire project (but within each shader, are also in the "
"global scope)."
msgstr ""
"*Global uniforms* ບໍ່ແມ່ນສິ່ງດຽວກັນກັບ *global scope* ສຳລັບ shader ແຕ່ລະອັນ. Global "
"uniforms ແມ່ນເປັນ global ສຳລັບທຸກໆ shaders ໃນໂປຣເຈັກທັງໝົດ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1000
msgid ""
"To create a global uniform, open the **Project Settings** then go to the "
"**Shader Globals** tab. Specify a name for the uniform (case-sensitive) and "
"a type, then click **Add** in the top-right corner of the dialog. You can "
"then edit the value assigned to the uniform by clicking the value in the "
"list of uniforms:"
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອສ້າງ global uniform, ໃຫ້ເປີດ **Project Settings** ຈາກນັ້ນໄປທີ່ແຖບ **Shader "
"Globals**. ລະບຸຊື່ສຳລັບ uniform ແລະ ປະເພດ, ຈາກນັ້ນກົດ **Add**. ທ່ານສາມາດແກ້ໄຂຄ່າໄດ້ໂດຍກາ"
"ນກົດທີ່ຄ່າໃນລາຍການ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1006
#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1010
msgid ""
"Adding a global uniform in the Shader Globals tab of the Project Settings"
msgstr "ການເພີ່ມ global uniform ໃນແຖບ Shader Globals ຂອງ Project Settings"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1012
msgid "After creating a global uniform, you can use it in a shader as follows:"
msgstr "ຫຼັງຈາກສ້າງ global uniform ແລ້ວ, ທ່ານສາມາດໃຊ້ມັນໃນ shader ໄດ້ດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1024
msgid ""
"Note that the global uniform *must* exist in the Project Settings at the "
"time the shader is saved, or compilation will fail. While you can assign a "
"default value using ``global uniform vec4 my_color = ...`` in the shader "
"code, it will be ignored as the global uniform must always be defined in the "
"Project Settings anyway."
msgstr ""
"ໝາຍເຫດວ່າ global uniform *ຕ້ອງ* ມີຢູ່ໃນ Project Settings ໃນເວລາທີ່ shader ຖືກບັນທຶກ, ຖ້າ"
"ບໍ່ດັ່ງນັ້ນການ compilation ຈະລົ້ມເຫຼວ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1030
msgid ""
"To change the value of a global uniform at runtime, use "
"the :ref:`RenderingServer.global_shader_parameter_set "
"<class_RenderingServer_method_global_shader_parameter_set>` method in a "
"script:"
msgstr ""
"ເພື່ອປ່ຽນຄ່າຂອງ global uniform ໃນລະຫວ່າງ runtime, ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ວິທີ "
":ref:`RenderingServer.global_shader_parameter_set "
"<class_RenderingServer_method_global_shader_parameter_set>` ໃນ script:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1038
msgid ""
"Assigning global uniform values can be done as many times as desired without "
"impacting performance, as setting data doesn't require synchronization "
"between the CPU and GPU."
msgstr ""
"ການກຳນົດຄ່າ global uniform ສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ຫຼາຍຄັ້ງຕາມທີ່ຕ້ອງການໂດຍບໍ່ສົ່ງຜົນກະທົບຕໍ່ປະສິດທິພາບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1042
msgid "You can also add or remove global uniforms at runtime:"
msgstr "ທ່ານຍັງສາມາດເພີ່ມ ຫຼື ລົບ global uniforms ໃນລະຫວ່າງ runtime ໄດ້ນຳ:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1049
msgid ""
"Adding or removing global uniforms at runtime has a performance cost, "
"although it's not as pronounced compared to getting global uniform values "
"from a script (see the warning below)."
msgstr ""
"ການເພີ່ມ ຫຼື ລົບ global uniforms ໃນລະຫວ່າງ runtime ມີຄ່າໃຊ້ຈ່າຍທາງດ້ານປະສິດທິພາບ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1055
msgid ""
"While you *can* query the value of a global uniform at runtime in a script "
"using ``RenderingServer.global_shader_parameter_get(\"uniform_name\")``, "
"this has a large performance penalty as the rendering thread needs to "
"synchronize with the calling thread."
msgstr ""
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າທ່ານ *ສາມາດ* ສອບຖາມຄ່າຂອງ global uniform ໃນລະຫວ່າງ runtime ໃນ script, ແຕ່"
"ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະສົ່ງຜົນກະທົບຕໍ່ປະສິດທິພາບຢ່າງຫຼວງຫຼາຍ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1060
msgid ""
"Therefore, it's not recommended to read global shader uniform values "
"continuously in a script. If you need to read values in a script after "
"setting them, consider creating an :ref:`autoload <doc_singletons_autoload>` "
"where you store the values you need to query at the same time you're setting "
"them as global uniforms."
msgstr ""
"ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ຈຶ່ງບໍ່ແນະນຳໃຫ້ອ່ານຄ່າ global shader uniform ຢ່າງຕໍ່ເນື່ອງໃນ script."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1069
msgid "Per-instance uniforms"
msgstr "Per-instance uniforms"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1073
msgid ""
"Per-instance uniforms are available in both ``canvas_item`` (2D) and "
"``spatial`` (3D) shaders."
msgstr ""
"Per-instance uniforms ມີໃຫ້ໃຊ້ທັງໃນ ``canvas_item`` (2D) ແລະ ``spatial`` (3D) "
"shaders."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1075
msgid ""
"Sometimes, you want to modify a parameter on each node using the material. "
"As an example, in a forest full of trees, when you want each tree to have a "
"slightly different color that is editable by hand. Without per-instance "
"uniforms, this requires creating a unique material for each tree (each with "
"a slightly different hue). This makes material management more complex, and "
"also has a performance overhead due to the scene requiring more unique "
"material instances. Vertex colors could also be used here, but they'd "
"require creating unique copies of the mesh for each different color, which "
"also has a performance overhead."
msgstr ""
"ບາງຄັ້ງ, ທ່ານຕ້ອງການປ່ຽນແປງ parameter ໃນແຕ່ລະ node ທີ່ໃຊ້ material ນັ້ນໆ. ຕົວຢ່າງ: ໃນປ່າທີ່ມີຕົ້"
"ນໄມ້ເຕັມໄປໝົດ, ເມື່ອທ່ານຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ຕົ້ນໄມ້ແຕ່ລະຕົ້ນມີສີທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນເລັກນ້ອຍ. ຖ້າບໍ່ມີ per-instance "
"uniforms, ສິ່ງນີ້ຈະຕ້ອງມີການສ້າງ material ທີ່ເປັນເອກະລັກສຳລັບຕົ້ນໄມ້ແຕ່ລະຕົ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1084
msgid ""
"Per-instance uniforms are set on each GeometryInstance3D, rather than on "
"each Material instance. Take this into account when working with meshes that "
"have multiple materials assigned to them, or MultiMesh setups."
msgstr ""
"Per-instance uniforms ຈະຖືກຕັ້ງຄ່າໃນແຕ່ລະ GeometryInstance3D, ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນໃນແຕ່ລະ "
"Material instance."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1100
msgid ""
"After saving the shader, you can change the per-instance uniform's value "
"using the inspector:"
msgstr ""
"ຫຼັງຈາກບັນທຶກ shader ແລ້ວ, ທ່ານສາມາດປ່ຽນຄ່າຂອງ per-instance uniform ໄດ້ໂດຍການໃຊ້ "
"inspector:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1103
#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1107
