msgstr ""
"Godot ມີມາໂຄຣຈັດການຂໍ້ຜິດພາດຫຼາຍຢ່າງເພື່ອໃຫ້ການລາຍງານຂໍ້ຜິດພາດສະດວກຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/common_engine_methods_and_macros.rst:194
msgid ""
"Conditions in error macros work in the **opposite** way of GDScript's built-"
"in ``assert()`` function. An error is reached if the condition inside "
"evaluates to ``true``, not ``false``."
msgstr ""
"ເງື່ອນໄຂໃນມາໂຄຣຈັດການຂໍ້ຜິດພາດຈະເຮັດວຽກ **ກົງກັນຂ້າມ** ກັບຟັງຊັນ ``assert()`` ຂອງ "
"GDScript. ຂໍ້ຜິດພາດຈະເກີດຂຶ້ນຫາກເງື່ອນໄຂພາຍໃນເປັນ ``true``, ບໍ່ແມ່ນ ``false``."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/common_engine_methods_and_macros.rst:200
msgid ""
"Only variants with custom messages are documented here, as these should "
"always be used in new contributions. Make sure the custom message provided "
"includes enough information for people to diagnose the issue, even if they "
"don't know C++. In case a method was passed invalid arguments, you can print "
"the invalid value in question to ease debugging."
msgstr ""
"ສະເພາະແບບທີ່ມີຂໍ້ຄວາມທີ່ກຳນົດເອງເທົ່ານັ້ນທີ່ຈະຖືກອະທິບາຍຢູ່ທີ່ນີ້, ເພາະມັນຄວນຈະຖືກໃຊ້ສະເໝີໃນການພັດທະນາໃ"
"ໝ່. ໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າຂໍ້ຄວາມທີ່ກຳນົດເອງນັ້ນມີຂໍ້ມູນພຽງພໍໃຫ້ຄົນອື່ນວິເຄາະຫາສາເຫດໄດ້ ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າພວກເຂົາຈະບໍ່ຮູ້ "
"C++ ກໍຕາມ. ໃນກໍລະນີທີ່ເມັດທອດໄດ້ຮັບອາຣ໌ກິວເມັນ (argument) ທີ່ບໍ່ຖືກຕ້ອງ, ເຈົ້າສາມາດສະແດງຄ່າທີ່ບໍ່ຖືກຕ້ອ"
"ງນັ້ນອອກມາເພື່ອໃຫ້ການດີບັກ (debug) ງ່າຍຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/common_engine_methods_and_macros.rst:206
msgid ""
"For internal error checking where displaying a human-readable message isn't "
"necessary, remove ``_MSG`` at the end of the macro name and don't supply a "
"message argument."
msgstr ""
"ສຳລັບການກວດສອບຂໍ້ຜິດພາດພາຍໃນທີ່ບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງສະແດງຂໍ້ຄວາມໃຫ້ຄົນອ່ານ, ໃຫ້ລຶບ ``_MSG`` ອອກຈາກທ້າຍຊື່"
"ມາໂຄຣ ແລະ ບໍ່ຕ້ອງໃສ່ອາຣ໌ກິວເມັນຂໍ້ຄວາມ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/common_engine_methods_and_macros.rst:210
msgid ""
"Also, always try to return processable data so the engine can keep running "
"well."
msgstr ""
"ນອກຈາກນັ້ນ, ພະຍາຍາມສົ່ງຂໍ້ມູນທີ່ສາມາດປະມວນຜົນໄດ້ຄືນສະເໝີ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ເອັນຈິນສາມາດເຮັດວຽກຕໍ່ໄປໄດ້ຢ່າງປົກກະ"
"ຕິ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/common_engine_methods_and_macros.rst:254
msgid ""
"See `core/error/error_macros.h <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/"
"master/core/error/error_macros.h>`__ in Godot's codebase for more "
"information about each error macro."
msgstr ""
"ເບິ່ງ `core/error/error_macros.h <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/"
"master/core/error/error_macros.h>`__ ໃນຊອດໂຄ້ດຂອງ Godot ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບແຕ່ລະ"
"ມາໂຄຣ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/common_engine_methods_and_macros.rst:257
msgid ""
"Some functions return an error code (materialized by a return type of "
"``Error``). This value can be returned directly from an error macro. See the "
"list of available error codes in `core/error/error_list.h <https://"
"github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/error/error_list.h>`__."
msgstr ""
"ບາງຟັງຊັນຈະສົ່ງລະຫັດຂໍ້ຜິດພາດຄືນມາ (ໂດຍມີປະເພດການສົ່ງຄ່າເປັນ ``Error``). ຄ່ານີ້ສາມາດຖືກສົ່ງຄືນໄດ້ໂດ"
"ຍກົງຈາກມາໂຄຣຂໍ້ຜິດພາດ. ເບິ່ງລາຍການລະຫັດຂໍ້ຜິດພາດທີ່ມີໄດ້ທີ່ `core/error/error_list.h "
"<https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/error/error_list.h>"
"`__."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:6
msgid ""
"Godot has a rich set of classes and templates that compose its core, and "
"everything is built upon them."
msgstr ""
"Godot ມີຄລາດ (classes) ແລະ ເທັມເພລດ (templates) ທີ່ຫຼາກຫຼາຍເຊິ່ງປະກອບເປັນສ່ວນຫຼັກ (core)"
", ແລະ ທຸກຢ່າງແມ່ນຖືກສ້າງຂຶ້ນມາຈາກສິ່ງເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:9
msgid ""
"This reference will try to list them in order for their better understanding."
msgstr ""
"ຄູ່ມືນີ້ຈະພະຍາຍາມລາຍຊື່ສິ່ງເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນຕາມລຳດັບເພື່ອໃຫ້ເຂົ້າໃຈໄດ້ງ່າຍຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:13
msgid "Allocating memory"
msgstr "ການຈອງໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳ (Allocating memory)"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:15
msgid ""
"Godot has many tricks for ensuring memory safety and tracking memory usage. "
"Because of this, the regular C and C++ library calls should not be used. "
"Instead, a few replacements are provided."
msgstr ""
"Godot ມີວິທີການຫຼາຍຢ່າງເພື່ອຮັບປະກັນຄວາມປອດໄພຂອງໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳ ແລະ ການຕິດຕາມການໃຊ້ງານ. ດ້ວຍເຫດ"
"ນີ້, ຈຶ່ງບໍ່ຄວນໃຊ້ການເອີ້ນໃຊ້ໄລບຣາຣີ C ແລະ C++ ແບບທົ່ວໄປ, ແຕ່ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ສິ່ງທົດແທນທີ່ກຳນົດມາໃຫ້ແທນ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:19
msgid "For C-style allocation, Godot provides a few macros:"
msgstr "ສຳລັບການຈອງໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳແບບ C, Godot ມີມາໂຄຣໃຫ້ດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:27
msgid ""
"These are equivalent to the usual ``malloc()``, ``realloc()``, and "
"``free()`` of the C standard library."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງເຫຼົ່ານີ້ທຽບເທົ່າກັບ ``malloc()``, ``realloc()``, ແລະ ``free()`` ຂອງໄລບຣາຣີມາດຕະຖານ "
"C ທົ່ວໄປ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:30
msgid "For C++-style allocation, special macros are provided:"
msgstr "ສຳລັບການຈອງໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳແບບ C++, ມີມາໂຄຣພິເສດໃຫ້ດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:41
msgid ""
"These are equivalent to ``new``, ``delete``, ``new[]``, and ``delete[]`` "
"respectively."
msgstr ""
"ສິ່ງເຫຼົ່ານີ້ທຽບເທົ່າກັບ ``new``, ``delete``, ``new[]``, ແລະ ``delete[]`` ຕາມລຳດັບ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:44
msgid ""
"``memnew``/``memdelete`` also use a little C++ magic to automatically call "
"post-init and pre-release functions. For example, this is used to notify "
"Objects right after they are created, and right before they are deleted."
msgstr ""
"``memnew``/``memdelete`` ຍັງໃຊ້ຄວາມສາມາດຂອງ C++ ເພື່ອເອີ້ນໃຊ້ຟັງຊັນຫຼັງການສ້າງ (post-"
"init) ແລະ ກ່ອນການປ່ອຍ (pre-release) ໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ. ຕົວຢ່າງ: ສິ່ງນີ້ໃຊ້ເພື່ອແຈ້ງເຕືອນ Object "
"ທັນທີຫຼັງຈາກທີ່ພວກມັນຖືກສ້າງ ແລະ ກ່ອນທີ່ຈະຖືກລຶບ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:48
msgid ""
"`core/os/memory.h <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/os/"
"memory.h>`__"
msgstr ""
"`core/os/memory.h <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/os/"
"memory.h>`__"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:51
msgid "Containers"
msgstr "ຄອນເທນເນີ (Containers)"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:53
msgid ""
"Godot provides its own set of containers, which means STL containers like "
"``std::string`` and ``std::vector`` are generally not used in the codebase. "
"See :ref:`doc_faq_why_not_stl` for more information."
msgstr ""
"Godot ມີຊຸດຄອນເທນເນີຂອງຕົນເອງ, ເຊິ່ງໝາຍຄວາມວ່າຄອນເທນເນີ STL ເຊັ່ນ ``std::string`` ແລະ "
"``std::vector`` ຈະບໍ່ຖືກໃຊ້ໃນຊອດໂຄ້ດໂດຍທົ່ວໄປ. ເບິ່ງ :ref:`doc_faq_why_not_stl` ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູ"
"ນເພີ່ມເຕີມ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:56
msgid ""
"A 📜 icon denotes the type is part of :ref:`Variant <doc_variant_class>`. "
"This means it can be used as a parameter or return value of a method exposed "
"to the scripting API."
msgstr ""
"ໄອຄອນ 📜 ໝາຍເຖິງປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນນັ້ນເປັນສ່ວນໜຶ່ງຂອງ :ref:`Variant <doc_variant_class>`. ນັ້ນໝາ"
"ຍຄວາມວ່າມັນສາມາດໃຊ້ເປັນພາຣາມິເຕີ (parameter) ຫຼື ຄ່າສົ່ງຄືນຂອງເມັດທອດທີ່ສະແດງໃຫ້ Scripting "
"API ເຫັນໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:61
#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:185
msgid "Godot datatype"
msgstr "ປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນ Godot"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:61
#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:185
msgid "Closest C++ STL datatype"
msgstr "ປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນ C++ STL ທີ່ໃກ້ຄຽງທີ່ສຸດ"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:63
msgid "|string| 📜"
msgstr "|string| 📜"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:63
#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:76
msgid "``std::string``"
msgstr "``std::string``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:63
msgid ""
"**Use this as the \"default\" string type.** ``String`` uses UTF-32 encoding "
"to simplify processing thanks to its fixed character size."
msgstr ""
"**ໃຊ້ສິ່ງນີ້ເປັນປະເພດຂໍ້ຄວາມ (string) ມາດຕະຖານ.** ``String`` ໃຊ້ການເຂົ້າລະຫັດ UTF-32 ເພື່ອໃ"
"ຫ້ການປະມວນຜົນງ່າຍຂຶ້ນຍ້ອນຂະໜາດຕົວອັກສອນທີ່ຄົງທີ່."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:66
#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:79
#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:83
#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:87
#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:90
msgid "``std::vector``"
msgstr "``std::vector``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:66
msgid ""
"**Use this as the \"default\" vector type.** Uses copy-on-write (COW) "
"semantics. This means it's generally slower but can be copied around almost "
"for free. Use ``LocalVector`` instead where COW isn't needed and performance "
"matters."
msgstr ""
"**ໃຊ້ສິ່ງນີ້ເປັນປະເພດ vector ມາດຕະຖານ.** ມັນໃຊ້ຫຼັກການ copy-on-write (COW). ນັ້ນໝາຍຄວາມວ່າ"
"ມັນຈະຊ້າກວ່າ ແຕ່ສາມາດກັອບປີ້ໄດ້ເກືອບບໍ່ມີຄ່າໃຊ້ຈ່າຍ. ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ ``LocalVector`` ແທນໃນບ່ອນທີ່ບໍ່ຕ້ອງການ "
"COW ແລະ ເນັ້ນເລື່ອງປະສິດທິພາບ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:70
msgid "|hash_set|"
msgstr "|hash_set|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:70
msgid "``std::unordered_set``"
msgstr "``std::unordered_set``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:70
msgid "**Use this as the \"default\" set type.**"
msgstr "**ໃຊ້ສິ່ງນີ້ເປັນປະເພດ set ມາດຕະຖານ.**"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:72
msgid "|a_hash_map|"
msgstr "|a_hash_map|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:72
#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:114
#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:123
#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:127
msgid "``std::unordered_map``"
msgstr "``std::unordered_map``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:72
msgid ""
"**Use this as the \"default\" map type.** Does not preserve insertion order. "
"Note that pointers into the map, as well as iterators, are not stable under "
"mutations. If either of these affordances are needed, use ``HashMap`` "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"**ໃຊ້ສິ່ງນີ້ເປັນປະເພດ map ມາດຕະຖານ.** ມັນບໍ່ຮັກສາລຳດັບການນຳເຂົ້າ. ໃຫ້ລະວັງວ່າພອຍເຕີ "
"(pointers) ແລະ ອິດເຕີເຣເຕີ (iterators) ພາຍໃນ map ຈະບໍ່ຄົງທີ່ຫາກມີການປ່ຽນແປງຂໍ້ມູນ. ຖ້າຕ້ອງກາ"
"ນສິ່ງເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນ, ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ ``HashMap`` ແທນ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:76
msgid "|string_name| 📜"
msgstr "|string_name| 📜"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:76
msgid ""
"Uses string interning for fast comparisons. Use this for static strings that "
"are referenced frequently and used in multiple locations in the engine."
msgstr ""
"ໃຊ້ລະບົບ string interning ເພື່ອການປຽບທຽບທີ່ໄວ. ໃຊ້ສິ່ງນີ້ສຳລັບຂໍ້ຄວາມຄົງທີ່ (static strings) ທີ່"
"ມີການອ້າງອີງເລື້ອຍໆ ແລະ ຖືກໃຊ້ໃນຫຼາຍບ່ອນໃນເອັນຈິນ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:79
msgid "|local_vector|"
msgstr "|local_vector|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:79
msgid ""
"Closer to ``std::vector`` in semantics, doesn't use copy-on-write (COW) thus "
"it's faster than ``Vector``. Prefer it over ``Vector`` when copying it "
"cheaply is not needed."
msgstr ""
"ມີຫຼັກການເຮັດວຽກໃກ້ຄຽງກັບ ``std::vector``, ບໍ່ໃຊ້ copy-on-write (COW) ຈຶ່ງເຮັດໃຫ້ມັນໄວກວ່າ "
"``Vector``. ຄວນໃຊ້ສິ່ງນີ້ແທນ ``Vector`` ເມື່ອບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງກັອບປີ້ຂໍ້ມູນແບບລາຄາຖືກ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:83
msgid "|array| 📜"
msgstr "|array| 📜"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:83
msgid ""
"Values can be of any Variant type. No static typing is imposed. Uses shared "
"reference counting, similar to ``std::shared_ptr``. Uses Vector<Variant> "
"internally."
msgstr ""
"ຄ່າສາມາດເປັນປະເພດ Variant ໃດກໍໄດ້. ບໍ່ມີການກຳນົດປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນຄົງທີ່. ໃຊ້ລະບົບການນັບການອ້າງອີງຮ່ວມກັ"
"ນ (shared reference counting) ຄ້າຍຄືກັບ ``std::shared_ptr``. ພາຍໃນແມ່ນໃຊ້ "
"Vector<Variant>."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:87
msgid "|typed_array| 📜"
msgstr "|typed_array| 📜"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:87
msgid ""
"Subclass of ``Array`` but with static typing for its elements. Not to be "
"confused with ``Packed*Array``, which is internally a ``Vector``."
msgstr ""
"ເປັນຄລາດຍ່ອຍຂອງ ``Array`` ແຕ່ມີການກຳນົດປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນຄົງທີ່ສຳລັບອົງປະກອບພາຍໃນ. ບໍ່ຄວນສັບສົນກັບ "
"``Packed*Array`` ເຊິ່ງພາຍໃນແມ່ນ ``Vector``."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:90
msgid "|packed_array| 📜"
msgstr "|packed_array| 📜"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:90
msgid ""
"Alias of ``Vector``, e.g. ``PackedColorArray = Vector<Color>``. Only a "
"limited list of packed array types are available (use ``TypedArray`` "
"otherwise)."
msgstr ""
"ເປັນຊື່ເອີ້ນ (Alias) ຂອງ ``Vector``, ເຊັ່ນ ``PackedColorArray = Vector<Color>``. ມີພຽ"
"ງບາງປະເພດຂອງ packed array ເທົ່ານັ້ນທີ່ມີໃຫ້ໃຊ້ (ຖ້າບໍ່ດັ່ງນັ້ນໃຫ້ໃຊ້ ``TypedArray``)."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:94
msgid "|list|"
msgstr "|list|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:94
msgid "``std::list``"
msgstr "``std::list``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:94
msgid ""
"Linked list type. Generally slower than other array/vector types. Prefer "
"using other types in new code, unless using ``List`` avoids the need for "
"type conversions."
msgstr ""
"ເປັນປະເພດ linked list. ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປຈະຊ້າກວ່າອາເຣ (array) ຫຼື ເວັກເຕີ (vector) ປະເພດອື່ນ. ຄວ"
"ນໃຊ້ປະເພດອື່ນໃນໂຄ້ດໃໝ່, ເວັ້ນເສຍແຕ່ວ່າການໃຊ້ ``List`` ຈະຊ່ວຍຫຼີກເວັ້ນການປ່ຽນປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:97
msgid "|fixed_vector|"
msgstr "|fixed_vector|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:97
msgid "``std::array``"
msgstr "``std::array``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:97
msgid ""
"Vector with a fixed capacity (more similar to "
"``boost::container::static_vector``). This container type is more efficient "
"than other vector-like types because it makes no heap allocations."
msgstr ""
"ເປັນ Vector ທີ່ມີຄວາມຈຸຄົງທີ່ (ໃກ້ຄຽງກັບ ``boost::container::static_vector``). ຄອນເທນເນີ"
"ປະເພດນີ້ມີປະສິດທິພາບຫຼາຍກວ່າປະເພດອື່ນໆ ເພາະມັນບໍ່ມີການຈອງໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳໃນ heap."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:101
msgid "|span|"
msgstr "|span|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:101
msgid "``std::span``"
msgstr "``std::span``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:101
msgid ""
"Represents read-only access to a contiguous array without needing to copy "
"any data. Note that ``Span`` is designed to be a high performance API: It "
"does not perform parameter correctness checks in the same way you might be "
"used to with other Godot containers. Use with care. `Span` can be "
"constructed from most array-like containers (e.g. ``vector.span()``)."
msgstr ""
"ໃຊ້ສຳລັບການເຂົ້າເຖິງອາເຣແບບອ່ານຢ່າງດຽວ (read-only) ໂດຍບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງກັອບປີ້ຂໍ້ມູນ. ໃຫ້ໝາຍເຫດວ່າ "
"``Span`` ຖືກອອກແບບມາໃຫ້ເປັນ API ທີ່ມີປະສິດທິພາບສູງ: ມັນບໍ່ມີການກວດສອບຄວາມຖືກຕ້ອງຂອງພາຣາມິເຕີຄືກັ"
"ບຄອນເທນເນີອື່ນໆຂອງ Godot. ຄວນໃຊ້ດ້ວຍຄວາມລະມັດລະວັງ. ``Span`` ສາມາດສ້າງຂຶ້ນມາໄດ້ຈາກຄອນເທນ"
"ເນີທີ່ຄ້າຍຄືອາເຣເກືອບທຸກຊະນິດ (ເຊັ່ນ ``vector.span()``)."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:107
msgid "|rb_set|"
msgstr "|rb_set|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:107
msgid "``std::set``"
msgstr "``std::set``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:107
msgid ""
"Uses a `red-black tree <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red-black_tree>`__ for "
"faster access."
msgstr ""
"ໃຊ້ `red-black tree <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red-black_tree>`__ ເພື່ອການເຂົ້"
"າເຖິງທີ່ໄວຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:110
msgid "|v_set|"
msgstr "|v_set|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:110
msgid "``std::flat_set``"
msgstr "``std::flat_set``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:110
msgid ""
"Uses copy-on-write (COW) semantics. This means it's generally slower but can "
"be copied around almost for free. The performance benefits of ``VSet`` "
"aren't established, so prefer using other types."
msgstr ""
"ໃຊ້ຫຼັກການ copy-on-write (COW). ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າມັນຈະຊ້າກວ່າ ແຕ່ກັອບປີ້ໄດ້ເກືອບບໍ່ມີຄ່າໃຊ້ຈ່າຍ. ຍ້ອນວ່າປ"
"ະສິດທິພາບຂອງ ``VSet`` ຍັງບໍ່ຊັດເຈນ, ຈຶ່ງແນະນຳໃຫ້ໃຊ້ປະເພດອື່ນກ່ອນ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:114
msgid "|hash_map|"
msgstr "|hash_map|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:114
msgid ""
"Defensive (robust but slow) map type. Preserves insertion order. Pointers to "
"keys and values, as well as iterators, are stable under mutation. Use this "
"map type when either of these affordances are needed. Use ``AHashMap`` "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""
"ເປັນປະເພດ map ທີ່ເນັ້ນຄວາມໝັ້ນຄົງ (ແຂງແຮງແຕ່ຊ້າ). ມັນຮັກສາລຳດັບການນຳເຂົ້າ. ພອຍເຕີຂອງຄີ (keys) "
"ແລະ ຄ່າ (values), ລວມທັງອິດເຕີເຣເຕີ ຈະຍັງຄົງທີ່ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຈະມີການປ່ຽນແປງຂໍ້ມູນ. ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ປະເພດນີ້ເມື່ອຕ້"
"ອງການຄວາມສາມາດດັ່ງກ່າວ, ຖ້າບໍ່ດັ່ງນັ້ນໃຫ້ໃຊ້ ``AHashMap``."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:119
msgid "|rb_map|"
msgstr "|rb_map|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:119
msgid "``std::map``"
msgstr "``std::map``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:119
msgid ""
"Map type that uses a `red-black tree <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red-"
"black_tree>`__ to find keys. The performance benefits of ``RBMap`` aren't "
"established, so prefer using other types."
msgstr ""
"ເປັນປະເພດ map ທີ່ໃຊ້ `red-black tree <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red-"
"black_tree>`__ ໃນການຄົ້ນຫາຄີ. ປະສິດທິພາບຂອງ ``RBMap`` ຍັງບໍ່ຊັດເຈນ, ຈຶ່ງແນະນຳໃຫ້ໃຊ້ປະເພດອື່"
"ນ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:123
msgid "|dictionary| 📜"
msgstr "|dictionary| 📜"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:123
msgid ""
"Keys and values can be of any Variant type. No static typing is imposed. "
"Uses shared reference counting, similar to ``std::shared_ptr``. Preserves "
"insertion order. Uses ``HashMap<Variant>`` internally."
msgstr ""
"ຄີ ແລະ ຄ່າສາມາດເປັນປະເພດ Variant ໃດກໍໄດ້. ບໍ່ມີການກຳນົດປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນຄົງທີ່. ໃຊ້ລະບົບການນັບການອ້າງອີ"
"ງຮ່ວມກັນ. ຮັກສາລຳດັບການນຳເຂົ້າ. ພາຍໃນແມ່ນໃຊ້ ``HashMap<Variant>``."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:127
msgid "|typed_dictionary| 📜"
msgstr "|typed_dictionary| 📜"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:127
msgid ""
"Subclass of ``Dictionary`` but with static typing for its keys and values."
msgstr ""
"ເປັນຄລາດຍ່ອຍຂອງ ``Dictionary`` ແຕ່ມີການກຳນົດປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນຄົງທີ່ສຳລັບຄີ ແລະ ຄ່າ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:129
msgid "|pair|"
msgstr "|pair|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:129
msgid "``std::pair``"
msgstr "``std::pair``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:129
msgid ""
"Stores a single pair. See also ``KeyValue`` in the same file, which uses "
"read-only keys."
msgstr ""
"ໃຊ້ເກັບຂໍ້ມູນຄູ່ດຽວ. ເບິ່ງ ``KeyValue`` ໃນໄຟລ໌ດຽວກັນນຳ ເຊິ່ງໃຊ້ຄີແບບອ່ານຢ່າງດຽວ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:154
msgid "Relocation safety"
msgstr "ຄວາມປອດໄພໃນການຍ້າຍຕຳແໜ່ງ (Relocation safety)"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:156
msgid ""
"Godot's containers assume their elements are `trivially relocatable <https://"
"open-std.org/JTC1/SC22/WG21/docs/papers/2020/p1144r5.html>`__."
msgstr ""
"ຄອນເທນເນີຂອງ Godot ສັນນິຖານວ່າອົງປະກອບຂອງມັນສາມາດ `ຍ້າຍບ່ອນໄດ້ແບບງ່າຍດາຍ (trivially "
"relocatable) <https://open-std.org/JTC1/SC22/WG21/docs/papers/2020/"
"p1144r5.html>`__."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:158
msgid ""
"This means that, if you store data types in it that have pointers to "
"themselves, or are otherwise `not trivially relocatable <https://open-"
"std.org/JTC1/SC22/WG21/docs/papers/2020/p1144r5.html#non-trivial-"
"samples>`__, Godot might crash. Note that storing **pointers to** objects "
"that are not trivially relocatable, such as some Object subclasses, is "
"unproblematic and supported."
msgstr ""
"ນັ້ນໝາຍຄວາມວ່າ, ຖ້າເຈົ້າເກັບປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນທີ່ມີພອຍເຕີຊີ້ຫາຕົນເອງ ຫຼື `ບໍ່ສາມາດຍ້າຍບ່ອນໄດ້ແບບງ່າຍດາຍ "
"<https://open-std.org/JTC1/SC22/WG21/docs/papers/2020/p1144r5.html#non-"
"trivial-samples>`__, Godot ອາດຈະຄ້າງ ຫຼື ເພ (crash). ໝາຍເຫດວ່າ ການເກັບ **ພອຍເຕີທີ່ຊີ້ໄປ"
"ຫາ** ວັດຖຸທີ່ບໍ່ແມ່ນ trivially relocatable (ເຊັ່ນ ບາງຄລາດຍ່ອຍຂອງ Object) ແມ່ນບໍ່ມີບັນຫາ ແລະ "
"ສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:163
msgid ""
"The reason to assume trivial relocatability is that it allows us to make use "
"of important optimization techniques, such as relocation by ``memcpy`` or "
"``realloc``."
msgstr ""
"ເຫດຜົນທີ່ສັນນິຖານແບບນັ້ນກໍເພື່ອໃຫ້ພວກເຮົາສາມາດໃຊ້ເຕັກນິກການເພີ່ມປະສິດທິພາບທີ່ສຳຄັນໄດ້ ເຊັ່ນ: ການຍ້າຍບ່ອນ"
"ດ້ວຍ ``memcpy`` ຫຼື ``realloc``."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:166
msgid ""
"`GH-100509 <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100509>`__ tracks "
"this decision."
msgstr ""
"`GH-100509 <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100509>`__ ຕິດຕາມການຕັດ"
"ສິນໃຈນີ້."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:171
msgid "Multithreading / Concurrency"
msgstr "ການເຮັດວຽກຫຼາຍເທຣດ / ການເຮັດວຽກພ້ອມກັນ (Multithreading / Concurrency)"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:175
msgid ""
"You can find more information on multithreading strategies "
"at :ref:`doc_using_multiple_threads`."
msgstr ""
"ເຈົ້າສາມາດເບິ່ງຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບກົນລະຍຸດການໃຊ້ຫຼາຍເທຣດໄດ້ທີ່ "
":ref:`doc_using_multiple_threads`."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:177
msgid ""
"None of Godot's containers are thread-safe. When you expect multiple threads "
"to access them, you must use multithread protections."
msgstr ""
"ບໍ່ມີຄອນເທນເນີໃດໆຂອງ Godot ທີ່ປອດໄພຕໍ່ເທຣດ (thread-safe). ເມື່ອເຈົ້າຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ຫຼາຍເທຣດເຂົ້າເຖິງ"
"ພວກມັນ, ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງໃຊ້ລະບົບປ້ອງກັນການເຮັດວຽກຫຼາຍເທຣດ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:180
msgid ""
"Note that some of the types listed here are also available through the "
"bindings, but the binding types are wrapped with :ref:`class_RefCounted` "
"(found in the ``CoreBind::`` namespace). Prefer the primitives listed here "
"when possible, for efficiency reasons."
msgstr ""
"ໝາຍເຫດວ່າ ບາງປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນທີ່ລະບຸຢູ່ນີ້ກໍມີໃຫ້ໃຊ້ຜ່ານ bindings ຄືກັນ, ແຕ່ປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນໃນ bindings ຈະຖືກຫຸ້"
"ມດ້ວຍ :ref:`class_RefCounted` (ຢູ່ໃນ namespace ``CoreBind::``). ຄວນເລືອກໃຊ້ປະເພດພື້ນ"
"ຖານ (primitives) ທີ່ລະບຸຢູ່ນີ້ຫາກເປັນໄປໄດ້ ເພື່ອປະສິດທິພາບທີ່ດີກວ່າ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:187
msgid "|mutex|"
msgstr "|mutex|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:187
msgid "``std::recursive_mutex``"
msgstr "``std::recursive_mutex``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:187
msgid "Recursive mutex type. Use ``MutexLock lock(mutex)`` to lock it."
msgstr ""
"ປະເພດ Mutex ແບບເອີ້ນຊ້ຳ (Recursive). ໃຊ້ ``MutexLock lock(mutex)`` ເພື່ອລັອກມັນ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:189
msgid "|binary_mutex|"
msgstr "|binary_mutex|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:189
#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:194
msgid "``std::mutex``"
msgstr "``std::mutex``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:189
msgid "Non-recursive mutex type. Use ``MutexLock lock(mutex)`` to lock it."
msgstr ""
"ປະເພດ Mutex ແບບບໍ່ເອີ້ນຊ້ຳ (Non-recursive). ໃຊ້ ``MutexLock lock(mutex)`` ເພື່ອລັອກມັນ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:191
msgid "|rw_lock|"
msgstr "|rw_lock|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:191
msgid "``std::shared_mutex``"
msgstr "``std::shared_mutex``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:191
msgid ""
"Read-write aware mutex type. Use ``RWLockRead lock(mutex)`` or ``RWLockWrite "
"lock(mutex)`` to lock it."
msgstr ""
"ປະເພດ Mutex ທີ່ຮອງຮັບການອ່ານ-ຂຽນ. ໃຊ້ ``RWLockRead lock(mutex)`` ຫຼື ``RWLockWrite "
"lock(mutex)`` ເພື່ອລັອກມັນ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:194
msgid "|safe_binary_mutex|"
msgstr "|safe_binary_mutex|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:194
msgid ""
"Recursive mutex type that can be used with ``ConditionVariable``. Use "
"``MutexLock lock(mutex)`` to lock it."
msgstr ""
"ປະເພດ Mutex ແບບເອີ້ນຊ້ຳທີ່ສາມາດໃຊ້ຮ່ວມກັບ ``ConditionVariable`` ໄດ້. ໃຊ້ ``MutexLock "
"lock(mutex)`` ເພື່ອລັອກມັນ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:197
msgid "|condition_variable|"
msgstr "|condition_variable|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:197
msgid "``std::condition_variable``"
msgstr "``std::condition_variable``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:197
msgid "Condition variable type, used with ``SafeBinaryMutex``."
msgstr ""
"ປະເພດຕົວປ່ຽນເງື່ອນໄຂ (Condition variable), ໃຊ້ຮ່ວມກັບ ``SafeBinaryMutex``."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:199
msgid "|semaphore|"
msgstr "|semaphore|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:199
msgid "``std::counting_semaphore``"
msgstr "``std::counting_semaphore``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:199
msgid "Counting semaphore type."
msgstr "ປະເພດເຊມາຟໍ (Semaphore) ແບບນັບ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:201
msgid "|safe_numeric|"
msgstr "|safe_numeric|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:201
#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:205
msgid "``std::atomic``"
msgstr "``std::atomic``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:201
msgid "Templated atomic type, designed for numbers."
msgstr "ປະເພດອາໂຕມິກ (atomic) ແບບເທັມເພລດ, ອອກແບບມາສຳລັບຕົວເລກ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:203
msgid "|safe_flag|"
msgstr "|safe_flag|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:203
msgid "``std::atomic_bool``"
msgstr "``std::atomic_bool``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:203
msgid "Bool atomic type."
msgstr "ປະເພດອາໂຕມິກ (atomic) ແບບ Bool."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:205
msgid "|safe_ref_count|"
msgstr "|safe_ref_count|"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:205
msgid ""
"Atomic type designed for reference counting. Will refuse to increment the "
"reference count if it is 0."
msgstr ""
"ປະເພດອາໂຕມິກອອກແບບມາສຳລັບການນັບການອ້າງອີງ. ມັນຈະບໍ່ຍອມເພີ່ມຈຳນວນການອ້າງອີງຫາກຄ່າມັນເປັນ 0."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:220
msgid "Math types"
msgstr "ປະເພດຄະນິດສາດ (Math types)"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:222
msgid ""
"There are several linear math types available in the ``core/math`` directory:"
msgstr ""
"ມີປະເພດຄະນິດສາດເຊິງເສັ້ນ (linear math) ຫຼາຍຢ່າງທີ່ມີໃຫ້ໃຊ້ໃນໂຟນເດີ ``core/math``:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:225
msgid ""
"`core/math <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/tree/master/core/math>`__"
msgstr ""
"`core/math <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/tree/master/core/math>`__"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:230
msgid ""
"This is a special datatype used for storing paths in a scene tree and "
"referencing them in an optimized manner:"
msgstr ""
"ນີ້ແມ່ນປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນພິເສດທີ່ໃຊ້ສຳລັບການເກັບເສັ້ນທາງ (paths) ໃນ Scene tree ແລະ ການອ້າງອີງພວກມັນດ້ວ"
"ຍວິທີທີ່ມີປະສິດທິພາບສູງ:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:233
msgid ""
"`core/string/node_path.h <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/"
"core/string/node_path.h>`__"
msgstr ""
"`core/string/node_path.h <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/"
"core/string/node_path.h>`__"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:238
msgid ""
"RIDs are *Resource IDs*. Servers use these to reference data stored in them. "
"RIDs are opaque, meaning that the data they reference can't be accessed "
"directly. RIDs are unique, even for different types of referenced data:"
msgstr ""
"RID ແມ່ນ *Resource ID*. ເຊີເວີໃຊ້ສິ່ງເຫຼົ່ານີ້ເພື່ອອ້າງອີງຂໍ້ມູນທີ່ເກັບໄວ້ໃນນັ້ນ. RID ເປັນຂໍ້ມູນແບບ "
"opaque, ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າຂໍ້ມູນທີ່ພວກມັນອ້າງອີງເຖິງນັ້ນບໍ່ສາມາດເຂົ້າເຖິງໄດ້ໂດຍກົງ. RID ແມ່ນຄ່າທີ່ບໍ່ຊ້ຳກັນ, ເຖິງ"
"ແມ່ນວ່າຈະເປັນຂໍ້ມູນຄົນລະປະເພດກໍຕາມ:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/core_types.rst:243
#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_godot_servers.rst:314
msgid ""
"`core/templates/rid.h <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/"
"templates/rid.h>`__"
msgstr ""
"`core/templates/rid.h <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/"
"templates/rid.h>`__"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/variant_class.rst:9
msgid ""
"Variant is the most important datatype in Godot. A Variant takes up only 24 "
"bytes on 64-bit platforms (20 bytes on 32-bit platforms) and can store "
"almost any engine datatype inside of it. Variants are rarely used to hold "
"information for long periods of time, instead they are used mainly for "
"communication, editing, serialization and generally moving data around."
msgstr ""
"Variant ແມ່ນປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນທີ່ສຳຄັນທີ່ສຸດໃນ Godot. ມັນໃຊ້ພື້ນທີ່ພຽງແຕ່ 24 ໄບຕ໌ (bytes) ໃນແພລດຟອມ "
"64-bit (20 ໄບຕ໌ ໃນ 32-bit) ແລະ ສາມາດເກັບປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນເກືອບທຸກຢ່າງຂອງເອັນຈິນໄວ້ພາຍໃນ. ໂດຍທົ່ວ"
"ໄປ Variant ຈະບໍ່ຖືກໃຊ້ເພື່ອເກັບຂໍ້ມູນໄວ້ດົນໆ, ແຕ່ຈະຖືກໃຊ້ເພື່ອການສື່ສານ, ການແກ້ໄຂ, ການເຮັດຊີຣີລຽວໄລເ"
"ຊຊັນ (serialization) ແລະ ການສົ່ງຂໍ້ມູນໄປມາໂດຍທົ່ວໄປ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/variant_class.rst:15
msgid "A Variant can:"
msgstr "Variant ສາມາດ:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/variant_class.rst:17
msgid "Store almost any datatype."
msgstr "ເກັບປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນເກືອບທຸກຢ່າງໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/variant_class.rst:18
msgid ""
"Perform operations between many variants (GDScript uses Variant as its "
"atomic/native datatype)."
msgstr ""
"ເຮັດວຽກຮ່ວມກັນລະຫວ່າງຫຼາຍ variant ໄດ້ (GDScript ໃຊ້ Variant ເປັນປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນພື້ນຖານ)."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/variant_class.rst:20
msgid "Be hashed, so it can be compared quickly to other variants."
msgstr "ຖືກແຮຊ (hashed) ໄດ້, ເພື່ອໃຫ້ສາມາດປຽບທຽບກັບ variant ອື່ນໄດ້ຢ່າງວ່ອງໄວ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/variant_class.rst:21
msgid "Be used to convert safely between datatypes."
msgstr "ໃຊ້ເພື່ອປ່ຽນປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນລະຫວ່າງກັນໄດ້ຢ່າງປອດໄພ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/variant_class.rst:22
msgid ""
"Be used to abstract calling methods and their arguments (Godot exports all "
"its functions through variants)."
msgstr ""
"ໃຊ້ເພື່ອເຮັດໃຫ້ການເອີ້ນໃຊ້ເມັດທອດ ແລະ ອາຣ໌ກິວເມັນເປັນແບບນາມມະທຳ (Godot ສົ່ງຟັງຊັນທັງໝົດອອກມາຜ່ານ "
"variant)."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/variant_class.rst:24
msgid "Be used to defer calls or move data between threads."
msgstr "ໃຊ້ເພື່ອເລື່ອນການເອີ້ນໃຊ້ ຫຼື ສົ່ງຂໍ້ມູນລະຫວ່າງເທຣດ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/variant_class.rst:25
msgid "Be serialized as binary and stored to disk, or transferred via network."
msgstr "ຖືກແປງເປັນຖານສອງ (serialized) ເພື່ອເກັບລົງດິສກ໌ ຫຼື ສົ່ງຜ່ານເຄືອຂ່າຍ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/variant_class.rst:27
msgid ""
"Be serialized to text and use it for printing values and editable settings."
msgstr "ຖືກແປງເປັນຂໍ້ຄວາມເພື່ອໃຊ້ສະແດງຄ່າ ຫຼື ໃຊ້ໃນການຕັ້ງຄ່າທີ່ແກ້ໄຂໄດ້."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/variant_class.rst:29
msgid "Work as an exported property, so the editor can edit it universally."
msgstr ""
"ເຮັດວຽກເປັນຄຸນສົມບັດທີ່ສົ່ງອອກ (exported property), ເພື່ອໃຫ້ editor ສາມາດແກ້ໄຂມັນໄດ້ທົ່ວເຖິງ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/variant_class.rst:30
msgid "Be used for dictionaries, arrays, parsers, etc."
msgstr "ໃຊ້ສຳລັບ dictionary, array, parser ແລະ ອື່ນໆ."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/variant_class.rst:32
msgid ""
"Basically, thanks to the Variant class, writing Godot itself was a much, "
"much easier task, as it allows for highly dynamic constructs not common of C+"
"+ with little effort. Become a friend of Variant today."
msgstr ""
"ເວົ້າງ່າຍໆກໍຄື ຍ້ອນມີຄລາດ Variant ນີ້ເອງທີ່ເຮັດໃຫ້ການຂຽນ Godot ງ່າຍຂຶ້ນຫຼາຍ, ເພາະມັນຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ສາມາດສ້"
"າງໂຄງສ້າງທີ່ມີຄວາມຢືດຢຸ່ນສູງ (Dynamic) ເຊິ່ງປົກກະຕິແລ້ວເຮັດໄດ້ຍາກໃນພາສາ C++. ມາເປັນເພື່ອນກັບ "
"Variant ໄດ້ເລີຍຕັ້ງແຕ່ມື້ນີ້."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/variant_class.rst:38
msgid ""
"All types within Variant except Nil and Object **cannot** be ``null`` and "
"must always store a valid value. These types within Variant are therefore "
"called *non-nullable* types."
msgstr ""
"ທຸກໆປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນພາຍໃນ Variant ຍົກເວັ້ນ Nil ແລະ Object ແມ່ນ **ບໍ່ສາມາດ** ເປັນ ``null`` ໄດ້ "
"ແລະ ຕ້ອງເກັບຄ່າທີ່ຖືກຕ້ອງສະເໝີ. ດັ່ງນັ້ນ ປະເພດຂໍ້ມູນເຫຼົ່ານີ້ໃນ Variant ຈຶ່ງຖືກເອີ້ນວ່າ ປະເພດທີ່ບໍ່ເປັນຄ່າຫວ່າ"
"ງ (*non-nullable*)."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/variant_class.rst:42
msgid ""
"One of the Variant types is *Nil* which can only store the value ``null``. "
"Therefore, it is possible for a Variant to contain the value ``null``, even "
"though all Variant types excluding Nil and Object are non-nullable."
msgstr ""
"ໜຶ່ງໃນປະເພດຂອງ Variant ຄື *Nil* ເຊິ່ງສາມາດເກັບໄດ້ພຽງຄ່າ ``null``. ດັ່ງນັ້ນ, ມັນຈຶ່ງເປັນໄປໄດ້ທີ່ "
"Variant ຈະມີຄ່າເປັນ ``null`` ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າປະເພດ Variant ອື່ນໆ (ຍົກເວັ້ນ Nil ແລະ Object) ຈະ"
"ບໍ່ຮອງຮັບຄ່າຫວ່າງກໍຕາມ."

